s","ru":"Навыки Базы Данных для Разработчиков","ar":"مهارات قاعدة البيانات للمطورين","en":"database"},"description":{"zh":"数据库设计、查询优化和PostgreSQL/MySQL最佳实践的技术总结","ja":"データベース設計、クエリ最適化、PostgreSQL/MySQLのベストプラクティスの技術的まとめ","ko":"데이터베이스 설계, 쿼리 최적화, PostgreSQL/MySQL 최적화 방법의 기술적 요약","es":"La habilidad de base de datos se centra en el diseño de esquemas, la optimización de consultas y las mejores prácticas para PostgreSQL y MySQL","fr":"La compétence base de données se concentre sur la conception de schémas, l''optimisation des requêtes et les meilleures pratiques pour PostgreSQL et MySQL","de":"Die Datenbankfähigkeit konzentriert sich auf das Design von Schemata, die Optimierung von Abfragen und die besten Praktiken für PostgreSQL und MySQL","pt":"Desenvolva habilidades em design de banco de dados, otimização de consultas e práticas recomendadas para PostgreSQL e MySQL","ru":"Разработайте навыки проектирования базы данных, оптимизации запросов и лучших практик для PostgreSQL и MySQL","ar":"طور مهاراتك في تصميم قواعد البيانات، وتحسين الاستعلامات، وأفضل الممارسات لبرامج PostgreSQL و MySQL","en":"Seamlessly route requests to your LLM backends—whether you''re using stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming via..."},"definition":{"en":"Seamlessly route requests to your LLM backends—whether you''re using stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming via Server-Sent Events (SSE). LLMProxy handles both modes out of the box, with zero buffering on streams, intelligent load balancing, and OpenAI-compatible API routing."},"features":{"zh":["数据库设计","查询优化","PostgreSQL/MySQL支持","索引设计","性能优化"],"ja":["データベース設計","クエリ最適化","PostgreSQL/MySQLサポート","インデックス設計","パフォーマンス最適化"],"ko":["데이터베이스 설계","쿼리 최적화","PostgreSQL/MySQL 지원","인덱스 설계","성능 최적화"],"es":["Diseño de esquemas de base de datos","Optimización de consultas","Creación de migraciones","Optimización del rendimiento","Diseño de índices"],"fr":["Conception de schémas de base de données","Optimisation des requêtes","Création de migrations","Optimisation des performances","Conception d''index"],"de":["Entwurf von Datenbankschemata","Optimierung von Abfragen","Erstellung von Migrationen","Leistungsoptimierung","Index-Design"],"pt":["Design de esquemas de banco de dados","Otimização de consultas","Criação de migrações","Otimização de desempenho","Design de índices"],"ru":["Проектирование схем базы данных","Оптимизация запросов","Создание миграций","Оптимизация производительности","Проектирование индексов"],"ar":["تصميم مخططات قواعد البيانات","تحسين الاستعلامات","إنشاء هجرات","تحسين الأداء","تصميم الفهارس"]},"keywords":{"zh":["数据库设计","查询优化","PostgreSQL","MySQL","索引设计","性能优化","数据库性能"],"ja":["データベース設計","クエリ最適化","PostgreSQL","MySQL","インデックス設計","パフォーマンス最適化","データベースパフォーマンス"],"ko":["데이터베이스 설계","쿼리 최적화","PostgreSQL","MySQL","인덱스 설계","성능 최적화","데이터베이스 성능"],"es":["base de datos","diseño de esquemas","optimización de consultas","PostgreSQL","MySQL","mejores prácticas","rendimiento","eficiencia"],"fr":["base de données","conception de schémas","optimisation des requêtes","PostgreSQL","MySQL","meilleures pratiques","performances","efficacité"],"de":["Datenbank","Datenbankschema","Abfrageoptimierung","PostgreSQL","MySQL","Best Practices","Leistung","Effizienz"],"pt":["banco de dados","design de esquemas","otimização de consultas","PostgreSQL","MySQL","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["база данных","проектирование схем","оптимизация запросов","PostgreSQL","MySQL","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["قاعدة البيانات","تصميم مخططات","تحسين الاستعلامات","PostgreSQL","MySQL","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"aiyuekuang","repo":"LLMProxy","repoPath":"aiyuekuang/LLMProxy","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.512Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"database","description":"Database design and optimization. Use for schema design, queries, migrations, indexing, and performance tuning.","bodyPreview":"# Database Skill\n\nDatabase design, query optimization, and best practices for PostgreSQL/MySQL.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing database schemas\n- Writing efficient queries\n- Creating migrations\n- Performance optimization\n- Index design\n\n---\n\n# 📐 Schema Design\n\n## Table Naming\n\n```sql\n-- ✅ Good: snake_case, plural, descriptive\nCREATE TABLE users (...);\nCREATE TABLE api_keys (...);\nCREATE TABLE model_providers (...);\nCREATE TABLE request_logs (...);\n\n-- ❌ Bad: CamelCase, singular, abbrev","body":"# Database Skill\n\nDatabase design, query optimization, and best practices for PostgreSQL/MySQL.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing database schemas\n- Writing efficient queries\n- Creating migrations\n- Performance optimization\n- Index design\n\n---\n\n# 📐 Schema Design\n\n## Table Naming\n\n```sql\n-- ✅ Good: snake_case, plural, descriptive\nCREATE TABLE users (...);\nCREATE TABLE api_keys (...);\nCREATE TABLE model_providers (...);\nCREATE TABLE request_logs (...);\n\n-- ❌ Bad: CamelCase, singular, abbreviations\nCREATE TABLE User (...);\nCREATE TABLE apiKey (...);\nCREATE TABLE mdl_prvdr (...);\n```\n\n## Column Naming\n\n```sql\n-- ✅ Good: snake_case, clear names\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    display_name VARCHAR(100),\n    is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),\n    updated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),\n    deleted_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE\n);\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Timestamps\n```sql\n-- Always include these columns\ncreated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),\nupdated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n\n-- Auto-update updated_at with trigger\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_updated_at()\nRETURNS TRIGGER AS $$\nBEGIN\n    NEW.updated_at = NOW();\n    RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;\n\nCREATE TRIGGER update_users_updated_at\n    BEFORE UPDATE ON users\n    FOR EACH ROW\n    EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at();\n```\n\n### Soft Deletes\n```sql\ndeleted_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE,\n\n-- Query active records\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;\n```\n\n### UUIDs vs Auto-increment\n```sql\n-- UUID (recommended for distributed systems)\nid UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\n-- Auto-increment (simpler, better for single DB)\nid SERIAL PRIMARY KEY\n-- or for larger tables\nid BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔗 Relationships\n\n## One-to-Many\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE api_keys (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    key_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    name VARCHAR(100)\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_api_keys_user_id ON api_keys(user_id);\n```\n\n## Many-to-Many\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE roles (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY,\n    name VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL UNIQUE\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE user_roles (\n    user_id UUID REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    role_id UUID REFERENCES roles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    granted_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),\n    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, role_id)\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔍 Query Optimization\n\n## Use EXPLAIN ANALYZE\n\n```sql\nEXPLAIN ANALYZE\nSELECT u.*, COUNT(ak.id) as key_count\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN api_keys ak ON ak.user_id = u.id\nWHERE u.is_active = true\nGROUP BY u.id;\n```\n\n## Avoid SELECT *\n\n```sql\n-- ❌ Bad: Fetches all columns\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1;\n\n-- ✅ Good: Only needed columns\nSELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE id = $1;\n```\n\n## Use Proper JOINs\n\n```sql\n-- ❌ Bad: Implicit join\nSELECT * FROM users, orders WHERE users.id = orders.user_id;\n\n-- ✅ Good: Explicit JOIN\nSELECT u.name, o.total\nFROM users u\nINNER JOIN orders o ON o.user_id = u.id;\n```\n\n## Batch Operations\n\n```sql\n-- ❌ Bad: Multiple INSERT statements\nINSERT INTO logs (message) VALUES (''log1'');\nINSERT INTO logs (message) VALUES (''log2'');\nINSERT INTO logs (message) VALUES (''log3'');\n\n-- ✅ Good: Single batch INSERT\nINSERT INTO logs (message) VALUES \n    (''log1''),\n    (''log2''),\n    (''log3'');\n```\n\n## Use EXISTS instead of IN for large sets\n\n```sql\n-- ❌ Slower for large subqueries\nSELECT * FROM users \nWHERE id IN (SELECT user_id FROM active_sessions);\n\n-- ✅ Better performance\nSELECT * FROM users u\nWHERE EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1 FROM active_sessions s WHERE s.user_id = u.id\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n# 📇 Indexing\n\n## When to Create Indexes\n\n- Columns in WHERE clauses\n- Columns in JOIN conditions\n- Columns in ORDER BY\n- Columns with high selectivity (many unique values)\n\n## Index Types\n\n```sql\n-- B-tree (default, most common)\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_email ON users(email);\n\n-- Composite index (order matters!)\nCREATE INDEX idx_logs_user_date ON request_logs(user_id, created_at DESC);\n\n-- Partial index (filtered)\nCREATE INDEX idx_active_users ON users(email) WHERE is_active = true;\n\n-- GIN index (for arrays, JSONB)\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_tags ON users USING GIN(tags);\n\n-- Unique index\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_users_email_unique ON users(email);\n```\n\n## Index Guidelines\n\n```sql\n-- ✅ Good: Frequently queried columns\nCREATE INDEX idx_api_keys_key_hash ON api_keys(key_hash);\n\n-- ✅ Good: Foreign keys\nCREATE INDEX idx_api_keys_user_id ON api_keys(user_id);\n\n-- ❌ Bad: Low cardinality columns\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_is_active ON users(is_active);  -- Only true/false\n\n-- ❌ Bad: Too many indexes (slow writes)\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔄 Migrations\n\n## Migration Best Practices\n\n```sql\n-- migrations/001_create_users.sql\n\n-- Up\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    name VARCHAR(100),\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_email ON users(email);\n\n-- Down\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS users;\n```\n\n## Safe Schema Changes\n\n```sql\n-- ✅ Safe: Add column with default (PostgreSQL 11+)\nALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN status VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT ''active'';\n\n-- ✅ Safe: Create index concurrently (no lock)\nCREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_users_status ON users(status);\n\n-- ⚠️ Careful: Add NOT NULL column\n-- First add nullable, backfill, then add constraint\nALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN role VARCHAR(50);\nUPDATE users SET role = ''user'' WHERE role IS NULL;\nALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN role SET NOT NULL;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔒 Security\n\n## Parameterized Queries\n\n```go\n// ❌ NEVER: String concatenation (SQL injection!)\nquery := \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ''\" + email + \"''\"\n\n// ✅ ALWAYS: Parameterized query\nquery := \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1\"\nrow := db.QueryRow(query, email)\n```\n\n## Least Privilege\n\n```sql\n-- Create read-only user for reporting\nCREATE USER report_user WITH PASSWORD ''secure_password'';\nGRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO report_user;\n\n-- App user with limited permissions\nCREATE USER app_user WITH PASSWORD ''secure_password'';\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON users, api_keys TO app_user;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 📊 JSONB Patterns (PostgreSQL)\n\n```sql\n-- Store flexible data\nCREATE TABLE model_configs (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY,\n    model_name VARCHAR(100),\n    parameters JSONB DEFAULT ''{}''::jsonb\n);\n\n-- Query JSONB\nSELECT * FROM model_configs \nWHERE parameters->>''temperature'' = ''0.7'';\n\n-- Index JSONB\nCREATE INDEX idx_configs_params ON model_configs USING GIN(parameters);\n\n-- Update JSONB\nUPDATE model_configs \nSET parameters = parameters || ''{\"max_tokens\": 1000}''::jsonb\nWHERE id = $1;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 📚 References\n\n- [PostgreSQL Documentation](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/)\n- [Use The Index, Luke](https://use-the-index-luke.com/)\n- [sanjay3290/postgres](https://github.com/sanjay3290/ai-skills/tree/main/skills/postgres)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:44:55.500Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced database design and query optimization capabilities for PostgreSQL and MySQL.","zh":"适合需要高级数据库设计和查询优化功能的数据分析代理，支持PostgreSQL和MySQL。","ja":"PostgreSQLとMySQLに対する高度なデータベース設計とクエリ最適化機能を必要とするデータ分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"데이터 분석 에이전트에게 PostgreSQL 및 MySQL을 위한 고급 데이터베이스 설계 및 쿼리 최적화 기능이 필요한 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan capacidades de diseño de base de datos avanzado y optimización de consultas para PostgreSQL y MySQL.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de données ayant besoin de capacités de conception de base de données avancées et d''optimisation de requêtes pour PostgreSQL et MySQL.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte Datenbankdesign- und Abfrageoptimierungsfunktionen für PostgreSQL und MySQL benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de design de banco de dados avançado e capacidades de otimização de consultas para PostgreSQL e MySQL.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы передовые возможности проектирования базы данных и оптимизации запросов для PostgreSQL и MySQL.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل البيانات الذي يحتاج إلى تصميم قاعدة بيانات متقدم وخصائص تحسين الاستعلامات لـ PostgreSQL و MySQL."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design efficient database schemas, write optimized queries, and perform intelligent load balancing using Server-Sent Events and OpenAPI, while ensuring zero buffering on streams.","zh":"赋予代理设计高效数据库模式、编写优化查询和执行智能负载均衡的能力，使用Server-Sent Events和OpenAPI，同时确保流的零缓冲。","ja":"エージェントに効率的なデータベーススキーマを設計し、最適化されたクエリを記述し、Server-Sent EventsとOpenAPIを使用してインテリジェントな負荷分散を実行する能力を付与し、ストリームのゼロバッファリングを保証します。","ko":"代理에게 효율적인 데이터베이스 스키마를 설계하고, 최적화된 쿼리를 작성하며, Server-Sent Events와 OpenAPI를 사용하여 지능형 부하 분산을 수행하는 능력을 부여하며, 스트림의 제로 버퍼링을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar esquemas de base de datos eficientes, escribir consultas optimizadas y realizar un equilibrio de carga inteligente utilizando Server-Sent Events y OpenAPI, garantizando cero almacenamiento en búfer en flujos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des schémas de base de données efficaces, d''écrire des requêtes optimisées et de réaliser un équilibrage de charge intelligent en utilisant les événements envoyés par le serveur et OpenAPI, tout en garantissant un tamponnage nul sur les flux.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, effiziente Datenbankschemata zu entwerfen, optimierte Abfragen zu schreiben und intelligente Lastverteilung mit Server-Sent Events und OpenAPI durchzuführen, während sie sicherstellen, dass in Datenströmen kein Pufferung erfolgt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar esquemas de banco de dados eficientes, escrever consultas otimizadas e realizar balanceamento de carga inteligente usando Server-Sent Events e OpenAPI, garantindo zero bufferização em fluxos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам проектировать эффективные схемы базы данных, писать оптимизированные запросы и выполнять интеллектуальный балансировку нагрузки с помощью Server-Sent Events и OpenAPI, обеспечивая отсутствие буферизации в потоках.","ar":"تمكن العملاء من تصميم مخططات قاعدة بيانات فعالة وكتابة استفسارات محسنة وتحقيق توازن ذكي في التحميل باستخدام Server-Sent Events و OpenAPI، مع ضمان عدم وجود حجز في التدفقات."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing database schemas for large-scale applications","Optimizing queries for improved performance","Creating migrations for database updates"],"zh":["为大规模应用程序设计数据库模式","优化查询以提高性能","为数据库更新创建迁移"],"ja":["大規模アプリケーションのデータベーススキーマを設計する","パフォーマンスの向上のためにクエリを最適化する","データベースの更新のためにマイグレーションを作成する"],"ko":["대규모 애플리케이션을 위한 데이터베이스 스키마 설계","성능 개선 위한 쿼리 최적화","데이터베이스 업데이트 위한 마이그레이션 생성"],"es":["Diseñar esquemas de base de datos para aplicaciones a gran escala","Optimizar consultas para mejorar el rendimiento","Crear migraciones para actualizaciones de base de datos"],"fr":["Concevoir des schémas de base de données pour des applications à grande échelle","Optimiser les requêtes pour améliorer les performances","Créer des migrations pour les mises à jour de base de données"],"de":["Entwerfen von Datenbankschemata für groß angelegte Anwendungen","Optimieren von Abfragen für verbesserte Leistung","Erstellen von Migrationen für Datenbankupdates"],"pt":["Projeto de esquemas de banco de dados para aplicações em larga escala","Otimização de consultas para melhorar o desempenho","Criação de migrações para atualizações de banco de dados"],"ru":["Проектирование схем базы данных для крупномасштабных приложений","Оптимизация запросов для улучшения производительности","Создание миграций для обновления базы данных"],"ar":["تصميم مخططات قاعدة بيانات لتطبيقات على نطاق واسع","تحسين الاستفسارات لتحسين الأداء","إنشاء هجرات لتحديث قاعدة البيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of PostgreSQL and MySQL","Limited to relational databases"],"zh":["需要PostgreSQL和MySQL的知识","仅限关系数据库"],"ja":["PostgreSQLとMySQLの知識が必要","リレーショナルデータベースに限定される"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 및 MySQL에 대한 지식이 필요","관계형 데이터베이스에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de PostgreSQL y MySQL","Limitado a bases de datos relacionales"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en PostgreSQL et MySQL","Limité aux bases de données relationnelles"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von PostgreSQL und MySQL","Begrenzt auf relationale Datenbanken"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de PostgreSQL e MySQL","Limitado a bancos de dados relacionais"],"ru":["Требует знания PostgreSQL и MySQL","Ограничен реляционными базами данных"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة ببرنامج PostgreSQL و MySQL","محدود بقواعد البيانات العلاقية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
