 stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["使用模拟数据","跳过 i18n","跳过 API 调用","匹配设计精度"],"ja":["モックデータを使用","i18n をスキップ","API 呼び出しをスキップ","デザイン精度を一致させる"],"ko":["모의 데이터 사용","i18n 생략","API 호출 생략","디자인 精度 일치"],"es":["Enfoque en la interfaz de usuario","Uso de datos ficticios","Priorización de la interfaz de usuario sobre la integración de datos","Implementación de diseños de Figma de manera precisa","Uso de bibliotecas de componentes para la implementación"],"fr":["Focus sur l''interface utilisateur","Utilisation de données fictives","Priorisation de l''interface utilisateur sur l''intégration de données","Mise en œuvre de conceptions Figma avec précision","Utilisation de bibliothèques de composants pour la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Fokus auf die Benutzeroberfläche","Verwendung von fiktionalem Daten","Priorisierung der Benutzeroberfläche gegenüber der Datenintegration","Implementierung von Figma-Designs mit Präzision","Verwendung von Komponentenbibliotheken für die Implementierung"],"pt":["Priorize a UI sobre a integração de dados","Use dados mock para testar a interface","Evite chamadas de API no início do projeto","Use bibliotecas de componentes para manter a consistência","Desenvolva uma interface de usuário pixel-perfeita"],"ru":["Отдавайте приоритет UI над интеграцией данных","Используйте.mock-данные для тестирования интерфейса","Избегайте вызовов API в начале проекта","Используйте библиотеки компонентов для поддержания согласованности","Разрабатывайте интерфейс пользователя с точностью до пикселя"],"ar":["أعطِ الأولوية لواجهة المستخدم على دمج البيانات","استخدم البيانات الخاضعة للتقليب لاختبار الواجهة","تجنب呼وات API في بداية المشروع","استخدم مكتبات المكونات للحفاظ على الاتساق","طور واجهة مستخدم بدقة عالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Figma 设计","UI 实现","模拟数据","i18n","API 调用","设计精度"],"ja":["Figma デザイン","UI 実装","モックデータ","i18n","API 呼び出し","デザイン精度"],"ko":["피그마 디자인","UI 구현","모의 데이터","i18n","API 호출","디자인 精度"],"es":["implementar diseños de Figma","interfaz de usuario","datos ficticios","priorización de la interfaz de usuario","bibliotecas de componentes","desarrollo de software","diseño de interfaz de usuario"],"fr":["mettre en œuvre des conceptions Figma","interface utilisateur","données fictives","priorisation de l''interface utilisateur","bibliothèques de composants","développement de logiciels","conception d''interface utilisateur"],"de":["Figma-Designs implementieren","Benutzeroberfläche","fiktionale Daten","Priorisierung der Benutzeroberfläche","Komponentenbibliotheken","Softwareentwicklung","Benutzeroberflächendesign"],"pt":["implementação de designs Figma","desenvolvimento de UI","bibliotecas de componentes","dados mock","integração de dados","pixel-perfeita"],"ru":["реализация дизайна Figma","разработка UI","библиотеки компонентов","mock-данные","интеграция данных","точная до пикселя"],"ar":["تنفيذ تصاميم فيجما","تطوير واجهة المستخدم","مكتبات المكونات","البيانات الخاضعة للتقليب","دمج البيانات","دقة عالية"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"implementing-figma-designs","description":"Implements Figma designs 1:1 using the projects component library. Use when implementing UI from Figma, converting designs to code, or building pages/components from design specs. Triggers on figma, design, UI, implementation, Button, Input, Badge, Icon, Stack, XStack, YStack, Dialog, Toast, Alert, Form, Select, Switch, Checkbox, Radio, Tabs, Popover, ActionList, Progress, Skeleton, Image, Avatar, Banner, Carousel, Table, Accordion, ScrollView, ListView, SectionList, Page, Divider, Empty, QRCode, Markdown, Spinner.","bodyPreview":"# Implementing Figma Designs\n\nThis skill helps you implement Figma designs 1:1 using the project''s component library.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Focus on UI First, Data Later\n\nWhen implementing Figma designs, prioritize **pixel-perfect UI** over data integration:\n\n1. **Use mock data** - Hardcode data that matches the design exactly\n2. **Skip i18n** - Use plain strings directly from the design, no `intl.formatMessage`\n3. **Skip API calls** - No need to fetch real data at this stage\n4. **Match the d","body":"# Implementing Figma Designs\n\nThis skill helps you implement Figma designs 1:1 using the project''s component library.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Focus on UI First, Data Later\n\nWhen implementing Figma designs, prioritize **pixel-perfect UI** over data integration:\n\n1. **Use mock data** - Hardcode data that matches the design exactly\n2. **Skip i18n** - Use plain strings directly from the design, no `intl.formatMessage`\n3. **Skip API calls** - No need to fetch real data at this stage\n4. **Match the design** - Focus on visual accuracy, spacing, colors, and layout\n\n### What NOT to do\n\n- Don''t worry about where data comes from\n- Don''t add translation keys (ETranslations)\n- Don''t create API integration or hooks for fetching\n- Don''t add complex state management\n\n### What TO do\n\n- Hardcode text exactly as shown in Figma\n- Create mock data arrays/objects that match the design\n- Focus on component structure and styling\n- Match spacing, colors, and typography from design\n\n## Component Lookup (On-Demand)\n\nWhen you need to use a component, look up its source and demo:\n\n### Source Code Location Pattern\n\n```text\npackages/components/src/{category}/{ComponentName}/\n```\n\nCategories:\n\n- `primitives/` - Button, Icon, Image, Skeleton, Spinner, Stack, Heading, SizeableText\n- `forms/` - Input, TextArea, Select, Checkbox, Radio, Switch, Slider, Form, OTPInput\n- `actions/` - IconButton, ActionList, Alert, Toast, Popover, SegmentControl, Pagination, Tooltip\n- `composite/` - Dialog, Tabs, Banner, Carousel, Table, Stepper\n- `content/` - Badge, Progress, Empty, Divider, QRCode, Markdown, LottieView, LinearGradient, BlurView\n- `layouts/` - Page, ScrollView, ListView, SectionList, Accordion, Swiper, SearchBar\n\n### Demo Location Pattern\n\n```text\npackages/kit/src/views/Developer/pages/Gallery/Components/stories/{ComponentName}.tsx\n```\n\nNote: Some demos have different names (e.g., `AccordionGallery.tsx`, `NewTabsGallery.tsx`)\n\n### How to Look Up a Component\n\n1. **Read the source** to understand props and structure:\n\n   ```text\n   Read: packages/components/src/{category}/{ComponentName}/index.tsx\n   ```\n\n2. **Read the demo** for usage examples:\n\n   ```text\n   Glob: packages/kit/src/views/Developer/pages/Gallery/Components/stories/*{ComponentName}*.tsx\n   ```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Component imports\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button, Stack, XStack, YStack, Icon, ... } from ''@{scope}/components'';\n```\n\n### Spacing Tokens\n\n- `$1` = 4px, `$2` = 8px, `$3` = 12px, `$4` = 16px\n- `$5` = 20px, `$6` = 24px, `$8` = 32px, `$10` = 40px\n\n### Color Tokens\n\n- Text: `$text`, `$textSubdued`, `$textDisabled`\n- Background: `$bg`, `$bgSubdued`, `$bgHover`, `$bgActive`\n- Border: `$border`, `$borderSubdued`, `$borderActive`\n- Icon: `$icon`, `$iconSubdued`, `$iconDisabled`\n\n### Font Size Tokens\n\nHeadings (large to small):\n\n- `$headingXxl`, `$headingXl`, `$headingLg`, `$headingMd`, `$headingSm`, `$headingXs`\n\nBody text (large to small):\n\n- `$bodyLg`, `$bodyMd`, `$bodySm`, `$bodyXs`\n\nWith medium weight (append `Medium`):\n\n- `$bodyLgMedium`, `$bodyMdMedium`, `$bodySmMedium`, `$bodyXsMedium`\n\nUsage with SizableText:\n\n```tsx\n<SizableText size=\"$bodyMd\">Regular text</SizableText>\n<SizableText size=\"$bodyMdMedium\">Medium weight text</SizableText>\n<SizableText size=\"$headingSm\">Small heading</SizableText>\n```\n\n### Common Patterns\n\n**Layout with Stack:**\n\n```tsx\n<YStack gap=\"$4\">        {/* Vertical */}\n<XStack gap=\"$4\">        {/* Horizontal */}\n<Stack gap=\"$4\">         {/* Default vertical */}\n```\n\n**Mock Data:**\n\n```tsx\nconst mockItems = [\n  { name: ''Bitcoin'', symbol: ''BTC'', value: ''$21,432.50'' },\n  { name: ''Ethereum'', symbol: ''ETH'', value: ''$5,892.30'' },\n];\n```\n\n**Button Actions:**\n\n```tsx\n<Button onPress={() => console.log(''clicked'')}>Action</Button>\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Analyze the Figma design using Figma MCP\n2. Identify which components are needed\n3. **Look up each component** - read source and demo on-demand\n4. Create mock data matching the design\n5. Implement the UI with hardcoded values\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:48:43.060Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing precise UI implementation from Figma designs.","zh":"非常适合需要从Figma设计中精确实现UI的前端代理。","ja":"Figmaデザインから正確なUIを実装する必要があるフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。","ko":"피그마 디자인에서 정확한 UI 구현이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan una implementación de UI precisa desde diseños de Figma.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin d''une mise en œuvre de l''UI précise à partir de conceptions Figma.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die eine präzise UI-Implementierung aus Figma-Entwürfen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de implementação de UI precisa a partir de designs do Figma.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым требуется точная реализация UI из дизайнов Figma.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامي الذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ واجهة المستخدم الدقيقة من تصاميم Figma."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement Figma designs 1:1 using a project''s component library, focusing on pixel-perfect UI with mock data, skipping i18n and API calls for initial development, and matching design specifications exactly.","zh":"赋予代理实现Figma设计1：1使用项目的组件库，专注于像素完美的UI，使用模拟数据，跳过初始开发中的i18n和API调用，并完全匹配设计规范。","ja":"プロジェクトのコンポーネントライブラリを使用してFigmaデザインを1：1で実装できるようにエージェントをエンパワーメントし、ピクセルパーフェクトなUIに焦点を当て、モックデータを使用し、初期開発でのi18nとAPI呼び出しをスキップし、デザイン仕様と完全に一致する。","ko":"에이전트가 프로젝트의 컴포넌트 라이브러리를 사용하여 피그마 디자인을 1:1로 구현할 수 있도록 하며, 픽셀 완벽한 UI에 중점을 두고 모의 데이터를 사용하며 초기 개발에서 i18n 및 API 호출을 건너뛰고 디자인 사양과完全 일치하도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar diseños de Figma de manera 1:1 utilizando la biblioteca de componentes de un proyecto, centrándose en una UI perfecta en píxeles con datos de simulación, saltando la internacionalización y las llamadas a la API para el desarrollo inicial, y coincidiendo exactamente con las especificaciones de diseño.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des conceptions Figma de manière 1:1 en utilisant la bibliothèque de composants d''un projet, en se concentrant sur une UI parfaite en pixels avec des données de模拟, en sautant l''internationalisation et les appels d''API pour le développement initial, et en correspondant exactement aux spécifications de conception.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Figma-Entwürfe 1:1 mithilfe der Komponentenbibliothek eines Projekts umzusetzen, wobei der Fokus auf einer pixelgenauen UI mit Mock-Daten liegt, die Internationalisierung und API-Aufrufe für die anfängliche Entwicklung überspringt und den Designspezifikationen genau entspricht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar designs do Figma na proporção 1:1, utilizando a biblioteca de componentes do projeto, focando em UI perfeita em termos de pixel com dados de simulação, pulando i18n e chamadas de API para o desenvolvimento inicial e correspondendo exatamente às especificações de design.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать дизайны Figma в соотношении 1:1, используя библиотеку компонентов проекта, фокусируясь на UI с точностью пикселя и данными-моками, пропуская i18n и вызовы API на начальном этапе разработки и точно соответствуя спецификациям дизайна.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ تصاميم Figma بنسبة 1:1 باستخدام مكتبة مكونات المشروع، مع التركيز على واجهة المستخدم المثالية من حيث البكسل باستخدام بيانات المحاكاة، وتجاوز i18n ونداءات API للتنمية الأولى، والتوافق الدقيق مع مواصفات التصميم."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing Figma designs with pixel-perfect accuracy","Generating UI components from Figma''s component library","Skipping data integration for rapid UI prototyping"],"zh":["使用像素级精度实现Figma设计","从Figma的组件库生成UI组件","跳过数据集成以进行快速UI原型设计"],"ja":["ピクセルレベルの精度でFigmaデザインを実装する","FigmaのコンポーネントライブラリからUIコンポーネントを生成する","データ統合をスキップして迅速なUIプロトタイピングを行う"],"ko":["픽셀 수준의 정확도로 피그마 디자인을 구현하는 것","피그마의 컴포넌트 라이브러리에서 UI 컴포넌트를 생성하는 것","데이터 통합을 건너뛰고 빠른 UI 프로토 타이핑을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Implementar diseños de Figma con precisión de píxeles perfecta","Generar componentes de UI a partir de la biblioteca de componentes de Figma","Saltar la integración de datos para un prototipado de UI rápido"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des conceptions Figma avec une précision de pixels parfaite","Générer des composants d''UI à partir de la bibliothèque de composants Figma","Sauter l''intégration des données pour un prototypage d''UI rapide"],"de":["Figma-Entwürfe mit pixelgenauer Genauigkeit implementieren","UI-Komponenten aus der Figma-Komponentenbibliothek generieren","Datenintegration für schnelles UI-Prototyping überspringen"],"pt":["Implementar designs do Figma com precisão perfeita em termos de pixel","Gerar componentes de UI a partir da biblioteca de componentes do Figma","Pular a integração de dados para prototipagem rápida de UI"],"ru":["Реализовывать дизайны Figma с точностью пикселя","Генерировать компоненты UI из библиотеки компонентов Figma","Пропускать интеграцию данных для быстрой прототипизации UI"],"ar":["تنفيذ تصاميم Figma بدقة مثالية من حيث البكسل","توليد مكونات واجهة المستخدم من مكتبة مكونات Figma","تجاوز تكامل البيانات للنمذجة السريعة لواجهة المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Figma design files","Initial development focuses on UI, not data integration","May require additional steps for i18n and API integration later"],"zh":["需要Figma设计文件","初始开发专注于UI，而不是数据集成","可能需要额外的步骤来实现i18n和API集成"],"ja":["Figmaデザインファイルが必要","初期開発ではUIに焦点を当て、データ統合には焦点を当てていない","i18nとAPI統合を実現するために追加のステップが必要になる可能性がある"],"ko":["피그마 디자인 파일이 필요합니다.","초기 개발은 UI에 중점을 두고 데이터 통합에는 중점을 두지 않음","i18n 및 API 통합을 구현하려면 추가 단계가 필요할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere archivos de diseño de Figma","El desarrollo inicial se centra en la UI, no en la integración de datos","Puede requerir pasos adicionales para la internacionalización y la integración de API más adelante"],"fr":["Nécessite des fichiers de conception Figma","Le développement initial se concentre sur l''UI, et non sur l''intégration des données","Peut nécessiter des étapes supplémentaires pour l''internationalisation et l''intégration d''API plus tard"],"de":["Benötigt Figma-Design-Dateien","Die anfängliche Entwicklung konzentriert sich auf die UI, nicht auf die Datenintegration","Kann zusätzliche Schritte für die Internationalisierung und API-Integration erfordern"],"pt":["Requer arquivos de design do Figma","O desenvolvimento inicial se concentra em UI, não na integração de dados","Pode exigir etapas adicionais para i18n e integração de API posteriormente"],"ru":["Требуется наличие файлов дизайна Figma","Первоначальная разработка фокусируется на UI, а не на интеграции данных","Может потребовать дополнительных шагов для i18n и интеграции API на позднем этапе"],"ar":["يتطلب ملفات تصميم Figma","التنمية الأولى تركز على واجهة المستخدم، وليس على تكامل البيانات","يمكن أن يتطلب خطوات إضافية لتكامل i18n و API في مرحلة لاحقة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/faq', 'community', 'Paxeer-Network', 'Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'faq', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z', '2026-02-18T12:48:42.853Z', NULL, '{"id":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/faq","name":"faq","description":{"zh":"Conventional Commits是一种轻量级的提交约定，用于实现自动化提交解析和版本管理。它提供了一种清晰的方式来表示提交的性质","ja":"Conventional Commitsは、自動化コミット解析とバージョン管理を実現するための軽量なコミット規約です。コミットの性質を明確に表現する方法を提供します","ko":"Conventional Commits는 자동화 커밋 분석 및 버전 관리를 구현하기 위한 경량 커밋 규약입니다. 커밋의 특성을 명확하게 표현하는 방법을 제공합니다","es":"Conventional Commits es un protocolo que facilita la gestión de commits y la generación de changelogs de forma automática","fr":"Conventional Commits est un protocole qui facilite la gestion des commits et la génération de changelogs de manière automatique","de":"Conventional Commits ist ein Protokoll, das die Verwaltung von Commits und die Generierung von Changelogs automatisch erleichtert","pt":"O protocolo de futuros sintéticos perpétuos é uma plataforma que permite aos traders abrir posições longas e curtas com alavancagem de até 1000x","ru":"Синтетический протокол вечных фьючерсов - это платформа, которая позволяет трейдерам открывать длинные и короткие позиции с левериджем до 1000х","ar":"بروتوكول المستقبل السنوي الاصطناعي هو منصة تسمح للمتداولين mởر Vịctions طويلة وقصيرة مع رافعة مالية تصل إلى 1000 مرة","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a cus..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Conventional Commits FAQ: 自动化提交解析","ja":"Conventional Commits FAQ: 自動化コミット解析","ko":"Conventional Commits FAQ: 자동화 커밋 분석","es":"FAQ de Conventional Commits","fr":"FAQ de Conventional Commits","de":"Conventional Commits FAQ","pt":"FAQ: Protocolo de Futuros Sintéticos Perpétuos","ru":"FAQ: Синтетический Протокол Вечных Фьючерсов","ar":"FAQ: بروتوكول المستقبل السنوي الاصطناعي","en":"faq"},"description":{"zh":"Conventional Commits是一种轻量级的提交约定，用于实现自动化提交解析和版本管理。它提供了一种清晰的方式来表示提交的性质","ja":"Conventional Commitsは、自動化コミット解析とバージョン管理を実現するための軽量なコミット規約です。コミットの性質を明確に表現する方法を提供します","ko":"Conventional Commits는 자동화 커밋 분석 및 버전 관리를 구현하기 위한 경량 커밋 규약입니다. 커밋의 특성을 명확하게 표현하는 방법을 제공합니다","es":"Conventional Commits es un protocolo que facilita la gestión de commits y la generación de changelogs de forma automática","fr":"Conventional Commits est un protocole qui facilite la gestion des commits et la génération de changelogs de manière automatique","de":"Conventional Commits ist ein Protokoll, das die Verwaltung von Commits und die Generierung von Changelogs automatisch erleichtert","pt":"O protocolo de futuros sintéticos perpétuos é uma plataforma que permite aos traders abrir posições longas e curtas com alavancagem de até 1000x","ru":"Синтетический протокол вечных фьючерсов - это платформа, которая позволяет трейдерам открывать длинные и короткие позиции с левериджем до 1000х","ar":"بروتوكول المستقبل السنوي الاصطناعي هو منصة تسمح للمتداولين mởر Vịctions طويلة وقصيرة مع رافعة مالية تصل إلى 1000 مرة","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["自动化提交解析","生成变更记录","确定语义版本","清晰地表示提交性质","触发构建和发布过程"],"ja":["自動化コミット解析","変更履歴の生成","セマンティックバージョンの決定","コミットの性質の明確な表現","ビルドと公開プロセスのトリガー"],"ko":["자동화 커밋 분석","변경 기록 생성","의미 버전 결정","커밋 특성의 명확한 표현","빌드 및 발행 프로세스 트리거"],"es":["Generación automática de changelogs","Determinación automática de versiones semánticas","Comunicación clara de cambios a stakeholders","Activación de procesos de construcción y publicación basados en tipos de commits","Soporte para commits con mensaje personalizado"],"fr":["Génération automatique de changelogs","Détermination automatique de versions sémantiques","Communication claire des modifications aux parties prenantes","Activation de processus de construction et de publication basés sur les types de commits","Prise en charge de commits avec message personnalisé"],"de":["Automatische Generierung von Changelogs","Automatische Bestimmung von semantischen Versionen","Klare Kommunikation von Änderungen an Stakeholdern","Auslösung von Build- und Publish-Prozessen basierend auf Commit-Typen","Unterstützung für Commits mit benutzerdefinierten Nachrichten"],"pt":["Suporte a ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices","Alavancagem de até 1000x","Caixa de liquidez centralizada","Preços combinados com oráculo personalizado, Virtual AMM e suavização TWAP"],"ru":["Поддержка активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов","Леверидж до 1000х","Централизованная ликвидационная коробка","Цены, объединенные с пользовательским оракулом, Virtual AMM и сглаживанием TWAP"],"ar":["دعم الأصول RWA والأصول الرقمية والأسهم والمؤشرات","رافعة مالية تصل إلى 1000 مرة","صندوق سيولة مركزي","أسعار مجتمعة مع أوراكل مخصص و AMM افتراضي وتنعيم TWAP"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Conventional Commits","提交消息规范","自动化工具","变更记录","版本管理","语义版本","提交性质"],"ja":["Conventional Commits","コミットメッセージ規約","自動化ツール","変更履歴","バージョン管理","セマンティックバージョン","コミットの性質"],"ko":["Conventional Commits","커밋 메시지 규약","자동화 도구","변경 기록","버전 관리","의미 버전","커밋 특성"],"es":["Conventional Commits","gestión de commits","generación de changelogs","automatización de procesos","versiones semánticas","commits personalizados"],"fr":["Conventional Commits","gestion des commits","génération de changelogs","automatisation des processus","versions sémantiques","commits personnalisés"],"de":["Conventional Commits","Verwaltung von Commits","Generierung von Changelogs","Automatisierung von Prozessen","semantische Versionen","benutzerdefinierte Commits"],"pt":["futuros sintéticos perpétuos","protocolo de futuros","ativos RWA","criptomoedas","ações","índices","alavancagem","caixa de liquidez centralizada"],"ru":["синтетический протокол вечных фьючерсов","протокол фьючерсов","активы RWA","криптовалюты","акции","индексы","леверидж","централизованная ликвидационная коробка"],"ar":["بروتوكول المستقبل السنوي الاصطناعي","بروتوكول المستقبل","أصول RWA","أصول رقمية","أسهم","مؤشرات","رافعة مالية","صندوق سيولة مركزي"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"faq","description":"Frequently asked questions and practical guidance for implementing Conventional Commits in your workflow.","bodyPreview":"# Conventional Commits FAQ\n\n## General Questions\n\n### What is the primary goal of Conventional Commits?\n\nThe primary goal is to provide a lightweight convention on top of commit messages that makes it easier to:\n- Write automated tools that act on commits\n- Generate changelogs automatically\n- Determine semantic version bumps automatically\n- Communicate the nature of changes clearly to all stakeholders\n- Trigger build and publish processes based on commit types\n\n### Why should I use Conventional","body":"# Conventional Commits FAQ\n\n## General Questions\n\n### What is the primary goal of Conventional Commits?\n\nThe primary goal is to provide a lightweight convention on top of commit messages that makes it easier to:\n- Write automated tools that act on commits\n- Generate changelogs automatically\n- Determine semantic version bumps automatically\n- Communicate the nature of changes clearly to all stakeholders\n- Trigger build and publish processes based on commit types\n\n### Why should I use Conventional Commits?\n\n**Benefits:**\n- **Automated Tooling**: Your commits become machine-readable for automated processing\n- **Clear History**: Easy to scan and understand what changed when looking at git log\n- **Semantic Versioning**: Automatic version bumping based on commit types\n- **Changelog Generation**: Auto-generate release notes from commits\n- **Team Communication**: Everyone understands the nature of changes at a glance\n- **Project Organization**: Encourages atomic, well-thought-out commits\n\n### Does using Conventional Commits add extra work?\n\nInitially, yes - it requires thinking about commit structure. However, it saves time by:\n- Enabling automation that would otherwise require manual work\n- Reducing back-and-forth communication about what changed\n- Making code reviews clearer\n- Reducing time spent understanding change history\n\n## Implementation Questions\n\n### How should I deal with commit messages in the initial development phase?\n\nWe recommend that you proceed as if you''ve already released the product. Typically someone, even if it''s your fellow software developers, is using your software. They''ll want to know what''s fixed, what breaks, etc. Starting with Conventional Commits from day one establishes good habits.\n\n### Are the types in the commit title uppercase or lowercase?\n\nAny casing may be used, but consistency is important. Lowercase is recommended:\n```\n✓ feat: add dark mode\n✓ fix: resolve null pointer\n✗ Feat: add dark mode\n✗ Fix: resolve null pointer\n```\n\n### What do I do if the commit conforms to more than one of the commit types?\n\nGo back and make multiple commits whenever possible. Part of the benefit of Conventional Commits is its ability to drive you to make more organized commits and PRs.\n\n**Example - Avoid:**\n```\nfeat: add payment processing and fix calculation bug\n```\n\n**Better - Make Two Commits:**\n```\nfeat: add Stripe payment integration\nfix: correct order total calculation\n```\n\n### How should I capitalize the description?\n\nStart with lowercase (unless using parenthesis for scope):\n\n```\n✓ feat: add dark mode support\n✓ feat(ui): add dark mode support\n✗ feat: Add dark mode support\n✗ feat(ui): Add dark mode support\n```\n\n### Should I use imperative or past tense?\n\nAlways use imperative mood (command form), not past tense:\n\n```\n✓ feat: add user authentication\n✓ fix: resolve login issue\n✓ refactor: simplify request handling\n\n✗ feat: added user authentication\n✗ fix: resolved login issue\n✗ refactor: simplified request handling\n```\n\nThis matches the convention used by git itself (e.g., \"revert: revert commit X\").\n\n### Should I include a period at the end of the description?\n\nNo, omit the period:\n\n```\n✓ feat: add authentication support\n✗ feat: add authentication support.\n```\n\n## Technical Questions\n\n### How long should the description be?\n\nKeep it concise - ideally 50 characters or less. This prevents truncation in various git tools and displays:\n\n```\n✓ feat: add OAuth2 authentication        (40 chars)\n✗ feat: add OAuth2 authentication support to the application  (too long)\n```\n\nIf you need more space, use the body.\n\n### What''s the difference between scope and body?\n\n- **Scope**: Brief context about which part of the system is affected (wrapped in parenthesis)\n  ```\n  feat(auth): add OAuth2 support\n  ```\n\n- **Body**: Detailed explanation of why and how, separated by blank line\n  ```\n  feat(auth): add OAuth2 support\n  \n  Implement OAuth2 authentication flow to provide better security\n  and support for federated identity providers. Users can now log in\n  with Google, GitHub, or Microsoft accounts.\n  ```\n\n### When should I include a body?\n\nInclude a body when:\n- The change is complex or non-obvious\n- You need to explain the \"why\" behind the change\n- There''s important context for future developers\n- The change has implications for other parts of the system\n\nSkip the body for:\n- Simple, obvious changes\n- Small bug fixes with clear intent\n- Documentation fixes\n- Basic refactoring\n\n### How do I indicate a breaking change?\n\nTwo ways:\n\n**Option 1: Use `!` before the colon**\n```\nfeat!: drop support for Node 6\nfeat(api)!: change authentication flow\n```\n\n**Option 2: Use footer**\n```\nfeat: change authentication flow\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: authentication now requires OAuth2 tokens\n```\n\n**Option 3: Both (redundant but clear)**\n```\nfeat!: change authentication flow\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: authentication now requires OAuth2 tokens\n```\n\n## Workflow Questions\n\n### Doesn''t this discourage rapid development and fast iteration?\n\nNo - it discourages moving fast in a disorganized way. It helps you:\n- Move fast long-term across multiple projects\n- Onboard new contributors more easily\n- Maintain clearer history that doesn''t need future investigation\n- Enable automation that would otherwise require manual processes\n\nFast iteration is still possible - you''re just being intentional about commits.\n\n### Might Conventional Commits limit developers to thinking only in the types provided?\n\nConventional Commits encourages us to make more of certain types of commits (like fixes and features). The specification explicitly allows custom types, so:\n\n```\nmycompany: proprietary integration with our system\nperformance-testing: results from performance benchmarks\n```\n\nYour team can extend the specification based on your needs.\n\n### Can I use Conventional Commits in a squash-merge workflow?\n\nYes! In fact, squash-merge workflows are ideal:\n- Casual contributors make any commits they want\n- Lead maintainers clean up commit history when merging\n- The final merged commit follows Conventional Commits\n- No burden on contributors to learn the convention\n\nThis is a common workflow for open source projects.\n\n## Tooling Questions\n\n### How does this relate to SemVer?\n\nConventional Commits enable automatic semantic versioning:\n\n| Commit Type | SemVer Change |\n|------------|---------------|\n| `fix` | PATCH (1.0.0 → 1.0.1) |\n| `feat` | MINOR (1.0.0 → 1.1.0) |\n| `BREAKING CHANGE` | MAJOR (1.0.0 → 2.0.0) |\n\nTools like `semantic-release` automatically parse commits and bump versions.\n\n### What tools support Conventional Commits?\n\nPopular tools that support or require Conventional Commits:\n- **commitlint**: Linter for commit messages\n- **semantic-release**: Automatic versioning and publishing\n- **standard-version**: Changelog generation and versioning\n- **gitflow**: Git workflow tools\n- **husky**: Git hooks for enforcing conventions\n- **conventional-changelog**: Generate changelogs from commits\n\n### Can I enforce Conventional Commits?\n\nYes, using tools like:\n\n**commitlint** - Validate commit message format\n```bash\nnpm install --save-dev @commitlint/config-conventional @commitlint/cli\n```\n\n**husky** - Run hooks on git events\n```bash\nnpm install husky --save-dev\nhusky install\n```\n\n## Common Issues\n\n### I accidentally used the wrong commit type. What do I do?\n\n**Before Merging/Release:**\nUse `git rebase -i` to edit the commit history:\n```bash\ngit rebase -i HEAD~3  # Edit last 3 commits\n```\n\n**After Release:**\nThe cleanup will depend on your tools and processes. Ideally, you''re using automation that can skip malformed commits or handle them gracefully.\n\n### I used a type not in the spec (e.g., \"feet\" instead of \"feat\")\n\nIt''s not the end of the world. The commit will simply be missed by tools that are based on the spec. Automated tools won''t recognize it, but it doesn''t break anything. Fix it in the next commit with a rebase if important.\n\n### What if I can''t follow Conventional Commits in my project?\n\nYou can still benefit from the concept:\n- Use automated tools to reformat commits during merge\n- Educate team members gradually about the benefits\n- Start with a subset of commit types that your team agrees on\n- Use commitlint to enforce the convention\n\n## Contributor Questions\n\n### Do all my contributors need to use Conventional Commits?\n\nNo! Many projects use approaches like:\n- **Squash merging**: PRs can have any commits; the merge commit follows convention\n- **Commit message templates**: Guide developers with templates\n- **Automated reformatting**: Tools clean up commit history on merge\n- **Gradual adoption**: Start with maintainers, encourage contributors over time\n\n### How do I explain Conventional Commits to my team?\n\n**Quick Explanation:**\n\"We use a standard format for commit messages so automated tools can understand what changed. It looks like: `type(scope): description`\"\n\n**Example:**\n```\nfeat(payment): add Stripe integration\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Automatic changelog generation\n- Automatic version bumping\n- Clear history for everyone\n- Tools can act on commits automatically\n\n### What if someone forgets to use the convention?\n\nOptions:\n1. **Gentle reminder**: Point them to your contribution guidelines\n2. **Automated enforcement**: Use commitlint to catch it automatically\n3. **Squash on merge**: Reformat during merge to main branch\n4. **Education**: Share examples and guidelines\n5. **Patience**: Most people adopt it quickly once they see the benefits\n\n## Revert Questions\n\n### How do I handle revert commits?\n\nThe Conventional Commits spec doesn''t define revert behavior explicitly. Recommended approach:\n\n```\nrevert: let us never again speak of the noodle incident\n\nRefs: 676104e, a215868\n```\n\nOr include the original type:\n\n```\nfix: revert incorrect authentication changes from commit a215868\n\nThis reverts commit a215868. The previous approach caused issues with\nfederated identity providers.\n```\n\n### Should I revert or create a new fix commit?\n\n**Revert if:**\n- The commit caused significant problems\n- It''s a recent commit that didn''t provide value\n- You need to preserve that it was reverted\n\n**Create new fix if:**\n- The original code had the right idea but a bug\n- You''re fixing a side effect or unforeseen issue\n- It''s the cleaner approach historically\n\n## Version Compatibility\n\n### How do I version my extensions to the Conventional Commits Specification?\n\nUse SemVer to version your extensions:\n- Document what custom types your project adds\n- Example: `@yourcompany/conventional-commits-config` version `1.0.0`\n- Update versions when you add new types or change rules\n\n---\n\n**License**: [Creative Commons - CC BY 3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/)\n\nSource: [Conventional Commits v1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:48:42.853Z","qualityScore":50}');
