incipes et les modèles de décision pour le développement Node.js en 2025","de":"Lernen Sie die Prinzipien und Entscheidungsmuster für die Entwicklung von Node.js in 2025","pt":"Princípios e tomada de decisões para desenvolvimento Node.js em 2025. Aprenda a pensar, não a memorizar padrões de código.","ru":"Принципы и принятие решений для разработки Node.js в 2025 году. Научитесь думать, а не запоминать шаблоны кода.","ar":"مبادئ واتخاذ القرارات لتطوير node.js في 2025. تعلم التفكير لا تذكر أنماطا من الكود","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["框架选择决策树","决策原则","代码质量优化","开发效率提高","上下文依赖的解决方案"],"ja":["フレームワーク選択の決定木","決定原則","コード品質の最適化","開発効率の向上","コンテキスト依存の解決策"],"ko":["프레임워크 선택 결정 트리","결정 원칙","코드 품질 최적화","개발 효율 향상","컨텍스트 종속의 해결책"],"es":["Selección de framework","Patrones de decisión para desarrollo de aplicaciones","Principios para desarrollo de aplicaciones escalables","Mejores prácticas para desarrollo de aplicaciones seguras","Patrones de diseño para aplicaciones Node.js"],"fr":["Sélection de framework","Modèles de décision pour le développement d''applications","Principes pour le développement d''applications évolutives","Meilleures pratiques pour le développement d''applications sécurisées","Modèles de conception pour les applications Node.js"],"de":["Framework-Auswahl","Entscheidungsmuster für die Anwendungsentwicklung","Prinzipien für die Entwicklung von skalierbaren Anwendungen","Best Practices für die Entwicklung von sicheren Anwendungen","Entwurfsmuster für Node.js-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Seleção de framework baseada no contexto","Princípios de tomada de decisões para desenvolvimento Node.js","Desenvolvimento de aplicações escaláveis e eficientes","Melhores práticas para desenvolvedores Node.js","Otimização de desempenho e segurança"],"ru":["Выбор фреймворка на основе контекста","Принципы принятия решений для разработки Node.js","Разработка масштабируемых и эффективных приложений","Лучшие практики для разработчиков Node.js","Оптимизация производительности и безопасности"],"ar":["اختيار الإطار على أساس السياق","مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات لتطوير node.js","تطوير تطبيقات قابلة للتوسعة والفعالية","أفضل الممارسات لمطوري node.js","تحسين الأداء والأمان"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Node.js","最佳实践","开发效率","代码质量","框架选择","决策原则"],"ja":["Node.js","ベストプラクティス","開発効率","コード品質","フレームワーク選択","決定原則"],"ko":["Node.js","최적화 프랙티스","개발 효율","코드 품질","프레임워크 선택","결정 원칙"],"es":["nodejs","mejores prácticas","desarrollo de aplicaciones","patrones de decisión","framework","escalabilidad","seguridad","diseño de aplicaciones"],"fr":["nodejs","meilleures pratiques","développement d''applications","modèles de décision","framework","évolutivité","sécurité","conception d''applications"],"de":["nodejs","best practices","anwendungsentwicklung","entscheidungsmuster","framework","skalierbarkeit","sicherheit","anwendungsdesign"],"pt":["nodejs","melhores práticas","desenvolvimento nodejs","framework nodejs","aplicações escaláveis","otimização de desempenho","segurança nodejs","princípios de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["nodejs","лучшие практики","разработка nodejs","фреймворк nodejs","масштабируемые приложения","оптимизация производительности","безопасность nodejs","принципы разработки"],"ar":["nodejs","أفضل الممارسات","تطوير nodejs","إطار nodejs","تطبيقات قابلة للتوسعة","تحسين الأداء","أمان nodejs","مبادئ التطوير"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nodejs-best-practices","description":"Node.js development principles and decision-making. Framework selection, async patterns, security, and architecture. Teaches thinking, not copying.","bodyPreview":"# Node.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles and decision-making for Node.js development in 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize code patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for preferences when unclear\n- Choose framework/pattern based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same solution every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── Edge/Serverless (Cloudflare","body":"# Node.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles and decision-making for Node.js development in 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize code patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for preferences when unclear\n- Choose framework/pattern based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same solution every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── Edge/Serverless (Cloudflare, Vercel)\n│   └── Hono (zero-dependency, ultra-fast cold starts)\n│\n├── High Performance API\n│   └── Fastify (2-3x faster than Express)\n│\n├── Enterprise/Team familiarity\n│   └── NestJS (structured, DI, decorators)\n│\n├── Legacy/Stable/Maximum ecosystem\n│   └── Express (mature, most middleware)\n│\n└── Full-stack with frontend\n    └── Next.js API Routes or tRPC\n```\n\n### Comparison Principles\n\n| Factor | Hono | Fastify | Express |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| **Best for** | Edge, serverless | Performance | Legacy, learning |\n| **Cold start** | Fastest | Fast | Moderate |\n| **Ecosystem** | Growing | Good | Largest |\n| **TypeScript** | Native | Excellent | Good |\n| **Learning curve** | Low | Medium | Low |\n\n### Selection Questions to Ask:\n1. What''s the deployment target?\n2. Is cold start time critical?\n3. Does team have existing experience?\n4. Is there legacy code to maintain?\n\n---\n\n## 2. Runtime Considerations (2025)\n\n### Native TypeScript\n\n```\nNode.js 22+: --experimental-strip-types\n├── Run .ts files directly\n├── No build step needed for simple projects\n└── Consider for: scripts, simple APIs\n```\n\n### Module System Decision\n\n```\nESM (import/export)\n├── Modern standard\n├── Better tree-shaking\n├── Async module loading\n└── Use for: new projects\n\nCommonJS (require)\n├── Legacy compatibility\n├── More npm packages support\n└── Use for: existing codebases, some edge cases\n```\n\n### Runtime Selection\n\n| Runtime | Best For |\n|---------|----------|\n| **Node.js** | General purpose, largest ecosystem |\n| **Bun** | Performance, built-in bundler |\n| **Deno** | Security-first, built-in TypeScript |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Architecture Principles\n\n### Layered Structure Concept\n\n```\nRequest Flow:\n│\n├── Controller/Route Layer\n│   ├── Handles HTTP specifics\n│   ├── Input validation at boundary\n│   └── Calls service layer\n│\n├── Service Layer\n│   ├── Business logic\n│   ├── Framework-agnostic\n│   └── Calls repository layer\n│\n└── Repository Layer\n    ├── Data access only\n    ├── Database queries\n    └── ORM interactions\n```\n\n### Why This Matters:\n- **Testability**: Mock layers independently\n- **Flexibility**: Swap database without touching business logic\n- **Clarity**: Each layer has single responsibility\n\n### When to Simplify:\n- Small scripts → Single file OK\n- Prototypes → Less structure acceptable\n- Always ask: \"Will this grow?\"\n\n---\n\n## 4. Error Handling Principles\n\n### Centralized Error Handling\n\n```\nPattern:\n├── Create custom error classes\n├── Throw from any layer\n├── Catch at top level (middleware)\n└── Format consistent response\n```\n\n### Error Response Philosophy\n\n```\nClient gets:\n├── Appropriate HTTP status\n├── Error code for programmatic handling\n├── User-friendly message\n└── NO internal details (security!)\n\nLogs get:\n├── Full stack trace\n├── Request context\n├── User ID (if applicable)\n└── Timestamp\n```\n\n### Status Code Selection\n\n| Situation | Status | When |\n|-----------|--------|------|\n| Bad input | 400 | Client sent invalid data |\n| No auth | 401 | Missing or invalid credentials |\n| No permission | 403 | Valid auth, but not allowed |\n| Not found | 404 | Resource doesn''t exist |\n| Conflict | 409 | Duplicate or state conflict |\n| Validation | 422 | Schema valid but business rules fail |\n| Server error | 500 | Our fault, log everything |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Async Patterns Principles\n\n### When to Use Each\n\n| Pattern | Use When |\n|---------|----------|\n| `async/await` | Sequential async operations |\n| `Promise.all` | Parallel independent operations |\n| `Promise.allSettled` | Parallel where some can fail |\n| `Promise.race` | Timeout or first response wins |\n\n### Event Loop Awareness\n\n```\nI/O-bound (async helps):\n├── Database queries\n├── HTTP requests\n├── File system\n└── Network operations\n\nCPU-bound (async doesn''t help):\n├── Crypto operations\n├── Image processing\n├── Complex calculations\n└── → Use worker threads or offload\n```\n\n### Avoiding Event Loop Blocking\n\n- Never use sync methods in production (fs.readFileSync, etc.)\n- Offload CPU-intensive work\n- Use streaming for large data\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation Principles\n\n### Validate at Boundaries\n\n```\nWhere to validate:\n├── API entry point (request body/params)\n├── Before database operations\n├── External data (API responses, file uploads)\n└── Environment variables (startup)\n```\n\n### Validation Library Selection\n\n| Library | Best For |\n|---------|----------|\n| **Zod** | TypeScript first, inference |\n| **Valibot** | Smaller bundle (tree-shakeable) |\n| **ArkType** | Performance critical |\n| **Yup** | Existing React Form usage |\n\n### Validation Philosophy\n\n- Fail fast: Validate early\n- Be specific: Clear error messages\n- Don''t trust: Even \"internal\" data\n\n---\n\n## 7. Security Principles\n\n### Security Checklist (Not Code)\n\n- [ ] **Input validation**: All inputs validated\n- [ ] **Parameterized queries**: No string concatenation for SQL\n- [ ] **Password hashing**: bcrypt or argon2\n- [ ] **JWT verification**: Always verify signature and expiry\n- [ ] **Rate limiting**: Protect from abuse\n- [ ] **Security headers**: Helmet.js or equivalent\n- [ ] **HTTPS**: Everywhere in production\n- [ ] **CORS**: Properly configured\n- [ ] **Secrets**: Environment variables only\n- [ ] **Dependencies**: Regularly audited\n\n### Security Mindset\n\n```\nTrust nothing:\n├── Query params → validate\n├── Request body → validate\n├── Headers → verify\n├── Cookies → validate\n├── File uploads → scan\n└── External APIs → validate response\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Testing Principles\n\n### Test Strategy Selection\n\n| Type | Purpose | Tools |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| **Unit** | Business logic | node:test, Vitest |\n| **Integration** | API endpoints | Supertest |\n| **E2E** | Full flows | Playwright |\n\n### What to Test (Priorities)\n\n1. **Critical paths**: Auth, payments, core business\n2. **Edge cases**: Empty inputs, boundaries\n3. **Error handling**: What happens when things fail?\n4. **Not worth testing**: Framework code, trivial getters\n\n### Built-in Test Runner (Node.js 22+)\n\n```\nnode --test src/**/*.test.ts\n├── No external dependency\n├── Good coverage reporting\n└── Watch mode available\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n### ❌ DON''T:\n- Use Express for new edge projects (use Hono)\n- Use sync methods in production code\n- Put business logic in controllers\n- Skip input validation\n- Hardcode secrets\n- Trust external data without validation\n- Block event loop with CPU work\n\n### ✅ DO:\n- Choose framework based on context\n- Ask user for preferences when unclear\n- Use layered architecture for growing projects\n- Validate all inputs\n- Use environment variables for secrets\n- Profile before optimizing\n\n---\n\n## 11. Decision Checklist\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- [ ] **Asked user about stack preference?**\n- [ ] **Chosen framework for THIS context?** (not just default)\n- [ ] **Considered deployment target?**\n- [ ] **Planned error handling strategy?**\n- [ ] **Identified validation points?**\n- [ ] **Considered security requirements?**\n\n---\n\n> **Remember**: Node.js best practices are about decision-making, not memorizing patterns. Every project deserves fresh consideration based on its requirements.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:49:34.149Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing advanced Node.js development principles and best practices","zh":"适合需要高级Node.js开发原则和最佳实践的全栈代理","ja":"高度なNode.js開発の原則とベストプラクティスを必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適","ko":"고급 Node.js 개발 원칙 및 모범 사례가 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes Full Stack que necesitan principios y mejores prácticas de desarrollo avanzados de Node.js","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin de principes et de meilleures pratiques de développement Node.js avancés","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die erweiterte Node.js-Entwicklungsprinzipien und -bestpraktiken benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que precisam de princípios avançados de desenvolvimento Node.js e melhores práticas","ru":"Идеально для полноценных агентов, требующих продвинутых принципов разработки Node.js и лучших практик","ar":"مثالي لعميل كامل الحزمة الذي يحتاج إلى مبادئ متقدمة لتطوير Node.js وأفضل الممارسات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to make informed decisions on framework selection, choosing between Edge/Serverless and traditional server-side architectures, and applying context-based pattern decisions using Node.js best practices and principles","zh":"赋予代理人选择框架、在Edge/Serverless和传统服务器端架构之间进行选择以及使用Node.js最佳实践和原则进行基于上下文的模式决策的能力","ja":"エージェントに、フレームワークの選択、Edge/Serverlessと従来のサーバーサイドアーキテクチャの選択、およびNode.jsのベストプラクティスと原則を使用したコンテキストベースのパターンデシジョンを行う決定を下す能力を付与する","ko":"에이전트가 프레임워크를 선택하고, Edge/Serverless와 전통적인 서버 측 아키텍처 사이에서 선택하며, Node.js의 모범 사례 및 원칙을 사용하여 컨텍스트 기반 패턴 결정을 내릴 수 있는 능력을 부여한다","es":"Permite a los agentes tomar decisiones informadas sobre la selección de marcos, eligiendo entre Edge/Serverless y arquitecturas tradicionales de servidor y aplicando decisiones de patrones basadas en el contexto utilizando las mejores prácticas y principios de Node.js","fr":"Permet aux agents de prendre des décisions éclairées sur la sélection des frameworks, en choisissant entre Edge/Serverless et les architectures traditionnelles de serveur et en appliquant des décisions de modèles basées sur le contexte en utilisant les meilleures pratiques et les principes de Node.js","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, fundierte Entscheidungen über die Auswahl von Frameworks zu treffen, zwischen Edge/Serverless und herkömmlichen Server-seitigen Architekturen zu wählen und kontextbasierte Musterentscheidungen unter Anwendung der Node.js-Bestpraktiken und -prinzipien zu treffen","pt":"Permite que os agentes tomem decisões informadas sobre a seleção de estruturas, escolhendo entre Edge/Serverless e arquiteturas tradicionais de servidor e aplicando decisões baseadas em contexto usando as melhores práticas e princípios do Node.js","ru":"Позволяет агентам принимать обоснованные решения о выборе фреймворка, выбирая между Edge/Serverless и традиционными серверными архитектурами, а также применять контекстно-зависимые решения, используя лучшие практики и принципы Node.js","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من اتخاذ قرارات مستنيرة حول اختيار الإطار ، واختيار بين Edge / Serverless والهياكل التقليدية للخادم وتطبيق قرارات قائمة على السياق باستخدام أفضل الممارسات ومبادئ Node.js"},"useCases":{"en":["Selecting optimal frameworks for Node.js projects based on specific requirements","Applying decision-making principles for Node.js development in various contexts","Choosing between Edge/Serverless and traditional server-side architectures for Node.js applications"],"zh":["根据特定要求选择Node.js项目的最佳框架","在各种上下文中应用Node.js开发的决策原则","为Node.js应用程序选择Edge/Serverless和传统服务器端架构"],"ja":["特定要件に基づいてNode.jsプロジェクトに最適なフレームワークを選択する","さまざまなコンテキストでNode.js開発の意思決定原則を適用する","Node.jsアプリケーションにEdge/Serverlessと従来のサーバーサイドアーキテクチャを選択する"],"ko":["특정 요구 사항에 따라 Node.js 프로젝트에 최적의 프레임워크를 선택","다양한 컨텍스트에서 Node.js 개발의 의사 결정 원칙을 적용","Node.js 애플리케이션에 대해 Edge/Serverless와 전통적인 서버 측 아키텍처를 선택"],"es":["Seleccionar marcos óptimos para proyectos Node.js en función de requisitos específicos","Aplicar principios de toma de decisiones para el desarrollo de Node.js en varios contextos","Elegir entre Edge/Serverless y arquitecturas tradicionales de servidor para aplicaciones Node.js"],"fr":["Sélectionner des frameworks optimaux pour les projets Node.js en fonction d''exigences spécifiques","Appliquer des principes de prise de décision pour le développement Node.js dans divers contextes","Choisir entre Edge/Serverless et les architectures traditionnelles de serveur pour les applications Node.js"],"de":["Auswahl optimaler Frameworks für Node.js-Projekte basierend auf spezifischen Anforderungen","Anwendung von Entscheidungsprinzipien für die Node.js-Entwicklung in verschiedenen Kontexten","Wahl zwischen Edge/Serverless und herkömmlichen Server-seitigen Architekturen für Node.js-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Selecionar estruturas ótimas para projetos Node.js com base em requisitos específicos","Aplicar princípios de tomada de decisão para desenvolvimento Node.js em vários contextos","Escolher entre Edge/Serverless e arquiteturas tradicionais de servidor para aplicações Node.js"],"ru":["Выбор оптимальных фреймворков для проектов Node.js на основе конкретных требований","Применение принципов принятия решений для разработки Node.js в различных контекстах","Выбор между Edge/Serverless и традиционными серверными архитектурами для приложений Node.js"],"ar":["اختيار الإطارات المثالية لمشاريع Node.js بناءً على متطلبات محددة","تطبيق مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات لتطوير Node.js في سياقات مختلفة","اختيار بين Edge / Serverless والهياكل التقليدية للخادم لتطبيقات Node.js"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Node.js development principles","Limited to Node.js ecosystem","Context-dependent decision-making required"],"zh":["需要了解Node.js开发原则","仅限于Node.js生态系统","需要基于上下文的决策"],"ja":["Node.js開発の原則を理解する必要がある","Node.jsエコシステムに限定される","コンテキストベースの意思決定が必要"],"ko":["Node.js 개발 원칙을 이해해야 함","Node.js 생태계에만 제한됨","컨텍스트 기반 의사 결정을 필요로 함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de desarrollo de Node.js","Limitado al ecosistema de Node.js","Se requiere toma de decisiones dependiente del contexto"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de développement Node.js","Limité à l''écosystème Node.js","La prise de décision dépendante du contexte est requise"],"de":["Benötigt ein Verständnis der Node.js-Entwicklungsprinzipien","Begrenzt auf das Node.js-Ökosystem","Kontextabhängige Entscheidungsfindung erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer compreensão dos princípios de desenvolvimento Node.js","Limitado ao ecossistema Node.js","Tomada de decisão dependente do contexto é necessária"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов разработки Node.js","Ограничен экосистемой Node.js","Требуется контекстно-зависимое принятие решений"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تطوير Node.js","محدود بنظام Node.js","يتطلب اتخاذ قرارات معتمدة على السياق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('eKoh951/hytale-gg/nextjs-app-router-patterns', 'community', 'eKoh951', 'hytale-gg', 'eKoh951/hytale-gg', 'nextjs-app-router-patterns', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z', '2026-02-18T12:49:42.906Z', NULL, '{"id":"eKoh951/hytale-gg/nextjs-app-router-patterns","name":"nextjs-app-router-patterns","description":{"zh":"Next.js 应用路由器模式提供了构建和优化 Next.js 应用的综合指南","ja":"Next.js アプリルーター パターンは、Next.js アプリの構築と最適化のための包括的なガイドを提供します","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터 패턴은 Next.js 애플리케이션을 구축하고 최적화하는 데 대한 종합 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"Patrones de router de aplicación para Next.js, incluyendo arquitectura de App Router, componentes de servidor y desarrollo de pilas completas de React.","fr":"Modèles de routeur d''application pour Next.js, notamment l''architecture de App Router, les composants serveur et le développement de piles complètes de React.","de":"App-Router-Muster für Next.js, einschließlich App-Router-Architektur, Server-Komponenten und Entwicklung von vollständigen React-Stacks.","pt":"Padrões de roteamento de aplicativos Next.js para desenvolver aplicações full-stack modernas com Server Components e streaming","ru":"Шаблоны маршрутизации приложений Next.js для разработки современных полнофункциональных приложений с Server Components и потоковой передачей","ar":"أنماط مخطط التوجيه لتطبيقات Next.js لتطوير تطبيقات كامل الحزمة الحديثة مع مكونات الخادم والبث","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Next.js 应用路由器模式","ja":"Next.js アプリルーター パターン","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터 패턴","es":"Patrones de Router de Aplicación de Next.js","fr":"Modèles de Routeur d''Application Next.js","de":"Next.js App Router Muster","pt":"Padrões de Roteamento de Aplicativos Next.js","ru":"Шаблоны маршрутизации приложений Next.js","ar":"أنماط مخطط التوجيه لتطبيقات Next.js","en":"nextjs-app-router-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"Next.js 应用路由器模式提供了构建和优化 Next.js 应用的综合指南","ja":"Next.js アプリルーター パターンは、Next.js アプリの構築と最適化のための包括的なガイドを提供します","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터 패턴은 Next.js 애플리케이션을 구축하고 최적화하는 데 대한 종합 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"Patrones de router de aplicación para Next.js, incluyendo arquitectura de App Router, componentes de servidor y desarrollo de pilas completas de React.","fr":"Modèles de routeur d''application pour Next.js, notamment l''architecture de App Router, les composants serveur et le développement de piles complètes de React.","de":"App-Router-Muster für Next.js, einschließlich App-Router-Architektur, Server-Komponenten und Entwicklung von vollständigen React-Stacks.","pt":"Padrões de roteamento de aplicativos Next.js para desenvolver aplicações full-stack modernas com Server Components e streaming","ru":"Шаблоны маршрутизации приложений Next.js для разработки современных полнофункциональных приложений с Server Components и потоковой передачей","ar":"أنماط مخطط التوجيه لتطبيقات Next.js لتطوير تطبيقات كامل الحزمة الحديثة مع مكونات الخادم والبث","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["应用路由器架构","服务器组件和流媒体","并行和拦截路由","数据获取和缓存优化","全栈功能构建"],"ja":["アプリルーター アーキテクチャ","サーバー コンポーネントとストリーミング","並列とインターセプト ルーティング","データ取得とキャッシュの最適化","フルスタック機能の構築"],"ko":["애플리케이션 라우터 아키텍처","서버 컴포넌트 및 스트리밍","병렬 및 인터셉트 라우팅","데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱 최적화","풀스택 기능 구축"],"es":["Arquitectura de App Router","Componentes de servidor y transmisión","Rutas paralelas e interceptadas","Optimización de la recuperación y almacenamiento en caché de datos","Características de pilas completas con acciones de servidor"],"fr":["Architecture de App Router","Composants serveur et diffusion en continu","Routes parallèles et interceptées","Optimisation de la récupération et du stockage en cache des données","Fonctionnalités de piles complètes avec actions de serveur"],"de":["App-Router-Architektur","Server-Komponenten und Streaming","Parallele und abfangende Routen","Optimierung der Datenabfrage und Zwischenspeicherung","Funktionen von vollständigen Stacks mit Server-Aktionen"],"pt":["Roteamento de aplicativos com App Router","Implementação de Server Components e streaming","Configuração de rotas paralelas e interceptadoras","Otimização de busca de dados e cache","Desenvolvimento de recursos full-stack com Server Actions"],"ru":["Маршрутизация приложений с App Router","Реализация Server Components и потоковой передачи","Настройка параллельных и перехватывающих маршрутов","Оптимизация поиска данных и кэша","Разработка полнофункциональных функций с Server Actions"],"ar":["مخطط التوجيه لتطبيقات مع App Router","تنفيذ مكونات الخادم والبث","إعداد مسارات موازية ومتجاوزة","تحسين استرجاع البيانات والذاكرة المؤقتة","بناء ميزات كامل الحزمة مع إجراءات الخادم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Next.js","应用路由器","服务器组件","全栈 React","数据获取","缓存优化","并行路由","拦截路由"],"ja":["Next.js","アプリルーター","サーバー コンポーネント","フルスタック React","データ取得","キャッシュ最適化","並列ルーティング","インターセプト ルーティング"],"ko":["Next.js","애플리케이션 라우터","서버 컴포넌트","풀스택 React","데이터 가져오기","캐싱 최적화","병렬 라우팅","인터셉트 라우팅"],"es":["Next.js","App Router","Componentes de servidor","Desarrollo de pilas completas de React","Arquitectura de aplicación web","Optimización de rendimiento","Recuperación y almacenamiento en caché de datos"],"fr":["Next.js","App Router","Composants serveur","Développement de piles complètes de React","Architecture d''application web","Optimisation des performances","Récupération et stockage en cache des données"],"de":["Next.js","App-Router","Server-Komponenten","Entwicklung von vollständigen React-Stacks","Webanwendungsarchitektur","Leistungsoptimierung","Datenabfrage und Zwischenspeicherung"],"pt":["Next.js","App Router","Server Components","full-stack","roteamento de aplicativos","desenvolvimento web","React","JavaScript"],"ru":["Next.js","App Router","Server Components","полнофункциональный","маршрутизация приложений","веб-разработка","React","JavaScript"],"ar":["Next.js","App Router","مكونات الخادم","كامل الحزمة","مخطط التوجيه لتطبيقات","تطوير الويب","React","JavaScript"]}},"owner":"eKoh951","repo":"hytale-gg","repoPath":"eKoh951/hytale-gg","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nextjs-app-router-patterns","description":"Master Next.js 14+ App Router with Server Components, streaming, parallel routes, and advanced data fetching. Use when building Next.js applications, implementing SSR/SSG, or optimizing React Server Components.","bodyPreview":"# Next.js App Router Patterns\n\nComprehensive patterns for Next.js 14+ App Router architecture, Server Components, and modern full-stack React development.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building new Next.js applications with App Router\n- Migrating from Pages Router to App Router\n- Implementing Server Components and streaming\n- Setting up parallel and intercepting routes\n- Optimizing data fetching and caching\n- Building full-stack features with Server Actions\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Rendering Mo","body":"# Next.js App Router Patterns\n\nComprehensive patterns for Next.js 14+ App Router architecture, Server Components, and modern full-stack React development.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building new Next.js applications with App Router\n- Migrating from Pages Router to App Router\n- Implementing Server Components and streaming\n- Setting up parallel and intercepting routes\n- Optimizing data fetching and caching\n- Building full-stack features with Server Actions\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Rendering Modes\n\n| Mode                  | Where        | When to Use                               |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| **Server Components** | Server only  | Data fetching, heavy computation, secrets |\n| **Client Components** | Browser      | Interactivity, hooks, browser APIs        |\n| **Static**            | Build time   | Content that rarely changes               |\n| **Dynamic**           | Request time | Personalized or real-time data            |\n| **Streaming**         | Progressive  | Large pages, slow data sources            |\n\n### 2. File Conventions\n\n```\napp/\n├── layout.tsx       # Shared UI wrapper\n├── page.tsx         # Route UI\n├── loading.tsx      # Loading UI (Suspense)\n├── error.tsx        # Error boundary\n├── not-found.tsx    # 404 UI\n├── route.ts         # API endpoint\n├── template.tsx     # Re-mounted layout\n├── default.tsx      # Parallel route fallback\n└── opengraph-image.tsx  # OG image generation\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\n// app/layout.tsx\nimport { Inter } from ''next/font/google''\nimport { Providers } from ''./providers''\n\nconst inter = Inter({ subsets: [''latin''] })\n\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: { default: ''My App'', template: ''%s | My App'' },\n  description: ''Built with Next.js App Router'',\n}\n\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\" suppressHydrationWarning>\n      <body className={inter.className}>\n        <Providers>{children}</Providers>\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/page.tsx - Server Component by default\nasync function getProducts() {\n  const res = await fetch(''https://api.example.com/products'', {\n    next: { revalidate: 3600 }, // ISR: revalidate every hour\n  })\n  return res.json()\n}\n\nexport default async function HomePage() {\n  const products = await getProducts()\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Products</h1>\n      <ProductGrid products={products} />\n    </main>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Server Components with Data Fetching\n\n```typescript\n// app/products/page.tsx\nimport { Suspense } from ''react''\nimport { ProductList, ProductListSkeleton } from ''@/components/products''\nimport { FilterSidebar } from ''@/components/filters''\n\ninterface SearchParams {\n  category?: string\n  sort?: ''price'' | ''name'' | ''date''\n  page?: string\n}\n\nexport default async function ProductsPage({\n  searchParams,\n}: {\n  searchParams: Promise<SearchParams>\n}) {\n  const params = await searchParams\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex gap-8\">\n      <FilterSidebar />\n      <Suspense\n        key={JSON.stringify(params)}\n        fallback={<ProductListSkeleton />}\n      >\n        <ProductList\n          category={params.category}\n          sort={params.sort}\n          page={Number(params.page) || 1}\n        />\n      </Suspense>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// components/products/ProductList.tsx - Server Component\nasync function getProducts(filters: ProductFilters) {\n  const res = await fetch(\n    `${process.env.API_URL}/products?${new URLSearchParams(filters)}`,\n    { next: { tags: [''products''] } }\n  )\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(''Failed to fetch products'')\n  return res.json()\n}\n\nexport async function ProductList({ category, sort, page }: ProductFilters) {\n  const { products, totalPages } = await getProducts({ category, sort, page })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div className=\"grid grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n        {products.map((product) => (\n          <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />\n        ))}\n      </div>\n      <Pagination currentPage={page} totalPages={totalPages} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Client Components with ''use client''\n\n```typescript\n// components/products/AddToCartButton.tsx\n''use client''\n\nimport { useState, useTransition } from ''react''\nimport { addToCart } from ''@/app/actions/cart''\n\nexport function AddToCartButton({ productId }: { productId: string }) {\n  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition()\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    setError(null)\n    startTransition(async () => {\n      const result = await addToCart(productId)\n      if (result.error) {\n        setError(result.error)\n      }\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={handleClick}\n        disabled={isPending}\n        className=\"btn-primary\"\n      >\n        {isPending ? ''Adding...'' : ''Add to Cart''}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p className=\"text-red-500 text-sm\">{error}</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Server Actions\n\n```typescript\n// app/actions/cart.ts\n\"use server\";\n\nimport { revalidateTag } from \"next/cache\";\nimport { cookies } from \"next/headers\";\nimport { redirect } from \"next/navigation\";\n\nexport async function addToCart(productId: string) {\n  const cookieStore = await cookies();\n  const sessionId = cookieStore.get(\"session\")?.value;\n\n  if (!sessionId) {\n    redirect(\"/login\");\n  }\n\n  try {\n    await db.cart.upsert({\n      where: { sessionId_productId: { sessionId, productId } },\n      update: { quantity: { increment: 1 } },\n      create: { sessionId, productId, quantity: 1 },\n    });\n\n    revalidateTag(\"cart\");\n    return { success: true };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { error: \"Failed to add item to cart\" };\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function checkout(formData: FormData) {\n  const address = formData.get(\"address\") as string;\n  const payment = formData.get(\"payment\") as string;\n\n  // Validate\n  if (!address || !payment) {\n    return { error: \"Missing required fields\" };\n  }\n\n  // Process order\n  const order = await processOrder({ address, payment });\n\n  // Redirect to confirmation\n  redirect(`/orders/${order.id}/confirmation`);\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Parallel Routes\n\n```typescript\n// app/dashboard/layout.tsx\nexport default function DashboardLayout({\n  children,\n  analytics,\n  team,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n  analytics: React.ReactNode\n  team: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"dashboard-grid\">\n      <main>{children}</main>\n      <aside className=\"analytics-panel\">{analytics}</aside>\n      <aside className=\"team-panel\">{team}</aside>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/dashboard/@analytics/page.tsx\nexport default async function AnalyticsSlot() {\n  const stats = await getAnalytics()\n  return <AnalyticsChart data={stats} />\n}\n\n// app/dashboard/@analytics/loading.tsx\nexport default function AnalyticsLoading() {\n  return <ChartSkeleton />\n}\n\n// app/dashboard/@team/page.tsx\nexport default async function TeamSlot() {\n  const members = await getTeamMembers()\n  return <TeamList members={members} />\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Intercepting Routes (Modal Pattern)\n\n```typescript\n// File structure for photo modal\n// app/\n// ├── @modal/\n// │   ├── (.)photos/[id]/page.tsx  # Intercept\n// │   └── default.tsx\n// ├── photos/\n// │   └── [id]/page.tsx            # Full page\n// └── layout.tsx\n\n// app/@modal/(.)photos/[id]/page.tsx\nimport { Modal } from ''@/components/Modal''\nimport { PhotoDetail } from ''@/components/PhotoDetail''\n\nexport default async function PhotoModal({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n}) {\n  const { id } = await params\n  const photo = await getPhoto(id)\n\n  return (\n    <Modal>\n      <PhotoDetail photo={photo} />\n    </Modal>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/photos/[id]/page.tsx - Full page version\nexport default async function PhotoPage({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n}) {\n  const { id } = await params\n  const photo = await getPhoto(id)\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"photo-page\">\n      <PhotoDetail photo={photo} />\n      <RelatedPhotos photoId={id} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/layout.tsx\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n  modal,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n  modal: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        {modal}\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Streaming with Suspense\n\n```typescript\n// app/product/[id]/page.tsx\nimport { Suspense } from ''react''\n\nexport default async function ProductPage({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n}) {\n  const { id } = await params\n\n  // This data loads first (blocking)\n  const product = await getProduct(id)\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Immediate render */}\n      <ProductHeader product={product} />\n\n      {/* Stream in reviews */}\n      <Suspense fallback={<ReviewsSkeleton />}>\n        <Reviews productId={id} />\n      </Suspense>\n\n      {/* Stream in recommendations */}\n      <Suspense fallback={<RecommendationsSkeleton />}>\n        <Recommendations productId={id} />\n      </Suspense>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// These components fetch their own data\nasync function Reviews({ productId }: { productId: string }) {\n  const reviews = await getReviews(productId) // Slow API\n  return <ReviewList reviews={reviews} />\n}\n\nasync function Recommendations({ productId }: { productId: string }) {\n  const products = await getRecommendations(productId) // ML-based, slow\n  return <ProductCarousel products={products} />\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: Route Handlers (API Routes)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/products/route.ts\nimport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\n\nexport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  const searchParams = request.nextUrl.searchParams;\n  const category = searchParams.get(\"category\");\n\n  const products = await db.product.findMany({\n    where: category ? { category } : undefined,\n    take: 20,\n  });\n\n  return NextResponse.json(products);\n}\n\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  const body = await request.json();\n\n  const product = await db.product.create({\n    data: body,\n  });\n\n  return NextResponse.json(product, { status: 201 });\n}\n\n// app/api/products/[id]/route.ts\nexport async function GET(\n  request: NextRequest,\n  { params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> },\n) {\n  const { id } = await params;\n  const product = await db.product.findUnique({ where: { id } });\n\n  if (!product) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Product not found\" }, { status: 404 });\n  }\n\n  return NextResponse.json(product);\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 8: Metadata and SEO\n\n```typescript\n// app/products/[slug]/page.tsx\nimport { Metadata } from ''next''\nimport { notFound } from ''next/navigation''\n\ntype Props = {\n  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>\n}\n\nexport async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {\n  const { slug } = await params\n  const product = await getProduct(slug)\n\n  if (!product) return {}\n\n  return {\n    title: product.name,\n    description: product.description,\n    openGraph: {\n      title: product.name,\n      description: product.description,\n      images: [{ url: product.image, width: 1200, height: 630 }],\n    },\n    twitter: {\n      card: ''summary_large_image'',\n      title: product.name,\n      description: product.description,\n      images: [product.image],\n    },\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function generateStaticParams() {\n  const products = await db.product.findMany({ select: { slug: true } })\n  return products.map((p) => ({ slug: p.slug }))\n}\n\nexport default async function ProductPage({ params }: Props) {\n  const { slug } = await params\n  const product = await getProduct(slug)\n\n  if (!product) notFound()\n\n  return <ProductDetail product={product} />\n}\n```\n\n## Caching Strategies\n\n### Data Cache\n\n```typescript\n// No cache (always fresh)\nfetch(url, { cache: \"no-store\" });\n\n// Cache forever (static)\nfetch(url, { cache: \"force-cache\" });\n\n// ISR - revalidate after 60 seconds\nfetch(url, { next: { revalidate: 60 } });\n\n// Tag-based invalidation\nfetch(url, { next: { tags: [\"products\"] } });\n\n// Invalidate via Server Action\n(\"use server\");\nimport { revalidateTag, revalidatePath } from \"next/cache\";\n\nexport async function updateProduct(id: string, data: ProductData) {\n  await db.product.update({ where: { id }, data });\n  revalidateTag(\"products\");\n  revalidatePath(\"/products\");\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Start with Server Components** - Add ''use client'' only when needed\n- **Colocate data fetching** - Fetch data where it''s used\n- **Use Suspense boundaries** - Enable streaming for slow data\n- **Leverage parallel routes** - Independent loading states\n- **Use Server Actions** - For mutations with progressive enhancement\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t pass serializable data** - Server → Client boundary limitations\n- **Don''t use hooks in Server Components** - No useState, useEffect\n- **Don''t fetch in Client Components** - Use Server Components or React Query\n- **Don''t over-nest layouts** - Each layout adds to the component tree\n- **Don''t ignore loading states** - Always provide loading.tsx or Suspense\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Next.js App Router Documentation](https://nextjs.org/docs/app)\n- [Server Components RFC](https://github.com/reactjs/rfcs/blob/main/text/0188-server-components.md)\n- [Vercel Templates](https://vercel.com/templates/next.js)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:49:42.906Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing advanced Next.js 14+ App Router architecture expertise.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Next.js 14+ App Router 架构专业知识的全栈开发代理。","ja":"Next.js 14+ の App Router アーキテクチャの高度な専門知識を必要とするフルスタック開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 Next.js 14+ App Router 아키텍처 전문 지식을 필요로 하는 풀스택 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo full-stack que necesitan experiencia avanzada en arquitectura de App Router de Next.js 14+.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement full-stack ayant besoin d''une expertise avancée en architecture App Router Next.js 14+.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Entwicklungsagenten, die Expertenwissen in der App-Router-Architektur von Next.js 14+ benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Full-Stack que necessitam de expertise avançada em arquitetura de App Router do Next.js 14+.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов полного стека разработки, которым требуется продвинутая экспертиза в архитектуре App Router Next.js 14+.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الكامل الذي يحتاج إلى خبرة متقدمة في هيكل маршروت التطبيق الخاص بـ Next.js 14+."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement Server Components, streaming data fetching, and parallel/intercepting routes while optimizing caching strategies and leveraging Server Actions for full-stack features.","zh":"使代理能够实现服务器组件、流数据获取和并行/拦截路由，同时优化缓存策略并利用服务器操作实现全栈功能。","ja":"エージェントがサーバーコンポーネント、ストリーミングデータ取得、および並行/インターセプトルーティングを実装し、キャッシュ戦略を最適化し、サーバーアクションを使用してフルスタック機能を実現できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 서버 컴포넌트, 스트리밍 데이터 가져오기 및 병렬/ 인터셉트 라우팅을 구현하고 캐싱 전략을 최적화하며 서버 액션을 사용하여 풀스택 기능을 구현할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar componentes de servidor, captura de datos de transmisión y rutas paralelas/interceptadas, al mismo tiempo que optimiza las estrategias de caché y aprovecha las acciones de servidor para características de full-stack.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des composants serveur, une collecte de données de streaming et des routes parallèles/interceptées, tout en optimisant les stratégies de mise en cache et en exploitant les actions serveur pour les fonctionnalités full-stack.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Serverkomponenten, Streaming-Datenabruf und parallele/interceptierende Routen zu implementieren, während sie gleichzeitig Caching-Strategien optimieren und Serveraktionen für Full-Stack-Funktionen nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementarem Componentes de Servidor, obtenção de dados em streaming e rotas paralelas/interceptadas, otimizando estratégias de cache e utilizando Ações de Servidor para recursos de pilha completa.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать компоненты сервера, потоковую загрузку данных и параллельные/перехватывающие маршруты, оптимизируя стратегии кэширования и используя действия сервера для функций полного стека.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية تنفيذ مكونات الخادم و استرجاع البيانات بالتدفق و المسارات الموازية / المُمسكة، مع تحسين استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت واستخدام إجراءات الخادم لميزات الستاك الكاملة."},"useCases":{"en":["Migrating legacy Pages Router applications to App Router","Implementing streaming UI with React Server Components","Setting up complex routing patterns with parallel and intercepting routes","Optimizing data fetching strategies with built-in caching mechanisms","Building full-stack features using Server Actions"],"zh":["将遗留的 Pages Router 应用程序迁移到 App Router","使用 React 服务器组件实现流 UI","使用并行和拦截路由设置复杂的路由模式","使用内置缓存机制优化数据获取策略","使用服务器操作构建全栈功能"],"ja":["レガシーの Pages Router アプリケーションを App Router に移行する","React サーバーコンポーネントを使用してストリーミング UI を実装する","並行およびインターセプトルーティングを使用して複雑なルーティングパターンを設定する","ビルトインキャッシュメカニズムを使用してデータ取得戦略を最適化する","サーバーアクションを使用してフルスタック機能を構築する"],"ko":["레거시 Pages Router 애플리케이션을 App Router로 마이그레이션","React 서버 컴포넌트를 사용하여 스트리밍 UI 구현","병렬 및 인터셉트 라우팅을 사용하여 복잡한 라우팅 패턴 설정","내장 캐싱 메커니즘을 사용하여 데이터 가져오기 전략 최적화","서버 액션을 사용하여 풀스택 기능 구축"],"es":["Migrar aplicaciones de Pages Router heredadas a App Router","Implementar interfaz de usuario de streaming con componentes de servidor de React","Configurar patrones de enrutamiento complejos con rutas paralelas e interceptadas","Optimizar estrategias de captura de datos con mecanismos de caché integrados","Crear características de full-stack utilizando acciones de servidor"],"fr":["Migrer des applications Pages Router héritées vers App Router","Mettre en œuvre une interface utilisateur de streaming avec des composants serveur React","Configurer des modèles de routage complexes avec des routes parallèles et interceptées","Optimiser les stratégies de collecte de données avec des mécanismes de mise en cache intégrés","Construire des fonctionnalités full-stack en utilisant des actions serveur"],"de":["Legacy-Seiten-Router-Anwendungen auf App-Router migrieren","Implementierung von Streaming-Benutzeroberflächen mit React-Serverkomponenten","Einrichten komplexer Routingmuster mit parallelen und interceptierenden Routen","Optimierung von Datenabrufstrategien mit integrierten Cachemechanismen","Erstellen von Full-Stack-Funktionen mithilfe von Serveraktionen"],"pt":["Migrar aplica