ion de plans: Protocole de futures synthétiques","de":"Ausführung von Plänen: Synthetisches Futures-Protokoll","pt":"Executando Planos com Eficiência","ru":"Выполнение Планов с Высокой Точностью","ar":"تنفيذ الخطط بفعالية","en":"executing-plans"},"description":{"zh":"执行计划技能是一种批量执行任务、审查检查点和实施计划的技术","ja":"計画の実行スキルは、バッチ実行、チェックポイントのレビュー、計画の実施を行う技術です","ko":"실행 계획 기술은 일괄 처리, 체크포인트 검토 및 계획 구현을 위한 기술입니다","es":"El protocolo de futuros sintéticos permite a los traders abrir posiciones apalancadas con un apalancamiento de hasta 1000x, con colateralización en monedas e...","fr":"Le protocole de futures synthétiques permet aux traders d''ouvrir des positions à effet de levier avec un effet de levier allant jusqu''à 1000x, avec une colla...","de":"Das synthetische Futures-Protokoll ermöglicht es Tradern, mit einem Hebel von bis zu 1000x zu handeln, mit einer Besicherung in stabilen Münzen","pt":"O skill de execução de planos permite que os desenvolvedores executem tarefas em lotes com pontos de verificação para revisão do arquiteto","ru":"Умение выполнения планов позволяет разработчикам выполнять задачи пакетно с контрольными точками для проверки архитектора","ar":"مهارة تنفيذ الخطط تمكن المطورين من تنفيذ المهام بشكل مجموعات مع نقاط فحص لمراجعة المصمم","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["批量执行任务","审查检查点","实施计划","使用scopecraft加载计划文件","批次之间报告审查结果","支持多种资产交易"],"ja":["バッチ実行","チェックポイントのレビュー","計画の実施","scopecraftを使用して計画ファイルをロード","バッチの間でレビュー結果を報告","多様なアセット取引をサポート"],"ko":["일괄 처리","체크포인트 검토","계획 구현","scopecraft를 사용하여 계획 파일 로드","배치 사이에서 검토 결과를 보고","다양한 자산 거래 지원"],"es":["Soporte para activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices","Apalancamiento de hasta 1000x con colateralización en monedas estables","Bóveda de liquidez centralizada como contraparte para todos los trades","Precios que combinan un oráculo personalizado, un AMM virtual y suavizado TWAP"],"fr":["Prise en charge des actifs RWA, des crypto-monnaies, des actions et des indices","Effet de levier allant jusqu''à 1000x avec une collatéralisation en monnaies stables","Chambre de liquidité centralisée en tant que contrepartie pour tous les trades","Prix qui combinent un oracle personnalisé, un AMM virtuel et un lissage TWAP"],"de":["Unterstützung für RWA-Assets, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes","Hebel von bis zu 1000x mit Besicherung in stabilen Münzen","Zentrale Liquiditätsbörse als Kontrahent für alle Trades","Preise, die einen benutzerdefinierten Oracle, ein virtuelles AMM und ein TWAP-Glättung kombinieren"],"pt":["Execução de tarefas em lotes","Pontos de verificação para revisão do arquiteto","Uso de oracle personalizado e Virtual AMM","Suporte a ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices","Posições alavancadas longas/curtas com até 1000x","Vault de liquidez central como contraparte para todas as negociações"],"ru":["Выполнение задач пакетно","Контрольные точки для проверки архитектора","Использование индивидуального оракула и виртуальной AMM","Поддержка активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов","Заложенные длинные/короткие позиции с до 1000x","Центральный vault ликвидности как контрагент для всех сделок"],"ar":["تنفيذ المهام بشكل مجموعات","نقاط فحص لمراجعة المصمم","استخدام أوراكل مخصص و AMM افتراضي","دعم للاصول RWA، العملات المشفرة، الأسهم، والفهارس","مراكز طويلة/قصيرة مرفوعة مع ما يصل إلى 1000x","خزانة السيولة المركزية كطرف مقابل لجميع الصفقات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["执行计划","批量执行","审查检查点","实施计划","scopecraft","计划文件","资产交易","合成永续期货协议"],"ja":["計画の実行","バッチ実行","チェックポイントのレビュー","計画の実施","scopecraft","計画ファイル","アセット取引","合成永続期貨プロトコル"],"ko":["실행 계획","일괄 처리","체크포인트 검토","계획 구현","scopecraft","계획 파일","자산 거래","합성 영속적 선물 프로토콜"],"es":["protocolo de futuros sintéticos","activos RWA","criptomonedas","acciones","índices","apalancamiento","colateralización","monedas estables"],"fr":["protocole de futures synthétiques","actifs RWA","crypto-monnaies","actions","indices","effet de levier","collatéralisation","monnaies stables"],"de":["synthetisches Futures-Protokoll","RWA-Assets","Kryptowährungen","Aktien","Indizes","Hebel","Besicherung","stabile Münzen"],"pt":["execução de planos","desenvolvimento de software","otimização de processos","oracle personalizado","Virtual AMM","RWA","criptomoedas","ações","índices","posições alavancadas"],"ru":["выполнение планов","разработка программного обеспечения","оптимизация процессов","индивидуальный оракул","виртуальная AMM","RWA","криптовалюты","акции","индексы","заложенные позиции"],"ar":["تنفيذ الخطط","تطوير البرمجيات","تحسين العمليات","أوراكل مخصص","AMM افتراضي","RWA","العملات المشفرة","الأسهم","الفهارس","مراكز مرفوعة"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"executing-plans","description":"Use when partner provides a complete implementation plan to execute in controlled batches with review checkpoints - loads plan, reviews critically, executes tasks in batches, reports for review between batches","bodyPreview":"# Executing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nLoad plan, review critically, execute tasks in batches, report for review between batches.\n\n**Core principle:** Batch execution with checkpoints for architect review.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the executing-plans skill to implement this plan.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Load and Review Plan\n1. Read plan file (use scopecraft to load it if not already)\n2. Review critically - identify any questions or concerns about the plan\n3. If concerns: Raise them with","body":"# Executing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nLoad plan, review critically, execute tasks in batches, report for review between batches.\n\n**Core principle:** Batch execution with checkpoints for architect review.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the executing-plans skill to implement this plan.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Load and Review Plan\n1. Read plan file (use scopecraft to load it if not already)\n2. Review critically - identify any questions or concerns about the plan\n3. If concerns: Raise them with your human partner before starting\n4. If no concerns: Create TodoWrite and proceed\n\n### Step 2: Execute Batch\n**Default: First 3 tasks**\n\nFor each task:\n1. Mark as in_progress\n2. Follow each step exactly (plan has bite-sized steps)\n3. Run verifications as specified\n4. Mark as completed\n\n### Step 3: Report\nWhen batch complete:\n- Show what was implemented\n- Show verification output\n- Say: \"Ready for feedback.\"\n\n### Step 4: Continue\nBased on feedback:\n- Apply changes if needed\n- Execute next batch\n- Repeat until complete\n\n### Step 5: Complete Development\n\nAfter all tasks complete and verified:\n- Announce: \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n- **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch\n- Follow that skill to verify tests, present options, execute choice\n\n## When to Stop and Ask for Help\n\n**STOP executing immediately when:**\n- Hit a blocker mid-batch (missing dependency, test fails, instruction unclear)\n- Plan has critical gaps preventing starting\n- You don''t understand an instruction\n- Verification fails repeatedly\n\n**Ask for clarification rather than guessing.**\n\n## When to Revisit Earlier Steps\n\n**Return to Review (Step 1) when:**\n- Partner updates the plan based on your feedback\n- Fundamental approach needs rethinking\n\n**Don''t force through blockers** - stop and ask.\n\n## Remember\n- Review plan critically first\n- Follow plan steps exactly\n- Don''t skip verifications\n- Reference skills when plan says to\n- Between batches: just report and wait\n- Stop when blocked, don''t guess\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:50:52.209Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Autonomous Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain needing structured plan execution and review protocols.","zh":"适用于 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 等自主代理，需要结构化计划执行和审查协议。","ja":"AutoGPTやLangChainなどの自律エージェントに適しており、構造化された計画の実行とレビューのプロトコルが必要です。","ko":"AutoGPT와 LangChain 같은 자율 에이전트에 적합하며, 구조화된 계획 실행 및 검토 프로토콜이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Autónomos como AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan protocolos de ejecución y revisión de planes estructurados.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents autonomes comme AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant des protocoles d''exécution et de révision de plans structurés.","de":"Ideal für autonome Agenten wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die strukturierte Plan-Ausführungs- und Überprüfungsprotokolle benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Autônomos como AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de protocolos de execução e revisão de planos estruturados.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, которым необходимы структурированные протоколы выполнения и проверки планов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المستقلين مثل AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى بروتوكولات تنفيذ وتحقق خطة منظمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to load, critically review, and execute plans in batches, utilizing protocols like scopecraft for plan loading, and facilitating architect review through checkpoint reporting, all while supporting tasks such as leveraged long/short positions and stablecoin collateralization.","zh":"赋予代理批量加载、批判性审查和执行计划的能力，利用scopecraft等协议进行计划加载，并通过检查点报告促进架构师审查，同时支持杠杆多头/空头仓位和稳定币抵押等任务。","ja":"エージェントに、プランをバッチでロードして批判的にレビューし、実行する機能を提供します。scopecraftなどのプロトコルを使用してプランをロードし、チェックポイントレポートを通じてアーキテクトのレビューを促進し、レバレッジのロング/ショートポジションやステーブルコインの担保などのタスクをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트에 배치로 계획을 로드하고 비판적으로 검토하여 실행하는 능력을 부여하며, scopecraft와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 계획을 로드하고, 체크포인트 보고를 통해 아키텍트의 검토를 촉진하며, 레버리지 롱/숏 포지션 및 스테이블코인 담보와 같은 태스크를 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a cargar, revisar críticamente y ejecutar planes en lotes, utilizando protocolos como scopecraft para la carga de planes y facilitando la revisión del arquitecto a través de informes de puntos de control, todo mientras admite tareas como posiciones largas/cortas apalancadas y colateralización de stablecoin.","fr":"Permet aux agents de charger, d''examiner de manière critique et d''exécuter des plans par lots, en utilisant des protocoles tels que scopecraft pour le chargement de plans et en facilitant la révision de l''architecte par le biais de rapports de points de contrôle, le tout tout en prenant en charge des tâches telles que des positions longues/courtes à effet de levier et une collatéralisation de stablecoin.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Pläne zu laden, kritisch zu überprüfen und in Batches auszuführen, indem Protokolle wie scopecraft für die Planladung verwendet werden und die Architektüberprüfung durch Checkpoint-Berichterstattung erleichtert wird, während gleichzeitig Aufgaben wie gehebelte Long-/Short-Positionen und Stablecoin-Besicherung unterstützt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a carregar, revisar criticamente e executar planos em lotes, utilizando protocolos como scopecraft para carregar planos e facilitar a revisão do arquiteto por meio de relatórios de pontos de verificação, ao mesmo tempo em que suporta tarefas como posições longas/curtas alavancadas e garantia de stablecoin.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью загружать, критически просматривать и выполнять планы пакетно, используя протоколы, такие как scopecraft, для загрузки планов, и облегчая проверку архитектора посредством отчетов о контрольных точках, при этом поддерживая задачи, такие как левериджные длинные/короткие позиции и обеспечение стейблкоином.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تحميل ومراجعة حرجة وتنفيذ خطط بالجملة، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل scopecraft لتحميل الخطط وتسهيل مراجعة المصمم من خلال تقارير نقاط التحقق، وفي الوقت نفسه دعم مهام مثل المواقف الطويلة / القصيرة المرفوعة وتأمين العملة المستقرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Executing synthetic perpetual futures protocols","Managing leveraged positions with stablecoin collateral","Implementing batch execution with checkpoints for review"],"zh":["执行合成永续期货协议","使用稳定币担保管理杠杆仓位","实施带检查点的批量执行"],"ja":["合成永続先物プロトコルの実行","ステーブルコイン担保を使用したレバレッジポジションの管理","チェックポイントを使用したバッチ実行の実装"],"ko":["합성 永續 선물 프로토콜의 실행","스테이블코인 담보를 사용한 레버리지 포지션 관리","체크포인트를 사용한 배치 실행 구현"],"es":["Ejecutar protocolos de futuros perpetuos sintéticos","Gestionar posiciones con apalancamiento con colateralización de stablecoin","Implementar ejecución por lotes con puntos de control para revisión"],"fr":["Exécuter des protocoles de futures perpétuels synthétiques","Gérer des positions à effet de levier avec une collatéralisation de stablecoin","Mettre en œuvre une exécution par lots avec des points de contrôle pour la révision"],"de":["Ausführen von Protokollen für synthetische Perpetual-Futures","Verwalten von Positionen mit Hebelwirkung mit Stablecoin-Besicherung","Umsetzen von Batch-Ausführung mit Checkpoints für Überprüfung"],"pt":["Execução de protocolos de futuros sintéticos perpétuos","Gerenciamento de posições alavancadas com garantia de stablecoin","Implementação de execução em lotes com pontos de verificação para revisão"],"ru":["Выполнение протоколов синтетических вечных фьючерсов","Управление левериджными позициями с обеспечением стейблкоином","Реализация пакетной обработки с контрольными точками для проверки"],"ar":["تنفيذ بروتوكولات العقود الآجلة الم합طة الدائمة","إدارة المواقف المرفوعة بالعملة المستقرة","تطبيق التنفيذ بالجملة مع نقاط التحقق للتحقق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires plan file access","Dependent on scopecraft for plan loading","Limited to batch execution with review checkpoints"],"zh":["需要计划文件访问","依赖scopecraft进行计划加载","仅限批量执行带检查点的审查"],"ja":["プランファイルへのアクセスが必要","scopecraftに依存してプランをロードする","チェックポイントを使用したバッチ実行のレビューのみ"],"ko":["계획 파일 액세스가 필요","scopecraft에 의존하여 계획을 로드","체크포인트를 사용한 배치 실행 검토만"],"es":["Requiere acceso al archivo de planes","Dependiente de scopecraft para la carga de planes","Limitado a la ejecución por lotes con puntos de control de revisión"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au fichier de plans","Dépendant de scopecraft pour le chargement de plans","Limité à l''exécution par lots avec des points de contrôle de révision"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Plan-Datei","Abhängig von scopecraft für die Planladung","Begrenzt auf Batch-Ausführung mit Checkpoints für Überprüfung"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arquivo de plano","Dependente de scopecraft para carregar planos","Limitado à execução em lotes com pontos de verificação para revisão"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлу плана","Зависит от scopecraft для загрузки планов","Ограничен пакетной обработкой с контрольными точками для проверки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملف الخطة","يعتمد على scopecraft لتحميل الخطط","محدود بالتنفيذ بالجملة مع نقاط التحقق للتحقق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/test-driven-development', 'community', 'Paxeer-Network', 'Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'test-driven-development', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z', '2026-02-18T12:51:01.365Z', NULL, '{"id":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/test-driven-development","name":"test-driven-development","description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发是一种软件开发过程，通过先写测试用例，然后编写代码来满足测试要求，确保代码质量和可靠性","ja":"テスト駆動開発は、テストケースを先に書き、コードを書いてテスト要件を満たすソフトウェア開発プロセスで、コードの品質と信頼性を確保する","ko":"테스트 주도 개발은 테스트 케이스를 먼저 작성한 다음 코드를 작성하여 테스트 요구 사항을 충족시키는 소프트웨어 개발 프로세스로 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 보장합니다","es":"TDD es una práctica de desarrollo que implica escribir las pruebas antes del código, mejorando la calidad y estabilidad del software","fr":"Le TDD est une pratique de développement qui consiste à écrire les tests avant le code, améliorant ainsi la qualité et la stabilité du logiciel","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungspraxis, bei der die Tests vor dem Code geschrieben werden, um die Qualität und Stabilität der Software zu verbessern","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por testes é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que envolve escrever testes antes de escrever o código","ru":"Разработка через тестирование - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, который включает в себя написание тестов до написания кода","ar":"التطوير الموجه من خلال الاختبار هو نهج لتطوير البرمجيات يتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة الشفرة","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a cus..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)","es":"Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD) para Devs","fr":"Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD) pour Développeurs","de":"Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) für Entwickler","pt":"Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","ru":"Разработка через тестирование","ar":"التطوير الموجه من خلال الاختبار","en":"test-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发是一种软件开发过程，通过先写测试用例，然后编写代码来满足测试要求，确保代码质量和可靠性","ja":"テスト駆動開発は、テストケースを先に書き、コードを書いてテスト要件を満たすソフトウェア開発プロセスで、コードの品質と信頼性を確保する","ko":"테스트 주도 개발은 테스트 케이스를 먼저 작성한 다음 코드를 작성하여 테스트 요구 사항을 충족시키는 소프트웨어 개발 프로세스로 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 보장합니다","es":"TDD es una práctica de desarrollo que implica escribir las pruebas antes del código, mejorando la calidad y estabilidad del software","fr":"Le TDD est une pratique de développement qui consiste à écrire les tests avant le code, améliorant ainsi la qualité et la stabilité du logiciel","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungspraxis, bei der die Tests vor dem Code geschrieben werden, um die Qualität und Stabilität der Software zu verbessern","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por testes é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que envolve escrever testes antes de escrever o código","ru":"Разработка через тестирование - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, который включает в себя написание тестов до написания кода","ar":"التطوير الموجه من خلال الاختبار هو نهج لتطوير البرمجيات يتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة الشفرة","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["先写测试用例","编写最小代码满足测试要求","确保代码质量和可靠性","适用于新特性、bug修复和重构","提高开发效率和代码可维护性"],"ja":["テストケースを先に書く","最小限のコードを書いてテスト要件を満たす","コードの品質と信頼性を確保する","新機能、バグ修正、リファクタリングに適する","開発効率とコードの保守性を向上させる"],"ko":["테스트 케이스를 먼저 작성","최소한의 코드를 작성하여 테스트 요구 사항을 충족","코드 품질과 신뢰성을 보장","새로운 기능, 버그 수정, 리팩토링에 적합","개발 효율성과 코드 유지 보수성을 향상"],"es":["Escribe las pruebas antes del código","Mejora la calidad y estabilidad del software","Reduce los errores y bugs","Facilita el refactoring y la refactorización"],"fr":["Écrivez les tests avant le code","Améliorez la qualité et la stabilité du logiciel","Réduisez les erreurs et les bogues","Facilitez le refactoring et la réorganisation"],"de":["Schreiben Sie die Tests vor dem Code","Verbessern Sie die Qualität und Stabilität der Software","Reduzieren Sie Fehler und Bugs","Erleichtern Sie das Refactoring und die Umstrukturierung"],"pt":["Escrever testes antes de escrever o código","Verificar a falha do teste","Escrever código mínimo para passar no teste","Refatorar o código","Aplicar em novos recursos, correções de bugs e refatoração"],"ru":["Написание тестов до написания кода","Проверка неудачи теста","Написание минимального кода для прохождения теста","Рефакторинг кода","Применение к новым функциям, исправлению багов и рефакторингу"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة الشفرة","تحقق فشل الاختبار","كتابة شفرة قليلة لاجتياز الاختبار","إعادة هيكلة الشفرة","تطبيق على ميزات جديدة وتصحيح الأخطاء وإعادة الهيكلة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","TDD","软件开发","代码质量","开发效率","测试用例","代码可维护性"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","TDD","ソフトウェア開発","コードの品質","開発効率","テストケース","コードの保守性"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","TDD","소프트웨어 개발","코드 품질","개발 효율성","테스트 케이스","코드 유지 보수성"],"es":["TDD","Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","pruebas unitarias","pruebas de integración","refactoring","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["TDD","Développement Piloté par les Tests","tests unitaires","tests d''intégration","refactoring","développement de logiciels"],"de":["TDD","Testgetriebene Entwicklung","Einheitstests","Integrationstests","Refactoring","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento dirigido por testes","tdd","testes unitários","refatoração","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software","práticas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["разработка через тестирование","tdd","юнит-тесты","рефакторинг","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения","практики разработки"],"ar":["التطوير الموجه من خلال الاختبار","tdd","اختبارات الوحدة","إعادة الهيكلة","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات","ممارسات التطوير"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"test-driven-development","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code - write the test first, watch it fail, write minimal code to pass; ensures tests actually verify behavior by requiring failure first","bodyPreview":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD","body":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That''s rationalization.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_red -> red [label=\"wrong\\nfailure\"];\n    green -> verify_green;\n    verify_green -> refactor [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_green -> green [label=\"no\"];\n    refactor -> verify_green [label=\"stay\\ngreen\"];\n    verify_green -> next;\n    next -> red;\n}\n```\n\n### RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\ntest(''retries failed operations 3 times'', async () => {\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const operation = () => {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts < 3) throw new Error(''fail'');\n    return ''success'';\n  };\n\n  const result = await retryOperation(operation);\n\n  expect(result).toBe(''success'');\n  expect(attempts).toBe(3);\n});\n```\nClear name, tests real behavior, one thing\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\ntest(''retry works'', async () => {\n  const mock = jest.fn()\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(''success'');\n  await retryOperation(mock);\n  expect(mock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);\n});\n```\nVague name, tests mock not code\n</Bad>\n\n**Requirements:**\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n### Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n**Test errors?** Fix error, re-run until it fails correctly.\n\n### GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      if (i === 2) throw e;\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(''unreachable'');\n}\n```\nJust enough to pass\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options?: {\n    maxRetries?: number;\n    backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n    onRetry?: (attempt: number) => void;\n  }\n): Promise<T> {\n  // YAGNI\n}\n```\nOver-engineered\n</Bad>\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n### Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n**Other tests fail?** Fix now.\n\n### REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n### Repeat\n\nNext failing test for next feature.\n\n## Good Tests\n\n| Quality | Good | Bad |\n|---------|------|-----|\n| **Minimal** | One thing. \"and\" in name? Split it. | `test(''validates email and domain and whitespace'')` |\n| **Clear** | Name describes behavior | `test(''test1'')` |\n| **Shows intent** | Demonstrates desired API | Obscures what code should do |\n\n## Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n- You never saw it catch the bug\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n- \"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive\n\nAutomated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust. Working code without real tests is technical debt.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower.\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required. You verify remembered edge cases, not discovered ones.\n\nTests-first force edge case discovery before implementing. Tests-after verify you remembered everything (you didn''t).\n\n30 minutes of tests after ≠ TDD. You get coverage, lose proof tests work.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference, write tests first\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n| \"TDD will slow me down\" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |\n| \"Manual test faster\" | Manual doesn''t prove edge cases. You''ll re-test every change. |\n| \"Existing code has no tests\" | You''re improving it. Add tests for existing code. |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- Rationalizing \"just this once\"\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n- \"TDD is dogmatic, I''m being pragmatic\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n## Example: Bug Fix\n\n**Bug:** Empty email accepted\n\n**RED**\n```typescript\ntest(''rejects empty email'', async () => {\n  const result = await submitForm({ email: '''' });\n  expect(result.error).toBe(''Email required'');\n});\n```\n\n**Verify RED**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nFAIL: expected ''Email required'', got undefined\n```\n\n**GREEN**\n```typescript\nfunction submitForm(data: FormData) {\n  if (!data.email?.trim()) {\n    return { error: ''Email required'' };\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Verify GREEN**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nPASS\n```\n\n**REFACTOR**\nExtract validation for multiple fields if needed.\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nBefore marking work complete:\n\n- [ ] Every new function/method has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n## When Stuck\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Don''t know how to test | Write wished-for API. Write assertion first. Ask your human partner. |\n| Test too complicated | Design too complicated. Simplify interface. |\n| Must mock everything | Code too coupled. Use dependency injection. |\n| Test setup huge | Extract helpers. Still complex? Simplify design. |\n\n## Debugging Integration\n\nBug found? Write failing test reproducing it. Follow TDD cycle. Test proves fix and prevents regression.\n\nNever fix bugs without a test.\n\n## Final Rule\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\nNo exceptions without your human partner''s permission.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:51:01.365Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents needing rigorous testing protocols like Test-Driven Development (TDD) for ensuring code reliability and stability.","zh":"适合需要严格测试协议的代码审查代理，例如测试驱动开发（TDD），以确保代码的可靠性和稳定性。","ja":"厳密なテストプロトコルが必要なコードレビューエージェントに適しています。たとえば、テスト駆動開発（TDD）によりコードの信頼性と安定性を確保します。","ko":"엄격한 테스트 프로토콜이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 예를 들어, 테스트 주도 개발(TDD)을 통해 코드의 신뢰성과 안정성을 보장합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan protocolos de prueba rigurosos como Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD) para garantizar la confiabilidad y estabilidad del código.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant des protocoles de test rigoureux tels que le développement piloté par les tests (TDD) pour assurer la fiabilité et la stabilité du code.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agenten, die strenge Testprotokolle wie Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) benötigen, um die Zuverlässigkeit und Stabilität des Codes zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de protocolos de teste rigorosos, como Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD), para garantir a confiabilidade e estabilidade do código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, требующих строгих протоколов тестирования, таких как Разработка, управляемая тестированием (TDD), для обеспечения надежности и стабильности кода.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل مراجعة الشفرة التي تحتاج إلى بروتوكولات اختبار صارمة مثل التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) لضمان موثوقية الشفرة وثباتها."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write robust tests, ensuring code correctness and reliability by following the TDD principle of writing tests before minimal code, leveraging core principles such as watching tests fail to validate their effectiveness, and combining this with libraries and protocols for comprehensive coverage.","zh":"使代理能够编写强大的测试，通过遵循TDD原则（在编写最少代码之前编写测试），确保代码的正确性和可靠性，并通过监视测试失败来验证其有效性，然后结合库和协议进行全面覆盖。","ja":"エージェントが強力なテストを記述できるようにし、TDDの原則（最小限のコードを記述する前にテストを記述する）に従ってコードの正しさと信頼性を確保し、テストの失敗を監視してその有効性を検証し、さらにライブラリやプロトコルと組み合わせて包括的なカバーを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 강력한 테스트를 작성할 수 있도록 해줍니다. TDD 원칙을 따르기 때문에(최소한의 코드를 작성하기 전에 테스트를 작성함) 코드의 올바름과 신뢰성을 보장하며, 테스트 실패를 감시하여 그 유효성을 검증하고, 추가로 라이브러리와 프로토콜을 결합하여 포괄적인 커버리지를 달성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas robustas, garantizando la corrección y la fiabilidad del código al seguir el principio de TDD de escribir pruebas antes de un código mínimo, aprovechando principios básicos como ver fallar las pruebas para validar su eficacia, y combinándolos con bibliotecas y protocolos para una cobertura integral.","fr":"Habilite les agents à écrire des tests robustes, en garantissant la correction et la fiabilité du code en suivant le principe du TDD d''écrire des tests avant un code minimal, en exploitant les principes fondamentaux tels que regarder les tests échouer pour valider leur efficacité, et en les combinant avec des bibliothèques et des protocoles pour une couverture complète.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, robuste Tests zu schreiben, um die Richtigkeit und Zuverlässigkeit des Codes zu gewährleisten, indem sie dem TDD-Prinzip folgen, Tests vor einem minimalen Code zu schreiben, Kernprinzipien wie das Beobachten von Testfehlern zur Überprüfung ihrer Wirksamkeit nutzen und diese mit Bibliotheken und Protokollen für eine umfassende Abdeckung kombinieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes robustos, garantindo a correção e confiabilidade do código, seguindo o princípio TDD de escrever testes antes do código mínimo, aproveitando princípios fundamentais, como assistir testes falharem para validar sua eficácia, e combinando isso com bibliotecas e protocolos para cobertura abrangente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать прочные тесты, гарантируя правильность и надежность кода, следуя принципу TDD о написании тестов до минимального кода, используя основополагающие принципы, такие как просмотр неудачных тестов для проверки их эффективности, и сочетая это с библиотеками и протоколами для всестороннего покрытия.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من كتابة اختبارات قوية، مما يضمن صحة الشفرة وموثوقيتها اتباعًا لمبدأ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) لكتابته اختبارات قبل كتابة الشفرة الدنيا، واستخدام المبادئ الأساسية مثل مشاهدة الاختبارات الفاشلة للتأكد من فعاليتها، ودمج ذلك مع المكتبات والبروتوكولات لتغطية شاملة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating unit testing for new features","Debugging existing codebases with TDD","Refactoring legacy code with confidence using TDD principles"],"zh":["为新功能自动化单元测试","使用TDD调试现有代码库","使用TDD原则自信地重构遗留代码"],"ja":["新機能のユニットテストを自動化する","TDDを使用して既存のコードベースをデバッグする","TDDの原則を使用してレガシーコードを自信を持ってリファクタリングする"],"ko":["새 기능을 위한 단위 테스트 자동화","기존 코드베이스를 TDD로 디버깅하기","TDD 원칙을 사용하여 레거시 코드를 자신감 있게 리팩토링하기"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas unitarias para nuevas características","Depuración de código existente con TDD","Reestructuración de código heredado con confianza utilizando principios de TDD"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests unitaires pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités","Débogage des bases de code existantes avec le TDD","Réorganisation du code hérité avec confiance en utilisant les principes du TDD"],"de":["Automatisierung von Einheitstests für neue Funktionen","Fehlerbehebung in bestehendem Code mit TDD","Umstrukturierung von Legacy-Code mit Vertrauen unter Verwendung von TDD-Prinzipien"],"pt":["Automatizar testes unitários para recursos novos","Depurar código existente com TDD","Reestruturar código legado com confiança usando princípios TDD"],"ru":["Автоматизация модульного тестирования для новых функций","Отладка существующего кода с помощью TDD","Перестройка устаревшего кода с уверенностью, используя принципы TDD"],"ar":["أتمتة الاختبارات الوحدوية للسمات الجديدة","تصحيح الأخطاء في قواعد الشفرة الحالية باستخدام التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)","إعادة هيكلة الشفرة التقليدية بثقة باستخدام مبادئ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to TDD principles","Exceptions for throwaway prototypes, generated code, and configuration files need human oversight"],"zh":["需要遵守TDD原则","抛弃式原型、生成代码和配置文件的异常需要人工监督"],"ja":["TDDの原則に従う必要がある","捨て原型、生成コード、設定ファイルの例外は人間の監督が必要"],"ko":["TDD 원칙을 준수해야 함","파기 가능한 프로토 타입, 생성된 코드 및 구성 파일의 예외는 인간의 감독이 필요"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a los principios de TDD","Excepciones para prototipos desechables, código generado y archivos de configuración necesitan supervisión humana"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion aux principes du TDD","Exceptions pour les prototypes jetables, le code généré et les fichiers de configuration nécessitant une surveillance humaine"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung der TDD-Prinzipien","Ausnahmen für verworfene Prototypen, generierten Code und Konfigurationsdateien benötigen menschliche Aufsicht"],"pt":["Exige aderência aos princípios TDD","Exceções para protótipos descartáveis, código gerado e arquivos de configuração precisam de supervisão humana"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения принципов TDD","Исключения для одноразовых прототипов, сгенерированного кода и файлов конфигурации требуют человеческого надзора"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع مبادئ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)","استثناءات للأنموذج الأولي الذي يمكن التخلص منه والشفرة المولدة وملفات التهيئة التي تحتاج إلى إشراف بشري"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
