"ja":"バックエンドアーキテクチャパターンは、メンテナンス性、テスト性、拡張性の高いシステムを設計して構築するための重要な概念です。Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture、Domain-Driven Designなどのパターンを学習しましょう","ko":"백엔드 아키텍처 패턴은 유지 보수 가능하고 테스트 가능하며 확장 가능한 시스템을 설계하고 구축하는 데 중요한 개념입니다. Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, Domain-Driven Design 등의 패턴을 학습하세요","es":"Aprende patrones de arquitectura de backend como Clean Architecture y Domain-Driven Design","fr":"Découvrez les modèles d''architecture de backend tels que Clean Architecture et Domain-Driven Design","de":"Lernen Sie Backend-Architekturmuster wie Clean Architecture und Domain-Driven Design","pt":"Domine padrões de arquitetura de backend para construir sistemas manuteníveis e escaláveis.","ru":"Освойте шаблоны архитектуры backend для создания поддерживаемых и масштабируемых систем.","ar":"استخدم أنماط الهندسة المعمارية الباك إند لإنشاء أنظمة قابلة للصيانة والتوسيع.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","可维护性","可测试性","可扩展性"],"ja":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","メンテナンス性","テスト性","拡張性"],"ko":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","유지 보수 가능","테스트 가능","확장 가능"],"es":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","Diseño de sistemas mantenibles","Refactorización de aplicaciones monolíticas","Establecimiento de estándares de arquitectura"],"fr":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","Conception de systèmes maintenables","Refactorisation d''applications monolithiques","Établissement de normes d''architecture"],"de":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","Entwurf von wartbaren Systemen","Refaktorisierung von monolithischen Anwendungen","Festlegung von Architekturstandards"],"pt":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","Sistemas escaláveis","Sistemas manuteníveis","Arquitetura de backend"],"ru":["Clean Архитектура","Hexagonal Архитектура","Domain-Driven Design","Масштабируемые системы","Поддерживаемые системы","Архитектура backend"],"ar":["هندسة معمارية نضيفة","هندسة معمارية سداسية","تصميم مدفوع بالمجال","أنظمة قابلة للتوسيع","أنظمة قابلة للصيانة","هندسة الباك إند"]},"keywords":{"zh":["后端架构模式","软件架构","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","可维护性","可测试性","可扩展性"],"ja":["バックエンドアーキテクチャパターン","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","メンテナンス性","テスト性","拡張性"],"ko":["백엔드 아키텍처 패턴","소프트웨어 아키텍처","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","유지 보수 가능","테스트 가능","확장 가능"],"es":["patrones de arquitectura de backend","clean architecture","domain-driven design","diseño de sistemas","refactorización de aplicaciones","estándares de arquitectura","arquitectura de software","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["modèles d''architecture de backend","clean architecture","domain-driven design","conception de systèmes","refactorisation d''applications","normes d''architecture","architecture de logiciel","développement de logiciel"],"de":["backend-architekturmuster","clean architecture","domain-driven design","entwurf von systemen","refaktorisierung von anwendungen","architekturstandards","software-architektur","software-entwicklung"],"pt":["padrões de arquitetura","arquitetura de backend","clean architecture","hexagonal architecture","domain-driven design","sistemas escaláveis","sistemas manuteníveis","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["шаблоны архитектуры","архитектура backend","clean архитектура","hexagonal архитектура","domain-driven design","масштабируемые системы","поддерживаемые системы","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["أنماط هندسية معمارية","هندسة الباك إند","هندسة معمارية نضيفة","هندسة معمارية سداسية","تصميم مدفوع بالمجال","أنظمة قابلة للتوسيع","أنظمة قابلة للصيانة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"ml_challenges","repoPath":"ollieb89/ml_challenges","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.513Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"architecture-patterns","description":"Implement proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design. Use when architecting complex backend systems or refactoring existing applications for better maintainability.","bodyPreview":"# Architecture Patterns\n\nMaster proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design to build maintainable, testable, and scalable systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new backend systems from scratch\n- Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability\n- Establishing architecture standards for your team\n- Migrating from tightly coupled to loosely coupled architectures\n- Implementing domain-driven design princ","body":"# Architecture Patterns\n\nMaster proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design to build maintainable, testable, and scalable systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new backend systems from scratch\n- Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability\n- Establishing architecture standards for your team\n- Migrating from tightly coupled to loosely coupled architectures\n- Implementing domain-driven design principles\n- Creating testable and mockable codebases\n- Planning microservices decomposition\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Clean Architecture (Uncle Bob)\n\n**Layers (dependency flows inward):**\n- **Entities**: Core business models\n- **Use Cases**: Application business rules\n- **Interface Adapters**: Controllers, presenters, gateways\n- **Frameworks & Drivers**: UI, database, external services\n\n**Key Principles:**\n- Dependencies point inward\n- Inner layers know nothing about outer layers\n- Business logic independent of frameworks\n- Testable without UI, database, or external services\n\n### 2. Hexagonal Architecture (Ports and Adapters)\n\n**Components:**\n- **Domain Core**: Business logic\n- **Ports**: Interfaces defining interactions\n- **Adapters**: Implementations of ports (database, REST, message queue)\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Swap implementations easily (mock for testing)\n- Technology-agnostic core\n- Clear separation of concerns\n\n### 3. Domain-Driven Design (DDD)\n\n**Strategic Patterns:**\n- **Bounded Contexts**: Separate models for different domains\n- **Context Mapping**: How contexts relate\n- **Ubiquitous Language**: Shared terminology\n\n**Tactical Patterns:**\n- **Entities**: Objects with identity\n- **Value Objects**: Immutable objects defined by attributes\n- **Aggregates**: Consistency boundaries\n- **Repositories**: Data access abstraction\n- **Domain Events**: Things that happened\n\n## Clean Architecture Pattern\n\n### Directory Structure\n```\napp/\n├── domain/           # Entities & business rules\n│   ├── entities/\n│   │   ├── user.py\n│   │   └── order.py\n│   ├── value_objects/\n│   │   ├── email.py\n│   │   └── money.py\n│   └── interfaces/   # Abstract interfaces\n│       ├── user_repository.py\n│       └── payment_gateway.py\n├── use_cases/        # Application business rules\n│   ├── create_user.py\n│   ├── process_order.py\n│   └── send_notification.py\n├── adapters/         # Interface implementations\n│   ├── repositories/\n│   │   ├── postgres_user_repository.py\n│   │   └── redis_cache_repository.py\n│   ├── controllers/\n│   │   └── user_controller.py\n│   └── gateways/\n│       ├── stripe_payment_gateway.py\n│       └── sendgrid_email_gateway.py\n└── infrastructure/   # Framework & external concerns\n    ├── database.py\n    ├── config.py\n    └── logging.py\n```\n\n### Implementation Example\n\n```python\n# domain/entities/user.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass\nclass User:\n    \"\"\"Core user entity - no framework dependencies.\"\"\"\n    id: str\n    email: str\n    name: str\n    created_at: datetime\n    is_active: bool = True\n\n    def deactivate(self):\n        \"\"\"Business rule: deactivating user.\"\"\"\n        self.is_active = False\n\n    def can_place_order(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Business rule: active users can order.\"\"\"\n        return self.is_active\n\n# domain/interfaces/user_repository.py\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\n\nclass IUserRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Port: defines contract, no implementation.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def find_by_id(self, user_id: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def find_by_email(self, email: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def save(self, user: User) -> User:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def delete(self, user_id: str) -> bool:\n        pass\n\n# use_cases/create_user.py\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\nfrom domain.interfaces.user_repository import IUserRepository\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport uuid\n\n@dataclass\nclass CreateUserRequest:\n    email: str\n    name: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass CreateUserResponse:\n    user: User\n    success: bool\n    error: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass CreateUserUseCase:\n    \"\"\"Use case: orchestrates business logic.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, user_repository: IUserRepository):\n        self.user_repository = user_repository\n\n    async def execute(self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> CreateUserResponse:\n        # Business validation\n        existing = await self.user_repository.find_by_email(request.email)\n        if existing:\n            return CreateUserResponse(\n                user=None,\n                success=False,\n                error=\"Email already exists\"\n            )\n\n        # Create entity\n        user = User(\n            id=str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            email=request.email,\n            name=request.name,\n            created_at=datetime.now(),\n            is_active=True\n        )\n\n        # Persist\n        saved_user = await self.user_repository.save(user)\n\n        return CreateUserResponse(\n            user=saved_user,\n            success=True\n        )\n\n# adapters/repositories/postgres_user_repository.py\nfrom domain.interfaces.user_repository import IUserRepository\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\nfrom typing import Optional\nimport asyncpg\n\nclass PostgresUserRepository(IUserRepository):\n    \"\"\"Adapter: PostgreSQL implementation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, pool: asyncpg.Pool):\n        self.pool = pool\n\n    async def find_by_id(self, user_id: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\", user_id\n            )\n            return self._to_entity(row) if row else None\n\n    async def find_by_email(self, email: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1\", email\n            )\n            return self._to_entity(row) if row else None\n\n    async def save(self, user: User) -> User:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            await conn.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at, is_active)\n                VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n                ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE\n                SET email = $2, name = $3, is_active = $5\n                \"\"\",\n                user.id, user.email, user.name, user.created_at, user.is_active\n            )\n            return user\n\n    async def delete(self, user_id: str) -> bool:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            result = await conn.execute(\n                \"DELETE FROM users WHERE id = $1\", user_id\n            )\n            return result == \"DELETE 1\"\n\n    def _to_entity(self, row) -> User:\n        \"\"\"Map database row to entity.\"\"\"\n        return User(\n            id=row[\"id\"],\n            email=row[\"email\"],\n            name=row[\"name\"],\n            created_at=row[\"created_at\"],\n            is_active=row[\"is_active\"]\n        )\n\n# adapters/controllers/user_controller.py\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException\nfrom use_cases.create_user import CreateUserUseCase, CreateUserRequest\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\nclass CreateUserDTO(BaseModel):\n    email: str\n    name: str\n\n@router.post(\"/users\")\nasync def create_user(\n    dto: CreateUserDTO,\n    use_case: CreateUserUseCase = Depends(get_create_user_use_case)\n):\n    \"\"\"Controller: handles HTTP concerns only.\"\"\"\n    request = CreateUserRequest(email=dto.email, name=dto.name)\n    response = await use_case.execute(request)\n\n    if not response.success:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=response.error)\n\n    return {\"user\": response.user}\n```\n\n## Hexagonal Architecture Pattern\n\n```python\n# Core domain (hexagon center)\nclass OrderService:\n    \"\"\"Domain service - no infrastructure dependencies.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        order_repository: OrderRepositoryPort,\n        payment_gateway: PaymentGatewayPort,\n        notification_service: NotificationPort\n    ):\n        self.orders = order_repository\n        self.payments = payment_gateway\n        self.notifications = notification_service\n\n    async def place_order(self, order: Order) -> OrderResult:\n        # Business logic\n        if not order.is_valid():\n            return OrderResult(success=False, error=\"Invalid order\")\n\n        # Use ports (interfaces)\n        payment = await self.payments.charge(\n            amount=order.total,\n            customer=order.customer_id\n        )\n\n        if not payment.success:\n            return OrderResult(success=False, error=\"Payment failed\")\n\n        order.mark_as_paid()\n        saved_order = await self.orders.save(order)\n\n        await self.notifications.send(\n            to=order.customer_email,\n            subject=\"Order confirmed\",\n            body=f\"Order {order.id} confirmed\"\n        )\n\n        return OrderResult(success=True, order=saved_order)\n\n# Ports (interfaces)\nclass OrderRepositoryPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def save(self, order: Order) -> Order:\n        pass\n\nclass PaymentGatewayPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        pass\n\nclass NotificationPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def send(self, to: str, subject: str, body: str):\n        pass\n\n# Adapters (implementations)\nclass StripePaymentAdapter(PaymentGatewayPort):\n    \"\"\"Primary adapter: connects to Stripe API.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, api_key: str):\n        self.stripe = stripe\n        self.stripe.api_key = api_key\n\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        try:\n            charge = self.stripe.Charge.create(\n                amount=amount.cents,\n                currency=amount.currency,\n                customer=customer\n            )\n            return PaymentResult(success=True, transaction_id=charge.id)\n        except stripe.error.CardError as e:\n            return PaymentResult(success=False, error=str(e))\n\nclass MockPaymentAdapter(PaymentGatewayPort):\n    \"\"\"Test adapter: no external dependencies.\"\"\"\n\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        return PaymentResult(success=True, transaction_id=\"mock-123\")\n```\n\n## Domain-Driven Design Pattern\n\n```python\n# Value Objects (immutable)\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Email:\n    \"\"\"Value object: validated email.\"\"\"\n    value: str\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        if \"@\" not in self.value:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid email\")\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Money:\n    \"\"\"Value object: amount with currency.\"\"\"\n    amount: int  # cents\n    currency: str\n\n    def add(self, other: \"Money\") -> \"Money\":\n        if self.currency != other.currency:\n            raise ValueError(\"Currency mismatch\")\n        return Money(self.amount + other.amount, self.currency)\n\n# Entities (with identity)\nclass Order:\n    \"\"\"Entity: has identity, mutable state.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, id: str, customer: Customer):\n        self.id = id\n        self.customer = customer\n        self.items: List[OrderItem] = []\n        self.status = OrderStatus.PENDING\n        self._events: List[DomainEvent] = []\n\n    def add_item(self, product: Product, quantity: int):\n        \"\"\"Business logic in entity.\"\"\"\n        item = OrderItem(product, quantity)\n        self.items.append(item)\n        self._events.append(ItemAddedEvent(self.id, item))\n\n    def total(self) -> Money:\n        \"\"\"Calculated property.\"\"\"\n        return sum(item.subtotal() for item in self.items)\n\n    def submit(self):\n        \"\"\"State transition with business rules.\"\"\"\n        if not self.items:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot submit empty order\")\n        if self.status != OrderStatus.PENDING:\n            raise ValueError(\"Order already submitted\")\n\n        self.status = OrderStatus.SUBMITTED\n        self._events.append(OrderSubmittedEvent(self.id))\n\n# Aggregates (consistency boundary)\nclass Customer:\n    \"\"\"Aggregate root: controls access to entities.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, id: str, email: Email):\n        self.id = id\n        self.email = email\n        self._addresses: List[Address] = []\n        self._orders: List[str] = []  # Order IDs, not full objects\n\n    def add_address(self, address: Address):\n        \"\"\"Aggregate enforces invariants.\"\"\"\n        if len(self._addresses) >= 5:\n            raise ValueError(\"Maximum 5 addresses allowed\")\n        self._addresses.append(address)\n\n    @property\n    def primary_address(self) -> Optional[Address]:\n        return next((a for a in self._addresses if a.is_primary), None)\n\n# Domain Events\n@dataclass\nclass OrderSubmittedEvent:\n    order_id: str\n    occurred_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.now)\n\n# Repository (aggregate persistence)\nclass OrderRepository:\n    \"\"\"Repository: persist/retrieve aggregates.\"\"\"\n\n    async def find_by_id(self, order_id: str) -> Optional[Order]:\n        \"\"\"Reconstitute aggregate from storage.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    async def save(self, order: Order):\n        \"\"\"Persist aggregate and publish events.\"\"\"\n        await self._persist(order)\n        await self._publish_events(order._events)\n        order._events.clear()\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/clean-architecture-guide.md**: Detailed layer breakdown\n- **references/hexagonal-architecture-guide.md**: Ports and adapters patterns\n- **references/ddd-tactical-patterns.md**: Entities, value objects, aggregates\n- **assets/clean-architecture-template/**: Complete project structure\n- **assets/ddd-examples/**: Domain modeling examples\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Dependency Rule**: Dependencies always point inward\n2. **Interface Segregation**: Small, focused interfaces\n3. **Business Logic in Domain**: Keep frameworks out of core\n4. **Test Independence**: Core testable without infrastructure\n5. **Bounded Contexts**: Clear domain boundaries\n6. **Ubiquitous Language**: Consistent terminology\n7. **Thin Controllers**: Delegate to use cases\n8. **Rich Domain Models**: Behavior with data\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Anemic Domain**: Entities with only data, no behavior\n- **Framework Coupling**: Business logic depends on frameworks\n- **Fat Controllers**: Business logic in controllers\n- **Repository Leakage**: Exposing ORM objects\n- **Missing Abstractions**: Concrete dependencies in core\n- **Over-Engineering**: Clean architecture for simple CRUD\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:52:11.511Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Software Development Agents needing expertise in Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design for building maintainable systems.","zh":"非常适合需要在清洁架构、六边形架构和领域驱动设计方面拥有专业知识的软件开发代理，以构建可维护的系统。","ja":"クリーンアーキテクチャ、ヘキサゴナルアーキテクチャ、ドメイン駆動設計の専門知識が必要なソフトウェア開発エージェントにとって最適で、メンテナンス可能なシステムを構築することができます。","ko":"클린 아키텍처, 육각 아키텍처, 도메인 주도 설계에 대한 전문 지식이 필요한 소프트웨어 개발 에이전트에게 적합하여 유지 보수 가능한 시스템을 구축할 수 있습니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de Software que necesitan experiencia en Arquitectura Limpia, Arquitectura Hexagonal y Diseño Dirigido por Dominio para construir sistemas mantenibles.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement de Logiciels ayant besoin d''expertise en Architecture Propre, Architecture Hexagonale et Conception Orientée Objet pour la construction de systèmes maintenables.","de":"Perfekt für Software-Entwicklungsagenten, die Expertenwissen in sauberer Architektur, hexagonaler Architektur und domaingetriebener Gestaltung für den Bau von wartbaren Systemen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Software que precisam de especialização em Arquitetura Limpa, Arquitetura Hexagonal e Design Dirigido por Domínio para construir sistemas mantidos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки программного обеспечения, которым необходимы знания в области Чистой Архитектуры, Шестиугольной Архитектуры и Дизайна, Ориентированного на Домен, для создания поддерживаемых систем.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى خبرة في الهندسة المعمارية النظيفة والهندسة السداسية والتصميم الموجه بال领域 لإنشاء أنظمة قابلة للصيانة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design scalable systems using proven backend architecture patterns, including implementing domain-driven design principles and establishing architecture standards for teams, all while ensuring maintainability and testability through loosely coupled architectures.","zh":"赋予代理设计可扩展系统的能力，使用已验证的后端架构模式，包括实施领域驱动设计原则和为团队建立架构标准，同时通过松散耦合的架构确保可维护性和可测试性。","ja":"エージェントにスケーラブルなシステムを設計する能力を与え、検証済みのバックエンドアーキテクチャパターンを使用し、ドメイン駆動設計の原則を実施し、チームのためのアーキテクチャ標準を確立し、同時に疎結合アーキテクチャを通じてメンテナンス性とテスト性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 검증된 백엔드 아키텍처 패턴을 사용하여 확장 가능한 시스템을 설계할 수 있도록 하고, 도메인 주도 설계 원칙을 구현하며, 팀을 위한 아키텍처 표준을 설정하며,同時に 느슨하게 결합된 아키텍처를 통해 유지 보수 가능성과 테스트 가능성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar sistemas escalables utilizando patrones de arquitectura de backend probados, incluyendo la implementación de principios de diseño dirigido por dominio y el establecimiento de estándares de arquitectura para equipos, todo ello garantizando la mantenibilidad y la probabilidad a través de arquitecturas sueltas.","fr":"Habilite les agents à concevoir des systèmes évolutifs en utilisant des modèles d''architecture backend éprouvés, y compris la mise en œuvre de principes de conception orientée objet et l''établissement de normes d''architecture pour les équipes, le tout en garantissant la maintenabilité et la testabilité grâce à des architectures déconnectées.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, skalierbare Systeme mit bewährten Backend-Architekturmuster zu entwerfen, einschließlich der Implementierung von domaingetriebenen Designprinzipien und der Festlegung von Architekturstandards für Teams, wodurch die Wartbarkeit und Testbarkeit durch lose gekoppelte Architekturen sichergestellt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar sistemas escaláveis usando padrões de arquitetura de backend comprovados, incluindo a implementação de princípios de design orientados a domínio e estabelecimento de padrões de arquitetura para equipes, garantindo ao mesmo tempo a manutenção e a testabilidade por meio de arquiteturas acopladas soltas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать масштабируемые системы с помощью проверенных шаблонов архитектуры бэкенда, включая реализацию принципов дизайна, ориентированного на домен, и установление архитектурных стандартов для команд, обеспечивая при этом поддерживаемость и тестируемость за счет слабо связанных архитектур.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تصميم أنظمة قابلة للتوسعة باستخدام أنماط هندسية خلفية مثبتة، بما في ذلك تنفيذ مبادئ تصميم موجهة بال领域 وتحديد معايير هندسية للفرق، مع ضمان الصيانة والاختبار من خلال هندسات ربط غير متصلة."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing new backend systems from scratch with Clean Architecture","Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability using Hexagonal Architecture","Establishing architecture standards for development teams based on Domain-Driven Design"],"zh":["使用清洁架构从头开始设计新的后端系统","使用六边形架构重构单体应用程序以提高可维护性","根据领域驱动设计为开发团队建立架构标准"],"ja":["クリーンアーキテクチャを使用して新しいバックエンドシステムをスクラッチから設計する","ヘキサゴナルアーキテクチャを使用してモノリシックアプリケーションをリファクタリングしてメンテナンス性を向上させる","ドメイン駆動設計に基づいて開発チームのためのアーキテクチャ標準を確立する"],"ko":["클린 아키텍처를 사용하여 새로운 백엔드 시스템을 처음부터 설계한다","육각 아키텍처를 사용하여 모놀리식 애플리케이션을 리팩토링하여 유지 보수성을 개선한다","도메인 주도 설계를 기반으로 개발 팀을 위한 아키텍처 표준을 설정한다"],"es":["Diseñar nuevos sistemas backend desde cero con Arquitectura Limpia","Reestructurar aplicaciones monolíticas para una mejor mantenibilidad utilizando Arquitectura Hexagonal","Establecer estándares de arquitectura para equipos de desarrollo basados en Diseño Dirigido por Dominio"],"fr":["Concevoir de nouveaux systèmes backend à partir de zéro avec une Architecture Propre","Réaménager des applications monolithiques pour une meilleure maintenabilité en utilisant une Architecture Hexagonale","Établir des normes d''architecture pour les équipes de développement basées sur la Conception Orientée Objet"],"de":["Neue Backend-Systeme von Grund auf mit sauberer Architektur entwerfen","Monolithische Anwendungen für eine bessere Wartbarkeit mit hexagonaler Architektur neu strukturieren","Architekturstandards für Entwicklerteams auf Basis von domaingetriebener Gestaltung festlegen"],"pt":["Projetar novos sistemas de backend do zero com Arquitetura Limpa","Refatorar aplicações monolíticas para melhor manutenção usando Arquitetura Hexagonal","Estabelecer padrões de arquitetura para equipes de desenvolvimento com base no Design Dirigido por Domínio"],"ru":["Проектировать новые системы бэкенда с нуля с помощью Чистой Архитектуры","Рефакторить монолитные приложения для лучшей поддерживаемости с помощью Шестиугольной Архитектуры","Устанавливать архитектурные стандарты для команд разработки на основе Дизайна, Ориентированного на Домен"],"ar":["تصميم أنظمة خلفية جديدة من الصفر باستخدام الهندسة المعمارية النظيفة","إعادة هيكلة التطبيقات أحادية القطعة لتحسين الصيانة باستخدام الهندسة السداسية","تحديد معايير هندسية للفرق التطويرية على أساس التصميم الموجه بال领域"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of software development principles","Limited to backend system architecture"],"zh":["需要了解软件开发原则","仅限于后端系统架构"],"ja":["ソフトウェア開発の原則を理解する必要がある","バックエンドシステムアーキテクチャに限定される"],"ko":["소프트웨어 개발 원칙을 이해해야 함","백엔드 시스템 아키텍처에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de desarrollo de software","Limitado a la arquitectura de sistemas backend"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de développement de logiciels","Limité à l''architecture des systèmes backend"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für Software-Entwicklungsprinzipien","Begrenzt auf die Architektur von Backend-Systemen"],"pt":["Requer entendimento de princípios de desenvolvimento de software","Limitado à arquitetura de sistemas de backend"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов разработки программного обеспечения","Ограничен архитектурой систем бэкенда"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تطوير البرمجيات","محدود في الهندسة المعمارية لأنظمة الخلفية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
