audiência e impulsionar metas de negócios. Aprenda a criar conteúdo engajador com nossa expertise","ru":"Социальное содержание является основным для построения аудитории и стимулирования бизнес-целей. Узнайте, как создавать привлекательный контент с нашей экспер...","ar":"المحتوى الاجتماعي ضروري لبناء الجمهور وتنفيذ أهداف الأعمال. تعلم كيفية إنشاء محتوى مميز مع خبرتنا","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Estrategias de contenido personalizadas","Análisis de audiencia y comportamiento","Creación de contenido atractivo y relevante","Optimización para búsqueda y recomendaciones","Medición y seguimiento del rendimiento"],"fr":["Stratégies de contenu personnalisées","Analyse du public et du comportement","Création de contenu attrayant et pertinent","Optimisation pour la recherche et les recommandations","Mesure et suivi des performances"],"de":["Maßgeschneiderte Inhaltsstrategien","Analyse der Zielgruppe und des Verhaltens","Erstellung ansprechender und relevanter Inhalte","Optimierung für Suche und Empfehlungen","Messung und Überwachung der Leistung"],"pt":["Criação de conteúdo engajador","Desenvolvimento de estratégia de mídia social","Análise de metas de negócios","Otimização de conteúdo para SEO","Integração com plataformas de mídia social"],"ru":["Создание привлекательного контента","Разработка стратегии социальных медиа","Анализ бизнес-целей","Оптимизация контента для SEO","Интеграция с платформами социальных медиа"],"ar":["إنشاء محتوى مميز","تنمية استراتيجية وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية","تحليل أهداف الأعمال","تحسين المحتوى لتحسين محركات البحث","التكامل مع منصات وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية"]},"keywords":{"es":["contenido social","estrategias de marketing","redes sociales","análisis de audiencia","creación de contenido","optimización para búsqueda"],"fr":["contenu social","stratégies de marketing","réseaux sociaux","analyse du public","création de contenu","optimisation pour la recherche"],"de":["soziale Inhalte","Marketingstrategien","soziale Netzwerke","Zielgruppenanalyse","InhaltsErstellung","Suchmaschinenoptimierung"],"pt":["conteúdo social","mídia social","estratégia de conteúdo","desenvolvimento de conteúdo","SEO para mídia social","análise de metas de negócios"],"ru":["социальное содержание","социальные медиа","стратегия контента","разработка контента","SEO для социальных медиа","анализ бизнес-целей"],"ar":["المحتوى الاجتماعي","وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية","استراتيجية المحتوى","تنمية المحتوى","تحسين محركات البحث لوسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية","تحليل أهداف الأعمال"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"social-content","description":"When the user wants help creating, scheduling, or optimizing social media content for LinkedIn, Twitter/X, Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, or other platforms. Also use when the user mentions LinkedIn post, Twitter thread, social media, content calendar, social scheduling, engagement, or viral content. This skill covers content creation, repurposing, and platform-specific strategies.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Social Content\n\nYou are an expert social media strategist. Your goal is to help create engaging content that builds audience, drives engagement, and supports business goals.\n\n## Before Creating Content\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Goals\n- What''s the pr","body":"# Social Content\n\nYou are an expert social media strategist. Your goal is to help create engaging content that builds audience, drives engagement, and supports business goals.\n\n## Before Creating Content\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Goals\n- What''s the primary objective? (Brand awareness, leads, traffic, community)\n- What action do you want people to take?\n- Are you building personal brand, company brand, or both?\n\n### 2. Audience\n- Who are you trying to reach?\n- What platforms are they most active on?\n- What content do they engage with?\n\n### 3. Brand Voice\n- What''s your tone? (Professional, casual, witty, authoritative)\n- Any topics to avoid?\n- Any specific terminology or style guidelines?\n\n### 4. Resources\n- How much time can you dedicate to social?\n- Do you have existing content to repurpose?\n- Can you create video content?\n\n---\n\n## Platform Quick Reference\n\n| Platform | Best For | Frequency | Key Format |\n|----------|----------|-----------|------------|\n| LinkedIn | B2B, thought leadership | 3-5x/week | Carousels, stories |\n| Twitter/X | Tech, real-time, community | 3-10x/day | Threads, hot takes |\n| Instagram | Visual brands, lifestyle | 1-2 posts + Stories daily | Reels, carousels |\n| TikTok | Brand awareness, younger audiences | 1-4x/day | Short-form video |\n| Facebook | Communities, local businesses | 1-2x/day | Groups, native video |\n\n**For detailed platform strategies**: See [references/platforms.md](references/platforms.md)\n\n---\n\n## Content Pillars Framework\n\nBuild your content around 3-5 pillars that align with your expertise and audience interests.\n\n### Example for a SaaS Founder\n\n| Pillar | % of Content | Topics |\n|--------|--------------|--------|\n| Industry insights | 30% | Trends, data, predictions |\n| Behind-the-scenes | 25% | Building the company, lessons learned |\n| Educational | 25% | How-tos, frameworks, tips |\n| Personal | 15% | Stories, values, hot takes |\n| Promotional | 5% | Product updates, offers |\n\n### Pillar Development Questions\n\nFor each pillar, ask:\n1. What unique perspective do you have?\n2. What questions does your audience ask?\n3. What content has performed well before?\n4. What can you create consistently?\n5. What aligns with business goals?\n\n---\n\n## Hook Formulas\n\nThe first line determines whether anyone reads the rest.\n\n### Curiosity Hooks\n- \"I was wrong about [common belief].\"\n- \"The real reason [outcome] happens isn''t what you think.\"\n- \"[Impressive result] — and it only took [surprisingly short time].\"\n\n### Story Hooks\n- \"Last week, [unexpected thing] happened.\"\n- \"I almost [big mistake/failure].\"\n- \"3 years ago, I [past state]. Today, [current state].\"\n\n### Value Hooks\n- \"How to [desirable outcome] (without [common pain]):\"\n- \"[Number] [things] that [outcome]:\"\n- \"Stop [common mistake]. Do this instead:\"\n\n### Contrarian Hooks\n- \"Unpopular opinion: [bold statement]\"\n- \"[Common advice] is wrong. Here''s why:\"\n- \"I stopped [common practice] and [positive result].\"\n\n**For post templates and more hooks**: See [references/post-templates.md](references/post-templates.md)\n\n---\n\n## Content Repurposing System\n\nTurn one piece of content into many:\n\n### Blog Post → Social Content\n\n| Platform | Format |\n|----------|--------|\n| LinkedIn | Key insight + link in comments |\n| LinkedIn | Carousel of main points |\n| Twitter/X | Thread of key takeaways |\n| Instagram | Carousel with visuals |\n| Instagram | Reel summarizing the post |\n\n### Repurposing Workflow\n\n1. **Create pillar content** (blog, video, podcast)\n2. **Extract key insights** (3-5 per piece)\n3. **Adapt to each platform** (format and tone)\n4. **Schedule across the week** (spread distribution)\n5. **Update and reshare** (evergreen content can repeat)\n\n---\n\n## Content Calendar Structure\n\n### Weekly Planning Template\n\n| Day | LinkedIn | Twitter/X | Instagram |\n|-----|----------|-----------|-----------|\n| Mon | Industry insight | Thread | Carousel |\n| Tue | Behind-scenes | Engagement | Story |\n| Wed | Educational | Tips tweet | Reel |\n| Thu | Story post | Thread | Educational |\n| Fri | Hot take | Engagement | Story |\n\n### Batching Strategy (2-3 hours weekly)\n\n1. Review content pillar topics\n2. Write 5 LinkedIn posts\n3. Write 3 Twitter threads + daily tweets\n4. Create Instagram carousel + Reel ideas\n5. Schedule everything\n6. Leave room for real-time engagement\n\n---\n\n## Engagement Strategy\n\n### Daily Engagement Routine (30 min)\n\n1. Respond to all comments on your posts (5 min)\n2. Comment on 5-10 posts from target accounts (15 min)\n3. Share/repost with added insight (5 min)\n4. Send 2-3 DMs to new connections (5 min)\n\n### Quality Comments\n\n- Add new insight, not just \"Great post!\"\n- Share a related experience\n- Ask a thoughtful follow-up question\n- Respectfully disagree with nuance\n\n### Building Relationships\n\n- Identify 20-50 accounts in your space\n- Consistently engage with their content\n- Share their content with credit\n- Eventually collaborate (podcasts, co-created content)\n\n---\n\n## Analytics & Optimization\n\n### Metrics That Matter\n\n**Awareness:** Impressions, Reach, Follower growth rate\n\n**Engagement:** Engagement rate, Comments (higher value than likes), Shares/reposts, Saves\n\n**Conversion:** Link clicks, Profile visits, DMs received, Leads attributed\n\n### Weekly Review\n\n- Top 3 performing posts (why did they work?)\n- Bottom 3 posts (what can you learn?)\n- Follower growth trend\n- Engagement rate trend\n- Best posting times (from data)\n\n### Optimization Actions\n\n**If engagement is low:**\n- Test new hooks\n- Post at different times\n- Try different formats\n- Increase engagement with others\n\n**If reach is declining:**\n- Avoid external links in post body\n- Increase posting frequency\n- Engage more in comments\n- Test video/visual content\n\n---\n\n## Content Ideas by Situation\n\n### When You''re Starting Out\n- Document your journey\n- Share what you''re learning\n- Curate and comment on industry content\n- Engage heavily with established accounts\n\n### When You''re Stuck\n- Repurpose old high-performing content\n- Ask your audience what they want\n- Comment on industry news\n- Share a failure or lesson learned\n\n---\n\n## Scheduling Best Practices\n\n### When to Schedule vs. Post Live\n\n**Schedule:** Core content posts, Threads, Carousels, Evergreen content\n\n**Post live:** Real-time commentary, Responses to news/trends, Engagement with others\n\n### Queue Management\n\n- Maintain 1-2 weeks of scheduled content\n- Review queue weekly for relevance\n- Leave gaps for spontaneous posts\n- Adjust timing based on performance data\n\n---\n\n## Reverse Engineering Viral Content\n\nInstead of guessing, analyze what''s working for top creators in your niche:\n\n1. **Find creators** — 10-20 accounts with high engagement\n2. **Collect data** — 500+ posts for analysis\n3. **Analyze patterns** — Hooks, formats, CTAs that work\n4. **Codify playbook** — Document repeatable patterns\n5. **Layer your voice** — Apply patterns with authenticity\n6. **Convert** — Bridge attention to business results\n\n**For the complete framework**: See [references/reverse-engineering.md](references/reverse-engineering.md)\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What platform(s) are you focusing on?\n2. What''s your current posting frequency?\n3. Do you have existing content to repurpose?\n4. What content has performed well in the past?\n5. How much time can you dedicate weekly?\n6. Are you building personal brand, company brand, or both?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **copywriting**: For longer-form content that feeds social\n- **launch-strategy**: For coordinating social with launches\n- **email-sequence**: For nurturing social audience via email\n- **marketing-psychology**: For understanding what drives engagement\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:54:03.416Z","qualityScore":25}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('tkykenmt/opensearch-feature-explorer/skill-creator', 'community', 'tkykenmt', 'opensearch-feature-explorer', 'tkykenmt/opensearch-feature-explorer', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z', '2026-02-18T12:54:35.958Z', NULL, '{"id":"tkykenmt/opensearch-feature-explorer/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"技能创建者提供创建有效技能的技术指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張するための専門知識を提供する","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장하는 데 필요한 기술 지식을 제공합니다","es":"El skill-creator es una herramienta para desarrolladores que proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas para Claude.","fr":"Le skill-creator est un outil pour développeurs qui fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces pour Claude.","de":"Der skill-creator ist ein Tool für Entwickler, das eine Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten für Claude bietet.","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendem as capacidades de Claude.","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude.","ar":"مبدع المهارات يقدم إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة التي توسع قدرات كلود.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"技能创建者 - 技术指南","ja":"スキルクリエーター - 開発者向けガイド","ko":"스킬 생성기 - 개발자용 기술 문서","es":"Creador de habilidades para desarrolladores","fr":"Créateur de compétences pour développeurs","de":"Fähigkeitscreator für Entwickler","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Guia para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Создатель Навыков: Руководство для Разработчиков","ar":"مبدع المهارات: دليل للمطورين","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"技能创建者提供创建有效技能的技术指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張するための専門知識を提供する","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장하는 데 필요한 기술 지식을 제공합니다","es":"El skill-creator es una herramienta para desarrolladores que proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas para Claude.","fr":"Le skill-creator est un outil pour développeurs qui fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces pour Claude.","de":"Der skill-creator ist ein Tool für Entwickler, das eine Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten für Claude bietet.","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendem as capacidades de Claude.","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude.","ar":"مبدع المهارات يقدم إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة التي توسع قدرات كلود.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提供创建有效技能的技术指南","帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","包括专门的工作流程和工具","支持多种开发任务","提供开发者社区支持"],"ja":["スキルの作成方法を指導する","開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張するためのサポート","専門のワークフローとツールを提供する","多種多様な開発タスクをサポート","開発者コミュニティのサポートを提供"],"ko":["스킬 생성을 위한 기술 문서 제공","개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장하는 데 필요한 기술 지식 제공","전문적인 워크플로우와 도구를 포함","다양한 개발 작업을 지원","개발자 커뮤니티 지원 제공"],"es":["Guía para crear habilidades efectivas","Permite la creación de flujos de trabajo personalizados","Amplía las capacidades de Claude","Proporciona conocimientos y herramientas especializados","Permite la transformación de Claude en un agente especializado","Facilita la creación de habilidades modulares y autocontenidas"],"fr":["Guide pour créer des compétences efficaces","Permet la création de flux de travail personnalisés","Étend les capacités de Claude","Fournit des connaissances et des outils spécialisés","Permet la transformation de Claude en un agent spécialisé","Facilite la création de compétences modulaires et autocontenues"],"de":["Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten","Ermöglicht die Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Workflows","Erweitert die Fähigkeiten von Claude","Bietet spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Tools","Ermöglicht die Transformation von Claude in einen spezialisierten Agenten","Erleichtert die Erstellung modulare und selbstenthaltener Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes","Permite a extensão das capacidades de Claude","Oferece conhecimento especializado para domínios específicos","Transforma Claude em um agente especializado","Fornece fluxos de trabalho personalizados"],"ru":["Предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков","Позволяет расширить возможности Claude","Предлагает специализированные знания для конкретных доменов","Преобразует Claude в специализированного агента","Предоставляет индивидуальные рабочие процессы"],"ar":["يقدم إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة","يمكّن توسعة قدرات كلود","يقدم معرفة متخصصة لمناطق معينة","يحول كلود إلى وكيل متخصص","يقدم سلاسل عمل مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建","技术指南","开发者工具","Claude扩展","技能开发","开发者社区"],"ja":["スキルの作成","技術ドキュメント","開発者ツール","Claudeの拡張","スキルの開発","開発者コミュニティ"],"ko":["스킬 생성","기술 문서","개발자 도구","Claude 확장","스킬 개발","개발자 커뮤니티"],"es":["skill-creator","desarrollo de habilidades","Claude","agentes especializados","flujos de trabajo personalizados","conocimientos especializados","herramientas de desarrollo","creación de habilidades","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["skill-creator","développement de compétences","Claude","agents spécialisés","flux de travail personnalisés","connaissances spécialisées","outils de développement","création de compétences","développement de logiciels"],"de":["skill-creator","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Claude","spezialisierte Agenten","benutzerdefinierte Workflows","spezialisierte Kenntnisse","Entwicklungstools","Erstellung von Fähigkeiten","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["criador de habilidades","desenvolvedores","claude","habilidades personalizadas","conhecimento especializado","fluxos de trabalho"],"ru":["создатель навыков","разработчики","claude","индивидуальные навыки","специализированные знания","рабочие процессы"],"ar":["مبدع المهارات","مطورين","كلود","مهارات مخصصة","معرفة متخصصة","سلاسل عمل"]}},"owner":"tkykenmt","repo":"opensearch-feature-explorer","repoPath":"tkykenmt/opensearch-feature-explorer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:54:35.958Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions","zh":"非常适合需要专业知识和工作流扩展的AI智能体（如Claude）","ja":"Claudeのような専門知識とワークフロー拡張を必要とするAIエージェントに最適","ko":"Claude와 같은 전문 지식과 워크플로 확장이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude que necesitan conocimientos especializados y extensiones de flujo de trabajo","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude nécessitant des connaissances spécialisées et des extensions de flux de travail","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Workflow-Erweiterungen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, требующих специализированных знаний и расширений рабочего процесса","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي مثل Claude التي تحتاج إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيع سير العمل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, providing modular and self-contained packages that extend capabilities through specialized workflows and tools, utilizing domain-specific onboarding guides","zh":"通过领域特定的入门指南，提供模块化和自包含的软件包，通过专业化工作流和工具扩展能力，使智能体转变为具备流程知识的专业化实体","ja":"専門的なオンボーディングガイドを活用し、専門的なワークフローとツールを通じて機能を拡張するモジュール式で自己完結型のパッケージを提供し、手続き型知識を備えた専門エンティティへのエージェント変革を実現","ko":"도메인별 온보딩 가이드를 활용하여 전문 워크플로와 도구를 통해 기능을 확장하는 모듈식 및 독립형 패키지를 제공함으로써 절차적 지식을 갖춘 전문 엔티티로 에이전트를 변환시키는 역할을 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en entidades especializadas equipadas con conocimientos procedimentales, proporcionando paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades a través de flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, utilizando guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en entités spécialisées équipées de connaissances procédurales, fournissant des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui étendent les capacités à travers des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, en utilisant des guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Einheiten mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, indem modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete bereitgestellt werden, die die Fähigkeiten durch spezialisierte Workflows und Tools erweitern, unter Nutzung von domänen-spezifischen Onboarding-Leitfäden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento procedural, fornecendo pacotes modulares e autocontidos que estendem as capacidades por meio de fluxos de trabalho especializados e ferramentas, utilizando guias de integração específicos de domínio","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, предоставляя модульные и самодостаточные пакеты, которые расширяют возможности за счет специализированных рабочих процессов и инструментов, используя руководства по интеграции, специфичные для домена","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التحول إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بمعرفة إجرائية، وتوفير حزم مودULAR ومتكاملة تمدد القدرات من خلال سير عمل وادوات متخصصة، باستخدام أدلة التأسيس الخاصة بالمجال"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating modular skill packages for domain-specific tasks","Developing specialized workflows for Claude","Extending agent capabilities with procedural knowledge"],"zh":["创建面向领域特定任务的模块化技能包","为Claude开发专业化工作流","通过流程知识扩展智能体能力"],"ja":["ドメイン固有タスクのためのモジュール式スキルパッケージの作成","Claudeのための専門ワークフローの開発","手続き型知識によるエージェント機能の拡張"],"ko":["도메인별 작업을 위한 모듈식 스킬 패키지 생성","Claude를 위한 전문 워크플로 개발","절차적 지식을 통한 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Crear paquetes de habilidades modulares para tareas específicas del dominio","Desarrollar flujos de trabajo especializados para Claude","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con conocimientos procedimentales"],"fr":["Créer des packages de compétences modulaires pour des tâches spécifiques du domaine","Développer des flux de travail spécialisés pour Claude","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des connaissances procédurales"],"de":["Modulare Skill-Pakete für domänen-spezifische Aufgaben erstellen","Spezialisierte Workflows für Claude entwickeln","Agenten-Fähigkeiten mit prozeduralem Wissen erweitern"],"pt":["Criar pacotes de habilidades modulares para tarefas específicas de domínio","Desenvolver fluxos de trabalho especializados para Claude","Estender as capacidades do agente com conhecimento procedural"],"ru":["Создание модульных пакетов навыков для задач, специфичных для домена","Разработка специализированных рабочих процессов для Claude","Расширение возможностей агента за счет процедурных знаний"],"ar":["إنشاء حزم مهارات مودULAR لمهام محددة بالمجال","تطوير سير عمل متخصصة لبرنامج Claude","تمديد قدرات الوكيل بمعرفة إجرائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude''s infrastructure for skill integration","Limited to Claude''s ecosystem and compatible agents"],"zh":["需要Claude的基础设施进行技能集成","仅限于Claude生态系统及兼容智能体"],"ja":["スキル統合にはClaudeのインフラストラクチャが必要","Claudeのエコシステムと互換性のあるエージェントに限定"],"ko":["스킬 통합을 위해 Claude의 인프라가 필요함","Claude의 생태계 및 호환 에이전트로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la infraestructura de Claude para la integración de habilidades","Limitado al ecosistema de Claude y a agentes compatibles"],"fr":["Nécessite l''infrastructure de Claude pour l''intégration des compétences","Limité à l''écosystème de Claude et aux agents compatibles"],"de":["Benötigt die Infrastruktur von Claude für die Integration von Fähigkeiten","Begrenzt auf das Ökosystem von Claude und kompatible Agents"],"pt":["Requer a infraestrutura do Claude para integração de habilidades","Limitado ao ecossistema do Claude e agentes compatíveis"],"ru":["Требует инфраструктуры Claude для интеграции навыков","Ограничен экосистемой Claude и совместимыми агентами"],"ar":["يتطلب بنية تحتية لبرنامج Claude من أجل دمج المهارات","محدود بنظام برامج Claude والوكلاء المتوافقين"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('captjay98/livestockai/Neon Database', 'community', 'captjay98', 'livestockai', 'captjay98/livestockai', 'Neon Database', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z', '2026-02-18T12:54:29.753Z', NULL, '{"id":"captjay98/livestockai/Neon Database","name":"Neon Database","description":{"zh":"Neon Database 是一个 serverless PostgreSQL 数据库，使用 Kysely 查询构建器实现类型安全的 SQL","ja":"Neon Database は、Kysely クエリビルダーを使用したサーバーレス PostgreSQL データベースです","ko":"Neon Database 는 Kysely 쿼리 빌더를 사용한 서버리스 PostgreSQL 데이터베이스입니다","es":"Neon Database es una solución serverless para PostgreSQL que utiliza Kysely para consultas SQL seguras. Ideal para desarrolladores que buscan una base de datos escalable","fr":"Neon Database est une solution serverless pour PostgreSQL qui utilise Kysely pour des requêtes SQL sécurisées. Idéal pour les développeurs qui recherchent une base de données scalable","de":"Neon Database ist eine serverless-Lösung für PostgreSQL, die Kysely für sichere SQL-Abfragen verwendet. Ideal für Entwickler, die eine skalierbare Datenbank suchen","pt":"O Neon Database é uma solução serverless para PostgreSQL que oferece tipo seguro SQL e escalabilidade para desenvolvedores.","ru":"Neon Database — это серверless-решение для PostgreSQL, которое предлагает типобезопасный SQL и масштабируемость для разработчиков.","ar":"Neon Database هو حل серверليس لبيستجول، يوفر SQL آمن من النوع وقابلية التوسع للمطورين.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Neon Database 技术解析","ja":"Neon Database の概要","ko":"Neon Database 기술 분석","es":"Base de Datos Neon: Solución Serverless para Desarrolladores","fr":"Base de Données Neon : Solution Serverless pour Développeurs","de":"Neon-Datenbank: Serverless-Lösung für Entwickler","pt":"Neon Database: Solução Serverless para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Neon Database: Серверless-решение для разработчиков","ar":"Neon Database: حل серверليس للمانحين","en":"Neon Database"},"description":{"zh":"Neon Database 是一个 serverless PostgreSQL 数据库，使用 Kysely 查询构建器实现类型安全的 SQL","ja":"Neon Database は、Kysely クエリビルダーを使用したサーバーレス PostgreSQL データベースです","ko":"Neon Database 는 Kysely 쿼리 빌더를 사용한 서버리스 PostgreSQL 데이터베이스입니다","es":"Neon Database es una solución serverless para PostgreSQL que utiliza Kysely para consultas SQL seguras. Ideal para desarrolladores que buscan una base de dat...","fr":"Neon Database est une solution serverless pour PostgreSQL qui utilise Kysely pour des requêtes SQL sécurisées. Idéal pour les développeurs qui recherchent un...","de":"Neon Database ist eine serverless-Lösung für PostgreSQL, die Kysely für sichere SQL-Abfragen verwendet. Ideal für Entwickler, die eine skalierbare Datenbank ...","pt":"O Neon Database é uma solução serverless para PostgreSQL que oferece tipo seguro SQL e escalabilidade para desenvolvedores.","ru":"Neon Database — это серверless-решение для PostgreSQL, которое предлагает типобезопасный SQL и масштабируемость для разработчиков.","ar":"Neon Database هو حل серверليس لبيستجول، يوفر SQL آمن من النوع وقابلية التوسع للمطورين.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Serverless PostgreSQL 数据库","Kysely 查询构建器","类型安全的 SQL","Cloudflare Workers 兼容性","app/lib/db/index.ts 连接管理"],"ja":["サーバーレス PostgreSQL データベース","Kysely クエリビルダー","型安全の SQL","Cloudflare Workers との互換性","app/lib/db/index.ts 接続管理"],"ko":["서버리스 PostgreSQL 데이터베이스","Kysely 쿼리 빌더","타입 안전 SQL","Cloudflare Workers 호환성","app/lib/db/index.ts 연결 관리"],"es":["Solución serverless para PostgreSQL","Kysely para consultas SQL seguras","Compatibilidad con Cloudflare Workers","Escalabilidad automática","Acceso a través de `app/lib/db/index.ts`"],"fr":["Solution serverless pour PostgreSQL","Kysely pour des requêtes SQL sécurisées","Compatibilité avec Cloudflare Workers","Scalabilité automatique","Accès via `app/lib/db/index.ts`"],"de":["Serverless-Lösung für PostgreSQL","Kysely für sichere SQL-Abfragen","Kompatibilität mit Cloudflare Workers","Automatische Skalierbarkeit","Zugriff über `app/lib/db/index.ts`"],"pt":["Solução serverless para PostgreSQL","Tipo seguro SQL com Kysely","Compatibilidade com Cloudflare Workers","Escalabilidade e desempenho","Acesso fácil com `getDb()`"],"ru":["Серверless-решение для PostgreSQL","Типобезопасный SQL с Kysely","Совместимость с Cloudflare Workers","Масштабируемость и производительность","Легкий доступ с `getDb()`"],"ar":["حل серверليس لبيستجول","SQL آمن من النوع مع Kysely","متوافق مع Cloudflare Workers","قابلية التوسع والأداء","دخول سهل مع `getDb()`"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Neon Database","Serverless PostgreSQL","Kysely","类型安全 SQL","Cloudflare Workers","数据库连接管理"],"ja":["Neon Database","サーバーレス PostgreSQL","Kysely","型安全の SQL","Cloudflare Workers","データベース接続管理"],"ko":["Neon Database","서버리스 PostgreSQL","Kysely","타입 안전 SQL","Cloudflare Workers","데이터베이스 연결 관리"],"es":["Neon Database","serverless","PostgreSQL","Kysely","Cloudflare Workers","desarrollo de aplicaciones","bases de datos escalables"],"fr":["Neon Database","serverless","PostgreSQL","Kysely","Cloudflare Workers","développement d''applications","bases de données scalables"],"de":["Neon Database","serverless","PostgreSQL","Kysely","Cloudflare Workers","Anwendungsentwicklung","skalierbare Datenbanken"],"pt":["Neon Database","serverless PostgreSQL","tipo seguro SQL","Kysely","Cloudflare Workers","desenvolvimento de software","escalabilidade","desempenho"],"ru":["Neon Database","серверless PostgreSQL","типобезопасный SQL","Kysely","Cloudflare Workers","разработка программного обеспечения","масштабируемость","производительность"],"ar":["Neon Database","حل серверليس لبيستجول","SQL آمن من النوع","Kysely","Cloudflare Workers","تطوير البرمجيات","قابلية التوسع","الأداء"]}},"owner":"captjay98","repo":"livestockai","repoPath":"captjay98/livestockai","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Neon Database","description":"Serverless PostgreSQL database patterns for LivestockAI using Neon and Kysely ORM","bodyPreview":"# Neon Database\n\nLivestockAI uses [Neon](https://neon.tech) as its serverless PostgreSQL database, accessed through the Kysely query builder for type-safe SQL.\n\n## Connection Pattern\n\nThe database connection is managed through `app/lib/db/index.ts` with two access patterns:\n\n### Server Functions (Cloudflare Workers)\n\n**ALWAYS use `getDb()` in server functions** - this is critical for Cloudflare Workers compatibility:\n\n```typescript\nexport const myServerFn = createServerFn({ method: ''GET'' }).hand","body":"# Neon Database\n\nLivestockAI uses [Neon](https://neon.tech) as its serverless PostgreSQL database, accessed through the Kysely query builder for type-safe SQL.\n\n## Connection Pattern\n\nThe database connection is managed through `app/lib/db/index.ts` with two access patterns:\n\n### Server Functions (Cloudflare Workers)\n\n**ALWAYS use `getDb()` in server functions** - this is critical for Cloudflare Workers compatibility:\n\n```typescript\nexport const myServerFn = createServerFn({ method: ''GET'' }).handler(\n  async () => {\n    const { getDb } = await import(''~/lib/db'')\n    const db = await getDb()\n    return db.selectFrom(''batches'').execute()\n  },\n)\n```\n\n### CLI Scripts (Node.js/Bun)\n\nFor seeders, migrations, and CLI scripts, use the direct export:\n\n```typescript\nimport { db } from ''~/lib/db''\nawait db.insertInto(''users'').values({...}).execute()\n```\n\n## Why `getDb()`?\n\nCloudflare Workers doesn''t support `process.env`. Environment variables come from the `env` binding via `cloudflare:workers`, which is only available during request handling. The `getDb()` function:\n\n1. Tries `process.env.DATABASE_URL` first (Node.js/Bun)\n2. Falls back to `cloudflare:workers` env binding\n3. Creates a singleton Kysely instance\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - breaks on Cloudflare Workers\nimport { db } from ''~/lib/db''\nexport const fn = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  return db.selectFrom(''users'').execute()\n})\n\n// ❌ WRONG - old pattern, doesn''t work\nconst { db } = await import(''~/lib/db'')\n\n// ✅ CORRECT\nconst { getDb } = await import(''~/lib/db'')\nconst db = await getDb()\n```\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n```bash\n# Local development (.env or .dev.vars)\nDATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@ep-xxx.region.neon.tech/livestockai?sslmode=require\n\n# Production (Cloudflare secrets)\nwrangler secret put DATABASE_URL\n\n# Test database\nDATABASE_URL_TEST=postgres://user:pass@ep-xxx.region.neon.tech/livestockai_test?sslmode=require\n```\n\n## Database Schema\n\nThe schema is defined in `app/lib/db/types.ts` with 23+ tables including:\n\n| Table               | Purpose                                 |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `users`             | User accounts (Better Auth)             |\n| `user_settings`     | Preferences (currency, units, language) |\n| `farms`             | Farm entities                           |\n| `farm_modules`      | Enabled livestock types per farm        |\n| `batches`           | Livestock batches (all 6 types)         |\n| `mortality_records` | Death tracking                          |\n| `feed_records`      | Feed consumption                        |\n| `weight_samples`    | Growth tracking                         |\n| `sales`             | Revenue records                         |\n| `expenses`          | Cost tracking                           |\n| `invoices`          | Customer invoices                       |\n\n## Migrations\n\nMigrations are in `app/lib/db/migrations/`:\n\n```bash\n# Run migrations\nbun run db:migrate\n\n# Rollback\nbun run db:rollback\n\n# Reset (drop all + migrate)\nbun run db:reset\n```\n\nMigration naming: `YYYY-MM-DD-NNN-description.ts`\n\n## Kysely Query Examples\n\n```typescript\n// Select with joins\nconst batches = await db\n  .selectFrom(''batches'')\n  .leftJoin(''farms'', ''farms.id'', ''batches.farmId'')\n  .select([''batches.id'', ''batches.species'', ''farms.name as farmName''])\n  .where(''batches.status'', ''='', ''active'')\n  .execute()\n\n// Insert with returning\nconst result = await db\n  .insertInto(''batches'')\n  .values({ farmId, species, initialQuantity })\n  .returning(''id'')\n  .executeTakeFirstOrThrow()\n\n// Update\nawait db\n  .updateTable(''batches'')\n  .set({ status: ''depleted'' })\n  .where(''id'', ''='', batchId)\n  .execute()\n\n// Aggregate\nconst stats = await db\n  .selectFrom(''sales'')\n  .select(sql<number>`sum(quantity)`.as(''totalSold''))\n  .where(''batchId'', ''='', batchId)\n  .executeTakeFirst()\n```\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- `kysely-orm` - Detailed Kysely patterns\n- `cloudflare-workers` - Deployment environment\n- `three-layer-architecture` - Repository layer patterns\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:54:29.753Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloudflare Worker Agents requiring serverless PostgreSQL database integration with type-safe SQL through Kysely query builder","zh":"适用于需要将服务器无 PostgreSQL 数据库集成到 Cloudflare Worker 代理的类型安全 SQL 通过 Kysely 查询生成器","ja":"Cloudflare Worker エージェントがサーバーレス PostgreSQL データベースを Kysely クエリ ビルダーを介して安全に統合する必要がある場合に最適","ko":"Cloudflare Worker 에이전트가 서버리스 PostgreSQL 데이터베이스를 Kysely 쿼리 빌더를 통해 안전하게 통합해야 하는 경우 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Cloudflare Worker que requieren integración de base de datos PostgreSQL sin servidor con SQL de tipo seguro a través del constructor de consultas Kysely","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Cloudflare Worker nécessitant une intégration de base de données PostgreSQL sans serveur avec un SQL de type sécurisé via le constructeur de requêtes Kysely","de":"Ideal für Cloudflare-Worker-Agents, die eine Integration der serverlosen PostgreSQL-Datenbank mit typsicherem SQL über den Kysely-Abfrage-Generator benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Trabalhador da Cloudflare que exigem integração de banco de dados PostgreSQL sem servidor com SQL de tipo seguro por meio do construtor de consultas Kysely","ru":"Идеально для агентов Cloudflare Worker, требующих интеграцию с серверной базой данных PostgreSQL через безопасный SQL с помощью конструктора запросов Kysely","ar":"مثالي لعميل Cloudflare Worker الذي يتطلب تكامل قاعدة بيانات PostgreSQL بدون خادم مع إمكانية إضافة SQL آمنة من خلال بناء جملة استعلام Kysely"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage database connections securely through the `getDb()` method, ensuring compatibility with Cloudflare Workers and providing a robust serverless PostgreSQL database experience with Neon, accessed via the Kysely query builder for type-safe SQL","zh":"赋予代理安全地管理数据库连接的能力，通过 `getDb()` 方法，确保与 Cloudflare Workers 兼容，并提供强大的服务器无 PostgreSQL 数据库体验，通过 Kysely 查询生成器访问 Neon 以获得类型安全的 SQL","ja":"エージェントが `getDb()` メソッドを介してデータベース接続を安全に管理できるようにし、Cloudflare Workers との互換性を確保し、Neon を介して Kysely クエリ ビルダーを使用してタイプセーフの SQL を実現することで、強力なサーバーレス PostgreSQL データベース体験を提供する","ko":"에이전트가 `getDb()` 메서드를 통해 데이터베이스 연결을 안전하게 관리할 수 있도록 하여 Cloudflare Workers와의 호환성을 보장하고, Kysely 쿼리 빌더를 통해 Neon에 접근하여 타입 안전한 SQL을 제공함으로써 강력한 서버리스 PostgreSQL 데이터베이스 경험을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar conexiones de base de datos de forma segura a través del método `getDb()`, garantizando la compatibilidad con Cloudflare Workers y proporcionando una experiencia de base de datos PostgreSQL sin servidor robusta con Neon, accesible a través del constructor de consultas Kysely para SQL de tipo seguro","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les connexions de base de données de manière sécurisée via la méthode `getDb()`, garantissant la compatibilité avec Cloudflare Workers et offrant une expérience de base de données PostgreSQL sans serveur robuste avec Neon, accessible via le constructeur de requêtes Kysely pour un SQL de type sécurisé","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, Datenbankverbindungen sicher über die `getDb()`-Methode zu verwalten, wodurch die Kompatibilität mit Cloudflare Workers sichergestellt und eine robuste serverlose PostgreSQL-Datenbankerfahrung mit Neon über den Kysely-Abfrage-Generator für typsicheren SQL ermöglicht wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar conexões de banco de dados de forma segura por meio do método `getDb()`, garantindo compatibilidade com os Trabalhadores da Cloudflare e fornecendo uma experiência robusta de banco de dados PostgreSQL sem servidor com Neon, acessada por meio do construtor de consultas Kysely para SQL de tipo seguro","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность безопасного управления соединениями с базой данных с помощью метода `getDb()`, обеспечивая совместимость с Cloudflare Workers и предоставляя надежный опыт работы с базой данных PostgreSQL без сервера с Neon, доступ к которой осуществляется через конструктор запросов Kysely для безопасного SQL","ar":"يمنح الوكيل إمكانية إدارة الاتصالات بقاعدة البيانات بشكل آمن من خلال طريقة `getDb()` ، مما يضمن التوافق مع عميل Cloudflare Worker و يوفر تجربة قوية لقاعدة بيانات PostgreSQL بدون خادم مع Neon ، يمكن الوصول إليها من خلال بناء جملة استعلام Kysely لإضافة SQL آمنة"},"useCases":{"en":["Managing serverless database connections for Cloudflare Workers","Building type-safe SQL queries with Kysely","Integrating Neon database into Cloudflare Worker applications"],"zh":["管理 Cloudflare Workers 的服务器无数据库连接","使用 Kysely 构建类型安全的 SQL 查询","将 Neon 数据库集成到 Cloudflare Worker 应用程序中"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workers のサーバーレス データベース接続を管理する","Kysely を使用してタイプセーフの SQL クエリを構築する","Neon データベースを Cloudflare Worker アプリケーションに統合する"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers의 서버리스 데이터베이스 연결을 관리","Kysely를 사용하여 타입 안전한 SQL 쿼리를 생성","Neon 데이터베이스를 Cloudflare Worker 애플리케이션에 통합"],"es":["Gestión de conexiones de base de datos sin servidor para Cloudflare Workers","Creación de consultas SQL de tipo seguro con Kysely","Integración de la base de datos Neon en aplicaciones de Cloudflare Worker"],"fr":["Gestion de connexions de base de données sans serveur pour Cloudflare Workers","Conception de requêtes SQL de type sécurisé avec Kysely","Intégration de la base de données Neon dans les applications Cloudflare Worker"],"de":["Verwaltung von serverlosen Datenbankverbindungen für Cloudflare-Worker","Erstellung von typsicheren SQL-Abfragen mit Kysely","Integration der Neon-Datenbank in Cloudflare-Worker-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Gerenciar conexões de banco de dados sem servidor para Trabalhadores da Cloudflare","Construir consultas SQL de tipo seguro com Kysely","Integrar banco de dados Neon em aplicações de Trabalhador da Cloudflare"],"ru":["Управление соединениями с базой данных без сервера для Cloudflare Workers","Создание безопасных запросов SQL с помощью Kysely","Интеграция базы данных Neon в приложения Cloudflare Worker"],"ar":["إدارة الاتصالات بقاعدة البيانات بدون خادم لعميل Cloudflare Worker","بناء استعلامات SQL آمنة مع Kysely","دمج قاعدة بيانات Neon في تطبيقات عميل Cloudflare Worker"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Cloudflare Workers compatibility","Neon database account needed","TypeScript environment required for `app/lib/db/index.ts` integration"],"zh":["需要 Cloudflare Workers 兼容性","需要 Neon 数据库账户","需要 TypeScript 环境以将 `app/lib/db/index.ts` 集成"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workers との互換性が必要","Neon データベース アカウントが必要","TypeScript 環境が `app/lib/db/index.ts` の統合に必要"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers와의 호환성이 필요","Neon 데이터베이스 계정이 필요","TypeScript 환경이 `app/lib/db/index.ts` 통합에 필요"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con Cloudflare Workers","Se necesita una cuenta de base de datos Neon","Se requiere un entorno de TypeScript para la integración de `app/lib/db/index.ts`"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec Cloudflare Workers","Un compte de base de données Neon est nécessaire","Un environnement TypeScript est requis pour l''intégration de `app/lib/db/index.ts`"],"de":["Erfordert Kompatibilität mit Cloudflare Workers","Ein Neon-Datenbankkonto ist erforderlich","Ein TypeScript-Umgebung ist für die Integration von `app/lib/db/index.ts` erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com os Trabalhadores da Cloudflare","Conta de banco de dados Neon necessária","Ambiente TypeScript necessário para integração `app/lib/db/index.ts`"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с Cloudflare Workers","Необходима учетная запись базы данных Neon","Требуется среда TypeScript для интеграции `app/lib/db/index.ts`"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع عميل Cloudflare Worker","حساب قاعدة بيانات Neon مطلوب","يتطلب بيئة TypeScript لإضافة `app/lib/db/index.ts`"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
