opment with Kiro CLI."},"features":{"zh":["快速浏览器自动化","持久的浏览器会话","复杂的多步骤工作流","安全的代码执行","游戏化和社交学习"],"ja":["高速ブラウザ自動化","持続的なブラウザセッション","複雑なマルチステップワークフロー","安全なコード実行","ゲーム化とソーシャルラーニング"],"ko":["빠른 브라우저 자동화","지속적인 브라우저 세션","복잡한 멀티 스텝 워크플ロー","안전한 코드 실행","게임화 및 소셜 러닝"],"es":["Automatización de navegador persistente","Mantenimiento de sesiones de navegador a través de comandos","Flujos de trabajo complejos","Instalación de dependencias de navegador","Compatibilidad con Chromium"],"fr":["Automation de navigateur persistante","Maintenance des sessions de navigateur à travers les commandes","Flux de travail complexes","Installation des dépendances de navigateur","Compatibilité avec Chromium"],"de":["Beständige Browser-Automatisierung","Beibehaltung von Browser-Sitzungen über Befehle hinweg","Komplexe Workflows","Installation von Browser-Abhängigkeiten","Kompatibilität mit Chromium"],"pt":["Automação de navegador persistente","Execução de comandos complexos","Instalação fácil com uvx e pip","Suporte a múltiplos navegadores","Documentação completa"],"ru":["Постоянная автоматизация браузера","Выполнение сложных команд","Легкая установка с помощью uvx и pip","Поддержка нескольких браузеров","Полная документация"],"ar":["أتمتة متصفح مستمرة","تشغيل أوامر معقدة","تثبيت سهل مع uvx و pip","دعم متصفحات متعددة","توثيق كامل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["浏览器自动化","browser-use","CLI工具","开发工具","自动化测试","浏览器会话"],"ja":["ブラウザ自動化","browser-use","CLIツール","開発ツール","自動化テスト","ブラウザセッション"],"ko":["브라우저 자동화","browser-use","CLI 도구","개발 도구","자동화 테스트","브라우저 세션"],"es":["automatización de navegador","browser-use","flujos de trabajo complejos","sesiones de navegador","Chromium","automatización de tareas","herramientas de desarrollo","línea de comandos"],"fr":["automation de navigateur","browser-use","flux de travail complexes","sessions de navigateur","Chromium","automation de tâches","outils de développement","ligne de commande"],"de":["Browser-Automatisierung","browser-use","komplexe Workflows","Browser-Sitzungen","Chromium","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Entwicklungstools","Befehlszeile"],"pt":["automação de navegador","browser-use","comandos persistentes","produtividade","desenvolvimento web","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["автоматизация браузера","browser-use","постоянные команды","производительность","веб-разработка","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["أتمتة متصفح","browser-use","أوامر مستمرة","إنتاجية","تطوير ويب","أدوات تطوير"]}},"owner":"khushparag","repo":"agentic_learning_coach","repoPath":"khushparag/agentic_learning_coach","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"browser-use","description":"Automates browser interactions for web testing, form filling, screenshots, and data extraction. Use when the user needs to navigate websites, interact with web pages, fill forms, take screenshots, or extract information from web pages.","bodyPreview":"# Browser Automation with browser-use CLI\n\nThe `browser-use` command provides fast, persistent browser automation. It maintains browser sessions across commands, enabling complex multi-step workflows.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Run without installing (recommended for one-off use)\nuvx browser-use[cli] open https://example.com\n\n# Or install permanently\nuv pip install browser-use[cli]\n\n# Install browser dependencies (Chromium)\nbrowser-use install\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use open https","body":"# Browser Automation with browser-use CLI\n\nThe `browser-use` command provides fast, persistent browser automation. It maintains browser sessions across commands, enabling complex multi-step workflows.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Run without installing (recommended for one-off use)\nuvx browser-use[cli] open https://example.com\n\n# Or install permanently\nuv pip install browser-use[cli]\n\n# Install browser dependencies (Chromium)\nbrowser-use install\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use open https://example.com           # Navigate to URL\nbrowser-use state                              # Get page elements with indices\nbrowser-use click 5                            # Click element by index\nbrowser-use type \"Hello World\"                 # Type text\nbrowser-use screenshot                         # Take screenshot\nbrowser-use close                              # Close browser\n```\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n1. **Navigate**: `browser-use open <url>` - Opens URL (starts browser if needed)\n2. **Inspect**: `browser-use state` - Returns clickable elements with indices\n3. **Interact**: Use indices from state to interact (`browser-use click 5`, `browser-use input 3 \"text\"`)\n4. **Verify**: `browser-use state` or `browser-use screenshot` to confirm actions\n5. **Repeat**: Browser stays open between commands\n\n## Browser Modes\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use --browser chromium open <url>      # Default: headless Chromium\nbrowser-use --browser chromium --headed open <url>  # Visible Chromium window\nbrowser-use --browser real open <url>          # User''s Chrome with login sessions\nbrowser-use --browser remote open <url>        # Cloud browser (requires API key)\n```\n\n- **chromium**: Fast, isolated, headless by default\n- **real**: Uses your Chrome with cookies, extensions, logged-in sessions\n- **remote**: Cloud-hosted browser with proxy support (requires BROWSER_USE_API_KEY)\n\n## Commands\n\n### Navigation\n```bash\nbrowser-use open <url>                    # Navigate to URL\nbrowser-use back                          # Go back in history\nbrowser-use scroll down                   # Scroll down\nbrowser-use scroll up                     # Scroll up\n```\n\n### Page State\n```bash\nbrowser-use state                         # Get URL, title, and clickable elements\nbrowser-use screenshot                    # Take screenshot (outputs base64)\nbrowser-use screenshot path.png           # Save screenshot to file\nbrowser-use screenshot --full path.png    # Full page screenshot\n```\n\n### Interactions (use indices from `browser-use state`)\n```bash\nbrowser-use click <index>                 # Click element\nbrowser-use type \"text\"                   # Type text into focused element\nbrowser-use input <index> \"text\"          # Click element, then type text\nbrowser-use keys \"Enter\"                  # Send keyboard keys\nbrowser-use keys \"Control+a\"              # Send key combination\nbrowser-use select <index> \"option\"       # Select dropdown option\n```\n\n### Tab Management\n```bash\nbrowser-use switch <tab>                  # Switch to tab by index\nbrowser-use close-tab                     # Close current tab\nbrowser-use close-tab <tab>               # Close specific tab\n```\n\n### JavaScript & Data\n```bash\nbrowser-use eval \"document.title\"         # Execute JavaScript, return result\nbrowser-use extract \"all product prices\"  # Extract data using LLM (requires API key)\n```\n\n### Python Execution (Persistent Session)\n```bash\nbrowser-use python \"x = 42\"               # Set variable\nbrowser-use python \"print(x)\"             # Access variable (outputs: 42)\nbrowser-use python \"print(browser.url)\"   # Access browser object\nbrowser-use python --vars                 # Show defined variables\nbrowser-use python --reset                # Clear Python namespace\nbrowser-use python --file script.py       # Execute Python file\n```\n\nThe Python session maintains state across commands. The `browser` object provides:\n- `browser.url` - Current page URL\n- `browser.title` - Page title\n- `browser.goto(url)` - Navigate\n- `browser.click(index)` - Click element\n- `browser.type(text)` - Type text\n- `browser.screenshot(path)` - Take screenshot\n- `browser.scroll()` - Scroll page\n- `browser.html` - Get page HTML\n\n### Agent Tasks (Requires API Key)\n```bash\nbrowser-use run \"Fill the contact form with test data\"    # Run AI agent\nbrowser-use run \"Extract all product prices\" --max-steps 50\n```\n\nAgent tasks use an LLM to autonomously complete complex browser tasks. Requires `BROWSER_USE_API_KEY` or configured LLM API key (OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, etc).\n\n### Session Management\n```bash\nbrowser-use sessions                      # List active sessions\nbrowser-use close                         # Close current session\nbrowser-use close --all                   # Close all sessions\n```\n\n### Server Control\n```bash\nbrowser-use server status                 # Check if server is running\nbrowser-use server stop                   # Stop server\nbrowser-use server logs                   # View server logs\n```\n\n### Setup\n```bash\nbrowser-use install                       # Install Chromium and system dependencies\n```\n\n## Global Options\n\n| Option | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `--session NAME` | Use named session (default: \"default\") |\n| `--browser MODE` | Browser mode: chromium, real, remote |\n| `--headed` | Show browser window (chromium mode) |\n| `--profile NAME` | Chrome profile (real mode only) |\n| `--json` | Output as JSON |\n| `--api-key KEY` | Override API key |\n\n**Session behavior**: All commands without `--session` use the same \"default\" session. The browser stays open and is reused across commands. Use `--session NAME` to run multiple browsers in parallel.\n\n## API Key Configuration\n\nSome features (`run`, `extract`, `--browser remote`) require an API key. The CLI checks these locations in order:\n\n1. `--api-key` command line flag\n2. `BROWSER_USE_API_KEY` environment variable\n3. `~/.config/browser-use/config.json` file\n\nTo configure permanently:\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.config/browser-use\necho ''{\"api_key\": \"your-key-here\"}'' > ~/.config/browser-use/config.json\n```\n\n## Examples\n\n### Form Submission\n```bash\nbrowser-use open https://example.com/contact\nbrowser-use state\n# Shows: [0] input \"Name\", [1] input \"Email\", [2] textarea \"Message\", [3] button \"Submit\"\nbrowser-use input 0 \"John Doe\"\nbrowser-use input 1 \"john@example.com\"\nbrowser-use input 2 \"Hello, this is a test message.\"\nbrowser-use click 3\nbrowser-use state  # Verify success\n```\n\n### Multi-Session Workflows\n```bash\nbrowser-use --session work open https://work.example.com\nbrowser-use --session personal open https://personal.example.com\nbrowser-use --session work state    # Check work session\nbrowser-use --session personal state  # Check personal session\nbrowser-use close --all             # Close both sessions\n```\n\n### Data Extraction with Python\n```bash\nbrowser-use open https://example.com/products\nbrowser-use python \"\nproducts = []\nfor i in range(20):\n    browser.scroll(''down'')\nbrowser.screenshot(''products.png'')\n\"\nbrowser-use python \"print(f''Captured {len(products)} products'')\"\n```\n\n### Using Real Browser (Logged-In Sessions)\n```bash\nbrowser-use --browser real open https://gmail.com\n# Uses your actual Chrome with existing login sessions\nbrowser-use state  # Already logged in!\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n1. **Always run `browser-use state` first** to see available elements and their indices\n2. **Use `--headed` for debugging** to see what the browser is doing\n3. **Sessions persist** - the browser stays open between commands\n4. **Use `--json` for parsing** output programmatically\n5. **Python variables persist** across `browser-use python` commands within a session\n6. **Real browser mode** preserves your login sessions and extensions\n7. **CLI aliases**: `bu`, `browser`, and `browseruse` all work identically to `browser-use`\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**Browser won''t start?**\n```bash\nbrowser-use install                   # Install/reinstall Chromium\nbrowser-use server stop               # Stop any stuck server\nbrowser-use --headed open <url>       # Try with visible window\n```\n\n**Element not found?**\n```bash\nbrowser-use state                     # Check current elements\nbrowser-use scroll down               # Element might be below fold\nbrowser-use state                     # Check again\n```\n\n**Session issues?**\n```bash\nbrowser-use sessions                  # Check active sessions\nbrowser-use close --all               # Clean slate\nbrowser-use open <url>                # Fresh start\n```\n\n## Cleanup\n\n**Always close the browser when done.** Run this after completing browser automation:\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use close\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:54:33.385Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Automation Agents needing persistent browser session management and complex workflow automation.","zh":"非常适合需要持久浏览器会话管理和复杂工作流自动化的自动化代理。","ja":"永続的なブラウザセッション管理と複雑なワークフロー自動化が必要な自動化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"지속적인 브라우저 세션 관리와 복잡한 워크플로 자동화가 필요한 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de automatización que necesitan gestión de sesión de navegador persistente y automatización de flujos de trabajo complejos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''automatisation ayant besoin d''une gestion de session de navigateur persistante et d''une automatisation de workflow complexe.","de":"Perfekt für Automatisierungsagenten, die eine persistente Browser-Sitzungsverwaltung und eine komplexe Workflow-Automatisierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação que necessitam de gerenciamento de sessões de navegador persistentes e automação de fluxos de trabalho complexos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации, которым требуется управление постоянными сессиями браузера и автоматизация сложных рабочих процессов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الآليين الذين بحاجة إلى إدارة جلسات المتصفح المستمرة وتشغيل سير عمل معقد"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate browser interactions using the browser-use CLI, maintaining sessions across commands and enabling multi-step workflows with FastAPI and Docker, while utilizing Chromium for browser dependencies.","zh":"赋予代理使用浏览器使用CLI自动化浏览器交互的能力，维持命令之间的会话，并通过FastAPI和Docker启用多步骤工作流，同时利用Chromium进行浏览器依赖。","ja":"エージェントにブラウザ使用CLIを使用してブラウザの相互作用を自動化する能力を与え、コマンド間のセッションを維持し、FastAPIとDockerを使用してマルチステップのワークフローを可能にし、同時にブラウザ依存関係のためにChromiumを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 브라우저 사용 CLI를 사용하여 브라우저 상호 작용을 자동화 할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 명령 간의 세션을 유지하고 FastAPI 및 Docker를 사용하여 다단계 워크플로를 가능하게 하면서 동시에 브라우저 종속성에 대해 Chromium을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar las interacciones del navegador mediante la CLI de uso del navegador, manteniendo las sesiones a través de los comandos y permitiendo flujos de trabajo multietapa con FastAPI y Docker, mientras utiliza Chromium para las dependencias del navegador.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser les interactions du navigateur en utilisant la CLI d''utilisation du navigateur, en maintenant les sessions à travers les commandes et en permettant des flux de travail multietapes avec FastAPI et Docker, tout en utilisant Chromium pour les dépendances du navigateur.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Browser-Interaktionen mithilfe der Browser-Verwendung-CLI zu automatisieren, Sitzungen über Befehle hinweg aufrechtzuerhalten und mehrstufige Workflows mit FastAPI und Docker zu ermöglichen, während Chromium für die Browser-Abhängigkeiten verwendet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar interações do navegador usando a CLI do navegador, mantendo sessões entre comandos e habilitando fluxos de trabalho multi-etapa com FastAPI e Docker, ao mesmo tempo em que utiliza o Chromium para dependências do navegador.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать взаимодействия с браузером с помощью браузер-CLI, сохраняя сессии между командами и ermöglicht многоступенчатые рабочие процессы с FastAPI и Docker, при этом используя Chromium для зависимостей браузера.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تشغيل التفاعلات المتصفح باستخدام سطر أوامر المتصفح، مع الحفاظ على الجلسات عبر الأوامر وتشغيل سير العمل متعددة الخطوات مع FastAPI و Docker، في الوقت نفسه استخدام كروم لاعتمادية المتصفح."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating browser-based data scraping","Generating persistent browser sessions for testing","Debugging complex web applications with multi-step workflows"],"