.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents CLI ayant besoin d''une gestion autonome de l''exécution de pipelines épiques pour l''édition et la mise à jour de PRD.","de":"Perfekt für CLI-Agents, die eine autonome Verwaltung der Ausführung von epischen Pipelines für die Bearbeitung und Aktualisierung von PRD benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes CLI que necessitam de gerenciamento de pipeline de execução épica autônoma para edição e atualização de PRD.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов CLI, которым необходима автономная система управления конвейером выполнения эпических задач для редактирования и обновления PRD.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة سطر الأوامر الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة трубة تنفيذ ذاتية لتعديل وتحديث وثائق المواصفات المنتج"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to follow the BMAD Method for editing PRD documents, applying best practices, and maintaining consistency while tracking changes, utilizing Markdown files and workflow execution.","zh":"赋予代理编辑 PRD 文档、应用最佳实践和保持一致性的能力，同时使用 Markdown 文件和工作流执行跟踪更改，遵循 BMAD 方法。","ja":"BMAD メソッドに従って PRD 文書を編集し、ベストプラクティスを適用し、一貫性を維持し、変更を追跡するために Markdown ファイルとワークフロー実行を使用するエージェントをエンパワーメントします。","ko":"에이전트가 BMAD 방법을 따르며 PRD 문서를 편집하고 최선의 사례를 적용하고 일관성을 유지하며 변경 사항을 추적하는 기능을 제공합니다. 마크다운 파일과 워크플로우 실행을 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a seguir el método BMAD para la edición de documentos PRD, aplicar las mejores prácticas y mantener la consistencia mientras se realizan seguimientos de cambios, utilizando archivos Markdown y ejecución de flujos de trabajo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de suivre la méthode BMAD pour l''édition de documents PRD, en appliquant les meilleures pratiques et en maintenant la cohérence tout en suivant les modifications, en utilisant des fichiers Markdown et l''exécution de flux de travail.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, die BMAD-Methode für die Bearbeitung von PRD-Dokumenten zu befolgen, bewährte Verfahren anzuwenden und die Konsistenz zu wahren, während Änderungen nachverfolgt werden, unter Verwendung von Markdown-Dateien und Workflow-Ausführung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a seguir o Método BMAD para edição de documentos PRD, aplicar as melhores práticas e manter a consistência, além de acompanhar as alterações, utilizando arquivos Markdown e execução de fluxo de trabalho.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью следовать Методу BMAD для редактирования документов PRD, применять лучшие практики и поддерживать согласованность, а также отслеживать изменения, используя файлы Markdown и выполнение рабочего процесса.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء متابعة طريقة BMAD لتحرير وثائق المواصفات المنتج، وتطبيق أفضل الممارسات والحفاظ على الاتساق، بالإضافة إلى تتبع التغييرات، باستخدام ملفات Markdown وتنفيذ سير عمل"},"useCases":{"en":["Updating existing PRD documents with requested changes","Maintaining consistency in PRD editing using the BMAD Method","Tracking changes in PRD documents for version control"],"zh":["使用请求的更改更新现有的 PRD 文档","使用 BMAD 方法保持 PRD 编辑的一致性","跟踪 PRD 文档的更改以进行版本控制"],"ja":["要求された変更を使用して既存の PRD 文書を更新する","BMAD メソッドを使用して PRD 編集の一貫性を維持する","バージョン管理のために PRD 文書の変更を追跡する"],"ko":["요청된 변경 사항을 사용하여 기존 PRD 문서를 업데이트합니다.","BMAD 방법을 사용하여 PRD 편집의 일관성을 유지합니다.","버전 관리를 위해 PRD 문서의 변경 사항을 추적합니다."],"es":["Actualizar documentos PRD existentes con los cambios solicitados","Mantener la consistencia en la edición de PRD utilizando el método BMAD","Realizar un seguimiento de los cambios en los documentos PRD para el control de versiones"],"fr":["Mettre à jour les documents PRD existants avec les modifications demandées","Maintenir la cohérence dans l''édition de PRD en utilisant la méthode BMAD","Suivre les modifications dans les documents PRD pour le contrôle de version"],"de":["Vorhandene PRD-Dokumente mit den angeforderten Änderungen aktualisieren","Konsistenz bei der Bearbeitung von PRD mithilfe der BMAD-Methode aufrechterhalten","Änderungen in PRD-Dokumenten für die Versionskontrolle nachverfolgen"],"pt":["Atualizar documentos PRD existentes com alterações solicitadas","Manter a consistência na edição de PRD usando o Método BMAD","Acompanhar alterações em documentos PRD para controle de versão"],"ru":["Обновление существующих документов PRD с запрошенными изменениями","Поддержание согласованности при редактировании PRD с помощью Метода BMAD","Отслеживание изменений в документах PRD для контроля версий"],"ar":["تحديث وثائق المواصفات المنتج الحالية بالتغيرات المطلوبة","الحفاظ على الاتساق في تحرير وثائق المواصفات المنتج باستخدام طريقة BMAD","تتبع التغييرات في وثائق المواصفات المنتج للسيطرة على الإصدارات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","Limited to Markdown file format for PRD documents"],"zh":["需要访问 _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","仅限 Markdown 文件格式用于 PRD 文档"],"ja":["_bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md にアクセスする必要があります","PRD 文書では Markdown ファイル形式のみが使用できます"],"ko":["_bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md에 액세스해야 합니다.","PRD 문서에서는 Markdown 파일 형식만 사용할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","Limitado al formato de archivo Markdown para documentos PRD"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","Limité au format de fichier Markdown pour les documents PRD"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","Begrenzt auf das Markdown-Dateiformat für PRD-Dokumente"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arquivo _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","Limitado ao formato de arquivo Markdown para documentos PRD"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлу _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","Ограничен форматом файла Markdown для документов PRD"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الملف _bmad/bmm/workflows/2-plan-workflows/create-prd/workflow-edit-prd.md","محدود بتنسيق ملف Markdown لوثائق المواصفات المنتج"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yura9011/PWV/skill-creator', 'community', 'yura9011', 'PWV', 'yura9011/PWV', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z', '2026-02-18T12:54:38.874Z', NULL, '{"id":"yura9011/PWV/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"技能创建者为开发者提供创建专业技能的指导，帮助 Claude 获得特定领域的知识和工作流程","ja":"スキルクリエイターは、開発者が特定のドメインやタスクに対応したスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供する","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 특정 도메인 또는 작업에 대한 맞춤형 스킬을 만들 수 있는 가이드를 제공","es":"El creador de habilidades es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite crear paquetes modulares de conocimientos especializados para Claude","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un outil pour développeurs qui permet de créer des packages modulaires de connaissances spécialisées pour Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Tool für Entwickler, mit dem modulare Pakete von spezialisierten Kenntnissen für Claude erstellt werden können","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendam as capacidades do Claude.","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude.","ar":"مبتكر المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة توسع قدرات كلود.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"技能创建者 - 为开发者打造专业技能","ja":"スキルクリエイター - 開発者のためのスキル作成","ko":"스킬 생성기 - 개발자를 위한 맞춤형 스킬","es":"Creador de Habilidades: Guía para Desarrolladores","fr":"Créateur de Compétences: Guide pour Développeurs","de":"Fähigkeits-Ersteller: Anleitung für Entwickler","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Extenda as Capacidades do Claude","ru":"Создатель Навыков: Расширьте Возможности Claude","ar":"مبتكر المهارات: وسّع قدرات كلود","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"技能创建者为开发者提供创建专业技能的指导，帮助 Claude 获得特定领域的知识和工作流程","ja":"スキルクリエイターは、開発者が特定のドメインやタスクに対応したスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供する","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 특정 도메인 또는 작업에 대한 맞춤형 스킬을 만들 수 있는 가이드를 제공","es":"El creador de habilidades es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite crear paquetes modulares de conocimientos especializados para Claude","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un outil pour développeurs qui permet de créer des packages modulaires de connaissances spécialisées pour Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Tool für Entwickler, mit dem modulare Pakete von spezialisierten Kenntnissen für Claude erstellt werden können","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendam as capacidades do Claude.","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude.","ar":"مبتكر المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة توسع قدرات كلود.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提供专业的工作流程","支持特定领域的知识和工具","帮助开发者创建自定义技能","扩展 Claude 的能力","支持多种开发任务"],"ja":["専門的なワークフローを提供","特定のドメインの知識とツールをサポート","開発者がカスタムスキルを作成するのを支援","Claude の能力を拡張","多様な開発タスクをサポート"],"ko":["전문적인 워크플로우 제공","특정 도메인의 지식과 툴 지원","개발자가 맞춤형 스킬을 생성할 수 있도록 지원","Claude의 능력을 확장","다양한 개발 작업 지원"],"es":["Creación de flujos de trabajo especializados","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude","Conocimientos procedimentales para tareas específicas","Paquetes modulares de conocimientos","Guías de incorporación para dominios específicos"],"fr":["Création de flux de travail spécialisés","Élargissement des capacités de Claude","Connaissances procédurales pour des tâches spécifiques","Packages modulaires de connaissances","Guides d''intégration pour des domaines spécifiques"],"de":["Erstellung von spezialisierten Workflows","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Prozedurale Kenntnisse für spezifische Aufgaben","Modulare Pakete von Kenntnissen","Einbindungsguides für spezifische Domänen"],"pt":["Fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes","Permite a criação de fluxos de trabalho especializados","Transforma o Claude em um agente especializado","Fornece conhecimento procedural avançado","Permite a extensão das capacidades do Claude"],"ru":["Предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков","Позволяет создавать специализированные рабочие процессы","Превращает Claude в специализированного агента","Предоставляет продвинутое процедурное знание","Позволяет расширить возможности Claude"],"ar":["يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة","يسمح بإنشاء سلاسل عمل متخصصة","يحول كلود إلى وكيل متخصص","يوفر معرفة إجرائية متقدمة","يسمح بتوسيع قدرات كلود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建者","专业技能","Claude","开发者工具","工作流程","特定领域知识","自定义技能","能力扩展"],"ja":["スキルクリエイター","専門スキル","Claude","開発者ツール","ワークフロー","特定ドメイン知識","カスタムスキル","能力拡張"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","맞춤형 스킬","Claude","개발자 툴","워크플로우","특정 도메인 지식","커스텀 스킬","능력 확장"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","Claude","conocimientos especializados","flujos de trabajo","tareas específicas","paquetes modulares","guías de incorporación"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","Claude","connaissances spécialisées","flux de travail","tâches spécifiques","packages modulaires","guides d''intégration"],"de":["Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Claude","spezialisierte Kenntnisse","Workflows","spezifische Aufgaben","modulare Pakete","Einbindungsguides"],"pt":["criador de habilidades","habilidades eficazes","capacidades do Claude","conhecimento procedural","agentes especializados","desenvolvimento de habilidades"],"ru":["создатель навыков","эффективные навыки","возможности Claude","процедурное знание","специализированные агенты","разработка навыков"],"ar":["مبتكر المهارات","مهارات فعالة","قدرات كلود","معرفة إجرائية","وكلاء متخصصون","تطوير المهارات"]}},"owner":"yura9011","repo":"PWV","repoPath":"yura9011/PWV","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These are the only fields that Claude reads to determine when the skill gets used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in describing what the skill is, and when it should be used.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:54:38.874Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions","zh":"非常适合需要专门知识和工作流扩展的代理人，如Claude","ja":"Claudeのような特殊な知識とワークフローの拡張が必要なエージェントに最適","ko":"클라우드와 같은 전문 지식 및 워크플로 확장 기능이 필요한 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfect for agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions","fr":"Perfect for agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions","de":"Perfect for agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions","pt":"Perfeito para agentes como Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Идеально для агентов, таких как Claude, требующих специализированных знаний и расширений рабочего процесса","ar":"مثالي لعميل مثل Claude الذي يحتاج إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيع عمليات العمل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages to extend capabilities, and providing specialized workflows and tools for specific domains or tasks","zh":"赋予代理人转化为具有程序化知识的专业实体的能力，利用模块化的自包含包来扩展能力，并为特定领域或任务提供专业的工作流和工具","ja":"エージェントが手順きょうかを持つ専門エンティティに変身できるようにし、モジュラーな自己完結型パッケージを使用して機能を拡張し、特定のドメインまたはタスクの専門的なワークフローとツールを提供する","ko":"에이전트가 절차적 지식을 갖춘 전문 엔티티로 변신할 수 있도록 하는 것으로, 모듈형 자체 완결 패키지를 사용하여 기능을 확장하고, 특정 도메인 또는 작업을 위한 전문 워크플로 및 도구를 제공한다","es":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages to extend capabilities, and providing specialized workflows and tools for specific domains or tasks","fr":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages to extend capabilities, and providing specialized workflows and tools for specific domains or tasks","de":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages to extend capabilities, and providing specialized workflows and tools for specific domains or tasks","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento procedural, utilizando pacotes modulares autocontidos para estender capacidades e fornecendo fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas especializados para domínios ou tarefas específicos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, использующие модульные самодостаточные пакеты для расширения возможностей и предоставляющие специализированные рабочие процессы и инструменты для конкретных областей или задач","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التحول إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بمعرفة إجرائية، باستخدام حزم منفصلة تحتوي على نفسها لتوسيع القدرات، وتوفير سير عمل وأدوات متخصصة لمجالات أو مهام محددة"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating modular skill packages for domain-specific tasks","Developing procedural knowledge for agents","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows and tools"],"zh":["为领域特定任务创建模块化技能包","为代理人开发程序化知识","使用专业工作流和工具扩展代理人功能"],"ja":["ドメイン特定タスクのモジュラー技能パッケージを作成する","エージェントの手順きょうかを開発する","専門のワークフローとツールを使用してエージェントの機能を拡張する"],"ko":["도메인 특정 작업을 위한 모듈형 기술 패키지 생성","에이전트를 위한 절차적 지식 개발","전문 워크플로 및 도구를 사용하여 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Creating modular skill packages for domain-specific tasks","Developing procedural knowledge for agents","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows and tools"],"fr":["Creating modular skill packages for domain-specific tasks","Developing procedural knowledge for agents","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows and tools"],"de":["Creating modular skill packages for domain-specific tasks","Developing procedural knowledge for agents","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows and tools"],"pt":["Criar pacotes de habilidades modulares para tarefas específicas de domínio","Desenvolver conhecimento procedural para agentes","Estender as capacidades dos agentes com fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas especializados"],"ru":["Создание модульных пакетов навыков для задач, специфичных для домена","Разработка процедурных знаний для агентов","Расширение возможностей агентов с помощью специализированных рабочих процессов и инструментов"],"ar":["إنشاء حزم مهارات منفصلة لمهام محددة للمجال","تطوير معرفة إجرائية للوكلاء","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء مع سير عمل وأدوات متخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Claude''s architecture and skill development framework"],"zh":["需要了解Claude的架构和技能开发框架"],"ja":["Claudeのアーキテクチャとスキル開発フレームワークを理解する必要がある"],"ko":["클라우드의 아키텍처 및 스킬 개발 프레임워크를 이해해야 함"],"es":["Requires understanding of Claude''s architecture and skill development framework"],"fr":["Requires understanding of Claude''s architecture and skill development framework"],"de":["Requires understanding of Claude''s architecture and skill development framework"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da arquitetura do Claude e do quadro de desenvolvimento de habilidades"],"ru":["Требует понимания архитектуры Claude и фреймворка разработки навыков"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا للهيكل المعماري لبرنامج Claude وإطار عمل تطوير المهارات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
