e banco de dados","Suporte a projetos TypeScript/JavaScript","Garantia de consistência do esquema em diferentes ambientes","Facilidade de uso e configuração"],"ru":["Поток разработки базы данных","Создание и управление схемами базы данных","Поддержка проектов TypeScript/JavaScript","Гарантия согласованности схемы в разных средах","Легкость использования и настройки"],"ar":["تدفق تطوير قاعدة البيانات","إنشاء وإدارة مخططات قاعدة البيانات","دعم مشاريع TypeScript/JavaScript","ضمان الاتساق في المخططات في بيئات مختلفة","سهولة الاستخدام والتكوين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Drizzle ORM","数据库迁移","TypeScript","JavaScript","数据库 Schema","migration-first","开发工作流"],"ja":["Drizzle ORM","データベースマイグレーション","TypeScript","JavaScript","データベースSchema","マイグレーションファースト","開発ワークフロー"],"ko":["드릴즈 ORM","데이터베이스 마이그레이션","TypeScript","JavaScript","데이터베이스 Schema","마이그레이션ファースト","개발 워크플로우"],"es":["drizzle orm","migraciones de base de datos","typescript","javascript","desarrollo de base de datos","gestión de esquemas"],"fr":["drizzle orm","migration de base de données","typescript","javascript","développement de base de données","gestion de schémas"],"de":["drizzle orm","datenbankmigrationen","typescript","javascript","datenbankentwicklung","verwaltung von schemata"],"pt":["drizzle migrations","desenvolvimento de banco de dados","gerenciamento de esquemas","typescript","javascript","banco de dados","esquema de banco de dados"],"ru":["drizzle миграции","разработка базы данных","управление схемами","typescript","javascript","база данных","схема базы данных"],"ar":["درزل المهاجرات","تطوير قاعدة البيانات","إدارة المخططات","typescript","javascript","قاعدة البيانات","مخطط قاعدة البيانات"]}},"owner":"multideskio","repo":"vinha_admin_center","repoPath":"multideskio/vinha_admin_center","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"drizzle-migrations","description":"Migration-first database development workflow using Drizzle ORM for TypeScript/J...","version":"1.0.0","tags":[""],"bodyPreview":"# Drizzle ORM Database Migrations (TypeScript)\n\nMigration-first database development workflow using Drizzle ORM for TypeScript/JavaScript projects.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- Working with Drizzle ORM in TypeScript/JavaScript projects\n- Need to create or modify database schema\n- Want migration-first development workflow\n- Setting up new database tables or columns\n- Need to ensure schema consistency across environments\n\n## Core Principle: Migration-First Development\n\n**Cri","body":"# Drizzle ORM Database Migrations (TypeScript)\n\nMigration-first database development workflow using Drizzle ORM for TypeScript/JavaScript projects.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- Working with Drizzle ORM in TypeScript/JavaScript projects\n- Need to create or modify database schema\n- Want migration-first development workflow\n- Setting up new database tables or columns\n- Need to ensure schema consistency across environments\n\n## Core Principle: Migration-First Development\n\n**Critical Rule**: Schema changes ALWAYS start with migrations, never code-first.\n\n### Why Migration-First?\n\n- ✅ SQL migrations are the single source of truth\n- ✅ Prevents schema drift between environments\n- ✅ Enables rollback and versioning\n- ✅ Forces explicit schema design decisions\n- ✅ TypeScript types generated from migrations\n- ✅ CI/CD can validate schema changes\n\n### Anti-Pattern (Code-First)\n\n❌ **WRONG**: Writing TypeScript schema first\n\n```typescript\n// DON''T DO THIS FIRST\nexport const users = pgTable(''users'', {\n  id: uuid(''id'').primaryKey(),\n  email: text(''email'').notNull(),\n})\n```\n\n### Correct Pattern (Migration-First)\n\n✅ **CORRECT**: Write SQL migration first\n\n```sql\n-- drizzle/0001_add_users_table.sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n```\n\n## Complete Migration Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Design Schema in SQL Migration\n\nCreate descriptive SQL migration file:\n\n```sql\n-- drizzle/0001_create_school_calendars.sql\nCREATE TABLE school_calendars (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  school_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES schools(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  start_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  end_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  academic_year TEXT NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),\n  updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- Add indexes for query performance\nCREATE INDEX idx_school_calendars_school_id ON school_calendars(school_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_school_calendars_academic_year ON school_calendars(academic_year);\n\n-- Add constraints\nALTER TABLE school_calendars\n  ADD CONSTRAINT check_date_range\n  CHECK (end_date > start_date);\n```\n\n**Naming Convention**:\n\n- Use sequential numbers: `0001_`, `0002_`, etc.\n- Descriptive names: `create_school_calendars`, `add_user_roles`\n- Format: `XXXX_descriptive_name.sql`\n\n### Step 2: Generate TypeScript Definitions\n\nDrizzle Kit generates TypeScript types from SQL:\n\n```bash\n# Generate TypeScript schema and snapshots\npnpm drizzle-kit generate\n\n# Or using npm\nnpm run db:generate\n```\n\n**What This Creates**:\n\n1. TypeScript schema files (if using `drizzle-kit push`)\n2. Snapshot files in `drizzle/meta/XXXX_snapshot.json`\n3. Migration metadata\n\n### Step 3: Create Schema Snapshot\n\nSnapshots enable schema drift detection:\n\n```json\n// drizzle/meta/0001_snapshot.json (auto-generated)\n{\n  \"version\": \"5\",\n  \"dialect\": \"postgresql\",\n  \"tables\": {\n    \"school_calendars\": {\n      \"name\": \"school_calendars\",\n      \"columns\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"name\": \"id\",\n          \"type\": \"uuid\",\n          \"primaryKey\": true,\n          \"notNull\": true,\n          \"default\": \"gen_random_uuid()\"\n        },\n        \"school_id\": {\n          \"name\": \"school_id\",\n          \"type\": \"uuid\",\n          \"notNull\": true\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Snapshots in Version Control**:\n\n- ✅ Commit snapshots to git\n- ✅ Enables drift detection in CI\n- ✅ Documents schema history\n\n### Step 4: Implement TypeScript Schema\n\nNow write TypeScript schema that mirrors SQL migration:\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/db/schema/school/calendar.ts\nimport { pgTable, uuid, date, text, timestamp } from ''drizzle-orm/pg-core''\nimport { schools } from ''./school''\n\nexport const schoolCalendars = pgTable(''school_calendars'', {\n  id: uuid(''id'').primaryKey().defaultRandom(),\n  schoolId: uuid(''school_id'')\n    .notNull()\n    .references(() => schools.id, { onDelete: ''cascade'' }),\n  startDate: date(''start_date'').notNull(),\n  endDate: date(''end_date'').notNull(),\n  academicYear: text(''academic_year'').notNull(),\n  createdAt: timestamp(''created_at'').defaultNow(),\n  updatedAt: timestamp(''updated_at'').defaultNow(),\n})\n\n// Type inference\nexport type SchoolCalendar = typeof schoolCalendars.$inferSelect\nexport type NewSchoolCalendar = typeof schoolCalendars.$inferInsert\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n\n- Column names match SQL exactly: `school_id` → `''school_id''`\n- TypeScript property names use camelCase: `schoolId`\n- Constraints and indexes defined in SQL, not TypeScript\n- Foreign keys reference other tables\n\n### Step 5: Organize Schemas by Domain\n\nStructure schemas for maintainability:\n\n```\nsrc/lib/db/schema/\n├── index.ts              # Export all schemas\n├── school/\n│   ├── index.ts\n│   ├── district.ts\n│   ├── holiday.ts\n│   ├── school.ts\n│   └── calendar.ts\n├── providers.ts\n├── cart.ts\n└── users.ts\n```\n\n**index.ts** (export all):\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/db/schema/index.ts\nexport * from ''./school''\nexport * from ''./providers''\nexport * from ''./cart''\nexport * from ''./users''\n```\n\n**school/index.ts**:\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/db/schema/school/index.ts\nexport * from ''./district''\nexport * from ''./holiday''\nexport * from ''./school''\nexport * from ''./calendar''\n```\n\n### Step 6: Add Quality Check to CI\n\nValidate schema consistency in CI/CD:\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/quality.yml\nname: Quality Checks\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main, develop]\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  quality:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: ''20''\n          cache: ''pnpm''\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\n\n      - name: Check database schema drift\n        run: pnpm drizzle-kit check\n\n      - name: Verify migrations (dry-run)\n        run: pnpm drizzle-kit push --dry-run\n        env:\n          DATABASE_URL: ${{ secrets.STAGING_DATABASE_URL }}\n\n      - name: Run type checking\n        run: pnpm tsc --noEmit\n\n      - name: Lint code\n        run: pnpm lint\n```\n\n**CI Checks Explained**:\n\n- `drizzle-kit check`: Validates snapshots match schema\n- `drizzle-kit push --dry-run`: Tests migration without applying\n- Type checking: Ensures TypeScript compiles\n- Linting: Enforces code style\n\n### Step 7: Test on Staging\n\nBefore production, test migration on staging:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Run migration on staging\nSTAGING_DATABASE_URL=\"...\" pnpm drizzle-kit push\n\n# 2. Verify schema\npnpm drizzle-kit check\n\n# 3. Test affected API routes\ncurl https://staging.example.com/api/schools/calendars\n\n# 4. Check for data integrity issues\n# Run queries to verify data looks correct\n\n# 5. Monitor logs for errors\n# Check application logs for migration-related errors\n```\n\n**Staging Checklist**:\n\n- [ ] Migration runs without errors\n- [ ] Schema drift check passes\n- [ ] API routes using new schema work correctly\n- [ ] No data integrity issues\n- [ ] Application logs show no errors\n- [ ] Query performance acceptable\n\n## Common Migration Patterns\n\n### Adding a Column\n\n```sql\n-- drizzle/0005_add_user_phone.sql\nALTER TABLE users\nADD COLUMN phone TEXT;\n\n-- Add index if querying by phone\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_phone ON users(phone);\n```\n\nTypeScript:\n\n```typescript\nexport const users = pgTable(''users'', {\n  id: uuid(''id'').primaryKey(),\n  email: text(''email'').notNull(),\n  phone: text(''phone''), // New column\n})\n```\n\n### Creating a Junction Table\n\n```sql\n-- drizzle/0006_create_provider_specialties.sql\nCREATE TABLE provider_specialties (\n  provider_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES providers(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  specialty_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES specialties(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  PRIMARY KEY (provider_id, specialty_id)\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_provider_specialties_provider ON provider_specialties(provider_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_provider_specialties_specialty ON provider_specialties(specialty_id);\n```\n\nTypeScript:\n\n```typescript\nexport const providerSpecialties = pgTable(\n  ''provider_specialties'',\n  {\n    providerId: uuid(''provider_id'')\n      .notNull()\n      .references(() => providers.id, { onDelete: ''cascade'' }),\n    specialtyId: uuid(''specialty_id'')\n      .notNull()\n      .references(() => specialties.id, { onDelete: ''cascade'' }),\n  },\n  (table) => ({\n    pk: primaryKey(table.providerId, table.specialtyId),\n  }),\n)\n```\n\n### Modifying Column Type\n\n```sql\n-- drizzle/0007_change_price_to_decimal.sql\nALTER TABLE services\nALTER COLUMN price TYPE DECIMAL(10, 2);\n```\n\nTypeScript:\n\n```typescript\nimport { decimal } from ''drizzle-orm/pg-core''\n\nexport const services = pgTable(''services'', {\n  id: uuid(''id'').primaryKey(),\n  name: text(''name'').notNull(),\n  price: decimal(''price'', { precision: 10, scale: 2 }).notNull(),\n})\n```\n\n### Adding Constraints\n\n```sql\n-- drizzle/0008_add_email_constraint.sql\nALTER TABLE users\nADD CONSTRAINT users_email_unique UNIQUE (email);\n\nALTER TABLE users\nADD CONSTRAINT users_email_format CHECK (email ~* ''^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z|a-z]{2,}$'');\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n### drizzle.config.ts\n\n```typescript\nimport type { Config } from ''drizzle-kit''\n\nexport default {\n  schema: ''./src/lib/db/schema/index.ts'',\n  out: ''./drizzle'',\n  driver: ''pg'',\n  dbCredentials: {\n    connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL!,\n  },\n} satisfies Config\n```\n\n### package.json Scripts\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"db:generate\": \"drizzle-kit generate:pg\",\n    \"db:push\": \"drizzle-kit push:pg\",\n    \"db:studio\": \"drizzle-kit studio\",\n    \"db:check\": \"drizzle-kit check:pg\",\n    \"db:up\": \"drizzle-kit up:pg\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Migration Testing Workflow\n\n### Local Testing\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create migration\necho \"CREATE TABLE test (...)\" > drizzle/0009_test.sql\n\n# 2. Generate TypeScript\npnpm db:generate\n\n# 3. Push to local database\npnpm db:push\n\n# 4. Verify schema\npnpm db:check\n\n# 5. Test in application\npnpm dev\n# Manually test affected features\n\n# 6. Run tests\npnpm test\n```\n\n### Rollback Strategy\n\n```sql\n-- drizzle/0010_add_feature.sql (up migration)\nCREATE TABLE new_feature (...);\n\n-- drizzle/0010_add_feature_down.sql (down migration)\nDROP TABLE new_feature;\n```\n\nApply rollback:\n\n```bash\n# Manually run down migration\npsql $DATABASE_URL -f drizzle/0010_add_feature_down.sql\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- ✅ Write SQL migrations first\n- ✅ Use descriptive migration names\n- ✅ Add indexes for foreign keys\n- ✅ Include constraints in migrations\n- ✅ Test migrations on staging before production\n- ✅ Commit snapshots to version control\n- ✅ Organize schemas by domain\n- ✅ Use `drizzle-kit check` in CI\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- ❌ Never write TypeScript schema before SQL migration\n- ❌ Don''t skip staging testing\n- ❌ Don''t modify old migrations (create new ones)\n- ❌ Don''t forget to add indexes\n- ❌ Don''t use `drizzle-kit push` in production (use proper migrations)\n- ❌ Don''t commit generated files without snapshots\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Schema Drift Detected\n\n**Error**: `Schema drift detected`\n\n**Solution**:\n\n```bash\n# Check what changed\npnpm drizzle-kit check\n\n# Regenerate snapshots\npnpm drizzle-kit generate\n\n# Review changes and commit\ngit add drizzle/meta/\ngit commit -m \"Update schema snapshots\"\n```\n\n### Migration Fails on Staging\n\n**Error**: Migration fails with data constraint violation\n\n**Solution**:\n\n1. Rollback migration\n2. Create data migration script\n3. Run data migration first\n4. Then run schema migration\n\n```sql\n-- First: Migrate data\nUPDATE users SET status = ''active'' WHERE status IS NULL;\n\n-- Then: Add constraint\nALTER TABLE users\nALTER COLUMN status SET NOT NULL;\n```\n\n### TypeScript Types Out of Sync\n\n**Error**: TypeScript types don''t match database\n\n**Solution**:\n\n```bash\n# Regenerate everything\npnpm db:generate\npnpm tsc --noEmit\n\n# If still broken, check schema files\n# Ensure column names match SQL exactly\n```\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- `universal-data-database-migration` - Universal migration patterns\n- `toolchains-typescript-data-drizzle` - Drizzle ORM usage patterns\n- `toolchains-typescript-core` - TypeScript best practices\n- `universal-debugging-verification-before-completion` - Verification workflows\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:56:14.118Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for TypeScript/JavaScript Agents needing database schema management with Drizzle ORM","zh":"非常适合需要使用 Drizzle ORM 进行数据库模式管理的 TypeScript/JavaScript 代理","ja":"Drizzle ORM を使用してデータベース スキーマを管理する必要がある TypeScript/JavaScript エージェントに最適","ko":"Drizzle ORM을 사용하여 데이터베이스 스키마를 관리해야 하는 TypeScript/JavaScript 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes TypeScript/JavaScript que necesitan administración de esquemas de bases de datos con Drizzle ORM","fr":"Parfait pour les agents TypeScript/JavaScript ayant besoin de gestion de schémas de base de données avec Drizzle ORM","de":"Perfekt für TypeScript/JavaScript-Agents, die eine Datenbank-Schemaverwaltung mit Drizzle ORM benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para agentes TypeScript/JavaScript que necessitam de gerenciamento de esquema de banco de dados com Drizzle ORM","ru":"Идеально для агентов TypeScript/JavaScript, которым необходимо управление схемой базы данных с помощью Drizzle ORM","ar":"مثالي لعمليات TypeScript/JavaScript التي تحتاج إلى إدارة مخطط قاعدة البيانات مع Drizzle ORM"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage database schema using a migration-first development workflow with Drizzle ORM, ensuring schema consistency across environments with TypeScript/JavaScript projects, and supporting the creation or modification of database tables and columns","zh":"赋予代理使用 Drizzle ORM 管理数据库模式的能力，通过迁移优先的开发工作流程确保跨环境的模式一致性，并支持 TypeScript/JavaScript 项目中的数据库表和列的创建或修改","ja":"Drizzle ORM を使用してデータベース スキーマを管理するエージェントを可能にし、移行優先の開発ワークフローで環境間のスキーマの一貫性を確保し、TypeScript/JavaScript プロジェクトでのデータベース テーブルと列の作成または変更をサポート","ko":"Drizzle ORM을 사용하여 데이터베이스 스키마를 관리하는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, 마이그레이션 우선 개발 워크플로를 통해 환경 간의 스키마 일관성을 보장하며, TypeScript/JavaScript 프로젝트에서 데이터베이스 테이블 및 열의 생성 또는 수정을 지원","es":"Habilita a los agentes a administrar el esquema de la base de datos utilizando un flujo de trabajo de desarrollo de migración con Drizzle ORM, garantizando la consistencia del esquema en todos los entornos con proyectos TypeScript/JavaScript y admitiendo la creación o modificación de tablas y columnas de la base de datos","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer le schéma de base de données en utilisant un flux de travail de développement de migration avec Drizzle ORM, assurant la cohérence du schéma dans tous les environnements avec des projets TypeScript/JavaScript et prenant en charge la création ou la modification de tables et de colonnes de base de données","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, das Datenbank-Schema mithilfe eines Migrations-First-Entwicklungs-Workflows mit Drizzle ORM zu verwalten, wodurch die Konsistenz des Schemas in allen Umgebungen mit TypeScript/JavaScript-Projekten gewährleistet wird und die Erstellung oder Modifizierung von Datenbank-Tabellen und -Spalten unterstützt wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar a schema do banco de dados usando um fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento baseado em migração com Drizzle ORM, garantindo a consistência da schema em diferentes ambientes com projetos TypeScript/JavaScript e suportando a criação ou modificação de tabelas e colunas de banco de dados","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять схемой базы данных, используя рабочий процесс разработки на основе миграции с Drizzle ORM, гарантируя согласованность схемы в различных средах с проектами TypeScript/JavaScript и поддерживая создание или изменение таблиц и столбцов базы данных","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من إدارة مخطط قاعدة البيانات باستخدام تدفق عمل تطوير قائم على الهجرة مع Drizzle ORM، مما يضمن συνέافية المخطط عبر بيئات مختلفة لمشاريع TypeScript/JavaScript، ودعم إنشاء أو تعديل جداول وأعمدة قاعدة البيانات"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating new database tables or columns with Drizzle ORM","Modifying existing database schema","Ensuring schema consistency across different environments"],"zh":["使用 Drizzle ORM 创建新数据库表或列","修改现有数据库模式","确保跨不同环境的模式一致性"],"ja":["Drizzle ORM を使用して新しいデータベース テーブルまたは列を作成","既存のデータベース スキーマを変更","異なる環境間のスキーマの一貫性を確保"],"ko":["Drizzle ORM을 사용하여 새로운 데이터베이스 테이블 또는 열을 생성","기존 데이터베이스 스키마를 수정","다른 환경 간의 스키마 일관성을 보장"],"es":["Crear nuevas tablas o columnas de base de datos con Drizzle ORM","Modificar el esquema de base de datos existente","Garantizar la consistencia del esquema en diferentes entornos"],"fr":["Créer de nouvelles tables ou colonnes de base de données avec Drizzle ORM","Modifier le schéma de base de données existant","Assurer la cohérence du schéma dans différents environnements"],"de":["Erstellen neuer Datenbank-Tabellen oder -Spalten mit Drizzle ORM","Ändern des bestehenden Datenbank-Schemas","Gewährleisten der Konsistenz des Schemas in verschiedenen Umgebungen"],"pt":["Criar novas tabelas ou colunas de banco de dados com Drizzle ORM","Modificar o esquema de banco de dados existente","Garantir a consistência do esquema em diferentes ambientes"],"ru":["Создание новых таблиц или столбцов базы данных с помощью Drizzle ORM","Модификация существующей схемы базы данных","Обеспечение согласованности схемы в различных средах"],"ar":["إنشاء جداول أو أعمدة جديدة لقاعدة البيانات مع Drizzle ORM","تعديل مخطط قاعدة البيانات الحالي","ضمان συνέافية المخطط عبر بيئات مختلفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Drizzle ORM setup in TypeScript/JavaScript project","Limited to TypeScript/JavaScript projects"],"zh":["需要在 TypeScript/JavaScript 项目中设置 Drizzle ORM","仅限于 TypeScript/JavaScript 项目"],"ja":["TypeScript/JavaScript プロジェクトで Drizzle ORM を設定する必要がある","TypeScript/JavaScript プロジェクトのみに限定"],"ko":["TypeScript/JavaScript 프로젝트에서 Drizzle ORM을 설정해야 함","TypeScript/JavaScript 프로젝트에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere la configuración de Drizzle ORM en el proyecto TypeScript/JavaScript","Limitado a proyectos TypeScript/JavaScript"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration de Drizzle ORM dans le projet TypeScript/JavaScript","Limité aux projets TypeScript/JavaScript"],"de":["Benötigt die Einrichtung von Drizzle ORM im TypeScript/JavaScript-Projekt","Begrenzt auf TypeScript/JavaScript-Projekte"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Drizzle ORM no projeto TypeScript/JavaScript","Limitado a projetos TypeScript/JavaScript"],"ru":["Требует настройки Drizzle ORM в проекте TypeScript/JavaScript","Ограничен проектами TypeScript/JavaScript"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد Drizzle ORM في مشروع TypeScript/JavaScript","محدود بمشاريع TypeScript/JavaScript"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z', '2026-02-18T12:56:26.619Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种通过找到根源原因来解决技术问题的方法，提高代码质量和调试效率。","ja":"体系的なデバッグは、根本原因を探ることで技術的な問題を解決する方法で、コード品質とデバッグ効率を向上させることができます。","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾는 방법으로 기술적인 문제를 해결하여 코드 품질과 디버깅 효율을 향상시킵니다.","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz, um technische Probleme zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen vorschlagen","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metódica para identificar e resolver problemas técnicos, garantindo que as soluções sejam eficazes e duradouras","ru":"Системная отладка - это методический подход к выявлению и решению технических проблем, гарантирующий, что решения будут эффективными и долговечными","ar":"التصحيح النمطي هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشاكل الفنية، مما يضمن أن الحلول تكون فعالة ومستدامة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统调试方法","ja":"体系的なデバッグ","ko":"시스템 디버깅 방법","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encontrar la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematische Fehlersuche: Die Ursache Finden","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка: найдите коренную причину","ar":"تصحيح نظامي: اكتشف السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种通过找到根源原因来解决技术问题的方法，提高代码质量和调试效率。","ja":"体系的なデバッグは、根本原因を探ることで技術的な問題を解決する方法で、コード品質とデバッグ効率を向上させることができます。","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾는 방법으로 기술적인 문제를 해결하여 코드 품질과 디버깅 효율을 향상시킵니다.","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de propos...","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz, um technische Probleme zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lös...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metódica para identificar e resolver problemas técnicos, garantindo que as soluções sejam eficazes e duradouras","ru":"Системная отладка - это методический подход к выявлению и решению технических проблем, гарантирующий, что решения будут эффективными и долговечными","ar":"التصحيح النمطي هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشاكل الفنية، مما يضمن أن الحلول تكون فعالة ومستدامة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["找到根源原因","提高代码质量","提高调试效率","解决技术问题","遵循铁律"],"ja":["根本原因を探る","コード品質を向上させる","デバッグ効率を向上させる","技術的な問題を解決する","鉄則に従う"],"ko":["근본 원인을 찾기","코드 품질 향상","디버깅 효율 향상","기술적인 문제 해결","철법 준수"],"es":["Identifica la causa raíz de los errores","Evita soluciones temporales","Optimiza el proceso de depuración","Reduce el tiempo de solución de problemas","Mejora la calidad del código"],"fr":["Identifie la cause profonde des erreurs","Évite les solutions temporaires","Optimise le processus de débogage","Réduit le temps de résolution des problèmes","Améliore la qualité du code"],"de":["Findet die Ursache von Fehlern","Vermeidet temporäre Lösungen","Optimiert den Fehlersuchprozess","Reduziert die Zeit zur Lösung von Problemen","Verbessert die Codequalität"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz dos problemas","Abordagem metódica para resolução de problemas","Garantia de soluções eficazes e duradouras","Redução do tempo de depuração","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Выявление коренной причины проблем","Методический подход к решению проблем","Гарантия эффективных и долговечных решений","Сокращение времени отладки","Улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري للمشاكل","نهج منهجي لمعالجة المشاكل","ضمان حلول فعالة ومستدامة","تقليل وقت التصحيح","تحسين جودة الشفرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","技术问题解决","代码质量","调试效率","根本原因","铁律"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグ","技術的な問題解決","コード品質","デバッグ効率","根本原因","鉄則"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술적인 문제 해결","코드 品質","디버깅 효율","근본 원인","철법"],"es":["depuración sistemática","causa raíz","solución de problemas","eficiencia","calidad del código","optimización","reducción de tiempo","mejora de la calidad"],"fr":["débogage systématique","cause profonde","résolution de problèmes","efficacité","qualité du code","optimisation","réduction de temps","amélioration de la qualité"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","Ursache","Fehlerbehebung","Effizienz","Codequalität","Optimierung","Zeitreduzierung","Qualitätsverbesserung"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","resolução de problemas","causa raiz","soluções eficazes","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade do código"],"ru":["системная отладка","решение проблем","коренная причина","эффективные решения","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода"],"ar":["التصحيح النمطي","حل المشاكل","السبب الجذري","حلول فعالة","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الشفرة"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:56:26.619Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Agents needing robust issue resolution through systematic debugging","zh":"非常适合需要通过系统化调试实现稳健问题解决的技术智能体","ja":"体系的なデバッグによる強固な問題解決を必要とするテクニカルエージェントに最適","ko":"체계적인 디버깅을 통해 강력한 문제 해결이 필요한 기술 에이전트에 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Técnicos que necesitan una resolución de problemas robusta a través de una depuración sistemática","fr":"Parfait pour les agents techniques ayant besoin d''une résolution de problèmes robuste par le biais d''un débogage systématique","de":"Perfekt für technische Agenten, die eine robuste Problemlösung durch systematische Fehlersuche benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Técnicos que necessitam de resolução robusta de problemas por meio de depuração sistemática","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов, которым необходима надежная решение проблем посредством системной отладки","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الفنيين الذين يحتاجون إلى حل قوي للمشكلات من خلال التصحيح المنهجي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify root causes of technical issues using the Iron Law, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, and providing a systematic approach to debugging test failures and bugs","zh":"赋能智能体运用铁律识别技术问题的根本原因，确保所有修复都建立在根本原因调查的基础上，并为调试测试失败和缺陷提供系统化方法","ja":"アイアンローア（鉄則）を使用して技術的問題の根本原因を特定し、根本原因調査なしに修正を行わないことを保証するとともに、テスト失敗やバグのデバッグに対する体系的なアプローチを提供する","ko":"아이언 법칙을 사용하여 기술적 문제의 근본 원인을 식별하고, 반드시 먼저 근본 원인 조사 후 수정을 보장하며, 테스트 실패와 버그 디버깅을 위한 체계적인 접근법을 제공함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar las causas raíz de los problemas técnicos utilizando la Ley de Hierro, asegurando NO HAY REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, y proporcionando un enfoque sistemático para depurar fallos de prueba y errores","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les causes profondes des problèmes techniques en utilisant la Loi de Fer, en garantissant AUCUNE CORRECTION SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, et en fournissant une approche systématique pour déboguer les échecs de test et les bogues","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Ursachen technischer Probleme mithilfe des Eisernen Gesetzes zu identifizieren, KEINE REPARIERUNG OHNE UNTERSUCHUNG DER URSACHE ERST und bietet einen systematischen Ansatz zur Fehlersuche bei Testfehlern und Fehlern","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar as causas raiz dos problemas técnicos usando a Lei de Ferro, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, e fornecendo uma abordagem sistemática para depurar falhas de teste e bugs","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять коренные причины технических проблем с помощью Железного закона, гарантируя НИКАКИХ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, и обеспечивая системный подход к отладке неисправностей тестирования и багов","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشكلات الفنية باستخدام قانون الحديد، مما يضمن عدم وجود إصلاحات بدون تحقيق في السبب الجذري أولاً، وتوفير نهج منهجي لتصحيح اختبارات الفشل والعيوب"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging test failures","Identifying root causes of bugs","Implementing systematic debugging protocols"],"zh":["调试测试失败","识别缺陷的根本原因","实施系统化调试协议"],"ja":["テスト失敗のデバッグ","バグの根本原因の特定","体系的なデバッグプロトコルの実装"],"ko":["테스트 실패 디버깅","버그의 근본 원인 식별","체계적인 디버깅 프로토콜 구현"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba","Identificación de causas raíz de errores","Implementación de protocolos de depuración sistemática"],"fr":["Débogage des échecs de test","Identification des causes profondes des bogues","Mise en œuvre de protocoles de débogage systématique"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei Testfehlern","Identifizierung der Ursachen von Fehlern","Implementierung systematischer Fehlersuchprotokolle"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste","Identificação de causas raiz de bugs","Implementação de protocolos de depuração sistemáticos"],"ru":["Отладка неисправностей тестирования","Выявление коренных причин багов","Реализация системных протоколов отладки"],"ar":["تصحيح اختبارات الفشل","تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للعيوب","تنفيذ بروتوكولات تصحيح منهجية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the process is violating the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要严格遵守铁律","违反流程字面要求即违背调试精神"],"ja":["アイアンローア（鉄則）への遵守が必要","プロセスの条文に違反することはデバッグの精神に違反することを意味する"],"ko":["아이언 법칙을 엄격히 준수해야 함","프로세스의 글자를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것임"],"es":["Requiere adherencia a la Ley de Hierro","Violación de la letra del proceso es violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à la Loi de Fer","La violation de la lettre du processus est une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes","Verletzung des Wortlautes des Prozesses ist eine Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige aderência à Lei de Ferro","Violar a letra do processo é violar o espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения Железного закона","Нарушение буквы процесса является нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بقانون الحديد","مخالفة حرفية العملية هي مخالفة روح التصحيح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
