on REST- und GraphQL-APIs","Authentifizierung OAuth2 und soziales Login","Rollenbasierte Zugriffskontrolle (RBAC)","Sitzungsverwaltung und Migration von Authentifizierungssystemen"],"pt":["Implementação de sistemas de autenticação de usuário","Proteção de APIs REST e GraphQL","Adição de login OAuth2 e social","Implementação de controle de acesso baseado em papéis","Gerenciamento de sessões"],"ru":["Реализация систем аутентификации пользователей","Защита API REST и GraphQL","Добавление входа OAuth2 и социального входа","Реализация контроля доступа на основе ролей","Управление сессиями"],"ar":["تنفيذ أنظمة مصادقة المستخدم","حماية واجهات برمجة التطبيقات REST وGraphQL","إضافة تسجيل الدخول OAuth2 والاجتماعي","تنفيذ التحكم في الوصول بالاعتماد على الأدوار","إدارة الجلسات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["身份验证","授权","安全","可扩展","行业标准","现代最佳实践","用户身份验证","REST API","GraphQL API","OAuth2"],"ja":["認証","認可","セキュリティ","スケーラブル","業界標準","モダンなベストプラクティス","ユーザー認証","REST API","GraphQL API","OAuth2"],"ko":["인증","인가","보안","확장성","산업 표준","현대 모범 사례","사용자 인증","REST API","GraphQL API","OAuth2"],"es":["patrones de autenticación","autenticación y autorización","seguridad de API","OAuth2","inicio de sesión social","control de acceso basado en roles","gestión de sesiones","migración de sistemas de autenticación"],"fr":["modèles d''authentification","authentification et autorisation","sécurité des API","OAuth2","connexion sociale","contrôle d''accès basé sur les rôles","gestion de sessions","migration de systèmes d''authentification"],"de":["Authentifizierungsmuster","Authentifizierung und Autorisierung","API-Sicherheit","OAuth2","soziales Login","rollenbasierte Zugriffskontrolle","Sitzungsverwaltung","Migration von Authentifizierungssystemen"],"pt":["autenticação e autorização","padrões de implementação","segurança de sistemas","API REST","API GraphQL","OAuth2","login social","controle de acesso"],"ru":["аутентификация и авторизация","шаблоны реализации","безопасность систем","API REST","API GraphQL","OAuth2","социальный вход","контроль доступа"],"ar":["المصادقة والتفويض","أنماط التنفيذ","أمن الأنظمة","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GraphQL","OAuth2","تسجيل الدخول الاجتماعي","التحكم في الوصول"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"auth-implementation-patterns","description":"Master authentication and authorization patterns including JWT, OAuth2, session management, and RBAC to build secure, scalable access control systems. Use when implementing auth systems, securing APIs, or debugging security issues.","bodyPreview":"# Authentication & Authorization Implementation Patterns\n\nBuild secure, scalable authentication and authorization systems using industry-standard patterns and modern best practices.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Implementing user authentication systems\n- Securing REST or GraphQL APIs\n- Adding OAuth2/social login\n- Implementing role-based access control (RBAC)\n- Designing session management\n- Migrating authentication systems\n- Debugging auth issues\n- Implementing SSO or multi-tenancy\n\n## Core Con","body":"# Authentication & Authorization Implementation Patterns\n\nBuild secure, scalable authentication and authorization systems using industry-standard patterns and modern best practices.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Implementing user authentication systems\n- Securing REST or GraphQL APIs\n- Adding OAuth2/social login\n- Implementing role-based access control (RBAC)\n- Designing session management\n- Migrating authentication systems\n- Debugging auth issues\n- Implementing SSO or multi-tenancy\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Authentication vs Authorization\n\n**Authentication (AuthN)**: Who are you?\n- Verifying identity (username/password, OAuth, biometrics)\n- Issuing credentials (sessions, tokens)\n- Managing login/logout\n\n**Authorization (AuthZ)**: What can you do?\n- Permission checking\n- Role-based access control (RBAC)\n- Resource ownership validation\n- Policy enforcement\n\n### 2. Authentication Strategies\n\n**Session-Based:**\n- Server stores session state\n- Session ID in cookie\n- Traditional, simple, stateful\n\n**Token-Based (JWT):**\n- Stateless, self-contained\n- Scales horizontally\n- Can store claims\n\n**OAuth2/OpenID Connect:**\n- Delegate authentication\n- Social login (Google, GitHub)\n- Enterprise SSO\n\n## JWT Authentication\n\n### Pattern 1: JWT Implementation\n\n```typescript\n// JWT structure: header.payload.signature\nimport jwt from ''jsonwebtoken'';\nimport { Request, Response, NextFunction } from ''express'';\n\ninterface JWTPayload {\n    userId: string;\n    email: string;\n    role: string;\n    iat: number;\n    exp: number;\n}\n\n// Generate JWT\nfunction generateTokens(userId: string, email: string, role: string) {\n    const accessToken = jwt.sign(\n        { userId, email, role },\n        process.env.JWT_SECRET!,\n        { expiresIn: ''15m'' }  // Short-lived\n    );\n\n    const refreshToken = jwt.sign(\n        { userId },\n        process.env.JWT_REFRESH_SECRET!,\n        { expiresIn: ''7d'' }  // Long-lived\n    );\n\n    return { accessToken, refreshToken };\n}\n\n// Verify JWT\nfunction verifyToken(token: string): JWTPayload {\n    try {\n        return jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET!) as JWTPayload;\n    } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof jwt.TokenExpiredError) {\n            throw new Error(''Token expired'');\n        }\n        if (error instanceof jwt.JsonWebTokenError) {\n            throw new Error(''Invalid token'');\n        }\n        throw error;\n    }\n}\n\n// Middleware\nfunction authenticate(req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) {\n    const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;\n    if (!authHeader?.startsWith(''Bearer '')) {\n        return res.status(401).json({ error: ''No token provided'' });\n    }\n\n    const token = authHeader.substring(7);\n    try {\n        const payload = verifyToken(token);\n        req.user = payload;  // Attach user to request\n        next();\n    } catch (error) {\n        return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Invalid token'' });\n    }\n}\n\n// Usage\napp.get(''/api/profile'', authenticate, (req, res) => {\n    res.json({ user: req.user });\n});\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Refresh Token Flow\n\n```typescript\ninterface StoredRefreshToken {\n    token: string;\n    userId: string;\n    expiresAt: Date;\n    createdAt: Date;\n}\n\nclass RefreshTokenService {\n    // Store refresh token in database\n    async storeRefreshToken(userId: string, refreshToken: string) {\n        const expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);\n        await db.refreshTokens.create({\n            token: await hash(refreshToken),  // Hash before storing\n            userId,\n            expiresAt,\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Refresh access token\n    async refreshAccessToken(refreshToken: string) {\n        // Verify refresh token\n        let payload;\n        try {\n            payload = jwt.verify(\n                refreshToken,\n                process.env.JWT_REFRESH_SECRET!\n            ) as { userId: string };\n        } catch {\n            throw new Error(''Invalid refresh token'');\n        }\n\n        // Check if token exists in database\n        const storedToken = await db.refreshTokens.findOne({\n            where: {\n                token: await hash(refreshToken),\n                userId: payload.userId,\n                expiresAt: { $gt: new Date() },\n            },\n        });\n\n        if (!storedToken) {\n            throw new Error(''Refresh token not found or expired'');\n        }\n\n        // Get user\n        const user = await db.users.findById(payload.userId);\n        if (!user) {\n            throw new Error(''User not found'');\n        }\n\n        // Generate new access token\n        const accessToken = jwt.sign(\n            { userId: user.id, email: user.email, role: user.role },\n            process.env.JWT_SECRET!,\n            { expiresIn: ''15m'' }\n        );\n\n        return { accessToken };\n    }\n\n    // Revoke refresh token (logout)\n    async revokeRefreshToken(refreshToken: string) {\n        await db.refreshTokens.deleteOne({\n            token: await hash(refreshToken),\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Revoke all user tokens (logout all devices)\n    async revokeAllUserTokens(userId: string) {\n        await db.refreshTokens.deleteMany({ userId });\n    }\n}\n\n// API endpoints\napp.post(''/api/auth/refresh'', async (req, res) => {\n    const { refreshToken } = req.body;\n    try {\n        const { accessToken } = await refreshTokenService\n            .refreshAccessToken(refreshToken);\n        res.json({ accessToken });\n    } catch (error) {\n        res.status(401).json({ error: ''Invalid refresh token'' });\n    }\n});\n\napp.post(''/api/auth/logout'', authenticate, async (req, res) => {\n    const { refreshToken } = req.body;\n    await refreshTokenService.revokeRefreshToken(refreshToken);\n    res.json({ message: ''Logged out successfully'' });\n});\n```\n\n## Session-Based Authentication\n\n### Pattern 1: Express Session\n\n```typescript\nimport session from ''express-session'';\nimport RedisStore from ''connect-redis'';\nimport { createClient } from ''redis'';\n\n// Setup Redis for session storage\nconst redisClient = createClient({\n    url: process.env.REDIS_URL,\n});\nawait redisClient.connect();\n\napp.use(\n    session({\n        store: new RedisStore({ client: redisClient }),\n        secret: process.env.SESSION_SECRET!,\n        resave: false,\n        saveUninitialized: false,\n        cookie: {\n            secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === ''production'',  // HTTPS only\n            httpOnly: true,  // No JavaScript access\n            maxAge: 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000,  // 24 hours\n            sameSite: ''strict'',  // CSRF protection\n        },\n    })\n);\n\n// Login\napp.post(''/api/auth/login'', async (req, res) => {\n    const { email, password } = req.body;\n\n    const user = await db.users.findOne({ email });\n    if (!user || !(await verifyPassword(password, user.passwordHash))) {\n        return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Invalid credentials'' });\n    }\n\n    // Store user in session\n    req.session.userId = user.id;\n    req.session.role = user.role;\n\n    res.json({ user: { id: user.id, email: user.email, role: user.role } });\n});\n\n// Session middleware\nfunction requireAuth(req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) {\n    if (!req.session.userId) {\n        return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Not authenticated'' });\n    }\n    next();\n}\n\n// Protected route\napp.get(''/api/profile'', requireAuth, async (req, res) => {\n    const user = await db.users.findById(req.session.userId);\n    res.json({ user });\n});\n\n// Logout\napp.post(''/api/auth/logout'', (req, res) => {\n    req.session.destroy((err) => {\n        if (err) {\n            return res.status(500).json({ error: ''Logout failed'' });\n        }\n        res.clearCookie(''connect.sid'');\n        res.json({ message: ''Logged out successfully'' });\n    });\n});\n```\n\n## OAuth2 / Social Login\n\n### Pattern 1: OAuth2 with Passport.js\n\n```typescript\nimport passport from ''passport'';\nimport { Strategy as GoogleStrategy } from ''passport-google-oauth20'';\nimport { Strategy as GitHubStrategy } from ''passport-github2'';\n\n// Google OAuth\npassport.use(\n    new GoogleStrategy(\n        {\n            clientID: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID!,\n            clientSecret: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET!,\n            callbackURL: ''/api/auth/google/callback'',\n        },\n        async (accessToken, refreshToken, profile, done) => {\n            try {\n                // Find or create user\n                let user = await db.users.findOne({\n                    googleId: profile.id,\n                });\n\n                if (!user) {\n                    user = await db.users.create({\n                        googleId: profile.id,\n                        email: profile.emails?.[0]?.value,\n                        name: profile.displayName,\n                        avatar: profile.photos?.[0]?.value,\n                    });\n                }\n\n                return done(null, user);\n            } catch (error) {\n                return done(error, undefined);\n            }\n        }\n    )\n);\n\n// Routes\napp.get(''/api/auth/google'', passport.authenticate(''google'', {\n    scope: [''profile'', ''email''],\n}));\n\napp.get(\n    ''/api/auth/google/callback'',\n    passport.authenticate(''google'', { session: false }),\n    (req, res) => {\n        // Generate JWT\n        const tokens = generateTokens(req.user.id, req.user.email, req.user.role);\n        // Redirect to frontend with token\n        res.redirect(`${process.env.FRONTEND_URL}/auth/callback?token=${tokens.accessToken}`);\n    }\n);\n```\n\n## Authorization Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n\n```typescript\nenum Role {\n    USER = ''user'',\n    MODERATOR = ''moderator'',\n    ADMIN = ''admin'',\n}\n\nconst roleHierarchy: Record<Role, Role[]> = {\n    [Role.ADMIN]: [Role.ADMIN, Role.MODERATOR, Role.USER],\n    [Role.MODERATOR]: [Role.MODERATOR, Role.USER],\n    [Role.USER]: [Role.USER],\n};\n\nfunction hasRole(userRole: Role, requiredRole: Role): boolean {\n    return roleHierarchy[userRole].includes(requiredRole);\n}\n\n// Middleware\nfunction requireRole(...roles: Role[]) {\n    return (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n        if (!req.user) {\n            return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Not authenticated'' });\n        }\n\n        if (!roles.some(role => hasRole(req.user.role, role))) {\n            return res.status(403).json({ error: ''Insufficient permissions'' });\n        }\n\n        next();\n    };\n}\n\n// Usage\napp.delete(''/api/users/:id'',\n    authenticate,\n    requireRole(Role.ADMIN),\n    async (req, res) => {\n        // Only admins can delete users\n        await db.users.delete(req.params.id);\n        res.json({ message: ''User deleted'' });\n    }\n);\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Permission-Based Access Control\n\n```typescript\nenum Permission {\n    READ_USERS = ''read:users'',\n    WRITE_USERS = ''write:users'',\n    DELETE_USERS = ''delete:users'',\n    READ_POSTS = ''read:posts'',\n    WRITE_POSTS = ''write:posts'',\n}\n\nconst rolePermissions: Record<Role, Permission[]> = {\n    [Role.USER]: [Permission.READ_POSTS, Permission.WRITE_POSTS],\n    [Role.MODERATOR]: [\n        Permission.READ_POSTS,\n        Permission.WRITE_POSTS,\n        Permission.READ_USERS,\n    ],\n    [Role.ADMIN]: Object.values(Permission),\n};\n\nfunction hasPermission(userRole: Role, permission: Permission): boolean {\n    return rolePermissions[userRole]?.includes(permission) ?? false;\n}\n\nfunction requirePermission(...permissions: Permission[]) {\n    return (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n        if (!req.user) {\n            return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Not authenticated'' });\n        }\n\n        const hasAllPermissions = permissions.every(permission =>\n            hasPermission(req.user.role, permission)\n        );\n\n        if (!hasAllPermissions) {\n            return res.status(403).json({ error: ''Insufficient permissions'' });\n        }\n\n        next();\n    };\n}\n\n// Usage\napp.get(''/api/users'',\n    authenticate,\n    requirePermission(Permission.READ_USERS),\n    async (req, res) => {\n        const users = await db.users.findAll();\n        res.json({ users });\n    }\n);\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Resource Ownership\n\n```typescript\n// Check if user owns resource\nasync function requireOwnership(\n    resourceType: ''post'' | ''comment'',\n    resourceIdParam: string = ''id''\n) {\n    return async (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n        if (!req.user) {\n            return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Not authenticated'' });\n        }\n\n        const resourceId = req.params[resourceIdParam];\n\n        // Admins can access anything\n        if (req.user.role === Role.ADMIN) {\n            return next();\n        }\n\n        // Check ownership\n        let resource;\n        if (resourceType === ''post'') {\n            resource = await db.posts.findById(resourceId);\n        } else if (resourceType === ''comment'') {\n            resource = await db.comments.findById(resourceId);\n        }\n\n        if (!resource) {\n            return res.status(404).json({ error: ''Resource not found'' });\n        }\n\n        if (resource.userId !== req.user.userId) {\n            return res.status(403).json({ error: ''Not authorized'' });\n        }\n\n        next();\n    };\n}\n\n// Usage\napp.put(''/api/posts/:id'',\n    authenticate,\n    requireOwnership(''post''),\n    async (req, res) => {\n        // User can only update their own posts\n        const post = await db.posts.update(req.params.id, req.body);\n        res.json({ post });\n    }\n);\n```\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\n### Pattern 1: Password Security\n\n```typescript\nimport bcrypt from ''bcrypt'';\nimport { z } from ''zod'';\n\n// Password validation schema\nconst passwordSchema = z.string()\n    .min(12, ''Password must be at least 12 characters'')\n    .regex(/[A-Z]/, ''Password must contain uppercase letter'')\n    .regex(/[a-z]/, ''Password must contain lowercase letter'')\n    .regex(/[0-9]/, ''Password must contain number'')\n    .regex(/[^A-Za-z0-9]/, ''Password must contain special character'');\n\n// Hash password\nasync function hashPassword(password: string): Promise<string> {\n    const saltRounds = 12;  // 2^12 iterations\n    return bcrypt.hash(password, saltRounds);\n}\n\n// Verify password\nasync function verifyPassword(\n    password: string,\n    hash: string\n): Promise<boolean> {\n    return bcrypt.compare(password, hash);\n}\n\n// Registration with password validation\napp.post(''/api/auth/register'', async (req, res) => {\n    try {\n        const { email, password } = req.body;\n\n        // Validate password\n        passwordSchema.parse(password);\n\n        // Check if user exists\n        const existingUser = await db.users.findOne({ email });\n        if (existingUser) {\n            return res.status(400).json({ error: ''Email already registered'' });\n        }\n\n        // Hash password\n        const passwordHash = await hashPassword(password);\n\n        // Create user\n        const user = await db.users.create({\n            email,\n            passwordHash,\n        });\n\n        // Generate tokens\n        const tokens = generateTokens(user.id, user.email, user.role);\n\n        res.status(201).json({\n            user: { id: user.id, email: user.email },\n            ...tokens,\n        });\n    } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof z.ZodError) {\n            return res.status(400).json({ error: error.errors[0].message });\n        }\n        res.status(500).json({ error: ''Registration failed'' });\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Rate Limiting\n\n```typescript\nimport rateLimit from ''express-rate-limit'';\nimport RedisStore from ''rate-limit-redis'';\n\n// Login rate limiter\nconst loginLimiter = rateLimit({\n    store: new RedisStore({ client: redisClient }),\n    windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,  // 15 minutes\n    max: 5,  // 5 attempts\n    message: ''Too many login attempts, please try again later'',\n    standardHeaders: true,\n    legacyHeaders: false,\n});\n\n// API rate limiter\nconst apiLimiter = rateLimit({\n    windowMs: 60 * 1000,  // 1 minute\n    max: 100,  // 100 requests per minute\n    standardHeaders: true,\n});\n\n// Apply to routes\napp.post(''/api/auth/login'', loginLimiter, async (req, res) => {\n    // Login logic\n});\n\napp.use(''/api/'', apiLimiter);\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Never Store Plain Passwords**: Always hash with bcrypt/argon2\n2. **Use HTTPS**: Encrypt data in transit\n3. **Short-Lived Access Tokens**: 15-30 minutes max\n4. **Secure Cookies**: httpOnly, secure, sameSite flags\n5. **Validate All Input**: Email format, password strength\n6. **Rate Limit Auth Endpoints**: Prevent brute force attacks\n7. **Implement CSRF Protection**: For session-based auth\n8. **Rotate Secrets Regularly**: JWT secrets, session secrets\n9. **Log Security Events**: Login attempts, failed auth\n10. **Use MFA When Possible**: Extra security layer\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Weak Passwords**: Enforce strong password policies\n- **JWT in localStorage**: Vulnerable to XSS, use httpOnly cookies\n- **No Token Expiration**: Tokens should expire\n- **Client-Side Auth Checks Only**: Always validate server-side\n- **Insecure Password Reset**: Use secure tokens with expiration\n- **No Rate Limiting**: Vulnerable to brute force\n- **Trusting Client Data**: Always validate on server\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/jwt-best-practices.md**: JWT implementation guide\n- **references/oauth2-flows.md**: OAuth2 flow diagrams and examples\n- **references/session-security.md**: Secure session management\n- **assets/auth-security-checklist.md**: Security review checklist\n- **assets/password-policy-template.md**: Password requirements template\n- **scripts/token-validator.ts**: JWT validation utility\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:56:27.903Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Security Agents implementing enterprise-grade authentication systems.","zh":"适用于实现企业级身份验证系统的安全代理。","ja":"エンタープライズグレードの認証システムを実装するセキュリティエージェントに不可欠です。","ko":"기업급 인증 시스템을 구현하는 보안 에이전트에 필수입니다.","es":"Esencial para Agentes de Seguridad que implementan sistemas de autenticación de grado empresarial.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents de Sécurité mettant en œuvre des systèmes d''authentification de niveau entreprise.","de":"Essenziell für Sicherheitsagenten, die Unternehmensklasse-Authentifizierungssysteme implementieren.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Segurança que implementam sistemas de autenticação de nível empresarial.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов безопасности, реализующих системы аутентификации класса предприятия.","ar":"ضروري لوكلاء الأمان الذين ينفذون أنظمة المصادقة على مستوى المؤسسة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables implementation of OAuth2 flows, JWT token validation, and RBAC policies for securing REST/GraphQL APIs. Provides patterns for session management, SSO integration, and multi-tenant authorization architectures.","zh":"实现OAuth2流程、JWT令牌验证和RBAC策略以保护REST/GraphQL API。为会话管理、SSO集成和多租户授权架构提供模式。","ja":"REST/GraphQL APIを保護するためにOAuth2フロー、JWTトークン検証、RBACポリシーを実装します。セッション管理、SSO統合、多テナント認証アーキテクチャのパターンを提供します。","ko":"REST/GraphQL API를 보호하기 위해 OAuth2 흐름, JWT 토큰 유효성 검사, RBAC 정책을 구현합니다. 세션 관리, SSO 통합, 다중 테넌트 인증 아키텍처를 위한 패턴을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite la implementación de flujos OAuth2, validación de tokens JWT y políticas RBAC para proteger las API REST/GraphQL. Proporciona patrones para la gestión de sesiones, integración de SSO y arquitecturas de autorización multiinquilino.","fr":"Permet la mise en œuvre des flux OAuth2, de la validation des jetons JWT et des politiques RBAC pour sécuriser les API REST/GraphQL. Fournit des modèles pour la gestion de session, l''intégration SSO et les architectures d''autorisation multi-locataires.","de":"Ermöglicht die Implementierung von OAuth2-Flüssen, die Validierung von JWT-Tokens und RBAC-Richtlinien zur Absicherung von REST/GraphQL-APIs. Bietet Muster für Sitzungsverwaltung, SSO-Integration und Multi-Tenant-Autorisierungsarchitekturen.","pt":"Permite a implementação de fluxos OAuth2, validação de token JWT e políticas RBAC para proteger APIs REST/GraphQL. Fornece padrões para gerenciamento de sessão, integração SSO e arquiteturas de autorização multi-locatário.","ru":"Позволяет реализовать потоки OAuth2, проверку токенов JWT и политики RBAC для защиты API REST/GraphQL. Предоставляет шаблоны для управления сессиями, интеграции SSO и многоарендаторных архитектур авторизации.","ar":"يسمح بتنفيذ تدفقات OAuth2 وتصديق رمز JWT وسياسات RBAC لحماية واجهات برمجة التطبيقات REST/GraphQL. يوفر أنماطًا لإدارة الجلسات وتكامل SSO وعمارة التأثير المتعددة المستأجرين."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing social login integrations","Securing REST/GraphQL API endpoints","Debugging authentication token issues","Migrating legacy auth systems","Designing role-based access control policies"],"zh":["实现社交登录集成","保护REST/GraphQL API端点","调试身份验证令牌问题","迁移遗留身份验证系统","设计基于角色的访问控制策略"],"ja":["ソーシャルログイン統合の実装","REST/GraphQL APIエンドポイントの保護","認証トークンの問題のデバッグ","レガシーアウセンスシステムの移行","ロールベースのアクセス制御ポリシーの設計"],"ko":["소셜 로그인 통합 구현","REST/GraphQL API 엔드포인트 보호","인증 토큰 문제 디버깅","레거시 인증 시스템 마이그레이션","역할 기반 접근 제어 정책 설계"],"es":["Implementar integraciones de inicio de sesión social","Proteger endpoints de API REST/GraphQL","Depurar problemas de tokens de autenticación","Migrar sistemas de autenticación heredados","Diseñar políticas de control de acceso basado en roles"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des intégrations de connexion sociale","Sécuriser les points de terminaison d''API REST/GraphQL","Déboguer les problèmes de jetons d''authentification","Migrer des systèmes d''authentification hérités","Concevoir des politiques de contrôle d''accès basé sur les rôles"],"de":["Implementierung von Social-Login-Integrationen","Absichern von REST/GraphQL-API-Endpunkten","Debugging von Authentifizierungstoken-Problemen","Migration von Legacy-Authentifizierungssystemen","Entwicklung von Richtlinien für rollenbasierten Zugriff"],"pt":["Implementar integrações de login social","Proteger pontos de extremidade de API REST/GraphQL","Depurar problemas de token de autenticação","Migrar sistemas de autenticação legados","Projetar políticas de controle de acesso baseadas em função"],"ru":["Реализовать интеграцию социального логина","Защитить конечные точки API REST/GraphQL","Отладить проблемы с токеном аутентификации","Мигрировать устаревшие системы аутентификации","Спроектировать политики контроля доступа на основе ролей"],"ar":["تنفيذ تكاملات تسجيل الدخول الاجتماعي","أمان نهاية نقطة واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST/GraphQL","تصحيح أخطاء/problems رموز المصادقة","نقل أنظمة المصادقة القديمة","تصميم سياسات التحكم في الوصول المستندة إلى الدور"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of security protocols","Needs backend infrastructure access","Implementation specific to application framework"],"zh":["需要了解安全协议","需要后端基础设施访问","实现特定于应用程序框架"],"ja":["セキュリティプロトコルの理解が必要","バックエンドインフラストラクチャへのアクセスが必要","実装はアプリケーションフレームワークに特有"],"ko":["보안 프로토콜에 대한 이해가 필요함","백엔드 인프라스트럭처에 대한 접근 권한이 필요함","구현은 애플리케이션 프레임워크에 특정"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de protocolos de seguridad","Necesita acceso a la infraestructura de backend","Implementación específica del framework de aplicación"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des protocoles de sécurité","Requiert un accès à l''infrastructure backend","Mise en œuvre spécifique au framework d''application"],"de":["Erfordert ein Verständnis von Sicherheitsprotokollen","Benötigt Zugriff auf die Backend-Infrastruktur","Implementierung ist an das Anwendungsframework gebunden"],"pt":["Requer entendimento de protocolos de segurança","Necessita acesso à infraestrutura de backend","Implementação específica do framework de aplicação"],"ru":["Требует понимания протоколов безопасности","Требует доступа к бэкэнд-инфраструктуре","Реализация специфична для фреймворка приложения"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم بروتوكولات الأمان","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى البنية التحتية للخلفية","تنفيذ محدد لإطار العمل للتطبيق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit/receiving-code-review', 'community', 'dwalleck', 'kiro-starter-kit', 'dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit', 'receiving-code-review', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z', '2026-02-18T12:56:53.442Z', NULL, '{"id":"dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit/receiving-code-review","name":"receiving-code-review","description":{"zh":"代码审查是一种技术性评估，需要遵循特定的原则和步骤来确保代码质量","ja":"コードレビューは技術的な評価であり、コード品質を確保するために特定の原則と手順に従う必要があります","ko":"코드 리뷰는 기술적인 평가로 코드 품질을 보장하기 위해 특정 원칙과 단계를 따라야 합니다","es":"La recepción de revisión de código es un proceso técnico que requiere evaluación y verificación para garantizar la calidad del código","fr":"La réception de la revue de code est un processus technique qui nécessite une évaluation et une vérification pour garantir la qualité du code","de":"Der Erhalt von Code-Reviews ist ein technischer Prozess, der eine Bewertung und Überprüfung erfordert, um die Code-Qualität zu gewährleisten","pt":"Receber revisão de código é um processo técnico que exige avaliação e verificação, melhorando a qualidade do código","ru":"Получение код-ревью - это технический процесс, требующий оценки и верификации, для улучшения качества кода","ar":"استلام مراجعة الكود هو عملية تقنية تتطلب تقييمًا وتنقيحًا لتحسين جودة الكود","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查接收技巧","ja":"コードレビュー受け入れスキル","ko":"코드 리뷰 수신 기술","es":"Recepción de revisión de código","fr":"Réception de la revue de code","de":"Erhalt von Code-Review","pt":"Receba Revisão de Código com Eficiência","ru":"Эффективное Получение Код-Ревью","ar":"استلام مراجعة الكود بفعالية","en":"receiving-code-review"},"description":{"zh":"代码审查是一种技术性评估，需要遵循特定的原则和步骤来确保代码质量","ja":"コードレビューは技術的な評価であり、コード品質を確保するために特定の原則と手順に従う必要があります","ko":"코드 리뷰는 기술적인 평가로 코드 품질을 보장하기 위해 특정 원칙과 단계를 따라야 합니다","es":"La recepción de revisión de código es un proceso técnico que requiere evaluación y verificación para garantizar la calidad del código","fr":"La réception de la revue de code est un processus technique qui nécessite une évaluation et une vérification pour garantir la qualité du code","de":"Der Erhalt von Code-Reviews ist ein technischer Prozess, der eine Bewertung und Überprüfung erfordert, um die Code-Qualität zu gewährleisten","pt":"Receber revisão de código é um processo técnico que exige avaliação e verificação, melhorando a qualidade do código","ru":"Получение код-ревью - это технический процесс, требующий оценки и верификации, для улучшения качества кода","ar":"استلام مراجعة الكود هو عملية تقنية تتطلب تقييمًا وتنقيحًا لتحسين جودة الكود","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["遵循特定的代码审查原则","技术性评估和验证","改进代码质量和团队协作","增强代码安全性和稳定性","减少代码错误和漏洞"],"ja":["特定のコードレビュー原則に従う","技術的な評価と検証","コード品質とチームコラボレーションの向上","コードセキュリティと安定性の強化","コードエラーと脆弱性の減少"],"ko":["특정 코드 리뷰 원칙을 따름","기술적인 평가 및 검증","코드 품질 및 팀 협력의 향상","코드 보안 및 안정性的 강화","코드 오류 및 취약점의 감소"],"es":["Evaluación técnica de cambios de código","Verificación de requisitos","Análisis de la solución","Respuesta constructiva a la revisión","Mejora de la calidad del código"],"fr":["Évaluation technique des modifications de code","Vérification des exigences","Analyse de la solution","Réponse constructive à la revue","Amélioration de la qualité du code"],"de":["Technische Bewertung von Code-Änderungen","Überprüfung von Anforderungen","Analyse der Lösung","Konstruktive Antwort auf die Überprüfung","Verbesserung der Code-Qualität"],"pt":["Leitura completa da revisão","Verificação da exigência","Verificação contra a realidade do código","Avaliação técnica","Resposta técnica"],"ru":["Полное чтение ревью","Проверка требований","Проверка против реальности кода","Техническая оценка","Технический ответ"],"ar":["قراءة كاملة لمراجعة الكود","التحقق من المتطلبات","التحقق ضد واقعية الكود","التقييم الفني","الجواب الفني"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码质量","团队协作","技术性评估","代码安全性","代码稳定性","代码错误","代码漏洞"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード品質","チームコラボレーション","技術的な評価","コードセキュリティ","コード安定性","コードエラー","コード脆弱性"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 품질","팀 협력","기술적인 평가","코드 보안","코드 안정성","코드 오류","코드 취약점"],"es":["revisión de código","evaluación técnica","verificación de requisitos","análisis de código","mejora de la calidad","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["revue de code","évaluation technique","vérification des exigences","analyse de code","amélioration de la qualité","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["Code-Review","technische Bewertung","Überprüfung von Anforderungen","Code-Analyse","Qualitätsverbesserung","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen"],"pt":["revisão de código","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade de código","eficiência de código","receber revisão de código","melhorar código"],"ru":["код-ревью","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","эффективность кода","получение код-ревью","улучшение кода"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود","فعالية الكود","استلام مراجعة الكود","تحسين الكود"]}},"owner":"dwalleck","repo":"kiro-starter-kit","repoPath":"dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"receiving-code-review","description":"Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response Pattern\n\n```\nWHEN receiving code review feedback:\n\n1. READ: Complete feedback without reacting\n2. UNDERSTAND: Restate requirement in own words (or ask)\n3. VERIFY: Check against codebase reality\n4. EVALUATE: Technically sound for THIS codebase?\n5. RESPOND: Techni","body":"# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response Pattern\n\n```\nWHEN receiving code review feedback:\n\n1. READ: Complete feedback without reacting\n2. UNDERSTAND: Restate requirement in own words (or ask)\n3. VERIFY: Check against codebase reality\n4. EVALUATE: Technically sound for THIS codebase?\n5. RESPOND: Technical acknowledgment or reasoned pushback\n6. IMPLEMENT: One item at a time, test each\n```\n\n## Forbidden Responses\n\n**NEVER:**\n- \"You''re absolutely right!\" (explicit AGENTS.md violation)\n- \"Great point!\" / \"Excellent feedback!\" (performative)\n- \"Let me implement that now\" (before verification)\n\n**INSTEAD:**\n- Restate the technical requirement\n- Ask clarifying questions\n- Push back with technical reasoning if wrong\n- Just start working (actions > words)\n\n## Handling Unclear Feedback\n\n```\nIF any item is unclear:\n  STOP - do not implement anything yet\n  ASK for clarification on unclear items\n\nWHY: Items may be related. Partial understanding = wrong implementation.\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n\n❌ WRONG: Implement 1,2,3,6 now, ask about 4,5 later\n✅ RIGHT: \"I understand items 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before proceeding.\"\n```\n\n## Source-Specific Handling\n\n### From your human partner\n- **Trusted** - implement after understanding\n- **Still ask** if scope unclear\n- **No performative agreement**\n- **Skip to action** or technical acknowledgment\n\n### From External Reviewers\n```\nBEFORE implementing:\n  1. Check: Technically correct for THIS codebase?\n  2. Check: Breaks existing functionality?\n  3. Check: Reason for current implementation?\n  4. Check: Works on all platforms/versions?\n  5. Check: Does reviewer understand full context?\n\nIF suggestion seems wrong:\n  Push back with technical reasoning\n\nIF can''t easily verify:\n  Say so: \"I can''t verify this without [X]. Should I [investigate/ask/proceed]?\"\n\nIF conflicts with your human partner''s prior decisions:\n  Stop and discuss with your human partner first\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"External feedback - be skeptical, but check carefully\"\n\n## YAGNI Check for \"Professional\" Features\n\n```\nIF reviewer suggests \"implementing properly\":\n  grep codebase for actual usage\n\n  IF unused: \"This endpoint isn''t called. Remove it (YAGNI)?\"\n  IF used: Then implement properly\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"You and reviewer both report to me. If we don''t need this feature, don''t add it.\"\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n```\nFOR multi-item feedback:\n  1. Clarify anything unclear FIRST\n  2. Then implement in this order:\n     - Blocking issues (breaks, security)\n     - Simple fixes (typos, imports)\n     - Complex fixes (refactoring, logic)\n  3. Test each fix individually\n  4. Verify no regressions\n```\n\n## When To Push Back\n\nPush back when:\n- Suggestion breaks existing functionality\n- Reviewer lacks full context\n- Violates YAGNI (unused feature)\n- Technically incorrect for this stack\n- Legacy/compatibility reasons exist\n- Conflicts with your human partner''s architectural decisions\n\n**How to push back:**\n- Use technical reasoning, not defensiveness\n- Ask specific questions\n- Reference working tests/code\n- Involve your human partner if architectural\n\n**Signal if uncomfortable pushing back out loud:** \"Strange things are afoot at the Circle K\"\n\n## Acknowledging Correct Feedback\n\nWhen feedback IS correct:\n```\n✅ \"Fixed. [Brief description of what changed]\"\n✅ \"Good catch - [specific issue]. Fixed in [location].\"\n✅ [Just fix it and show in the code]\n\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right!\"\n❌ \"Great point!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for catching that!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for [anything]\"\n❌ ANY gratitude expression\n```\n\n**Why no thanks:** Actions speak. Just fix it. The code itself shows you heard the feedback.\n\n**If you catch yourself about to write \"Thanks\":** DELETE IT. State the fix instead.\n\n## Gracefully Correcting Your Pushback\n\nIf you pushed back and were wrong:\n```\n✅ \"You were right - I checked [X] and it does [Y]. Implementing now.\"\n✅ \"Verified this and you''re correct. My initial understanding was wrong because [reason]. Fixing.\"\n\n❌ Long apology\n❌ Defending why you pushed back\n❌ Over-explaining\n```\n\nState the correction factually and move on.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| Performative agreement | State requirement or just act |\n| Blind implementation | Verify against codebase first |\n| Batch without testing | One at a time, test each |\n| Assuming reviewer is right | Check if breaks things |\n| Avoiding pushback | Technical correctness > comfort |\n| Partial implementation | Clarify all items first |\n| Can''t verify, proceed anyway | State limitation, ask for direction |\n\n## Real Examples\n\n**Performative Agreement (Bad):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right! Let me remove that...\"\n```\n\n**Technical Verification (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n✅ \"Checking... build target is 10.15+, this API needs 13+. Need legacy for backward compat. Current impl has wrong bundle ID - fix it or drop pre-13 support?\"\n```\n\n**YAGNI (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Implement proper metrics tracking with database, date filters, CSV export\"\n✅ \"Grepped codebase - nothing calls this endpoint. Remove it (YAGNI)? Or is there usage I''m missing?\"\n```\n\n**Unclear Item (Good):**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix items 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n✅ \"Understand 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before implementing.\"\n```\n\n## GitHub Thread Replies\n\nWhen replying to inline review comments on GitHub, reply in the comment thread (`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{pr}/comments/{id}/replies`), not as a top-level PR comment.\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**External feedback = suggestions to evaluate, not orders to follow.**\n\nVerify. Question. Then implement.\n\nNo performative agreement. Technical rigor always.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:56:53.442Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Code Review Agents requiring structured feedback processing and technical validation.","zh":"适用于需要结构化反馈处理和技术验证的代码审查代理的必备条件","ja":"構造化フィードバック処理と技術検証を必要とするコードレビューエージェントに不可欠","ko":"구조화된 피드백 처리 및 기술 검증이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 필수적인 요소","es":"Esencial para los Agentes de Revisión de Código que requieren un procesamiento de comentarios estructurados y una validación técnica.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents de Révision de Code nécessitant un traitement de commentaires structurés et une validation technique.","de":"Wesentlich für Code-Review-Agenten, die ein strukturiertes Feedback-Verarbeitung und technische Validierung erfordern.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Revisão de Código que exigem processamento de feedback estruturado e validação técnica.","ru":"Необходимо для Агентов Кодового Обзора, требующих структурированной обработки обратной связи и технической проверки.","ar":"ضروري لعميل مراجعة الشفرة الذي يتطلب معالجة ملاحظات منظمّة وتأكيد فني."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables systematic processing of code review feedback through a five-stage technical evaluation pattern: READ, UNDERSTAND, VERIFY, EVALUATE, RESPOND. Ensures technical correctness over social comfort by prioritizing codebase reality verification before implementation.","zh":"通过五个阶段的技术评估模式（READ、UNDERSTAND、VERIFY、EVALUATE、RESPOND）实现代码审查反馈的系统处理，确保技术正确性优先于社会舒适度，并在实施之前优先进行代码库现实性验证","ja":"READ、UNDERSTAND、VERIFY、EVALUATE、RESPONDの5段階の技術評価パターンを通じて、コードレビューのフィードバックを体系的に処理する。実装前にコードベースの現実性の検証を優先し、技術的正しさを社会的快適性よりも優先する","ko":"READ, UNDERSTAND, VERIFY, EVALUATE, RESPOND의 5단계 기술 평가 패턴을 통해 코드 리뷰 피드백을 체계적으로 처리한다. 구현 전에 코드베이스 현실성 검증을 우선하고 기술적 올바름을 사회적 편안함보다 우선한다","es":"Permite el procesamiento sistemático de los comentarios de revisión de código a través de un patrón de evaluación técnica de cinco etapas: LEER, ENTENDER, VERIFICAR, EVALUAR, RESPONDER. Asegura la corrección técnica sobre la comodidad social al priorizar la verificación de la realidad del código antes de la implementación.","fr":"Permet le traitement systématique des commentaires de révision de code à travers un modèle d''évaluation technique en cinq étapes : LIRE, COMPRENDRE, VÉRIFIER, ÉVALUER, RÉPONDRE. Assure la correction technique plutôt que le confort social en donnant la priorité à la vérification de la réalité du code avant la mise en œuvre.","de":"Ermöglicht die systematische Verarbeitung von Code-Review-Kommentaren durch ein fünfstufiges technisches Bewertungsmuster: LESEN, VERSTEHEN, ÜBERPRÜFEN, BEWERTEN, ANTWORTEN. Stellt die technische Richtigkeit über den sozialen Komfort, indem der Code-Realitäts-Check vor der Implementierung priorisiert wird.","pt":"Permite o processamento sistemático de feedback de revisão de código por meio de um padrão de avaliação técnica em cinco etapas: LER, ENTENDER, VERIFICAR, AVALIAR, RESPONDER. Garante a correção técnica sobre o conforto social, priorizando a verificação da realidade do código antes da implementação.","ru":"Позволяет осуществлять системную обработку обратной связи кодового обзора через пятиэтапный технический шаблон оценки: ПРОЧИТАТЬ, ПОНИМАТЬ, ПРОВЕРИТЬ, ОЦЕНИТЬ, ОТВЕТИТЬ. Обеспечивает техническую правильность над социальным комфортом, отдавая приоритет проверке реальности кодовой базы перед реализацией.","ar":"يسمح بمعالجة منهجية لملاحظات مراجعة الشفرة من خلال نمط تقييم تقني في خمس مراحل: قراءة، فهم، التحقق، تقييم، الاستجابة. يضمن الدقة الفنية على الراحة الاجتماعية، مع تقديم التحقق من واقع قاعدة الشفرة قبل التنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Processing pull request comments","Validating technical feedback against codebase","Implementing structured response protocols","Reducing emotional reactivity in technical discussions"],"zh":["处理拉取请求评论","验证技术反馈与代码库","实施结构化响应协议","减少技术讨论中的情感反应性"],"ja":["プルリクエストのコメントを処理する","コードベースに対する技術的フィードバックを検証する","構造化されたレスポンスプロトコルを実装する","技術的な議論における感情的反応性を減らす"],"ko":["풀 리퀘스트 댓글 처리","코드베이스에 대한 기술적 피드백 검증","구조화된 응답 프로토콜 구현","기술적 토론에서의 감정적 반응성 감소"],"es":["Procesamiento de comentarios de solicitudes de extracción","Validación de comentarios técnicos frente al código","Implementación de protocolos de respuesta estructurados","Reducción de la reactividad emocional en discusiones técnicas"],"fr":["Traitement des commentaires de demandes d''extraction","Validation des commentaires techniques par rapport au code","Mise en œuvre de protocoles de réponse structurés","Réduction de la réactivité émotionnelle dans les discussions techniques"],"de":["Verarbeitung von Kommentaren zu Pull-Requests","Validierung von technischen Kommentaren gegenüber dem Code","Implementierung von strukturierten Antwortprotokollen","Verringerung der emotionalen Reaktivität in technischen Diskussionen"],"pt":["Processamento de comentários de solicitações de pull","Validação de feedback técnico contra a base de código","Implementação de protocolos de resposta estruturados","Redução da reatividade emocional em discussões técnicas"],"ru":["Обработка комментариев к запросам на слияние","Проверка технической обратной связи против кодовой базы","Реализация структурированных протоколов ответа","Снижение эмоциональной реактивности в технических обсуждениях"],"ar":["معالجة التعليقات على طلبات السحب","التحقق من الملاحظات الفنية مقابل قاعدة الشفرة","تنفيذ بروتوكولات استجابة منظمّة","تقليل التفاعل العاطفي في المناقشات الفنية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to complete codebase for verification","Assumes technical rather than subjective feedback","Depends on clear restatement of requirements"],"zh":["需要访问完整的代码库进行验证","假设技术反馈而非主观反馈","依赖于要求的明确重述"],"ja":["検証のために完全なコードベースへのアクセスが必要","主観的なフィードバックではなく技術的なフィードバックを仮定","要件の明確な再述に依存"],"ko":["검증을 위해 완전한 코드베이스에 대한 액세스가 필요","주관적인 피드백이 아닌 기술적인 피드백을 가정","요구 사항의 명확한 재술에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso al código completo para la verificación","Supone comentarios técnicos en lugar de subjetivos","Depende de una restatement clara de los requisitos"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au code complet pour la vérification","Suppose des commentaires techniques plutôt que subjectifs","Dépend d''un réétat clair des exigences"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf den vollständigen Code für die Überprüfung","Geht von technischen statt subjektiven Kommentaren aus","Hängt von einer klaren Wiederholung der Anforderungen ab"],"pt":["Exige acesso à base de código completa para verificação","Supõe feedback técnico em vez de subjetivo","Depende de uma reformulação clara dos requisitos"],"ru":["Требует доступа к полной кодовой базе для проверки","Предполагает техническую обратную связь, а не субъективную","Зависит от четкого переформулирования требований"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة الكاملة للتحقق","يفترض الملاحظات الفنية بدلاً من الملاحظات الذاتية","يعتمد على إعادة صياغة واضحة للمتطلبات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HNULS-LabHub/HNULS-KnowledgeDatabase/Summarize', 'community', 'HNULS-LabHub', 'HNULS-KnowledgeDatabase', 'HNULS-LabHub/HNULS-KnowledgeDatabase', 'Summarize', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z', '2026-02-18T12:57:28.548Z', NULL, '{"id":"HNULS-LabHub/HNULS-KnowledgeDatabase/Summarize","name":"Summarize","description":{"es":"El Skill ''Summarize'' genera un resumen de documentación para la entrega de proyectos, facilitando la comprensión del estado del proyecto.","fr":"Le Skill ''Summarize'' génère un résumé de documentation pour le relais de projets, facilitant la compréhension de l''état du projet.","de":"Das Skill ''Summarize'' generiert eine Zusammenfassung der Dokumentation für die Übergabe von Projekten, um das Verständnis des Projektstatus zu erleichtern.","pt":"O skill ''Summarize'' gera documentação técnica para modelos AI, garantindo uma transição suave entre equipes e projetos.","ru":"Навык ''Summarize'' генерирует техническую документацию для моделей AI, обеспечивающую бесшовную передачу между командами и проектами.","ar":"مهارة ''Summarize'' تولد وثائق فنية لنماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يضمن انتقالا سليما بين الفرق والمشاريع.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Resumen de Documentación para Entrega","fr":"Résumé de Documentation pour Relais","de":"Zusammenfassung der Dokumentation für Übergabe","pt":"Resumo Técnico: Documentação de Entrega para Modelos AI","ru":"Технический обзор: Документация для передачи моделей AI","ar":"ملخص تقني: وثائق التسليم لنماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"Summarize"},"description":{"es":"El Skill ''Summarize'' genera un resumen de documentación para la entrega de proyectos, facilitando la comprensión del estado del proyecto.","fr":"Le Skill ''Summarize'' génère un résumé de documentation pour le relais de projets, facilitant la compréhension de l''état du projet.","de":"Das Skill ''Summarize'' generiert eine Zusammenfassung der Dokumentation für die Übergabe von Projekten, um das Verständnis des Projektstatus zu erleichtern.","pt":"O skill ''Summarize'' gera documentação técnica para modelos AI, garantindo uma transição suave entre equipes e projetos.","ru":"Навык ''Summarize'' генерирует техническую документацию для моделей AI, обеспечивающую бесшовную передачу между командами и проектами.","ar":"مهارة ''Summarize'' تولد وثائق فنية لنماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يضمن انتقالا سليما بين الفرق والمشاريع.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Generación de lista de archivos","Descripción de la lógica del proyecto","Identificación de tareas pendientes","Creación de instrucciones para el siguiente modelo de IA","Mejora de la comprensión del estado del proyecto","Facilitación de la entrega de proyectos"],"fr":["Génération de la liste de fichiers","Description de la logique du projet","Identification des tâches pendantes","Création d''instructions pour le prochain modèle de IA","Amélioration de la compréhension de l''état du projet","Facilitation de la relance de projets"],"de":["Erstellung einer Dateiliste","Beschreibung der Logik des Projekts","Identifizierung offener Aufgaben","Erstellung von Anweisungen für das nächste IA-Modell","Verbesserung des Verständnisses des Projektstatus","Erleichterung der Übergabe von Projekten"],"pt":["Geração de lista de arquivos","Criação de lógica de resumo","Definição de intentos pendentes","Injeção de instruções para modelos AI"],"ru":["Генерация списка файлов","Создание логики обзора","Определение незавершенных намерений","Внедрение инструкций для моделей AI"],"ar":["توليد قائمة الملفات","إنشاء منطق الملخص","تحديد النوايا المعلقة","حقن الإرشادات لنماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"es":["resumen de documentación","entrega de proyectos","lista de archivos","lógica del proyecto","tareas pendientes","modelo de IA","comprensión del estado del proyecto","desarrollo de software","colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["résumé de documentation","relais de projets","liste de fichiers","logique du projet","tâches pendantes","modèle de IA","compréhension de l''état du projet","développement de logiciels","collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["Zusammenfassung der Dokumentation","Übergabe von Projekten","Dateiliste","Logik des Projekts","offene Aufgaben","IA-Modell","Verständnis des Projektstatus","Softwareentwicklung","Teamkollaboration"],"pt":["documentação técnica","modelos AI","transição suave","lista de arquivos","lógica de resumo","intentos pendentes","injeção de instruções"],"ru":["техническая документация","модели AI","бесшовная передача","список файлов","логика обзора","незавершенные намерения","внедрение инструкций"],"ar":["الوثائق الفنية","نماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","الإنتقال السلس","قائمة الملفات","منطق الملخص","النوايا المعلقة","حقن الإرشادات"]}},"owner":"HNULS-LabHub","repo":"HNULS-KnowledgeDatabase","repoPath":"HNULS-LabHub/HNULS-KnowledgeDatabase","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.514Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Summarize","description":"总结当前项目状态，生成一份交接文档，帮助下一个 AI 模型快速理解并接手工作","bodyPreview":"请按照【上下文锚点协议】为我们的当前工作生成一份“交接文档”。\n目标：这份文档将作为下一个（能力较弱的）AI 模型的系统级输入，帮助它快速理解项目状态并无缝接手。\n\n要求：\n1. **文件清单 (Manifest)**：列出本轮对话中我们修改、创建或重点引用的所有文件路径。必须精确，便于我让下一个模型读取。\n2. **逻辑快照 (Logic Snapshot)**：用最精炼的技术语言解释核心改动点（比如：数据流变动、接口签名更改、架构调整）。不要废话。\n3. **未竟事务 (Pending Intent)**：明确指出当前代码是“已完成”、“由于报错暂停”还是“开发中途”。\n4. **强引导指令 (The Injection)**：最后生成一段专门写给“下一个 AI”的 Prompt，命令它按照特定方式读取上述文件并准备就绪。","body":"请按照【上下文锚点协议】为我们的当前工作生成一份“交接文档”。\n目标：这份文档将作为下一个（能力较弱的）AI 模型的系统级输入，帮助它快速理解项目状态并无缝接手。\n\n要求：\n1. **文件清单 (Manifest)**：列出本轮对话中我们修改、创建或重点引用的所有文件路径。必须精确，便于我让下一个模型读取。\n2. **逻辑快照 (Logic Snapshot)**：用最精炼的技术语言解释核心改动点（比如：数据流变动、接口签名更改、架构调整）。不要废话。\n3. **未竟事务 (Pending Intent)**：明确指出当前代码是“已完成”、“由于报错暂停”还是“开发中途”。\n4. **强引导指令 (The Injection)**：最后生成一段专门写给“下一个 AI”的 Prompt，命令它按照特定方式读取上述文件并准备就绪。\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:57:28.548Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code requiring advanced document summarization capabilities for efficient knowledge transfer.","zh":"适用于像Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code这样的AI代理，它们需要高级文档摘要功能以实现高效的知识转移。","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、Claude CodeなどのAIエージェントに適しており、効率的なナレッジ転移のために高度なドキュメント要約機能を必要とします。","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 효율적인 지식 전달을 위해 고급 문서 요약 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que requieren capacidades avanzadas de resumen de documentos para una transferencia de conocimiento eficiente.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code nécessitant des capacités de résumé de documents avancées pour un transfert de connaissances efficace.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agenten wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die erweiterte Dokumentzusammenfassungsfähigkeiten für einen effizienten WissensTransfer benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que exigem capacidades avançadas de resumo de documentos para transferência eficiente de conhecimento.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, требующих продвинутых возможностей суммирования документов для эффективной передачи знаний.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code الذين يتطلبون قدرات متقدمة لتلخيص المستندات لنقل المعرفة بكفاءة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate concise manifest files, logic snapshots, and pending intent reports using precise technical language, facilitating seamless project handovers via protocols like 上下文锚点协议, and enables them to create specialized prompts for subsequent AI models.","zh":"赋予代理生成使用精确技术语言的简洁清单文件、逻辑快照和待处理意图报告的能力，通过协议如上下文锚点协议实现无缝的项目交接，并使它们能够为后续AI模型创建专用提示。","ja":"エージェントに、精密なテクニカル言語を使用したコンサイスなマニフェストファイル、ロジックスナップショット、以及保留中の意図レポートを生成する能力を与え、上下文锚点协议などのプロトコルを介してプロジェクトのハンドオーバーを円滑に行い、後続のAIモデル用の特化されたプロンプトを作成することを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 정교한 기술 언어를 사용하여 간결한 매니페스트 파일, 논리 스냅샷 및 대기 중인 의도 보고서를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 프로토콜과 같은 上下文锚点协议을 통해 무결점 프로젝트 인도를 용이하게 하며, 이후 AI 모델을 위한 전문 프롬프트를 생성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes generar archivos de manifiesto concisos, instantáneas de lógica y informes de intención pendientes utilizando un lenguaje técnico preciso, facilitando una entrega de proyectos sin problemas a través de protocolos como 上下文锚点协议, y les permite crear prompts especializados para modelos de IA posteriores.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des fichiers de manifeste concis, des instantanés de logique et des rapports d''intention en attente en utilisant un langage technique précis, facilitant une rétrocession de projets sans heurts via des protocoles comme 上下文锚点协议, et leur permet de créer des invites spécialisées pour les modèles de IA ultérieurs.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, knappe Manifestdateien, Logik-Schnappschüsse und Berichte über ausstehende Absichten unter Verwendung präziser technischer Sprache zu generieren, wodurch eine nahtlose Projekthandover über Protokolle wie 上下文锚点协议 erleichtert wird und sie spezielle Prompts für nachfolgende KI-Modelle erstellen können.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar arquivos de manifesto concisos, instantâneos de lógica e relatórios de intenção pendentes usando linguagem técnica precisa, facilitando a transferência de projetos sem interrupções via protocolos como 上下文锚点协议, e permite que criem prompts especializados para modelos de IA subsequentes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать краткие манифестные файлы, логические снимки и отчеты о挂起ших намерениях с использованием точного технического языка, облегчая бесшовную передачу проектов через протоколы, такие как 上下文锚点协议, и позволяет создавать специализированные подсказки для последующих моделей ИИ.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من توليد ملفات إعلان مختصرة وصور منطقية وتقارير نوايا معلقة باستخدام لغة تقنية دقيقة، وتسهل عمليات نقل المشروع بسلاسة عبر بروتوكولات مثل بروتوكول 上下文锚点协议، وتمكنهم من إنشاء دوافع متخصصة لنماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي اللاحقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating project handover documents","Creating logic snapshots for code reviews","Automating manifest file creation for file tracking"],"zh":["生成项目交接文档","为代码审查创建逻辑快照","自动创建文件跟踪的清单文件"],"ja":["プロジェクトハンドオーバードキュメントを生成する","コードレビュー用のロジックスナップショットを作成する","ファイル追跡用のマニフェストファイルの自動生成"],"ko":["프로젝트 인도 문서 생성","코드 리뷰를 위한 논리 스냅샷 생성","파일 추적을 위한 매니페스트 파일 자동 생성"],"es":["Generación de documentos de entrega de proyectos","Creación de instantáneas de lógica para revisiones de código","Automatización de la creación de archivos de manifiesto para el seguimiento de archivos"],"fr":["Génération de documents de rétrocession de projets","Création d''instantanés de logique pour les revues de code","Automatisation de la création de fichiers de manifeste pour le suivi de fichiers"],"de":["Erstellung von Projekthandover-Dokumenten","Erstellung von Logik-Schnappschüssen für Code-Reviews","Automatisierung der Erstellung von Manifestdateien für die Dateiverfolgung"],"pt":["Gerar documentos de transferência de projeto","Criar instantâneos de lógica para revisões de código","Automatizar a criação de arquivos de manifesto para rastreamento de arquivos"],"ru":["Генерировать документы передачи проекта","Создавать логические снимки для обзора кода","Автоматизировать создание манифестных файлов для отслеживания файлов"],"ar":["توليد وثائق نقل المشروع","إنشاء صور منطقية لمراجعة الكود","أتمتة إنشاء ملفات الإعلان لتتبع الملفات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires precise technical language understanding","Limited to text-based project documentation"],"zh":["需要精确的技术语言理解","仅限文本 기반项目文档"],"ja":["精密なテクニカル言語の理解が必要","テキストベースのプロジェクトドキュメントのみに限定"],"ko":["정교한 기술 언어 이해가 필요","텍스트 기반 프로젝트 문서만 제한"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del lenguaje técnico preciso","Limitado a la documentación de proyectos basada en texto"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du langage technique précis","Limité à la documentation de projets basée sur le texte"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis der präzisen technischen Sprache","Begrenzt auf textbasierte Projektdokumentation"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de linguagem técnica precisa","Limitado à documentação de projeto baseada em texto"],"ru":["Требует точного понимания технического языка","Ограничен документацией проекта на основе текста"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا دقيقًا للغة التقنية","محدود bằng توثيق المشروع القائم على النص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
