thon: Melhores Práticas","ru":"Стиль кода Python: современные инструменты","ar":"أسلوب كود بايثون: أفضل الممارسات","en":"python-code-style"},"description":{"zh":"Python 代码风格和文档是代码可维护性和协作性的关键。这个技能涵盖了现代 Python 工具、命名约定和文档标准","ja":"Python コーディングスタイルとドキュメントはコードのメンテナンス性と協作性の重要な要素です。このスキルでは、モダンな Python ツール、命名規則、ドキュメント規格をカバーします","ko":"파이썬 코드 스타일 및 문서는 코드의 유지 보수성 및 협업성의 핵심입니다. 이 스킬은 최신 파이썬 툴, 명명 규칙 및 문서 표준을 다룹니다","es":"El estilo de código Python y la documentación clara son fundamentales para proyectos colaborativos y mantenibles. Esta habilidad cubre herramientas modernas ...","fr":"Le style de code Python et la documentation claire sont essentiels pour les projets collaboratifs et maintenables. Cette compétence couvre les outils moderne...","de":"Der Python-Code-Stil und die klare Dokumentation sind grundlegend für kollaborative und wartbare Projekte. Diese Fähigkeit deckt moderne Python-Tools, Namens...","pt":"O estilo de código Python é fundamental para projetos colaborativos e fáceis de manter, abordando convenções de nomenclatura e padrões de documentação","ru":"Стиль кода Python имеет важное значение для совместных и поддерживаемых проектов, охватывающих соглашения об именах и стандарты документации","ar":"أسلوب كود بايثون أساسي لمشاريع تعاونية وسهلة الصيانة، يشمل اتفاقيات التسمية ومعايير التوثيق","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["现代 Python 工具","命名约定","文档标准","代码风格一致性","项目文档创建","代码审查"],"ja":["モダンな Python ツール","命名規則","ドキュメント規格","コードスタイルの一貫性","プロジェクトドキュメントの作成","コードレビュー"],"ko":["최신 파이썬 툴","명명 규칙","문서 표준","코드 스타일 일관성","프로젝트 문서 생성","코드 리뷰"],"es":["Herramientas modernas de Python para linting y formato","Convenciones de nomenclatura para código legible","Estándares de documentación para proyectos colaborativos","Configuración de herramientas como ruff, mypy y pyright","Revisión de código para consistencia de estilo","Creación de documentación de proyectos"],"fr":["Outils modernes Python pour le linting et le formatage","Conventions de nommage pour un code lisible","Normes de documentation pour les projets collaboratifs","Configuration d''outils tels que ruff, mypy et pyright","Révision de code pour la cohérence de style","Création de documentation de projet"],"de":["Moderne Python-Tools für Linting und Formatierung","Namenskonventionen für lesbaren Code","Dokumentationsstandards für kollaborative Projekte","Konfiguration von Tools wie ruff, mypy und pyright","Code-Überprüfung für Stil-Konsistenz","Erstellung von Projekt-Dokumentation"],"pt":["Convenções de nomenclatura","Padrões de documentação","Ferramentas de linting e formatação","Configuração de ruff, mypy e pyright","Revisão de código para consistência de estilo","Criação de documentação de projeto"],"ru":["Соглашения об именах","Стандарты документации","Инструменты linting и форматирования","Настройка ruff, mypy и pyright","Проверка кода на последовательность стиля","Создание документации проекта"],"ar":["اتفاقيات التسمية","معايير التوثيق","أدوات linting وتنسيق","تكوين ruff وmypy وpyright","مراجعة الكود لاتساق الأسلوب","إنشاء توثيق المشروع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python 代码风格","Python 文档","代码可维护性","代码协作性","Python 工具","命名约定","文档标准","代码审查","项目文档"],"ja":["Python コーディングスタイル","Python ドキュメント","コードメンテナンス性","コード協作性","Python ツール","命名規則","ドキュメント規格","コードレビュー","プロジェクトドキュメント"],"ko":["파이썬 코드 스타일","파이썬 문서","코드 유지 보수성","코드 협업성","파이썬 툴","명명 규칙","문서 표준","코드 리뷰","프로젝트 문서"],"es":["estilo de código Python","documentación de código","herramientas de Python","convenciones de nomenclatura","estándares de documentación","linting y formato","ruff","mypy","pyright","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["style de code Python","documentation de code","outils Python","conventions de nommage","normes de documentation","linting et formatage","ruff","mypy","pyright","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Python-Code-Stil","Code-Dokumentation","Python-Tools","Namenskonventionen","Dokumentationsstandards","Linting und Formatierung","ruff","mypy","pyright","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["estilo de código python","documentação python","convenções de nomenclatura python","ferramentas de linting python","formatação de código python","desenvolvimento de software python","melhores práticas python","padrões de código python","colaboração de código python"],"ru":["стиль кода python","документация python","соглашения об именах python","инструменты linting python","форматирование кода python","разработка программного обеспечения python","лучшие практики python","стандарты кода python","совместная работа над кодом python"],"ar":["أسلوب كود بايثون","توثيق بايثون","اتفاقيات التسمية بايثون","أدوات linting بايثون","تنسيق كود بايثون","تطوير برنامج بايثون","أفضل الممارسات بايثون","معايير كود بايثون","تعاون كود بايثون"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-code-style","description":"Python code style, linting, formatting, naming conventions, and documentation standards. Use when writing new code, reviewing style, configuring linters, writing docstrings, or establishing project standards.","bodyPreview":"# Python Code Style & Documentation\n\nConsistent code style and clear documentation make codebases maintainable and collaborative. This skill covers modern Python tooling, naming conventions, and documentation standards.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up linting and formatting for a new project\n- Writing or reviewing docstrings\n- Establishing team coding standards\n- Configuring ruff, mypy, or pyright\n- Reviewing code for style consistency\n- Creating project documentation\n\n## Core Concepts","body":"# Python Code Style & Documentation\n\nConsistent code style and clear documentation make codebases maintainable and collaborative. This skill covers modern Python tooling, naming conventions, and documentation standards.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up linting and formatting for a new project\n- Writing or reviewing docstrings\n- Establishing team coding standards\n- Configuring ruff, mypy, or pyright\n- Reviewing code for style consistency\n- Creating project documentation\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Automated Formatting\n\nLet tools handle formatting debates. Configure once, enforce automatically.\n\n### 2. Consistent Naming\n\nFollow PEP 8 conventions with meaningful, descriptive names.\n\n### 3. Documentation as Code\n\nDocstrings should be maintained alongside the code they describe.\n\n### 4. Type Annotations\n\nModern Python code should include type hints for all public APIs.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# Install modern tooling\npip install ruff mypy\n\n# Configure in pyproject.toml\n[tool.ruff]\nline-length = 120\ntarget-version = \"py312\"  # Adjust based on your project''s minimum Python version\n\n[tool.mypy]\nstrict = true\n```\n\n## Fundamental Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Modern Python Tooling\n\nUse `ruff` as an all-in-one linter and formatter. It replaces flake8, isort, and black with a single fast tool.\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.ruff]\nline-length = 120\ntarget-version = \"py312\"  # Adjust based on your project''s minimum Python version\n\n[tool.ruff.lint]\nselect = [\n    \"E\",    # pycodestyle errors\n    \"W\",    # pycodestyle warnings\n    \"F\",    # pyflakes\n    \"I\",    # isort\n    \"B\",    # flake8-bugbear\n    \"C4\",   # flake8-comprehensions\n    \"UP\",   # pyupgrade\n    \"SIM\",  # flake8-simplify\n]\nignore = [\"E501\"]  # Line length handled by formatter\n\n[tool.ruff.format]\nquote-style = \"double\"\nindent-style = \"space\"\n```\n\nRun with:\n\n```bash\nruff check --fix .  # Lint and auto-fix\nruff format .       # Format code\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Type Checking Configuration\n\nConfigure strict type checking for production code.\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.mypy]\npython_version = \"3.12\"\nstrict = true\nwarn_return_any = true\nwarn_unused_ignores = true\ndisallow_untyped_defs = true\ndisallow_incomplete_defs = true\n\n[[tool.mypy.overrides]]\nmodule = \"tests.*\"\ndisallow_untyped_defs = false\n```\n\nAlternative: Use `pyright` for faster checking.\n\n```toml\n[tool.pyright]\npythonVersion = \"3.12\"\ntypeCheckingMode = \"strict\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Naming Conventions\n\nFollow PEP 8 with emphasis on clarity over brevity.\n\n**Files and Modules:**\n\n```python\n# Good: Descriptive snake_case\nuser_repository.py\norder_processing.py\nhttp_client.py\n\n# Avoid: Abbreviations\nusr_repo.py\nord_proc.py\nhttp_cli.py\n```\n\n**Classes and Functions:**\n\n```python\n# Classes: PascalCase\nclass UserRepository:\n    pass\n\nclass HTTPClientFactory:  # Acronyms stay uppercase\n    pass\n\n# Functions and variables: snake_case\ndef get_user_by_email(email: str) -> User | None:\n    retry_count = 3\n    max_connections = 100\n```\n\n**Constants:**\n\n```python\n# Module-level constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\nMAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 3\nDEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30\nAPI_BASE_URL = \"https://api.example.com\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Import Organization\n\nGroup imports in a consistent order: standard library, third-party, local.\n\n```python\n# Standard library\nimport os\nfrom collections.abc import Callable\nfrom typing import Any\n\n# Third-party packages\nimport httpx\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column\n\n# Local imports\nfrom myproject.models import User\nfrom myproject.services import UserService\n```\n\nUse absolute imports exclusively:\n\n```python\n# Preferred\nfrom myproject.utils import retry_decorator\n\n# Avoid relative imports\nfrom ..utils import retry_decorator\n```\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Pattern 5: Google-Style Docstrings\n\nWrite docstrings for all public classes, methods, and functions.\n\n**Simple Function:**\n\n```python\ndef get_user(user_id: str) -> User:\n    \"\"\"Retrieve a user by their unique identifier.\"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\n**Complex Function:**\n\n```python\ndef process_batch(\n    items: list[Item],\n    max_workers: int = 4,\n    on_progress: Callable[[int, int], None] | None = None,\n) -> BatchResult:\n    \"\"\"Process items concurrently using a worker pool.\n\n    Processes each item in the batch using the configured number of\n    workers. Progress can be monitored via the optional callback.\n\n    Args:\n        items: The items to process. Must not be empty.\n        max_workers: Maximum concurrent workers. Defaults to 4.\n        on_progress: Optional callback receiving (completed, total) counts.\n\n    Returns:\n        BatchResult containing succeeded items and any failures with\n        their associated exceptions.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If items is empty.\n        ProcessingError: If the batch cannot be processed.\n\n    Example:\n        >>> result = process_batch(items, max_workers=8)\n        >>> print(f\"Processed {len(result.succeeded)} items\")\n    \"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\n**Class Docstring:**\n\n```python\nclass UserService:\n    \"\"\"Service for managing user operations.\n\n    Provides methods for creating, retrieving, updating, and\n    deleting users with proper validation and error handling.\n\n    Attributes:\n        repository: The data access layer for user persistence.\n        logger: Logger instance for operation tracking.\n\n    Example:\n        >>> service = UserService(repository, logger)\n        >>> user = service.create_user(CreateUserInput(...))\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, repository: UserRepository, logger: Logger) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initialize the user service.\n\n        Args:\n            repository: Data access layer for users.\n            logger: Logger for tracking operations.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.repository = repository\n        self.logger = logger\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Line Length and Formatting\n\nSet line length to 120 characters for modern displays while maintaining readability.\n\n```python\n# Good: Readable line breaks\ndef create_user(\n    email: str,\n    name: str,\n    role: UserRole = UserRole.MEMBER,\n    notify: bool = True,\n) -> User:\n    ...\n\n# Good: Chain method calls clearly\nresult = (\n    db.query(User)\n    .filter(User.active == True)\n    .order_by(User.created_at.desc())\n    .limit(10)\n    .all()\n)\n\n# Good: Format long strings\nerror_message = (\n    f\"Failed to process user {user_id}: \"\n    f\"received status {response.status_code} \"\n    f\"with body {response.text[:100]}\"\n)\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: Project Documentation\n\n**README Structure:**\n\n```markdown\n# Project Name\n\nBrief description of what the project does.\n\n## Installation\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\npip install myproject\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Quick Start\n\n\\`\\`\\`python\nfrom myproject import Client\n\nclient = Client(api_key=\"...\")\nresult = client.process(data)\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Configuration\n\nDocument environment variables and configuration options.\n\n## Development\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\npip install -e \".[dev]\"\npytest\n\\`\\`\\`\n```\n\n**CHANGELOG Format (Keep a Changelog):**\n\n```markdown\n# Changelog\n\n## [Unreleased]\n\n### Added\n- New feature X\n\n### Changed\n- Modified behavior of Y\n\n### Fixed\n- Bug in Z\n```\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Use ruff** - Single tool for linting and formatting\n2. **Enable strict mypy** - Catch type errors before runtime\n3. **120 character lines** - Modern standard for readability\n4. **Descriptive names** - Clarity over brevity\n5. **Absolute imports** - More maintainable than relative\n6. **Google-style docstrings** - Consistent, readable documentation\n7. **Document public APIs** - Every public function needs a docstring\n8. **Keep docs updated** - Treat documentation as code\n9. **Automate in CI** - Run linters on every commit\n10. **Target Python 3.10+** - For new projects, Python 3.12+ is recommended for modern language features\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:57:44.537Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing consistent Python code formatting and documentation standards","zh":"非常适合需要一致的Python代码格式和文档标准的代码审查代理","ja":"Pythonコードの整形と文書化標準を一貫して適用するコードレビュー代理に最適","ko":"일관된 Python 코드 형식 및 문서화 표준이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan un formato de código Python y estándares de documentación consistentes","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant un formatage de code Python et des normes de documentation cohérents","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die ein konsistentes Python-Code-Formatting und Dokumentationsstandards benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam de formatação de código Python consistente e padrões de documentação","ru":"Идеально для агентов код-ревью, которым необходима последовательная форматировка кода на Python и стандарты документации","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المراجعة اللغوية الذين يحتاجون إلى تنسيق ثابت للغة بايثون وتقنيات توثيق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce PEP-compliant naming conventions, configure linting tools like ruff, mypy, or pyright, and generate high-quality docstrings for enhanced code readability and maintainability","zh":"赋予代理应用PEP兼容的命名约定，配置类似ruff、mypy或pyright的lint工具，并生成高质量的文档字符串以提高代码的可读性和可维护性","ja":"PEP準拠の命名規則を適用し、ruff、mypy、pyrightなどのLintツールを設定し、高品質のドキュメンテーション文字列を生成して、コードの可読性とメンテナンス性を向上させる","ko":"PEP 호환命명 규칙 적용, ruff, mypy 또는 pyright와 같은 린트 도구 구성 및 고급 문서 문자열 생성을 통해 코드의 가독성 및 유지 보수성을 향상","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar convenciones de nomenclatura compatibles con PEP, configurar herramientas de lintado como ruff, mypy o pyright, y generar cadenas de documentación de alta calidad para una mayor legibilidad y mantenibilidad del código","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des conventions de nommage conformes à PEP, de configurer des outils de lintage tels que ruff, mypy ou pyright, et de générer des docstrings de haute qualité pour améliorer la lisibilité et la maintenabilité du code","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, PEP-konforme Benennungskonventionen durchzusetze