angage"],"de":["Ausführung von Aufgaben mit fortschrittlichen Sprachmodellen","Anpassbare Modell-Optionen","Anpassbares Sandbox für Tests und Debugging","Argumentationskonfiguration für komplexe Aufgaben","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Sprachmodellen"],"pt":["Execução de tarefas com o modelo GPT-5.2","Opções de configuração personalizáveis","Modos de sandbox para controle de acesso","Suporte a override de modelo","Integração com AskUserQuestion"],"ru":["Выполнение задач с моделью GPT-5.2","Настраиваемые опции конфигурации","Режимы sandbox для контроля доступа","Поддержка переопределения модели","Интеграция с AskUserQuestion"],"ar":["تشغيل المهام باستخدام نموذج GPT-5.2","خيارات التكوين القابلة للتعديل","أوضاع Sandbox للتحكم في الوصول","دعم إعادة تعريف النموذج","التكامل مع AskUserQuestion"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Codex技能","AI开发","模型选项","沙盒模式","推理努力","AI开发者","Codex指南"],"ja":["Codexスキル","AI開発","モデルオプション","サンドボックスモード","推論労力","AI開発者","Codexガイド"],"ko":["Codex 스킬","AI 개발","모델 옵션","샌드박스 모드","추론 노력","AI 개발자","Codex 가이드"],"es":["desarrollo de software","modelos de lenguaje","sandbox","configuración de razón","tareas complejas","compatibilidad de modelos","desarrolladores","programación","inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["développement de logiciels","modèles de langage","bac à sable","configuration de raisonnement","tâches complexes","compatibilité de modèles","développeurs","programmation","intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Software-Entwicklung","Sprachmodelle","Sandbox","Argumentationskonfiguration","komplexe Aufgaben","Modell-Kompatibilität","Entwickler","Programmierung","Künstliche Intelligenz"],"pt":["Codex","GPT-5.2","Desenvolvimento de software","Modelos de linguagem","Opções de configuração","Sandbox","AskUserQuestion","Desenvolvedores","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Codex","GPT-5.2","Разработка программного обеспечения","Языковые модели","Опции конфигурации","Sandbox","AskUserQuestion","Разработчики","Инструменты разработки"],"ar":["Codex","GPT-5.2","تطوير البرمجيات","نماذج اللغة","خيارات التكوين","Sandbox","AskUserQuestion","المطورون","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"codex","description":"Use when the user asks to run Codex CLI (codex exec, codex resume) or references OpenAI Codex for code analysis, refactoring, or automated editing. Uses GPT-5.2 by default for state-of-the-art software engineering.","bodyPreview":"# Codex Skill Guide\n\n## Running a Task\n1. Default to `gpt-5.2` model. Ask the user (via `AskUserQuestion`) which reasoning effort to use (`xhigh`,`high`, `medium`, or `low`). User can override model if needed (see Model Options below).\n2. Select the sandbox mode required for the task; default to `--sandbox read-only` unless edits or network access are necessary.\n3. Assemble the command with the appropriate options:\n   - `-m, --model <MODEL>`\n   - `--config model_reasoning_effort=\"<high|medium|lo","body":"# Codex Skill Guide\n\n## Running a Task\n1. Default to `gpt-5.2` model. Ask the user (via `AskUserQuestion`) which reasoning effort to use (`xhigh`,`high`, `medium`, or `low`). User can override model if needed (see Model Options below).\n2. Select the sandbox mode required for the task; default to `--sandbox read-only` unless edits or network access are necessary.\n3. Assemble the command with the appropriate options:\n   - `-m, --model <MODEL>`\n   - `--config model_reasoning_effort=\"<high|medium|low>\"`\n   - `--sandbox <read-only|workspace-write|danger-full-access>`\n   - `--full-auto`\n   - `-C, --cd <DIR>`\n   - `--skip-git-repo-check`\n3. Always use --skip-git-repo-check.\n4. When continuing a previous session, use `codex exec --skip-git-repo-check resume --last` via stdin. When resuming don''t use any configuration flags unless explicitly requested by the user e.g. if he species the model or the reasoning effort when requesting to resume a session. Resume syntax: `echo \"your prompt here\" | codex exec --skip-git-repo-check resume --last 2>/dev/null`. All flags have to be inserted between exec and resume.\n5. **IMPORTANT**: By default, append `2>/dev/null` to all `codex exec` commands to suppress thinking tokens (stderr). Only show stderr if the user explicitly requests to see thinking tokens or if debugging is needed.\n6. Run the command, capture stdout/stderr (filtered as appropriate), and summarize the outcome for the user.\n7. **After Codex completes**, inform the user: \"You can resume this Codex session at any time by saying ''codex resume'' or asking me to continue with additional analysis or changes.\"\n\n### Quick Reference\n| Use case | Sandbox mode | Key flags |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Read-only review or analysis | `read-only` | `--sandbox read-only 2>/dev/null` |\n| Apply local edits | `workspace-write` | `--sandbox workspace-write --full-auto 2>/dev/null` |\n| Permit network or broad access | `danger-full-access` | `--sandbox danger-full-access --full-auto 2>/dev/null` |\n| Resume recent session | Inherited from original | `echo \"prompt\" \\| codex exec --skip-git-repo-check resume --last 2>/dev/null` (no flags allowed) |\n| Run from another directory | Match task needs | `-C <DIR>` plus other flags `2>/dev/null` |\n\n## Model Options\n\n| Model | Best for | Context window | Key features |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `gpt-5.2-max` | **Max model**: Ultra-complex reasoning, deep problem analysis | 400K input / 128K output | 76.3% SWE-bench, adaptive reasoning, $1.25/$10.00 |\n| `gpt-5.2` ⭐ | **Flagship model**: Software engineering, agentic coding workflows | 400K input / 128K output | 76.3% SWE-bench, adaptive reasoning, $1.25/$10.00 |\n| `gpt-5.2-mini` | Cost-efficient coding (4x more usage allowance) | 400K input / 128K output | Near SOTA performance, $0.25/$2.00 |\n| `gpt-5.1-thinking` | Ultra-complex reasoning, deep problem analysis | 400K input / 128K output | Adaptive thinking depth, runs 2x slower on hardest tasks |\n\n**GPT-5.2 Advantages**: 76.3% SWE-bench (vs 72.8% GPT-5), 30% faster on average tasks, better tool handling, reduced hallucinations, improved code quality. Knowledge cutoff: September 30, 2024.\n\n**Reasoning Effort Levels**:\n- `xhigh` - Ultra-complex tasks (deep problem analysis, complex reasoning, deep understanding of the problem)\n- `high` - Complex tasks (refactoring, architecture, security analysis, performance optimization)\n- `medium` - Standard tasks (refactoring, code organization, feature additions, bug fixes)\n- `low` - Simple tasks (quick fixes, simple changes, code formatting, documentation)\n\n**Cached Input Discount**: 90% off ($0.125/M tokens) for repeated context, cache lasts up to 24 hours.\n\n## Following Up\n- After every `codex` command, immediately use `AskUserQuestion` to confirm next steps, collect clarifications, or decide whether to resume with `codex exec resume --last`.\n- When resuming, pipe the new prompt via stdin: `echo \"new prompt\" | codex exec resume --last 2>/dev/null`. The resumed session automatically uses the same model, reasoning effort, and sandbox mode from the original session.\n- Restate the chosen model, reasoning effort, and sandbox mode when proposing follow-up actions.\n\n## Error Handling\n- Stop and report failures whenever `codex --version` or a `codex exec` command exits non-zero; request direction before retrying.\n- Before you use high-impact flags (`--full-auto`, `--sandbox danger-full-access`, `--skip-git-repo-check`) ask the user for permission using AskUserQuestion unless it was already given.\n- When output includes warnings or partial results, summarize them and ask how to adjust using `AskUserQuestion`.\n\n## CLI Version\n\nRequires Codex CLI v0.57.0 or later for GPT-5.2 model support. The CLI defaults to `gpt-5.2` on macOS/Linux and `gpt-5.2` on Windows. Check version: `codex --version`\n\nUse `/model` slash command within a Codex session to switch models, or configure default in `~/.codex/config.toml`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:59:08.351Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Language Agents requiring flexible model selection and sandboxed task execution.","zh":"适用于需要灵活模型选择和沙盒任务执行的高级语言代理。","ja":"高度な言語エージェントに適しており、柔軟なモデル選択とサンドボックスでのタスク実行を必要とする。","ko":"고급 언어 에이전트에게 적합하며, 유연한 모델 선택과 샌드박스 작업 실행이 필요한 경우에 사용됩니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Lenguaje Avanzados que requieren una selección de modelo flexible y una ejecución de tareas en un entorno aislado.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Langage Avancés nécessitant une sélection de modèle flexible et une exécution de tâches dans un environnement sandboxé.","de":"Ideal für erweiterte Sprachagenten, die eine flexible Modellauswahl und eine Aufgabenausführung in einer Sandbox-Umgebung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem Avançados que requerem seleção de modelo flexível e execução de tarefas em sandbox.","ru":"Идеально для Продвинутых Языковых Агентов, требующих гибкого выбора модели и выполнения задач в песочнице.","ar":"مثالي لعميل لغة متقدم يتطلب اختيار نموذج مرن وتنفيذ مهام في sandbox."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute tasks with customizable reasoning efforts via `gpt-5.2` model, leveraging options like `--sandbox read-only` for secure operations and model overrides for specialized tasks, all while specifying model reasoning efforts such as `xhigh`, `high`, `medium`, or `low`.","zh":"赋予代理执行任务的能力，通过自定义推理努力，利用 `gpt-5.2` 模型，并通过选项如 `--sandbox read-only` 进行安全操作和模型重写以适用于专用任务，同时指定模型推理努力，如 `xhigh`、`high`、`medium` 或 `low`。","ja":"エージェントにタスクを実行する能力を付与し、`gpt-5.2` モデルを使用してカスタマイズされた推論労力を提供し、`--sandbox read-only` などのオプションを使用して安全な操作とモデルオーバーライドを実行し、専用タスクに特化したモデル推論労力を指定することができる、たとえば `xhigh`、`high`、`medium`、または `low`。","ko":"에이전트에 작업을 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, `gpt-5.2` 모델을 사용하여 사용자 지정된 推論 노력을 제공하며, `--sandbox read-only`와 같은 옵션을 사용하여 안전한 작업과 모델 재정의를 수행하며,専用 작업을 위한 모델 推論 노력을 지정할 수 있습니다. 예를 들어, `xhigh`, `high`, `medium`, 또는 `low`.","es":"Permite a los agentes ejecutar tareas con esfuerzos de razonamiento personalizables a través del modelo `gpt-5.2`, aprovechando opciones como `--sandbox de solo lectura` para operaciones seguras y anulaciones de modelo para tareas especializadas, todo mientras se especifican esfuerzos de razonamiento del modelo como `xhigh`, `high`, `medium` o `low`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des tâches avec des efforts de raisonnement personnalisables via le modèle `gpt-5.2`, en exploitant des options comme `--sandbox en lecture seule` pour des opérations sécurisées et des substitutions de modèle pour des tâches spécialisées, le tout en spécifiant des efforts de raisonnement de modèle tels que `xhigh`, `high`, `medium` ou `low`.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Aufgaben mit anpassbaren Bemühungen um Denkleistung auszuführen, über das `gpt-5.2`-Modell, wobei Optionen wie `--sandbox schreibgeschützt` für sichere Operationen und Modellüberschreibungen für spezielle Aufgaben genutzt werden, während Denkleistungsanstrengungen des Modells wie `xhigh`, `high`, `medium` oder `low` angegeben werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar tarefas com esforços de raciocínio personalizáveis via modelo `gpt-5.2`, aproveitando opções como `--sandbox read-only` para operações seguras e substituições de modelo para tarefas especializadas, tudo especificando esforços de raciocínio do modelo como `xhigh`, `high`, `medium` ou `low`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять задачи с настраиваемыми усилиями рассуждения через модель `gpt-5.2`, используя опции, такие как `--sandbox read-only` для безопасных операций и замену моделей для специализированных задач, все, указывая усилия рассуждения модели, такие как `xhigh`, `high`, `medium` или `low`.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تنفيذ المهام مع جهود التفكير القابلة للتعديل عبر نموذج `gpt-5.2`، وتحقيق خيارات مثل `--sandbox read-only` للعمليات الآمنة وبدائل النموذج للمهام المتخصصة، والكل متوافق مع جهود التفكير للنموذج مثل `xhigh`، `high`، `medium` أو `low`."},"useCases":{"en":["Executing tasks with variable reasoning efforts","Overriding default models for specialized tasks","Sandboxing tasks for secure read-only operations"],"zh":["执行具有可变推理努力的任务","覆盖默认模型以执行专用任务","沙盒任务以进行安全的只读操作"],"ja":["可変な推論労力を使用したタスクの実行","デフォルトモデルのオーバーライドによる専用タスクの実行","セキュアな読み取り専用操作のためのタスクのサンドボックス化"],"ko":["가변적인 推論 노력을 사용한 작업의 실행","기본 모델을 재정의하여専用 작업을 수행하는 것","安全한 읽기 전용 작업을 위한 작업의 샌드박스화"],"es":["Ejecutar tareas con esfuerzos de razonamiento variables","Anular los modelos predeterminados para tareas especializadas","Crear un entorno aislado para operaciones de solo lectura seguras"],"fr":["Exécuter des tâches avec des efforts de raisonnement variables","Substituer les modèles par défaut pour des tâches spécialisées","Créer un environnement sandboxé pour des opérations de lecture seule sécurisées"],"de":["Aufgaben mit variablen Denkleistungsanstrengungen ausführen","Standardmodelle für spezielle Aufgaben überschreiben","Ein Sandbox-Umfeld für sichere schreibgeschützte Operationen erstellen"],"pt":["Executar tarefas com esforços de raciocínio variáveis","Substituir modelos padrão para tarefas especializadas","Sandboxing de tarefas para operações seguras de apenas leitura"],"ru":["Выполнение задач с переменными усилиями рассуждения","Замена стандартных моделей для специализированных задач","Сandboxing задач для безопасных операций только для чтения"],"ar":["تنفيذ المهام مع جهود التفكير المتغيرة","استبدال النماذج الافتراضية للمهام المتخصصة","sandboxing المهام للعمليات الآمنة للقراءة فقط"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input for reasoning effort and model override","Default model set to `gpt-5.2` unless overridden","Sandbox mode defaults to `read-only` unless edits or network access are necessary"],"zh":["需要用户输入推理努力和模型重写","默认模型设置为 `gpt-5.2`，除非被重写","沙盒模式默认为 `read-only`，除非需要编辑或网络访问"],"ja":["推論労力とモデルオーバーライドのためにユーザー入力を必要とする","デフォルトモデルが `gpt-5.2` に設定されることを除き、オーバーライドされる","サンドボックスモードが `read-only` にデフォルト設定されることを除き、編集またはネットワークアクセスが必要な場合は変更される"],"ko":["推論 노력과 모델 재정의를 위한 사용자 입력이 필요함","기본 모델이 `gpt-5.2`로 설정되며, 재정의되지 않는 한 변경되지 않음","샌드박스 모드가 `read-only`로 기본 설정되며, 편집 또는 네트워크 접근이 필요한 경우에만 변경됨"],"es":["Requiere la entrada del usuario para el esfuerzo de razonamiento y la anulación del modelo","El modelo predeterminado se establece en `gpt-5.2` a menos que se anule","El modo sandbox se establece de forma predeterminada en `de solo lectura` a menos que se necesiten ediciones o acceso a la red"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée utilisateur pour les efforts de raisonnement et la substitution de modèle","Le modèle par défaut est défini sur `gpt-5.2` sauf si celui-ci est substitué","Le mode sandbox est défini par défaut sur `en lecture seule` sauf si des éditions ou un accès au réseau sont nécessaires"],"de":["Benutzereingabe für Denkleistungsanstrengung und Modellüberschreibung erforderlich","Das Standardmodell wird auf `gpt-5.2` festgelegt, sofern es nicht überschrieben wird","Der Sandbox-Modus wird standardmäßig auf `schreibgeschützt` festgelegt, sofern keine Bearbeitungen oder Netzwerkzugriff erforderlich sind"],"pt":["Requer entrada do usuário para esforço de raciocínio e substituição de modelo","Modelo padrão definido como `gpt-5.2` a menos que substituído","Modo sandbox padrão definido como `read-only` a menos que edição ou acesso à rede sejam necessários"],"ru":["Требует ввода пользователя для усилий рассуждения и замены модели","Стандартная модель задана как `gpt-5.2`, если не заменена","Режим песочницы по умолчанию задан как `read-only`, если редактирование или доступ к сети не необходимы"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال المستخدم لجهود التفكير وبدائل النموذج","النموذج الافتراضي محدد كـ `gpt-5.2` إلا إذا تم استبداله","الوضع الرمل defaults إلى `read-only` trừ إذا كان التعديل أو الوصول إلى الشبكة ضروريان"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/nextjs-app-router-patterns', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'nextjs-app-router-patterns', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z', '2026-02-18T12:59:13.422Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/nextjs-app-router-patterns","name":"nextjs-app-router-patterns","description":{"zh":"Next.js 应用路由器模式提供了构建现代全栈 React 应用的综合指南","ja":"Next.js アプリルーター パターンは、モダンなフルスタック React アプリを構築するための包括的なガイドを提供します","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터 패턴은 현대적인 풀스택 리액트 애플리케이션을 구축하기 위한 포괄적인 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"Patrones de enrutador de aplicaciones para Next.js 14+ con Server Components y desarrollo full-stack React","fr":"Modèles de routage d''applications pour Next.js 14+ avec des composants serveur et développement full-stack React","de":"App-Router-Muster für Next.js 14+ mit Server-Komponenten und Full-Stack-React-Entwicklung","pt":"Padrões de roteamento de aplicativos Next.js para desenvolvimento full-stack moderno com Server Components e App Router","ru":"Шаблоны маршрутизации приложений Next.js для современного полноэкранного разработки с Server Components и App Router","ar":"نماذج توجيه تطبيقات Next.js لتطوير تطبيقات متكاملة حديثة مع Server Components و App Router","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Next.js 应用路由器模式","ja":"Next.js アプリルーター パターン","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터 패턴","es":"Patrones de enrutador de aplicaciones Next.js","fr":"Modèles de routage d''applications Next.js","de":"Next.js App-Router-Muster","pt":"Padrões de Roteamento de Aplicativos Next.js","ru":"Шаблоны маршрутизации приложений Next.js","ar":"نماذج توجيه تطبيقات Next.js","en":"nextjs-app-router-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"Next.js 应用路由器模式提供了构建现代全栈 React 应用的综合指南","ja":"Next.js アプリルーター パターンは、モダンなフルスタック React アプリを構築するための包括的なガイドを提供します","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터 패턴은 현대적인 풀스택 리액트 애플리케이션을 구축하기 위한 포괄적인 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"Patrones de enrutador de aplicaciones para Next.js 14+ con Server Components y desarrollo full-stack React","fr":"Modèles de routage d''applications pour Next.js 14+ avec des composants serveur et développement full-stack React","de":"App-Router-Muster für Next.js 14+ mit Server-Komponenten und Full-Stack-React-Entwicklung","pt":"Padrões de roteamento de aplicativos Next.js para desenvolvimento full-stack moderno com Server Components e App Router","ru":"Шаблоны маршрутизации приложений Next.js для современного полноэкранного разработки с Server Components и App Router","ar":"نماذج توجيه تطبيقات Next.js لتطوير تطبيقات متكاملة حديثة مع Server Components و App Router","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持 Next.js 14+ 应用路由器架构","实现服务器组件和流媒体","设置并行和拦截路由","优化数据获取和缓存","构建全栈功能与服务器操作"],"ja":["Next.js 14+ アプリルーター アーキテクチャのサポート","サーバーコンポーネントとストリーミングの実装","並行とインターセプト ルーティングの設定","データ取得とキャッシュの最適化","フルスタック機能とサーバー アクションの構築"],"ko":["Next.js 14+ 애플리케이션 라우터 아키텍처 지원","서버 컴포넌트와 스트리밍 구현","병렬 및 인터셉트 라우팅 설정","데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱 최적화","풀스택 기능 및 서버 액션 구축"],"es":["Arquitectura de App Router para Next.js 14+","Implementación de Server Components y streaming","Configuración de rutas paralelas e interceptadoras","Optimización de la recuperación de datos y caché","Desarrollo de características full-stack con Server Actions"],"fr":["Architecture de routage d''applications pour Next.js 14+","Mise en œuvre de composants serveur et de streaming","Configuration de routes parallèles et d''interception","Optimisation de la récupération de données et du cache","Développement de fonctionnalités full-stack avec des actions de serveur"],"de":["App-Router-Architektur für Next.js 14+","Implementierung von Server-Komponenten und Streaming","Einrichtung von parallelen und abfangenden Routen","Optimierung der Datenabruf und Caching","Entwicklung von Full-Stack-Funktionen mit Server-Aktionen"],"pt":["Roteamento de aplicativos com App Router","Implementação de Server Components e streaming","Configuração de rotas paralelas e interceptação","Otimização de busca de dados e cache","Desenvolvimento de recursos full-stack com Server Actions"],"ru":["Маршрутизация приложений с App Router","Реализация Server Components и потоковой передачи","Настройка параллельных и перехватывающих маршрутов","Оптимизация поиска данных и кэша","Разработка полноэкранных функций с Server Actions"],"ar":["توجيه تطبيقات مع App Router","تنفيذ Server Components و البث","تكوين مسارات متوازية و اعتراض","تحسين استرجاع البيانات و الذاكرة المؤقتة","بناء ميزات متكاملة مع Server Actions"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Next.js","应用路由器","服务器组件","全栈 React","现代前端开发","路由器模式"],"ja":["Next.js","アプリルーター","サーバーコンポーネント","フルスタック React","モダンなフロントエンド開発","ルーティング パターン"],"ko":["Next.js","애플리케이션 라우터","서버 컴포넌트","풀스택 리액트","현대적인 프론트엔드 개발","라우팅 패턴"],"es":["Next.js","App Router","Server Components","full-stack React","desarrollo web","arquitectura de aplicaciones","patrones de enrutador"],"fr":["Next.js","routage d''applications","composants serveur","full-stack React","développement web","architecture d''applications","modèles de routage"],"de":["Next.js","App-Router","Server-Komponenten","Full-Stack-React","Webentwicklung","Anwendungsarchitektur","App-Router-Muster"],"pt":["Next.js","App Router","Server Components","Desenvolvimento full-stack","Roteamento de aplicativos","Otimização de busca de dados","Cache","Server Actions"],"ru":["Next.js","App Router","Server Components","Полноэкранная разработка","Маршрутизация приложений","Оптимизация поиска данных","Кэш","Server Actions"],"ar":["Next.js","App Router","Server Components","تطوير تطبيقات متكاملة","توجيه تطبيقات","تحسين استرجاع البيانات","الذاكرة المؤقتة","Server Actions"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nextjs-app-router-patterns","description":"Master Next.js 14+ App Router with Server Components, streaming, parallel routes, and advanced data fetching. Use when building Next.js applications, implementing SSR/SSG, or optimizing React Server Components.","bodyPreview":"# Next.js App Router Patterns\n\nComprehensive patterns for Next.js 14+ App Router architecture, Server Components, and modern full-stack React development.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building new Next.js applications with App Router\n- Migrating from Pages Router to App Router\n- Implementing Server Components and streaming\n- Setting up parallel and intercepting routes\n- Optimizing data fetching and caching\n- Building full-stack features with Server Actions\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Rendering Mo","body":"# Next.js App Router Patterns\n\nComprehensive patterns for Next.js 14+ App Router architecture, Server Components, and modern full-stack React development.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building new Next.js applications with App Router\n- Migrating from Pages Router to App Router\n- Implementing Server Components and streaming\n- Setting up parallel and intercepting routes\n- Optimizing data fetching and caching\n- Building full-stack features with Server Actions\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Rendering Modes\n\n| Mode                  | Where        | When to Use                               |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| **Server Components** | Server only  | Data fetching, heavy computation, secrets |\n| **Client Components** | Browser      | Interactivity, hooks, browser APIs        |\n| **Static**            | Build time   | Content that rarely changes               |\n| **Dynamic**           | Request time | Personalized or real-time data            |\n| **Streaming**         | Progressive  | Large pages, slow data sources            |\n\n### 2. File Conventions\n\n```\napp/\n├── layout.tsx       # Shared UI wrapper\n├── page.tsx         # Route UI\n├── loading.tsx      # Loading UI (Suspense)\n├── error.tsx        # Error boundary\n├── not-found.tsx    # 404 UI\n├── route.ts         # API endpoint\n├── template.tsx     # Re-mounted layout\n├── default.tsx      # Parallel route fallback\n└── opengraph-image.tsx  # OG image generation\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\n// app/layout.tsx\nimport { Inter } from ''next/font/google''\nimport { Providers } from ''./providers''\n\nconst inter = Inter({ subsets: [''latin''] })\n\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: { default: ''My App'', template: ''%s | My App'' },\n  description: ''Built with Next.js App Router'',\n}\n\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\" suppressHydrationWarning>\n      <body className={inter.className}>\n        <Providers>{children}</Providers>\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/page.tsx - Server Component by default\nasync function getProducts() {\n  const res = await fetch(''https://api.example.com/products'', {\n    next: { revalidate: 3600 }, // ISR: revalidate every hour\n  })\n  return res.json()\n}\n\nexport default async function HomePage() {\n  const products = await getProducts()\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Products</h1>\n      <ProductGrid products={products} />\n    </main>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Server Components with Data Fetching\n\n```typescript\n// app/products/page.tsx\nimport { Suspense } from ''react''\nimport { ProductList, ProductListSkeleton } from ''@/components/products''\nimport { FilterSidebar } from ''@/components/filters''\n\ninterface SearchParams {\n  category?: string\n  sort?: ''price'' | ''name'' | ''date''\n  page?: string\n}\n\nexport default async function ProductsPage({\n  searchParams,\n}: {\n  searchParams: Promise<SearchParams>\n}) {\n  const params = await searchParams\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex gap-8\">\n      <FilterSidebar />\n      <Suspense\n        key={JSON.stringify(params)}\n        fallback={<ProductListSkeleton />}\n      >\n        <ProductList\n          category={params.category}\n          sort={params.sort}\n          page={Number(params.page) || 1}\n        />\n      </Suspense>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// components/products/ProductList.tsx - Server Component\nasync function getProducts(filters: ProductFilters) {\n  const res = await fetch(\n    `${process.env.API_URL}/products?${new URLSearchParams(filters)}`,\n    { next: { tags: [''products''] } }\n  )\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(''Failed to fetch products'')\n  return res.json()\n}\n\nexport async function ProductList({ category, sort, page }: ProductFilters) {\n  const { products, totalPages } = await getProducts({ category, sort, page })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div className=\"grid grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n        {products.map((product) => (\n          <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />\n        ))}\n      </div>\n      <Pagination currentPage={page} totalPages={totalPages} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Client Components with ''use client''\n\n```typescript\n// components/products/AddToCartButton.tsx\n''use client''\n\nimport { useState, useTransition } from ''react''\nimport { addToCart } from ''@/app/actions/cart''\n\nexport function AddToCartButton({ productId }: { productId: string }) {\n  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition()\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    setError(null)\n    startTransition(async () => {\n      const result = await addToCart(productId)\n      if (result.error) {\n        setError(result.error)\n      }\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={handleClick}\n        disabled={isPending}\n        className=\"btn-primary\"\n      >\n        {isPending ? ''Adding...'' : ''Add to Cart''}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p className=\"text-red-500 text-sm\">{error}</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Server Actions\n\n```typescript\n// app/actions/cart.ts\n\"use server\";\n\nimport { revalidateTag } from \"next/cache\";\nimport { cookies } from \"next/headers\";\nimport { redirect } from \"next/navigation\";\n\nexport async function addToCart(productId: string) {\n  const cookieStore = await cookies();\n  const sessionId = cookieStore.get(\"session\")?.value;\n\n  if (!sessionId) {\n    redirect(\"/login\");\n  }\n\n  try {\n    await db.cart.upsert({\n      where: { sessionId_productId: { sessionId, productId } },\n      update: { quantity: { increment: 1 } },\n      create: { sessionId, productId, quantity: 1 },\n    });\n\n    revalidateTag(\"cart\");\n    return { success: true };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { error: \"Failed to add item to cart\" };\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function checkout(formData: FormData) {\n  const address = formData.get(\"address\") as string;\n  const payment = formData.get(\"payment\") as string;\n\n  // Validate\n  if (!address || !payment) {\n    return { error: \"Missing required fields\" };\n  }\n\n  // Process order\n  const order = await processOrder({ address, payment });\n\n  // Redirect to confirmation\n  redirect(`/orders/${order.id}/confirmation`);\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Parallel Routes\n\n```typescript\n// app/dashboard/layout.tsx\nexport default function DashboardLayout({\n  children,\n  analytics,\n  team,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n  analytics: React.ReactNode\n  team: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"dashboard-grid\">\n      <main>{children}</main>\n      <aside className=\"analytics-panel\">{analytics}</aside>\n      <aside className=\"team-panel\">{team}</aside>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/dashboard/@analytics/page.tsx\nexport default async function AnalyticsSlot() {\n  const stats = await getAnalytics()\n  return <AnalyticsChart data={stats} />\n}\n\n// app/dashboard/@analytics/loading.tsx\nexport default function AnalyticsLoading() {\n  return <ChartSkeleton />\n}\n\n// app/dashboard/@team/page.tsx\nexport default async function TeamSlot() {\n  const members = await getTeamMembers()\n  return <TeamList members={members} />\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Intercepting Routes (Modal Pattern)\n\n```typescript\n// File structure for photo modal\n// app/\n// ├── @modal/\n// │   ├── (.)photos/[id]/page.tsx  # Intercept\n// │   └── default.tsx\n// ├── photos/\n// │   └── [id]/page.tsx            # Full page\n// └── layout.tsx\n\n// app/@modal/(.)photos/[id]/page.tsx\nimport { Modal } from ''@/components/Modal''\nimport { PhotoDetail } from ''@/components/PhotoDetail''\n\nexport default async function PhotoModal({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n}) {\n  const { id } = await params\n  const photo = await getPhoto(id)\n\n  return (\n    <Modal>\n      <PhotoDetail photo={photo} />\n    </Modal>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/photos/[id]/page.tsx - Full page version\nexport default async function PhotoPage({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n}) {\n  const { id } = await params\n  const photo = await getPhoto(id)\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"photo-page\">\n      <PhotoDetail photo={photo} />\n      <RelatedPhotos photoId={id} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// app/layout.tsx\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n  modal,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n  modal: React.ReactNode\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        {modal}\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Streaming with Suspense\n\n```typescript\n// app/product/[id]/page.tsx\nimport { Suspense } from ''react''\n\nexport default async function ProductPage({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n}) {\n  const { id } = await params\n\n  // This data loads first (blocking)\n  const product = await getProduct(id)\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Immediate render */}\n      <ProductHeader product={product} />\n\n      {/* Stream in reviews */}\n      <Suspense fallback={<ReviewsSkeleton />}>\n        <Reviews productId={id} />\n      </Suspense>\n\n      {/* Stream in recommendations */}\n      <Suspense fallback={<RecommendationsSkeleton />}>\n        <Recommendations productId={id} />\n      </Suspense>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// These components fetch their own data\nasync function Reviews({ productId }: { productId: string }) {\n  const reviews = await getReviews(productId) // Slow API\n  return <ReviewList reviews={reviews} />\n}\n\nasync function Recommendations({ productId }: { productId: string }) {\n  const products = await getRecommendations(productId) // ML-based, slow\n  return <ProductCarousel products={products} />\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: Route Handlers (API Routes)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/products/route.ts\nimport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\n\nexport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  const searchParams = request.nextUrl.searchParams;\n  const category = searchParams.get(\"category\");\n\n  const products = await db.product.findMany({\n    where: category ? { category } : undefined,\n    take: 20,\n  });\n\n  return NextResponse.json(products);\n}\n\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  const body = await request.json();\n\n  const product = await db.product.create({\n    data: body,\n  });\n\n  return NextResponse.json(product, { status: 201 });\n}\n\n// app/api/products/[id]/route.ts\nexport async function GET(\n  request: NextRequest,\n  { params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> },\n) {\n  const { id } = await params;\n  const product = await db.product.findUnique({ where: { id } });\n\n  if (!product) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Product not found\" }, { status: 404 });\n  }\n\n  return NextResponse.json(product);\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 8: Metadata and SEO\n\n```typescript\n// app/products/[slug]/page.tsx\nimport { Metadata } from ''next''\nimport { notFound } from ''next/navigation''\n\ntype Props = {\n  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>\n}\n\nexport async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {\n  const { slug } = await params\n  const product = await getProduct(slug)\n\n  if (!product) return {}\n\n  return {\n    title: product.name,\n    description: product.description,\n    openGraph: {\n      title: product.name,\n      description: product.description,\n      images: [{ url: product.image, width: 1200, height: 630 }],\n    },\n    twitter: {\n      card: ''summary_large_image'',\n      title: product.name,\n      description: product.description,\n      images: [product.image],\n    },\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function generateStaticParams() {\n  const products = await db.product.findMany({ select: { slug: true } })\n  return products.map((p) => ({ slug: p.slug }))\n}\n\nexport default async function ProductPage({ params }: Props) {\n  const { slug } = await params\n  const product = await getProduct(slug)\n\n  if (!product) notFound()\n\n  return <ProductDetail product={product} />\n}\n```\n\n## Caching Strategies\n\n### Data Cache\n\n```typescript\n// No cache (always fresh)\nfetch(url, { cache: \"no-store\" });\n\n// Cache forever (static)\nfetch(url, { cache: \"force-cache\" });\n\n// ISR - revalidate after 60 seconds\nfetch(url, { next: { revalidate: 60 } });\n\n// Tag-based invalidation\nfetch(url, { next: { tags: [\"products\"] } });\n\n// Invalidate via Server Action\n(\"use server\");\nimport { revalidateTag, revalidatePath } from \"next/cache\";\n\nexport async function updateProduct(id: string, data: ProductData) {\n  await db.product.update({ where: { id }, data });\n  revalidateTag(\"products\");\n  revalidatePath(\"/products\");\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Start with Server Components** - Add ''use client'' only when needed\n- **Colocate data fetching** - Fetch data where it''s used\n- **Use Suspense boundaries** - Enable streaming for slow data\n- **Leverage parallel routes** - Independent loading states\n- **Use Server Actions** - For mutations with progressive enhancement\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t pass serializable data** - Server → Client boundary limitations\n- **Don''t use hooks in Server Components** - No useState, useEffect\n- **Don''t fetch in Client Components** - Use Server Components or React Query\n- **Don''t over-nest layouts** - Each layout adds to the component tree\n- **Don''t ignore loading states** - Always provide loading.tsx or Suspense\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Next.js App Router Documentation](https://nextjs.org/docs/app)\n- [Server Components RFC](https://github.com/reactjs/rfcs/blob/main/text/0188-server-components.md)\n- [Vercel Templates](https://vercel.com/templates/next.js)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:59:13.422Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full-Stack Agents needing advanced Next.js App Router architecture and Server Components integration.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Next.js App Router 架构和服务器组件集成的全栈代理。","ja":"Next.js App Router アーキテクチャとサーバー コンポーネントの統合が必要なフルスタック エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Next.js App Router 아키텍처와 서버 컴포넌트 통합이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Full-Stack que necesitan una arquitectura avanzada de App Router de Next.js y una integración de Componentes de Servidor.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full-Stack ayant besoin d''une architecture avancée de App Router de Next.js et d''une intégration de Composants de Serveur.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine fortschrittliche App Router-Architektur und eine Integration von Server-Komponenten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full-Stack que necessitam de arquitetura avançada de Next.js App Router e integração de Componentes de Servidor.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full-Stack, которым требуется продвинутая архитектура Next.js App Router и интеграция с Серверными Компонентами.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الكاملين الذين يحتاجون إلى هيكل متقدم لموجه التطبيقات Next.js وتكامل مكونات الخادم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build modern full-stack React applications with optimized data fetching and caching using Next.js 14+ App Router, Server Components, and parallel routing patterns.","zh":"赋予代理构建现代化全栈 React 应用程序的能力，使用 Next.js 14+ App Router、服务器组件和并行路由模式实现优化的数据获取和缓存。","ja":"Next.js 14+ App Router、サーバー コンポーネント、並列ルーティング パターンを使用して、最適化されたデータ取得とキャッシュを実現することで、モダンなフルスタック React アプリケーションの構築をエージェントに可能にします。","ko":"Next.js 14+ App Router, 서버 컴포넌트 및 병렬 路由 패턴을 사용하여 최적화된 데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱을 구현함으로써 현대적인 풀스택 React 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear aplicaciones full-stack de React modernas con obtención y almacenamiento en caché de datos optimizados utilizando App Router de Next.js 14+, Componentes de Servidor y patrones de enrutamiento paralelo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des applications full-stack React modernes avec une obtention et un stockage de données optimisés en utilisant App Router de Next.js 14+, Composants de Serveur et des modèles d''acheminement parallèle.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, moderne Full-Stack-React-Anwendungen mit optimierter Datenabfrage und -zwischenspeicherung zu erstellen, indem sie Next.js 14+ App Router, Server-Komponenten und parallele Routing-Muster verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir aplicações React de pilha completa modernas com busca de dados otimizada e cache utilizando o Next.js 14+ App Router, Componentes de Servidor e padrões de roteamento paralelo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать современные полнофункциональные приложения React с оптимизированным получением данных и кэшированием, используя Next.js 14+ App Router, Серверные Компоненты и параллельные шаблоны маршрутизации.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من بناء تطبيقات رياكت حديثة بالكامل مع جلب بيانات محسّن وتخزين مؤقت باستخدام موجه تطبيقات Next.js 14+ ومكونات الخادم وأنماط التوجيه الموازي."},"useCases":{"en":["Migrating legacy Pages Router applications to App Router","Implementing Server Components for streaming and dynamic rendering","Optimizing data fetching and caching for improved performance"],"zh":["将传统的 Pages Router 应用程序迁移到 App Router","为流媒体和动态渲染实现服务器组件","优化数据获取和缓存以提高性能"],"ja":["レガシーの Pages Router アプリケーションを App Router に移行する","ストリーミングと動的レンダリングのためにサーバー コンポーネントを実装する","パフォーマンスの向上のためにデータ取得とキャッシュを最適化する"],"ko":["레거시 Pages Router 애플리케이션을 App Router로 마이그레이션","스트리밍 및 동적 렌더링을 위한 서버 컴포넌트 구현","성능 향상을 위한 데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱 최적화"],"es":["Migrar aplicaciones de Pages Router heredadas a App Router","Implementar Componentes de Servidor para transmisión y renderizado dinámico","Optimizar la obtención y el almacenamiento en caché de datos para un mejor rendimiento"],"fr":["Migrer des applications Pages Router héritées vers App Router","Implémenter des Composants de Serveur pour le streaming et le rendu dynamique","Optimiser la récupération et le stockage de données pour améliorer les performances"],"de":["Migration von Legacy-Pages-Router-Anwendungen zu App Router","Implementierung von Server-Komponenten für Streaming und dynamisches Rendern","Optimierung der Datenabfrage und -zwischenspeicherung für verbesserte Leistung"],"pt":["Migrar aplicações legadas do Pages Router para o App Router","Implementar Componentes de Servidor para transmissão e renderização dinâmica","Otimizar a busca de dados e o cache para melhorar o desempenho"],"ru":["Миграция устаревших приложений Pages Router на App Router","Реализация Серверных Компонентов для потоковой передачи и динамического рендеринга","Оптимизация получения данных и кэширования для улучшения производительности"],"ar":["نقل تطبيقات Pages Router القديمة إلى موجه التطبيقات","تطبيق مكونات الخادم للبث والتحديث الديناميكي","تحسين جلب البيانات وتخزينها المؤقت لتحسين الأداء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Next.js 14 or higher","Limited to React-based applications"],"zh":["需要 Next.js 14 或更高版本","仅限于基于 React 的应用程序"],"ja":["Next.js 14 以上が必要","React ベースのアプリケーションに限定される"],"ko":["Next.js 14 이상이 필요","React 기반 애플리케이션으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere Next.js 14 o superior","Limitado a aplicaciones basadas en React"],"fr":["Nécessite Next.js 14 ou supérieur","Limité aux applications basées sur React"],"de":["Benötigt Next.js 14 oder höher","Begrenzt auf React-basierte Anwendungen"],"pt":["Requer Next.js 14 ou superior","Limitado a aplicações baseadas em React"],"ru":["Требуется Next.js 14 или выше","Ограничен для приложений на основе React"],"ar":["يتطلب Next.js 14 أو أعلى","محدود لتطبيقات قاعدة رياكت"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/tinacms', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'tinacms', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z', '2026-02-18T12:59:27.330Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/tinacms","name":"tinacms","description":{"zh":"TinaCMS是一个基于Git的头部CMS，提供可视化编辑功能，适用于内容密集型网站。支持pnpm、npm和yarn等包管理器","ja":"TinaCMSはGitベースのヘッドレスCMSで、ビジュアルエディタ機能を提供し、コンテンツ重視のサイトに適しています。pnpm、npm、yarnなどのパッケージマネージャーをサポートしています","ko":"TinaCMS는 Git 기반의 헤드리스 CMS로, 시각적 편집 기능을 제공하여 콘텐츠가 많은 웹사이트에 적합합니다. pnpm, npm, yarn 등의 패키지 매니저를 지원합니다","es":"TinaCMS es un CMS headless con edición visual para sitios web con mucho contenido. Ofrece una forma fácil de administrar contenido sin sacrificar la personalización.","fr":"TinaCMS est un CMS headless avec édition visuelle pour les sites web à fort contenu. Il offre un moyen facile de gérer le contenu sans sacrifier la personnalisation.","de":"TinaCMS ist ein headless CMS mit visueller Bearbeitung für inhaltsreiche Websites. Es bietet eine einfache Möglichkeit, Inhalte zu verwalten, ohne die Anpassungsfähigkeit zu beeinträchtigen.","pt":"TinaCMS é um CMS headless com edição visual para sites com muito conteúdo. Ele oferece uma solução escalável e flexível para gerenciar conteúdo","ru":"TinaCMS - это Гит-бэкенд CMS с визуальным редактированием для сайтов с большим количеством контента. Он предлагает масштабируемое и гибкое решение для управления контентом","ar":"TinaCMS هو نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس مع تحرير مرئي لsites ذات المحتوى الكثيف. يقدم حلًا مرنًا ومتجاوبًا لإدارة المحتوى","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"TinaCMS: 基于Git的头部CMS","ja":"TinaCMS: GitベースのヘッドレスCMS","ko":"TinaCMS: Git 기반 헤드리스 CMS","es":"TinaCMS: CMS Headless con Edición Visual","fr":"TinaCMS: CMS Headless avec Édition Visuelle","de":"TinaCMS: Headless CMS mit visueller Bearbeitung","pt":"TinaCMS: CMS Headless com Edição Visual","ru":"TinaCMS: Гит-бэкенд CMS с визуальным редактированием","ar":"TinaCMS: نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس مع تحرير مرئي","en":"tinacms"},"description":{"zh":"TinaCMS是一个基于Git的头部CMS，提供可视化编辑功能，适用于内容密集型网站。支持pnpm、npm和yarn等包管理器","ja":"TinaCMSはGitベースのヘッドレスCMSで、ビジュアルエディタ機能を提供し、コンテンツ重視のサイトに適しています。pnpm、npm、yarnなどのパッケージマネージャーをサポートしています","ko":"TinaCMS는 Git 기반의 헤드리스 CMS로, 시각적 편집 기능을 제공하여 콘텐츠가 많은 웹사이트에 적합합니다. pnpm, npm, yarn 등의 패키지 매니저를 지원합니다","es":"TinaCMS es un CMS headless con edición visual para sitios web con mucho contenido. Ofrece una forma fácil de administrar contenido sin sacrificar la personal...","fr":"TinaCMS est un CMS headless avec édition visuelle pour les sites web à fort contenu. Il offre un moyen facile de gérer le contenu sans sacrifier la personnal...","de":"TinaCMS ist ein headless CMS mit visueller Bearbeitung für inhaltsreiche Websites. Es bietet eine einfache Möglichkeit, Inhalte zu verwalten, ohne die Anpass...","pt":"TinaCMS é um CMS headless com edição visual para sites com muito conteúdo. Ele oferece uma solução escalável e flexível para gerenciar conteúdo","ru":"TinaCMS - это Гит-бэкенд CMS с визуальным редактированием для сайтов с большим количеством контента. Он предлагает масштабируемое и гибкое решение для управл...","ar":"TinaCMS هو نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس مع تحرير مرئي لsites ذات المحتوى الكثيف. يقدم حلًا مرنًا ومتجاوبًا لإدارة المحتوى","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["基于Git的头部CMS","可视化编辑功能","支持pnpm、npm和yarn","适用于内容密集型网站"],"ja":["GitベースのヘッドレスCMS","ビジュアルエディタ機能","pnpm、npm、yarnのサポート","コンテンツ重視のサイトに適しています"],"ko":["Git 기반의 헤드리스 CMS","시각적 편집 기능","pnpm, npm, yarn의 지원","콘텐츠가 많은 웹사이트에 적합합니다"],"es":["Edición visual para sitios web","Backend basado en Git","Compatibilidad con pnpm, npm y yarn","Instalación fácil con @tinacms/cli","Personalización avanzada"],"fr":["Édition visuelle pour les sites web","Backend basé sur Git","Compatibilité avec pnpm, npm et yarn","Installation facile avec @tinacms/cli","Personnalisation avancée"],"de":["Visuelle Bearbeitung für Websites","Git-basiertes Backend","Kompatibilität mit pnpm, npm und yarn","Einfache Installation mit @tinacms/cli","Erweiterte Anpassung"],"pt":["Edição visual para sites com muito conteúdo","Integração com o Git para versionamento de conteúdo","Suporte a vários formatos de arquivo","Flexibilidade e escalabilidade para gerenciar conteúdo","Compatibilidade com pnpm, npm e yarn"],"ru":["Визуальное редактирование для сайтов с большим количеством контента","Интеграция с Git для версионирования контента","Поддержка нескольких форматов файлов","Гибкость и масштабируемость для управления контентом","Совместимость с pnpm, npm и yarn"],"ar":["تحرير مرئي لsites ذات المحتوى الكثيف","التكامل مع Git لنسخ المحتوى","دعم صيغ ملفات متعددة","مرنة ومتجاوبة لإدارة المحتوى","التوافق مع pnpm وnpm وyarn"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TinaCMS","头部CMS","Git","可视化编辑","内容管理系统","pnpm","npm","yarn"],"ja":["TinaCMS","ヘッドレスCMS","Git","ビジュアルエディタ","コンテンツ管理システム","pnpm","npm","yarn"],"ko":["TinaCMS","헤드리스 CMS","Git","시각적 편집","콘텐츠 관리 시스템","pnpm","npm","yarn"],"es":["TinaCMS","CMS headless","edición visual","sitios web con mucho contenido","pnpm","npm","yarn","Git","desarrollo web"],"fr":["TinaCMS","CMS headless","édition visuelle","sites web à fort contenu","pnpm","npm","yarn","Git","développement web"],"de":["TinaCMS","headless CMS","visuelle Bearbeitung","inhaltsreiche Websites","pnpm","npm","yarn","Git","Webentwicklung"],"pt":["TinaCMS","CMS headless","edição visual","gerenciamento de conteúdo","Git","pnpm","npm","yarn","desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["TinaCMS","Гит-бэкенд CMS","визуальное редактирование","управление контентом","Git","pnpm","npm","yarn","веб-разработка"],"ar":["TinaCMS","نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس","تحرير مرئي","إدارة المحتوى","Git","pnpm","npm","yarn","تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tinacms","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# TinaCMS\n\nGit-backed headless CMS with visual editing for content-heavy sites.\n\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-21\n**Versions**: tinacms@3.3.1, @tinacms/cli@2.1.1\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Package Manager Recommendation:**\n- **Recommended**: pnpm (required for TinaCMS >2.7.3)\n- **Alternative**: npm or yarn (may have module resolution issues in newer versions)\n\n```bash\n# Install pnpm (if needed)\nnpm install -g pnpm\n\n# Initialize TinaCMS\nnpx @tinacms/cli@latest init\n\n# Install dependencies with pnpm\npnpm","body":"# TinaCMS\n\nGit-backed headless CMS with visual editing for content-heavy sites.\n\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-21\n**Versions**: tinacms@3.3.1, @tinacms/cli@2.1.1\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Package Manager Recommendation:**\n- **Recommended**: pnpm (required for TinaCMS >2.7.3)\n- **Alternative**: npm or yarn (may have module resolution issues in newer versions)\n\n```bash\n# Install pnpm (if needed)\nnpm install -g pnpm\n\n# Initialize TinaCMS\nnpx @tinacms/cli@latest init\n\n# Install dependencies with pnpm\npnpm install\n\n# Update package.json scripts\n{\n  \"dev\": \"tinacms dev -c \\\"next dev\\\"\",\n  \"build\": \"tinacms build && next build\"\n}\n\n# Set environment variables\nNEXT_PUBLIC_TINA_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id\nTINA_TOKEN=your_read_only_token\n\n# Start dev server\npnpm run dev\n\n# Access admin interface\nhttp://localhost:3000/admin/index.html\n```\n\n**Version Locking (Recommended):**\n\nPin exact versions to prevent breaking changes from automatic CLI/UI updates:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"tinacms\": \"3.3.1\",  // NOT \"^3.3.1\"\n    \"@tinacms/cli\": \"2.1.1\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Why**: TinaCMS UI assets are served from CDN and may update before your local CLI, causing incompatibilities.\n\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #5838](https://github.com/tinacms/tinacms/issues/5838)\n\n---\n\n## Next.js Integration\n\n**useTina Hook** (enables visual editing):\n```tsx\nimport { useTina } from ''tinacms/dist/react''\nimport { client } from ''../../tina/__generated__/client''\n\nexport default function BlogPost(props) {\n  const { data } = useTina({\n    query: props.query,\n    variables: props.variables,\n    data: props.data\n  })\n\n  return <article><h1>{data.post.title}</h1></article>\n}\n\nexport async function getStaticProps({ params }) {\n  const response = await client.queries.post({\n    relativePath: `${params.slug}.md`\n  })\n\n  return {\n    props: {\n      data: response.data,\n      query: response.query,\n      variables: response.variables\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**App Router**: Admin route at `app/admin/[[...index]]/page.tsx`\n**Pages Router**: Admin route at `pages/admin/[[...index]].tsx`\n\n---\n\n## Schema Configuration\n\n**tina/config.ts** structure:\n```typescript\nimport { defineConfig } from ''tinacms''\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  branch: process.env.GITHUB_BRANCH || ''main'',\n  clientId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_TINA_CLIENT_ID,\n  token: process.env.TINA_TOKEN,\n  build: {\n    outputFolder: ''admin'',\n    publicFolder: ''public'',\n  },\n  schema: {\n    collections: [/* ... */],\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Collection Example** (Blog Post):\n```typescript\n{\n  name: ''post'',           // Alphanumeric + underscores only\n  label: ''Blog Posts'',\n  path: ''content/posts'',  // No trailing slash\n  format: ''mdx'',\n  fields: [\n    {\n      type: ''string'',\n      name: ''title'',\n      label: ''Title'',\n      isTitle: true,\n      required: true\n    },\n    {\n      type: ''rich-text'',\n      name: ''body'',\n      label: ''Body'',\n      isBody: true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Field Types**: `string`, `rich-text`, `number`, `datetime`, `boolean`, `image`, `reference`, `object`\n\n**Reference Field Note**: When a reference field references multiple collection types with shared field names, ensure the field types match. Conflicting types (e.g., `bio: string` vs `bio: rich-text`) cause GraphQL schema errors.\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Reference field referencing multiple collections\n{\n  type: ''reference'',\n  name: ''contributor'',\n  collections: [''author'', ''editor'']  // Ensure shared fields have same type\n}\n```\n\n**Source**: [Community-sourced](https://adamcogan.com/2024/08/27/7-important-updates-to-tinacms-2-0/)\n\n---\n\n## Common Errors & Solutions\n\n### 1. ❌ ESbuild Compilation Errors\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nERROR: Schema Not Successfully Built\nERROR: Config Not Successfully Executed\n```\n\n**Causes:**\n- Importing code with custom loaders (webpack, babel plugins, esbuild loaders)\n- Importing frontend-only code (uses `window`, DOM APIs, React hooks)\n- Importing entire component libraries instead of specific modules\n\n**Solution:**\n\nImport only what you need:\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad - Imports entire component directory\nimport { HeroComponent } from ''../components/''\n\n// ✅ Good - Import specific file\nimport { HeroComponent } from ''../components/blocks/hero''\n```\n\n**Prevention Tips:**\n- Keep `tina/config.ts` imports minimal\n- Only import type definitions and simple utilities\n- Avoid importing UI components directly\n- Create separate `.schema.ts` files if needed\n\n**Reference**: See `references/common-errors.md#esbuild`\n\n---\n\n### 2. ❌ Module Resolution: \"Could not resolve ''tinacms''\"\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nError: Could not resolve \"tinacms\"\n```\n\n**Causes:**\n- Corrupted or incomplete installation\n- Version mismatch between dependencies\n- Missing peer dependencies\n\n**Solution:**\n```bash\n# Clear cache and reinstall\nrm -rf node_modules package-lock.json\nnpm install\n\n# Or with pnpm\nrm -rf node_modules pnpm-lock.yaml\npnpm install\n\n# Or with yarn\nrm -rf node_modules yarn.lock\nyarn install\n```\n\n**Prevention:**\n- Use lockfiles (`package-lock.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `yarn.lock`)\n- Don''t use `--no-optional` or `--omit=optional` flags\n- Ensure `react` and `react-dom` are installed (even for non-React frameworks)\n\n---\n\n### 3. ❌ Field Naming Constraints\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nField name contains invalid characters\n```\n\n**Cause:**\n- TinaCMS field names can only contain: letters, numbers, underscores\n- Hyphens, spaces, special characters are NOT allowed\n\n**Solution:**\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad - Uses hyphens\n{\n  name: ''hero-image'',\n  label: ''Hero Image'',\n  type: ''image''\n}\n\n// ❌ Bad - Uses spaces\n{\n  name: ''hero image'',\n  label: ''Hero Image'',\n  type: ''image''\n}\n\n// ✅ Good - Uses underscores\n{\n  name: ''hero_image'',\n  label: ''Hero Image'',\n  type: ''image''\n}\n\n// ✅ Good - CamelCase also works\n{\n  name: ''heroImage'',\n  label: ''Hero Image'',\n  type: ''image''\n}\n```\n\n**Note**: This is a **breaking change** from Forestry.io migration\n\n---\n\n### 4. ❌ Docker Binding Issues\n\n**Error:**\n- TinaCMS admin not accessible from outside Docker container\n\n**Cause:**\n- TinaCMS binds to `127.0.0.1` (localhost only) by default\n- Docker containers need `0.0.0.0` binding to accept external connections\n\n**Solution:**\n```bash\n# Ensure framework dev server listens on all interfaces\ntinacms dev -c \"next dev --hostname 0.0.0.0\"\ntinacms dev -c \"vite --host 0.0.0.0\"\ntinacms dev -c \"astro dev --host 0.0.0.0\"\n```\n\n**Docker Compose Example:**\n```yaml\nservices:\n  app:\n    build: .\n    ports:\n      - \"3000:3000\"\n    command: npm run dev  # Which runs: tinacms dev -c \"next dev --hostname 0.0.0.0\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. ❌ Missing `_template` Key Error\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nGetCollection failed: Unable to fetch\ntemplate name was not provided\n```\n\n**Cause:**\n- Collection uses `templates` array (multiple schemas)\n- Document missing `_template` field in frontmatter\n- Migrating from `templates` to `fields` and documents not updated\n\n**Solution:**\n\n**Option 1: Use `fields` instead (recommended for single template)**\n```typescript\n{\n  name: ''post'',\n  path: ''content/posts'',\n  fields: [/* ... */]  // No _template needed\n}\n```\n\n**Option 2: Ensure `_template` exists in frontmatter**\n```yaml\n---\n_template: article  # ← Required when using templates array\ntitle: My Post\n---\n```\n\n**Migration Script** (if converting from templates to fields):\n```bash\n# Remove _template from all files in content/posts/\nfind content/posts -name \"*.md\" -exec sed -i ''/_template:/d'' {} +\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. ❌ Path Mismatch Issues\n\n**Error:**\n- Files not appearing in Tina admin\n- \"File not found\" errors when saving\n- GraphQL queries return empty results\n\n**Cause:**\n- `path` in collection config doesn''t match actual file directory\n- Relative vs absolute path confusion\n- Trailing slash issues\n\n**Solution:**\n```typescript\n// Files located at: content/posts/hello.md\n\n// ✅ Correct\n{\n  name: ''post'',\n  path: ''content/posts'',  // Matches file location\n  fields: [/* ... */]\n}\n\n// ❌ Wrong - Missing ''content/''\n{\n  name: ''post'',\n  path: ''posts'',  // Files won''t be found\n  fields: [/* ... */]\n}\n\n// ❌ Wrong - Trailing slash\n{\n  name: ''post'',\n  path: ''content/posts/'',  // May cause issues\n  fields: [/* ... */]\n}\n```\n\n**Debugging:**\n1. Run `npx @tinacms/cli@latest audit` to check paths\n2. Verify files exist in specified directory\n3. Check file extensions match `format` field\n\n---\n\n### 7. ❌ Build Script Ordering Problems\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nERROR: Cannot find module ''../tina/__generated__/client''\nERROR: Property ''queries'' does not exist on type ''{}''\n```\n\n**Cause:**\n- Framework build running before `tinacms build`\n- Tina types not generated before TypeScript compilation\n- CI/CD pipeline incorrect order\n\n**Solution:**\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tinacms build && next build\"  // ✅ Tina FIRST\n    // NOT: \"build\": \"next build && tinacms build\"  // ❌ Wrong order\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**CI/CD Example (GitHub Actions):**\n```yaml\n- name: Build\n  run: |\n    npx @tinacms/cli@latest build  # Generate types first\n    npm run build                   # Then build framework\n```\n\n**Why This Matters:**\n- `tinacms build` generates TypeScript types in `tina/__generated__/`\n- Framework build needs these types to compile successfully\n- Running in wrong order causes type errors\n\n---\n\n### 8. ❌ Failed Loading TinaCMS Assets\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nFailed to load resource: net::ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED\nhttp://localhost:4001/...\n```\n\n**Causes:**\n- Pushed development `admin/index.html` to production (loads assets from localhost)\n- Site served on subdirectory but `basePath` not configured\n\n**Solution:**\n\n**For Production Deploys:**\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tinacms build && next build\"  // ✅ Always build\n    // NOT: \"build\": \"tinacms dev\"          // ❌ Never dev in production\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**For Subdirectory Deployments:**\n\n> **⚠️ Sub-path Deployment Limitation**: TinaCMS has known issues loading assets correctly when deployed to a sub-path (e.g., `example.com/cms/admin` instead of `example.com/admin`). This is a limitation even with `basePath` configuration.\n>\n> **Workaround**: Deploy TinaCMS admin at root path (`/admin`) or use reverse proxy rewrite rules.\n>\n> **Source**: [Community-sourced](https://adamcogan.com/2024/08/27/7-important-updates-to-tinacms-2-0/)\n\n```typescript\n// tina/config.ts\nexport default defineConfig({\n  build: {\n    outputFolder: ''admin'',\n    publicFolder: ''public'',\n    basePath: ''your-subdirectory''  // ← May have asset loading issues on sub-paths\n  }\n})\n```\n\n**CI/CD Fix:**\n```yaml\n# GitHub Actions / Vercel / Netlify\n- run: npx @tinacms/cli@latest build  # Always use build, not dev\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. ❌ Reference Field 503 Service Unavailable\n\n**Error:**\n- Reference field dropdown times out with 503 error\n- Admin interface becomes unresponsive when loading reference field\n\n**Cause:**\n- Too many items in referenced collection (100s or 1000s)\n- No pagination support for reference fields currently\n\n**Solutions:**\n\n**Option 1: Split collections**\n```typescript\n// Instead of one huge \"authors\" collection\n// Split by active status or alphabetically\n\n{\n  name: ''active_author'',\n  label: ''Active Authors'',\n  path: ''content/authors/active'',\n  fields: [/* ... */]\n}\n\n{\n  name: ''archived_author'',\n  label: ''Archived Authors'',\n  path: ''content/authors/archived'',\n  fields: [/* ... */]\n}\n```\n\n**Option 2: Use string field with validation**\n```typescript\n// Instead of reference\n{\n  type: ''string'',\n  name: ''authorId'',\n  label: ''Author ID'',\n  ui: {\n    component: ''select'',\n    options: [''author-1'', ''author-2'', ''author-3'']  // Curated list\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Option 3: Custom field component** (advanced)\n- Implement pagination in custom component\n- See TinaCMS docs: https://tina.io/docs/extending-tina/custom-field-components/\n\n---\n\n### 10. ❌ Media Manager Upload Timeouts (Ghost Uploads)\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nUpload failed\nError uploading image\n```\n\n**Cause:**\n- Media Manager shows error but image uploads successfully in background\n- UI timeout doesn''t reflect actual upload status\n- Similar issue occurs with deletion (error shown but deletion succeeds)\n\n**Solution:**\n\nIf upload shows error:\n1. Wait 5-10 seconds\n2. Close and reopen Media Manager\n3. Check if image already uploaded before retrying\n4. Avoid duplicate upload attempts\n\n**Status**: Known issue (high priority)\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #6325](https://github.com/tinacms/tinacms/issues/6325)\n\n---\n\n## Deployment Options\n\n### TinaCloud (Managed) - Recommended\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Sign up at https://app.tina.io\n2. Get Client ID and Read Only Token\n3. Set env vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_TINA_CLIENT_ID`, `TINA_TOKEN`\n4. Deploy to Vercel/Netlify/Cloudflare Pages\n\n**Pros**: Zero config, free tier (10k requests/month)\n\n---\n\n### Self-Hosted on Node.js\n\n> **⚠️ Edge Runtime Limitation**: Self-hosted TinaCMS does NOT work in Edge Runtime environments (Cloudflare Workers, Vercel Edge Functions) due to Node.js dependencies in `@tinacms/datalayer` and `@tinacms/graphql`. Use TinaCloud (managed service) for edge deployments.\n>\n> **Source**: [GitHub Issue #4363](https://github.com/tinacms/tinacms/issues/4363) (labeled \"wontfix\")\n\n> **⚠️ Self-Hosted Examples May Be Outdated**: Official self-hosted examples in the TinaCMS repository are acknowledged by the team as \"quite out of date\". Always cross-reference with latest documentation instead of relying solely on example repos.\n>\n> **Source**: [GitHub Issue #6365](https://github.com/tinacms/tinacms/issues/6365)\n\n**For Node.js environments only** (not edge runtime):\n\n```bash\npnpm install @tinacms/datalayer tinacms-authjs\nnpx @tinacms/cli@latest init backend\n```\n\n**Example (Node.js server, not Workers)**:\n```typescript\nimport { TinaNodeBackend, LocalBackendAuthProvider } from ''@tinacms/datalayer''\nimport { AuthJsBackendAuthProvider, TinaAuthJSOptions } from ''tinacms-authjs''\nimport databaseClient from ''../../tina/__generated__/databaseClient''\n\nconst isLocal = process.env.TINA_PUBLIC_IS_LOCAL === ''true''\n\n// This ONLY works in Node.js runtime, NOT edge runtime\nconst handler = TinaNodeBackend({\n  authProvider: isLocal\n    ? LocalBackendAuthProvider()\n    : AuthJsBackendAuthProvider({\n        authOptions: TinaAuthJSOptions({\n          databaseClient,\n          secret: process.env.NEXTAUTH_SECRET,\n        }),\n      }),\n  databaseClient,\n})\n```\n\n**Pros**: Full control, self-hosted\n**Cons**: Requires Node.js runtime (cannot use edge computing)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:59:27.330Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Content Management Agents requiring a Git-backed headless CMS with visual editing capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要 Git-backed 无头 CMS 和可视化编辑功能的内容管理代理。","ja":"Git-backed ヘッドレス CMS と視覚的な編集機能を必要とするコンテンツ管理エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Git-backed 헤드리스 CMS 및 시각적 편집 기능을 필요로 하는 콘텐츠 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de gestión de contenido que requieren un CMS headless con respaldo de Git y capacidades de edición visual.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de gestion de contenu nécessitant un CMS headless avec prise en charge Git et des capacités d''édition visuelle.","de":"Ideal für Content-Management-Agents, die ein Git-basiertes headless CMS mit visuellen Bearbeitungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Conteúdo que exigem um CMS headless com suporte ao Git e capacidades de edição visual.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления контентом, требующих CMS без видимой головной части с поддержкой Git и возможностями визуального редактирования.","ar":"مثالي لوسائل إدارة المحتوى التي تتطلب نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس مع دعم Git وقدرات تحرير مرئي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage content-heavy sites with tinacms, utilizing pnpm for package management and leveraging visual editing for efficient content updates, while ensuring compatibility with versions like tinacms@3.3.1 and @tinacms/cli@2.1.1.","zh":"赋予代理管理内容密集型站点的能力，利用 tinacms 和 pnpm 进行包管理，并利用视觉编辑进行高效的内容更新，同时确保与版本如 tinacms@3.3.1 和 @tinacms/cli@2.1.1 的兼容性。","ja":"エージェントがコンテンツ重視のサイトを管理できるようにし、tinacms と pnpm を使用してパッケージを管理し、視覚的な編集を使用して効率的なコンテンツ更新を行い、tinacms@3.3.1 や @tinacms/cli@2.1.1 などのバージョンとの互換性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 콘텐츠가 많은 사이트를 관리할 수 있도록하며 tinacms 및 pnpm을 사용하여 패키지를 관리하고 시각적 편집을 사용하여 효율적인 콘텐츠 업데이트를 수행하며 tinacms@3.3.1 및 @tinacms/cli@2.1.1과 같은 버전과의 호환성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar sitios con contenido pesado con tinacms, utilizando pnpm para la gestión de paquetes y aprovechando la edición visual para actualizaciones de contenido eficientes, garantizando la compatibilidad con versiones como tinacms@3.3.1 y @tinacms/cli@2.1.1.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des sites à fort contenu avec tinacms, en utilisant pnpm pour la gestion des packages et en exploitant l''édition visuelle pour des mises à jour de contenu efficaces, tout en assurant la compatibilité avec des versions comme tinacms@3.3.1 et @tinacms/cli@2.1.1.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Inhaltsreiche Seiten mit tinacms zu verwalten, indem pnpm für das Paketmanagement verwendet und visuelle Bearbeitung für effiziente Inhaltsaktualisierungen genutzt wird, während die Kompatibilität mit Versionen wie tinacms@3.3.1 und @tinacms/cli@2.1.1 sichergestellt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar sites com muito conteúdo com o tinacms, utilizando o pnpm para gerenciamento de pacotes e aproveitando a edição visual para atualizações de conteúdo eficientes, garantindo a compatibilidade com versões como tinacms@3.3.1 e @tinacms/cli@2.1.1.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять контенто-емкими сайтами с помощью tinacms, используя pnpm для управления пакетами и используя визуальное редактирование для эффективного обновления контента, обеспечивая совместимость с версиями, такими как tinacms@3.3.1 и @tinacms/cli@2.1.1.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إدارة مواقع ذات محتوى ثقيل مع tinacms، باستخدام pnpm لإدارة الحزم وتحقيق التحرير المرئي لتحديثات المحتوى الكفئ، مع ضمان التوافق مع الإصدارات مثل tinacms@3.3.1 و @tinacms/cli@2.1.1."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing TinaCMS projects with npx @tinacms/cli","Managing dependencies with pnpm for seamless module resolution","Utilizing Git-backed headless CMS for version-controlled content updates"],"zh":["使用 npx @tinacms/cli 初始化 TinaCMS 项目","使用 pnpm 管理依赖项以实现无缝模块解析","使用 Git-backed 无头 CMS 进行版本控制的内容更新"],"ja":["npx @tinacms/cli を使用して TinaCMS プロジェクトを初期化する","pnpm を使用して依存関係を管理し、シームレスなモジュール解決を行う","Git-backed ヘッドレス CMS を使用してバージョン管理されたコンテンツ更新を行う"],"ko":["npx @tinacms/cli를 사용하여 TinaCMS 프로젝트 초기화","pnpm을 사용하여 의존성 관리 및 모듈 해석을 원활하게 수행","Git-backed 헤드리스 CMS를 사용하여 버전 관리된 콘텐츠 업데이트를 수행"],"es":["Inicializar proyectos TinaCMS con npx @tinacms/cli","Gestionar dependencias con pnpm para una resolución de módulos sin problemas","Utilizar un CMS headless con respaldo de Git para actualizaciones de contenido controladas por versión"],"fr":["Initialiser des projets TinaCMS avec npx @tinacms/cli","Gérer les dépendances avec pnpm pour une résolution de modules sans problème","Utiliser un CMS headless avec prise en charge Git pour des mises à jour de contenu contrôlées par version"],"de":["TinaCMS-Projekte mit npx @tinacms/cli initialisieren","Abhängigkeiten mit pnpm verwalten, um eine reibungslose Modulauflösung zu gewährleisten","Ein Git-basiertes headless CMS für versionskontrollierte Inhaltsaktualisierungen nutzen"],"pt":["Inicializar projetos TinaCMS com npx @tinacms/cli","Gerenciar dependências com pnpm para resolução de módulos sem problemas","Utilizar CMS headless com suporte ao Git para atualizações de conteúdo controladas por versão"],"ru":["Инициализировать проекты TinaCMS с помощью npx @tinacms/cli","Управлять зависимостями с помощью pnpm для бесперебойного разрешения модулей","Использовать CMS без видимой головной части с поддержкой Git для обновлений контента, управляемых версиями"],"ar":["تثبيت مشاريع TinaCMS مع npx @tinacms/cli","إدارة التبعيات مع pnpm لحل المكونات الإضافية بدون مشاكل","استخدام نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس مع دعم Git لتحديثات المحتوى المخزنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires pnpm for versions above 2.7.3","May have module resolution issues with npm or yarn in newer versions"],"zh":["需要 pnpm，以支持 2.7.3 以上的版本","可能与 npm 或 yarn 的新版本存在模块解析问题"],"ja":["2.7.3 より後のバージョンのサポートには pnpm が必要である","npm または yarn の新しいバージョンではモジュール解決の問題が発生する可能性がある"],"ko":["2.7.3 이상의 버전을 지원하려면 pnpm이 필요합니다.","npm 또는 yarn의 새로운 버전과 함께 모듈 해석 문제가 발생할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere pnpm para versiones superiores a 2.7.3","Puede tener problemas de resolución de módulos con npm o yarn en versiones más recientes"],"fr":["Nécessite pnpm pour les versions supérieures à 2.7.3","Peut avoir des problèmes de résolution de modules avec npm ou yarn dans les versions plus récentes"],"de":["Erfordert pnpm für Versionen über 2.7.3","Kann Probleme mit der Modulauflösung mit npm oder yarn in neueren Versionen haben"],"pt":["Exige pnpm para versões acima de 2.7.3","Pode ter problemas de resolução de módulos com npm ou yarn em versões mais recentes"],"ru":["Требует pnpm для версий выше 2.7.3","Может иметь проблемы с разрешением модулей с npm или yarn в более новых версиях"],"ar":["يتطلب pnpm للإصدارات أعلى من 2.7.3","يمكن أن يكون لديها مشاكل في حل المكونات الإضافية مع npm أو yarn في الإصدارات الأحدث"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
