AG 2.1 Level AA\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n### 1. Semantic HTML Foundation\n\nChoose the right element - don''t use `div` for everything:\n\n```html\n<!-- ❌ WRONG - divs with onClick -->\n<div onclick=\"submit()\">Submit</div>\n<div onclick=\"navigate()\">Next page</div>\n\n<!-- ✅ CORRECT - semantic elements -->\n<button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>","body":"# Web Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-14\n**Dependencies**: None (framework-agnostic)\n**Standards**: WCAG 2.1 Level AA\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n### 1. Semantic HTML Foundation\n\nChoose the right element - don''t use `div` for everything:\n\n```html\n<!-- ❌ WRONG - divs with onClick -->\n<div onclick=\"submit()\">Submit</div>\n<div onclick=\"navigate()\">Next page</div>\n\n<!-- ✅ CORRECT - semantic elements -->\n<button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n<a href=\"/next\">Next page</a>\n```\n\n**Why this matters:**\n- Semantic elements have built-in keyboard support\n- Screen readers announce role automatically\n- Browser provides default accessible behaviors\n\n### 2. Focus Management\n\nMake interactive elements keyboard-accessible:\n\n```css\n/* ❌ WRONG - removes focus outline */\nbutton:focus { outline: none; }\n\n/* ✅ CORRECT - custom accessible outline */\nbutton:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid var(--primary);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n```\n\n**CRITICAL:**\n- Never remove focus outlines without replacement\n- Use `:focus-visible` to show only on keyboard focus\n- Ensure 3:1 contrast ratio for focus indicators\n\n### 3. Text Alternatives\n\nEvery non-text element needs a text alternative:\n\n```html\n<!-- ❌ WRONG - no alt text -->\n<img src=\"logo.png\">\n<button><svg>...</svg></button>\n\n<!-- ✅ CORRECT - proper alternatives -->\n<img src=\"logo.png\" alt=\"Company Name\">\n<button aria-label=\"Close dialog\"><svg>...</svg></button>\n```\n\n---\n\n## The 5-Step Accessibility Process\n\n### Step 1: Choose Semantic HTML\n\n**Decision tree for element selection:**\n\n```\nNeed clickable element?\n├─ Navigates to another page? → <a href=\"...\">\n├─ Submits form? → <button type=\"submit\">\n├─ Opens dialog? → <button aria-haspopup=\"dialog\">\n└─ Other action? → <button type=\"button\">\n\nGrouping content?\n├─ Self-contained article? → <article>\n├─ Thematic section? → <section>\n├─ Navigation links? → <nav>\n└─ Supplementary info? → <aside>\n\nForm element?\n├─ Text input? → <input type=\"text\">\n├─ Multiple choice? → <select> or <input type=\"radio\">\n├─ Toggle? → <input type=\"checkbox\"> or <button aria-pressed>\n└─ Long text? → <textarea>\n```\n\n**See `references/semantic-html.md` for complete guide.**\n\n### Step 2: Add ARIA When Needed\n\n**Golden rule: Use ARIA only when HTML can''t express the pattern.**\n\n```html\n<!-- ❌ WRONG - unnecessary ARIA -->\n<button role=\"button\">Click me</button>  <!-- Button already has role -->\n\n<!-- ✅ CORRECT - ARIA fills semantic gap -->\n<div role=\"dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"title\" aria-modal=\"true\">\n  <h2 id=\"title\">Confirm action</h2>\n  <!-- No HTML dialog yet, so role needed -->\n</div>\n\n<!-- ✅ BETTER - Use native HTML when available -->\n<dialog aria-labelledby=\"title\">\n  <h2 id=\"title\">Confirm action</h2>\n</dialog>\n```\n\n**Common ARIA patterns:**\n- `aria-label` - When visible label doesn''t exist\n- `aria-labelledby` - Reference existing text as label\n- `aria-describedby` - Additional description\n- `aria-live` - Announce dynamic updates\n- `aria-expanded` - Collapsible/expandable state\n\n**See `references/aria-patterns.md` for complete patterns.**\n\n### Step 3: Implement Keyboard Navigation\n\n**All interactive elements must be keyboard-accessible:**\n\n```typescript\n// Tab order management\nfunction Dialog({ onClose }) {\n  const dialogRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n  const previousFocus = useRef<HTMLElement | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Save previous focus\n    previousFocus.current = document.activeElement as HTMLElement;\n\n    // Focus first element in dialog\n    const firstFocusable = dialogRef.current?.querySelector(''button, [href], input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex=\"-1\"])'');\n    (firstFocusable as HTMLElement)?.focus();\n\n    // Trap focus within dialog\n    const handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {\n      if (e.key === ''Escape'') onClose();\n      if (e.key === ''Tab'') {\n        // Focus trap logic here\n      }\n    };\n\n    document.addEventListener(''keydown'', handleKeyDown);\n    return () => {\n      document.removeEventListener(''keydown'', handleKeyDown);\n      // Restore focus on close\n      previousFocus.current?.focus();\n    };\n  }, [onClose]);\n\n  return <div ref={dialogRef} role=\"dialog\">...</div>;\n}\n```\n\n**Essential keyboard patterns:**\n- Tab/Shift+Tab: Navigate between focusable elements\n- Enter/Space: Activate buttons/links\n- Arrow keys: Navigate within components (tabs, menus)\n- Escape: Close dialogs/menus\n- Home/End: Jump to first/last item\n\n**See `references/focus-management.md` for complete patterns.**\n\n### Step 4: Ensure Color Contrast\n\n**WCAG AA requirements:**\n- Normal text (under 18pt): 4.5:1 contrast ratio\n- Large text (18pt+ or 14pt+ bold): 3:1 contrast ratio\n- UI components (buttons, borders): 3:1 contrast ratio\n\n```css\n/* ❌ WRONG - insufficient contrast */\n:root {\n  --background: #ffffff;\n  --text: #999999;  /* 2.8:1 - fails WCAG AA */\n}\n\n/* ✅ CORRECT - sufficient contrast */\n:root {\n  --background: #ffffff;\n  --text: #595959;  /* 4.6:1 - passes WCAG AA */\n}\n```\n\n**Testing tools:**\n- Browser DevTools (Chrome/Firefox have built-in checkers)\n- Contrast checker extensions\n- axe DevTools extension\n\n**See `references/color-contrast.md` for complete guide.**\n\n### Step 5: Make Forms Accessible\n\n**Every form input needs a visible label:**\n\n```html\n<!-- ❌ WRONG - placeholder is not a label -->\n<input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email address\">\n\n<!-- ✅ CORRECT - proper label -->\n<label for=\"email\">Email address</label>\n<input type=\"email\" id=\"email\" name=\"email\" required aria-required=\"true\">\n```\n\n**Error handling:**\n\n```html\n<label for=\"email\">Email address</label>\n<input\n  type=\"email\"\n  id=\"email\"\n  name=\"email\"\n  aria-invalid=\"true\"\n  aria-describedby=\"email-error\"\n>\n<span id=\"email-error\" role=\"alert\">\n  Please enter a valid email address\n</span>\n```\n\n**Live regions for dynamic errors:**\n\n```html\n<div role=\"alert\" aria-live=\"assertive\" aria-atomic=\"true\">\n  Form submission failed. Please fix the errors above.\n</div>\n```\n\n**See `references/forms-validation.md` for complete patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n### Always Do\n\n✅ Use semantic HTML elements first (button, a, nav, article, etc.)\n✅ Provide text alternatives for all non-text content\n✅ Ensure 4.5:1 contrast for normal text, 3:1 for large text/UI\n✅ Make all functionality keyboard accessible\n✅ Test with keyboard only (unplug mouse)\n✅ Test with screen reader (NVDA on Windows, VoiceOver on Mac)\n✅ Use proper heading hierarchy (h1 → h2 → h3, no skipping)\n✅ Label all form inputs with visible labels\n✅ Provide focus indicators (never just `outline: none`)\n✅ Use `aria-live` for dynamic content updates\n\n### Never Do\n\n❌ Use `div` with `onClick` instead of `button`\n❌ Remove focus outlines without replacement\n❌ Use color alone to convey information\n❌ Use placeholders as labels\n❌ Skip heading levels (h1 → h3)\n❌ Use `tabindex` > 0 (messes with natural order)\n❌ Add ARIA when semantic HTML exists\n❌ Forget to restore focus after closing dialogs\n❌ Use `role=\"presentation\"` on focusable elements\n❌ Create keyboard traps (no way to escape)\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues Prevention\n\nThis skill prevents **12** documented accessibility issues:\n\n### Issue #1: Missing Focus Indicators\n\n**Error**: Interactive elements have no visible focus indicator\n**Source**: WCAG 2.4.7 (Focus Visible)\n**Why It Happens**: CSS reset removes default outline\n**Prevention**: Always provide custom focus-visible styles\n\n### Issue #2: Insufficient Color Contrast\n\n**Error**: Text has less than 4.5:1 contrast ratio\n**Source**: WCAG 1.4.3 (Contrast Minimum)\n**Why It Happens**: Using light gray text on white background\n**Prevention**: Test all text colors with contrast checker\n\n### Issue #3: Missing Alt Text\n\n**Error**: Images missing alt attributes\n**Source**: WCAG 1.1.1 (Non-text Content)\n**Why It Happens**: Forgot to add or thought it was optional\n**Prevention**: Add alt=\"\" for decorative, descriptive alt for meaningful images\n\n### Issue #4: Keyboard Navigation Broken\n\n**Error**: Interactive elements not reachable by keyboard\n**Source**: WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard)\n**Why It Happens**: Using div onClick instead of button\n**Prevention**: Use semantic interactive elements (button, a)\n\n### Issue #5: Form Inputs Without Labels\n\n**Error**: Input fields missing associated labels\n**Source**: WCAG 3.3.2 (Labels or Instructions)\n**Why It Happens**: Using placeholder as label\n**Prevention**: Always use `<label>` element with for/id association\n\n### Issue #6: Skipped Heading Levels\n\n**Error**: Heading hierarchy jumps from h1 to h3\n**Source**: WCAG 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships)\n**Why It Happens**: Using headings for visual styling instead of semantics\n**Prevention**: Use headings in order, style with CSS\n\n### Issue #7: No Focus Trap in Dialogs\n\n**Error**: Tab key exits dialog to background content\n**Source**: WCAG 2.4.3 (Focus Order)\n**Why It Happens**: No focus trap implementation\n**Prevention**: Implement focus trap for modal dialogs\n\n### Issue #8: Missing aria-live for Dynamic Content\n\n**Error**: Screen reader doesn''t announce updates\n**Source**: WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages)\n**Why It Happens**: Dynamic content added without announcement\n**Prevention**: Use aria-live=\"polite\" or \"assertive\"\n\n### Issue #9: Color-Only Information\n\n**Error**: Using only color to convey status\n**Source**: WCAG 1.4.1 (Use of Color)\n**Why It Happens**: Red text for errors without icon/text\n**Prevention**: Add icon + text label, not just color\n\n### Issue #10: Non-descriptive Link Text\n\n**Error**: Links with \"click here\" or \"read more\"\n**Source**: WCAG 2.4.4 (Link Purpose)\n**Why It Happens**: Generic link text without context\n**Prevention**: Use descriptive link text or aria-label\n\n### Issue #11: Auto-playing Media\n\n**Error**: Video/audio auto-plays without user control\n**Source**: WCAG 1.4.2 (Audio Control)\n**Why It Happens**: Autoplay attribute without controls\n**Prevention**: Require user interaction to start media\n\n### Issue #12: Inaccessible Custom Controls\n\n**Error**: Custom select/checkbox without keyboard support\n**Source**: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value)\n**Why It Happens**: Building from divs without ARIA\n**Prevention**: Use native elements or implement full ARIA pattern\n\n---\n\n## WCAG 2.1 AA Quick Checklist\n\n### Perceivable\n\n- [ ] All images have alt text (or alt=\"\" if decorative)\n- [ ] Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (normal), ≥ 3:1 (large)\n- [ ] Color not used alone to convey information\n- [ ] Text can be resized to 200% without loss of content\n- [ ] No auto-playing audio >3 seconds\n\n### Operable\n\n- [ ] All functionality keyboard accessible\n- [ ] No keyboard traps\n- [ ] Visible focus indicators\n- [ ] Users can pause/stop/hide moving content\n- [ ] Page titles describe purpose\n- [ ] Focus order is logical\n- [ ] Link purpose clear from text or context\n- [ ] Multiple ways to find pages (menu, search, sitemap)\n- [ ] Headings and labels describe purpose\n\n### Understandable\n\n- [ ] Page language specified (`<html lang=\"en\">`)\n- [ ] Language changes marked (`<span lang=\"es\">`)\n- [ ] No unexpected context changes on focus/input\n- [ ] Consistent navigation across site\n- [ ] Form labels/instructions provided\n- [ ] Input errors identified and described\n- [ ] Error prevention for legal/financial/data changes\n\n### Robust\n\n- [ ] Valid HTML (no parsing errors)\n- [ ] Name, role, value available for all UI components\n- [ ] Status messages identified (aria-live)\n\n---\n\n## Testing Workflow\n\n### 1. Keyboard-Only Testing (5 minutes)\n\n```\n1. Unplug mouse or hide cursor\n2. Tab through entire page\n   - Can you reach all interactive elements?\n   - Can you activate all buttons/links?\n   - Is focus order logical?\n3. Use Enter/Space to activate\n4. Use Escape to close dialogs\n5. Use arrow keys in menus/tabs\n```\n\n### 2. Screen Reader Testing (10 minutes)\n\n**NVDA (Windows - Free)**:\n- Download: https://www.nvaccess.org/download/\n- Start: Ctrl+Alt+N\n- Navigate: Arrow keys or Tab\n- Read: NVDA+Down arrow\n- Stop: NVDA+Q\n\n**VoiceOver (Mac - Built-in)**:\n- Start: Cmd+F5\n- Navigate: VO+Right/Left arrow (VO = Ctrl+Option)\n- Read: VO+A (read all)\n- Stop: Cmd+F5\n\n**What to test:**\n- Are all interactive elements announced?\n- Are images described properly?\n- Are form labels read with inputs?\n- Are dynamic updates announced?\n- Is heading structure clear?\n\n### 3. Automated Testing\n\n**axe DevTools** (Browser extension - highly recommended):\n- Install: Chrome/Firefox extension\n- Run: F12 → axe DevTools tab → Scan\n- Fix: Review violations, follow remediation\n- Retest: Scan again after fixes\n\n**Lighthouse** (Built into Chrome):\n- Open DevTools (F12)\n- Lighthouse tab\n- Select \"Accessibility\" category\n- Generate report\n- Score 90+ is good, 100 is ideal\n\n---\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Accessible Dialog/Modal\n\n```typescript\ninterface DialogProps {\n  isOpen: boolean;\n  onClose: () => void;\n  title: string;\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}\n\nfunction Dialog({ isOpen, onClose, title, children }: DialogProps) {\n  const dialogRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!isOpen) return;\n\n    const previousFocus = document.activeElement as HTMLElement;\n\n    // Focus first focusable element\n    const firstFocusable = dialogRef.current?.querySelector(\n      ''button, [href], input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex=\"-1\"])''\n    ) as HTMLElement;\n    firstFocusable?.focus();\n\n    // Focus trap\n    const handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {\n      if (e.key === ''Escape'') {\n        onClose();\n      }\n      if (e.key === ''Tab'') {\n        const focusableElements = dialogRef.current?.querySelectorAll(\n          ''button, [href], input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex=\"-1\"])''\n        );\n        if (!focusableElements?.length) return;\n\n        const first = focusableElements[0] as HTMLElement;\n        const last = focusableElements[focusableElements.length - 1] as HTMLElement;\n\n        if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) {\n          e.preventDefault();\n          last.focus();\n        } else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) {\n          e.preventDefault();\n          first.focus();\n        }\n      }\n    };\n\n    document.addEventListener(''keydown'', handleKeyDown);\n\n    return () => {\n      document.removeEventListener(''keydown'', handleKeyDown);\n      previousFocus?.focus();\n    };\n  }, [isOpen, onClose]);\n\n  if (!isOpen) return null;\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {/* Backdrop */}\n      <div\n        className=\"dialog-backdrop\"\n        onClick={onClose}\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\n      />\n\n      {/* Dialog */}\n      <div\n        ref={dialogRef}\n        role=\"dialog\"\n        aria-modal=\"true\"\n        aria-labelledby=\"dialog-title\"\n        className=\"dialog\"\n      >\n        <h2 id=\"dialog-title\">{title}</h2>\n        <div className=\"dialog-content\">{children}</div>\n        <button onClick={onClose} aria-label=\"Close dialog\">×</button>\n      </div>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**When to use**: Any modal dialog or overlay that blocks interaction with background content.\n\n### Pattern 2: Accessible Tabs\n\n```typescript\nfunction Tabs({ tabs }: { tabs: Array<{ label: string; content: React.ReactNode }> }) {\n  const [activeIndex, setActiveIndex] = useState(0);\n\n  const handleKeyDown = (e: React.KeyboardEvent, index: number) => {\n    if (e.key === ''ArrowLeft'') {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      const newIndex = index === 0 ? tabs.length - 1 : index - 1;\n      setActiveIndex(newIndex);\n    } else if (e.key === ''ArrowRight'') {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      const newIndex = index === tabs.length - 1 ? 0 : index + 1;\n      setActiveIndex(newIndex);\n    } else if (e.key === ''Home'') {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      setActiveIndex(0);\n    } else if (e.key === ''End'') {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      setActiveIndex(tabs.length - 1);\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Content tabs\">\n        {tabs.map((tab, index) => (\n          <button\n            key={index}\n            role=\"tab\"\n            aria-selected={activeIndex === index}\n            aria-controls={`panel-${index}`}\n            id={`tab-${index}`}\n            tabIndex={activeIndex === index ? 0 : -1}\n            onClick={() => setActiveIndex(index)}\n            onKeyDown={(e) => handleKeyDown(e, index)}\n          >\n            {tab.label}\n          </button>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n      {tabs.map((tab, index) => (\n        <div\n          key={index}\n          role=\"tabpanel\"\n          id={`panel-${index}`}\n          aria-labelledby={`tab-${index}`}\n          hidden={activeIndex !== index}\n          tabIndex={0}\n        >\n          {tab.content}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**When to use**: Tabbed interface with multiple panels.\n\n### Pattern 3: Skip Links\n\n```html\n<!-- Place at very top of body -->\n<a href=\"#main-content\" class=\"skip-link\">\n  Skip to main content\n</a>\n\n<style>\n.skip-link {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: -40px;\n  left: 0;\n  background: var(--primary);\n  color: white;\n  padding: 8px 16px;\n  z-index: 9999;\n}\n\n.skip-link:focus {\n  top: 0;\n}\n</style>\n\n<!-- Then in your layout -->\n<main id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n  <!-- Page content -->\n</main>\n```\n\n**When to use**: All multi-page websites with navigation/header before main content.\n\n### Pattern 4: Accessible Form with Validation\n\n```typescript\nfunction ContactForm() {\n  const [errors, setErrors] = useState<Record<string, string>>({});\n  const [touched, setTouched] = useState<Record<string, boolean>>({});\n\n  const validateEmail = (email: string) => {\n    if (!email) return ''Email is required'';\n    if (!/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/.test(email)) return ''Email is invalid'';\n    return '''';\n  };\n\n  const handleBlur = (field: string, value: string) => {\n    setTouched(prev => ({ ...prev, [field]: true }));\n    const error = validateEmail(value);\n    setErrors(prev => ({ ...prev, [field]: error }));\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <form>\n      <div>\n        <label htmlFor=\"email\">Email address *</label>\n        <input\n          type=\"email\"\n          id=\"email\"\n          name=\"email\"\n          required\n          aria-required=\"true\"\n          aria-invalid={touched.email && !!errors.email}\n          aria-describedby={errors.email ? ''email-error'' : undefined}\n          onBlur={(e) => handleBlur(''email'', e.target.value)}\n        />\n        {touched.email && errors.email && (\n          <span id=\"email-error\" role=\"alert\" className=\"error\">\n            {errors.email}\n          </span>\n        )}\n      </div>\n\n      <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n\n      {/* Global form error */}\n      <div role=\"alert\" aria-live=\"assertive\" aria-atomic=\"true\">\n        {/* Dynamic error message appears here */}\n      </div>\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**When to use**: All forms with validation.\n\n---\n\n## Using Bundled Resources\n\n### References (references/)\n\nDetailed documentation for deep dives:\n\n- **wcag-checklist.md** - Complete WCAG 2.1 Level A & AA requirements with examples\n- **semantic-html.md** - Element selection guide, when to use which tag\n- **aria-patterns.md** - ARIA roles, states, properties, and when to use them\n- **focus-management.md** - Focus order, focus traps, focus restoration patterns\n- **color-contrast.md** - Contrast requirements, testing tools, color palette tips\n- **forms-validation.md** - Accessible form patterns, error handling, announcements\n\n**When Claude should load these**:\n- User asks for complete WCAG checklist\n- Deep dive into specific pattern (tabs, accordions, etc.)\n- Color contrast issues or palette design\n- Complex form validation scenarios\n\n### Agents (agents/)\n\n- **a11y-auditor.md** - Automated accessibility auditor that checks pages for violations\n\n**When to use**: Request accessibility audit of existing page/component.\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Topics\n\n### ARIA Live Regions\n\nThree politeness levels:\n\n```html\n<!-- Polite: Wait for screen reader to finish current announcement -->\n<div aria-live=\"polite\">New messages: 3</div>\n\n<!-- Assertive: Interrupt immediately -->\n<div aria-live=\"assertive\" role=\"alert\">\n  Error: Form submission failed\n</div>\n\n<!-- Off: Don''t announce (default) -->\n<div aria-live=\"off\">Loading...</div>\n```\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Use `polite` for non-critical updates (notifications, counters)\n- Use `assertive` for errors and critical alerts\n- Use `aria-atomic=\"true\"` to read entire region on change\n- Keep messages concise and meaningful\n\n### Focus Management in SPAs\n\nReact Router doesn''t reset focus on navigation - you need to handle it:\n\n```typescript\nfunction App() {\n  const location = useLocation();\n  const mainRef = useRef<HTMLElement>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Focus main content on route change\n    mainRef.current?.focus();\n    // Announce page title to screen readers\n    const title = document.title;\n    const announcement = document.createElement(''div'');\n    announcement.setAttribute(''role'', ''status'');\n    announcement.setAttribute(''aria-live'', ''polite'');\n    announcement.textContent = `Navigated to ${title}`;\n    document.body.appendChild(announcement);\n    setTimeout(() => announcement.remove(), 1000);\n  }, [location.pathname]);\n\n  return <main ref={mainRef} tabIndex={-1} id=\"main-content\">...</main>;\n}\n```\n\n### Accessible Data Tables\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <caption>Monthly sales by region</caption>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th scope=\"col\">Region</th>\n      <th scope=\"col\">Q1</th>\n      <th scope=\"col\">Q2</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th scope=\"row\">North</th>\n      <td>$10,000</td>\n      <td>$12,000</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\n**Key attributes:**\n- `<caption>` - Describes table purpose\n- `scope=\"col\"` - Identifies column headers\n- `scope=\"row\"` - Identifies row headers\n- Associates data cells with headers for screen readers\n\n---\n\n## Official Documentation\n\n- **WCAG 2.1**: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/quickref/\n- **MDN Accessibility**: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility\n- **ARIA Authoring Practices**: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/\n- **WebAIM**: https://webaim.org/articles/\n- **axe DevTools**: https://www.deque.com/axe/devtools/\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Problem: Focus indicators not visible\n\n**Symptoms**: Can tab through page but don''t see where focus is\n**Cause**: CSS removed outlines or insufficient contrast\n**Solution**:\n```css\n*:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid var(--primary);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n```\n\n### Problem: Screen reader not announcing updates\n\n**Symptoms**: Dynamic content changes but no announcement\n**Cause**: No aria-live region\n**Solution**: Wrap dynamic content in `<div aria-live=\"polite\">` or use role=\"alert\"\n\n### Problem: Dialog focus escapes to background\n\n**Symptoms**: Tab key navigates to elements behind dialog\n**Cause**: No focus trap\n**Solution**: Implement focus trap (see Pattern 1 above)\n\n### Problem: Form errors not announced\n\n**Symptoms**: Visual errors appear but screen reader doesn''t notice\n**Cause**: No aria-invalid or role=\"alert\"\n**Solution**: Use aria-invalid + aria-describedby pointing to error message with role=\"alert\"\n\n---\n\n## Complete Setup Checklist\n\nUse this for every page/component:\n\n- [ ] All interactive elements are keyboard accessible\n- [ ] Visible focus indicators on all focusable elements\n- [ ] Images have alt text (or alt=\"\" if decorative)\n- [ ] Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (test with axe or Lighthouse)\n- [ ] Form inputs have associated labels (not just placeholders)\n- [ ] Heading hierarchy is logical (no skipped levels)\n- [ ] Page has `<html lang=\"en\">` or appropriate language\n- [ ] Dialogs have focus trap and restore focus on close\n- [ ] Dynamic content uses aria-live or role=\"alert\"\n- [ ] Color not used alone to convey information\n- [ ] Tested with keyboard only (no mouse)\n- [ ] Tested with screen reader (NVDA or VoiceOver)\n- [ ] Ran axe DevTools scan (0 violations)\n- [ ] Lighthouse accessibility score ≥ 90\n\n---\n\n**Questions? Issues?**\n\n1. Check `references/wcag-checklist.md` for complete requirements\n2. Use `/a11y-auditor` agent to scan your page\n3. Run axe DevTools for automated testing\n4. Test with actual keyboard + screen reader\n\n---\n\n**Standards**: WCAG 2.1 Level AA\n**Testing Tools**: axe DevTools, Lighthouse, NVDA, VoiceOver\n**Success Criteria**: 90+ Lighthouse score, 0 critical violations\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:02:21.094Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Web Development Agents requiring WCAG 2.1 AA compliance validation and semantic HTML implementation.","zh":"适用于需要WCAG 2.1 AA合规验证和语义HTML实现的Web开发代理。","ja":"WCAG 2.1 AA準拠の検証とセマンティックHTMLの実装を必要とするWeb開発エージェントに不可欠。","ko":"WCAG 2.1 AA 규정 준수 검증 및 의미 있는 HTML 구현이 필요한 웹 개발 에이전트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para agentes de desarrollo web que requieren validación de cumplimiento de WCAG 2.1 AA y implementación de HTML semántico.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de développement Web nécessitant une validation de conformité WCAG 2.1 AA et une mise en œuvre de HTML sémantique.","de":"Wesentlich für Webentwicklungsagenten, die eine Validierung der Konformität mit WCAG 2.1 AA und eine Implementierung von semantischem HTML erfordern.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Web que exigem validação de conformidade WCAG 2.1 AA e implementação de HTML semântico.","ru":"Необходим для агентов веб-разработки, требующих проверки соответствия WCAG 2.1 AA и реализации семантического HTML.","ar":"ضروري لعمليات تطوير الويب التي تتطلب التحقق من مطابقة معايير الويب WCAG 2.1 AA وتطبيق HTML семантиكي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables automatic detection of accessibility violations and provides framework-agnostic semantic HTML recommendations, transforming inaccessible div-based structures into WCAG-compliant code without external dependencies.","zh":"可以自动检测到无障碍违规并提供框架无关的语义HTML建议，将无法访问的div基于结构转换为WCAG合规代码，无需外部依赖。","ja":"アクセシビリティの違反を自動的に検出して、フレームワークに依存しないセマンティックHTMLの推奨事項を提供し、外部依存関係なく、不正アクセスdivベースの構造をWCAG準拠コードに変換します。","ko":"접근성 위반을 자동으로 감지하고 프레임워크에 종속되지 않는 의미 있는 HTML 권장 사항을 제공하여 外部 의존성 없이 접근할 수 없는 div 기반 구조를 WCAG 규정 준수 코드로 변환합니다.","es":"Permite la detección automática de violaciones de accesibilidad y proporciona recomendaciones de HTML semántico independientes del marco, transformando estructuras basadas en div inaccesibles en código compatible con WCAG sin dependencias externas.","fr":"Permet la détection automatique des violations d''accessibilité et fournit des recommandations de HTML sémantique indépendantes du cadre, transformant des structures de div inaccessibles en code conforme à WCAG sans dépendances externes.","de":"Ermöglicht die automatische Erkennung von Barriereverletzungen und bietet framework-unabhängige Empfehlungen für semantisches HTML, indem unzugängliche div-basierte Strukturen in WCAG-konformen Code ohne externe Abhängigkeiten umgewandelt werden.","pt":"Permite a detecção automática de violações de acessibilidade e fornece recomendações de HTML semântico independentes de framework, transformando estruturas baseadas em div inacessíveis em código compatível com WCAG sem dependências externas.","ru":"Позволяет автоматически обнаруживать нарушения доступности и предоставляет рекомендации по семантическому HTML, независимые от фреймворка, преобразуя недоступные структуры, основанные на div, в код, соответствующий WCAG, без внешних зависимостей.","ar":"يمكن الكشف التلقائي عن انتهاكات إمكانية الوصول ويوفر توصيات HTML семантиكي غير معتمدة على الإطار، ويحول البنى التي تعتمد على div غير القابلة للوصول إلى código متوافق مع WCAG بدون зависимости خارجية."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing existing websites for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance","Converting onclick div elements to proper semantic buttons","Generating accessibility reports for client deliverables","Validating form element accessibility attributes"],"zh":["审核现有网站的WCAG 2.1 AA合规性","将onclick div元素转换为适当的语义按钮","为客户交付生成无障碍报告","验证表单元素的无障碍属性"],"ja":["既存のWebサイトのWCAG 2.1 AA準拠のオーディット","onclick div要素を適切なセマンティックボタンに変換","クライアント向けのアクセシビリティレポートの生成","フォーム要素のアクセシビリティ属性の検証"],"ko":["既存 웹사이트의 WCAG 2.1 AA 규정 준수 감사","onclick div 요소를 적절한 의미 있는 버튼으로 변환","클라이언트에 대한 접근성 보고서 생성","폼 요소의 접근성 속성 검증"],"es":["Auditoría de sitios web existentes para la conformidad con WCAG 2.1 AA","Conversión de elementos de div con onclick en botones semánticos adecuados","Generación de informes de accesibilidad para entregas a clientes","Validación de atributos de accesibilidad de elementos de formulario"],"fr":["Audit de sites Web existants pour la conformité à WCAG 2.1 AA","Conversion d''éléments de div avec onclick en boutons sémantiques appropriés","Génération de rapports d''accessibilité pour les livrables clients","Validation des attributs d''accessibilité des éléments de formulaire"],"de":["Prüfung bestehender Websites auf Konformität mit WCAG 2.1 AA","Umwandlung von Div-Elementen mit onclick in ordnungsgemäße semantische Schaltflächen","Erstellung von Barrierefreiheitsberichten für Kundenlieferungen","Validierung von Barrierefreiheitsattributen von Formularelementen"],"pt":["Auditoria de sites existentes para conformidade com WCAG 2.1 AA","Conversão de elementos div onclick em botões semânticos adequados","Geração de relatórios de acessibilidade para entregas de clientes","Validação de atributos de acessibilidade de elementos de formulário"],"ru":["Проверка существующих сайтов на соответствие WCAG 2.1 AA","Преобразование элементов div onclick в правильные семантические кнопки","Генерация отчетов об доступности для клиентских материалов","Проверка атрибутов доступности элементов формы"],"ar":["فحص المواقع الحالية لمطابقة معايير الويب WCAG 2.1 AA","تحويل عناصر div onclick إلى أزرار семантиكية مناسبة","генерация تقارير إمكانية الوصول لتسليم العملاء","التحقق من سمات إمكانية الوصول إلى عناصر النماذج"]},"limitations":{"en":["Focuses exclusively on WCAG 2.1 AA standards","Requires HTML content for analysis","Does not cover automated screen reader testing"],"zh":["仅关注WCAG 2.1 AA标准","需要HTML内容进行分析","不涵盖自动化屏幕阅读器测试"],"ja":["WCAG 2.1 AA標準のみに焦点を当てている","分析のためのHTMLコンテンツが必要","自動スクリーンリーダーテストはカバーしていない"],"ko":["WCAG 2.1 AA 규정만을 중점적으로 다룸","분석을 위한 HTML 콘텐츠가 필요함","자동화된 화면 리더기 테스트는 포함하지 않음"],"es":["Se centra exclusivamente en los estándares WCAG 2.1 AA","Requiere contenido HTML para el análisis","No cubre la prueba automática de lectura de pantalla"],"fr":["Se concentre exclusivement sur les normes WCAG 2.1 AA","Nécessite un contenu HTML pour l''analyse","Ne couvre pas les tests automatiques de lecteur d''écran"],"de":["Konzentriert sich ausschließlich auf die WCAG 2.1 AA-Standards","Benötigt HTML-Inhalt für die Analyse","Umschließt keine automatisierte Bildschirmlese-Testung"],"pt":["Concentra-se exclusivamente nos padrões WCAG 2.1 AA","Exige conteúdo HTML para análise","Não cobre testes automatizados de leitor de tela"],"ru":["Сосредоточен исключительно на стандартах WCAG 2.1 AA","Требует HTML-контента для анализа","Не покрывает автоматизированное тестирование экранных читателей"],"ar":["يركز حصريًا على معايير الويب WCAG 2.1 AA","يتطلب المحتوى HTML للتحليل","لا يغطي الاختبارات الآلية للقارئ الشاشاتي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/ml-pipeline-workflow', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'ml-pipeline-workflow', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z', '2026-02-18T13:02:00.025Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/ml-pipeline-workflow","name":"ml-pipeline-workflow","description":{"zh":"ML ","ja":"ML","ko":"ML ","es":"Nuestra guía de orquestación de pipeline de ML proporciona una visión general completa para la creación de pipelines de producción que manejan el ciclo de vida completo","fr":"Notre guide d''orchestration de pipeline de ML fournit une vue d''ensemble complète pour la création de pipelines de production qui gèrent le cycle de vie complet","de":"Unsere ML-Pipeline-Workflow-Anleitung bietet eine umfassende Übersicht für die Erstellung von Produktions-Pipelines, die den gesamten Lebenszyklus abdecken","pt":"O skill ml-pipeline-workflow fornece orientação abrangente para construir pipelines de ML de produção","ru":"Навык ml-pipeline-workflow предоставляет всестороннее руководство по созданию конвейеров ML для производства","ar":"المهارة ml-pipeline-workflow توفر إرشادات شاملة لإنشاء خطوط أنابيب ML للإنتاج","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"ML ","ja":"ML","ko":"ML ","es":"Orquestación de Pipeline de Aprendizaje Automático","fr":"Orchestration de Pipeline d''Apprentissage Automatique","de":"ML-Pipeline-Workflow-Orchestrierung","pt":"MLOps Pipeline Completa","ru":"Полный конвейер MLOps","ar":"管道 MLOps الكامل","en":"ml-pipeline-workflow"},"description":{"zh":"ML ","ja":"ML","ko":"ML ","es":"Nuestra guía de orquestación de pipeline de ML proporciona una visión general completa para la creación de pipelines de producción que manejan el ciclo de vi...","fr":"Notre guide d''orchestration de pipeline de ML fournit une vue d''ensemble complète pour la création de pipelines de production qui gèrent le cycle de vie complet","de":"Unsere ML-Pipeline-Workflow-Anleitung bietet eine umfassende Übersicht für die Erstellung von Produktions-Pipelines, die den gesamten Lebenszyklus abdecken","pt":"O skill ml-pipeline-workflow fornece orientação abrangente para construir pipelines de ML de produção","ru":"Навык ml-pipeline-workflow предоставляет всестороннее руководство по созданию конвейеров ML для производства","ar":"المهارة ml-pipeline-workflow توفر إرشادات شاملة لإنشاء خطوط أنابيب ML للإنتاج","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["ML","MLOps","ML","ML","ML"],"ja":["ML","MLOps","ML","ML","ML"],"ko":["ML","MLOps","ML","ML","ML"],"es":["Orquestación de pipeline de ML completa","Automatización del ciclo de vida de los modelos","Creación de pipelines de producción","Integración de datos y modelos","Implementación de validación y monitoreo","Despliegue de modelos en producción"],"fr":["Orchestration de pipeline de ML complète","Automatisation du cycle de vie des modèles","Création de pipelines de production","Intégration de données et de modèles","Mise en œuvre de validation et de surveillance","Déploiement de modèles en production"],"de":["Vollständige ML-Pipeline-Workflow-Orchestrierung","Automatisierung des Lebenszyklus von Modellen","Erstellung von Produktions-Pipelines","Integration von Daten und Modellen","Implementierung von Validierung und Überwachung","Bereitstellung von Modellen in Produktion"],"pt":["Orquestração de workflow de ML","Automação de dados para modelos","Implantação de modelos","Monitoramento de desempenho","Preparação de dados","Treinamento de modelos"],"ru":["Оркестрация рабочего процесса ML","Автоматизация данных для моделей","Развертывание моделей","Мониторинг производительности","Подготовка данных","Обучение моделей"],"ar":["توجيه سير عمل ML","أتمتة البيانات لنماذج","نشر النماذج","مراقبة الأداء","تحضير البيانات","تدريب النماذج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["ML","MLOps","ML","ML","ML","ML"],"ja":["ML","MLOps","ML","ML","ML","ML"],"ko":["ML","MLOps","ML","ML","ML","ML"],"es":["orquestación de pipeline de ML","aprendizaje automático","MLOps","automatización de modelos","despliegue de modelos","validación de modelos","monitoreo de modelos","integración de datos","creación de pipelines de producción"],"fr":["orchestration de pipeline de ML","apprentissage automatique","MLOps","automatisation de modèles","déploiement de modèles","validation de modèles","surveillance de modèles","intégration de données","création de pipelines de production"],"de":["ML-Pipeline-Workflow-Orchestrierung","Machine Learning","MLOps","Automatisierung von Modellen","Bereitstellung von Modellen","Validierung von Modellen","Überwachung von Modellen","Integration von Daten","Erstellung von Produktions-Pipelines"],"pt":["MLOps","pipeline de ML","orquestração de workflow","automação de dados","implantação de modelos","monitoramento de desempenho","preparação de dados","treinamento de modelos"],"ru":["MLOps","конвейер ML","оркестрация рабочего процесса","автоматизация данных","развертывание моделей","мониторинг производительности","подготовка данных","обучение моделей"],"ar":["MLOps","خط أنابيب ML","توجيه سير عمل","أتمتة البيانات","نشر النماذج","مراقبة الأداء","تحضير البيانات","تدريب النماذج"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ml-pipeline-workflow","description":"Build end-to-end MLOps pipelines from data preparation through model training, validation, and production deployment. Use when creating ML pipelines, implementing MLOps practices, or automating model training and deployment workflows.","bodyPreview":"# ML Pipeline Workflow\n\nComplete end-to-end MLOps pipeline orchestration from data preparation through model deployment.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive guidance for building production ML pipelines that handle the full lifecycle: data ingestion → preparation → training → validation → deployment → monitoring.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building new ML pipelines from scratch\n- Designing workflow orchestration for ML systems\n- Implementing data → model → deployment automation\n-","body":"# ML Pipeline Workflow\n\nComplete end-to-end MLOps pipeline orchestration from data preparation through model deployment.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive guidance for building production ML pipelines that handle the full lifecycle: data ingestion → preparation → training → validation → deployment → monitoring.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building new ML pipelines from scratch\n- Designing workflow orchestration for ML systems\n- Implementing data → model → deployment automation\n- Setting up reproducible training workflows\n- Creating DAG-based ML orchestration\n- Integrating ML components into production systems\n\n## What This Skill Provides\n\n### Core Capabilities\n\n1. **Pipeline Architecture**\n   - End-to-end workflow design\n   - DAG orchestration patterns (Airflow, Dagster, Kubeflow)\n   - Component dependencies and data flow\n   - Error handling and retry strategies\n\n2. **Data Preparation**\n   - Data validation and quality checks\n   - Feature engineering pipelines\n   - Data versioning and lineage\n   - Train/validation/test splitting strategies\n\n3. **Model Training**\n   - Training job orchestration\n   - Hyperparameter management\n   - Experiment tracking integration\n   - Distributed training patterns\n\n4. **Model Validation**\n   - Validation frameworks and metrics\n   - A/B testing infrastructure\n   - Performance regression detection\n   - Model comparison workflows\n\n5. **Deployment Automation**\n   - Model serving patterns\n   - Canary deployments\n   - Blue-green deployment strategies\n   - Rollback mechanisms\n\n### Reference Documentation\n\nSee the `references/` directory for detailed guides:\n\n- **data-preparation.md** - Data cleaning, validation, and feature engineering\n- **model-training.md** - Training workflows and best practices\n- **model-validation.md** - Validation strategies and metrics\n- **model-deployment.md** - Deployment patterns and serving architectures\n\n### Assets and Templates\n\nThe `assets/` directory contains:\n\n- **pipeline-dag.yaml.template** - DAG template for workflow orchestration\n- **training-config.yaml** - Training configuration template\n- **validation-checklist.md** - Pre-deployment validation checklist\n\n## Usage Patterns\n\n### Basic Pipeline Setup\n\n```python\n# 1. Define pipeline stages\nstages = [\n    \"data_ingestion\",\n    \"data_validation\",\n    \"feature_engineering\",\n    \"model_training\",\n    \"model_validation\",\n    \"model_deployment\"\n]\n\n# 2. Configure dependencies\n# See assets/pipeline-dag.yaml.template for full example\n```\n\n### Production Workflow\n\n1. **Data Preparation Phase**\n   - Ingest raw data from sources\n   - Run data quality checks\n   - Apply feature transformations\n   - Version processed datasets\n\n2. **Training Phase**\n   - Load versioned training data\n   - Execute training jobs\n   - Track experiments and metrics\n   - Save trained models\n\n3. **Validation Phase**\n   - Run validation test suite\n   - Compare against baseline\n   - Generate performance reports\n   - Approve for deployment\n\n4. **Deployment Phase**\n   - Package model artifacts\n   - Deploy to serving infrastructure\n   - Configure monitoring\n   - Validate production traffic\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Pipeline Design\n\n- **Modularity**: Each stage should be independently testable\n- **Idempotency**: Re-running stages should be safe\n- **Observability**: Log metrics at every stage\n- **Versioning**: Track data, code, and model versions\n- **Failure Handling**: Implement retry logic and alerting\n\n### Data Management\n\n- Use data validation libraries (Great Expectations, TFX)\n- Version datasets with DVC or similar tools\n- Document feature engineering transformations\n- Maintain data lineage tracking\n\n### Model Operations\n\n- Separate training and serving infrastructure\n- Use model registries (MLflow, Weights & Biases)\n- Implement gradual rollouts for new models\n- Monitor model performance drift\n- Maintain rollback capabilities\n\n### Deployment Strategies\n\n- Start with shadow deployments\n- Use canary releases for validation\n- Implement A/B testing infrastructure\n- Set up automated rollback triggers\n- Monitor latency and throughput\n\n## Integration Points\n\n### Orchestration Tools\n\n- **Apache Airflow**: DAG-based workflow orchestration\n- **Dagster**: Asset-based pipeline orchestration\n- **Kubeflow Pipelines**: Kubernetes-native ML workflows\n- **Prefect**: Modern dataflow automation\n\n### Experiment Tracking\n\n- MLflow for experiment tracking and model registry\n- Weights & Biases for visualization and collaboration\n- TensorBoard for training metrics\n\n### Deployment Platforms\n\n- AWS SageMaker for managed ML infrastructure\n- Google Vertex AI for GCP deployments\n- Azure ML for Azure cloud\n- Kubernetes + KServe for cloud-agnostic serving\n\n## Progressive Disclosure\n\nStart with the basics and gradually add complexity:\n\n1. **Level 1**: Simple linear pipeline (data → train → deploy)\n2. **Level 2**: Add validation and monitoring stages\n3. **Level 3**: Implement hyperparameter tuning\n4. **Level 4**: Add A/B testing and gradual rollouts\n5. **Level 5**: Multi-model pipelines with ensemble strategies\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Batch Training Pipeline\n\n```yaml\n# See assets/pipeline-dag.yaml.template\nstages:\n  - name: data_preparation\n    dependencies: []\n  - name: model_training\n    dependencies: [data_preparation]\n  - name: model_evaluation\n    dependencies: [model_training]\n  - name: model_deployment\n    dependencies: [model_evaluation]\n```\n\n### Real-time Feature Pipeline\n\n```python\n# Stream processing for real-time features\n# Combined with batch training\n# See references/data-preparation.md\n```\n\n### Continuous Training\n\n```python\n# Automated retraining on schedule\n# Triggered by data drift detection\n# See references/model-training.md\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n- **Pipeline failures**: Check dependencies and data availability\n- **Training instability**: Review hyperparameters and data quality\n- **Deployment issues**: Validate model artifacts and serving config\n- **Performance degradation**: Monitor data drift and model metrics\n\n### Debugging Steps\n\n1. Check pipeline logs for each stage\n2. Validate input/output data at boundaries\n3. Test components in isolation\n4. Review experiment tracking metrics\n5. Inspect model artifacts and metadata\n\n## Next Steps\n\nAfter setting up your pipeline:\n\n1. Explore **hyperparameter-tuning** skill for optimization\n2. Learn **experiment-tracking-setup** for MLflow/W&B\n3. Review **model-deployment-patterns** for serving strategies\n4. Implement monitoring with observability tools\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **experiment-tracking-setup**: MLflow and Weights & Biases integration\n- **hyperparameter-tuning**: Automated hyperparameter optimization\n- **model-deployment-patterns**: Advanced deployment strategies\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:02:00.025Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain needing comprehensive MLOps pipeline orchestration for end-to-end machine learning workflows","zh":"适合像 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的 AI 代理，需要全面的 MLOps 流水线编排以进行端到端的机器学习工作流","ja":"AutoGPTやLangChainのようなAIエージェントに最適で、エンドツーエンドのマシンラーニングワークフローを実現するための包括的なMLOpsパイプラインオーケストレーションが必要","ko":"AutoGPT와 LangChain 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 엔드투엔드 머신 러닝 워크플로우를 위한 포괄적인 MLOps 파이프라인 오케스트레이션이 필요함","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan una orquestación de pipeline de MLOps integral para flujos de trabajo de aprendizaje automático de extremo a extremo","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant une orchestration de pipeline MLOps complète pour les flux de travail d''apprentissage automatique de bout en bout","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine umfassende MLOps-Pipeline-Orchestrierung für End-to-End-Machine-Learning-Workflows benötigen","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de orquestração abrangente de pipeline MLOps para fluxos de trabalho de aprendizado de máquina de ponta a ponta","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих всесторонней оркестрации конвейера MLOps для конвейеров машинного обучения от начала до конца","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي مثل AutoGPT و LangChain التي تحتاج إلى أوركسترا خط أنابيب MLOps شاملة لتدفقات العمل من خلال التعلم الآلي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate the full ML lifecycle, from data ingestion to model deployment, using workflow orchestration and MLOps best practices, including data preparation, training, validation, and monitoring","zh":"赋予代理自动化全生命周期的机器学习，从数据摄取到模型部署，使用工作流编排和MLOps最佳实践，包括数据准备、训练、验证和监控","ja":"ワークフロー オーケストレーションと MLOps のベスト プラクティスを使用して、データ インジェストからモデル デプロイまで、エージェントがマシン ラーニングのフル ライフサイクルを自動化できるようにし、データ準備、トレーニング、検証、監視など","ko":"에이전트가 데이터摄取부터 모델 배포까지의 머신 러닝 전체 라이프사이클을 자동화할 수 있도록 워크플로 오케스트레이션과 MLOps 최적实践을 사용하며, 데이터 준비, 훈련, 검증, 모니터링 등을 포함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar el ciclo de vida completo de ML, desde la ingesta de datos hasta la implementación de modelos, utilizando la orquestación de flujos de trabajo y las mejores prácticas de MLOps, incluyendo la preparación de datos, el entrenamiento, la validación y el monitoreo","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser le cycle de vie complet de ML, de l''ingestion de données à la mise en production de modèles, en utilisant l''orchestration de flux de travail et les meilleures pratiques de MLOps, notamment la préparation de données, la formation, la validation et la surveillance","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, den gesamten ML-Lebenszyklus zu automatisieren, von der Datenübernahme bis zur Modellbereitstellung, unter Verwendung der Workflow-Orchestrierung und der besten MLOps-Praktiken, einschließlich der Datenvorbereitung, des Trainings, der Validierung und der Überwachung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar o ciclo de vida completo de ML, desde a ingestão de dados até a implantação do modelo, usando orquestração de fluxo de trabalho e as melhores práticas de MLOps, incluindo preparação de dados, treinamento, validação e monitoramento","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать полный цикл жизни ML, от ингестии данных до развертывания модели, используя оркестрацию рабочих процессов и лучшие практики MLOps, включая подготовку данных, обучение, проверку и мониторинг","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تلقيم دورة حياة كاملة ل ML، من استهلاك البيانات إلى نشر النموذج، باستخدام أوركسترا تدفق العمل وأفضل ممارسات MLOps، بما في ذلك підготовة البيانات و التدريب و التحقق و مراقبة"},"useCases":{"en":["Building new ML pipelines from scratch","Designing workflow orchestration for ML systems","Implementing data-to-model-to-deployment automation","Deploying models to production environments"],"zh":["从头开始构建新的机器学习管道","为机器学习系统设计工作流编排","实现从数据到模型到部署的自动化","将模型部署到生产环境"],"ja":["新しいマシンラーニング パイプラインをスクラッチから構築する","マシンラーニング システムのワークフロー オーケストレーションを設計する","データからモデルへのデプロイまでの自動化を実装する","モデルをプロダクション環境にデプロイする"],"ko":["새로운 머신 러닝 파이프라인을 스크래치부터 구축","머신 러닝 시스템의 워크플로 오케스트레이션 설계","데이터에서 모델로의 배포까지의 자동화 구현","모델을 프로덕션 환경에 배포"],"es":["Construir nuevos pipelines de ML desde cero","Diseñar la orquestación de flujos de trabajo para sistemas de ML","Implementar la automatización de datos a modelo a implementación","Implementar modelos en entornos de producción"],"fr":["Construire de nouveaux pipelines de ML à partir de zéro","Concevoir l''orchestration de flux de travail pour les systèmes de ML","Mettre en œuvre l''automatisation des données au modèle à la mise en production","Déployer des modèles dans des environnements de production"],"de":["Neue ML-Pipelines von Grund auf erstellen","Die Workflow-Orchestrierung für ML-Systeme entwerfen","Die Automatisierung von Daten zu Modell zu Bereitstellung implementieren","Modelle in Produktionsumgebungen bereitstellen"],"pt":["Construir novos pipelines de ML do zero","Projetar orquestração de fluxo de trabalho para sistemas de ML","Implementar automação de dados para modelo para implantação","Implantar modelos em ambientes de produção"],"ru":["Создание новых конвейеров ML с нуля","Проектирование оркестрации рабочих процессов для систем ML","Реализация автоматизации данных для модели для развертывания","Развертывание моделей в производственных средах"],"ar":["بناء خطوط أنابيب ML جديدة من الصفر","تصميم أوركسترا تدفق العمل لأنظمة ML","تنفيذ آلية أتمتة البيانات إلى النموذج إلى النشر","نشر النماذج في بيئات الإنتاج"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires expertise in ML pipeline development","Limited to machine learning workflows only"],"zh":["需要机器学习管道开发的专业知识","仅限于机器学习工作流"],"ja":["マシンラーニング パイプライン開発の専門知識が必要","マシンラーニング ワークフローのみに限定"],"ko":["머신 러닝 파이프라인 개발에 대한 전문 지식이 필요","머신 러닝 워크플로우만으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere experiencia en el desarrollo de pipelines de ML","Limitado a flujos de trabajo de aprendizaje automático solamente"],"fr":["Nécessite une expertise dans le développement de pipelines de ML","Limité aux flux de travail d''apprentissage automatique uniquement"],"de":["Benötigt Erfahrung in der Entwicklung von ML-Pipelines","Begrenzt auf Machine-Learning-Workflows"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento especializado no desenvolvimento de pipelines de ML","Limitado apenas a fluxos de trabalho de aprendizado de máquina"],"ru":["Требует специализированных знаний в области разработки конвейеров ML","Ограничен только конвейерами машинного обучения"],"ar":["يتطلب خبرة متخصصة في تطوير خطوط أنابيب ML","محدود بالتحديد بتدفقات العمل من خلال التعلم الآلي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant/skill-creator', 'community', 'rongma1sheng', 'kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant', 'rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z', '2026-02-18T13:02:44.969Z', NULL, '{"id":"rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"Kiro智能开发助手提供了创建有效技能的指导，帮助开发者提升开发效率和智能化水平","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者が効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供し、開発効率と智能化の向上を支援","ko":"스킬 크리에이터는 개발자가 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공하여 개발 효율과智能화 수준을 향상시킵니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es un sistema de desarrollo de habilidades que proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas para Claude","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un système de développement de compétences qui fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces pour Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeitscreator ist ein Fähigkeitsentwicklungssystem, das Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten für Claude bietet","pt":"O Skill Creator é uma ferramenta que fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes e personalizadas","ru":"Skill Creator — это инструмент, предоставляющий руководство для создания эффективных и индивидуальных навыков","ar":"Skill Creator هو أداة توفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة و مخصصة","en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统","ja":"スキルクリエーター - AI駆動の開発サポートシステム","ko":"스킬 크리에이터 - AI 기반 개발 지원 시스템","es":"Creador de habilidades: Desarrollo de capacidades de Claude","fr":"Créateur de compétences: Développement des capacités de C...","de":"Fähigkeitscreator: Entwicklung von Claudes Fähigkeiten","pt":"Crie Habilidades com o Skill Creator","ru":"Создание навыков с Skill Creator","ar":"إنشاء مهارات مع Skill Creator","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"Kiro智能开发助手提供了创建有效技能的指导，帮助开发者提升开发效率和智能化水平","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者が効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供し、開発効率と智能化の向上を支援","ko":"스킬 크리에이터는 개발자가 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공하여 개발 효율과智能화 수준을 향상시킵니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es un sistema de desarrollo de habilidades que proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas para Claude","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un système de développement de compétences qui fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces pour Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeitscreator ist ein Fähigkeitsentwicklungssystem, das Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten für Claude bietet","pt":"O Skill Creator é uma ferramenta que fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes e personalizadas","ru":"Skill Creator — это инструмент, предоставляющий руководство для создания эффективных и индивидуальных навыков","ar":"Skill Creator هو أداة توفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة و مخصصة","en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"definition":{"en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"features":{"zh":["提供创建有效技能的指导","支持开发者提升开发效率和智能化水平","实现专门化工作流程和工具","提供多样化的技能模板和示例","支持技能的创建、管理和共享"],"ja":["効果的なスキルの作成を支援","開発効率と智能化の向上を支援","専門化されたワークフローとツールを実現","多様なスキルテンプレートとサンプルを提供","スキルの作成、管理、共有をサポート"],"ko":["효과적인 스킬 생성을 지원","개발 효율과智能化 수준의 향상을 지원","전문화된 워크플로우와 툴을 구현","다양한 스킬 템플릿과 샘플을 제공","스킬의 생성, 관리, 공유를 지원"],"es":["Desarrollo de flujos de trabajo especializados","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude","Creación de habilidades efectivas","Guía para el desarrollo de habilidades","Soporte para el desarrollo de capacidades especializadas"],"fr":["Développement de flux de travail spécialisés","Élargissement des capacités de Claude","Création de compétences efficaces","Guide pour le développement de compétences","Support pour le développement de capacités spécialisées"],"de":["Entwicklung spezialisierter Workflows","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten","Anleitung zur Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Unterstützung für die Entwicklung spezialisierter Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Extensão das capacidades do Claude","Fornecimento de conhecimento especializado","Melhoria das workflows","Suporte ao desenvolvimento de habilidades"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных навыков","Расширение возможностей Claude","Предоставление специализированных знаний","Улучшение рабочих процессов","Поддержка разработки навыков"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","توسيع قدرات Claude","توفير معرفة متخصصة","تحسين سير العمل","دعم تطوير المهارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kiro智能开发助手","AI驱动的开发支持系统","创建有效技能","开发效率","智能化水平","专门化工作流程","技能管理"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","AI駆動の開発サポートシステム","効果的なスキルの作成","開発効率","智能化の向上","専門化されたワークフロー","スキル管理"],"ko":["스킬 크리에이터","AI 기반 개발 지원 시스템","효과적인 스킬 생성","개발 효율","智能化 수준","전문화된 워크플로우","스킬 관리"],"es":["desarrollo de habilidades","creador de habilidades","Claude","capacidades especializadas","flujos de trabajo especializados","desarrollo de software","inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["développement de compétences","créateur de compétences","Claude","capacités spécialisées","flux de travail spécialisés","développement de logiciels","intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Fähigkeitsentwicklung","Fähigkeitscreator","Claude","spezialisierte Fähigkeiten","spezifizierte Workflows","Softwareentwicklung","künstliche Intelligenz"],"pt":["criação de habilidades","desenvolvimento de habilidades","ferramenta de criação de habilidades","extensão de capacidades","conhecimento especializado","workflows personalizadas"],"ru":["создание навыков","разработка навыков","инструмент для создания навыков","расширение возможностей","специализированные знания","индивидуальные рабочие процессы"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات","تطوير المهارات","أداة لإنشاء المهارات","توسيع القدرات","معرفة متخصصة","سير عمل مخصص"]}},"owner":"rongma1sheng","repo":"kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","repoPath":"rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These are the only fields that Claude reads to determine when the skill gets used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in describing what the skill is, and when it should be used.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:02:44.969Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的 AI 代理，它们需要专门的知识和工作流扩展。","ja":"Claude、AutoGPT、LangChain などの特別な知識とワークフローの拡張が必要な AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클라우드, 오토지피티, 랭체인などの 전문 지식과 워크플로 확장이 필요한 인공지능 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan conocimientos especializados y extensiones de flujo de trabajo.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude, AutoGPT et LangChain ayant besoin de connaissances spécialisées et d''extensions de flux de travail.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude, AutoGPT und LangChain, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Workflow-Erweiterungen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих специализированных знаний и расширений рабочего процесса.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيعات سير العمل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create modular, self-contained packages extending their capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools, utilizing procedural knowledge and domain-specific onboarding guides, and transforming them into specialized agents equipped with multi-step workflows.","zh":"赋予代理创建模块化、自包含的软件包的能力，扩展其能力，利用专门的知识、工作流程和工具，并利用过程性知识和领域特定的入门指南，将其转化为具有多步骤工作流程的专用代理。","ja":"エージェントがモジュール化された自己完結的なパッケージを作成する能力を付与し、専門知識、ワークフロー、ツールを利用して能力を拡張し、手続き知識とドメイン特有のオンボーディングガイドを利用して、多段階のワークフローを備えた専用エージェントに変換します。","ko":"에이전트가 모듈화된 자체 포함된 패키지를 생성할 수 있는 기능을 부여하여 전문 지식, 워크플로우, 도구를 활용하여 능력을 확장하고, 절차적 지식과 도메인 특정 온보딩 가이드를 활용하여 다단계 워크플로우를 갖춘 전문 에이전트로 변환합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían sus capacidades con conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas, utilizando conocimiento procedural y guías de incorporación específicas del dominio, y transformándolos en agentes especializados equipados con flujos de trabajo de varios pasos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui étendent leurs capacités avec des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils, en utilisant des connaissances procédurales et des guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine, et en les transformant en agents spécialisés équipés de flux de travail à plusieurs étapes.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete zu erstellen, die ihre Fähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen, Workflows und Tools erweitern, unter Verwendung von prozeduralem Wissen und domänen-spezifischen Onboarding-Leitfäden, und sie in spezialisierte Agenten mit mehrschrittigen Workflows umwandelt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar pacotes modulares e autocontidos que estendem suas capacidades com conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas, utilizando conhecimento procedural e guias de integração específicos de domínio, e transformando-os em agentes especializados equipados com fluxos de trabalho em várias etapas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать модульные, самодостаточные пакеты, расширяющие их возможности за счет специализированных знаний, рабочих процессов и инструментов, используя процедурные знания и доменно-специфические руководства по интеграции, и превращая их в специализированных агентов, оснащенных многоступенчатыми рабочими процессами.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء حزم مُستقلة ومتكاملة تمدد قدراتهم بالمعرفة المتخصصة وسير العمل والأدوات، باستخدام المعرفة الإجرائية ودلائل التكامل الخاصة بالمجال، وتحويلهم إلى وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بسير العمل المتعددة المراحل."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific onboarding guides","Developing specialized workflows for tasks","Extending agent capabilities with procedural knowledge"],"zh":["创建领域特定的入门指南","开发任务的专用工作流程","使用过程性知识扩展代理能力"],"ja":["ドメイン特有のオンボーディングガイドを作成する","タスクの専用ワークフローを開発する","手続き知識を使用してエージェントの能力を拡張する"],"ko":["도메인 특정 온보딩 가이드を作成하는 것","작업을 위한 전문 워크플로우를 개발하는 것","절차적 지식을 사용하여 에이전트의 능력을 확장하는 것"],"es":["Creación de guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","Desarrollo de flujos de trabajo especializados para tareas","Ampliación de las capacidades del agente con conocimiento procedural"],"fr":["Création de guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","Développement de flux de travail spécialisés pour les tâches","Extension des capacités de l''agent avec des connaissances procédurales"],"de":["Erstellung von domänen-spezifischen Onboarding-Leitfäden","Entwicklung von spezialisierten Workflows für Aufgaben","Erweiterung der Agenten-Fähigkeiten mit prozeduralem Wissen"],"pt":["Criação de guias de integração específicos de domínio","Desenvolvimento de fluxos de trabalho especializados para tarefas","Extensão das capacidades do agente com conhecimento procedural"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции, специфичных для домена","Разработка специализированных рабочих процессов для задач","Расширение возможностей агента за счет процедурных знаний"],"ar":["إنشاء دلائل التكامل الخاصة بالمجال","تطوير سير عمل متخصصة للمهام","توسيع قدرات العميل بالمعرفة الإجرائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude or compatible agent architecture","Dependent on agent''s existing knowledge base and capabilities"],"zh":["需要克劳德或兼容的代理架构","依赖于代理的现有知识库和能力"],"ja":["Claude または互換性のあるエージェントアーキテクチャが必要","エージェントの既存の知識ベースと能力に依存する"],"ko":["클라우드 또는 호환 에이전트 아키텍처가 필요","에이전트의 기존 지식 베이스와 능력에 의존"],"es":["Requiere Claude o una arquitectura de agente compatible","Dependiente de la base de conocimientos existente del agente y sus capacidades"],"fr":["Nécessite Claude ou une architecture d''agent compatible","Dépendante de la base de connaissances existante de l''agent et de ses capacités"],"de":["Benötigt Claude oder eine kompatible Agenten-Architektur","Abhängig von der bestehenden Wissensbasis und den Fähigkeiten des Agents"],"pt":["Requer Claude ou arquitetura de agente compatível","Dependente da base de conhecimento existente do agente e de suas capacidades"],"ru":["Требует Claude или совместимой архитектуры агента","Зависит от существующей базы знаний агента и его возможностей"],"ar":["يتطلب Claude أو هيكل وكيل متوافق","يعتمد على قاعدة المعرفة الحالية للوكيل وقدراته"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/frontend-design', 'community', 'yashvinthan', 'DuskSpendr', 'yashvinthan/DuskSpendr', 'frontend-design', 0, 0, 25, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z', '2026-02-18T13:02:44.402Z', NULL, '{"id":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/frontend-design","name":"frontend-design","description":{"zh":"前端设计技能指导创建独特的生产级界面，重点关注美学细节和创意选择","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキルは、独自のプロダクショングレードインターフェイスを作成するためのガイダンスを提供し、美学的細部と創造的な選択に重点を置いています","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 스킬은 독특한 생산급 인터페이스를 생성하기 위한 가이드를 제공하며, 미학적 세부 사항과 창의적인 선택에 중점을 둡니다","es":"Este skill permite crear interfaces de frontend personalizadas y de alta calidad, evitando estéticas genéricas","fr":"Cette compétence permet de créer des interfaces de frontend personnalisées et de haute qualité, en évitant les esthétiques génériques","de":"Dieser Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung benutzerdefinierter und hochwertiger Frontend-Schnittstellen, ohne generische Ästhetik","pt":"Desenvolva interfaces de usuário personalizadas e de alta qualidade com atenção aos detalhes estéticos e criativos","ru":"Разработайте уникальные и высококачественные интерфейсы с вниманием к эстетическим деталям и творческим решениям","ar":"أنشئ واجهات مستخدم مخصصة وعالية الجودة مع اهتمام بالتفاصيل الجمالية والخيارات الإبداعية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"前端设计技能 - 创建独特的生产级界面","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキル - 独自のプロダクショングレードインターフェイスを作成","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 스킬 - 독특한 생산급 인터페이스 생성","es":"Diseño de frontend personalizado","fr":"Conception de frontend sur mesure","de":"Benutzerdefiniertes Frontend-Design","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Frontend Personalizado","ru":"Индивидуальный Фронтенд-Дизайн","ar":"تصميم واجهة المستخدم الأمامية المخصصة","en":"frontend-design"},"description":{"zh":"前端设计技能指导创建独特的生产级界面，重点关注美学细节和创意选择","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキルは、独自のプロダクショングレードインターフェイスを作成するためのガイダンスを提供し、美学的細部と創造的な選択に重点を置いています","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 스킬은 독특한 생산급 인터페이스를 생성하기 위한 가이드를 제공하며, 미학적 세부 사항과 창의적인 선택에 중점을 둡니다","es":"Este skill permite crear interfaces de frontend personalizadas y de alta calidad, evitando estéticas genéricas","fr":"Cette compétence permet de créer des interfaces de frontend personnalisées et de haute qualité, en évitant les esthétiques génériques","de":"Dieser Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung benutzerdefinierter und hochwertiger Frontend-Schnittstellen, ohne generische Ästhetik","pt":"Desenvolva interfaces de usuário personalizadas e de alta qualidade com atenção aos detalhes estéticos e criativos","ru":"Разработайте уникальные и высококачественные интерфейсы с вниманием к эстетическим деталям и творческим решениям","ar":"أنشئ واجهات مستخدم مخصصة وعالية الجودة مع اهتمام بالتفاصيل الجمالية والخيارات الإبداعية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["创建独特的生产级界面","注重美学细节和创意选择","避免通用AI风格","支持多种技术约束"],"ja":["独自のプロダクショングレードインターフェイスを作成","美学的細部と創造的な選択に重点を置く","一般的なAIスタイルを避ける","複数の技術的制約をサポート"],"ko":["독특한 생산급 인터페이스 생성","미학적 세부 사항과 창의적인 선택에 중점","일반적인 AI 스타일 피하기","여러 기술적 제약 поддерж하기"],"es":["Creación de interfaces de usuario personalizadas","Enfoque en la estética y el diseño","Implementación de código de producción","Atención al detalle y opciones creativas","Compatibilidad con componentes, páginas y aplicaciones","Consideración de la audiencia y el propósito"],"fr":["Création d''interfaces utilisateur personnalisées","Accent sur l''esthétique et la conception","Mise en œuvre de code de production","Attention aux détails et options créatives","Compatibilité avec les composants, les pages et les applications","Prise en compte de l''audience et de l''objectif"],"de":["Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Benutzeroberflächen","Fokus auf Ästhetik und Design","Implementierung von Produktionscode","Aufmerksamkeit für Details und kreative Optionen","Kompatibilität mit Komponenten, Seiten und Anwendungen","Berücksichtigung der Zielgruppe und des Zwecks"],"pt":["Criação de interfaces de usuário personalizadas","Atenção aos detalhes estéticos e criativos","Desenvolvimento de componentes e páginas","Implementação de soluções técnicas inovadoras","Otimização para dispositivos móveis e desktop","Integração com tecnologias de backend"],"ru":["Создание уникальных интерфейсов","Внимание к эстетическим деталям и творческим решениям","Разработка компонентов и страниц","Реализация инновационных технических решений","Оптимизация для мобильных и настольных устройств","Интеграция с технологиями бэкенда"],"ar":["إنشاء واجهات مستخدم مخصصة","الاهتمام بالتفاصيل الجمالية والخيارات الإبداعية","تطوير المكونات والصفحات","تنفيذ حلول تقنية مبتكرة","تحسين الأداء للجهاز المحمول والكمبيوتر","التكامل مع تقنيات الخلفية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["前端设计","生产级界面","独特美学","AI设计","界面设计","前端开发"],"ja":["フロントエンドデザイン","プロダクショングレードインターフェイス","独自の美学","AIデザイン","インターフェイスデザイン","フロントエンド開発"],"ko":["프론트엔드 디자인","생산급 인터페이스","독특한 미학","AI 디자인","인터페이스 디자인","프론트엔드 개발"],"es":["diseño de frontend","interfaces de usuario personalizadas","estética y diseño","código de producción","desarrollo de frontend","creación de aplicaciones web","diseño de experiencia de usuario","desarrollo de software","tecnologías web"],"fr":["conception de frontend","interfaces utilisateur personnalisées","esthétique et conception","code de production","développement de frontend","création d''applications web","conception d''expérience utilisateur","développement de logiciels","technologies web"],"de":["Frontend-Design","benutzerdefinierte Benutzeroberflächen","Ästhetik und Design","Produktionscode","Frontend-Entwicklung","Erstellung von Webanwendungen","Benutzererfahrung-Design","Software-Entwicklung","Web-Technologien"],"pt":["frontend design","desenvolvimento de frontend","interfaces de usuário personalizadas","design de interface","desenvolvimento web","tecnologias de frontend","otimização de desempenho","experiência do usuário"],"ru":["фронтенд-дизайн","разработка фронтенда","уникальные интерфейсы","дизайн интерфейса","веб-разработка","технологии фронтенда","оптимизация производительности","пользовательский опыт"],"ar":["تصميم الواجهة الأمامية","تطوير الواجهة الأمامية","واجهات مستخدم مخصصة","تصميم الواجهة","تطوير الويب","تقنيات الواجهة الأمامية","تحسين الأداء","تجربة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-design","description":"Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality. Use this skill when the user asks to build web components, pages, or applications. Generates creative, polished code that avoids generic AI aesthetics.","bodyPreview":"This skill guides creation of distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces that avoid generic \"AI slop\" aesthetics. Implement real working code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details and creative choices.\n\nThe user provides frontend requirements: a component, page, application, or interface to build. They may include context about the purpose, audience, or technical constraints.\n\n## Design Thinking\n\nBefore coding, understand the context and commit to a BOLD aesthetic direction:\n- *","body":"This skill guides creation of distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces that avoid generic \"AI slop\" aesthetics. Implement real working code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details and creative choices.\n\nThe user provides frontend requirements: a component, page, application, or interface to build. They may include context about the purpose, audience, or technical constraints.\n\n## Design Thinking\n\nBefore coding, understand the context and commit to a BOLD aesthetic direction:\n- **Purpose**: What problem does this interface solve? Who uses it?\n- **Tone**: Pick an extreme: brutally minimal, maximalist chaos, retro-futuristic, organic/natural, luxury/refined, playful/toy-like, editorial/magazine, brutalist/raw, art deco/geometric, soft/pastel, industrial/utilitarian, etc. There are so many flavors to choose from. Use these for inspiration but design one that is true to the aesthetic direction.\n- **Constraints**: Technical requirements (framework, performance, accessibility).\n- **Differentiation**: What makes this UNFORGETTABLE? What''s the one thing someone will remember?\n\n**CRITICAL**: Choose a clear conceptual direction and execute it with precision. Bold maximalism and refined minimalism both work - the key is intentionality, not intensity.\n\nThen implement working code (HTML/CSS/JS, React, Vue, etc.) that is:\n- Production-grade and functional\n- Visually striking and memorable\n- Cohesive with a clear aesthetic point-of-view\n- Meticulously refined in every detail\n\n## Frontend Aesthetics Guidelines\n\nFocus on:\n- **Typography**: Choose fonts that are beautiful, unique, and interesting. Avoid generic fonts like Arial and Inter; opt instead for distinctive choices that elevate the frontend''s aesthetics; unexpected, characterful font choices. Pair a distinctive display font with a refined body font.\n- **Color & Theme**: Commit to a cohesive aesthetic. Use CSS variables for consistency. Dominant colors with sharp accents outperform timid, evenly-distributed palettes.\n- **Motion**: Use animations for effects and micro-interactions. Prioritize CSS-only solutions for HTML. Use Motion library for React when available. Focus on high-impact moments: one well-orchestrated page load with staggered reveals (animation-delay) creates more delight than scattered micro-interactions. Use scroll-triggering and hover states that surprise.\n- **Spatial Composition**: Unexpected layouts. Asymmetry. Overlap. Diagonal flow. Grid-breaking elements. Generous negative space OR controlled density.\n- **Backgrounds & Visual Details**: Create atmosphere and depth rather than defaulting to solid colors. Add contextual effects and textures that match the overall aesthetic. Apply creative forms like gradient meshes, noise textures, geometric patterns, layered transparencies, dramatic shadows, decorative borders, custom cursors, and grain overlays.\n\nNEVER use generic AI-generated aesthetics like overused font families (Inter, Roboto, Arial, system fonts), cliched color schemes (particularly purple gradients on white backgrounds), predictable layouts and component patterns, and cookie-cutter design that lacks context-specific character.\n\nInterpret creatively and make unexpected choices that feel genuinely designed for the context. No design should be the same. Vary between light and dark themes, different fonts, different aesthetics. NEVER converge on common choices (Space Grotesk, for example) across generations.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Match implementation complexity to the aesthetic vision. Maximalist designs need elaborate code with extensive animations and effects. Minimalist or refined designs need restraint, precision, and careful attention to spacing, typography, and subtle details. Elegance comes from executing the vision well.\n\nRemember: Claude is capable of extraordinary creative work. Don''t hold back, show what can truly be created when thinking outside the box and committing fully to a distinctive vision."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:02:44.402Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Interface Agents requiring production-grade frontend interface creation with attention to aesthetic details and creative choices.","zh":"适用于需要生产级前端接口创建并注重美观细节和创意选择的接口代理。","ja":"生産レベルのフロントエンドインターフェイスの作成と美的細部への注意が必要なインターフェイスエージェントに適しています。","ko":"생산급 프론트엔드 인터페이스 생성과 미적 세부 사항 및 창의적 선택에 주의가 필요한 인터페이스 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Interfaz que requieren la creación de interfaz de frontend de nivel de producción con atención a los detalles estéticos y opciones creativas.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Interface nécessitant la création d''une interface frontend de niveau de production avec attention aux détails esthétiques et aux choix créatifs.","de":"Ideal für Interface-Agents, die eine erstklassige Frontend-Oberflächenerstellung mit besonderer Aufmerksamkeit für ästhetische Details und kreative Entscheidungen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Interface que requerem criação de interface de frontend de nível de produção com atenção a detalhes estéticos e escolhas criativas.","ru":"Идеально для Интерфейсных Агентов, требующих создания интерфейса frontend уровня производства с учетом эстетических деталей и творческих решений.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة يتطلب إنشاء واجهة أمامية من الدرجة الأولى مع اهتمام بالتفاصيل الجمالية والخيارات الإبداعية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement real working code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details, utilizing HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to create distinctive interfaces that avoid generic ''AI slop'' aesthetics, and supporting various file formats like .svg for creative and technical flexibility.","zh":"赋予代理实现真正可运行的代码，并注重美观细节，利用HTML、CSS和JavaScript创建独特的界面，避免通用的人工智能外观，并支持各种文件格式，如.svg，以实现创意和技术灵活性。","ja":"エージェントに実行可能なコードを実装し、美的細部に注意を払い、HTML、CSS、JavaScriptを使用して独自のインターフェイスを作成し、汎用的な「AI外観」を避け、.svgなどの様々なファイル形式をサポートして創造性と技術的柔軟性を実現します。","ko":"에이전트에 실제 작동하는 코드를 구현할 수 있는 권한을 부여하고, 미적 세부 사항에 주의를 기울이며, HTML, CSS 및 JavaScript를 사용하여 고유한 인터페이스를 생성하고, 일반적인 ''AI 외관''을 피하고, .svg와 같은 다양한 파일 형식을 지원하여 창의적이고 기술적으로 유연한 구현을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar código de trabajo real con una atención excepcional a los detalles estéticos, utilizando HTML, CSS y JavaScript para crear interfaces distintivas que evitan la estética genérica de ''suciedad de IA'', y que admiten varios formatos de archivo como .svg para flexibilidad creativa y técnica.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre un code de travail réel avec une attention exceptionnelle aux détails esthétiques, en utilisant HTML, CSS et JavaScript pour créer des interfaces distinctives qui évitent l''esthétique générique de ''sucée d''IA'', et qui prennent en charge divers formats de fichiers comme .svg pour une flexibilité créative et technique.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, echten Arbeitscode mit außergewöhnlicher Aufmerksamkeit für ästhetische Details zu implementieren, indem HTML, CSS und JavaScript verwendet werden, um einzigartige Schnittstellen zu erstellen, die eine generische ''KI-Schlamperei''-Ästhetik vermeiden und verschiedene Dateiformate wie .svg für kreative und technische Flexibilität unterstützen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar código de trabalho real com atenção excepcional a detalhes estéticos, utilizando HTML, CSS e JavaScript para criar interfaces distintas que evitam estética genérica ''slop de IA'', e que suportam vários formatos de arquivo como .svg para flexibilidade criativa e técnica.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать рабочий код с исключительным вниманием к эстетическим деталям, используя HTML, CSS и JavaScript для создания характерных интерфейсов, избегая.generic ''сlop ИИ'' эстетики, и поддерживая различные форматы файлов, такие как .svg для творческой и технической гибкости.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنفيذ رموز العمل الحقيقي مع اهتمام استثنائي بالتفاصيل الجمالية، باستخدام HTML و CSS و JavaScript لإنشاء واجهات متميزة تتجنب جماليات ''سلوك الذكاء الاصطناعي'' العامة، ودعم تنسيقات الملفات المختلفة مثل .svg من أجل المرونة الإبداعية والفنية."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing custom UI components for web applications","Building responsive and adaptive webpage layouts","Creating interactive frontend interfaces for user engagement"],"zh":["为Web应用程序设计自定义UI组件","构建响应式和自适应网页布局","创建交互式前端接口以提高用户参与度"],"ja":["WebアプリケーションのためのカスタムUIコンポーネントを設計する","レスポンシブでアダプティブなWebページレイアウトを構築する","ユーザー参加を促進するためのインタラクティブなフロントエンドインターフェイスを作成する"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션을 위한 사용자 지정 UI 컴포넌트를 설계하는 것","반응형 및 적응형 웹 페이지 레이아웃을 구축하는 것","사용자 참여를 높이기 위한 상호작용형 프론트엔드 인터페이스를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Diseñar componentes de interfaz de usuario personalizados para aplicaciones web","Crear diseños de página web responsivos y adaptativos","Crear interfaces de frontend interactivas para la participación del usuario"],"fr":["Concevoir des composants d''interface utilisateur personnalisés pour les applications Web","Créer des dispositions de page Web réactives et adaptatives","Créer des interfaces frontend interactives pour la participation de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten für Webanwendungen entwerfen","Responsive und adaptive Webseitengestaltungen erstellen","Interaktive Frontend-Oberflächen für die Benutzerverbindung erstellen"],"pt":["Projeto de componentes de UI personalizados para aplicações web","Construção de layouts de páginas web responsivas e adaptáveis","Criação de interfaces de frontend interativas para envolvimento do usuário"],"ru":["Проектирование пользовательских компонентов UI для веб-приложений","Построение адаптивных и отзывчивых макетов веб-страниц","Создание интерактивных интерфейсов frontend для вовлечения пользователя"],"ar":["تصميم مكونات واجهة المستخدم المخصصة لتطبيقات الويب","بناء تخطيطات صفحات الويب المستجيبة والتكيفية","إنشاء واجهات أمامية تفاعلية لاستثارة المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user-provided frontend requirements and context","Dependent on technical constraints and compatibility with existing systems"],"zh":["需要用户提供前端要求和上下文","依赖于技术约束和与现有系统的兼容性"],"ja":["ユーザーが提供するフロントエンドの要件とコンテキストが必要","技術的制約と既存のシステムとの互換性に依存する"],"ko":["사용자가 제공하는 프론트엔드 요구 사항과 컨텍스트가 필요함","기술적 제약과 기존 시스템과의 호환성에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere requisitos y contexto de frontend proporcionados por el usuario","Dependiente de las limitaciones técnicas y la compatibilidad con los sistemas existentes"],"fr":["Nécessite des exigences et un contexte de frontend fournis par l''utilisateur","Dépend des contraintes techniques et de la compatibilité avec les systèmes existants"],"de":["Benötigt vom Benutzer bereitgestellte Anforderungen und Kontext für die Oberfläche","Abhängig von technischen Einschränkungen und der Kompatibilität mit bestehenden Systemen"],"pt":["Exige requisitos e contexto de frontend fornecidos pelo usuário","Depende de restrições técnicas e compatibilidade com sistemas existentes"],"ru":["Требует предоставления пользователями требований и контекста frontend","Зависит от технических ограничений и совместимости с существующими системами"],"ar":["يتطلب متطلبات وسياق واجهة أمامية مقدمة من قبل المستخدم","يعتمد على القيود الفنية والتوافق مع الأنظمة الحالية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":25}');
