ートの保存を含む、特定の要件と規範を満たす必要があります","ko":"xlsx 파일에는 0개 공식 오류 및 기존 템플릿 보존을 포함하여 특정 요구 사항 및 규범을 충족해야 합니다","es":"La generación de archivos xlsx requiere cero errores de fórmula y la conservación de formatos existentes. Aprende a crear modelos financieros precisos.","fr":"La génération de fichiers xlsx nécessite zéro erreur de formule et la conservation des formats existants. Apprenez à créer des modèles financiers précis.","de":"Die Erstellung von xlsx-Dateien erfordert null Formel-fehler und die Erhaltung bestehender Formate. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie präzise Finanzmodelle erstellen.","pt":"O skill xlsx é uma ferramenta para criar arquivos Excel perfeitos, sem erros de fórmula e preservando os modelos existentes.","ru":"Навык xlsx - это инструмент для создания идеальных файлов Excel, без ошибок формул и сохранения существующих шаблонов.","ar":"مهارة xlsx هي أداة لإنشاء ملفات إكسل مثالية، بدون أخطاء صيغ و الحفاظ على القوالب الحالية.","en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"definition":{"en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"features":{"zh":["零公式错误","保留现有模板","财务模型的色彩编码","Excel文件格式要求","公式错误检查"],"ja":["零フォーミュラエラー","既存のテンプレートの保存","財務モデルの色コード","Excelファイル形式の要件","フォーミュラエラーのチェック"],"ko":["0개 공식 오류","기존 템플릿 보존","재무 모델의 색상 코드","Excel 파일 형식 요구 사항","공식 오류 확인"],"es":["Cero errores de fórmula","Conservación de formatos existentes","Modelos financieros precisos","Color coding para una mejor visualización","Compatibilidad con archivos xlsx"],"fr":["Zéro erreur de formule","Conservation des formats existants","Modèles financiers précis","Color coding pour une meilleure visualisation","Compatibilité avec les fichiers xlsx"],"de":["Null Formel-fehler","Erhaltung bestehender Formate","Präzise Finanzmodelle","Color coding für eine bessere Visualisierung","Kompatibilität mit xlsx-Dateien"],"pt":["Criação de arquivos XLSX sem erros de fórmula","Preservação de modelos existentes","Manutenção de templates personalizados","Suporte a modelos financeiros","Coloração de células para destacar informações importantes","Compatibilidade com diferentes versões do Excel"],"ru":["Создание файлов XLSX без ошибок формул","Сохранение существующих шаблонов","Поддержка пользовательских шаблонов","Поддержка финансовых моделей","Цветовая кодировка ячеек для выделения важной информации","Совместимость с разными версиями Excel"],"ar":["إنشاء ملفات XLSX بدون أخطاء صيغ","الحفاظ على القوالب الحالية","دعم القوالب المخصصة","دعم نماذج مالية","تلوين الخلايا لتحديد المعلومات المهمة","التوافق مع إصدارات مختلفة من إكسل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["xlsx格式","Excel文件","零公式错误","保留现有模板","财务模型","色彩编码","公式错误检查"],"ja":["xlsx形式","Excelファイル","零フォーミュラエラー","既存のテンプレートの保存","財務モデルの色コード","フォーミュラエラーのチェック"],"ko":["xlsx 형식","Excel 파일","0개 공식 오류","기존 템플릿 보존","재무 모델의 색상 코드","공식 오류 확인"],"es":["xlsx","generación de archivos xlsx","cero errores de fórmula","modelos financieros","color coding","compatibilidad con xlsx","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["xlsx","génération de fichiers xlsx","zéro erreur de formule","modèles financiers","color coding","compatibilité avec xlsx","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["xlsx","erstellung von xlsx-dateien","null formel-fehler","finanzmodelle","color coding","kompatibilität mit xlsx","software-entwicklung","software-ingeneur"],"pt":["xlsx","arquivos excel","erros de fórmula","modelos financeiros","templates personalizados","coloração de células","compatibilidade excel","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de produtividade"],"ru":["xlsx","файлы excel","ошибки формул","финансовые модели","пользовательские шаблоны","цветовая кодировка ячеек","совместимость excel","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты производительности"],"ar":["xlsx","ملفات إكسل","أخطاء صيغ","نماذج مالية","قوالب مخصصة","تلوين الخلايا","توافق إكسل","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات الإنتاجية"]}},"owner":"rongma1sheng","repo":"kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","repoPath":"rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"xlsx","description":"Comprehensive spreadsheet creation, editing, and analysis with support for formulas, formatting, data analysis, and visualization. When Claude needs to work with spreadsheets (.xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, .tsv, etc) for: (1) Creating new spreadsheets with formulas and formatting, (2) Reading or analyzing data, (3) Modify existing spreadsheets while preserving formulas, (4) Data analysis and visualization in spreadsheets, or (5) Recalculating formulas","bodyPreview":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding S","body":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding Standards\nUnless otherwise stated by the user or existing template\n\n#### Industry-Standard Color Conventions\n- **Blue text (RGB: 0,0,255)**: Hardcoded inputs, and numbers users will change for scenarios\n- **Black text (RGB: 0,0,0)**: ALL formulas and calculations\n- **Green text (RGB: 0,128,0)**: Links pulling from other worksheets within same workbook\n- **Red text (RGB: 255,0,0)**: External links to other files\n- **Yellow background (RGB: 255,255,0)**: Key assumptions needing attention or cells that need to be updated\n\n### Number Formatting Standards\n\n#### Required Format Rules\n- **Years**: Format as text strings (e.g., \"2024\" not \"2,024\")\n- **Currency**: Use $#,##0 format; ALWAYS specify units in headers (\"Revenue ($mm)\")\n- **Zeros**: Use number formatting to make all zeros \"-\", including percentages (e.g., \"$#,##0;($#,##0);-\")\n- **Percentages**: Default to 0.0% format (one decimal)\n- **Multiples**: Format as 0.0x for valuation multiples (EV/EBITDA, P/E)\n- **Negative numbers**: Use parentheses (123) not minus -123\n\n### Formula Construction Rules\n\n#### Assumptions Placement\n- Place ALL assumptions (growth rates, margins, multiples, etc.) in separate assumption cells\n- Use cell references instead of hardcoded values in formulas\n- Example: Use =B5*(1+$B$6) instead of =B5*1.05\n\n#### Formula Error Prevention\n- Verify all cell references are correct\n- Check for off-by-one errors in ranges\n- Ensure consistent formulas across all projection periods\n- Test with edge cases (zero values, negative numbers)\n- Verify no unintended circular references\n\n#### Documentation Requirements for Hardcodes\n- Comment or in cells beside (if end of table). Format: \"Source: [System/Document], [Date], [Specific Reference], [URL if applicable]\"\n- Examples:\n  - \"Source: Company 10-K, FY2024, Page 45, Revenue Note, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Company 10-Q, Q2 2025, Exhibit 99.1, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Bloomberg Terminal, 8/15/2025, AAPL US Equity\"\n  - \"Source: FactSet, 8/20/2025, Consensus Estimates Screen\"\n\n# XLSX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA user may ask you to create, edit, or analyze the contents of an .xlsx file. You have different tools and workflows available for different tasks.\n\n## Important Requirements\n\n**LibreOffice Required for Formula Recalculation**: You can assume LibreOffice is installed for recalculating formula values using the `recalc.py` script. The script automatically configures LibreOffice on first run\n\n## Reading and analyzing data\n\n### Data analysis with pandas\nFor data analysis, visualization, and basic operations, use **pandas** which provides powerful data manipulation capabilities:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read Excel\ndf = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'')  # Default: first sheet\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', sheet_name=None)  # All sheets as dict\n\n# Analyze\ndf.head()      # Preview data\ndf.info()      # Column info\ndf.describe()  # Statistics\n\n# Write Excel\ndf.to_excel(''output.xlsx'', index=False)\n```\n\n## Excel File Workflows\n\n## CRITICAL: Use Formulas, Not Hardcoded Values\n\n**Always use Excel formulas instead of calculating values in Python and hardcoding them.** This ensures the spreadsheet remains dynamic and updateable.\n\n### ❌ WRONG - Hardcoding Calculated Values\n```python\n# Bad: Calculating in Python and hardcoding result\ntotal = df[''Sales''].sum()\nsheet[''B10''] = total  # Hardcodes 5000\n\n# Bad: Computing growth rate in Python\ngrowth = (df.iloc[-1][''Revenue''] - df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']) / df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']\nsheet[''C5''] = growth  # Hardcodes 0.15\n\n# Bad: Python calculation for average\navg = sum(values) / len(values)\nsheet[''D20''] = avg  # Hardcodes 42.5\n```\n\n### ✅ CORRECT - Using Excel Formulas\n```python\n# Good: Let Excel calculate the sum\nsheet[''B10''] = ''=SUM(B2:B9)''\n\n# Good: Growth rate as Excel formula\nsheet[''C5''] = ''=(C4-C2)/C2''\n\n# Good: Average using Excel function\nsheet[''D20''] = ''=AVERAGE(D2:D19)''\n```\n\nThis applies to ALL calculations - totals, percentages, ratios, differences, etc. The spreadsheet should be able to recalculate when source data changes.\n\n## Common Workflow\n1. **Choose tool**: pandas for data, openpyxl for formulas/formatting\n2. **Create/Load**: Create new workbook or load existing file\n3. **Modify**: Add/edit data, formulas, and formatting\n4. **Save**: Write to file\n5. **Recalculate formulas (MANDATORY IF USING FORMULAS)**: Use the recalc.py script\n   ```bash\n   python recalc.py output.xlsx\n   ```\n6. **Verify and fix any errors**: \n   - The script returns JSON with error details\n   - If `status` is `errors_found`, check `error_summary` for specific error types and locations\n   - Fix the identified errors and recalculate again\n   - Common errors to fix:\n     - `#REF!`: Invalid cell references\n     - `#DIV/0!`: Division by zero\n     - `#VALUE!`: Wrong data type in formula\n     - `#NAME?`: Unrecognized formula name\n\n### Creating new Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl for formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, PatternFill, Alignment\n\nwb = Workbook()\nsheet = wb.active\n\n# Add data\nsheet[''A1''] = ''Hello''\nsheet[''B1''] = ''World''\nsheet.append([''Row'', ''of'', ''data''])\n\n# Add formula\nsheet[''B2''] = ''=SUM(A1:A10)''\n\n# Formatting\nsheet[''A1''].font = Font(bold=True, color=''FF0000'')\nsheet[''A1''].fill = PatternFill(''solid'', start_color=''FFFF00'')\nsheet[''A1''].alignment = Alignment(horizontal=''center'')\n\n# Column width\nsheet.column_dimensions[''A''].width = 20\n\nwb.save(''output.xlsx'')\n```\n\n### Editing existing Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl to preserve formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\n\n# Load existing file\nwb = load_workbook(''existing.xlsx'')\nsheet = wb.active  # or wb[''SheetName''] for specific sheet\n\n# Working with multiple sheets\nfor sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n    sheet = wb[sheet_name]\n    print(f\"Sheet: {sheet_name}\")\n\n# Modify cells\nsheet[''A1''] = ''New Value''\nsheet.insert_rows(2)  # Insert row at position 2\nsheet.delete_cols(3)  # Delete column 3\n\n# Add new sheet\nnew_sheet = wb.create_sheet(''NewSheet'')\nnew_sheet[''A1''] = ''Data''\n\nwb.save(''modified.xlsx'')\n```\n\n## Recalculating formulas\n\nExcel files created or modified by openpyxl contain formulas as strings but not calculated values. Use the provided `recalc.py` script to recalculate formulas:\n\n```bash\npython recalc.py <excel_file> [timeout_seconds]\n```\n\nExample:\n```bash\npython recalc.py output.xlsx 30\n```\n\nThe script:\n- Automatically sets up LibreOffice macro on first run\n- Recalculates all formulas in all sheets\n- Scans ALL cells for Excel errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, etc.)\n- Returns JSON with detailed error locations and counts\n- Works on both Linux and macOS\n\n## Formula Verification Checklist\n\nQuick checks to ensure formulas work correctly:\n\n### Essential Verification\n- [ ] **Test 2-3 sample references**: Verify they pull correct values before building full model\n- [ ] **Column mapping**: Confirm Excel columns match (e.g., column 64 = BL, not BK)\n- [ ] **Row offset**: Remember Excel rows are 1-indexed (DataFrame row 5 = Excel row 6)\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n- [ ] **NaN handling**: Check for null values with `pd.notna()`\n- [ ] **Far-right columns**: FY data often in columns 50+ \n- [ ] **Multiple matches**: Search all occurrences, not just first\n- [ ] **Division by zero**: Check denominators before using `/` in formulas (#DIV/0!)\n- [ ] **Wrong references**: Verify all cell references point to intended cells (#REF!)\n- [ ] **Cross-sheet references**: Use correct format (Sheet1!A1) for linking sheets\n\n### Formula Testing Strategy\n- [ ] **Start small**: Test formulas on 2-3 cells before applying broadly\n- [ ] **Verify dependencies**: Check all cells referenced in formulas exist\n- [ ] **Test edge cases**: Include zero, negative, and very large values\n\n### Interpreting recalc.py Output\nThe script returns JSON with error details:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",           // or \"errors_found\"\n  \"total_errors\": 0,              // Total error count\n  \"total_formulas\": 42,           // Number of formulas in file\n  \"error_summary\": {              // Only present if errors found\n    \"#REF!\": {\n      \"count\": 2,\n      \"locations\": [\"Sheet1!B5\", \"Sheet1!C10\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Library Selection\n- **pandas**: Best for data analysis, bulk operations, and simple data export\n- **openpyxl**: Best for complex formatting, formulas, and Excel-specific features\n\n### Working with openpyxl\n- Cell indices are 1-based (row=1, column=1 refers to cell A1)\n- Use `data_only=True` to read calculated values: `load_workbook(''file.xlsx'', data_only=True)`\n- **Warning**: If opened with `data_only=True` and saved, formulas are replaced with values and permanently lost\n- For large files: Use `read_only=True` for reading or `write_only=True` for writing\n- Formulas are preserved but not evaluated - use recalc.py to update values\n\n### Working with pandas\n- Specify data types to avoid inference issues: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', dtype={''id'': str})`\n- For large files, read specific columns: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', usecols=[''A'', ''C'', ''E''])`\n- Handle dates properly: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', parse_dates=[''date_column''])`\n\n## Code Style Guidelines\n**IMPORTANT**: When generating Python code for Excel operations:\n- Write minimal, concise Python code without unnecessary comments\n- Avoid verbose variable names and redundant operations\n- Avoid unnecessary print statements\n\n**For Excel files themselves**:\n- Add comments to cells with complex formulas or important assumptions\n- Document data sources for hardcoded values\n- Include notes for key calculations and model sections"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:03:20.151Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced Excel file manipulation and formula error handling capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级Excel文件操作和公式错误处理能力的数据分析代理。","ja":"高度なExcelファイル操作と式のエラーハンドリング機能が必要なデータ分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 Excel 파일 조작 및 수식 오류 처리 기능이 필요한 데이터 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de datos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de manipulación de archivos de Excel y manejo de errores de fórmulas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données ayant besoin de capacités avancées de manipulation de fichiers Excel et de gestion des erreurs de formules.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte Excel-Dateimanipulation und Formel-Fehlerbehandlungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de manipulação de arquivos do Excel e tratamento de erros de fórmulas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности манипулирования файлами Excel и обработки ошибок формул.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل البيانات التي تحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتعامل مع ملفات إكسل ومعالجة أخطاء الصيغ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate and modify Excel files with zero formula errors, preserving existing templates and conventions, while utilizing financial modeling color coding standards and handling files in .xlsx format.","zh":"使代理能够生成和修改Excel文件，且不包含公式错误，保留现有的模板和约定，同时使用财务建模颜色编码标准，并处理.xlsx格式的文件。","ja":"エージェントがゼロの式エラーでExcelファイルを生成および変更できるようにし、既存のテンプレートと規約を保持しながら、財務モデリングのカラーコーディング規格を使用し、.xlsx形式のファイルを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 공식을 포함하지 않는 Excel 파일을 생성 및 수정할 수 있게 하여 기존 템플릿 및 규약을 유지하면서 재무 모델링 색상 코드 표준을 사용하고 .xlsx 형식의 파일을 처리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar y modificar archivos de Excel con cero errores de fórmulas, preservando plantillas y convenciones existentes, al mismo tiempo que utiliza estándares de codificación de colores de modelado financiero y maneja archivos en formato .xlsx.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer et de modifier des fichiers Excel avec zéro erreur de formule, en préservant les modèles et conventions existants, tout en utilisant des normes de codage de couleurs de modélisation financière et en gérant des fichiers au format .xlsx.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Excel-Dateien mit null Formelfehlern zu generieren und zu ändern, vorhandene Vorlagen und Konventionen zu erhalten, während sie Finanzmodellierungs-Farbcodierungsstandards nutzen und Dateien im .xlsx-Format verarbeiten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar e modificar arquivos do Excel sem erros de fórmulas, preservando modelos e convenções existentes, utilizando padrões de codificação de cores de modelagem financeira e manipulando arquivos no formato .xlsx.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать и изменять файлы Excel без ошибок формул, сохраняя существующие шаблоны и соглашения, используя стандарты цветового кодирования финансового моделирования и обрабатывая файлы в формате .xlsx.","ar":"تمكن العميل من إنشاء وتعديل ملفات إكسل دون أخطاء في الصيغ، مع الحفاظ على القوالب والاتفاقيات الموجودة، واستخدام معايير الترميز بالألوان للنمذجة المالية، وتعامل مع الملفات بامتداد .xlsx."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Excel file updates with exact format matching","Debugging formula errors in complex financial models","Generating new Excel files with standardized color coding"],"zh":["自动更新Excel文件以匹配确切格式","调试复杂财务模型中的公式错误","生成具有标准颜色编码的新Excel文件"],"ja":["正確な形式の一致でExcelファイルを自動更新する","複雑な財務モデルの式エラーをデバッグする","標準的なカラーコーディングを持つ新しいExcelファイルを生成する"],"ko":["정확한 형식 일치로 Excel 파일을 자동으로 업데이트하는 것","복잡한 재무 모델의 수식 오류를 디버깅하는 것","표준적인 색상 코드를 갖는 새로운 Excel 파일을 생성하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar actualizaciones de archivos de Excel con coincidencia de formato exacta","Depurar errores de fórmulas en modelos financieros complejos","Generar nuevos archivos de Excel con codificación de colores estandarizada"],"fr":["Automatiser les mises à jour de fichiers Excel avec une correspondance de format exacte","Déboguer les erreurs de formules dans les modèles financiers complexes","Générer de nouveaux fichiers Excel avec une codification des couleurs standardisée"],"de":["Automatisierung von Excel-Datei-Aktualisierungen mit exakter Formatübereinstimmung","Fehlerbehebung in komplexen Finanzmodellen","Erzeugen neuer Excel-Dateien mit standardisierter Farbcodierung"],"pt":["Automatizar atualizações de arquivos do Excel com correspondência de formato exata","Depurar erros de fórmulas em modelos financeiros complexos","Gerar novos arquivos do Excel com codificação de cores padronizada"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обновления файлов Excel с точным соответствием формата","Отладить ошибки формул в сложных финансовых моделях","Генерировать новые файлы Excel с стандартизированной цветовой кодировкой"],"ar":["أتمتة تحديث ملفات إكسل مع مطابقة صيغة دقيقة","تصحيح أخطاء الصيغ في نماذج مالية معقدة","إنشاء ملفات إكسل جديدة مع ترميز ألوان معياري"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires exact matching of existing template formats and styles","Limited to .xlsx file format","Must handle zero formula errors, including #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"zh":["需要确切匹配现有的模板格式和样式","仅限于.xlsx文件格式","必须处理零公式错误，包括#REF!、#DIV/0!、#VALUE!、#N/A、#NAME?"],"ja":["既存のテンプレート形式とスタイルを正確に一致させる必要がある",".xlsx形式のファイルのみに限定される","ゼロの式エラーを処理する必要がある、#REF!、#DIV/0!、#VALUE!、#N/A、#NAME?を含む"],"ko":["기존 템플릿 형식 및 스타일을 정확히 일치시켜야 함",".xlsx 형식의 파일만으로 제한됨","공식 오류를 0개로 처리해야 함, #REF!、#DIV/0!、#VALUE!、#N/A、#NAME?를 포함하여"],"es":["Requiere una coincidencia exacta de formatos y estilos de plantilla existentes","Limitado al formato de archivo .xlsx","Debe manejar cero errores de fórmulas, incluyendo #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"fr":["Nécessite une correspondance exacte des formats et styles de modèle existants","Limité au format de fichier .xlsx","Doit gérer zéro erreur de formule, y compris #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"de":["Erfordert eine exakte Übereinstimmung von vorhandenen Vorlagenformaten und -stilen","Begrenzt auf das Dateiformat .xlsx","Muss null Formelfehler verarbeiten, einschließlich #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"pt":["Exige correspondência exata de formatos e estilos de modelos existentes","Limitado ao formato de arquivo .xlsx","Deve lidar com zero erros de fórmulas, incluindo #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"ru":["Требует точного соответствия существующих форматов и стилей шаблонов","Ограничен форматом файла .xlsx","Должен обрабатывать нулевые ошибки формул, включая #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"ar":["يتطلب مطابقة دقيقة لتنسيقات وأساليب القوالب الموجودة","محدود بامتداد ملف .xlsx","يجب التعامل مع صفر أخطاء في الصيغ، بما في ذلك #REF! ، #DIV/0! ، #VALUE! ، #N/A ، #NAME?"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('feed-mob/feedmob-adpilot-mcp/mcp-builder', 'community', 'feed-mob', 'feedmob-adpilot-mcp', 'feed-mob/feedmob-adpilot-mcp', 'mcp-builder', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.516Z', '2026-02-18T13:03:45.770Z', NULL, '{"id":"feed-mob/feedmob-adpilot-mcp/mcp-builder","name":"mcp-builder","description":{"zh":"MCP Builder 是用于创建高质量 MCP 服务器的工具，实现 LLM 与外部服务的交互","ja":"MCP Builder は、高品質の MCP サーバーを作成して LLM と外部サービスを接続するためのツールです","ko":"MCP 빌더는 높은 품질의 MCP 서버를 생성하여 LLM과 외부 서비스를 연동하는 데 사용되는 툴입니다","es":"El servidor MCP permite a los LLM interactuar con servicios externos a través de herramientas bien diseñadas","fr":"Le serveur MCP permet aux LLM d''interagir avec des services externes via des outils bien conçus","de":"Der MCP-Server ermöglicht es LLM, mit externen Diensten über gut gestaltete Tools zu interagieren","pt":"Desenvolva servidores MCP para permitir que LLMs realizem tarefas do mundo real de forma eficaz","ru":"Разработайте серверы MCP, чтобы позволить LLM выполнять реальные задачи эффективно","ar":"طور خوادم MCP لتمكين LLMs من إنجاز مهام العالم الحقيقي بفعالية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"MCP Builder 技术指南","ja":"MCP Builder 技術ガイド","ko":"MCP 빌더 개발 가이드","es":"Guía de desarrollo de servidores MCP","fr":"Guide de développement de serveurs MCP","de":"MCP-Server-Entwicklungsleitfaden","pt":"Guia de Desenvolvimento de Servidor MCP","ru":"Руководство по разработке сервера MCP","ar":"دليل تطوير خادم MCP","en":"mcp-builder"},"description":{"zh":"MCP Builder 是用于创建高质量 MCP 服务器的工具，实现 LLM 与外部服务的交互","ja":"MCP Builder は、高品質の MCP サーバーを作成して LLM と外部サービスを接続するためのツールです","ko":"MCP 빌더는 높은 품질의 MCP 서버를 생성하여 LLM과 외부 서비스를 연동하는 데 사용되는 툴입니다","es":"El servidor MCP permite a los LLM interactuar con servicios externos a través de herramientas bien diseñadas","fr":"Le serveur MCP permet aux LLM d''interagir avec des services externes via des outils bien conçus","de":"Der MCP-Server ermöglicht es LLM, mit externen Diensten über gut gestaltete Tools zu interagieren","pt":"Desenvolva servidores MCP para permitir que LLMs realizem tarefas do mundo real de forma eficaz","ru":"Разработайте серверы MCP, чтобы позволить LLM выполнять реальные задачи эффективно","ar":"طور خوادم MCP لتمكين LLMs من إنجاز مهام العالم الحقيقي بفعالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["创建高质量的 MCP 服务器","实现 LLM 与外部服务的交互","支持现代 MCP 设计","提供 API 覆盖和工作流工具","支持深入研究和规划","高级工作流"],"ja":["高品質の MCP サーバーの作成","LLM と外部サービスの接続","モダンな MCP デザインのサポート","API カバレッジとワークフロー ツールの提供","深入的な研究と計画のサポート","高度なワークフロー"],"ko":["높은 품질의 MCP 서버 생성","LLM과 외부 서비스의 연동","최신 MCP 설계 지원","API 커버리지 및 워크플로우 툴 제공","심도 있는 연구 및 계획 지원","고급 워크플로우"],"es":["Diseño de API de cobertura vs. herramientas de flujo de trabajo","Investigación y planificación en profundidad","Creación de servidores MCP de alta calidad","Interacción con servicios externos","Realización de tareas del mundo real"],"fr":["Conception d''API de couverture vs. outils de flux de travail","Recherche et planification en profondeur","Création de serveurs MCP de haute qualité","Interaction avec des services externes","Réalisation de tâches du monde réel"],"de":["API-Abdeckungsdesign vs. Workflow-Tools","Tiefe Forschung und Planung","Erstellung von hochwertigen MCP-Servern","Interaktion mit externen Diensten","Ausführung von realen Aufgaben"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de servidores MCP personalizados","Integração com serviços externos","Otimização para LLMs","Ferramentas de workflow avançadas","Cobertura de API abrangente","Planejamento e pesquisa aprofundados"],"ru":["Разработка индивидуальных серверов MCP","Интеграция с внешними сервисами","Оптимизация для LLM","Продвинутые инструменты workflow","Полное покрытие API","Глубокое планирование и исследование"],"ar":["تطوير خوادم MCP مخصصة","التكامل مع الخدمات الخارجية","تحسين الأداء ل LLMs","أدوات سير عمل متقدمة","تغطية واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الشاملة","التخطيط والبحث العميق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["MCP 服务器开发","LLM 交互","外部服务集成","MCP 设计","API 覆盖","工作流工具","深入研究","规划","高级工作流"],"ja":["MCP サーバーの開発","LLM の接続","外部サービスの統合","MCP デザイン","API カバレッジ","ワークフロー ツール","深入的な研究","計画","高度なワークフロー"],"ko":["MCP 서버 개발","LLM 연동","외부 서비스 통합","MCP 설계","API 커버리지","워크플로우 툴","심도 있는 연구","계획","고급 워크플로우"],"es":["desarrollo de servidores MCP","LLM","servicios externos","herramientas de flujo de trabajo","diseño de API","interacción con servicios externos"],"fr":["développement de serveurs MCP","LLM","services externes","outils de flux de travail","conception d''API","interaction avec des services externes"],"de":["MCP-Server-Entwicklung","LLM","externe Dienste","Workflow-Tools","API-Design","Interaktion mit externen Diensten"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de servidor MCP","LLM","serviços externos","ferramentas de workflow","API","planejamento","pesquisa","otimização"],"ru":["разработка сервера MCP","LLM","внешние сервисы","инструменты workflow","API","планирование","исследование","оптимизация"],"ar":["تطوير خادم MCP","LLM","الخدمات الخارجية","أدوات سير عمل","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","التخطيط","البحث","تحسين الأداء"]}},"owner":"feed-mob","repo":"feedmob-adpilot-mcp","repoPath":"feed-mob/feedmob-adpilot-mcp","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.516Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mcp-builder","description":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK).","bodyPreview":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalan","body":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalance comprehensive API endpoint coverage with specialized workflow tools. Workflow tools can be more convenient for specific tasks, while comprehensive coverage gives agents flexibility to compose operations. Performance varies by client—some clients benefit from code execution that combines basic tools, while others work better with higher-level workflows. When uncertain, prioritize comprehensive API coverage.\n\n**Tool Naming and Discoverability:**\nClear, descriptive tool names help agents find the right tools quickly. Use consistent prefixes (e.g., `github_create_issue`, `github_list_repos`) and action-oriented naming.\n\n**Context Management:**\nAgents benefit from concise tool descriptions and the ability to filter/paginate results. Design tools that return focused, relevant data. Some clients support code execution which can help agents filter and process data efficiently.\n\n**Actionable Error Messages:**\nError messages should guide agents toward solutions with specific suggestions and next steps.\n\n#### 1.2 Study MCP Protocol Documentation\n\n**Navigate the MCP specification:**\n\nStart with the sitemap to find relevant pages: `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`\n\nThen fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix for markdown format (e.g., `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft.md`).\n\nKey pages to review:\n- Specification overview and architecture\n- Transport mechanisms (streamable HTTP, stdio)\n- Tool, resource, and prompt definitions\n\n#### 1.3 Study Framework Documentation\n\n**Recommended stack:**\n- **Language**: TypeScript (high-quality SDK support and good compatibility in many execution environments e.g. MCPB. Plus AI models are good at generating TypeScript code, benefiting from its broad usage, static typing and good linting tools)\n- **Transport**: Streamable HTTP for remote servers, using stateless JSON (simpler to scale and maintain, as opposed to stateful sessions and streaming responses). stdio for local servers.\n\n**Load framework documentation:**\n\n- **MCP Best Practices**: [📋 View Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Core guidelines\n\n**For TypeScript (recommended):**\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - TypeScript patterns and examples\n\n**For Python:**\n- **Python SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Python patterns and examples\n\n#### 1.4 Plan Your Implementation\n\n**Understand the API:**\nReview the service''s API documentation to identify key endpoints, authentication requirements, and data models. Use web search and WebFetch as needed.\n\n**Tool Selection:**\nPrioritize comprehensive API coverage. List endpoints to implement, starting with the most common operations.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Implementation\n\n#### 2.1 Set Up Project Structure\n\nSee language-specific guides for project setup:\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Project structure, package.json, tsconfig.json\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Module organization, dependencies\n\n#### 2.2 Implement Core Infrastructure\n\nCreate shared utilities:\n- API client with authentication\n- Error handling helpers\n- Response formatting (JSON/Markdown)\n- Pagination support\n\n#### 2.3 Implement Tools\n\nFor each tool:\n\n**Input Schema:**\n- Use Zod (TypeScript) or Pydantic (Python)\n- Include constraints and clear descriptions\n- Add examples in field descriptions\n\n**Output Schema:**\n- Define `outputSchema` where possible for structured data\n- Use `structuredContent` in tool responses (TypeScript SDK feature)\n- Helps clients understand and process tool outputs\n\n**Tool Description:**\n- Concise summary of functionality\n- Parameter descriptions\n- Return type schema\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Async/await for I/O operations\n- Proper error handling with actionable messages\n- Support pagination where applicable\n- Return both text content and structured data when using modern SDKs\n\n**Annotations:**\n- `readOnlyHint`: true/false\n- `destructiveHint`: true/false\n- `idempotentHint`: true/false\n- `openWorldHint`: true/false\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Review and Test\n\n#### 3.1 Code Quality\n\nReview for:\n- No duplicated code (DRY principle)\n- Consistent error handling\n- Full type coverage\n- Clear tool descriptions\n\n#### 3.2 Build and Test\n\n**TypeScript:**\n- Run `npm run build` to verify compilation\n- Test with MCP Inspector: `npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector`\n\n**Python:**\n- Verify syntax: `python -m py_compile your_server.py`\n- Test with MCP Inspector\n\nSee language-specific guides for detailed testing approaches and quality checklists.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Create Evaluations\n\nAfter implementing your MCP server, create comprehensive evaluations to test its effectiveness.\n\n**Load [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) for complete evaluation guidelines.**\n\n#### 4.1 Understand Evaluation Purpose\n\nUse evaluations to test whether LLMs can effectively use your MCP server to answer realistic, complex questions.\n\n#### 4.2 Create 10 Evaluation Questions\n\nTo create effective evaluations, follow the process outlined in the evaluation guide:\n\n1. **Tool Inspection**: List available tools and understand their capabilities\n2. **Content Exploration**: Use READ-ONLY operations to explore available data\n3. **Question Generation**: Create 10 complex, realistic questions\n4. **Answer Verification**: Solve each question yourself to verify answers\n\n#### 4.3 Evaluation Requirements\n\nEnsure each question is:\n- **Independent**: Not dependent on other questions\n- **Read-only**: Only non-destructive operations required\n- **Complex**: Requiring multiple tool calls and deep exploration\n- **Realistic**: Based on real use cases humans would care about\n- **Verifiable**: Single, clear answer that can be verified by string comparison\n- **Stable**: Answer won''t change over time\n\n#### 4.4 Output Format\n\nCreate an XML file with this structure:\n\n```xml\n<evaluation>\n  <qa_pair>\n    <question>Find discussions about AI model launches with animal codenames. One model needed a specific safety designation that uses the format ASL-X. What number X was being determined for the model named after a spotted wild cat?</question>\n    <answer>3</answer>\n  </qa_pair>\n<!-- More qa_pairs... -->\n</evaluation>\n```\n\n---\n\n# Reference Files\n\n## 📚 Documentation Library\n\nLoad these resources as needed during development:\n\n### Core MCP Documentation (Load First)\n- **MCP Protocol**: Start with sitemap at `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`, then fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix\n- [📋 MCP Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Universal MCP guidelines including:\n  - Server and tool naming conventions\n  - Response format guidelines (JSON vs Markdown)\n  - Pagination best practices\n  - Transport selection (streamable HTTP vs stdio)\n  - Security and error handling standards\n\n### SDK Documentation (Load During Phase 1/2)\n- **Python SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n\n### Language-Specific Implementation Guides (Load During Phase 2)\n- [🐍 Python Implementation Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Complete Python/FastMCP guide with:\n  - Server initialization patterns\n  - Pydantic model examples\n  - Tool registration with `@mcp.tool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n- [⚡ TypeScript Implementation Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Complete TypeScript guide with:\n  - Project structure\n  - Zod schema patterns\n  - Tool registration with `server.registerTool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n### Evaluation Guide (Load During Phase 4)\n- [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) - Complete evaluation creation guide with:\n  - Question creation guidelines\n  - Answer verification strategies\n  - XML format specifications\n  - Example questions and answers\n  - Running an evaluation with the provided scripts\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:03:45.770Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for LLM Agents needing to interact with external services through Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers.","zh":"非常适合需要通过模型上下文协议（MCP）服务器与外部服务交互的LLM代理。","ja":"モデルコンテキストプロトコル（MCP）サーバーを介して外部サービスと交互作用する必要があるLLMエージェントに最適です。","ko":"외부 서비스와 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜(MCP) 서버를 통해 상호 작용할 필요가 있는 LLM 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes LLM que necesitan interactuar con servicios externos a través de servidores de Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo (MCP).","fr":"Parfait pour les agents LLM ayant besoin d''interagir avec des services externes via des serveurs de Protocole de Contexte de Modèle (MCP).","de":"Perfekt für LLM-Agents, die mit externen Diensten über Model Context Protocol (MCP)-Server interagieren müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes LLM que precisam interagir com serviços externos por meio de servidores do Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo (MCP).","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов LLM, которым необходимо взаимодействовать с внешними сервисами через серверы Протокола контекста модели (MCP).","ar":"مثالي لعميل LLM الذين يحتاجون إلى التفاعل مع الخدمات الخارجية من خلال خادم بروتوكول سياق النموذج (MCP)."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create high-quality MCP servers that enable seamless interaction with external services, leveraging well-designed tools and APIs for workflow automation and API coverage.","zh":"赋予代理创建高质量的MCP服务器的能力，使其能够与外部服务进行无缝交互，利用设计良好的工具和API实现工作流自动化和API覆盖。","ja":"エージェントに、高品質のMCPサーバーを作成する能力を与え、外部サービスとの無頓着なやり取りを可能にし、ワークフローの自動化とAPIカバレッジのための設計の優れたツールとAPIを利用できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 높은 품질의 MCP 서버를 생성하여 외부 서비스와의 무61334 상호 작용을 가능하게 하며, 워크플로 자동화 및 API 커버리지에 대한 잘設計된 도구 및 API를 활용할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear servidores MCP de alta calidad que permiten una interacción sin problemas con servicios externos, aprovechando herramientas y API bien diseñadas para la automatización de flujos de trabajo y la cobertura de API.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des serveurs MCP de haute qualité qui permettent une interaction transparente avec des services externes, en exploitant des outils et des API bien conçus pour l''automatisation des flux de travail et la couverture d''API.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, hochwertige MCP-Server zu erstellen, die eine nahtlose Interaktion mit externen Diensten ermöglichen, indem sie gut konzipierte Tools und APIs für die Workflow-Automatisierung und API-Abdeckung nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar servidores MCP de alta qualidade que permitem interação sem problemas com serviços externos, aproveitando ferramentas e APIs bem projetadas para automação de fluxo de trabalho e cobertura de API.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать высококачественные серверы MCP, которые обеспечивают беспрепятственное взаимодействие с внешними сервисами, используя хорошо спроектированные инструменты и API для автоматизации рабочего процесса и покрытия API.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية إنشاء خوادم MCP ذات جودة عالية تتيح التفاعل السلس مع الخدمات الخارجية، مستفيدة من أدوات وواجهات برمجة التطبيقات المصممة جيدًا للautomação وتغطية واجهة برمجة التطبيقات."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing MCP servers for real-world task automation","Developing workflow tools for LLMs to interact with external services","Implementing API coverage for MCP servers"],"zh":["为现实世界任务自动化设计MCP服务器","为LLM与外部服务交互开发工作流工具","为MCP服务器实现API覆盖"],"ja":["実世界のタスク自動化のためのMCPサーバーの設計","LLMが外部サービスとやり取りするためのワークフローツールの開発","MCPサーバーのAPIカバレッジの実装"],"ko":["실제 세계 작업 자동화를 위한 MCP 서버 설계","LLM이 외부 서비스와 상호 작용하기 위한 워크플로우 도구 개발","MCP 서버의 API 커버리지 구현"],"es":["Diseñar servidores MCP para la automatización de tareas del mundo real","Desarrollar herramientas de flujo de trabajo para que los LLM interactúen con servicios externos","Implementar la cobertura de API para servidores MCP"],"fr":["Concevoir des serveurs MCP pour l''automatisation de tâches du monde réel","Développer des outils de flux de travail pour que les LLM interagissent avec des services externes","Mettre en œuvre la couverture d''API pour les serveurs MCP"],"de":["MCP-Server für die Automatisierung von realen Aufgaben entwerfen","Workflow-Tools für die Interaktion von LLM mit externen Diensten entwickeln","API-Abdeckung für MCP-Server implementieren"],"pt":["Projetar servidores MCP para automação de tarefas do mundo real","Desenvolver ferramentas de fluxo de trabalho para LLMs interagirem com serviços externos","Implementar cobertura de API para servidores MCP"],"ru":["Проектирование серверов MCP для автоматизации реальных задач","Разработка инструментов рабочего процесса для взаимодействия LLM с внешними сервисами","Реализация покрытия API для серверов MCP"],"ar":["تصميم خوادم MCP لأتمتة المهام الواقعية","تطوير أدوات سير العمل للوكلاء LLM للتفاعل مع الخدمات الخارجية","تنفيذ تغطية واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لخوادم MCP"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires deep research and planning for effective MCP server development","Dependent on the quality of MCP server design for successful LLM interaction"],"zh":["需要深入研究和规划以有效地开发MCP服务器","依赖于MCP服务器设计的质量以实现LLM的成功交互"],"ja":["効果的なMCPサーバーの開発には深い研究と計画が必要","LLMの成功したやり取りにはMCPサーバーの設計の品質に依存"],"ko":["효과적인 MCP 서버 개발을 위해서는 깊은 연구와 계획이 필요","LLM의 성공적인 상호 작용을 위해서는 MCP 서버 디자인의 품질에 의존"],"es":["Requiere una investigación y planificación profundas para un desarrollo eficaz de servidores MCP","Depende de la calidad del diseño del servidor MCP para una interacción LLM exitosa"],"fr":["Nécessite une recherche et une planification approfondies pour un développement efficace de serveurs MCP","Dépend de la qualité de la conception du serveur MCP pour une interaction LLM réussie"],"de":["Benötigt tiefe Forschung und Planung für eine effektive MCP-Server-Entwicklung","Hängt von der Qualität des MCP-Server-Designs für eine erfolgreiche LLM-Interaktion ab"],"pt":["Exige pesquisas profundas e planejamento para desenvolvimento eficaz de servidores MCP","Depende da qualidade do design do servidor MCP para interação bem-sucedida do LLM"],"ru":["Требует глубоких исследований и планирования для эффективного развития серверов MCP","Зависит от качества конструкции сервера MCP для успешного взаимодействия LLM"],"ar":["يتطلب بحوثًا عميقة وتخطيطًا لتنمية خوادم MCP فعالة","يعتمد على جودة تصميم خادم MCP للتفاعل الناجح للعميل LLM"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
