e alto nível","Suporte ao desenvolvimento de LLMs"],"ru":["Разработка серверов MCP высокого качества","Эффективное взаимодействие с внешними сервисами","Современные инструменты дизайна","Глубокое планирование и исследование","Высокий уровень рабочего процесса","Поддержка разработки LLM"],"ar":["تطوير خواديم MCP ذات جودة عالية","التفاعل الفعال مع الخدمات الخارجية","أدوات تصميم حديثة","التخطيط والبحث المتعمقين","مستوى رفيع من سير العمل","دعم تطوير LLMs"]},"keywords":{"zh":["MCP Builder","AI开发支持系统","MCP服务器开发","LLM交互","外部服务集成","开发工具","workflow","API设计"],"ja":["MCP Builder","AI開発サポートシステム","MCPサーバー開発","LLM交互","外部サービス統合","開発ツール","ワークフロー","API設計"],"ko":["MCP Builder","인공지능 개발 지원 시스템","MCP 서버 개발","LLM 상호 작용","외부 서비스 통합","개발 도구","워크플로우","API 설계"],"es":["desarrollo de servidor MCP","LLM","servicios externos","herramientas de diseño","API de cobertura","flujo de trabajo","planificación","investigación"],"fr":["développement de serveur MCP","LLM","services externes","outils de conception","API de couverture","flux de travail","planification","recherche"],"de":["MCP-Server-Entwicklung","LLM","externe Dienste","Design-Tools","API-Abdeckung","Workflow","Planung","Recherche"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de servidores MCP","MCP Builder","LLMs","serviços externos","ferramentas de design","planejamento e pesquisa","fluxo de trabalho de alto nível","suporte ao desenvolvimento de LLMs","qualidade de servidores MCP"],"ru":["разработка серверов MCP","MCP Builder","LLM","внешние сервисы","инструменты дизайна","планирование и исследование","высокий уровень рабочего процесса","поддержка разработки LLM","качество серверов MCP"],"ar":["تطوير خواديم MCP","MCP Builder","LLMs","الخدمات الخارجية","أدوات التصميم","التخطيط والبحث","مستوى رفيع من سير العمل","دعم تطوير LLMs","جودة خواديم MCP"]}},"owner":"rongma1sheng","repo":"kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","repoPath":"rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.516Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mcp-builder","description":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK).","bodyPreview":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalan","body":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalance comprehensive API endpoint coverage with specialized workflow tools. Workflow tools can be more convenient for specific tasks, while comprehensive coverage gives agents flexibility to compose operations. Performance varies by client—some clients benefit from code execution that combines basic tools, while others work better with higher-level workflows. When uncertain, prioritize comprehensive API coverage.\n\n**Tool Naming and Discoverability:**\nClear, descriptive tool names help agents find the right tools quickly. Use consistent prefixes (e.g., `github_create_issue`, `github_list_repos`) and action-oriented naming.\n\n**Context Management:**\nAgents benefit from concise tool descriptions and the ability to filter/paginate results. Design tools that return focused, relevant data. Some clients support code execution which can help agents filter and process data efficiently.\n\n**Actionable Error Messages:**\nError messages should guide agents toward solutions with specific suggestions and next steps.\n\n#### 1.2 Study MCP Protocol Documentation\n\n**Navigate the MCP specification:**\n\nStart with the sitemap to find relevant pages: `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`\n\nThen fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix for markdown format (e.g., `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft.md`).\n\nKey pages to review:\n- Specification overview and architecture\n- Transport mechanisms (streamable HTTP, stdio)\n- Tool, resource, and prompt definitions\n\n#### 1.3 Study Framework Documentation\n\n**Recommended stack:**\n- **Language**: TypeScript (high-quality SDK support and good compatibility in many execution environments e.g. MCPB. Plus AI models are good at generating TypeScript code, benefiting from its broad usage, static typing and good linting tools)\n- **Transport**: Streamable HTTP for remote servers, using stateless JSON (simpler to scale and maintain, as opposed to stateful sessions and streaming responses). stdio for local servers.\n\n**Load framework documentation:**\n\n- **MCP Best Practices**: [📋 View Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Core guidelines\n\n**For TypeScript (recommended):**\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - TypeScript patterns and examples\n\n**For Python:**\n- **Python SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Python patterns and examples\n\n#### 1.4 Plan Your Implementation\n\n**Understand the API:**\nReview the service''s API documentation to identify key endpoints, authentication requirements, and data models. Use web search and WebFetch as needed.\n\n**Tool Selection:**\nPrioritize comprehensive API coverage. List endpoints to implement, starting with the most common operations.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Implementation\n\n#### 2.1 Set Up Project Structure\n\nSee language-specific guides for project setup:\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Project structure, package.json, tsconfig.json\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Module organization, dependencies\n\n#### 2.2 Implement Core Infrastructure\n\nCreate shared utilities:\n- API client with authentication\n- Error handling helpers\n- Response formatting (JSON/Markdown)\n- Pagination support\n\n#### 2.3 Implement Tools\n\nFor each tool:\n\n**Input Schema:**\n- Use Zod (TypeScript) or Pydantic (Python)\n- Include constraints and clear descriptions\n- Add examples in field descriptions\n\n**Output Schema:**\n- Define `outputSchema` where possible for structured data\n- Use `structuredContent` in tool responses (TypeScript SDK feature)\n- Helps clients understand and process tool outputs\n\n**Tool Description:**\n- Concise summary of functionality\n- Parameter descriptions\n- Return type schema\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Async/await for I/O operations\n- Proper error handling with actionable messages\n- Support pagination where applicable\n- Return both text content and structured data when using modern SDKs\n\n**Annotations:**\n- `readOnlyHint`: true/false\n- `destructiveHint`: true/false\n- `idempotentHint`: true/false\n- `openWorldHint`: true/false\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Review and Test\n\n#### 3.1 Code Quality\n\nReview for:\n- No duplicated code (DRY principle)\n- Consistent error handling\n- Full type coverage\n- Clear tool descriptions\n\n#### 3.2 Build and Test\n\n**TypeScript:**\n- Run `npm run build` to verify compilation\n- Test with MCP Inspector: `npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector`\n\n**Python:**\n- Verify syntax: `python -m py_compile your_server.py`\n- Test with MCP Inspector\n\nSee language-specific guides for detailed testing approaches and quality checklists.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Create Evaluations\n\nAfter implementing your MCP server, create comprehensive evaluations to test its effectiveness.\n\n**Load [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) for complete evaluation guidelines.**\n\n#### 4.1 Understand Evaluation Purpose\n\nUse evaluations to test whether LLMs can effectively use your MCP server to answer realistic, complex questions.\n\n#### 4.2 Create 10 Evaluation Questions\n\nTo create effective evaluations, follow the process outlined in the evaluation guide:\n\n1. **Tool Inspection**: List available tools and understand their capabilities\n2. **Content Exploration**: Use READ-ONLY operations to explore available data\n3. **Question Generation**: Create 10 complex, realistic questions\n4. **Answer Verification**: Solve each question yourself to verify answers\n\n#### 4.3 Evaluation Requirements\n\nEnsure each question is:\n- **Independent**: Not dependent on other questions\n- **Read-only**: Only non-destructive operations required\n- **Complex**: Requiring multiple tool calls and deep exploration\n- **Realistic**: Based on real use cases humans would care about\n- **Verifiable**: Single, clear answer that can be verified by string comparison\n- **Stable**: Answer won''t change over time\n\n#### 4.4 Output Format\n\nCreate an XML file with this structure:\n\n```xml\n<evaluation>\n  <qa_pair>\n    <question>Find discussions about AI model launches with animal codenames. One model needed a specific safety designation that uses the format ASL-X. What number X was being determined for the model named after a spotted wild cat?</question>\n    <answer>3</answer>\n  </qa_pair>\n<!-- More qa_pairs... -->\n</evaluation>\n```\n\n---\n\n# Reference Files\n\n## 📚 Documentation Library\n\nLoad these resources as needed during development:\n\n### Core MCP Documentation (Load First)\n- **MCP Protocol**: Start with sitemap at `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`, then fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix\n- [📋 MCP Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Universal MCP guidelines including:\n  - Server and tool naming conventions\n  - Response format guidelines (JSON vs Markdown)\n  - Pagination best practices\n  - Transport selection (streamable HTTP vs stdio)\n  - Security and error handling standards\n\n### SDK Documentation (Load During Phase 1/2)\n- **Python SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n\n### Language-Specific Implementation Guides (Load During Phase 2)\n- [🐍 Python Implementation Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Complete Python/FastMCP guide with:\n  - Server initialization patterns\n  - Pydantic model examples\n  - Tool registration with `@mcp.tool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n- [⚡ TypeScript Implementation Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Complete TypeScript guide with:\n  - Project structure\n  - Zod schema patterns\n  - Tool registration with `server.registerTool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n### Evaluation Guide (Load During Phase 4)\n- [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) - Complete evaluation creation guide with:\n  - Question creation guidelines\n  - Answer verification strategies\n  - XML format specifications\n  - Example questions and answers\n  - Running an evaluation with the provided scripts\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:03:43.803Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing to interact with external services through Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers.","zh":"非常适合需要通过模型上下文协议（MCP）服务器与外部服务交互的AI代理。","ja":"モデルコンテキストプロトコル（MCP）サーバーを介して外部サービスと交互作用する必要があるAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"외부 서비스와 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜(MCP) 서버를 통해 상호 작용하는 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan interactuar con servicios externos a través de servidores de Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo (MCP).","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui ont besoin d''interagir avec des services externes via des serveurs de protocole de contexte de modèle (MCP).","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die mit externen Diensten über Model Context Protocol (MCP)-Server interagieren müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam interagir com serviços externos por meio de servidores do Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo (MCP).","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, которым необходимо взаимодействовать с внешними сервисами через серверы Протокола контекста модели (MCP).","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى التفاعل مع الخدمات الخارجية من خلال خوادم بروتوكول سياق النموذج (MCP)."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create high-quality MCP servers that enable Large Language Models (LLMs) to accomplish real-world tasks through well-designed tools and APIs, leveraging the Model Context Protocol for seamless interaction.","zh":"赋予代理创建高质量的MCP服务器的能力，使大型语言模型（LLM）能够通过精心设计的工具和API执行实际任务，利用模型上下文协议实现无缝交互。","ja":"エージェントが、高品質のMCPサーバーを作成できるようにし、大規模言語モデル（LLM）が、よく設計されたツールやAPIを利用して、実世界のタスクを実行できるようにし、モデルコンテキストプロトコルを使用して無断交互作用を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 높은 품질의 MCP 서버를 생성할 수 있도록 하여, 대규모 언어 모델(LLM)이 잘设计된 도구와 API를 활용하여 실제 작업을 수행할 수 있게 하며, 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜을 사용하여 무결한 상호 작용을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear servidores MCP de alta calidad que permiten a los Grandes Modelos de Lenguaje (LLMs) realizar tareas del mundo real a través de herramientas y API bien diseñadas, aprovechando el Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo para una interacción sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des serveurs MCP de haute qualité qui permettent aux grands modèles de langage (LLM) d''accomplir des tâches du monde réel grâce à des outils et des API bien conçus, en exploitant le protocole de contexte de modèle pour une interaction sans accroc.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, hochwertige MCP-Server zu erstellen, die es Großen Sprachmodellen (LLMs) ermöglichen, reale Aufgaben durch gut gestaltete Tools und APIs zu erledigen, indem sie das Model Context Protocol für eine nahtlose Interaktion nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar servidores MCP de alta qualidade que permitem que os Grandes Modelos de Linguagem (LLMs) realizem tarefas do mundo real por meio de ferramentas e APIs bem projetadas, aproveitando o Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo para interação sem problemas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать высококачественные серверы MCP, которые позволяют большим языковым моделям (LLM) выполнять реальные задачи с помощью хорошо спроектированных инструментов и API, используя Протокол контекста модели для беспрепятственного взаимодействия.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء خوادم MCP عالية الجودة تمكن نماذج اللغة الكبيرة (LLM) من إنجاز مهام العالم الحقيقي من خلال أدوات وواجهات برمجة التطبيقات المصممة جيدًا، واستخدام بروتوكول سياق النموذج للتفاعل دون مشاكل."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing MCP servers for LLMs to interact with external services","Developing workflow tools for MCP servers","Creating high-quality MCP servers for real-world task automation"],"zh":["为LLM设计MCP服务器以与外部服务交互","为MCP服务器开发工作流工具","为实际任务自动化创建高质量的MCP服务器"],"ja":["LLMが外部サービスと交互作用するためのMCPサーバーの設計","MCPサーバーのワークフロー ツールの開発","実世界のタスク自動化のための高品質なMCPサーバーの作成"],"ko":["외부 서비스와 상호 작용하는 LLM을 위한 MCP 서버 설계","MCP 서버를 위한 워크플로우 도구 개발","실제 작업 자동화를 위한 높은 품질의 MCP 서버 생성"],"es":["Diseñar servidores MCP para que los LLM interactúen con servicios externos","Desarrollar herramientas de flujo de trabajo para servidores MCP","Crear servidores MCP de alta calidad para la automatización de tareas del mundo real"],"fr":["Concevoir des serveurs MCP pour que les LLM interagissent avec des services externes","Développer des outils de workflow pour les serveurs MCP","Créer des serveurs MCP de haute qualité pour l''automatisation de tâches du monde réel"],"de":["MCP-Server für die Interaktion von LLM mit externen Diensten entwerfen","Workflow-Tools für MCP-Server entwickeln","Erstellung von hochwertigen MCP-Servern für die Automatisierung von realen Aufgaben"],"pt":["Projetar servidores MCP para LLMs interagirem com serviços externos","Desenvolver ferramentas de fluxo de trabalho para servidores MCP","Criar servidores MCP de alta qualidade para automação de tarefas do mundo real"],"ru":["Проектирование серверов MCP для взаимодействия LLM с внешними сервисами","Разработка инструментов рабочего процесса для серверов MCP","Создание высококачественных серверов MCP для автоматизации реальных задач"],"ar":["تصميم خوادم MCP لتفاعل نماذج اللغة الكبيرة مع الخدمات الخارجية"," تطوير أدوات سير العمل لخوادم MCP","إنشاء خوادم MCP عالية الجودة لأتمتة مهام العالم الحقيقي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of MCP design and development","Limited to LLMs that support Model Context Protocol"],"zh":["需要了解MCP设计和开发","仅限于支持模型上下文协议的LLM"],"ja":["MCP設計および開発の理解が必要","モデルコンテキストプロトコルをサポートするLLMのみ"],"ko":["MCP 설계 및 개발에 대한 이해가 필요","모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜을 지원하는 LLM만 해당"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del diseño y desarrollo de MCP","Limitado a LLM que admiten el Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la conception et du développement de MCP","Limité aux LLM qui prennent en charge le protocole de contexte de modèle"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für MCP-Design und -Entwicklung","Begrenzt auf LLM, die das Model Context Protocol unterstützen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do design e desenvolvimento de MCP","Limitado a LLMs que suportam o Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo"],"ru":["Требует понимания проектирования и разработки MCP","Ограничен для LLM, которые поддерживают Протокол контекста модели"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم التصميم وتطوير بروتوكول سياق النموذج","محدود بنماذج اللغة الكبيرة التي تدعم 