èmes","Approche théorique pour la construction de systèmes distribués fiables","Applications dans les systèmes de bases de données et les réseaux d''ordinateurs"],"de":["Logische Uhren für die Koordination von verteilten Systemen","Paxos-Konsens für die verteilte Entscheidungsfindung","Formale Spezifikation mit TLA+ für die Überprüfung von Systemen","Theoretischer Ansatz für den Bau von zuverlässigen verteilten Systemen","Anwendungen in Datenbank- und Computernetzwerken"],"pt":["Relógios lógicos","Consenso (Paxos)","Especificação formal (TLA+)","Sistemas distribuídos escaláveis","Tolerância a falhas","Desempenho otimizado"],"ru":["Логические часы","Консенсус (Paxos)","Формальная спецификация (TLA+)","Масштабируемые распределенные системы","Толерантность к сбоям","Оптимизированное производительность"],"ar":["الساعات المنطقية","الإجماع (Paxos)","التحديد الشكلي (TLA+)","النظم الموزعة القابلة للتحجيم","التحمل للعطل","الأداء المحسن"]},"keywords":{"zh":["分布式系统","Lamport","逻辑时钟","共识算法","正式规范","可靠性","容错性","分散システム"],"ja":["分散システム","Lamport","論理時計","コンセンサスアルゴリズム","正式な仕様","信頼性","故障耐性","分散システム理論"],"ko":["분산 시스템","Lamport","논리 시계","합의 알고리즘","공식 사양","신뢰성","고장 허용","분산 시스템 이론"],"es":["sistemas distribuidos","relojes lógicos","consenso de Paxos","especificación formal","TLA+","Leslie Lamport","sistemas de bases de datos","redes de computadoras"],"fr":["systèmes distribués","horloges logiques","consensus de Paxos","spécification formelle","TLA+","Leslie Lamport","systèmes de bases de données","réseaux d''ordinateurs"],"de":["verteilte Systeme","logische Uhren","Paxos-Konsens","formale Spezifikation","TLA+","Leslie Lamport","Datenbank-Systeme","Computernetzwerke"],"pt":["sistemas distribuídos","leslie lamport","relógios lógicos","consenso","especificação formal","tlap","paxos","engenharia de software"],"ru":["распределенные системы","лесли лампорт","логические часы","консенсус","формальная спецификация","tlap","paxos","программная инженерия"],"ar":["أنظمة موزعة","ليزلي لامبورت","الساعات المنطقية","الإجماع","التحديد الشكلي","tlap","paxos","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.517Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"lamport-distributed-systems","description":"Design distributed systems using Leslie Lamports rigorous approach. Emphasizes formal reasoning, logical time, consensus protocols, and state machine replication. Use when building systems where correctness under concurrency and partial failure is critical.","bodyPreview":"# Leslie Lamport Style Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nLeslie Lamport transformed distributed systems from ad-hoc engineering into a rigorous science. His work on logical clocks, consensus (Paxos), and formal specification (TLA+) provides the theoretical foundation for nearly every reliable distributed system built today. Turing Award winner (2013).\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n> \"A distributed system is one in which the failure of a computer you didn''t even know existed can render your own computer unusable.\"\n\n> \"","body":"# Leslie Lamport Style Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nLeslie Lamport transformed distributed systems from ad-hoc engineering into a rigorous science. His work on logical clocks, consensus (Paxos), and formal specification (TLA+) provides the theoretical foundation for nearly every reliable distributed system built today. Turing Award winner (2013).\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n> \"A distributed system is one in which the failure of a computer you didn''t even know existed can render your own computer unusable.\"\n\n> \"If you''re thinking without writing, you only think you''re thinking.\"\n\n> \"The way to be a good programmer is to write programs, not to learn languages.\"\n\n## Design Principles\n\n1. **Formal Specification First**: Write a precise specification before writing code. If you can''t specify it precisely, you don''t understand it.\n\n2. **Time is Relative**: There is no global clock in a distributed system. Use logical time (happens-before) to reason about ordering.\n\n3. **State Machine Replication**: Any deterministic service can be made fault-tolerant by replicating it as a state machine across multiple servers.\n\n4. **Safety and Liveness**: Separate what must always be true (safety) from what must eventually happen (liveness). Prove both.\n\n5. **Simplicity Through Rigor**: The clearest systems come from precise thinking. Formalism isn''t overhead—it''s the path to simplicity.\n\n## When Designing Systems\n\n### Always\n\n- Write a specification before implementation (TLA+, Alloy, or precise prose)\n- Define the safety properties: what bad things must never happen\n- Define the liveness properties: what good things must eventually happen\n- Reason about all possible interleavings of concurrent operations\n- Use logical timestamps when physical time isn''t reliable\n- Make system state explicit and transitions clear\n- Document invariants that must hold across all states\n\n### Never\n\n- Assume messages arrive in order (unless you''ve proven it)\n- Assume clocks are synchronized (they''re not)\n- Assume failures are independent (they''re often correlated)\n- Hand-wave about \"eventually\" without defining what guarantees that\n- Trust intuition for concurrent systems—prove it or test it exhaustively\n- Confuse the specification with the implementation\n\n### Prefer\n\n- State machines over ad-hoc event handling\n- Logical clocks over physical timestamps for ordering\n- Consensus protocols over optimistic concurrency for critical state\n- Explicit failure handling over implicit assumptions\n- Proved algorithms over clever heuristics\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### Logical Clocks (Lamport Timestamps)\n\n```\nEach process maintains a counter C:\n1. Before any event, increment C\n2. When sending a message, include C\n3. When receiving a message with timestamp T, set C = max(C, T) + 1\n\nThis gives a partial ordering: if a → b, then C(a) < C(b)\n(But C(a) < C(b) does NOT imply a → b)\n```\n\n### The Happens-Before Relation (→)\n\n```\na → b (a happens before b) if:\n1. a and b are in the same process and a comes before b, OR\n2. a is a send and b is the corresponding receive, OR\n3. There exists c such that a → c and c → b (transitivity)\n\nIf neither a → b nor b → a, events are CONCURRENT.\n```\n\n### State Machine Replication\n\n```\nTo replicate a service:\n1. Model the service as a deterministic state machine\n2. Replicate the state machine across N servers\n3. Use consensus (Paxos/Raft) to agree on the sequence of inputs\n4. Each replica applies inputs in the same order → same state\n\nTolerates F failures with 2F+1 replicas.\n```\n\n### Paxos (Simplified)\n\n```\nThree roles: Proposers, Acceptors, Learners\n\nPhase 1 (Prepare):\n  Proposer sends PREPARE(n) to acceptors\n  Acceptor responds with highest-numbered proposal it accepted (if any)\n  \nPhase 2 (Accept):\n  If proposer receives majority responses:\n    Send ACCEPT(n, v) where v is highest-numbered value seen (or new value)\n  Acceptor accepts if it hasn''t promised to a higher proposal\n\nConsensus reached when majority accept the same (n, v).\n```\n\n## Mental Model\n\nLamport approaches distributed systems as a mathematician:\n\n1. **Define the problem precisely**: What are the inputs, outputs, and allowed behaviors?\n2. **Identify the invariants**: What must always be true?\n3. **Consider all interleavings**: What happens if events occur in any order?\n4. **Prove correctness**: Show that safety and liveness hold.\n5. **Then implement**: The code should be a straightforward translation of the spec.\n\n### The TLA+ Approach\n\n```\n1. Define the state space (all possible states)\n2. Define the initial state predicate\n3. Define the next-state relation (allowed transitions)\n4. Specify safety as invariants (always true)\n5. Specify liveness as temporal properties (eventually true)\n6. Model-check or prove that the spec satisfies properties\n```\n\n## Code Patterns\n\n### Implementing Logical Clocks\n\n```python\nclass LamportClock:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._time = 0\n    \n    def tick(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Increment before local event.\"\"\"\n        self._time += 1\n        return self._time\n    \n    def send_timestamp(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Get timestamp for outgoing message.\"\"\"\n        self._time += 1\n        return self._time\n    \n    def receive(self, msg_timestamp: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Update clock on message receipt.\"\"\"\n        self._time = max(self._time, msg_timestamp) + 1\n        return self._time\n```\n\n### Vector Clocks (for Causality Detection)\n\n```python\nclass VectorClock:\n    def __init__(self, node_id: str, num_nodes: int):\n        self._id = node_id\n        self._clock = {f\"node_{i}\": 0 for i in range(num_nodes)}\n    \n    def tick(self):\n        self._clock[self._id] += 1\n    \n    def send(self) -> dict:\n        self.tick()\n        return self._clock.copy()\n    \n    def receive(self, other: dict):\n        for node, time in other.items():\n            self._clock[node] = max(self._clock.get(node, 0), time)\n        self.tick()\n    \n    def happens_before(self, other: dict) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if self → other.\"\"\"\n        return all(self._clock[k] <= other.get(k, 0) for k in self._clock) \\\n           and any(self._clock[k] < other.get(k, 0) for k in self._clock)\n```\n\n## Warning Signs\n\nYou''re violating Lamport''s principles if:\n\n- You assume \"this will never happen in practice\" without proof\n- Your distributed algorithm works \"most of the time\"\n- You can''t write down the invariants your system maintains\n- You''re using wall-clock time for ordering in a distributed system\n- You haven''t considered what happens during network partitions\n- Your system has no formal specification\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- For detailed philosophy, see [philosophy.md](philosophy.md)\n- For references (papers, talks), see [references.md](references.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:11:24.821Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Distributed System Agents needing rigorous consensus protocols and logical clock synchronization.","zh":"适用于需要严格共识协议和逻辑时钟同步的分布式系统代理。","ja":"厳密なコンセンサスプロトコルと論理時計同期が必要な分散システムエージェントに適しています。","ko":"严格한 합의 프로토콜 및 논리적 시계 동기화가 필요한 분산 시스템 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de sistemas distribuidos que necesitan protocolos de consenso rigurosos y sincronización de reloj lógico.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de systèmes distribués nécessitant des protocoles de consensus rigoureux et une synchronisation d''horloge logique.","de":"Perfekt für verteilte Systemagenten, die strenge Konsensprotokolle und eine logische Uhrsynchronisierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuídos que necessitam de protocolos de consenso rigorosos e sincronização de relógios lógicos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов распределенных систем, требующих строгих протоколов консенсуса и логической синхронизации часов.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل النظام الموزع التي تحتاج إلى بروتوكولات إجماع صارمة وتزامن ساعة منطقية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design and implement reliable distributed systems using Paxos consensus and TLA+ formal specification, ensuring robust fault tolerance and consistency across nodes.","zh":"赋予代理设计和实现可靠的分布式系统的能力，使用Paxos共识和TLA+形式规范，确保节点之间的强健容错和一致性。","ja":"PaxosコンセンサスとTLA+形式仕様を使用して、エージェントが信頼性の高い分散システムを設計して実装できるようにし、ノード間の堅牢な障害耐性と一貫性を保証します。","ko":"Paxos 합의 및 TLA+ 형식 사양을 사용하여 에이전트가 신뢰할 수 있는 분산 시스템을 설계하고 구현할 수 있도록 하여 노드 간의 강력한 장애 내성 및 일관성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar e implementar sistemas distribuidos confiables utilizando el consenso de Paxos y la especificación formal TLA+, garantizando una tolerancia a fallos robusta y coherencia en todos los nodos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir et de mettre en œuvre des systèmes distribués fiables en utilisant le consensus de Paxos et la spécification formelle TLA+, garantissant une tolérance aux pannes robuste et une cohérence sur tous les nœuds.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, zuverlässige verteilte Systeme mithilfe des Paxos-Konsens und der formalen Spezifikation TLA+ zu entwerfen und zu implementieren, wodurch eine robuste Fehlertoleranz und Konsistenz über alle Knoten hinweg gewährleistet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar e implementar sistemas distribuídos confiáveis usando o consenso Paxos e a especificação formal TLA+, garantindo robustez, tolerância a falhas e consistência em todos os nós.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать и реализовывать надежные распределенные системы, используя консенсус Paxos и формальную спецификацию TLA+, обеспечивая прочную устойчивость к отказам и согласованность во всех узлах.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تصميم وتنفيذ أنظمة موزعة موثوقة باستخدام إجماع باكسوس والمواصفة الرسمية TLA+، مما يضمن المتانة وتحمل الأعطال والاتساق عبر جميع العقد."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing Paxos consensus for distributed database replication","Designing fault-tolerant systems using logical clocks and TLA+","Analyzing distributed system failures using Leslie Lamport''s principles"],"zh":["为分布式数据库复制实现Paxos共识","使用逻辑时钟和TLA+设计容错系统","使用Leslie Lamport的原理分析分布式系统故障"],"ja":["分散データベース複製のためにPaxosコンセンサスを実装する","論理時計とTLA+を使用して障害耐性システムを設計する","Leslie Lamportの原理を使用して分散システムの障害を分析する"],"ko":["분산 데이터베이스 복제를 위한 Paxos 합의 구현","논리적 시계 및 TLA+를 사용한 장애 내성 시스템 설계","Leslie Lamport의 원리를 사용한 분산 시스템 장애 분석"],"es":["Implementación del consenso de Paxos para la replicación de bases de datos distribuidas","Diseño de sistemas tolerantes a fallos utilizando relojes lógicos y TLA+","Análisis de fallos de sistemas distribuidos utilizando los principios de Leslie Lamport"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre du consensus de Paxos pour la réplication de bases de données distribuées","Conception de systèmes tolérants aux pannes en utilisant des horloges logiques et TLA+","Analyse des défail