iguration simple sans clés API"],"de":["Automatisierung von Canva-Designoperationen","Integration mit Rube MCP","Aktive Verbindung zu Canva","Verwendung der Composio-Tool","Einfache Konfiguration ohne API-Schlüssel"],"pt":["Automação de operações de design do Canva","Integração com Rube MCP","Ferramentas personalizadas para melhorar a produtividade","Suporte à criação de ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Compatibilidade com diferentes ambientes de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Автоматизация операций дизайна Canva","Интеграция с Rube MCP","Индивидуальные инструменты для повышения производительности","Поддержка создания инструментов разработки","Совместимость с разными средами разработки"],"ar":["أتمتة العمليات التلقائية لتصميم كانفا","التكامل مع ربي ام سي بي","أدوات مخصصة لتحسين الإنتاجية","دعم إنشاء أدوات التطوير","التوافق مع بيئات التطوير المختلفة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Canva 自动化","Rube MCP","Composio","设计操作自动化","开发效率","自动化工具","Canva 工具包","MCP 服务器"],"ja":["Canva 自動化","Rube MCP","Composio","デザイン操作自動化","開発効率","自動化ツール","Canva 工具包","MCP サーバー"],"ko":["Canva 자동화","Rube MCP","Composio","디자인 작업 자동화","개발 효율성","자동화 도구","Canva 툴킷","MCP 서버"],"es":["automatización de Canva","desarrollo de software","herramientas de diseño","Rube MCP","Composio","integración de Canva","automatización de diseño"],"fr":["automatisation de Canva","développement de logiciels","outils de conception","Rube MCP","Composio","intégration de Canva","automatisation de conception"],"de":["Canva-Automatisierung","Software-Entwicklung","Design-Tools","Rube MCP","Composio","Canva-Integration","Automatisierung von Design"],"pt":["automação canva","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Rube MCP","Composio","produtividade","desenvolvimento de software","design de interface","ferramentas de design"],"ru":["автоматизация Canva","инструменты разработки","Rube MCP","Composio","производительность","разработка программного обеспечения","дизайн интерфейса","инструменты дизайна"],"ar":["أتمتة كانفا","أدوات التطوير","ربي ام سي بي","كومبوسيو","الإنتاجية","تطوير البرمجيات","تصميم الواجهة","أدوات التصميم"]}},"owner":"SamarthaKV29","repo":"antigravity-god-mode","repoPath":"SamarthaKV29/antigravity-god-mode","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.517Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"canva-automation","description":"Automate Canva tasks via Rube MCP (Composio): designs, exports, folders, brand templates, autofill. Always search tools first for current schemas.","bodyPreview":"# Canva Automation via Rube MCP\n\nAutomate Canva design operations through Composio''s Canva toolkit via Rube MCP.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Rube MCP must be connected (RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available)\n- Active Canva connection via `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `canva`\n- Always call `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` first to get current tool schemas\n\n## Setup\n\n**Get Rube MCP**: Add `https://rube.app/mcp` as an MCP server in your client configuration. No API keys needed — just add the endpoint and it works.\n\n\n1.","body":"# Canva Automation via Rube MCP\n\nAutomate Canva design operations through Composio''s Canva toolkit via Rube MCP.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Rube MCP must be connected (RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available)\n- Active Canva connection via `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `canva`\n- Always call `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` first to get current tool schemas\n\n## Setup\n\n**Get Rube MCP**: Add `https://rube.app/mcp` as an MCP server in your client configuration. No API keys needed — just add the endpoint and it works.\n\n\n1. Verify Rube MCP is available by confirming `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` responds\n2. Call `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `canva`\n3. If connection is not ACTIVE, follow the returned auth link to complete Canva OAuth\n4. Confirm connection status shows ACTIVE before running any workflows\n\n## Core Workflows\n\n### 1. List and Browse Designs\n\n**When to use**: User wants to find existing designs or browse their Canva library\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS` - List all designs with optional filters [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `query`: Search term to filter designs by name\n- `continuation`: Pagination token from previous response\n- `ownership`: Filter by ''owned'', ''shared'', or ''any''\n- `sort_by`: Sort field (e.g., ''modified_at'', ''title'')\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Results are paginated; follow `continuation` token until absent\n- Deleted designs may still appear briefly; check design status\n- Search is substring-based, not fuzzy matching\n\n### 2. Create and Design\n\n**When to use**: User wants to create a new Canva design from scratch or from a template\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST` - Browse available brand templates [Optional]\n2. `CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_WITH_OPTIONAL_ASSET` - Create a new design [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `design_type`: Type of design (e.g., ''Presentation'', ''Poster'', ''SocialMedia'')\n- `title`: Name for the new design\n- `asset_id`: Optional asset to include in the design\n- `width` / `height`: Custom dimensions in pixels\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Design type must match Canva''s predefined types exactly\n- Custom dimensions have minimum and maximum limits\n- Asset must be uploaded first via CANVA_CREATE_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB before referencing\n\n### 3. Upload Assets\n\n**When to use**: User wants to upload images or files to Canva for use in designs\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_CREATE_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB` - Initiate the asset upload [Required]\n2. `CANVA_FETCH_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB_STATUS` - Poll until upload completes [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `name`: Display name for the asset\n- `url`: Public URL of the file to upload (for URL-based uploads)\n- `job_id`: Upload job ID returned from step 1 (for status polling)\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Upload is asynchronous; you MUST poll the job status until it completes\n- Supported formats include PNG, JPG, SVG, MP4, GIF\n- File size limits apply; large files may take longer to process\n- The `job_id` from CREATE returns the ID needed for status polling\n- Status values: ''in_progress'', ''success'', ''failed''\n\n### 4. Export Designs\n\n**When to use**: User wants to download or export a Canva design as PDF, PNG, or other format\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS` - Find the design to export [Prerequisite]\n2. `CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB` - Start the export process [Required]\n3. `CANVA_GET_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB_RESULT` - Poll until export completes and get download URL [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `design_id`: ID of the design to export\n- `format`: Export format (''pdf'', ''png'', ''jpg'', ''svg'', ''mp4'', ''gif'', ''pptx'')\n- `pages`: Specific page numbers to export (array)\n- `quality`: Export quality (''regular'', ''high'')\n- `job_id`: Export job ID for polling status\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Export is asynchronous; you MUST poll the job result until it completes\n- Download URLs from completed exports expire after a limited time\n- Large designs with many pages take longer to export\n- Not all formats support all design types (e.g., MP4 only for animations)\n- Poll interval: wait 2-3 seconds between status checks\n\n### 5. Organize with Folders\n\n**When to use**: User wants to create folders or organize designs into folders\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_POST_FOLDERS` - Create a new folder [Required]\n2. `CANVA_MOVE_ITEM_TO_SPECIFIED_FOLDER` - Move designs into folders [Optional]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `name`: Folder name\n- `parent_folder_id`: Parent folder for nested organization\n- `item_id`: ID of the design or asset to move\n- `folder_id`: Target folder ID\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Folder names must be unique within the same parent folder\n- Moving items between folders updates their location immediately\n- Root-level folders have no parent_folder_id\n\n### 6. Autofill from Brand Templates\n\n**When to use**: User wants to generate designs by filling brand template placeholders with data\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST` - List available brand templates [Required]\n2. `CANVA_INITIATE_CANVA_DESIGN_AUTOFILL_JOB` - Start autofill with data [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `brand_template_id`: ID of the brand template to use\n- `title`: Title for the generated design\n- `data`: Key-value mapping of placeholder names to replacement values\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Template placeholders must match exactly (case-sensitive)\n- Autofill is asynchronous; poll for completion\n- Only brand templates support autofill, not regular designs\n- Data values must match the expected type for each placeholder (text, image URL)\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Async Job Pattern\n\nMany Canva operations are asynchronous:\n```\n1. Initiate job (upload, export, autofill) -> get job_id\n2. Poll status endpoint with job_id every 2-3 seconds\n3. Check for ''success'' or ''failed'' status\n4. On success, extract result (asset_id, download_url, design_id)\n```\n\n### ID Resolution\n\n**Design name -> Design ID**:\n```\n1. Call CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS with query=design_name\n2. Find matching design in results\n3. Extract id field\n```\n\n**Brand template name -> Template ID**:\n```\n1. Call CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST\n2. Find template by name\n3. Extract brand_template_id\n```\n\n### Pagination\n\n- Check response for `continuation` token\n- Pass token in next request''s `continuation` parameter\n- Continue until `continuation` is absent or empty\n\n## Known Pitfalls\n\n**Async Operations**:\n- Uploads, exports, and autofills are all asynchronous\n- Always poll job status; do not assume immediate completion\n- Download URLs from exports expire; use them promptly\n\n**Asset Management**:\n- Assets must be uploaded before they can be used in designs\n- Upload job must reach ''success'' status before the asset_id is valid\n- Supported formats vary; check Canva documentation for current limits\n\n**Rate Limits**:\n- Canva API has rate limits per endpoint\n- Implement exponential backoff for bulk operations\n- Batch operations where possible to reduce API calls\n\n**Response Parsing**:\n- Response data may be nested under `data` key\n- Job status responses include different fields based on completion state\n- Parse defensively with fallbacks for optional fields\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Tool Slug | Key Params |\n|------|-----------|------------|\n| List designs | CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS | query, continuation |\n| Create design | CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_WITH_OPTIONAL_ASSET | design_type, title |\n| Upload asset | CANVA_CREATE_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB | name, url |\n| Check upload | CANVA_FETCH_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB_STATUS | job_id |\n| Export design | CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB | design_id, format |\n| Get export | CANVA_GET_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB_RESULT | job_id |\n| Create folder | CANVA_POST_FOLDERS | name, parent_folder_id |\n| Move to folder | CANVA_MOVE_ITEM_TO_SPECIFIED_FOLDER | item_id, folder_id |\n| List templates | CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST | (none) |\n| Autofill template | CANVA_INITIATE_CANVA_DESIGN_AUTOFILL_JOB | brand_template_id, data |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:12:28.115Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Visual Design Agents needing automated Canva operations via Rube MCP and Composio''s Canva toolkit.","zh":"非常适合需要通过 Rube MCP 和 Composio 的 Canva 工具包进行自动化 Canva 操作的视觉设计代理。","ja":"Rube MCP と Composio の Canva ツールキットを使用して自動化された Canva 操作が必要なビジュアルデザインエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Rube MCP와 Composio의 Canva 툴킷을 통해 자동화된 Canva 작동이 필요한 시각 디자이너 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de diseño visual que necesitan operaciones automatizadas de Canva a través de Rube MCP y la herramienta de Canva de Composio.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de conception visuelle ayant besoin d''opérations Canva automatisées via Rube MCP et la trousse à outils Canva de Composio.","de":"Perfekt für Visuelle-Design-Agenten, die automatisierte Canva-Operationen über Rube MCP und Composios Canva-Toolkit benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Design Visual que precisam de operações automatizadas do Canva via Rube MCP e kit de ferramentas do Canva da Composio.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов визуального дизайна, которым необходимы автоматизированные операции Canva через Rube MCP и набор инструментов Canva от Composio.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التصميم المرئي الذين يحتاجون إلى عمليات أوتوماتيكية في كانفا عبر روبي إم سي بي وأدوات كانفا من كومبوزيو."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate Canva design operations through Composio''s Canva toolkit, enabling seamless integration with Rube MCP for efficient design workflows, utilizing RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS and RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS for streamlined connectivity.","zh":"赋予代理自动化 Canva 设计操作的能力，通过 Composio 的 Canva 工具包实现与 Rube MCP 的无缝集成，利用 RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS 和 RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS 实现流畅的连接，从而实现高效的设计工作流。","ja":"エージェントが Composio の Canva ツールキットを使用して Canva デザイン操作を自動化できるようにし、Rube MCP とシームレスに統合して効率的なデザインワークフローを実現します。RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS と RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS を使用して接続を簡素化します。","ko":"에이전트가 Composio의 Canva 툴킷을 통해 Canva 디자인 작동을 자동화할 수 있도록 하여 Rube MCP와의 무결점 통합을 통해 효율적인 디자인 워크플로우를实现하며, RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS와 RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS를 사용하여 연결을 간소화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar operaciones de diseño de Canva a través de la herramienta de Canva de Composio, permitiendo una integración perfecta con Rube MCP para flujos de trabajo de diseño eficientes, utilizando RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS y RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS para una conectividad optimizada.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser les opérations de conception de Canva via la trousse à outils Canva de Composio, permettant une intégration transparente avec Rube MCP pour des flux de travail de conception efficaces, en utilisant RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS et RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS pour une connectivité rationalisée.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Canva-Designoperationen über Composios Canva-Toolkit zu automatisieren, wodurch eine nahtlose Integration mit Rube MCP für effiziente Design-Workflows ermöglicht wird, unter Nutzung von RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS und RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS für eine optimierte Konnektivität.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar operações de design do Canva por meio do kit de ferramentas do Canva da Composio, permitindo uma integração perfeita com o Rube MCP para fluxos de trabalho de design eficientes, utilizando RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS e RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS para conectividade otimizada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать операции по дизайну Canva с помощью набора инструментов Canva от Composio, обеспечивая бесперебойную интеграцию с Rube MCP для эффективных рабочих процессов дизайна, используя RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS и RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS для оптимизированного подключения.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على أتمتة عمليات تصميم كانفا من خلال أدوات كانفا من كومبوزيو، وتمكين التكامل السلس مع روبي إم سي بي من أجل تدفقات عمل تصميم فعالة، واستخدام أدوات البحث روبي وأدوات إدارة الاتصال من أجل اتصال مُستَقر."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Canva design tasks via Rube MCP","Generating designs with Composio''s Canva toolkit","Managing Canva connections through RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"zh":["通过 Rube MCP 自动化 Canva 设计任务","使用 Composio 的 Canva 工具包生成设计","通过 RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS 管理 Canva 连接"],"ja":["Rube MCP を使用した Canva デザインタスクの自動化","Composio の Canva ツールキットを使用したデザインの生成","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS を使用した Canva 接続の管理"],"ko":["Rube MCP를 통해 Canva 디자인 작업 자동화","Composio의 Canva 툴킷을 사용한 디자인 생성","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS를 통해 Canva 연결 관리"],"es":["Automatizar tareas de diseño de Canva a través de Rube MCP","Generar diseños con la herramienta de Canva de Composio","Administrar conexiones de Canva a través de RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"fr":["Automatiser les tâches de conception de Canva via Rube MCP","Générer des conceptions avec la trousse à outils Canva de Composio","Gérer les connexions Canva via RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"de":["Automatisierung von Canva-Designtasks über Rube MCP","Erzeugen von Designs mit Composios Canva-Toolkit","Verwalten von Canva-Verbindungen über RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"pt":["Automatizar tarefas de design do Canva via Rube MCP","Gerar designs com o kit de ferramentas do Canva da Composio","Gerenciar conexões do Canva por meio de RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"ru":["Автоматизировать задачи дизайна Canva через Rube MCP","Генерировать дизайны с помощью набора инструментов Canva от Composio","Управлять подключениями Canva через RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS"],"ar":["أتمتة مهام تصميم كانفا عبر روبي إم سي بي","إنتاج تصاميم باستخدام أدوات كانفا من كومبوزيو","إدارة الاتصالات بكانفا من خلال أدوات إدارة الاتصال روبي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rube MCP connection with RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available","Needs active Canva connection via RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS with toolkit canva"],"zh":["需要具有 RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS 的 Rube MCP 连接","需要通过 RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS 具有工具包 canva 的活跃 Canva 连接"],"ja":["RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS を使用した Rube MCP 接続が必要","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS を使用したツールキット canva を使用したアクティブな Canva 接続が必要"],"ko":["RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS를 사용하는 Rube MCP 연결이 필요","RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS를 통해 툴킷 canva를 사용하는 활성 Canva 연결이 필요"],"es":["Requiere conexión con Rube MCP con RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS disponibles","Necesita una conexión activa de Canva a través de RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS con la herramienta de Canva"],"fr":["Nécessite une connexion Rube MCP avec RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS disponibles","Nécessite une connexion active Canva via RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS avec la trousse à outils Canva"],"de":["Benötigt eine Verbindung mit Rube MCP mit verfügbaren RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS","Benötigt eine aktive Canva-Verbindung über RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS mit dem Canva-Toolkit"],"pt":["Requer conexão com Rube MCP com RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS disponíveis","Necessita de conexão ativa do Canva via RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS com toolkit canva"],"ru":["Требует подключения к Rube MCP с доступными RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS","Требует активного подключения Canva через RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS с toolkit canva"],"ar":["يتطلب اتصالاً بروبي إم سي بي مع أدوات البحث روبي المتاحة","يتطلب اتصالاً نشطاً بكانفا عبر أدوات إدارة الاتصال روبي مع أدوات كانفا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('pengelbrecht/ticks/ticks', 'community', 'pengelbrecht', 'ticks', 'pengelbrecht/ticks', 'ticks', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.517Z', '2026-02-18T13:12:55.816Z', NULL, '{"id":"pengelbrecht/ticks/ticks","name":"ticks","description":{"zh":"Ticks 是一种工作流管理工具，用于管理 AI 代理的任务和依赖关系","ja":"Ticks は AI エージェントのタスクと依存関係を管理するワークフロー管理ツールです","ko":"Ticks는 AI 에이전트의 작업과 의존성을 관리하는 작업 흐름 관리 도구입니다","es":"Ticks es una herramienta de seguimiento de problemas para agentes de IA que gestiona tareas y proporciona una tabla web para el monitoreo","fr":"Ticks est un outil de suivi des problèmes pour les agents d''IA qui gère les tâches et fournit un tableau web pour le suivi","de":"Ticks ist ein Tool zur Fehlerverfolgung für KI-Agenten, das Aufgaben verwaltet und eine Web-Tabelle für die Überwachung bereitstellt","pt":"Ticks é uma ferramenta de rastreamento de problemas projetada para agentes de IA, permitindo gerenciar tarefas e problemas de forma eficiente","ru":"Ticks - это инструмент отслеживания проблем, предназначенный для агентов ИИ, позволяющий эффективно управлять задачами и проблемами","ar":"Ticks هو أداة تتبع المشكلات مصممة لمحاكي الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يسمح بإدارة المهام والمشكلات بفعالية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Ticks 工作流管理","ja":"ティックス ワークフロー管理","ko":"틱스 작업 흐름 관리","es":"Ticks: Seguimiento de problemas para agentes de IA","fr":"Ticks: Suivi des problèmes pour les agents d''IA","de":"Ticks: Problemmelder für KI-Agenten","pt":"Ticks: Ferramenta de Rastreamento de Problemas para Agent...","ru":"Ticks: Инструмент отслеживания проблем для агентов ИИ","ar":"Ticks: أداة تتبع المشكلات لمحاكي الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"ticks"},"description":{"zh":"Ticks 是一种工作流管理工具，用于管理 AI 代理的任务和依赖关系","ja":"Ticks は AI エージェントのタスクと依存関係を管理するワークフロー管理ツールです","ko":"Ticks는 AI 에이전트의 작업과 의존성을 관리하는 작업 흐름 관리 도구입니다","es":"Ticks es una herramienta de seguimiento de problemas para agentes de IA que gestiona tareas y proporciona una tabla web para el monitoreo","fr":"Ticks est un outil de suivi des problèmes pour les agents d''IA qui gère les tâches et fournit un tableau web pour le suivi","de":"Ticks ist ein Tool zur Fehlerverfolgung für KI-Agenten, das Aufgaben verwaltet und eine Web-Tabelle für die Überwachung bereitstellt","pt":"Ticks é uma ferramenta de rastreamento de problemas projetada para agentes de IA, permitindo gerenciar tarefas e problemas de forma eficiente","ru":"Ticks - это инструмент отслеживания проблем, предназначенный для агентов ИИ, позволяющий эффективно управлять задачами и проблемами","ar":"Ticks هو أداة تتبع المشكلات مصممة لمحاكي الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يسمح بإدارة المهام والمشكلات بفعالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["任务管理","持续循环运行","Web 基于监控面板","依赖关系管理","持久历史记录"],"ja":["タスク管理","継続的ループ実行","Web ベースの監視パネル","依存関係管理","永続的履歴"],"ko":["작업 관리","지속적인 루프 실행","웹 기반 모니터링 패널","의존성 관리","영구적 기록"],"es":["Gestión de tareas","Ejecución de agentes en bucles continuos","Tabla web para el monitoreo","Historial persistente y notas","Posibilidad de handoff humano y puertas de aprobación"],"fr":["Gestion des tâches","Exécution des agents en boucles continues","Tableau web pour le suivi","Historique persistant et notes","Possibilité de handoff humain et de portes d''approbation"],"de":["Aufgabenverwaltung","Ausführung von Agenten in kontinuierlichen Schleifen","Web-Tabelle für die Überwachung","Persistenter Historie und Notizen","Möglichkeit von Handoff und Genehmigungsschwellen"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de tarefas","Execução de agentes em loops contínuos","Quadro web para monitoramento","Dependências entre tarefas","Histórico persistente e anotações"],"ru":["Управление задачами","Выполнение агентов в непрерывных циклах","Веб-интерфейс для мониторинга","Зависимости между задачами","Постоянная история и заметки"],"ar":["إدارة المهام","تشغيل الوكلاء في دورات مستمرة","لوحة ويب للرصد","الاعتماد بين المهام","التاريخ المستمر والملاحظات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 代理","issue 跟踪","工作流管理","任务管理","持续集成","Web 监控"],"ja":["AI エージェント","Issue トラッカー","ワークフロー管理","タスク管理","継続的インテグレーション","Web 監視"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","이슈 추적","작업 흐름 관리","작업 관리","지속적인 통합","웹 모니터링"],"es":["seguimiento de problemas","agentes de IA","gestión de tareas","tabla web","historial persistente","handoff humano","puertas de aprobación","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["suivi des problèmes","agents d''IA","gestion des tâches","tableau web","historique persistant","handoff humain","portes d''approbation","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["Fehlerverfolgung","KI-Agenten","Aufgabenverwaltung","Web-Tabelle","persistente Historie","Handoff","Genehmigungsschwellen","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["rastreamento de problemas","agentes de IA","gerenciamento de tarefas","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de produtividade","tecnologia de IA"],"ru":["отслеживание проблем","агенты ИИ","управление задачами","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты повышения производительности","технология ИИ"],"ar":["تتبع المشكلات","محاكي الذكاء الاصطناعي","إدارة المهام","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات زيادة الإنتاجية","تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"pengelbrecht","repo":"ticks","repoPath":"pengelbrecht/ticks","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.517Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ticks","description":"Work with Ticks issue tracker and AI agent runner. Use when managing tasks or issues with tk commands, running AI agents on epics, creating ticks from a SPEC.md, or working in a repo with a .tick directory. Triggers on phrases like create ticks, tk, run ticker, epic, close the task, plan this, break this down.","bodyPreview":"# Ticks Workflow\n\nTicks is an issue tracker designed for AI agents. The `tk` CLI manages tasks, runs agents in continuous loops, and provides a web-based board for monitoring.\n\n## When to Use Ticks vs TodoWrite\n\n**Use Ticks (`tk`) for work that:**\n- Spans multiple sessions or conversations\n- Has dependencies on other tasks\n- Is discovered during other work and should be tracked\n- Needs human handoff or approval gates\n- Benefits from persistent history and notes\n\n**Use TodoWrite for:**\n- Simple s","body":"# Ticks Workflow\n\nTicks is an issue tracker designed for AI agents. The `tk` CLI manages tasks, runs agents in continuous loops, and provides a web-based board for monitoring.\n\n## When to Use Ticks vs TodoWrite\n\n**Use Ticks (`tk`) for work that:**\n- Spans multiple sessions or conversations\n- Has dependencies on other tasks\n- Is discovered during other work and should be tracked\n- Needs human handoff or approval gates\n- Benefits from persistent history and notes\n\n**Use TodoWrite for:**\n- Simple single-session tasks\n- Work that will be completed in the current conversation\n- Tracking progress on immediate work\n\nDon''t over-index on creating ticks for every small thing. Use your judgment.\n\n## Skill Workflow\n\nWhen invoked, follow this workflow:\n\n### Step 0: Check Prerequisites\n\n**1. Git repository:**\n```bash\ngit status 2>/dev/null || git init\n```\n\n**2. Ticks initialized:**\n```bash\nls .tick/ 2>/dev/null || tk init\n```\n\n**3. tk installed:**\n```bash\nwhich tk || echo \"Install: curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengelbrecht/ticks/main/scripts/install.sh | sh\"\n```\n\n**4. Git tracking (important):**\n\nThe `.tick/` directory should be tracked by git, not gitignored. Ticks are designed to be version-controlled so they sync across machines and team members via normal git workflows.\n\nIf you see `.tick` or `.tick/` in the project''s `.gitignore`, remove it. The only things that should be gitignored are internal/local files, which is handled by `.tick/.gitignore` (ignores `.index.json` and `logs/`).\n\n```bash\n# Check if .tick is gitignored (should return nothing)\ngit check-ignore .tick/\n\n# If it returns \".tick/\", remove the entry from .gitignore\n```\n\n### Step 1: Check for SPEC.md\n\nLook for a SPEC.md (or similar spec file) in the repo root.\n\n**If no spec exists:** Go to Step 2a (Create Spec)\n**If spec exists but incomplete:** Go to Step 2b (Complete Spec)\n**If spec is complete:** Skip to Step 3 (Create Ticks)\n\n### Step 2a: Create Spec Through Conversation\n\nHave a natural conversation with the user to understand their idea:\n\n1. **Let them describe it** - Don''t interrupt, let them explain the full vision\n2. **Ask clarifying questions** - Dig into unclear areas through back-and-forth dialogue\n3. **Optionally use AskUserQuestion** - For quick multiple-choice decisions\n4. **Write SPEC.md** - Once you have enough detail, generate the spec\n\n**Conversation topics to explore:**\n- What problem does this solve? Who''s it for?\n- Core features vs nice-to-haves\n- Technical constraints or preferences\n- How will users interact with it?\n- What does \"done\" look like?\n\n### Step 2b: Complete Existing Spec\n\nIf SPEC.md exists but has gaps:\n\n1. **Read the spec** - Identify what''s missing or unclear\n2. **Ask targeted questions** - Focus on the gaps, don''t re-ask obvious things\n3. **Update SPEC.md** - Fill in the missing details\n\n## Creating Good Tasks\n\n**Every task should be an atomic, committable piece of work with tests.**\n\nThe ideal task:\n- Has a clear, single deliverable\n- Can be verified by running tests\n- Results in demoable software that builds on previous work\n- Is completable in 1-3 agent iterations\n\n**Good task:**\n```bash\ntk create \"Add email validation to registration\" \\\n  -d \"Validate email format on blur, show error below input.\n\nTest cases:\n- valid@example.com -> valid\n- invalid@ -> invalid\n- @nodomain.com -> invalid\n\nRun: go test ./internal/validation/...\" \\\n  -acceptance \"All validation tests pass\" \\\n  -parent <epic-id>\n```\n\n**Bad task:**\n```bash\ntk create \"Add email validation\" -d \"Make sure emails are valid\"\n# No test cases, no verification criteria - agent will guess\n```\n\nSee `references/tick-patterns.md` for more patterns.\n\n### Step 3: Create Ticks from Spec\n\nTransform the spec into ticks organized by epic.\n\n**For phased specs:** Focus on creating ticks for the current/next phase only. Don''t create ticks for future phases - they may change based on learnings.\n\n**Epic organization:**\n1. Group related tasks into logical epics (auth, API, UI, etc.)\n2. Create tasks with dependencies using `-blocked-by`\n3. Mark human-required tasks with `--awaiting work`\n\n**Designing for parallel execution:**\nTasks in the same wave (no blocking relationship) may run concurrently. To avoid file conflicts:\n- If two tasks edit the same file, make one block the other\n- Use `tk graph <epic>` to visualize waves and verify parallel tasks touch different files\n- Example: Task A edits `auth.go`, Task B edits `auth.go` → B should block on A\n\n```bash\n# Create epics\ntk create \"Authentication\" -t epic\ntk create \"API Endpoints\" -t epic\n\n# Create tasks with acceptance criteria\ntk create \"Add JWT token generation\" \\\n  -d \"Implement JWT signing and verification\" \\\n  -acceptance \"JWT tests pass\" \\\n  -parent <auth-epic>\n\ntk create \"Add login endpoint\" \\\n  -d \"POST /api/login with email/password\" \\\n  -acceptance \"Login endpoint tests pass\" \\\n  -parent <api-epic> \\\n  -blocked-by <jwt-task>\n\n# Human-only tasks (skipped by tk next)\ntk create \"Set up production database\" --awaiting work \\\n  -d \"Create RDS instance and configure access\"\n\ntk create \"Create Stripe API keys\" --awaiting work \\\n  -d \"Set up Stripe account and get API credentials\"\n```\n\n### Step 4: Guide User Through Blocking Human Tasks\n\nIf human tasks block automated tasks, guide the user through them before running the agent.\n\n```bash\n# Check for blocking human tasks\ntk list --awaiting work\ntk blocked  # See what''s waiting\n```\n\nWalk the user through each blocking task, then close it:\n```bash\ntk close <id> \"Completed - connection string in .env\"\n```\n\n### Step 5: Choose Execution Mode\n\nTicks supports two execution approaches. If the user hasn''t specified a preference, ask:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"How would you like to execute this epic?\"\nHeader: \"Execution\"\nOptions:\n  - \"tk run\" - \"Rich monitoring via tickboard, HITL support, cost tracking, git worktree isolation\"\n  - \"Claude Code\" - \"Native parallel subagents, seamless session execution, direct visibility\"\n```\n\n#### Option A: tk run\n\nUses the Ticks agent runner with tickboard monitoring.\n\n```bash\n# Run on specific epic\ntk run <epic-id>\n\n# Pool mode - N concurrent workers within single epic\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4\n\n# Pool with custom stale timeout\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4 --stale-timeout 2h\n\n# Run in isolated worktree\ntk run <epic-id> --worktree\n\n# Parallel epics (each in own worktree)\ntk run <epic-id> --parallel 2\n\n# Combined: parallel epics with pool workers each\ntk run epic1 epic2 --parallel 2 --pool 4\n\n# With cost limit\ntk run <epic-id> --max-cost 5.00\n```\n\n**Monitor:** `tk board` opens local web interface.\n\n**Best for:** Production epics, rich HITL workflows, long-running tasks, cost tracking.\n\n#### Option B: Claude Code Native\n\nUses Claude Code''s Task tool to spawn parallel subagents.\n\n**Best for:** Quick parallel execution within a Claude session, direct visibility into agents.\n\nSee **`references/claude-runner.md`** for full documentation including:\n- Task tool parameters and options\n- Agent naming conventions (epic/tick/wave)\n- Wave orchestration algorithm\n- Polling strategy to avoid hangs\n- HITL-aware state transitions\n- Example session\n\n#### Quick Comparison\n\n| Aspect | `tk run` | Claude Code |\n|--------|----------|-------------|\n| Monitoring | Tickboard | Claude Code UI |\n| HITL | Rich (approvals, checkpoints) | Basic (conversation) |\n| Parallelization | Pool workers (`--pool`) or worktrees (`--parallel`) | Task subagents |\n| File isolation | Worktrees (proven) | Shared workspace |\n| State persistence | Tick files (survives crashes) | Session-bound |\n| Cost tracking | Built-in (`--max-cost`) | Manual |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Creating Ticks\n\n```bash\ntk create \"Title\" -d \"Description\" -acceptance \"Tests pass\"  # Task\ntk create \"Title\" -t epic                                    # Epic\ntk create \"Title\" -parent <epic-id>                          # Under epic\ntk create \"Title\" -blocked-by <task-id>                      # Blocked\ntk create \"Title\" --awaiting work                            # Human task\ntk create \"Title\" --requires approval                        # Needs approval gate\n```\n\n### Querying\n\n```bash\ntk list                      # All open ticks\ntk list -t epic              # Epics only\ntk list -parent <epic-id>    # Tasks in epic\ntk ready                     # Unblocked tasks\ntk next <epic-id>            # Next task for agent\ntk blocked                   # Blocked tasks\ntk list --awaiting           # Tasks awaiting human\ntk graph <epic-id>           # Dependency graph with parallelization\ntk graph <epic-id> --json    # JSON output for agents\n```\n\n### Managing\n\n```bash\ntk show <id>                 # Show details\ntk close <id> \"reason\"       # Close tick\ntk note <id> \"text\"          # Add note\ntk approve <id>              # Approve awaiting tick\ntk reject <id> \"feedback\"    # Reject with feedback\n```\n\n### Running Agent (Two Modes)\n\n**Mode A: Native tk run**\n```bash\ntk run <epic-id>                      # Run on epic\ntk run --auto                         # Auto-select epic\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4             # Pool mode (4 concurrent workers)\ntk run <epic-id> --pool 4 --stale-timeout 2h  # Custom stale timeout\ntk run <epic-id> --worktree           # Use git worktree\ntk run <epic-id> --parallel 3         # 3 epics in parallel worktrees\ntk run a b --parallel 2 --pool 4      # 2 epics, 4 workers each\ntk run <epic-id> --max-iterations 10  # Limit iterations\ntk run <epic-id> --max-cost 5.00      # Cost limit\ntk run <epic-id> --watch              # Restart when tasks ready\ntk board                              # Web interface\n```\n\n**Mode B: Claude Code Native**\n```bash\n# See references/claude-runner.md for full details\n\n# 1. Get dependency graph\ntk graph <epic-id> --json\n\n# 2. Ask user for MAX_AGENTS (1-10)\n\n# 3. For each wave, launch Task agents:\n#    Task(subagent_type: \"general-purpose\",\n#         name: \"<epic>-w<wave>-<tick>\",\n#         run_in_background: true,\n#         mode: \"bypassPermissions\")\n\n# 4. Poll for completion, sync to ticks\ntk close <tick-id> --reason \"Completed via Claude runner\"\n```\n\n### Planning Parallel Execution\n\nBefore running agents, use `tk graph` to understand parallelization opportunities:\n\n```bash\ntk graph <epic-id>        # Human-readable wave breakdown\ntk graph <epic-id> --json # Machine-readable for planning\n```\n\nThe graph shows:\n- **Waves**: Groups of tasks that can run in parallel\n- **Max parallel**: How many workers you could use at once\n- **Critical path**: Minimum sequential steps to complete the epic\n- **Dependencies**: What each task is blocked by\n\nUse this to decide:\n- `--pool N` for N concurrent workers within one epic (recommended)\n- `--parallel N` for N epics in separate worktrees\n- Combine both: `--parallel 2 --pool 4` for 2 epics with 4 workers each\n\nSee `references/tk-commands.md` for full reference.\n\n## Assisting with Awaiting Ticks\n\nWhen working interactively, help users process awaiting ticks:\n\n```bash\ntk list --awaiting    # Find ticks awaiting human\ntk next --awaiting    # Next one needing attention\n```\n\nUse AskUserQuestion to help users decide, then execute:\n\n```bash\n# User approves\ntk approve <id>\n\n# User rejects\ntk reject <id> \"feedback here\"\n\n# User provides input\ntk note <id> \"Use sliding window algorithm\" --from human\ntk approve <id>\n```\n\nAlways use `--from human` when adding notes on behalf of the user.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:12:55.816Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Autonomous Task Management Agents orchestrating complex, multi-step projects with dependencies.","zh":"适用于自治任务管理代理，用于编排具有依赖关系的复杂、多步骤项目。","ja":"複雑な多段階プロジェクトの依存関係を持つオーケストレーションを担当するAutonomous Task Managementエージェントに不可欠。","ko":"의존 관계가 있는 복잡한 多段階 프로젝트의 오케스트레이션을 담당하는 자율적 태스크 관리 에이전트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de gestión de tareas autónomos que orquestan proyectos complejos y multietapa con dependencias.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de gestion de tâches autonomes orchestrant des projets complexes et multétapes avec des dépendances.","de":"Wesentlich für autonome Task-Management-Agents, die komplexe, mehrstufige Projekte mit Abhängigkeiten orchestrieren.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Tarefas Autônomas que orquestram projetos complexos, multi-etapas com dependências.","ru":"Необходим для автономных агентов управления задачами, которые управляют сложными, многоступенчатыми проектами с зависимостями.","ar":"ضروري لموكلات إدارة المهام المستقلة التي تضبط مشاريع معقدة متعددة المراحل مع التبعيات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables persistent tracking of tasks across multiple sessions, managing dependencies between tasks, and operating agents in continuous loops. Provides a web-based board for human oversight and approval gates, ensuring complex work is properly documented and coordinated.","zh":"实现任务在多个会话中的持久跟踪、管理任务之间的依赖关系以及代理在连续循环中的操作。提供基于Web的看板用于人类监督和审批门，确保复杂工作得到适当的文档记录和协调。","ja":"複数のセッションを横断するタスクの永続的な追跡、タスク間の依存関係の管理、およびエージェントの連続ループでの操作を可能にします。人間の監視と承認ゲートを可能にするWebベースのボードを提供し、複雑な作業が適切に文書化および調整されることを保証します。","ko":"여러 세션에 걸친 태스크의 지속적인 추적, 태스크 간의 의존 관계 관리, 및 에이전트의 연속 루프에서 동작을 가능하게 합니다. 인간의 감독 및 승인 게이트를 가능하게 하는 웹 기반의 보드를 제공하여, 복잡한 작업이 적절히 문서화되고 조정되도록 보장합니다.","es":"Permite el seguimiento persistente de tareas en varias sesiones, la gestión de dependencias entre tareas y la operación de agentes en bucles continuos. Proporciona una tabla web para la supervisión y las puertas de aprobación humanas, asegurando que el trabajo complejo esté debidamente documentado y coordinado.","fr":"Permet un suivi persistant des tâches sur plusieurs sessions, la gestion des dépendances entre les tâches et le fonctionnement des agents en boucles continues. Fournit un tableau web pour la surveillance et les portes d''approbation humaines, garantissant que les travaux complexes soient correctement documentés et coordonnés.","de":"Ermöglicht das persistente Nachverfolgen von Aufgaben über mehrere Sitzungen hinweg, die Verwaltung von Abhängigkeiten zwischen Aufgaben und den Betrieb von Agenten in kontinuierlichen Schleifen. Bietet eine Web-Tafel für die Überwachung durch Menschen und Genehmigungsschranken, um sicherzustellen, dass komplexe Arbeiten ordnungsgemäß dokumentiert und koordiniert werden.","pt":"Permite o acompanhamento persistente de tarefas em várias sessões, gerenciamento de dependências entre tarefas e operação de agentes em loops contínuos. Fornece um quadro baseado na web para supervisão humana e portas de aprovação, garantindo que o trabalho complexo seja adequadamente documentado e coordenado.","ru":"Позволяет обеспечить постоянную отслеживаемость задач в нескольких сессиях, управление зависимостями между задачами и работу агентов в непрерывных циклах. Предоставляет веб-интерфейс для надзора и ворот утверждения, гарантируя, что сложная работа правильно документирована и скоординирована.","ar":"يسمح بالتتبع المستمر للمهام عبر عدة جلسات، وإدارة التبعيات بين المهام، وتشغيل الوكلاء في الحلقات المستمرة. يوفر لوحة ويب لمراقبة الإنسان وبوابات الموافقة، مما يضمن أن يتم توثيق العمل المعقد بشكل صحيح وتنسيقه."},"useCases":{"en":["Managing multi-session project backlogs","Orchestrating tasks with complex dependencies","Running agents in continuous monitoring loops","Handing off tasks for human approval","Tracking work discovered during other operations"],"zh":["管理多会话项目积压","编排具有复杂依赖关系的任务","在连续监控循环中运行代理","将任务移交给人类审批","跟踪在其他操作期间发现的工作"],"ja":["複数セッションのプロジェクトバックログの管理","複雑な依存関係を持つタスクのオーケストレーション","連続モニタリングループでエージェントを実行","タスクを人間の承認に引き渡す","他の作業中に見つかった作業の追跡"],"ko":["다중 세션 프로젝트 백로그 관리","복잡한 의존 관계를 가진 태스크의 오케스트레이션","연속 모니터링 루프에서 에이전트 실행","태스크를 인간의 승인으로 전달","다른 작업 중에 발견된 작업의 추적"],"es":["Gestión de proyectos de varias sesiones","Orquestación de tareas con dependencias complejas","Ejecución de agentes en bucles de monitoreo continuo","Entrega de tareas para la aprobación humana","Seguimiento del trabajo descubierto durante otras operaciones"],"fr":["Gestion de projets de plusieurs sessions","Orchestration de tâches avec des dépendances complexes","Exécution d''agents en boucles de surveillance continues","Remise de tâches pour approbation humaine","Suivi des travaux découverts lors d''autres opérations"],"de":["Verwaltung von Projekten mit mehreren Sitzungen","Orchestrierung von Aufgaben mit komplexen Abhängigkeiten","Ausführung von Agenten in kontinuierlichen Überwachungsschleifen","Übergabe von Aufgaben für die menschliche Genehmigung","Nachverfolgung der Arbeiten, die während anderer Operationen entdeckt werden"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de backlogs de projetos em multi-sessões","Orquestração de tarefas com dependências complexas","Execução de agentes em loops de monitoramento contínuo","Transferência de tarefas para aprovação humana","Rastreamento de trabalhos descobertos durante outras operações"],"ru":["Управление запасом проектов в нескольких сессиях","Оркестровка задач с сложными зависимостями","Выполнение агентов в непрерывных циклах мониторинга","Передача задач для утверждения человеком","Отслеживание работы, обнаруженной во время других операций"],"ar":["إدارة ذخيرة المشاريع في جلسات متعددة","توجيه المهام بالتبعيات المعقدة","تشغيل الوكلاء في الحلقات المستمرة للرصد","نقل المهام للموافقة البشرية","تتبع الأعمال المكتشفة أثناء العمليات الأخرى"]},"limitations":{"en":["Designed specifically for AI agent workflows","Requires CLI (`tk`) for full functionality","Web board needed for visual monitoring"],"zh":["专门为AI代理工作流设计","需要CLI（`tk`）以获得全部功能","需要Web看板进行可视化监控"],"ja":["AIエージェントのワークフロー専用に設計","CLI（`tk`）が必要な全機能","Webボードが視覚的な監視に必要"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 워크플로우専门으로 설계됨","CLI(`tk`)가 필요함으로써 모든 기능을 사용할 수 있습니다.","웹 보드가 시각적 모니터링에 필요"],"es":["Diseñado específicamente para flujos de trabajo de agentes de IA","Requiere CLI (tk) para la funcionalidad completa","Se necesita tabla web para la supervisión visual"],"fr":["Conçu spécifiquement pour les flux de travail d''agents IA","Nécessite CLI (tk) pour la fonctionnalité complète","Tableau web nécessaire pour la surveillance visuelle"],"de":["Speziell für AI-Agent-Workflows konzipiert","Benötigt CLI (tk) für die volle Funktionalität","Web-Tafel erforderlich für die visuelle Überwachung"],"pt":["Projetado especificamente para fluxos de trabalho de agentes de IA","Requer CLI (`tk`) para funcionalidade completa","Quadro web necessário para monitoramento visual"],"ru":["Разработан специально для рабочих процессов агентов ИИ","Требует CLI (`tk`) для полной функциональности","Веб-интерфейс необходим для визуального мониторинга"],"ar":["صُمّم خصيصًا لمسارات عمل وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","يتطلب CLI (`tk`) للوظائف الكاملة","لوحة ويب ضرورية للرصد المرئي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
