one: Produktmanagement-Framework","pt":"Jobs-to-be-Done: Framework para Gestão de Produto","ru":"Jobs-to-be-Done: Фреймворк для управления продуктом","ar":"jobs-to-be-done: إطار عمل لإدارة المنتج","en":"jobs-to-be-done"},"description":{"zh":"Jobs-to-be-Done 框架是一种产品管理技能框架，帮助开发者了解客户的功能性、社会性和情感性需求","ja":"Jobs-to-be-Done フレームワークは、開発者が顧客の機能的、社会的、感情的ニーズを理解するための製品管理スキル フレームワークです","ko":"Jobs-to-be-Done 프레임워크는 개발자가 고객의 기능적, 사회적, 감정적 요구를 이해하는 데 도움이 되는 제품 관리 스킬 프레임워크입니다","es":"El marco de habilidades de gestión de productos ''jobs-to-be-done'' es una estructura para entender las necesidades de los clientes y validar ideas de productos","fr":"Le cadre de compétences de gestion de produits ''jobs à accomplir'' est une structure pour comprendre les besoins des clients et valider les idées de produits","de":"Das Produktmanagement-Framework ''Jobs-to-be-done'' ist eine Struktur, um die Bedürfnisse der Kunden zu verstehen und Produktideen zu validieren","pt":"O framework Jobs-to-be-Done é uma estrutura de gestão de produto baseada em métodos testados para entender as necessidades dos clientes.","ru":"Фреймворк Jobs-to-be-Done - это структура управления продуктом, основанная на проверенных методах для понимания потребностей клиентов.","ar":"إطار عمل jobs-to-be-done هو هيكل لإدارة المنتج يعتمد على أساليب متقدمة لفهم احتياجات العملاء.","en":"Product Management skills framework built on battle-tested methods for Claude Code, Cowork, Codex, and AI agents."},"definition":{"en":"Product Management skills framework built on battle-tested methods for Claude Code, Cowork, Codex, and AI agents."},"features":{"zh":["系统地探索客户的功能性、社会性和情感性需求","了解客户的痛点和收益","验证产品创意和解决方案","确保解决方案满足实际动机","结构化的客户需求理解框架"],"ja":["顧客の機能的、社会的、感情的ニーズを体系的に探索する","顧客の痛みと利益を理解する","製品アイデアとソリューションを検証する","ソリューションが実際の動機を満たしていることを確認する","構造化された顧客ニーズ理解フレームワーク"],"ko":["고객의 기능적, 사회적, 감정적 요구를 체계적으로 탐색","고객의 고통과 이익을 이해","제품 아이디어와 솔루션을 검증","솔루션이 실제 동기를 충족하는지 확인","구조화된 고객 요구 이해 프레임워크"],"es":["Exploración sistemática de las necesidades de los clientes","Validación de ideas de productos","Identificación de necesidades no satisfechas","Análisis de las motivaciones de los clientes","Mejora de la experiencia del cliente"],"fr":["Exploration systématique des besoins des clients","Validation des idées de produits","Identification des besoins non satisfaits","Analyse des motivations des clients","Amélioration de l''expérience client"],"de":["Systematische Erforschung der Bedürfnisse der Kunden","Validierung von Produktideen","Identifizierung ungedeckter Bedürfnisse","Analyse der Motivationen der Kunden","Verbesserung der Kundenerfahrung"],"pt":["Entenda as necessidades funcionais, sociais e emocionais dos clientes","Identifique as dores e ganhos dos usuários","Desenvolva produtos que atendam às motivações reais dos usuários","Validação de ideias de produto","Análise de necessidades não atendidas"],"ru":["Понимайте функциональные, социальные и эмоциональные потребности клиентов","Определите боли и выгоды пользователей","Разрабатывайте продукты, отвечающие реальным мотивациям пользователей","Валидация идей продукта","Анализ неудовлетворенных потребностей"],"ar":["فهم الاحتياجات الوظيفية والاجتماعية والانفعالية للعملاء","تحديد آلام ومكاسب المستخدمين","قم بإنشاء منتجات تلبي التحفيزات الحقيقية للمستخدمين","تحقق من فكرة المنتج","تحليل الاحتياجات غير الملباة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Jobs-to-be-Done","产品管理技能","客户需求","产品创意","解决方案","功能性需求","社会性需求","情感性需求"],"ja":["Jobs-to-be-Done","製品管理スキル","顧客ニーズ","製品アイデア","ソリューション","機能的ニーズ","社会的ニーズ","感情的ニーズ"],"ko":["Jobs-to-be-Done","제품 관리 스킬","고객 요구","제품 아이디어","솔루션","기능적 요구","사회적 요구","감정적 요구"],"es":["gestión de productos","jobs-to-be-done","necesidades de los clientes","validación de ideas de productos","experiencia del cliente","análisis de motivaciones"],"fr":["gestion de produits","jobs à accomplir","besoins des clients","validation des idées de produits","expérience client","analyse des motivations"],"de":["Produktmanagement","Jobs-to-be-done","Bedürfnisse der Kunden","Validierung von Produktideen","Kundenerfahrung","Analyse der Motivationen"],"pt":["jobs-to-be-done","gestão de produto","necessidades dos clientes","motivações dos usuários","desenvolvimento de produtos","validação de ideias","análise de necessidades"],"ru":["jobs-to-be-done","управление продуктом","потребности клиентов","мотивации пользователей","разработка продуктов","валидация идей","анализ потребностей"],"ar":["jobs-to-be-done","إدارة المنتج","احتياجات العملاء","تحفيزات المستخدمين","تطوير المنتجات","تحقق من الفكرة","تحليل الاحتياجات"]}},"owner":"deanpeters","repo":"Product-Manager-Skills","repoPath":"deanpeters/Product-Manager-Skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"jobs-to-be-done","description":"Systematically explore what customers are trying to accomplish (functional, social, emotional jobs), the pains they experience, and the gains they seek. Use this framework to uncover unmet needs, vali","bodyPreview":"## Purpose\nSystematically explore what customers are trying to accomplish (functional, social, emotional jobs), the pains they experience, and the gains they seek. Use this framework to uncover unmet needs, validate product ideas, and ensure your solution addresses real motivations—not just surface-level feature requests.\n\nThis is not a survey—it''s a structured lens for understanding *why* customers \"hire\" your product and what would make them \"fire\" it.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### The Jobs-to-be-Done","body":"## Purpose\nSystematically explore what customers are trying to accomplish (functional, social, emotional jobs), the pains they experience, and the gains they seek. Use this framework to uncover unmet needs, validate product ideas, and ensure your solution addresses real motivations—not just surface-level feature requests.\n\nThis is not a survey—it''s a structured lens for understanding *why* customers \"hire\" your product and what would make them \"fire\" it.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### The Jobs-to-be-Done Framework\nInfluenced by Clayton Christensen and the Value Proposition Canvas (Osterwalder), JTBD breaks customer needs into three categories:\n\n**1. Customer Jobs:**\n- **Functional jobs:** Tasks customers need to perform (e.g., \"send an invoice\")\n- **Social jobs:** How customers want to be perceived (e.g., \"look professional to clients\")\n- **Emotional jobs:** Emotional states customers seek or avoid (e.g., \"feel confident in my work\")\n\n**2. Pains:**\n- **Challenges:** Obstacles customers face\n- **Costliness:** What''s too expensive in time, money, or effort\n- **Common mistakes:** Errors customers make that could be prevented\n- **Unresolved problems:** Gaps in current solutions\n\n**3. Gains:**\n- **Expectations:** What would exceed current solutions\n- **Savings:** Time, money, or effort reductions that delight\n- **Adoption factors:** What increases likelihood of switching\n- **Life improvement:** How a solution makes life easier or more enjoyable\n\n### Why This Structure Works\n- **Separates job from solution:** \"Communicate with my team\" (job) ≠ \"email\" (solution)\n- **Reveals underlying motivations:** Functional job may be \"track expenses,\" but emotional job is \"feel in control of finances\"\n- **Surfaces competition you didn''t see:** Customers \"hire\" non-obvious alternatives (pen and paper, spreadsheets, workarounds)\n- **Prioritizes by intensity:** Not all pains are equal—focus on the most acute\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What This Is NOT)\n- **Not a feature wishlist:** \"I want AI, automation, and dashboards\" is not a job\n- **Not demographics:** \"Millennials want mobile-first\" is a persona trait, not a job\n- **Not generic:** \"Be more productive\" is too vague—dig into *which* tasks and *why*\n- **Not one-dimensional:** Focusing only on functional jobs misses social/emotional motivations\n\n### When to Use This\n- Early-stage discovery (before you know the solution)\n- Validating product-market fit (does your solution address the right jobs?)\n- Prioritizing roadmap (which jobs are most painful/important?)\n- Competitive analysis (what are customers \"hiring\" competitors for?)\n- Marketing messaging (speak to jobs, not features)\n\n### When NOT to Use This\n- After you''ve already built the product (too late for discovery)\n- For trivial features (don''t over-analyze small tweaks)\n- As a substitute for quantitative validation (JTBD informs hypotheses; data validates them)\n\n---\n\n## Application\n\nUse `template.md` for the full fill-in structure.\n\n### Step 1: Define the Context\nBefore exploring JTBD, clarify:\n- **Target customer segment:** Who are you studying? (reference `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md`)\n- **Situation:** In what context does the job arise? (e.g., \"When managing a project deadline...\")\n- **Current solutions:** What do they use today? (competitors, workarounds, doing nothing)\n\n**If missing context:** Conduct customer interviews, contextual inquiries, or \"switch interviews\" (why they switched from a previous solution).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Explore Customer Jobs\n\n#### Functional Jobs\nAsk: \"What tasks are you trying to complete?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Functional Jobs:\n- [Task 1 customer needs to perform]\n- [Task 2 customer needs to perform]\n- [Task 3 customer needs to perform]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Reconcile monthly expenses for tax filing\"\n- \"Onboard a new team member in under 2 hours\"\n- \"Deploy code to production without downtime\"\n\n**Quality checks:**\n- **Verb-driven:** Jobs are actions (\"send,\" \"analyze,\" \"coordinate\")\n- **Solution-agnostic:** Don''t say \"use email to communicate\"—say \"communicate with remote teammates\"\n- **Specific:** \"Manage finances\" is too broad; \"Track business expenses for tax deductions\" is specific\n\n---\n\n#### Social Jobs\nAsk: \"How do you want to be perceived by others?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Social Jobs:\n- [Way customer wants to be perceived socially 1]\n- [Way customer wants to be perceived socially 2]\n- [Way customer wants to be perceived socially 3]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Be seen as a strategic thinker by my exec team\"\n- \"Appear responsive and reliable to clients\"\n- \"Look tech-savvy to my younger colleagues\"\n\n**Quality checks:**\n- **Audience-specific:** Who is the customer trying to impress? (boss, clients, peers, etc.)\n- **Emotional weight:** Social jobs often drive adoption more than functional jobs\n\n---\n\n#### Emotional Jobs\nAsk: \"What emotional state do you want to achieve or avoid?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Emotional Jobs:\n- [Emotional state customer seeks or avoids 1]\n- [Emotional state customer seeks or avoids 2]\n- [Emotional state customer seeks or avoids 3]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Feel confident I''m not missing important details\"\n- \"Avoid the anxiety of manual data entry errors\"\n- \"Feel a sense of accomplishment at the end of the day\"\n\n**Quality checks:**\n- **Positive and negative:** Include both what they seek (\"feel in control\") and what they avoid (\"avoid embarrassment\")\n- **Rooted in research:** Don''t fabricate emotions—use customer quotes\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Identify Pains\n\n#### Challenges\nAsk: \"What obstacles are preventing you from completing this job?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Challenges:\n- [Obstacle customer faces 1]\n- [Obstacle customer faces 2]\n- [Obstacle customer faces 3]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Tools don''t integrate, forcing manual data entry\"\n- \"No visibility into what teammates are working on\"\n- \"Approval processes take 3+ days, blocking progress\"\n\n---\n\n#### Costliness\nAsk: \"What takes too much time, money, or effort?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Costliness:\n- [What''s too costly in time, money, or effort 1]\n- [What''s too costly in time, money, or effort 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Generating monthly reports takes 8 hours of manual work\"\n- \"Hiring a specialist costs $10k, which we can''t afford\"\n- \"Learning the current tool requires 20+ hours of training\"\n\n---\n\n#### Common Mistakes\nAsk: \"What errors do you make frequently that could be prevented?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Common Mistakes:\n- [Frequent error 1]\n- [Frequent error 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Forgetting to CC stakeholders on critical emails\"\n- \"Miscalculating tax deductions due to missing receipts\"\n- \"Accidentally overwriting someone else''s work in shared files\"\n\n---\n\n#### Unresolved Problems\nAsk: \"What problems do current solutions fail to address?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Unresolved Problems:\n- [Problem not solved by current solutions 1]\n- [Problem not solved by current solutions 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Current CRM doesn''t track customer health scores\"\n- \"Email doesn''t preserve conversation context when people are added mid-thread\"\n- \"Existing tools require technical expertise we don''t have\"\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Uncover Gains\n\n#### Expectations\nAsk: \"What would make you love a solution?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Expectations:\n- [What could exceed expectations 1]\n- [What could exceed expectations 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Automatically categorizes expenses without manual tagging\"\n- \"Suggests next steps based on project status\"\n- \"Integrates seamlessly with tools we already use\"\n\n---\n\n#### Savings\nAsk: \"What savings in time, money, or effort would delight you?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Savings:\n- [Way of saving time, money, or effort 1]\n- [Way of saving time, money, or effort 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Reduce report generation from 8 hours to 10 minutes\"\n- \"Eliminate the need for a full-time admin\"\n- \"Cut onboarding time from 2 weeks to 2 days\"\n\n---\n\n#### Adoption Factors\nAsk: \"What would make you switch from your current solution?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Adoption Factors:\n- [Factor increasing likelihood of adoption 1]\n- [Factor increasing likelihood of adoption 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Free trial with no credit card required\"\n- \"Migration support to import existing data\"\n- \"Testimonials from companies like ours\"\n\n---\n\n#### Life Improvement\nAsk: \"How would your life be better if this job were easier?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Life Improvement:\n- [How solution makes life easier or more enjoyable 1]\n- [How solution makes life easier or more enjoyable 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"I could leave work on time instead of staying late to finish reports\"\n- \"I''d feel less stressed about missing important deadlines\"\n- \"I could focus on strategic work instead of busywork\"\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Prioritize and Validate\n\n- **Rank pains by intensity:** Which pains are acute vs. mild annoyances?\n- **Identify must-have vs. nice-to-have gains:** What would drive adoption vs. what''s just a bonus?\n- **Cross-reference with personas:** Do different personas have different jobs/pains/gains? (reference `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md`)\n- **Validate with data:** Survey a broader audience to confirm JTBD insights from interviews\n\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nSee `examples/sample.md` for full JTBD examples.\n\nMini example excerpt:\n\n```markdown\n**Functional Jobs:** Coordinate tasks across a distributed team\n**Pains - Challenges:** Team members use different tools, creating silos\n**Gains - Savings:** Reduce status reporting time from 3 hours to 15 minutes\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### Pitfall 1: Confusing Jobs with Solutions\n**Symptom:** \"I need to use Slack\" or \"I need AI-powered analytics\"\n\n**Consequence:** You''ve anchored on a solution, not the underlying job.\n\n**Fix:** Ask \"Why?\" 5 times. \"I need Slack\" → \"Why?\" → \"To communicate with my team\" → \"Why?\" → \"To get quick answers\" → \"Why?\" → \"To avoid project delays.\"\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 2: Generic Jobs\n**Symptom:** \"Be more productive\" or \"Save time\"\n\n**Consequence:** Too vague to inform product decisions.\n\n**Fix:** Get specific. \"Save time\" → \"Reduce time spent generating monthly reports from 8 hours to 1 hour.\"\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 3: Ignoring Social/Emotional Jobs\n**Symptom:** Only documenting functional jobs\n\n**Consequence:** You miss powerful motivators. People often buy based on emotional/social needs, not just functional.\n\n**Fix:** Explicitly ask about perception and emotions in interviews. \"How would solving this make you feel?\" \"Who would notice if you solved this?\"\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 4: Fabricating JTBD Without Research\n**Symptom:** Filling out the template based on assumptions\n\n**Consequence:** You''re guessing. JTBD analysis is only valuable if grounded in real customer insights.\n\n**Fix:** Conduct \"switch interviews\" (ask why they switched from a previous solution), contextual inquiries, or problem validation interviews.\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 5: Treating All Pains as Equal\n**Symptom:** Listing 20 pains without prioritization\n\n**Consequence:** No clarity on what to solve first.\n\n**Fix:** Rank pains by intensity (acute vs. mild). Ask \"If we only solved one pain, which would have the biggest impact?\"\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n### Related Skills\n- `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md` — Defines who has these jobs/pains/gains\n- `skills/problem-statement/SKILL.md` — JTBD informs the \"Trying to\" and \"But\" sections\n- `skills/positioning-statement/SKILL.md` — JTBD informs the \"that need\" statement\n\n### External Frameworks\n- Clayton Christensen, *Competing Against Luck* (2016) — Origin of Jobs-to-be-Done theory\n- Tony Ulwick, *Outcome-Driven Innovation* (2016) — Quantifying jobs and outcomes\n- Alexander Osterwalder, *Value Proposition Canvas* (2014) — Customer jobs/pains/gains framework\n\n### Dean''s Work\n- [Link to relevant Dean Peters'' Substack articles if applicable]\n\n### Provenance\n- Adapted from `prompts/jobs-to-be-done.md` in the `https://github.com/deanpeters/product-manager-prompts` repo.\n\n---\n\n**Skill type:** Component\n**Suggested filename:** `jobs-to-be-done.md`\n**Suggested placement:** `/skills/components/`\n**Dependencies:** References `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md`\n**Used by:** `skills/positioning-statement/SKILL.md`, `skills/problem-statement/SKILL.md`, `skills/epic-hypothesis/SKILL.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:15:46.656Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Product Management Agents seeking to understand customer motivations and unmet needs through jobs-to-be-done analysis.","zh":"适合产品管理代理寻求通过任务分析理解客户动机和未满足需求。","ja":"プロダクトマネジメントエージェントがジョブズトゥービーダン分析を通じて顧客の動機と未満足のニーズを理解しようとする場合に最適です。","ko":"제품 관리 에이전트가 작업을 통해 고객의 동기와 미충족 된 nhu cầu를 이해하려고 하는 경우 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de gestión de productos que buscan comprender las motivaciones y necesidades insatisfechas de los clientes a través del análisis de trabajos por hacer.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de gestion de produits cherchant à comprendre les motivations et les besoins non satisfaits des clients grâce à l''analyse des tâches à accomplir.","de":"Ideal für Product Management Agents, die die Motivationen und unerfüllten Bedürfnisse von Kunden durch die Analyse der Aufgaben verstehen möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gestão de Produtos que buscam compreender as motivações e necessidades não atendidas dos clientes por meio da análise de trabalhos a serem feitos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления продуктами, стремящихся понять мотивацию и неудовлетворенные потребности клиентов посредством анализа работ, которые необходимо выполнить.","ar":"مثالي لوفاء إدارة المنتجات الذين يرغبون في فهم دوافع العملاء والاحتياجات غير الملبية من خلال تحليل الوظائف التي يجب القيام بها."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically explore customer jobs, pains, and gains, ensuring solutions address real motivations and not just surface-level feature requests, utilizing battle-tested methods for Claude Code, Cowork, Codex, and other AI agents.","zh":"赋予代理系统地探索客户的工作、痛点和收益，确保解决方案能够解决真正的动机，而不仅仅是表面层面的功能请求，利用Claude Code、Cowork、Codex和其他AI代理的经过验证的方法。","ja":"エージェントは、クライアントのジョブ、ペイン、ゲインを体系的に調査し、ソリューションが表面的な機能リクエストではなく、実際の動機に対処することを保証する。Claude Code、Cowork、Codex、その他のAIエージェントの戦闘テスト済みの方法を使用します。","ko":"에이전트는 고객의 작업, 고통, 이익을 체계적으로 조사하여 솔루션이 단순한 기능 요청이 아닌 실제 동기를 해결하도록 보장합니다. Claude Code, Cowork, Codex 및 기타 AI 에이전트의 검증된 방법을 사용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes explorar sistemáticamente los trabajos, dolores y beneficios de los clientes, asegurando que las soluciones aborden las motivaciones reales y no solo las solicitudes de características de nivel superficial, utilizando métodos probados en batalla para Claude Code, Cowork, Codex y otros agentes de inteligencia artificial.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''explorer systématiquement les tâches, les douleurs et les avantages des clients, en veillant à ce que les solutions répondent aux motivations réelles et non seulement aux demandes de fonctionnalités de niveau superficiel, en utilisant des méthodes éprouvées pour Claude Code, Cowork, Codex et d''autres agents d''intelligence artificielle.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Kundenarbeiten, Schmerzen und Gewinne systematisch zu erforschen, um sicherzustellen, dass die Lösungen die realen Motivationen und nicht nur die oberflächlichen Funktionsanforderungen ansprechen, unter Verwendung von erprobten Methoden für Claude Code, Cowork, Codex und andere KI-Agents.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a explorar sistematicamente os trabalhos, dores e ganhos dos clientes, garantindo que as soluções abordem as motivações reais e não apenas solicitações de recursos de nível superficial, utilizando métodos testados em batalha para Claude Code, Cowork, Codex e outros agentes de IA.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически исследовать работы, боли и выгоды клиентов, гарантируя, что решения решают реальные мотивации, а не только поверхностные запросы функций, используя методы, проверенные в бою, для Claude Code, Cowork, Codex и других агентов ИИ.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من استكشاف الوظائف والألم والفوائد الخاصة بالعملاء بطريقة منهجية، مما يضمن أن الحلول تتصدى للدوافع الحقيقية وليس فقط لطلبات الميزات السطحية، باستخدام أساليب مُختبرة في معارك حقيقية من أجل Claude Code و Cowork و Codex ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الآخرين."},"useCases":{"en":["Uncovering unmet customer needs through jobs-to-be-done frameworks","Validating product ideas against real customer motivations","Analyzing customer pains and gains to inform product development"],"zh":["通过任务分析框架揭示未满足的客户需求","验证产品创意是否符合实际客户动机","分析客户的痛点和收益以指导产品开发"],"ja":["ジョブズトゥービーダン分析フレームワークを通じて未満足の顧客ニーズを明らかにする","実際の顧客動機に対する製品アイデアの検証","顧客のペインとゲインを分析して製品開発に役立てる"],"ko":["작업을 통해 미충족 된 고객 nhu cầu를 발견하는 것","실제 고객 동기에 대한 제품 아이디어의 검증","고객의 고통과 이익을 분석하여 제품 개발에 정보를 제공하는 것"],"es":["Descubrir necesidades insatisfechas de los clientes a través de marcos de trabajo por hacer","Validar ideas de productos frente a motivaciones reales de los clientes","Analizar dolores y beneficios de los clientes para informar el desarrollo de productos"],"fr":["Découvrir les besoins non satisfaits des clients grâce à des cadres de tâches à accomplir","Valider les idées de produits face aux motivations réelles des clients","Analyser les douleurs et les avantages des clients pour éclairer le développement de produits"],"de":["Unerfüllte Kundenbedürfnisse durch Aufgabenframeworks aufdecken","Produktideen anhand realer Kundenmotivationen validieren","Kundenschmerzen und -gewinne analysieren, um die Produktentwicklung zu unterstützen"],"pt":["Descobrir necessidades não atendidas dos clientes por meio de estruturas de trabalhos a serem feitos","Validar ideias de produto contra motivações reais dos clientes","Analisar dores e ganhos dos clientes para informar o desenvolvimento de produtos"],"ru":["Раскрытие неудовлетворенных потребностей клиентов посредством рамок работ, которые необходимо выполнить","Проверка идей продукта на соответствие реальным мотивациям клиентов","Анализ болей и выгод клиентов для информирования разработки продукта"],"ar":["كشف الاحتياجات غير الملبئة للعملاء من خلال إطارات الوظائف التي يجب القيام بها","تحقق من أفكار المنتج مقابل دوافع العملاء الحقيقية","تحليل آلام وفوائد العملاء لتزويد تطوير المنتج بالمعلومات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of customer needs and motivations","May not be suitable for surface-level feature request analysis"],"zh":["需要了解客户的需求和动机","可能不适合表面层面的功能请求分析"],"ja":["顧客のニーズと動機の理解が必要","表面的な機能リクエストの分析には不向き"],"ko":["고객의 nhu cầu와 동기의 이해가 필요합니다","표면적인 기능 요청 분석에는 적합하지 않을 수 있습니다"],"es":["Requiere una comprensión de las necesidades y motivaciones de los clientes","Puede que no sea adecuado para el análisis de solicitudes de características de nivel superficial"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des besoins et des motivations des clients","Peut ne pas être adapté à l''analyse des demandes de fonctionnalités de niveau superficiel"],"de":["Benötigt ein Verständnis der Kundenbedürfnisse und -motivationen","Kann für die Analyse von oberflächlichen Funktionsanforderungen nicht geeignet sein"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das necessidades e motivações dos clientes","Pode não ser adequado para análise de solicitações de recursos de nível superficial"],"ru":["Требует понимания потребностей и мотиваций клиентов","Может быть не подходящим для анализа поверхностных запросов функций"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا للاحتياجات والدوافع الخاصة بالعملاء","قد لا يكون مناسبًا لتحليل طلبات الميزات السطحية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('EthanAlgoX/MarketBot/ordercli', 'community', 'EthanAlgoX', 'MarketBot', 'EthanAlgoX/MarketBot', 'ordercli', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z', '2026-02-18T13:15:45.296Z', NULL, '{"id":"EthanAlgoX/MarketBot/ordercli","name":"ordercli","description":{"zh":"ordercli是一个命令行工具，用于检查过去的订单和跟踪Foodora的活跃订单状态","ja":"ordercliは、過去の注文を確認し、Foodoraのアクティブな注文のステータスを追跡するためのコマンドラインツールです","ko":"ordercli는 과거의 주문을 확인하고 Foodora의 활성 주문 상태를 추적하는 명령줄 도구입니다","es":"Ordercli es una herramienta de línea de comandos para verificar pedidos pasados y rastrear el estado de los pedidos activos en Foodora.","fr":"Ordercli est un outil de ligne de commande pour vérifier les commandes passées et suivre l''état des commandes actives sur Foodora.","de":"Ordercli ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool, um vergangene Bestellungen zu überprüfen und den Status aktiver Bestellungen in Foodora zu verfolgen.","pt":"O ordercli é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para análise de pedidos e rastreamento de status de pedidos na Foodora","ru":"ordercli — это инструмент командной строки для анализа заказов и отслеживания статуса заказов в Foodora","ar":"أمر(cli) هو أداة سطر الأوامر لتحليل الطلبات وتتبع حالة الطلبات في Foodora","en":"MarketBot is a finance-customized version of openclaw, built as a dedicated AI agent for market intelligence, trading analysis, and decision support."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"ordercli命令行工具","ja":"ordercliコマンドラインツール","ko":"ordercli 명령줄 도구","es":"ordercli: Herramienta de seguimiento de pedidos","fr":"ordercli : Outil de suivi des commandes","de":"ordercli: Bestellverfolgungstool","pt":"ordercli: Ferramenta de Análise de Pedidos","ru":"ordercli: Инструмент анализа заказов","ar":"أمر(cli): أداة تحليل الطلبات","en":"ordercli"},"description":{"zh":"ordercli是一个命令行工具，用于检查过去的订单和跟踪Foodora的活跃订单状态","ja":"ordercliは、過去の注文を確認し、Foodoraのアクティブな注文のステータスを追跡するためのコマンドラインツールです","ko":"ordercli는 과거의 주문을 확인하고 Foodora의 활성 주문 상태를 추적하는 명령줄 도구입니다","es":"Ordercli es una herramienta de línea de comandos para verificar pedidos pasados y rastrear el estado de los pedidos activos en Foodora.","fr":"Ordercli est un outil de ligne de commande pour vérifier les commandes passées et suivre l''état des commandes actives sur Foodora.","de":"Ordercli ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool, um vergangene Bestellungen zu überprüfen und den Status aktiver Bestellungen in Foodora zu verfolgen.","pt":"O ordercli é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para análise de pedidos e rastreamento de status de pedidos na Foodora","ru":"ordercli — это инструмент командной строки для анализа заказов и отслеживания статуса заказов в Foodora","ar":"أمر(cli) هو أداة سطر الأوامر لتحليل الطلبات وتتبع حالة الطلبات في Foodora","en":"MarketBot is a finance-customized version of openclaw, built as a dedicated AI agent for market intelligence, trading analysis, and decision support."},"definition":{"en":"MarketBot is a finance-customized version of openclaw, built as a dedicated AI agent for market intelligence, trading analysis, and decision support."},"features":{"zh":["检查过去的订单","跟踪Foodora的活跃订单状态","支持快速启动和配置","提供订单历史记录和详细信息"],"ja":["過去の注文を確認する","Foodoraのアクティブな注文のステータスを追跡する","クイックスタートと設定をサポートする","注文履歴と詳細を提供する"],"ko":["과거의 주문을 확인한다","Foodora의 활성 주문 상태를 추적한다","빠른 시작 및 구성 지원","주문 기록 및 세부 정보 제공"],"es":["Verificación de pedidos pasados","Seguimiento del estado de los pedidos activos","Compatibilidad con Foodora","Opción de ver el historial de pedidos","Opción de establecer un límite para el historial de pedidos","Opción de visualizar el detalle de un pedido"],"fr":["Vérification des commandes passées","Suivi de l''état des commandes actives","Compatibilité avec Foodora","Option d''afficher l''historique des commandes","Option de définir une limite pour l''historique des commandes","Option d''afficher les détails d''une commande"],"de":["Überprüfung vergangener Bestellungen","Verfolgung des Status aktiver Bestellungen","Kompatibilität mit Foodora","Option zum Anzeigen des Bestellverlaufs","Option zum Festlegen einer Grenze für den Bestellverlauf","Option zum Anzeigen der Details einer Bestellung"],"pt":["Rastrear pedidos ativos","Verificar status de pedidos passados","Suporte à Foodora","Interface de linha de comando","Opção de assistir pedidos","Filtrar pedidos por limite"],"ru":["Отслеживать активные заказы","Проверять статус прошлых заказов","Поддержка Foodora","Интерфейс командной строки","Возможность наблюдать за заказами","Фильтровать заказы по лимиту"],"ar":["تتبع الطلبات النشطة","التحقق من حالة الطلبات السابقة","دعم Foodora","واجهة سطر الأوامر","خيار مشاهدة الطلبات","filtrar الطلبات حسب الحد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["ordercli","命令行工具","订单跟踪","Foodora","快速启动","配置设置"],"ja":["ordercli","コマンドラインツール","注文追跡","Foodora","クイックスタート","設定"],"ko":["ordercli","명령줄 도구","주문 추적","Foodora","빠른 시작","구성 설정"],"es":["ordercli","seguimiento de pedidos","estado de pedidos","Foodora","herramienta de línea de comandos","inteligencia de mercado","análisis de trading","decisión de trading","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["ordercli","suivi des commandes","état des commandes","Foodora","outil de ligne de commande","intelligence de marché","analyse de trading","décision de trading","développement de logiciels"],"de":["ordercli","Bestellverfolgung","Bestellstatus","Foodora","Kommandozeilen-Tool","Marktintelligenz","Trading-Analyse","Entscheidungsfindung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["ordercli","análise de pedidos","rastreamento de pedidos","Foodora","ferramenta de linha de comando","gerenciamento de pedidos","desenvolvimento de software","tecnologia de informação"],"ru":["ordercli","анализ заказов","отслеживание заказов","Foodora","инструмент командной строки","управление заказами","разработка программного обеспечения","информационные технологии"],"ar":["أمر(cli)","تحليل الطلبات","تتبع الطلبات","Foodora","أداة سطر الأوامر","إدارة الطلبات","تطوير البرمجيات","تكنولوجيا المعلومات"]}},"owner":"EthanAlgoX","repo":"MarketBot","repoPath":"EthanAlgoX/MarketBot","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ordercli","description":"Foodora-only CLI for checking past orders and active order status (Deliveroo WIP).","bodyPreview":"# ordercli\n\nUse `ordercli` to check past orders and track active order status (Foodora only right now).\n\nQuick start (Foodora)\n- `ordercli foodora countries`\n- `ordercli foodora config set --country AT`\n- `ordercli foodora login --email you@example.com --password-stdin`\n- `ordercli foodora orders`\n- `ordercli foodora history --limit 20`\n- `ordercli foodora history show <orderCode>`\n\nOrders\n- Active list (arrival/status): `ordercli foodora orders`\n- Watch: `ordercli foodora orders --watch`\n- Acti","body":"# ordercli\n\nUse `ordercli` to check past orders and track active order status (Foodora only right now).\n\nQuick start (Foodora)\n- `ordercli foodora countries`\n- `ordercli foodora config set --country AT`\n- `ordercli foodora login --email you@example.com --password-stdin`\n- `ordercli foodora orders`\n- `ordercli foodora history --limit 20`\n- `ordercli foodora history show <orderCode>`\n\nOrders\n- Active list (arrival/status): `ordercli foodora orders`\n- Watch: `ordercli foodora orders --watch`\n- Active order detail: `ordercli foodora order <orderCode>`\n- History detail JSON: `ordercli foodora history show <orderCode> --json`\n\nReorder (adds to cart)\n- Preview: `ordercli foodora reorder <orderCode>`\n- Confirm: `ordercli foodora reorder <orderCode> --confirm`\n- Address: `ordercli foodora reorder <orderCode> --confirm --address-id <id>`\n\nCloudflare / bot protection\n- Browser login: `ordercli foodora login --email you@example.com --password-stdin --browser`\n- Reuse profile: `--browser-profile \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/ordercli/browser-profile\"`\n- Import Chrome cookies: `ordercli foodora cookies chrome --profile \"Default\"`\n\nSession import (no password)\n- `ordercli foodora session chrome --url https://www.foodora.at/ --profile \"Default\"`\n- `ordercli foodora session refresh --client-id android`\n\nDeliveroo (WIP, not working yet)\n- Requires `DELIVEROO_BEARER_TOKEN` (optional `DELIVEROO_COOKIE`).\n- `ordercli deliveroo config set --market uk`\n- `ordercli deliveroo history`\n\nNotes\n- Use `--config /tmp/ordercli.json` for testing.\n- Confirm before any reorder or cart-changing action.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:15:45.296Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Finance Analysis Agents requiring order tracking and status updates via command-line interfaces like ordercli","zh":"適合需要通過命令行界面（如ordercli）進行訂單跟蹤和狀態更新的金融分析代理","ja":"金融分析エージェント向けに、ordercliなどのコマンドラインインターフェイスを使用してオーダーの追跡とステータス更新を行うには最適","ko":"주문 추적 및 상태 업데이트를 명령줄 인터페이스(예: ordercli)를 통해 수행해야 하는 금융 분석 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis Financiero que requieren seguimiento de pedidos y actualizaciones de estado a través de interfaces de línea de comandos como ordercli","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse financière nécessitant un suivi de commande et des mises à jour de statut via des interfaces de ligne de commande comme ordercli","de":"Ideal für Finanzanalyse-Agents, die eine Orderverfolgung und Statusupdates über Kommandozeilen-Oberflächen wie ordercli benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise Financeira que exigem acompanhamento de pedidos e atualizações de status via interfaces de linha de comando como ordercli","ru":"Идеально для финансовых аналитических агентов, требующих отслеживания заказов и обновления статуса через командные интерфейсы, такие как ordercli","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل المالية التي تتطلب تتبع الطلبات وتحديث الحالة عبر واجهات سطر الأوامر مثل ordercli"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to track active order status and check past orders using protocols like stdin for password input, and provides country-specific configuration settings for platforms such as Foodora, utilizing command-line arguments for efficient data retrieval","zh":"啟用代理跟蹤活動訂單狀態和檢查過去訂單，使用stdin等協議進行密碼輸入，並為Foodora等平台提供國家特定的配置設定，以命令行引數實現高效的數據檢索","ja":"エージェントがアクティブなオーダーのステータスを追跡し、過去のオーダーを確認することを可能にし、stdinなどのプロトコルを使用してパスワード入力を行い、Foodoraなどのプラットフォーム向けに国別の設定を提供し、コマンドライン引数を使用して効率的なデータ取得を実現する","ko":"에이전트가 활동 주문 상태를 추적하고 과거 주문을 확인할 수 있도록 하며, stdin과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 비밀번호 입력을 수행하고, Foodora와 같은 플랫폼을 위한 국가별 설정을 제공하며, 명령줄 인수를 사용하여 효율적인 데이터 검색을 구현","es":"Habilita a los agentes para rastrear el estado de los pedidos activos y verificar los pedidos pasados utilizando protocolos como stdin para la entrada de contraseñas, y proporciona configuraciones de ajustes específicos de país para plataformas como Foodora, utilizando argumentos de línea de comandos para una recuperación eficiente de datos","fr":"Permet aux agents de suivre l''état des commandes actives et de vérifier les commandes passées en utilisant des protocoles tels que stdin pour la saisie de mots de passe, et fournit des paramètres de configuration spécifiques au pays pour les plates-formes telles que Foodora, en utilisant des arguments de ligne de commande pour une récupération efficace des données","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, den Status von aktiven Bestellungen zu verfolgen und vergangene Bestellungen zu überprüfen, indem Protokolle wie stdin für die Passworteingabe verwendet werden, und bietet länderspezifische Konfigurationseinstellungen für Plattformen wie Foodora, wobei Kommandozeilenargumente für eine effiziente Datenerfassung verwendet werden","pt":"Permite que os agentes acompanhem o status de pedidos ativos e verifiquem pedidos anteriores usando protocolos como stdin para entrada de senha e fornece configurações de configuração específicas do país para plataformas como Foodora, utilizando argumentos de linha de comando para recuperação eficiente de dados","ru":"Позволяет агентам отслеживать статус активных заказов и проверять прошлые заказы, используя протоколы, такие как stdin для ввода пароля, и предоставляет настройки конфигурации, специфичные для страны, для платформ, таких как Foodora, с использованием аргументов командной строки для эффективного извлечения данных","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تتبع حالة الطلبات النشطة والتحقق من الطلبات السابقة باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل stdin لإدخال كلمة المرور وتوفر إعدادات تكوين محددة للبلد منصات مثل Foodora، مع استخدام حجة سطر الأوامر لاسترجاع البيانات بكفاءة"},"useCases":{"en":["Tracking active orders with real-time status updates","Retrieving order history with specific limit parameters","Configuring country settings for Foodora order analysis"],"zh":["跟蹤活動訂單的實時狀態更新","檢索具有特定限制參數的訂單歷史","配置Foodora訂單分析的國家設置"],"ja":["アクティブなオーダーのリアルタイムステータス更新を追跡する","特定の制限パラメータを持つオーダーヒストリを取得する","Foodoraのオーダー分析の国設定を構成する"],"ko":["활동 주문에 대한 실시간 상태 업데이트를 추적","특정 제한 매개 변수가 있는 주문 기록을 검색","Foodora 주문 분석을 위한 국가 설정을 구성"],"es":["Seguimiento de pedidos activos con actualizaciones de estado en tiempo real","Recuperación del historial de pedidos con parámetros de límite específicos","Configuración de ajustes de país para el análisis de pedidos de Foodora"],"fr":["Suivi des commandes actives avec des mises à jour de statut en temps réel","Récupération de l''historique des commandes avec des paramètres de limite spécifiques","Configuration des paramètres de pays pour l''analyse des commandes Foodora"],"de":["Verfolgung von aktiven Bestellungen mit Echtzeit-Statusupdates","Abruf des Bestellverlaufs mit spezifischen Limitparametern","Konfiguration von Ländereinstellungen für die Bestellanalyse von Foodora"],"pt":["Acompanhar pedidos ativos com atualizações de status em tempo real","Recuperar histórico de pedidos com parâmetros de limite específicos","Configurar configurações de país para análise de pedidos Foodora"],"ru":["Отслеживать активные заказы с обновлениями статуса в режиме реального времени","Извлекать историю заказов с конкретными параметрами ограничения","Настроить настройки страны для анализа заказов Foodora"],"ar":["تتبع الطلبات النشطة مع تحديثات الحالة في الوقت الفعلي","استرجاع تاريخ الطلبات مع معلمات حد محددة","تكوين إعدادات البلد لتحليل الطلبات في Foodora"]},"limitations":{"en":["Currently supports Foodora only","Requires email and password for login authentication","Dependent on command-line interface for user interaction"],"zh":["目前僅支持Foodora","需要電子郵件和密碼進行登錄身份驗證","依賴於命令行界面進行用戶交互"],"ja":["現在はFoodoraのみをサポート","ログイン認証にはメールアドレスとパスワードが必要","ユーザーインタラクションにはコマンドラインインターフェイスに依存"],"ko":["현재 Foodora만 지원","로그인 인증에는 이메일과 비밀번호가 필요","사용자 상호 작용에는 명령줄 인터페이스에 의존"],"es":["Actualmente solo admite Foodora","Requiere correo electrónico y contraseña para la autenticación de inicio de sesión","Depende de la interfaz de línea de comandos para la interacción del usuario"],"fr":["Prend actuellement en charge uniquement Foodora","Nécessite un e-mail et un mot de passe pour l''authentification de connexion","Dépend de l''interface de ligne de commande pour l''interaction utilisateur"],"de":["Unterstützt derzeit nur Foodora","Benötigt E-Mail-Adresse und Passwort für die Anmeldeauthentifizierung","Ist von der Kommandozeilen-Oberfläche für die Benutzerinteraktion abhängig"],"pt":["Até o momento, suporta apenas Foodora","Exige e-mail e senha para autenticação de login","Depende da interface de linha de comando para interação do usuário"],"ru":["На данный момент поддерживает только Foodora","Требует электронной почты и пароля для аутентификации входа","Зависит от командного интерфейса для взаимодействия с пользователем"],"ar":["يدعم حاليًا فقط منصة Foodora","يتطلب البريد الإلكتروني وكلمة المرور للتحقق من حساب المستخدم","يعتمد على واجهة سطر الأوامر للتفاعل مع المستخدم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('PaulRBerg/agent-skills/bump-deps', 'community', 'PaulRBerg', 'agent-skills', 'PaulRBerg/agent-skills', 'bump-deps', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z', '2026-02-18T13:16:00.782Z', NULL, '{"id":"PaulRBerg/agent-skills/bump-deps","name":"bump-deps","description":{"zh":"bump-deps 技能使用 taze CLI 智能更新 Node.js 依赖，支持自动应用 MINOR/PATCH 更新和个别 MAJOR 更新","ja":"bump-deps スキルは、taze CLI を使用して Node.js 依存関係をスマートに更新します","ko":"bump-deps 스킬은 taze CLI를 사용하여 Node.js 의존성을智能으로 업데이트 합니다","es":"Bump-deps es una habilidad de agente que actualiza dependencias de Node.js usando taze CLI con promoción inteligente","fr":"Bump-deps est une compétence d''agent qui met à jour les dépendances Node.js en utilisant taze CLI avec une promotion intelligente","de":"Bump-deps ist eine Agentenfähigkeit, die Abhängigkeiten von Node.js mithilfe von taze CLI mit intelligenter Förderung aktualisiert","pt":"O skill bump-deps atualiza dependências Node.js usando Taze CLI com prompts inteligentes. Ele aplica atualizações MINOR/PATCH automaticamente e solicita confirmação para atualizações MAJOR.","ru":"Умение bump-deps обновляет зависимости Node.js с помощью Taze CLI и интеллектуальными подсказками. Он автоматически применяет обновления MINOR/PATCH и запрашивает подтверждение для обновлений MAJOR.","ar":"المهارة bump-deps تحديث الإعتماديات Node.js باستخدام Taze CLI وتنبيهات ذكية. أنها تطبق تحديثات MINOR/PATCH تلقائيًا وتطلب تأكيدًا لتحديثات MAJOR.","en":"PRB''s collection of agent skills"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"bump-deps 技能：智能更新 Node.js 依赖","ja":"bump-deps スキル：Node.js 依存関係のスマート更新","ko":"bump-deps 스킬: Node.js 의존성智能 업데이트","es":"Actualiza dependencias con bump-deps","fr":"Mettre à jour les dépendances avec bump-deps","de":"Aktualisieren Sie Abhängigkeiten mit bump-deps","pt":"Bump Deps: Atualize Dependências Node.js com Taze CLI","ru":"Bump Deps: Обновите з