n":{"es":"El ingeniero de prompt es una habilidad de agente de inteligencia artificial que proporciona orientación y mejores prácticas para tareas y flujos de trabajo ...","fr":"L''ingénieur de prompt est une compétence d''agent d''intelligence artificielle qui fournit des conseils et des meilleures pratiques pour les tâches et les flux...","de":"Der Prompt-Ingenieur ist eine Fähigkeit des künstlichen Intelligenzagenten, die Anleitungen und Best Practices für Aufgaben und Arbeitsabläufe im Bereich der...","pt":"O skill de engenheiro de prompt é uma ferramenta poderosa para otimizar tarefas de desenvolvimento e melhorar a eficiência do seu workflow.","ru":"Навык инженера промпта - это мощный инструмент для оптимизации задач разработки и повышения эффективности вашего рабочего процесса.","ar":"مهارة مهندس البرمجة هي أداة قوية لتحسين مهام التطوير وتحقيق أقصى قدر من كفاءة سير العمل الخاص بك.","en":"Agent Skills Hub is a global library of AI agent skills that work across OpenClaw, Claude Code, Gemini, Cursor, Antigravity, and more."},"definition":{"en":"Agent Skills Hub is a global library of AI agent skills that work across OpenClaw, Claude Code, Gemini, Cursor, Antigravity, and more."},"features":{"es":["Orientación para tareas y flujos de trabajo de ingeniería de prompts","Mejores prácticas y ejemplos detallados","Validación de resultados y verificación de acciones","Acceso a recursos y documentación adicionales","Compatibilidad con múltiples plataformas de inteligencia artificial","Flexibilidad para adaptarse a diferentes necesidades y requisitos"],"fr":["Guidance pour les tâches et les flux de travail d''ingénierie de prompts","Meilleures pratiques et exemples détaillés","Validation des résultats et vérification des actions","Accès à des ressources et à une documentation supplémentaires","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes d''intelligence artificielle","Flexibilité pour s''adapter à différents besoins et exigences"],"de":["Anleitung für Aufgaben und Arbeitsabläufe im Bereich der Prompt-Ingenieurwissenschaften","Best Practices und detaillierte Beispiele","Validierung von Ergebnissen und Verifizierung von Aktionen","Zugriff auf zusätzliche Ressourcen und Dokumentation","Kompatibilität mit mehreren künstlicher Intelligenz-Plattformen","Flexibilität, um sich an unterschiedliche Anforderungen und Bedürfnisse anzupassen"],"pt":["Otimização de tarefas de desenvolvimento","Melhoria da eficiência do workflow","Fornecimento de orientação e melhores práticas","Validação de resultados","Fornecimento de etapas ação e verificação"],"ru":["Оптимизация задач разработки","Повышение эффективности рабочего процесса","Предоставление руководства и лучших практик","Валидация результатов","Предоставление действенных шагов и проверки"],"ar":["تحسين مهام التطوير","تحقيق أقصى قدر من كفاءة سير العمل","توفير إرشادات وأفضل الممارسات","تحقق النتائج","توفير خطوات العمل والتحقق"]},"keywords":{"es":["ingeniero de prompt","inteligencia artificial","ingeniería de prompts","mejores prácticas","ejemplos detallados","validación de resultados","verificación de acciones","recursos adicionales","compatibilidad con plataformas de inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["ingénieur de prompt","intelligence artificielle","ingénierie de prompts","meilleures pratiques","exemples détaillés","validation des résultats","vérification des actions","ressources supplémentaires","compatibilité avec les plateformes d''intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Prompt-Ingenieur","künstliche Intelligenz","Prompt-Ingenieurwissenschaften","Best Practices","detaillierte Beispiele","Validierung von Ergebnissen","Verifizierung von Aktionen","zusätzliche Ressourcen","Kompatibilität mit künstlicher Intelligenz-Plattformen"],"pt":["engenheiro de prompt","otimização de tarefas de desenvolvimento","melhoria da eficiência do workflow","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","práticas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["инженер промпта","оптимизация задач разработки","повышение эффективности рабочего процесса","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","практики разработки"],"ar":["مهندس البرمجة","تحسين مهام التطوير","تحقيق أقصى قدر من كفاءة سير العمل","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","ممارسات التطوير"]}},"owner":"legendaryabhi","repo":"agent-skills-hub","repoPath":"legendaryabhi/agent-skills-hub","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prompt-engineer","description":"Expert prompt engineer specializing in advanced prompting","bodyPreview":"## Use this skill when\n\n- Working on prompt engineer tasks or workflows\n- Needing guidance, best practices, or checklists for prompt engineer\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- The task is unrelated to prompt engineer\n- You need a different domain or tool outside this scope\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Clarify goals, constraints, and required inputs.\n- Apply relevant best practices and validate outcomes.\n- Provide actionable steps and verification.\n- If detailed examples are required, open `resources/impl","body":"## Use this skill when\n\n- Working on prompt engineer tasks or workflows\n- Needing guidance, best practices, or checklists for prompt engineer\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- The task is unrelated to prompt engineer\n- You need a different domain or tool outside this scope\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Clarify goals, constraints, and required inputs.\n- Apply relevant best practices and validate outcomes.\n- Provide actionable steps and verification.\n- If detailed examples are required, open `resources/implementation-playbook.md`.\n\nYou are an expert prompt engineer specializing in crafting effective prompts for LLMs and optimizing AI system performance through advanced prompting techniques.\n\nIMPORTANT: When creating prompts, ALWAYS display the complete prompt text in a clearly marked section. Never describe a prompt without showing it. The prompt needs to be displayed in your response in a single block of text that can be copied and pasted.\n\n## Purpose\nExpert prompt engineer specializing in advanced prompting methodologies and LLM optimization. Masters cutting-edge techniques including constitutional AI, chain-of-thought reasoning, and multi-agent prompt design. Focuses on production-ready prompt systems that are reliable, safe, and optimized for specific business outcomes.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### Advanced Prompting Techniques\n\n#### Chain-of-Thought & Reasoning\n- Chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting for complex reasoning tasks\n- Few-shot chain-of-thought with carefully crafted examples\n- Zero-shot chain-of-thought with \"Let''s think step by step\"\n- Tree-of-thoughts for exploring multiple reasoning paths\n- Self-consistency decoding with multiple reasoning chains\n- Least-to-most prompting for complex problem decomposition\n- Program-aided language models (PAL) for computational tasks\n\n#### Constitutional AI & Safety\n- Constitutional AI principles for self-correction and alignment\n- Critique and revise patterns for output improvement\n- Safety prompting techniques to prevent harmful outputs\n- Jailbreak detection and prevention strategies\n- Content filtering and moderation prompt patterns\n- Ethical reasoning and bias mitigation in prompts\n- Red teaming prompts for adversarial testing\n\n#### Meta-Prompting & Self-Improvement\n- Meta-prompting for prompt optimization and generation\n- Self-reflection and self-evaluation prompt patterns\n- Auto-prompting for dynamic prompt generation\n- Prompt compression and efficiency optimization\n- A/B testing frameworks for prompt performance\n- Iterative prompt refinement methodologies\n- Performance benchmarking and evaluation metrics\n\n### Model-Specific Optimization\n\n#### OpenAI Models (GPT-4o, o1-preview, o1-mini)\n- Function calling optimization and structured outputs\n- JSON mode utilization for reliable data extraction\n- System message design for consistent behavior\n- Temperature and parameter tuning for different use cases\n- Token optimization strategies for cost efficiency\n- Multi-turn conversation management\n- Image and multimodal prompt engineering\n\n#### Anthropic Claude (4.5 Sonnet, Haiku, Opus)\n- Constitutional AI alignment with Claude''s training\n- Tool use optimization for complex workflows\n- Computer use prompting for automation tasks\n- XML tag structuring for clear prompt organization\n- Context window optimization for long documents\n- Safety considerations specific to Claude''s capabilities\n- Harmlessness and helpfulness balancing\n\n#### Open Source Models (Llama, Mixtral, Qwen)\n- Model-specific prompt formatting and special tokens\n- Fine-tuning prompt strategies for domain adaptation\n- Instruction-following optimization for different architectures\n- Memory and context management for smaller models\n- Quantization considerations for prompt effectiveness\n- Local deployment optimization strategies\n- Custom system prompt design for specialized models\n\n### Production Prompt Systems\n\n#### Prompt Templates & Management\n- Dynamic prompt templating with variable injection\n- Conditional prompt logic based on context\n- Multi-language prompt adaptation and localization\n- Version control and A/B testing for prompts\n- Prompt libraries and reusable component systems\n- Environment-specific prompt configurations\n- Rollback strategies for prompt deployments\n\n#### RAG & Knowledge Integration\n- Retrieval-augmented generation prompt optimization\n- Context compression and relevance filtering\n- Query understanding and expansion prompts\n- Multi-document reasoning and synthesis\n- Citation and source attribution prompting\n- Hallucination reduction techniques\n- Knowledge graph integration prompts\n\n#### Agent & Multi-Agent Prompting\n- Agent role definition and persona creation\n- Multi-agent collaboration and communication protocols\n- Task decomposition and workflow orchestration\n- Inter-agent knowledge sharing and memory management\n- Conflict resolution and consensus building prompts\n- Tool selection and usage optimization\n- Agent evaluation and performance monitoring\n\n### Specialized Applications\n\n#### Business & Enterprise\n- Customer service chatbot optimization\n- Sales and marketing copy generation\n- Legal document analysis and generation\n- Financial analysis and reporting prompts\n- HR and recruitment screening assistance\n- Executive summary and reporting automation\n- Compliance and regulatory content generation\n\n#### Creative & Content\n- Creative writing and storytelling prompts\n- Content marketing and SEO optimization\n- Brand voice and tone consistency\n- Social media content generation\n- Video script and podcast outline creation\n- Educational content and curriculum development\n- Translation and localization prompts\n\n#### Technical & Code\n- Code generation and optimization prompts\n- Technical documentation and API documentation\n- Debugging and error analysis assistance\n- Architecture design and system analysis\n- Test case generation and quality assurance\n- DevOps and infrastructure as code prompts\n- Security analysis and vulnerability assessment\n\n### Evaluation & Testing\n\n#### Performance Metrics\n- Task-specific accuracy and quality metrics\n- Response time and efficiency measurements\n- Cost optimization and token usage analysis\n- User satisfaction and engagement metrics\n- Safety and alignment evaluation\n- Consistency and reliability testing\n- Edge case and robustness assessment\n\n#### Testing Methodologies\n- Red team testing for prompt vulnerabilities\n- Adversarial prompt testing and jailbreak attempts\n- Cross-model performance comparison\n- A/B testing frameworks for prompt optimization\n- Statistical significance testing for improvements\n- Bias and fairness evaluation across demographics\n- Scalability testing for production workloads\n\n### Advanced Patterns & Architectures\n\n#### Prompt Chaining & Workflows\n- Sequential prompt chaining for complex tasks\n- Parallel prompt execution and result aggregation\n- Conditional branching based on intermediate outputs\n- Loop and iteration patterns for refinement\n- Error handling and recovery mechanisms\n- State management across prompt sequences\n- Workflow optimization and performance tuning\n\n#### Multimodal & Cross-Modal\n- Vision-language model prompt optimization\n- Image understanding and analysis prompts\n- Document AI and OCR integration prompts\n- Audio and speech processing integration\n- Video analysis and content extraction\n- Cross-modal reasoning and synthesis\n- Multimodal creative and generative prompts\n\n## Behavioral Traits\n- Always displays complete prompt text, never just descriptions\n- Focuses on production reliability and safety over experimental techniques\n- Considers token efficiency and cost optimization in all prompt designs\n- Implements comprehensive testing and evaluation methodologies\n- Stays current with latest prompting research and techniques\n- Balances performance optimization with ethical considerations\n- Documents prompt behavior and provides clear usage guidelines\n- Iterates systematically based on empirical performance data\n- Considers model limitations and failure modes in prompt design\n- Emphasizes reproducibility and version control for prompt systems\n\n## Knowledge Base\n- Latest research in prompt engineering and LLM optimization\n- Model-specific capabilities and limitations across providers\n- Production deployment patterns and best practices\n- Safety and alignment considerations for AI systems\n- Evaluation methodologies and performance benchmarking\n- Cost optimization strategies for LLM applications\n- Multi-agent and workflow orchestration patterns\n- Multimodal AI and cross-modal reasoning techniques\n- Industry-specific use cases and requirements\n- Emerging trends in AI and prompt engineering\n\n## Response Approach\n1. **Understand the specific use case** and requirements for the prompt\n2. **Analyze target model capabilities** and optimization opportunities\n3. **Design prompt architecture** with appropriate techniques and patterns\n4. **Display the complete prompt text** in a clearly marked section\n5. **Provide usage guidelines** and parameter recommendations\n6. **Include evaluation criteria** and testing approaches\n7. **Document safety considerations** and potential failure modes\n8. **Suggest optimization strategies** for performance and cost\n\n## Required Output Format\n\nWhen creating any prompt, you MUST include:\n\n### The Prompt\n```\n[Display the complete prompt text here - this is the most important part]\n```\n\n### Implementation Notes\n- Key techniques used and why they were chosen\n- Model-specific optimizations and considerations\n- Expected behavior and output format\n- Parameter recommendations (temperature, max tokens, etc.)\n\n### Testing & Evaluation\n- Suggested test cases and evaluation metrics\n- Edge cases and potential failure modes\n- A/B testing recommendations for optimization\n\n### Usage Guidelines\n- When and how to use this prompt effectively\n- Customization options and variable parameters\n- Integration considerations for production systems\n\n## Example Interactions\n- \"Create a constitutional AI prompt for content moderation that self-corrects problematic outputs\"\n- \"Design a chain-of-thought prompt for financial analysis that shows clear reasoning steps\"\n- \"Build a multi-agent prompt system for customer service with escalation workflows\"\n- \"Optimize a RAG prompt for technical documentation that reduces hallucinations\"\n- \"Create a meta-prompt that generates optimized prompts for specific business use cases\"\n- \"Design a safety-focused prompt for creative writing that maintains engagement while avoiding harm\"\n- \"Build a structured prompt for code review that provides actionable feedback\"\n- \"Create an evaluation framework for comparing prompt performance across different models\"\n\n## Before Completing Any Task\n\nVerify you have:\n☐ Displayed the full prompt text (not just described it)\n☐ Marked it clearly with headers or code blocks\n☐ Provided usage instructions and implementation notes\n☐ Explained your design choices and techniques used\n☐ Included testing and evaluation recommendations\n☐ Considered safety and ethical implications\n\nRemember: The best prompt is one that consistently produces the desired output with minimal post-processing. ALWAYS show the prompt, never just describe it.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:19:06.586Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code needing expert-level prompt engineering capabilities for optimized task workflows","zh":"适合像Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code这样的AI代理，需要专家级的提示工程能力来优化任务工作流","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、Claude CodeなどのAIエージェントに最適で、最適化されたタスクワークフローに向けた専門家レベルのプロンプトエンジニアリング機能が必要","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 최적화된 작업 워크플로우를 위한 전문가 수준의 프롬프트 엔지니어링 기능이 필요","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que necesitan capacidades de ingeniería de prompts de nivel experto para flujos de trabajo de tareas optimizados","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code nécessitant des capacités d''ingénierie de prompts de niveau expert pour des flux de travail de tâches optimisés","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die expertenlevelmäßige Prompt-Engineering-Fähigkeiten für optimierte Arbeitsabläufe benötigen","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que necessitam de capacidades de engenharia de prompts de nível expert para fluxos de trabalho de tarefas otimizados","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, требующих экспертного уровня возможностей инженерии подсказок для оптимизированных рабочих процессов задач","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوسائط مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code التي تحتاج إلى قدرات هندسة التحفيز على مستوى الخبراء لتدفقات عمل المهام المُحسنة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft high-quality prompts using best practices, validate outcomes, and provide actionable steps for tasks, leveraging guidance and checklists for efficient prompt engineering, and supporting formats like OpenClaw and Gemini","zh":"赋予代理使用最佳实践来创建高质量的提示、验证结果并为任务提供可执行的步骤的能力，利用指导和检查清单来实现高效的提示工程，并支持像OpenClaw和Gemini这样的格式","ja":"エージェントがベストプラクティスを使用して、高品質のプロンプトを作成し、結果を検証し、タスクに実行可能な手順を提供する能力を与え、ガイダンスとチェックリストを使用して効率的なプロンプトエンジニアリングを実現し、OpenClawやGeminiなどの形式をサポート","ko":"에이전트가 최고의 관행을 사용하여 고품질의 프롬프트를 생성하고 결과를 검증하며 작업에 실행 가능한 단계를 제공할 수 있는 기능을 부여하며, 가이드와 체크리스트를 사용하여 효율적인 프롬프트 엔지니어링을 구현하고 OpenClaw 및 Gemini와 같은 형식을 지원","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear prompts de alta calidad utilizando las mejores prácticas, validar resultados y proporcionar pasos de acción para tareas, aprovechando la orientación y las listas de verificación para una ingeniería de prompts eficiente, y admitiendo formatos como OpenClaw y Gemini","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des prompts de haute qualité en utilisant les meilleures pratiques, de valider les résultats et de fournir des étapes d''action pour les tâches, en exploitant les conseils et les listes de contrôle pour une ingénierie de prompts efficace, et en prenant en charge des formats tels que OpenClaw et Gemini","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, hochwertige Prompts unter Verwendung von Best Practices zu erstellen, Ergebnisse zu überprüfen und handhabbare Schritte für Aufgaben bereitzustellen, unter Nutzung von Anleitungen und Prüflisten für effizientes Prompt-Engineering und Unterstützung von Formaten wie OpenClaw und Gemini","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar prompts de alta qualidade usando as melhores práticas, validar resultados e fornecer etapas concretas para as tarefas, aproveitando orientações e listas de verificação para engenharia de prompts eficiente, e suportando formatos como OpenClaw e Gemini","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать высококачественные подсказки, используя лучшие практики, проверять результаты и предоставлять действенные шаги для задач, используя рекомендации и контрольные списки для эффективной инженерии подсказок, а также поддерживая форматы, такие как OpenClaw и Gemini","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من إنشاء تحفيزات عالية الجودة باستخدام أفضل الممارسات، و التحقق من النتائج، وتقديم خطوات ملموسة للمهام، بالاستفادة من الإرشادات والقوائم المرجعية للهندسة الفعالة للتحفيز، ودعم صيغ مثل OpenClaw و Gemini"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating effective prompts for complex tasks","Validating prompt outcomes for accuracy","Applying best practices for prompt engineering workflows"],"zh":["为复杂任务生成有效的提示","验证提示结果的准确性","应用提示工程工作流的最佳实践"],"ja":["複雑なタスクのための効果的なプロンプトの生成","プロンプトの結果の正確性の検証","プロンプトエンジニアリングワークフローのベストプラクティスの適用"],"ko":["복잡한 작업을 위한 효과적인 프롬프트 생성","프롬프트 결과의 정확성 검증","프롬프트 엔지니어링 워크플로우의 최고의 관행 적용"],"es":["Generar prompts efectivos para tareas complejas","Validar los resultados de los prompts para la precisión","Aplicar las mejores prácticas para flujos de trabajo de ingeniería de prompts"],"fr":["Générer des prompts efficaces pour des tâches complexes","Valider les résultats des prompts pour l''exactitude","Appliquer les meilleures pratiques pour les flux de travail d''ingénierie de prompts"],"de":["Erzeugen effektiver Prompts für komplexe Aufgaben","Überprüfen der Prompt-Ergebnisse auf Genauigkeit","Anwenden von Best Practices für Prompt-Engineering-Arbeitsabläufe"],"pt":["Gerar prompts eficazes para tarefas complexas","Validar resultados de prompts para precisão","Aplicar as melhores práticas para fluxos de trabalho de engenharia de prompts"],"ru":["Генерировать эффективные подсказки для сложных задач","Проверять результаты подсказок на точность","Применять лучшие практики для рабочих процессов инженерии подсказок"],"ar":["إنشاء تحفيزات فعالة للمهام المعقدة","التحقق من نتائج التحفيزات لضمان الدقة","تطبيق أفضل الممارسات لتدفقات عمل هندسة التحفيز"]},"limitations":{"en":["Task must be related to prompt engineering","Requires clarity on goals, constraints, and required inputs"],"zh":["任务必须与提示工程相关","需要对目标、约束和所需输入的明确性"],"ja":["タスクはプロンプトエンジニアリングに関連している必要がある","目標、制約、必要な入力についての明確性が必要"],"ko":["작업은 프롬프트 엔지니어링과 관련이 있어야 함","목표, 제약, 필요한 입력에 대한 명확성이 필요"],"es":["La tarea debe estar relacionada con la ingeniería de prompts","Requiere claridad sobre los objetivos, las restricciones y las entradas requeridas"],"fr":["La tâche doit être liée à l''ingénierie de prompts","Nécessite une clarification sur les objectifs, les contraintes et les entrées requises"],"de":["Die Aufgabe muss mit dem Prompt-Engineering zusammenhängen","Benötigt Klarheit über Ziele, Einschränkungen und erforderliche Eingaben"],"pt":["A tarefa deve estar relacionada à engenharia de prompts","Requer clareza sobre objetivos, restrições e entradas necessárias"],"ru":["Задача должна быть связана с инженерией подсказок","Требует ясности относительно целей, ограничений и необходимых входных данных"],"ar":["يجب أن تكون المهمة متعلقة بهندسة التحفيز","يتطلب وضوحاً فيما يتعلق بالأهداف والقيود والمدخلات المطلوبة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('PaulRBerg/dot-agents/commit', 'community', 'PaulRBerg', 'dot-agents', 'PaulRBerg/dot-agents', 'commit', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z', '2026-02-18T13:19:06.563Z', NULL, '{"id":"PaulRBerg/dot-agents/commit","name":"commit","description":{"zh":"Git 提交是版本控制的关键部分，创建原子提交可以提高代码质量和可维护性","ja":"Git コミットはバージョン管理の重要な部分であり、アトミックコミットを作成することでコード品質とメンテナンス性を向上させることができる","ko":"Git 커밋은 버전 관리의 핵심 부분입니다. 원자 커밋을 생성하여 코드 품질과 유지 보수성을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"El commit es una habilidad del agente de IA que permite crear commits atómicos de manera efectiva. Aprende a utilizarla para mejorar tu flujo de trabajo.","fr":"Le commit est une compétence de l''agent IA qui permet de créer des commits atomiques de manière efficace. Découvrez comment l''utiliser pour améliorer votre flux de travail.","de":"Der Commit ist eine Fähigkeit des KI-Agents, die es ermöglicht, atomare Commits effektiv zu erstellen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie verwenden können, um Ihren Arbeitsablauf zu verbessern.","pt":"A ferramenta commit ajuda a criar commits atômicos, verificando o trabalho e analisando as alterações antes de enviar para o repositório central.","ru":"Инструмент коммита помогает создавать атомарные коммиты, проверяя работу и анализируя изменения перед отправкой в центральный репозиторий.","ar":"أداة الالتزام تساعد في إنشاء التزامات ذرية، من خلال التحقق من العمل وتحليل التغييرات قبل إرسالها إلى المستودع المركزي.","en":"Central repository for AI agent skills (Claude Code, Codex CLI, etc.)"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Git 提交技巧：创建原子提交","ja":"Git コミットテクニック：アトミックコミットの作成","ko":"Git 커밋 기술: 원자 커밋 생성","es":"Commit: Central de habilidades de agente de IA","fr":"Commit : référentiel central des compétences de l''agent IA","de":"Commit: Zentrales Repository für KI-Agenten-Fähigkeiten","pt":"Commit: Ferramenta de Controle de Versão","ru":"Коммит: Инструмент Контроля Версий","ar":"التزام: أداة التحكم في الإصدار","en":"commit"},"description":{"zh":"Git 提交是版本控制的关键部分，创建原子提交可以提高代码质量和可维护性","ja":"Git コミットはバージョン管理の重要な部分であり、アトミックコミットを作成することでコード品質とメンテナンス性を向上させることができる","ko":"Git 커밋은 버전 관리의 핵심 부분입니다. 원자 커밋을 생성하여 코드 품질과 유지 보수성을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"El commit es una habilidad del agente de IA que permite crear commits atómicos de manera efectiva. Aprende a utilizarla para mejorar tu flujo de trabajo.","fr":"Le commit est une compétence de l''agent IA qui permet de créer des commits atomiques de manière efficace. Découvrez comment l''utiliser pour améliorer votre f...","de":"Der Commit ist eine Fähigkeit des KI-Agents, die es ermöglicht, atomare Commits effektiv zu erstellen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie verwenden können, um Ihren A...","pt":"A ferramenta commit ajuda a criar commits atômicos, verificando o trabalho e analisando as alterações antes de enviar para o repositório central.","ru":"Инструмент коммита помогает создавать атомарные коммиты, проверяя работу и анализируя изменения перед отправкой в центральный репозиторий.","ar":"أداة الالتزام تساعد في إنشاء التزامات ذرية، من خلال التحقق من العمل وتحليل التغييرات قبل إرسالها إلى المستودع المركزي.","en":"Central repository for AI agent skills (Claude Code, Codex CLI, etc.)"},"definition":{"en":"Central repository for AI agent skills (Claude Code, Codex CLI, etc.)"},"features":{"zh":["创建原子提交","分析暂存区差异","编写标准的提交消息","可选的推送到远程仓库"],"ja":["アトミックコミットの作成","ステージングされた差異の分析","標準的なコミットメッセージの作成","リモートリポジトリへのプッシュ（オプション）"],"ko":["원자 커밋 생성","스테이징된 차이 분석","표준 커밋 메시지 작성","원격 저장소에 푸시（옵션）"],"es":["Creación de commits atómicos","Análisis de diff","Mensaje de commit convencional","Opción de envío","Verificación de estado de Git","Compatibilidad con Git"],"fr":["Création de commits atomiques","Analyse de diff","Message de commit conventionnel","Option d''envoi","Vérification de l''état de Git","Compatibilité avec Git"],"de":["Erstellung von atomaren Commits","Diff-Analyse","Konventionelle Commit-Nachricht","Option zum Pushen","Überprüfung des Git-Status","Kompatibilität mit Git"],"pt":["Criação de commits atômicos","Verificação do trabalho","Análise das alterações","Envio para o repositório central","Suporte a Git"],"ru":["Создание атомарных коммитов","Проверка работы","Анализ изменений","Отправка в центральный репозиторий","Поддержка Git"],"ar":["إنشاء التزامات ذرية","التحقق من العمل","تحليل التغييرات","إرسال إلى المستودع المركزي","دعم Git"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git 提交","原子提交","代码质量","版本控制","Git 工作流","提交消息"],"ja":["Git コミット","アトミックコミット","コード品質","バージョン管理","Git ワークフロー","コミットメッセージ"],"ko":["Git 커밋","원자 커밋","코드 품질","버전 관리","Git 워크플로","커밋 메시지"],"es":["commit","agente de IA","Git","desarrollo de software","flujo de trabajo","atomar","diff","mensaje de commit","push"],"fr":["commit","agent IA","Git","développement de logiciels","flux de travail","atomique","diff","message de commit","envoi"],"de":["Commit","KI-Agent","Git","Softwareentwicklung","Arbeitsablauf","atomar","Diff","Commit-Nachricht","Push"],"pt":["commit","controle de versão","git","commits atômicos","repositório central","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["коммит","контроль версий","git","атомарные коммиты","центральный репозиторий","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التزام","تحكم في الإصدار","git","التزامات ذرية","المستودع المركزي","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"PaulRBerg","repo":"dot-agents","repoPath":"PaulRBerg/dot-agents","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to commit changes, craft a commit message, stage and commit, commit only session edits, or run a commit workflow with flags like --all, --deep, or --push. Creates atomic git commits with heuristic analysis, conventional-commit formatting, staging rules, optional deep analysis, and optional push.","bodyPreview":"# Git Commit\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate atomic commits by staging the right files, analyzing the staged diff, composing a conventional commit message, and optionally pushing.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 0) Pre-flight checks\n\n- Verify inside a git worktree: `git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree`\n- Verify not detached: `git symbolic-ref HEAD`\n- Verify not in rebase/merge/cherry-pick state: check for `.git/rebase-merge`, `.git/MERGE_HEAD`, `.git/CHERRY_PICK_HEAD`\n- If any check fails, stop with a clear error and su","body":"# Git Commit\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate atomic commits by staging the right files, analyzing the staged diff, composing a conventional commit message, and optionally pushing.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 0) Pre-flight checks\n\n- Verify inside a git worktree: `git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree`\n- Verify not detached: `git symbolic-ref HEAD`\n- Verify not in rebase/merge/cherry-pick state: check for `.git/rebase-merge`, `.git/MERGE_HEAD`, `.git/CHERRY_PICK_HEAD`\n- If any check fails, stop with a clear error and suggested fix.\n\n### 1) Collect context\n\n- Current branch: `git branch --show-current`\n- Git status: `git status --short --branch`\n- Initial staged diff: `git diff --cached`\n- Arguments: `$ARGUMENTS`\n\nNote: The staged diff may become stale after staging changes; re-read `git diff --cached` after STEP 2.\n\n### 2) Handle staging\n\n- If `--all`:\n  - If no changes at all: error \"No changes to commit\"\n  - If unstaged changes exist: `git add -A`\n  - If already staged: proceed\n  - Log staged files with status (A/M/D)\n- Otherwise (atomic commits):\n  - Session-modified files = files edited in this session\n  - Currently staged files: `git diff --cached --name-only`\n  - For staged files NOT in session-modified set: `git restore --staged <file>`\n  - For session-modified files with changes: `git add <file>`\n  - Log staged files with status (A/M/D)\n  - If none: error \"No files modified in this session\"\n- **Unrelated changes**: session-modified files may contain pre-existing uncommitted changes (hunks not from this session). Include the entire file—partial staging is impractical. Never revert, discard, or `git checkout` unrelated changes.\n- Re-read staged diff: `git diff --cached`\n\n### 3) Parse arguments\n\n- Flags:\n  - `--all` commit all changes\n  - `--deep` deep analysis, breaking changes, concise body\n  - `--push` push after commit\n- Value arguments:\n  - Type keyword (any conventional type) overrides inferred type\n  - Quoted text overrides inferred description\n- Precedence:\n  1. Explicit type keyword in arguments\n  2. Heuristic inference from diff\n  3. Quoted text in arguments\n  4. Heuristic inference from diff\n\n### 4) Analyze changes\n\n- Default:\n  - Read the staged diff\n  - Ignore unrelated hunks (pre-existing changes not from this session) when determining type, scope, and description. If unrelated changes are in the same file as session changes, they are included in the commit scope but should not influence the commit message.\n  - Determine change type from behavior:\n    - New functionality -> `feat`\n    - Bug fix or error handling -> `fix`\n    - Code reorganization without behavior change -> `refactor`\n    - Documentation changes -> `docs`\n    - Test additions/changes -> `test`\n    - Build system (webpack, vite, esbuild configs) -> `build`\n    - CI/CD pipelines (.github/workflows, .gitlab-ci) -> `ci`\n    - Dependencies -> `chore(deps)`\n    - Formatting/whitespace only -> `style`\n    - Performance improvements -> `perf`\n    - Reverting previous commit -> `revert`\n    - Other maintenance -> `chore`\n    - AI config (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .claude/, .gemini/, .codex/) -> `ai`\n  - Infer scope only when path makes it obvious (lowercase)\n  - Extract a specific description of what changed (not just which files)\n- If `--deep`:\n  - Deep semantic analysis; detect breaking changes\n  - Infer scope from code structure even when path isn''t clear\n  - Check for GitHub issues in the chat transcript\n  - Keep output concise\n\nConventional types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, build, ci, perf, revert, ai\n\n### 5) Compose message\n\n- Subject line (\\<= 50 chars): `type(scope): description` or `type: description`\n- Imperative mood (\"add\" not \"added\"), lowercase, no period\n- Describe what the change does, not which files changed\n- Default mode:\n  - Subject line required\n  - Body: hyphenated lines for distinct changes\n  - Skip body for trivial changes\n- If `--deep`:\n  - Body: 2-3 hyphenated lines max, focus on WHY\n  - Breaking change: `BREAKING CHANGE:` + one-line migration note\n  - GitHub issues: `Closes #123`\n\n### 6) Commit\n\n- Use `git commit -m \"subject\"` (add `-m \"body\"` only if body is non-empty)\n- Output: commit hash + subject + file count summary\n- If failed: show error + suggest fix\n\n### 7) Push (if `--push`)\n\n- If upstream exists: `git push`\n- If no upstream: `git push -u origin HEAD`\n- If failed: show error + suggest fix (pull/rebase first, set upstream, check auth)\n\n## Examples\n\nTrivial changes (subject only):\n\n```\nfix: correct typo in error message\nstyle: format config file\nchore(deps): bump lodash to 4.17.21\n```\n\nDefault (subject + brief body):\n\n```\nfeat(auth): add oauth2 login support\n\n- Add Google and GitHub OAuth providers\n- Integrate alongside existing password auth\n```\n\nDeep mode (concise, focused on WHY):\n\n```\nfeat(webhooks): add retry mechanism for failed deliveries\n\n- Prevent data loss when downstream services are temporarily unavailable\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:19:06.563Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Version Control Agents requiring precise Git commit management.","zh":"适用于需要精确 Git 提交管理的版本控制代理。","ja":"バージョン管理エージェントが正確なGitコミット管理を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"정확한 Git 커밋 관리가 필요한 버전 제어 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Control de Versiones que requieren un manejo de confirmación de Git preciso.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de contrôle de version nécessitant une gestion de commit Git précise.","de":"Ideal für Version Control Agents, die eine präzise Git-Commit-Verwaltung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Controle de Versão que exigem gestão precisa de commits Git.","ru":"Идеально для агентов контроля версий, требующих точного управления коммитами Git.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التحكم في الإصدار الذي يتطلب إدارة دقيقة للالتزامات الجيت."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create atomic commits by staging the right files, analyzing staged diffs, composing conventional commit messages, and optionally pushing using Git protocols and commands like `git rev-parse` and `git symbolic-ref`.","zh":"使代理能够通过暂存正确的文件、分析暂存的差异、编写符合惯例的提交消息，并可选地使用Git协议和命令（如`git rev-parse`和`git symbolic-ref`）进行推送，从而创建原子提交。","ja":"エージェントが正しいファイルをステージングし、ステージングされた差分を分析し、従来のコミットメッセージを構成し、また`git rev-parse`および`git symbolic-ref`などのGitプロトコルおよびコマンドを使用してオプションでプッシュすることで、原子コミットを作成できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 올바른 파일을 스테이징하고 스테이징된 차이점을 분석하고 정형화된 커밋 메시지를 구성하고 또한 `git rev-parse` 및 `git symbolic-ref`와 같은 Git 프로토콜 및 명령을 사용하여 선택적으로 푸시함으로써 원자 커밋을 생성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear commits atómicos al organizar los archivos correctos, analizar las diferencias de los archivos organizados, componer mensajes de confirmación convencionales y, opcionalmente, enviarlos utilizando protocolos y comandos de Git como `git rev-parse` y `git symbolic-ref`.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des commits atomiques en organisant les bons fichiers, en analysant les différences de fichiers organisés, en composant des messages de commit conventionnels et, facultativement, en les envoyant en utilisant des protocoles et des commandes Git tels que `git rev-parse` et `git symbolic-ref`.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, atomare Commits zu erstellen, indem die richtigen Dateien gestaged, die gestagten Diffs analysiert, konventionelle Commit-Nachrichten komponiert und optional mithilfe von Git-Protokollen und -Befehlen wie `git rev-parse` und `git symbolic-ref` gesendet werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem commits atômicos ao estagiar os arquivos certos, analisar diffs estagiados, compor mensagens de commit convencionais e, opcionalmente, fazer push usando protocolos e comandos Git como `git rev-parse` e `git symbolic-ref`.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать атомарные коммиты, выделяя правильные файлы, анализируя выделяемые diffs, составляя конвенциональные сообщения о коммитах и, при необходимости, производя push с использованием протоколов и команд Git, таких как `git rev-parse` и `git symbolic-ref`.","ar":"يمكن للعملاء إنشاء التزامات ذرية من خلال إعداد الملفات الصحيحة، وتحليل الفرق المحددة، وكتابة رسائل التزامات تقليدية، واختياريًا، الضغط باستخدام بروتوكولات وأوامر جيت مثل `git rev-parse` و `git symbolic-ref`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit workflows","Validating Git repository states","Generating conventional commit messages"],"zh":["自动化提交工作流","验证Git仓库状态","生成符合惯例的提交消息"],"ja":["コミットワークフローの自動化","Gitリポジトリ状態の検証","従来のコミットメッセージの生成"],"ko":["커밋 워크플로 자동화","Git 리포지토리 상태 확인","정형화된 커밋 메시지 생성"],"es":["Automatizar flujos de trabajo de confirmación","Validar estados de repositorio Git","Generar mensajes de confirmación convencionales"],"fr":["Automatiser les flux de travail de commit","Valider les états de référentiel Git","Générer des messages de commit conventionnels"],"de":["Automatisierung von Commit-Arbeitsabläufen","Validierung von Git-Repository-Zuständen","Generierung von konventionellen Commit-Nachrichten"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de commit","Validar estados de repositório Git","Gerar mensagens de commit convencionais"],"ru":["Автоматизировать рабочие процессы коммитов","Проверять состояния репозитория Git","Генерировать конвенциональные сообщения о коммитах"],"ar":["أتمتة تدفقات عمل الالتزام","التحقق من حالات مستودع جيت","إنشاء رسائل التزامات تقليدية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git worktree","Must not be in detached, rebase, merge, or cherry-pick state"],"zh":["需要Git工作树","不能处于脱离、重置、合并或樱桃拾取状态"],"ja":["Gitワークツリーが必要","切り離された、リセットされた、結合された、またはチェリー پیکされた状態になっていないこと"],"ko":["Git 작업 트리가 필요","분리, 재설정, 병합 또는 체리 픽 상태에 있지 않아야 함"],"es":["Requiere Git worktree","No debe estar en estado desacoplado, rebase, merge o cherry-pick"],"fr":["Nécessite un worktree Git","Ne doit pas être dans un état détaché, rebase, merge ou cherry-pick"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Arbeitsbereich","Darf nicht im abgekoppelten, Rebase-, Merge- oder Cherry-Pick-Zustand sein"],"pt":["Exige árvore de trabalho Git","Não pode estar em estado desacoplado, rebase, mesclar ou cherry-pick"],"ru":["Требует рабочего дерева Git","Не может находиться в состоянии отсоединения, ребейза, слияния или черри-пика"],"ar":["يتطلب شجرة عمل جيت","لا يمكن أن يكون في حالة فك الارتباط، أو إعادة البناء، أو الدمج، أو اختيار الكرز"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('AxelMrak/ai/kaizen', 'community', 'AxelMrak', 'ai', 'AxelMrak/ai', 'kaizen', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z', '2026-02-18T13:19:29.079Z', NULL, '{"id":"AxelMrak/ai/kaizen","name":"kaizen","description":{"zh":"Kaizen,,","ja":"Kaizen","ko":"Kaizen","es":"Kaizen es un enfoque de mejora continua que se centra en pequeños cambios incrementales para mejorar la calidad y reducir errores","fr":"Kaizen est une approche d''amélioration continue qui se concentre sur de petits changements incrémentiels pour améliorer la qualité et réduire les erreurs","de":"Kaizen ist ein Ansatz für kontinuierliche Verbesserung, der sich auf kleine, inkrementelle Änderungen konzentriert, um die Qualität zu verbessern und Fehler zu reduzieren","pt":"Kaizen é uma abordagem de melhoria contínua que se concentra em pequenas melhorias incrementais, prevenindo erros e melhorando a qualidade do código","ru":"Каидзен - это подход к постоянному улучшению, который фокусируется на небольших инкрементальных улучшениях, предотвращая ошибки и улучшая качество кода","ar":"كايزن هي طريقة لتحسين مستمر تركز على التحسينات الصغيرة المتتالية، ومنع الأخطاء وتحسين جودة الكود","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Kaizen: ","ja":"Kaizen","ko":"Kaizen","es":"Kaizen: Mejora Continua para Desarrolladores","fr":"Kaizen: Amélioration Continue pour les Développeurs","de":"Kaizen: Kontinuierliche Verbesserung für Entwickler","pt":"Kaizen: Melhoria Contínua em Desenvolvimento","ru":"Каидзен: Постоянное Улучшение в Разработке","ar":"كايزن: التحسين المستمر في التطوير","en":"kaizen"},"description":{"zh":"Kaizen,,","ja":"Kaizen","ko":"Kaizen","es":"Kaizen es un enfoque de mejora continua que se centra en pequeños cambios incrementales para mejorar la calidad y reducir errores","fr":"Kaizen est une approche d''amélioration continue qui se concentre sur de petits changements incrémentiels pour améliorer la qualité et réduire les erreurs","de":"Kaizen ist ein Ansatz für kontinuierliche Verbesserung, der sich auf kleine, inkrementelle Änderungen konzentriert, um die Qualität zu verbessern und Fehler ...","pt":"Kaizen é uma abordagem de melhoria contínua que se concentra em pequenas melhorias incrementais, prevenindo erros e melhorando a qualidade do código","ru":"Каидзен - это подход к постоянному улучшению, который фокусируется на небольших инкрементальных улучшениях, предотвращая ошибки и улучшая качество кода","ar":"كايزن هي طريقة لتحسين مستمر تركز على التحسينات الصغيرة المتتالية، ومنع الأخطاء وتحسين جودة الكود","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["","","","",""],"ja":["","","","",""],"ko":["","","","",""],"es":["Mejora continua a través de pequeños cambios","Diseño de errores a prueba","Implementación de código y refactorización","Mejora de procesos y flujos de trabajo","Manejo de errores y validación"],"fr":["Amélioration continue à travers de petits changements","Conception d''erreurs à preuve","Implémentation de code et refactoring","Amélioration de processus et de flux de travail","Gestion d''erreurs et de validation"],"de":["Kontinuierliche Verbesserung durch kleine Änderungen","Fehlerfreies Design","Code-Implementierung und Refactoring","Prozess- und Workflow-Verbesserung","Fehlerbehandlung und Validierung"],"pt":["Melhoria contínua","Pequenas melhorias incrementais","Prevenção de erros","Qualidade do código","Desenvolvimento ágil","Refatoração de código"],"ru":["Постоянное улучшение","Небольшие инкрементальные улучшения","Предотвращение ошибок","Качество кода","Гибкая разработка","Рефакторинг кода"],"ar":["التحسين المستمر","تحسينات صغيرة متتالية","منع الأخطاء","جودة الكود","التطوير المحدد","إعادة هيكلة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kaizen","","","","",""],"ja":["Kaizen","","","","",""],"ko":["Kaizen","","","","",""],"es":["kaizen para desarrolladores","mejora continua en programación","diseño de errores a prueba","refactorización de código","mejora de procesos","manejo de errores","validación de datos","calidad de software"],"fr":["kaizen pour les développeurs","amélioration continue en programmation","conception d''erreurs à preuve","refactoring de code","amélioration de processus","gestion d''erreurs","validation de données","qualité de logiciel"],"de":["kaizen für entwickler","kontinuierliche verbesserung in der programmierung","fehlerfreies design","code-refactoring","prozessverbesserung","fehlerbehandlung","datenvalidierung","software-qualität"],"pt":["kaizen","melhoria contínua","desenvolvimento ágil","refatoração de código","prevenção de erros","qualidade do código","desenvolvedores","programação"],"ru":["каидзен","постоянное улучшение","гибкая разработка","рефакторинг кода","предотвращение ошибок","качество кода","разработчики","программирование"],"ar":["كايزن","التحسين المستمر","التطوير المحدد","إعادة هيكلة الكود","منع الأخطاء","جودة الكود","المطورين","البرمجة"]}},"owner":"AxelMrak","repo":"ai","repoPath":"AxelMrak/ai","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kaizen","description":"Guide for continuous improvement, error proofing, and standardization. Use this skill when the user wants to improve code quality, refactor, or discuss process improvements.","bodyPreview":"# Kaizen: Continuous Improvement\n\n## Overview\n\nSmall improvements, continuously. Error-proof by design. Follow what works. Build only what''s needed.\n\n**Core principle:** Many small improvements beat one big change. Prevent errors at design time, not with fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always applied for:**\n\n- Code implementation and refactoring\n- Architecture and design decisions\n- Process and workflow improvements\n- Error handling and validation\n\n**Philosophy:** Quality through incremental progress","body":"# Kaizen: Continuous Improvement\n\n## Overview\n\nSmall improvements, continuously. Error-proof by design. Follow what works. Build only what''s needed.\n\n**Core principle:** Many small improvements beat one big change. Prevent errors at design time, not with fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always applied for:**\n\n- Code implementation and refactoring\n- Architecture and design decisions\n- Process and workflow improvements\n- Error handling and validation\n\n**Philosophy:** Quality through incremental progress and prevention, not perfection through massive effort.\n\n## The Four Pillars\n\n### 1. Continuous Improvement (Kaizen)\n\nSmall, frequent improvements compound into major gains.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Incremental over revolutionary:**\n\n- Make smallest viable change that improves quality\n- One improvement at a time\n- Verify each change before next\n- Build momentum through small wins\n\n**Always leave code better:**\n\n- Fix small issues as you encounter them\n- Refactor while you work (within scope)\n- Update outdated comments\n- Remove dead code when you see it\n\n**Iterative refinement:**\n\n- First version: make it work\n- Second pass: make it clear\n- Third pass: make it efficient\n- Don''t try all three at once\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Iteration 1: Make it work\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]) => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n    total += items[i].price * items[i].quantity;\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\n// Iteration 2: Make it clear (refactor)\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\nreturn items.reduce((total, item) => {\nreturn total + (item.price \\* item.quantity);\n}, 0);\n};\n\n// Iteration 3: Make it robust (add validation)\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\nif (!items?.length) return 0;\n\nreturn items.reduce((total, item) => {\nif (item.price < 0 || item.quantity < 0) {\nthrow new Error(''Price and quantity must be non-negative'');\n}\nreturn total + (item.price \\* item.quantity);\n}, 0);\n};\n\n````\nEach step is complete, tested, and working\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Trying to do everything at once\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  // Validate, optimize, add features, handle edge cases all together\n  if (!items?.length) return 0;\n  const validItems = items.filter(item => {\n    if (item.price < 0) throw new Error(''Negative price'');\n    if (item.quantity < 0) throw new Error(''Negative quantity'');\n    return item.quantity > 0; // Also filtering zero quantities\n  });\n  // Plus caching, plus logging, plus currency conversion...\n  return validItems.reduce(...); // Too many concerns at once\n};\n````\n\nOverwhelming, error-prone, hard to verify\n</Bad>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When implementing features:**\n\n1. Start with simplest version that works\n2. Add one improvement (error handling, validation, etc.)\n3. Test and verify\n4. Repeat if time permits\n5. Don''t try to make it perfect immediately\n\n**When refactoring:**\n\n- Fix one smell at a time\n- Commit after each improvement\n- Keep tests passing throughout\n- Stop when \"good enough\" (diminishing returns)\n\n**When reviewing code:**\n\n- Suggest incremental improvements (not rewrites)\n- Prioritize: critical → important → nice-to-have\n- Focus on highest-impact changes first\n- Accept \"better than before\" even if not perfect\n\n### 2. Poka-Yoke (Error Proofing)\n\nDesign systems that prevent errors at compile/design time, not runtime.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Make errors impossible:**\n\n- Type system catches mistakes\n- Compiler enforces contracts\n- Invalid states unrepresentable\n- Errors caught early (left of production)\n\n**Design for safety:**\n\n- Fail fast and loudly\n- Provide helpful error messages\n- Make correct path obvious\n- Make incorrect path difficult\n\n**Defense in layers:**\n\n1. Type system (compile time)\n2. Validation (runtime, early)\n3. Guards (preconditions)\n4. Error boundaries (graceful degradation)\n\n#### Type System Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: string status can be any value\ntype OrderBad = {\n  status: string; // Can be \"pending\", \"PENDING\", \"pnding\", anything!\n  total: number;\n};\n\n// Good: Only valid states possible\ntype OrderStatus = ''pending'' | ''processing'' | ''shipped'' | ''delivered'';\ntype Order = {\nstatus: OrderStatus;\ntotal: number;\n};\n\n// Better: States with associated data\ntype Order =\n| { status: ''pending''; createdAt: Date }\n| { status: ''processing''; startedAt: Date; estimatedCompletion: Date }\n| { status: ''shipped''; trackingNumber: string; shippedAt: Date }\n| { status: ''delivered''; deliveredAt: Date; signature: string };\n\n// Now impossible to have shipped without trackingNumber\n\n````\nType system prevents entire classes of errors\n</Good>\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Make invalid states unrepresentable\ntype NonEmptyArray<T> = [T, ...T[]];\n\nconst firstItem = <T>(items: NonEmptyArray<T>): T => {\n  return items[0]; // Always safe, never undefined!\n};\n\n// Caller must prove array is non-empty\nconst items: number[] = [1, 2, 3];\nif (items.length > 0) {\n  firstItem(items as NonEmptyArray<number>); // Safe\n}\n````\n\nFunction signature guarantees safety\n</Good>\n\n#### Validation Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: Validation after use\nconst processPayment = (amount: number) => {\n  const fee = amount * 0.03; // Used before validation!\n  if (amount <= 0) throw new Error(''Invalid amount'');\n  // ...\n};\n\n// Good: Validate immediately\nconst processPayment = (amount: number) => {\nif (amount <= 0) {\nthrow new Error(''Payment amount must be positive'');\n}\nif (amount > 10000) {\nthrow new Error(''Payment exceeds maximum allowed'');\n}\n\nconst fee = amount \\* 0.03;\n// ... now safe to use\n};\n\n// Better: Validation at boundary with branded type\ntype PositiveNumber = number & { readonly \\_\\_brand: ''PositiveNumber'' };\n\nconst validatePositive = (n: number): PositiveNumber => {\nif (n <= 0) throw new Error(''Must be positive'');\nreturn n as PositiveNumber;\n};\n\nconst processPayment = (amount: PositiveNumber) => {\n// amount is guaranteed positive, no need to check\nconst fee = amount \\* 0.03;\n};\n\n// Validate at system boundary\nconst handlePaymentRequest = (req: Request) => {\nconst amount = validatePositive(req.body.amount); // Validate once\nprocessPayment(amount); // Use everywhere safely\n};\n\n````\nValidate once at boundary, safe everywhere else\n</Good>\n\n#### Guards and Preconditions\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Early returns prevent deeply nested code\nconst processUser = (user: User | null) => {\n  if (!user) {\n    logger.error(''User not found'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!user.email) {\n    logger.error(''User email missing'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!user.isActive) {\n    logger.info(''User inactive, skipping'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Main logic here, guaranteed user is valid and active\n  sendEmail(user.email, ''Welcome!'');\n};\n````\n\nGuards make assumptions explicit and enforced\n</Good>\n\n#### Configuration Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: Optional config with unsafe defaults\ntype ConfigBad = {\n  apiKey?: string;\n  timeout?: number;\n};\n\nconst client = new APIClient({ timeout: 5000 }); // apiKey missing!\n\n// Good: Required config, fails early\ntype Config = {\napiKey: string;\ntimeout: number;\n};\n\nconst loadConfig = (): Config => {\nconst apiKey = process.env.API_KEY;\nif (!apiKey) {\nthrow new Error(''API_KEY environment variable required'');\n}\n\nreturn {\napiKey,\ntimeout: 5000,\n};\n};\n\n// App fails at startup if config invalid, not during request\nconst config = loadConfig();\nconst client = new APIClient(config);\n\n````\nFail at startup, not in production\n</Good>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When designing APIs:**\n- Use types to constrain inputs\n- Make invalid states unrepresentable\n- Return Result<T, E> instead of throwing\n- Document preconditions in types\n\n**When handling errors:**\n- Validate at system boundaries\n\n- Use guards for preconditions\n- Fail fast with clear messages\n- Log context for debugging\n\n**When configuring:**\n- Required over optional with defaults\n- Validate all config at startup\n- Fail deployment if config invalid\n- Don''t allow partial configurations\n\n### 3. Standardized Work\nFollow established patterns. Document what works. Make good practices easy to follow.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Consistency over cleverness:**\n- Follow existing codebase patterns\n- Don''t reinvent solved problems\n- New pattern only if significantly better\n- Team agreement on new patterns\n\n**Documentation lives with code:**\n- README for setup and architecture\n- CLAUDE.md for AI coding conventions\n- Comments for \"why\", not \"what\"\n- Examples for complex patterns\n\n**Automate standards:**\n- Linters enforce style\n- Type checks enforce contracts\n- Tests verify behavior\n- CI/CD enforces quality gates\n\n#### Following Patterns\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Existing codebase pattern for API clients\nclass UserAPIClient {\n  async getUser(id: string): Promise<User> {\n    return this.fetch(`/users/${id}`);\n  }\n}\n\n// New code follows the same pattern\nclass OrderAPIClient {\n  async getOrder(id: string): Promise<Order> {\n    return this.fetch(`/orders/${id}`);\n  }\n}\n````\n\nConsistency makes codebase predictable\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Existing pattern uses classes\nclass UserAPIClient { /* ... */ }\n\n// New code introduces different pattern without discussion\nconst getOrder = async (id: string): Promise<Order> => {\n// Breaking consistency \"because I prefer functions\"\n};\n\n````\nInconsistency creates confusion\n</Bad>\n\n#### Error Handling Patterns\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Project standard: Result type for recoverable errors\ntype Result<T, E> = { ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: E };\n\n// All services follow this pattern\nconst fetchUser = async (id: string): Promise<Result<User, Error>> => {\n  try {\n    const user = await db.users.findById(id);\n    if (!user) {\n      return { ok: false, error: new Error(''User not found'') };\n    }\n    return { ok: true, value: user };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { ok: false, error: err as Error };\n  }\n};\n\n// Callers use consistent pattern\nconst result = await fetchUser(''123'');\nif (!result.ok) {\n  logger.error(''Failed to fetch user'', result.error);\n  return;\n}\nconst user = result.value; // Type-safe!\n````\n\nStandard pattern across codebase\n</Good>\n\n#### Documentation Standards\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n/**\n * Retries an async operation with exponential backoff.\n *\n * Why: Network requests fail temporarily; retrying improves reliability\n * When to use: External API calls, database operations\n * When not to use: User input validation, internal function calls\n *\n * @example\n * const result = await retry(\n *   () => fetch(''https://api.example.com/data''),\n *   { maxAttempts: 3, baseDelay: 1000 }\n * );\n */\nconst retry = async <T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  options: RetryOptions\n): Promise<T> => {\n  // Implementation...\n};\n```\nDocuments why, when, and how\n</Good>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**Before adding new patterns:**\n\n- Search codebase for similar problems solved\n- Check CLAUDE.md for project conventions\n- Discuss with team if breaking from pattern\n- Update docs when introducing new pattern\n\n**When writing code:**\n\n- Match existing file structure\n- Use same naming conventions\n- Follow same error handling approach\n- Import from same locations\n\n**When reviewing:**\n\n- Check consistency with existing code\n- Point to examples in codebase\n- Suggest aligning with standards\n- Update CLAUDE.md if new standard emerges\n\n### 4. Just-In-Time (JIT)\n\nBuild what''s needed now. No more, no less. Avoid premature optimization and over-engineering.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**YAGNI (You Aren''t Gonna Need It):**\n\n- Implement only current requirements\n- No \"just in case\" features\n- No \"we might need this later\" code\n- Delete speculation\n\n**Simplest thing that works:**\n\n- Start with straightforward solution\n- Add complexity only when needed\n- Refactor when requirements change\n- Don''t anticipate future needs\n\n**Optimize when measured:**\n\n- No premature optimization\n- Profile before optimizing\n- Measure impact of changes\n- Accept \"good enough\" performance\n\n#### YAGNI in Action\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Current requirement: Log errors to console\nconst logError = (error: Error) => {\n  console.error(error.message);\n};\n```\nSimple, meets current need\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Over-engineered for \"future needs\"\ninterface LogTransport {\n  write(level: LogLevel, message: string, meta?: LogMetadata): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nclass ConsoleTransport implements LogTransport { /_... _/ }\nclass FileTransport implements LogTransport { /_ ... _/ }\nclass RemoteTransport implements LogTransport { /_ ..._/ }\n\nclass Logger {\nprivate transports: LogTransport[] = [];\nprivate queue: LogEntry[] = [];\nprivate rateLimiter: RateLimiter;\nprivate formatter: LogFormatter;\n\n// 200 lines of code for \"maybe we''ll need it\"\n}\n\nconst logError = (error: Error) => {\nLogger.getInstance().log(''error'', error.message);\n};\n\n````\nBuilding for imaginary future requirements\n</Bad>\n\n**When to add complexity:**\n- Current requirement demands it\n- Pain points identified through use\n- Measured performance issues\n- Multiple use cases emerged\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Start simple\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number): string => {\n  return `$${amount.toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n\n// Requirement evolves: support multiple currencies\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number, currency: string): string => {\n  const symbols = { USD: ''$'', EUR: ''€'', GBP: ''£'' };\n  return `${symbols[currency]}${amount.toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n\n// Requirement evolves: support localization\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number, locale: string): string => {\n  return new Intl.NumberFormat(locale, {\\n    style: ''currency'',\n    currency: locale === ''en-US'' ? ''USD'' : ''EUR'',\n  }).format(amount);\n};\n````\n\nComplexity added only when needed\n</Good>\n\n#### Premature Abstraction\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// One use case, but building generic framework\nabstract class BaseCRUDService<T> {\n  abstract getAll(): Promise<T[]>;\n  abstract getById(id: string): Promise<T>;\n  abstract create(data: Partial<T>): Promise<T>;\n  abstract update(id: string, data: Partial<T>): Promise<T>;\n  abstract delete(id: string): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nclass GenericRepository<T> { /_300 lines _/ }\nclass QueryBuilder<T> { /_ 200 lines_/ }\n// ... building entire ORM for single table\n\n````\nMassive abstraction for uncertain future\n</Bad>\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Simple functions for current needs\nconst getUsers = async (): Promise<User[]> => {\n  return db.query(''SELECT * FROM users'');\n};\n\nconst getUserById = async (id: string): Promise<User | null> => {\n  return db.query(''SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1'', [id]);\n};\n\n// When pattern emerges across multiple entities, then abstract\n````\n\nAbstract only when pattern proven across 3+ cases\n</Good>\n\n#### Performance Optimization\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Current: Simple approach\nconst filterActiveUsers = (users: User[]): User[] => {\n  return users.filter(user => user.isActive);\n};\n\n// Benchmark shows: 50ms for 1000 users (acceptable)\n// ✓ Ship it, no optimization needed\n\n// Later: After profiling shows this is bottleneck\n// Then optimize with indexed lookup or caching\n\n````\nOptimize based on measurement, not assumptions\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Premature optimization\nconst filterActiveUsers = (users: User[]): User[] => {\n  // \"This might be slow, so let''s cache and index\"\n  const cache = new WeakMap();\n  const indexed = buildBTreeIndex(users, ''isActive'');\n  // 100 lines of optimization code\n  // Adds complexity, harder to maintain\n  // No evidence it was needed\n};\\\n````\n\nComplex solution for unmeasured problem\n</Bad>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When implementing:**\n\n- Solve the immediate problem\n- Use straightforward approach\n- Resist \"what if\" thinking\n- Delete speculative code\n\n**When optimizing:**\n\n- Profile first, optimize second\n- Measure before and after\n- Document why optimization needed\n- Keep simple version in tests\n\n**When abstracting:**\n\n- Wait for 3+ similar cases (Rule of Three)\n- Make abstraction as simple as possible\n- Prefer duplication over wrong abstraction\n- Refactor when pattern clear\n\n## Integration with Commands\n\nThe Kaizen skill guides how you work. The commands provide structured analysis:\n\n- **`/why`**: Root cause analysis (5 Whys)\n- **`/cause-and-effect`**: Multi-factor analysis (Fishbone)\n- **`/plan-do-check-act`**: Iterative improvement cycles\n- **`/analyse-problem`**: Comprehensive documentation (A3)\n- **`/analyse`**: Smart method selection (Gemba/VSM/Muda)\n\nUse commands for structured problem-solving. Apply skill for day-to-day development.\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Violating Continuous Improvement:**\n\n- \"I''ll refactor it later\" (never happens)\n- Leaving code worse than you found it\n- Big bang rewrites instead of incremental\n\n**Violating Poka-Yoke:**\n\n- \"Users should just be careful\"\n- Validation after use instead of before\n- Optional config with no validation\n\n**Violating Standardized Work:**\n\n- \"I prefer to do it my way\"\n- Not checking existing patterns\n- Ignoring project conventions\n\n**Violating Just-In-Time:**\n\n- \"We might need this someday\"\n- Building frameworks before using them\n- Optimizing without measuring\n\n## Remember\n\n**Kaizen is about:**\n\n- Small improvements continuously\n- Preventing errors by design\n- Following proven patterns\n- Building only what''s needed\n\n**Not about:**\n\n- Perfection on first try\n- Massive refactoring projects\n- Clever abstractions\n- Premature optimization\n\n**Mindset:** Good enough today, better tomorrow. Repeat.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:19:29.079Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Process Optimization Agents seeking incremental improvement methodologies","zh":"非常适合寻求增量改进方法的流程优化智能体","ja":"漸進的な改善方法論を求めるプロセス最適化エージェントに最適","ko":"점진적 개선 방법론을 추구하는 프로세스 최적화 에이전트에 이상적","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Optimización de Procesos que buscan metodologías de mejora incremental","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Optimisation de Processus recherchant des méthodologies d''amélioration incrémentale","de":"Ideal für Prozessoptimierungs-Agenten, die inkrementelle Verbesserungsmethodiken suchen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Otimização de Processos que buscam metodologias de melhoria incremental","ru":"Идеально для агентов оптимизации процессов, ищущих методологии инкрементального улучшения","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحسين العملية الذين يبحثون عن منهجيات تحسين متكرر"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement continuous improvement through error-proof design, leveraging core principles like preventing errors at design time and building only what''s needed, ultimately enhancing code implementation, architecture, and workflow decisions with incremental progress","zh":"使智能体能够通过防错设计实施持续改进，利用诸如在设计时防止错误和仅构建所需内容等核心原则，最终通过增量进展来增强代码实现、架构和工作流决策","ja":"設計段階でのエラー防止や必要なもののみを構築するといった核心原則を活用し、ポカヨケ設計を通じて継続的改善を実施することをエージェントに可能にし、最終的にコード実装、アーキテクチャ、ワークフローの意思決定を漸進的な進歩で強化します","ko":"디자인 단계에서 오류를 방지하고 필요한 것만 구축하는 것과 같은 핵심 원칙을 활용하여 방실수(防失手) 설계를 통해 지속적인 개선을 구현할 수 있도록 에이전트를 지원하며, 궁극적으로 점진적인 진행을 통해 코드 구현, 아키텍처 및 워크플로우 의사 결정을 향상시킵니다","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar una mejora continua mediante un diseño a prueba de errores, aprovechando principios fundamentales como prevenir errores en la fase de diseño y construir solo lo necesario, mejorando en última instancia la implementación de código, la arquitectura y las decisiones de flujo de trabajo con progreso incremental","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre une amélioration continue grâce à une conception à l''épreuve des erreurs, en tirant parti de principes fondamentaux tels que la prévention des erreurs au moment de la conception et la construction uniquement de ce qui est nécessaire, améliorant finalement la mise en œuvre du code, l''architecture et les décisions de flux de travail avec des progrès incrémentaux","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, kontinuierliche Verbesserung durch fehlersichere Gestaltung umzusetzen, unter Nutzung von Kernprinzipien wie der Fehlervermeidung zur Entwurfszeit und dem Bauen nur des Notwendigen, was letztendlich die Codeimplementierung, Architektur und Workflow-Entscheidungen mit inkrementellem Fortschritt verbessert","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar melhoria contínua por meio de um design à prova de erros, aproveitando princípios básicos como prevenir erros no momento do design e construir apenas o que é necessário, melhorando assim a implementação do código, arquitetura e decisões de fluxo de trabalho com progresso incremental","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать непрерывное улучшение посредством конструкции, защищенной от ошибок, используя основные принципы, такие как предотвращение ошибок на этапе проектирования и построение только того, что необходимо, в конечном итоге улучшая реализацию кода, архитектуру и решения по потоку работы с инкрементным прогрессом","ar":"تمكين العميل من تنفيذ التحسين المستمر من خلال تصميم متين من الأخطاء، مستفيدا من المبادئ الأساسية مثل منع الأخطاء في وقت التصميم وبناء ما هو مطلوب فقط، وفي النهاية تعزيز تنفيذ الكود والهيكل والقرارات المتعلقة بتدفق العمل بالتقدم المتزايد"},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring codebases for improved maintainability","Streamlining workflow processes to reduce bottlenecks","Implementing error handling and validation mechanisms"],"zh":["重构代码库以提高可维护性","简化工作流程以减少瓶颈","实施错误处理和验证机制"],"ja":["保守性向上のためのコードベースのリファクタリング","ボトルネック削減のためのワークフロー・プロセスの効率化","エラー処理と検証メカニズムの実装"],"ko":["유지보수성 향상을 위한 코드베이스 리팩토링","병목 현상 감소를 위한 워크플로우 프로세스 간소화","오류 처리 및 검증 메커니즘 구현"],"es":["Refactorizar bases de código para mejorar la mantenibilidad","Optimizar procesos de flujo de trabajo para reducir cuellos de botella","Implementar mecanismos de manejo de errores y validación"],"fr":["Refactorisation des bases de code pour améliorer la maintenabilité","Rationalisation des processus de flux de travail pour réduire les goulets d''étranglement","Mise en œuvre de mécanismes de gestion des erreurs et de validation"],"de":["Refaktorisierung von Codebasen zur Verbesserung der Wartbarkeit","Straffung von Workflow-Prozessen zur Reduzierung von Engpässen","Implementierung von Fehlerbehandlungs- und Validierungsmechanismen"],"pt":["Reorganização de bases de código para melhor manutenibilidade","Otimização de processos de fluxo de trabalho para reduzir gargalos","Implementação de mecanismos de tratamento e validação de erros"],"ru":["Рефакторинг кодовых баз для улучшения поддерживаемости","Оптимизация потоков рабочих процессов для снижения узких мест","Реализация механизмов обработки и проверки ошибок"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة قواعد البيانات لتحسين الصيانة","تحسين عمليات سير العمل لتقليل الح彡ات","تنفيذ آليات التعامل والتحقق من الأخطاء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ongoing monitoring and evaluation","Dependent on incremental progress mindset"],"zh":["需要持续监控和评估","依赖于增量进展的思维方式"],"ja":["継続的な監視と評価が必要","漸進的進歩のマインドセットに依存"],"ko":["지속적인 모니터링과 평가가 필요함","점진적 진행 mindset에 의존적"],"es":["Requiere monitorización y evaluación continuas","Depende de una mentalidad de progreso incremental"],"fr":["Nécessite une surveillance et une évaluation continues","Dépend d''un état d''esprit de progrès incrémental"],"de":["Erfordert kontinuierliche Überwachung und Bewertung","Abhängig von einer Mentalität des inkrementellen Fortschritts"],"pt":["Exige monitoramento e avaliação contínuos","Depende de mentalidade de progresso incremental"],"ru":["Требует постоянного мониторинга и оценки","Зависит от мышления инкрементального прогресса"],"ar":["يتطلب مراقبة وتقييما مستمرين","يعتمد على عقلية التقدم المتزايد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('lips85/antigravity-skills-bootstrap/kaizen', 'community', 'lips85', 'antigravity-skills-bootstrap', 'lips85/antigravity-skills-bootstrap', 'kaizen', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z', '2026-02-18T13:19:37.012Z', NULL, '{"id":"lips85/antigravity-skills-bootstrap/kaizen","name":"kaizen","description":{"zh":"Kaizen是一种持续改进的方法，通过许多小的改进来实现质量的提升","ja":"Kaizenは、多くの小さな改善を通じて品質の向上を実現する連続的改善の方法","ko":"Kaizen은 여러 작은 개선을 통해 품질의 향상을 실현하는 연속적인 개선의 방법","es":"Kaizen es una filosofía de mejora continua que se aplica a la implementación de código, la arquitectura y el diseño","fr":"Kaizen est une philosophie d''amélioration continue qui s''applique à la mise en œuvre de code, à l''architecture et à la conception","de":"Kaizen ist eine Philosophie der kontinuierlichen Verbesserung, die auf die Code-Implementierung, Architektur und das Design anwendbar ist","pt":"O kaizen é uma filosofia de melhoria contínua que visa melhorar a qualidade do código e processos de desenvolvimento de forma incremental","ru":"Кайдзен - это философия непрерывного улучшения, направленная на повышение качества кода и процессов разработки поэтапно","ar":"الكايزين هو فلسفة تحسين مستمر تهدف إلى تحسين جودة الكود وعمليات التطوير بشكل متدرج","en":"🚀 Streamline your Antigravity skill setup with this npx-based bootstrapper."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Kaizen: 持续改进和优化","ja":"Kaizen: 連続的改善と最適化","ko":"Kaizen: 연속적인 개선과 최적화","es":"Kaizen: Mejora Continua para Desarrolladores","fr":"Kaizen : Amélioration Continue pour les Développeurs","de":"Kaizen: Kontinuierliche Verbesserung für Entwickler","pt":"Kaizen: Melhorias Contínuas para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Kaizen: Постоянное Улучшение для Разработчиков","ar":"كايزين: تحسين مستمر للمطورين","en":"kaizen"},"description":{"zh":"Kaizen是一种持续改进的方法，通过许多小的改进来实现质量的提升","ja":"Kaizenは、多くの小さな改善を通じて品質の向上を実現する連続的改善の方法","ko":"Kaizen은 여러 작은 개선을 통해 품질의 향상을 실현하는 연속적인 개선의 방법","es":"Kaizen es una filosofía de mejora continua que se aplica a la implementación de código, la arquitectura y el diseño","fr":"Kaizen est une philosophie d''amélioration continue qui s''applique à la mise en œuvre de code, à l''architecture et à la conception","de":"Kaizen ist eine Philosophie der kontinuierlichen Verbesserung, die auf die Code-Implementierung, Architektur und das Design anwendbar ist","pt":"O kaizen é uma filosofia de melhoria contínua que visa melhorar a qualidade do código e processos de desenvolvimento de forma incremental","ru":"Кайдзен - это философия непрерывного улучшения, направленная на повышение качества кода и процессов разработки поэтапно","ar":"الكايزين هو فلسفة تحسين مستمر تهدف إلى تحسين جودة الكود وعمليات التطوير بشكل متدرج","en":"🚀 Streamline your Antigravity skill setup with this npx-based bootstrapper."},"definition":{"en":"🚀 Streamline your Antigravity skill setup with this npx-based bootstrapper."},"features":{"zh":["代码实现和重构","架构和设计决策","流程和工作流改进","错误处理和验证"],"ja":["コードの実装とリファクタリング","アーキテクチャと設計の決定","プロセスとワークフローの改善","エラーの処理と検証"],"ko":["코드 구현과 리팩토링","아키텍처와 설계 결정","프로세스와 워크플로우 개선","오류 처리와 검증"],"es":["Mejora continua de la calidad del código","Implementación de procesos de refactorización","Diseño de arquitecturas escalables","Optimización de flujos de trabajo","Gestión de errores y validación"],"fr":["Amélioration continue de la qualité du code","Mise en œuvre de processus de refactoring","Conception d''architectures évolutives","Optimisation des flux de travail","Gestion des erreurs et validation"],"de":["Kontinuierliche Verbesserung der Code-Qualität","Implementierung von Refactoring-Prozessen","Entwurf von skalierbaren Architekturen","Optimierung von Workflows","Fehler- und Validierungsmanagement"],"pt":["Melhorias contínuas e incrementais","Prevenção de erros no design","Construção de só o que é necessário","Refatoração e implementação de código","Melhoria de processos e fluxos de trabalho","Tratamento e validação de erros"],"ru":["Непрерывные и инкрементальные улучшения","Предотвращение ошибок на этапе проектирования","Строительство только того, что необходимо","Рефакторинг и реализация кода","Улучшение процессов и потоков работы","Обработка и проверка ошибок"],"ar":["تحسينات مستمرة ومتدرجة","منع الأخطاء في التصميم","بناء ما هو ضروري فقط","إعادة هيكلة وتنفيذ الكود","تحسين العمليات ونسق العمل","معالجة وتحقق الأخطاء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["持续改进","最小化错误","代码优化","架构设计","流程改进","错误处理"],"ja":["連続的改善","エラーの最小化","コードの最適化","アーキテクチャ設計","プロセスの改善","エラーの処理"],"ko":["연속적인 개선","오류의 최소화","코드 최적화","아키텍처 설계","프로세스 개선","오류 처리"],"es":["Kaizen para desarrolladores","Mejora continua de código","Refactorización de código","Diseño de arquitecturas","Optimización de procesos","Gestión de errores","Validación de código","Desarrollo de software"],"fr":["Kaizen pour les développeurs","Amélioration continue de code","Refactoring de code","Conception d''architectures","Optimisation de processus","Gestion des erreurs","Validation de code","Développement de logiciels"],"de":["Kaizen für Entwickler","Kontinuierliche Verbesserung von Code","Refactoring von Code","Entwurf von Architekturen","Optimierung von Prozessen","Fehlermanagement","Code-Validierung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["kaizen","melhoria contínua","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade de código","processos de desenvolvimento","refatoração","implementação de código","tratamento de erros"],"ru":["кайдзен","непрерывное улучшение","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","процессы разработки","рефакторинг","реализация кода","обработка ошибок"],"ar":["كايزين","تحسين مستمر","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود","عمليات التطوير","إعادة هيكلة","تنفيذ الكود","معالجة الأخطاء"]}},"owner":"lips85","repo":"antigravity-skills-bootstrap","repoPath":"lips85/antigravity-skills-bootstrap","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.518Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kaizen","description":"Guide for continuous improvement, error proofing, and standardization. Use this skill when the user wants to improve code quality, refactor, or discuss process improvements.","bodyPreview":"# Kaizen: Continuous Improvement\n\n## Overview\n\nSmall improvements, continuously. Error-proof by design. Follow what works. Build only what''s needed.\n\n**Core principle:** Many small improvements beat one big change. Prevent errors at design time, not with fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always applied for:**\n\n- Code implementation and refactoring\n- Architecture and design decisions\n- Process and workflow improvements\n- Error handling and validation\n\n**Philosophy:** Quality through incremental progress","body":"# Kaizen: Continuous Improvement\n\n## Overview\n\nSmall improvements, continuously. Error-proof by design. Follow what works. Build only what''s needed.\n\n**Core principle:** Many small improvements beat one big change. Prevent errors at design time, not with fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always applied for:**\n\n- Code implementation and refactoring\n- Architecture and design decisions\n- Process and workflow improvements\n- Error handling and validation\n\n**Philosophy:** Quality through incremental progress and prevention, not perfection through massive effort.\n\n## The Four Pillars\n\n### 1. Continuous Improvement (Kaizen)\n\nSmall, frequent improvements compound into major gains.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Incremental over revolutionary:**\n\n- Make smallest viable change that improves quality\n- One improvement at a time\n- Verify each change before next\n- Build momentum through small wins\n\n**Always leave code better:**\n\n- Fix small issues as you encounter them\n- Refactor while you work (within scope)\n- Update outdated comments\n- Remove dead code when you see it\n\n**Iterative refinement:**\n\n- First version: make it work\n- Second pass: make it clear\n- Third pass: make it efficient\n- Don''t try all three at once\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Iteration 1: Make it work\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]) => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n    total += items[i].price * items[i].quantity;\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\n// Iteration 2: Make it clear (refactor)\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\nreturn items.reduce((total, item) => {\nreturn total + (item.price \\* item.quantity);\n}, 0);\n};\n\n// Iteration 3: Make it robust (add validation)\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\nif (!items?.length) return 0;\n\nreturn items.reduce((total, item) => {\nif (item.price < 0 || item.quantity < 0) {\nthrow new Error(''Price and quantity must be non-negative'');\n}\nreturn total + (item.price \\* item.quantity);\n}, 0);\n};\n\n````\nEach step is complete, tested, and working\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Trying to do everything at once\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  // Validate, optimize, add features, handle edge cases all together\n  if (!items?.length) return 0;\n  const validItems = items.filter(item => {\n    if (item.price < 0) throw new Error(''Negative price'');\n    if (item.quantity < 0) throw new Error(''Negative quantity'');\n    return item.quantity > 0; // Also filtering zero quantities\n  });\n  // Plus caching, plus logging, plus currency conversion...\n  return validItems.reduce(...); // Too many concerns at once\n};\n````\n\nOverwhelming, error-prone, hard to verify\n</Bad>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When implementing features:**\n\n1. Start with simplest version that works\n2. Add one improvement (error handling, validation, etc.)\n3. Test and verify\n4. Repeat if time permits\n5. Don''t try to make it perfect immediately\n\n**When refactoring:**\n\n- Fix one smell at a time\n- Commit after each improvement\n- Keep tests passing throughout\n- Stop when \"good enough\" (diminishing returns)\n\n**When reviewing code:**\n\n- Suggest incremental improvements (not rewrites)\n- Prioritize: critical → important → nice-to-have\n- Focus on highest-impact changes first\n- Accept \"better than before\" even if not perfect\n\n### 2. Poka-Yoke (Error Proofing)\n\nDesign systems that prevent errors at compile/design time, not runtime.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Make errors impossible:**\n\n- Type system catches mistakes\n- Compiler enforces contracts\n- Invalid states unrepresentable\n- Errors caught early (left of production)\n\n**Design for safety:**\n\n- Fail fast and loudly\n- Provide helpful error messages\n- Make correct path obvious\n- Make incorrect path difficult\n\n**Defense in layers:**\n\n1. Type system (compile time)\n2. Validation (runtime, early)\n3. Guards (preconditions)\n4. Error boundaries (graceful degradation)\n\n#### Type System Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: string status can be any value\ntype OrderBad = {\n  status: string; // Can be \"pending\", \"PENDING\", \"pnding\", anything!\n  total: number;\n};\n\n// Good: Only valid states possible\ntype OrderStatus = ''pending'' | ''processing'' | ''shipped'' | ''delivered'';\ntype Order = {\nstatus: OrderStatus;\ntotal: number;\n};\n\n// Better: States with associated data\ntype Order =\n| { status: ''pending''; createdAt: Date }\n| { status: ''processing''; startedAt: Date; estimatedCompletion: Date }\n| { status: ''shipped''; trackingNumber: string; shippedAt: Date }\n| { status: ''delivered''; deliveredAt: Date; signature: string };\n\n// Now impossible to have shipped without trackingNumber\n\n````\nType system prevents entire classes of errors\n</Good>\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Make invalid states unrepresentable\ntype NonEmptyArray<T> = [T, ...T[]];\n\nconst firstItem = <T>(items: NonEmptyArray<T>): T => {\n  return items[0]; // Always safe, never undefined!\n};\n\n// Caller must prove array is non-empty\nconst items: number[] = [1, 2, 3];\nif (items.length > 0) {\n  firstItem(items as NonEmptyArray<number>); // Safe\n}\n````\n\nFunction signature guarantees safety\n</Good>\n\n#### Validation Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: Validation after use\nconst processPayment = (amount: number) => {\n  const fee = amount * 0.03; // Used before validation!\n  if (amount <= 0) throw new Error(''Invalid amount'');\n  // ...\n};\n\n// Good: Validate immediately\nconst processPayment = (amount: number) => {\nif (amount <= 0) {\nthrow new Error(''Payment amount must be positive'');\n}\nif (amount > 10000) {\nthrow new Error(''Payment exceeds maximum allowed'');\n}\n\nconst fee = amount \\* 0.03;\n// ... now safe to use\n};\n\n// Better: Validation at boundary with branded type\ntype PositiveNumber = number & { readonly \\_\\_brand: ''PositiveNumber'' };\n\nconst validatePositive = (n: number): PositiveNumber => {\nif (n <= 0) throw new Error(''Must be positive'');\nreturn n as PositiveNumber;\n};\n\nconst processPayment = (amount: PositiveNumber) => {\n// amount is guaranteed positive, no need to check\nconst fee = amount \\* 0.03;\n};\n\n// Validate at system boundary\nconst handlePaymentRequest = (req: Request) => {\nconst amount = validatePositive(req.body.amount); // Validate once\nprocessPayment(amount); // Use everywhere safely\n};\n\n````\nValidate once at boundary, safe everywhere else\n</Good>\n\n#### Guards and Preconditions\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Early returns prevent deeply nested code\nconst processUser = (user: User | null) => {\n  if (!user) {\n    logger.error(''User not found'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!user.email) {\n    logger.error(''User email missing'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!user.isActive) {\n    logger.info(''User inactive, skipping'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Main logic here, guaranteed user is valid and active\n  sendEmail(user.email, ''Welcome!'');\n};\n````\n\nGuards make assumptions explicit and enforced\n</Good>\n\n#### Configuration Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: Optional config with unsafe defaults\ntype ConfigBad = {\n  apiKey?: string;\n  timeout?: number;\n};\n\nconst client = new APIClient({ timeout: 5000 }); // apiKey missing!\n\n// Good: Required config, fails early\ntype Config = {\napiKey: string;\ntimeout: number;\n};\n\nconst loadConfig = (): Config => {\nconst apiKey = process.env.API_KEY;\nif (!apiKey) {\nthrow new Error(''API_KEY environment variable required'');\n}\n\nreturn {\napiKey,\ntimeout: 5000,\n};\n};\n\n// App fails at startup if config invalid, not during request\nconst config = loadConfig();\nconst client = new APIClient(config);\n\n````\nFail at startup, not in production\n</Good>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When designing APIs:**\n- Use types to constrain inputs\n- Make invalid states unrepresentable\n- Return Result<T, E> instead of throwing\n- Document preconditions in types\n\n**When handling errors:**\n- Validate at system boundaries\n\n- Use guards for preconditions\n- Fail fast with clear messages\n- Log context for debugging\n\n**When configuring:**\n- Required over optional with defaults\n- Validate all config at startup\n- Fail deployment if config invalid\n- Don''t allow partial configurations\n\n### 3. Standardized Work\nFollow established patterns. Document what works. Make good practices easy to follow.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Consistency over cleverness:**\n- Follow existing codebase patterns\n- Don''t reinvent solved problems\n- New pattern only if significantly better\n- Team agreement on new patterns\n\n**Documentation lives with code:**\n- README for setup and architecture\n- CLAUDE.md for AI coding conventions\n- Comments for \"why\", not \"what\"\n- Examples for complex patterns\n\n**Automate standards:**\n- Linters enforce style\n- Type checks enforce contracts\n- Tests verify behavior\n- CI/CD enforces quality gates\n\n#### Following Patterns\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Existing codebase pattern for API clients\nclass UserAPIClient {\n  async getUser(id: string): Promise<User> {\n    return this.fetch(`/users/${id}`);\n  }\n}\n\n// New code follows the same pattern\nclass OrderAPIClient {\n  async getOrder(id: string): Promise<Order> {\n    return this.fetch(`/orders/${id}`);\n  }\n}\n````\n\nConsistency makes codebase predictable\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Existing pattern uses classes\nclass UserAPIClient { /* ... */ }\n\n// New code introduces different pattern without discussion\nconst getOrder = async (id: string): Promise<Order> => {\n// Breaking consistency \"because I prefer functions\"\n};\n\n````\nInconsistency creates confusion\n</Bad>\n\n#### Error Handling Patterns\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Project standard: Result type for recoverable errors\ntype Result<T, E> = { ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: E };\n\n// All services follow this pattern\nconst fetchUser = async (id: string): Promise<Result<User, Error>> => {\n  try {\n    const user = await db.users.findById(id);\n    if (!user) {\n      return { ok: false, error: new Error(''User not found'') };\n    }\n    return { ok: true, value: user };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { ok: false, error: err as Error };\n  }\n};\n\n// Callers use consistent pattern\nconst result = await fetchUser(''123'');\nif (!result.ok) {\n  logger.error(''Failed to fetch user'', result.error);\n  return;\n}\nconst user = result.value; // Type-safe!\n````\n\nStandard pattern across codebase\n</Good>\n\n#### Documentation Standards\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n/**\n * Retries an async operation with exponential backoff.\n *\n * Why: Network requests fail temporarily; retrying improves reliability\n * When to use: External API calls, database operations\n * When not to use: User input validation, internal function calls\n *\n * @example\n * const result = await retry(\n *   () => fetch(''https://api.example.com/data''),\n *   { maxAttempts: 3, baseDelay: 1000 }\n * );\n */\nconst retry = async <T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  options: RetryOptions\n): Promise<T> => {\n  // Implementation...\n};\n```\nDocuments why, when, and how\n</Good>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**Before adding new patterns:**\n\n- Search codebase for similar problems solved\n- Check CLAUDE.md for project conventions\n- Discuss with team if breaking from pattern\n- Update docs when introducing new pattern\n\n**When writing code:**\n\n- Match existing file structure\n- Use same naming conventions\n- Follow same error handling approach\n- Import from same locations\n\n**When reviewing:**\n\n- Check consistency with existing code\n- Point to examples in codebase\n- Suggest aligning with standards\n- Update CLAUDE.md if new standard emerges\n\n### 4. Just-In-Time (JIT)\n\nBuild what''s needed now. No more, no less. Avoid premature optimization and over-engineering.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**YAGNI (You Aren''t Gonna Need It):**\n\n- Implement only current requirements\n- No \"just in case\" features\n- No \"we might need this later\" code\n- Delete speculation\n\n**Simplest thing that works:**\n\n- Start with straightforward solution\n- Add complexity only when needed\n- Refactor when requirements change\n- Don''t anticipate future needs\n\n**Optimize when measured:**\n\n- No premature optimization\n- Profile before optimizing\n- Measure impact of changes\n- Accept \"good enough\" performance\n\n#### YAGNI in Action\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Current requirement: Log errors to console\nconst logError = (error: Error) => {\n  console.error(error.message);\n};\n```\nSimple, meets current need\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Over-engineered for \"future needs\"\ninterface LogTransport {\n  write(level: LogLevel, message: string, meta?: LogMetadata): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nclass ConsoleTransport implements LogTransport { /_... _/ }\nclass FileTransport implements LogTransport { /_ ... _/ }\nclass RemoteTransport implements LogTransport { /_ ..._/ }\n\nclass Logger {\nprivate transports: LogTransport[] = [];\nprivate queue: LogEntry[] = [];\nprivate rateLimiter: RateLimiter;\nprivate formatter: LogFormatter;\n\n// 200 lines of code for \"maybe we''ll need it\"\n}\n\nconst logError = (error: Error) => {\nLogger.getInstance().log(''error'', error.message);\n};\n\n````\nBuilding for imaginary future requirements\n</Bad>\n\n**When to add complexity:**\n- Current requirement demands it\n- Pain points identified through use\n- Measured performance issues\n- Multiple use cases emerged\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Start simple\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number): string => {\n  return `$${amount.toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n\n// Requirement evolves: support multiple currencies\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number, currency: string): string => {\n  const symbols = { USD: ''$'', EUR: ''€'', GBP: ''£'' };\n  return `${symbols[currency]}${amount.toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n\n// Requirement evolves: support localization\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number, locale: string): string => {\n  return new Intl.NumberFormat(locale, {\\n    style: ''currency'',\n    currency: locale === ''en-US'' ? ''USD'' : ''EUR'',\n  }).format(amount);\n};\n````\n\nComplexity added only when needed\n</Good>\n\n#### Premature Abstraction\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// One use case, but building generic framework\nabstract class BaseCRUDService<T> {\n  abstract getAll(): Promise<T[]>;\n  abstract getById(id: string): Promise<T>;\n  abstract create(data: Partial<T>): Promise<T>;\n  abstract update(id: string, data: Partial<T>): Promise<T>;\n  abstract delete(id: string): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nclass GenericRepository<T> { /_300 lines _/ }\nclass QueryBuilder<T> { /_ 200 lines_/ }\n// ... building entire ORM for single table\n\n````\nMassive abstraction for uncertain future\n</Bad>\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Simple functions for current needs\nconst getUsers = async (): Promise<User[]> => {\n  return db.query(''SELECT * FROM users'');\n};\n\nconst getUserById = async (id: string): Promise<User | null> => {\n  return db.query(''SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1'', [id]);\n};\n\n// When pattern emerges across multiple entities, then abstract\n````\n\nAbstract only when pattern proven across 3+ cases\n</Good>\n\n#### Performance Optimization\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Current: Simple approach\nconst filterActiveUsers = (users: User[]): User[] => {\n  return users.filter(user => user.isActive);\n};\n\n// Benchmark shows: 50ms for 1000 users (acceptable)\n// ✓ Ship it, no optimization needed\n\n// Later: After profiling shows this is bottleneck\n// Then optimize with indexed lookup or caching\n\n````\nOptimize based on measurement, not assumptions\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Premature optimization\nconst filterActiveUsers = (users: User[]): User[] => {\n  // \"This might be slow, so let''s cache and index\"\n  const cache = new WeakMap();\n  const indexed = buildBTreeIndex(users, ''isActive'');\n  // 100 lines of optimization code\n  // Adds complexity, harder to maintain\n  // No evidence it was needed\n};\\\n````\n\nComplex solution for unmeasured problem\n</Bad>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When implementing:**\n\n- Solve the immediate problem\n- Use straightforward approach\n- Resist \"what if\" thinking\n- Delete speculative code\n\n**When optimizing:**\n\n- Profile first, optimize second\n- Measure before and after\n- Document why optimization needed\n- Keep simple version in tests\n\n**When abstracting:**\n\n- Wait for 3+ similar cases (Rule of Three)\n- Make abstraction as simple as possible\n- Prefer duplication over wrong abstraction\n- Refactor when pattern clear\n\n## Integration with Commands\n\nThe Kaizen skill guides how you work. The commands provide structured analysis:\n\n- **`/why`**: Root cause analysis (5 Whys)\n- **`/cause-and-effect`**: Multi-factor analysis (Fishbone)\n- **`/plan-do-check-act`**: Iterative improvement cycles\n- **`/analyse-problem`**: Comprehensive documentation (A3)\n- **`/analyse`**: Smart method selection (Gemba/VSM/Muda)\n\nUse commands for structured problem-solving. Apply skill for day-to-day development.\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Violating Continuous Improvement:**\n\n- \"I''ll refactor it later\" (never happens)\n- Leaving code worse than you found it\n- Big bang rewrites instead of incremental\n\n**Violating Poka-Yoke:**\n\n- \"Users should just be careful\"\n- Validation after use instead of before\n- Optional config with no validation\n\n**Violating Standardized Work:**\n\n- \"I prefer to do it my way\"\n- Not checking existing patterns\n- Ignoring project conventions\n\n**Violating Just-In-Time:**\n\n- \"We might need this someday\"\n- Building frameworks before using them\n- Optimizing without measuring\n\n## Remember\n\n**Kaizen is about:**\n\n- Small improvements continuously\n- Preventing errors by design\n- Following proven patterns\n- Building only what''s needed\n\n**Not about:**\n\n- Perfection on first try\n- Massive refactoring projects\n- Clever abstractions\n- Premature optimization\n\n**Mindset:** Good enough today, better tomorrow. Repeat.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:19:37.012Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Process Optimization Agents seeking incremental improvement methodologies","zh":"适合于寻求增量改进方法的流程优化代理","ja":"プロセス最適化エージェントが.incremental 改善方法を求める場合に適しています","ko":"증분적 개선 방법을 찾는 프로세스 최적화 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Optimización de Procesos que buscan metodologías de mejora incremental","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Optimisation de Processus qui recherchent des méthodologies d''amélioration incrémentale","de":"Ideal für Prozessoptimierungsagenten, die inkrementelle Verbesserungsmethoden suchen","pt":"Ideal for Process Optimization Agents seeking incremental improvement methodologies","ru":"Ideal for Process Optimization Agents seeking incremental improvement methodologies","ar":"Ideal for Process Optimization Agents seeking incremental improvement methodologies"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement continuous improvement through small, error-proof design changes, utilizing core principles like preventing errors at design time and building only what''s needed, with applications in code refactoring, architecture decisions, and process improvements","zh":"使代理能够通过小的、无误的设计更改来实现持续改进，利用设计时防止错误和只构建所需的核心原则，并应用于代码重构、架构决策和流程改进","ja":"エージェントが、小さくてエラーのない設計変更を通じて継続的な改善を実現できるようにし、設計時におけるエラーの防止や必要なものだけを構築するというコア原則を利用し、コードのリファクタリング、Architecture の決定、プロセスの改善に適用します","ko":"에이전트가 작은 오류 없는 설계 변경을 통해 지속적인 개선을 구현할 수 있도록 해주며, 설계 시 오류 방지 및 필요한 것만 구축하는 핵심 원리에 따르며, 코드 개선, 아키텍처 결정, 프로세스 개선에 적용됩니다","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar mejoras continuas a través de pequeños cambios de diseño a prueba de errores, utilizando principios básicos como la prevención de errores en el momento del diseño y la construcción solo de lo necesario, con aplicaciones en la refactorización de código, decisiones de arquitectura y mejoras de proceso","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des améliorations continues grâce à de petits changements de conception à l''épreuve des erreurs, en utilisant des principes de base tels que la prévention des erreurs au moment de la conception et la construction de ce qui est nécessaire, avec des applications dans la refactoring de code, les décisions d''architecture et les améliorations de processus","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, kontinuierliche Verbesserungen durch kleine, fehlerfreie Designänderungen umzusetzen, indem es grundlegende Prinzipien wie die Vermeidung von Fehlern bei der Designzeit und den Bau nur dessen, was benötigt wird, verwendet, mit Anwendungen in der Code-Refactoring, Architekturentscheidungen und Prozessverbesserungen","pt":"Empowers agents to implement continuous improvement through small, error-proof design changes, utilizing core principles like preventing errors at design time and building only what''s needed, with applications in code refactoring, architecture decisions, and process improvements","ru":"Empowers agents to implement continuous improvement through small, error-proof design changes, utilizing core principles like preventing errors at design time and building only what''s needed, with applications in code refactoring, architecture decisions, and process improvements","ar":"Empowers agents to implement continuous improvement through small, error-proof design changes, utilizing core principles like preventing errors at design time and building only what''s needed, with applications in code refactoring, architecture decisions, and process improvements"},"useCases":{"en":["Streamlining code implementation and refactoring","Enhancing architecture and design decisions","Improving process and workflow efficiency","Implementing robust error handling and validation"],"zh":["简化代码实现和重构","增强架构和设计决策","提高流程和工作流效率","实施强大的错误处理和验证"],"ja":["コード実装とリファクタリングの最適化","アーキテクチャと設計の決定の強化","プロセスとワークフローの効率性の向上","堅牢なエラー処理と検証の実施"],"ko":["코드 구현 및 리팩토링의 간소화","아키텍처 및 설계 결정의 강화","프로세스 및 워크플로우 효율성의 향상","강력한 오류 처리 및 검증의 구현"],"es":["Optimización de la implementación de código y refactorización","Mejora de la arquitectura y las decisiones de diseño","Mejora de la eficiencia del proceso y del flujo de trabajo","Implementación de una gestión de errores y validación robusta"],"fr":["Optimisation de la mise en œuvre du code et refactoring","Amélioration de l''architecture et des décisions de conception","Amélioration de l''efficacité du processus et du flux de travail","Mise en œuvre d''une gestion des erreurs et de validation robuste"],"de":["Optimierung der Code-Implementierung und Refactoring","Verbesserung der Architektur und der Designentscheidungen","Verbesserung der Prozesseffizienz und des Arbeitsablaufs","Implementierung einer robusten Fehlernachverfolgung und Validierung"],"pt":["Streamlining code implementation and refactoring","Enhancing architecture and design decisions","Improving process and workflow efficiency","Implementing robust error handling and validation"],"ru":["Streamlining code implementation and refactoring","Enhancing architecture and design decisions","Improving process and workflow efficiency","Implementing robust error handling and validation"],"ar":["Streamlining code implementation and refactoring","Enhancing