rrollo dirigido por pruebas a la documentación de procesos, mejorando la calidad y la eficiencia","fr":"Les compétences en écriture appliquent le développement piloté par les tests à la documentation de processus, améliorant la qualité et l''efficacité","de":"Die Schreibfähigkeiten wenden das testgetriebene Entwicklung auf die Prozessdokumentation an, um die Qualität und Effizienz zu verbessern","pt":"As habilidades de escrita aplicam TDD à documentação de processos, melhorando a eficiência","ru":"Навыки письма применяют TDD к документации процессов, повышая эффективность","ar":"مهارات الكتابة تطبق التطوير القائم على الاختبار على توثيق العمليات، مما يحسن الفعالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","文档化","测试案例","重构","文档准确性","文档完整性"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","文書化","テストケース","リファクタリング","文書の正確性","文書の完全性"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","문서화","테스트 케이스","리팩터링","문서 정확성","문서 완전성"],"es":["Desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","Documentación de procesos","Pruebas de escenarios de presión","Refactorización de código","Mejora de la calidad y la eficiencia","Integración con agentes específicos"],"fr":["Développement piloté par les tests","Documentation de processus","Tests de scénarios de pression","Refactorisation de code","Amélioration de la qualité et de l''efficacité","Intégration avec des agents spécifiques"],"de":["Testgetriebene Entwicklung","Prozessdokumentation","Drucktestszenarien","Code-Refaktorisierung","Qualitäts- und Effizienzsteigerung","Integration mit agentspezifischen Verzeichnissen"],"pt":["Aplicação de TDD à documentação de processos","Melhoria da eficiência na escrita de documentação","Uso de testes para garantir a qualidade da documentação","Refinamento contínuo da documentação","Integração com agentes específicos"],"ru":["Применение TDD к документации процессов","Повышение эффективности написания документации","Использование тестов для обеспечения качества документации","Постоянное усовершенствование документации","Интеграция с агентами-специалистами"],"ar":["تطبيق التطوير القائم على الاختبار على توثيق العمليات","تحسين الفعالية في كتابة التوثيق","استخدام الاختبارات لضمان جودة التوثيق","تحسين التوثيق المستمر","التكامل مع الوكلاء المحددين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","文档化","编写技能","测试案例","重构","文档准确性","文档完整性","开发文档"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","文書化","書き込みスキル","テストケース","リファクタリング","文書の正確性","文書の完全性","開発文書"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","문서화","작성 스킬","테스트 케이스","리팩터링","문서 정확성","문서 완전성","개발 문서"],"es":["habilidades de escritura","desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","documentación de procesos","pruebas de software","refactorización de código","mejora de la calidad","eficiencia en el desarrollo","agentes específicos","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["compétences en écriture","développement piloté par les tests","documentation de processus","tests de logiciel","refactorisation de code","amélioration de la qualité","efficacité dans le développement","agents spécifiques","développement de logiciel"],"de":["Schreibfähigkeiten","testgetriebene Entwicklung","Prozessdokumentation","Software-Tests","Code-Refaktorisierung","Qualitätssteigerung","Effizienzsteigerung im Entwicklung","agentspezifische Verzeichnisse","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["habilidades de escrita","TDD","documentação de processos","testes","refinamento","agentes específicos","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["навыки письма","TDD","документация процессов","тесты","усовершенствование","агенты-специалисты","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مهارات الكتابة","التطوير القائم على الاختبار","توثيق العمليات","الاختبارات","التحسين","الوكلاء المحددين","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"jlaws","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"jlaws/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"writing-skills","description":"Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment","bodyPreview":"# Writing Skills\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal skills live in agent-specific directories (`~/.claude/skills` for Claude Code, `~/.codex/skills` for Codex)**\n\nYou write test cases (pressure scenarios with subagents), watch them fail (baseline behavior), write the skill (documentation), watch tests pass (agents comply), and refactor (close loopholes).\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch an agent fail without the skill, you don''t k","body":"# Writing Skills\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal skills live in agent-specific directories (`~/.claude/skills` for Claude Code, `~/.codex/skills` for Codex)**\n\nYou write test cases (pressure scenarios with subagents), watch them fail (baseline behavior), write the skill (documentation), watch tests pass (agents comply), and refactor (close loopholes).\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch an agent fail without the skill, you don''t know if the skill teaches the right thing.\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\n**Create when:** Technique wasn''t intuitively obvious, reusable across projects, pattern applies broadly, others would benefit.\n\n**Don''t create for:** One-off solutions, standard well-documented practices, project-specific conventions (use CLAUDE.md), mechanically enforceable constraints (automate instead).\n\n## Skill Types\n\n- **Technique**: Concrete method with steps (condition-based-waiting)\n- **Pattern**: Way of thinking about problems (flatten-with-flags)\n- **Reference**: API docs, syntax guides, tool documentation\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\nskills/\n  skill-name/\n    SKILL.md              # Main reference (required)\n    supporting-file.*     # Only if needed\n```\n\nSeparate files for: heavy reference (100+ lines), reusable tools. Keep everything else inline.\n\n## SKILL.md Structure\n\n**Frontmatter:** Only `name` (letters/numbers/hyphens) and `description` (max 1024 chars, third-person, starts with \"Use when...\")\n\n**CRITICAL:** Description = triggering conditions ONLY. Never summarize the skill''s workflow in description. Testing showed Claude follows description shortcuts instead of reading skill body.\n\n```yaml\n# BAD: Summarizes workflow\ndescription: Use when executing plans - dispatches subagent per task with code review between tasks\n\n# GOOD: Just triggers\ndescription: Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session\n```\n\n**Body structure:**\n```markdown\n# Skill Name\n## Overview (1-2 sentences, core principle)\n## When to Use (flowchart IF decision non-obvious, bullets with symptoms)\n## Core Pattern (before/after code)\n## Quick Reference (table/bullets)\n## Common Mistakes (what goes wrong + fixes)\n```\n\n## Claude Search Optimization (CSO)\n\n- Use concrete triggers/symptoms in description, not language-specific symptoms\n- Include keywords Claude would search: error messages, symptoms, tool names\n- Name by what you DO: `condition-based-waiting` not `async-test-helpers`\n- Gerunds work well: `creating-skills`, `debugging-with-logs`\n\n**Token Efficiency:**\n- Getting-started workflows: <150 words\n- Frequently-loaded skills: <200 words\n- Other skills: <500 words\n- Move details to `--help`, use cross-references, compress examples\n\n**Cross-References:** Use `**REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:skill-name`. Never use `@` links (force-loads, burns context).\n\n## Flowchart Usage\n\nUse ONLY for: non-obvious decisions, process loops, \"when to use A vs B\".\nNever for: reference material, code examples, linear instructions.\n\n## The Iron Law (Same as TDD)\n\n```\nNO SKILL WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nApplies to new skills AND edits. Write skill before testing? Delete it. Start over. No exceptions.\n\n## RED-GREEN-REFACTOR for Skills\n\n**RED:** Run pressure scenario WITHOUT skill. Document exact failures and rationalizations.\n\n**GREEN:** Write minimal skill addressing those specific failures. Re-test with skill.\n\n**REFACTOR:** Agent found new rationalization? Add explicit counter. Re-test until bulletproof.\n\n## Testing Skills With Subagents\n\nRun scenarios without skill (RED), write skill addressing failures (GREEN), close loopholes (REFACTOR).\n\n### RED Phase: Baseline Testing\n\nRun pressure scenario WITHOUT skill. Document exact failures.\n\n**Process:**\n- [ ] Create pressure scenarios (3+ combined pressures)\n- [ ] Run WITHOUT skill\n- [ ] Document choices and rationalizations verbatim\n- [ ] Identify patterns\n\n### Pressure Types\n\n| Pressure | Example |\n|----------|---------|\n| Time | Emergency, deadline, deploy window |\n| Sunk cost | Hours of work, \"waste\" to delete |\n| Authority | Senior says skip it |\n| Exhaustion | End of day, want to go home |\n| Pragmatic | \"Being pragmatic vs dogmatic\" |\n\n**Best tests combine 3+ pressures.**\n\n### Key Elements\n1. Concrete A/B/C choices (not open-ended)\n2. Real constraints (specific times, consequences)\n3. Real file paths\n4. Make agent act (\"What do you do?\" not \"What should you do?\")\n\n### REFACTOR Phase: Close Loopholes\n\nCapture new rationalizations verbatim. For each, add:\n1. **Explicit negation** in rules\n2. **Rationalization table** entry\n3. **Red flag** entry\n4. **Updated description** with violation symptoms\n\nRe-test after each refactor. Continue until no new rationalizations.\n\n### Meta-Testing\n\nAfter agent chooses wrong: \"You read the skill and chose wrong. How could it be clearer?\"\n\nThree responses:\n1. \"Skill WAS clear, I chose to ignore\" -> Need stronger foundational principle\n2. \"Skill should have said X\" -> Add their suggestion\n3. \"I didn''t see section Y\" -> Make it more prominent\n\n## Persuasion Principles for Skill Design\n\nLLMs respond to the same persuasion principles as humans. Meincke et al. (2025) tested 7 principles with N=28,000 AI conversations. Persuasion techniques doubled compliance rates (33% -> 72%, p < .001).\n\n### Effective Principles\n\n- **Authority**: Imperative language (\"YOU MUST\", \"Never\", \"Always\"), non-negotiable framing. For discipline-enforcing skills.\n- **Commitment**: Require announcements, force explicit choices. For ensuring skills are followed.\n- **Scarcity**: Time-bound requirements (\"Before proceeding\"), sequential dependencies. For immediate verification.\n- **Social Proof**: Universal patterns (\"Every time\", \"Always\"), failure modes. For documenting universal practices.\n- **Unity**: Collaborative language (\"our codebase\", \"we''re colleagues\"). For collaborative workflows.\n- **Reciprocity & Liking**: Use sparingly or avoid.\n\n| Skill Type | Use | Avoid |\n|------------|-----|-------|\n| Discipline-enforcing | Authority + Commitment + Social Proof | Liking, Reciprocity |\n| Guidance/technique | Moderate Authority + Unity | Heavy authority |\n| Collaborative | Unity + Commitment | Authority, Liking |\n| Reference | Clarity only | All persuasion |\n\n## Anthropic Best Practices\n\n### Core Principles\n- **Concise is key**: Only add what Claude doesn''t already know. Challenge each piece: \"Does Claude need this?\"\n- **Degrees of freedom**: High (text instructions) for multiple valid approaches; Medium (pseudocode) for preferred patterns; Low (exact scripts) for fragile operations\n\n### Anti-Patterns\n- Offering too many library options (provide a default with escape hatch)\n- Assuming packages installed (list dependencies)\n- Deeply nested references (keep one level deep)\n- Time-sensitive information (use \"old patterns\" section)\n\n### Evaluation-Driven Development\n1. Run Claude on tasks without Skill, document failures\n2. Create 3+ evaluation scenarios\n3. Establish baseline performance\n4. Write minimal instructions to pass evaluations\n5. Iterate: evaluate, compare baseline, refine\n\n## Skill Creation Checklist\n\n**RED Phase:**\n- [ ] Create pressure scenarios (3+ combined pressures for discipline skills)\n- [ ] Run WITHOUT skill - document baseline failures verbatim\n- [ ] Identify rationalization patterns\n\n**GREEN Phase:**\n- [ ] YAML frontmatter: name (letters/numbers/hyphens), description (Use when..., third-person)\n- [ ] Address specific baseline failures\n- [ ] Keywords throughout for search\n- [ ] One excellent code example (not multi-language)\n- [ ] Run WITH skill - verify compliance\n\n**REFACTOR Phase:**\n- [ ] Add counters for new rationalizations\n- [ ] Build rationalization table and red flags list\n- [ ] Re-test until bulletproof\n\n**Deployment:**\n- [ ] Commit and push\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:22:37.188Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and Codex needing advanced process documentation through Test-Driven Development","zh":"适合于 Claude Code 和 Codex 等需要高级过程文档和测试驱动开发的 AI 代理","ja":"Claude CodeやCodexのような高度なプロセス文書化とテスト駆動開発を必要とするAIエージェントに最適","ko":"클라우드 코드 및 코декс와 같은 고급 프로세스 문서화 및 테스트 주도 개발이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y Codex que necesitan documentación de procesos avanzada a través del Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code et Codex ayant besoin d''une documentation de processus avancée via le Développement Dirigé par les Tests","de":"Ideal für KI-Agenten wie Claude Code und Codex, die eine fortgeschrittene Prozessdokumentation durch testgetriebene Entwicklung benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e Codex que necessitam de documentação de processo avançada por meio do Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и Codex, которые требуют продвинутой документации процесса через Test-Driven Development","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي مثل Claude Code و Codex التي تحتاج إلى توثيق متقدم للعمليات من خلال التطوير الموجه بالاختبار"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply Test-Driven Development principles to writing skills, utilizing pressure scenarios and subagents for robust documentation, ensuring compliance through test cases and continuous refactoring, all within agent-specific directories like ~/.claude/skills","zh":"使得代理能够将测试驱动开发原则应用于写作技能，利用压力场景和子代理进行强大的文档编制，通过测试用例和持续重构确保合规性，所有这些都在代理特定的目录中完成，如 ~/.claude/skills","ja":"エージェントがテスト駆動開発の原則を書き込みスキルに適用できるようにし、圧力シナリオとサブエージェントを使用して堅牢なドキュメントを生成し、テストケースと継続的なリファクタリングを通じてコンプライアンスを確保する。これらはすべて、~/.claude/skillsのようなエージェント固有のディレクトリ内で実行される","ko":"에이전트가 테스트 주도 개발 원칙을 작성技能에 적용할 수 있도록 하며, 압력 시나리오와 하위 에이전트를 사용하여 견고한 문서를 생성하고, 테스트 케이스와 지속적인 리팩토링을 통해 규정 준수를 보장하며, 모든 내용은 ~/.claude/skills와 같은 에이전트 전용 디렉토리 내에서 처리됨","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar los principios del Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas a las habilidades de escritura, utilizando escenarios de presión y subagentes para una documentación robusta, garantizando el cumplimiento a través de casos de prueba y refactorización continua, todo dentro de directorios específicos del agente como ~/.claude/skills","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer les principes du Développement Dirigé par les Tests aux compétences d''écriture, en utilisant des scénarios de pression et des sous-agents pour une documentation robuste, en garantissant la conformité via des cas de test et une refactoring continue, le tout au sein de répertoires spécifiques à l''agent comme ~/.claude/skills","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die Prinzipien der testgetriebenen Entwicklung auf Schreibfähigkeiten anzuwenden, unter Nutzung von Druckszenarien und Subagenten für eine robuste Dokumentation, um die Einhaltung durch Testfälle und kontinuierliche Refactoring sicherzustellen, alles innerhalb von agentenspezifischen Verzeichnissen wie ~/.claude/skills","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar os princípios do Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes às habilidades de escrita, utilizando cenários de pressão e subagentes para documentação robusta, garantindo a conformidade por meio de casos de teste e refatoração contínua, tudo dentro de diretórios específicos do agente, como ~/.claude/skills","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять принципы Test-Driven Development к навыкам письма, используя сценарии давления и субагентов для создания прочной документации, обеспечивая соблюдение требований посредством тестовых случаев и непрерывной рефакторинга, все в рамках директорий, специфичных для агента, таких как ~/.claude/skills","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تطبيق مبادئ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار على مهارات الكتابة، باستخدام سيناريوهات الضغط والوكيلات الفرعية للتوثيق المتين، وضمان الامتثال من خلال حالات الاختبار وإعادة الهيكلة المستمرة، وكل ذلك داخل دلائل محددة للوكيل، مثل ~/.claude/skills"},"useCases":{"en":["Writing test cases for pressure scenarios","Refactoring documentation to close loopholes","Ensuring agent compliance through passing test cases"],"zh":["编写压力场景的测试用例","重构文档以关闭漏洞","通过测试用例确保代理合规性"],"ja":["圧力シナリオのテストケースを書き込む","ドキュメントをリファクタリングしてループホールを閉じる","テストケースをパスすることでエージェントのコンプライアンスを確保する"],"ko":["압력 시나리오에 대한 테스트 케이스 작성","문서를 리팩토링하여 루프홀을 닫음","테스트 케이스를 통과하여 에이전트 규정 준수를 보장"],"es":["Escribir casos de prueba para escenarios de presión","Reestructurar la documentación para cerrar lagunas","Garantizar el cumplimiento del agente a través de casos de prueba aprobados"],"fr":["Écrire des cas de test pour les scénarios de pression","Réorganiser la documentation pour fermer les lacunes","Assurer la conformité de l''agent via des cas de test passés"],"de":["Testfälle für Druckszenarien schreiben","Dokumentation umstrukturieren, um Lücken zu schließen","Sicherstellen, dass der Agent die Testfälle besteht und somit die Einhaltung gewährleistet"],"pt":["Escrita de casos de teste para cenários de pressão","Refatoração de documentação para fechar lacunas","Garantia de conformidade do agente por meio de casos de teste aprovados"],"ru":["Написание тестовых случаев для сценариев давления","Рефакторинг документации для закрытия лазеек","Обеспечение соблюдения агентом требований посредством проходящих тестовых случаев"],"ar":["كتابة حالات اختبار لسيناريوهات الضغط","إعادة هيكلة التوثيق لإغلاق الثغرات","ضمان امتثال الوكيل من خلال حالات الاختبار الناجحة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires agent-specific directory setup","Limited to Test-Driven Development methodology"],"zh":["需要代理特定的目录设置","仅限于测试驱动开发方法论"],"ja":["エージェント固有のディレクトリ設定が必要","テスト駆動開発方法論のみに限定される"],"ko":["에이전트 전용 디렉토리 설정이 필요","테스트 주도 개발 방법론에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere configuración de directorio específico del agente","Limitado a la metodología de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de répertoire spécifique à l''agent","Limité à la méthodologie du Développement Dirigé par les Tests"],"de":["Benötigt eine agentenspezifische Verzeichniskonfiguration","Begrenzt auf die Methodik der testgetriebenen Entwicklung"],"pt":["Requer configuração de diretório específico do agente","Limitado à metodologia do Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes"],"ru":["Требует настройки директории, специфичной для агента","Ограничен методологией Test-Driven Development"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد دليل محدد للوكيل","محدود بمетодولوجيا التطوير الموجه بالاختبار"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
