 Überprüfung von Dokumentation","Überprüfung von Problemen und Branches","Analyse der Repository-Struktur","Benutzerdefinierte Benachrichtigungen und Warnungen","Integration mit Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Verificação de frescor da documentação","Verificação de problemas e branches","Verificação da estrutura do repositório","Execução periódica de verificações de saúde","Integração com o ciclo de vida do código"],"ru":["Проверка свежести документации","Проверка проблем и веток","Проверка структуры репозитория","Регулярное выполнение проверок здоровья","Интеграция с жизненным циклом кода"],"ar":["فحص طازجة التوثيق","فحص المشاكل والفروع","فحص هيكل المستودع","تشغيل دوري لفحوصات الصحة","التكامل مع دورة حياة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["staleness-check","代码库健康检查","文档新鲜度","问题跟踪","分支管理","存储库结构优化","代码库维护"],"ja":["staleness-check","コードベースのヘルスチェック","ドキュメントの新鮮度","問題の追跡","ブランチ管理","リポジトリ構造の最適化","コードベースのメンテナンス"],"ko":["staleness-check","코드베이스 건강 체크","문서 신선도","문제 추적","분기 관리","저장소 구조 최적화","코드베이스 유지 보수"],"es":["comprobación de obsolescencia","mantenimiento de proyectos","documentación actualizada","problemas y ramas","estructura de repositorio","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["vérification de l''obsolescence","maintenance de projets","documentation à jour","problèmes et branches","structure du référentiel","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["Überprüfung von Veraltetheit","Wartung von Projekten","aktualisierte Dokumentation","Probleme und Branches","Repository-Struktur","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["verificador de obsolescência","ferramenta de verificação de código","manutenção de código","documentação de código","verificação de saúde","ciclo de vida do código"],"ru":["проверка устаревшего кода","инструмент проверки кода","поддержка кода","документация кода","проверка здоровья","жизненный цикл кода"],"ar":["فحص القديم","أداة فحص الكود","صيانة الكود","توثيق الكود","فحص الصحة","دورة حياة الكود"]}},"owner":"AJB-ajb","repo":"MeshIt","repoPath":"AJB-ajb/MeshIt","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"staleness-check","description":"Checks for stale artifacts across the repo — outdated docs, orphaned issues, stale branches, and repo structure drift. Run weekly or before releases.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Staleness Check\n\nPeriodic health check for documentation, issues, branches, and repo structure. Ensures everything stays current as the codebase evolves.\n\n## When to Run\n\n- Weekly (recommended)\n- Before major releases\n- After completing a milestone or closing an epic\n- When onboarding new contributors\n\n## Checklist\n\n### 1. Documentation Freshness (HIGH)\n\n| Check                                  | Rule               | How                                     |\n| ---------------------------------","body":"# Staleness Check\n\nPeriodic health check for documentation, issues, branches, and repo structure. Ensures everything stays current as the codebase evolves.\n\n## When to Run\n\n- Weekly (recommended)\n- Before major releases\n- After completing a milestone or closing an epic\n- When onboarding new contributors\n\n## Checklist\n\n### 1. Documentation Freshness (HIGH)\n\n| Check                                  | Rule               | How                                     |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------- |\n| `docs/` files match current code       | `stale-docs`       | Compare docs claims against actual code |\n| `spec/` files reflect current features | `stale-specs`      | Check spec vs implementation            |\n| `data-model.md` matches DB schema      | `stale-data-model` | Compare with migrations                 |\n| README.md is accurate                  | `stale-readme`     | Verify setup instructions work          |\n| `.AGENTS.md` conventions are current   | `stale-agents`     | Check commands, paths, patterns         |\n\n### 2. GitHub Issues (MEDIUM)\n\n| Check                             | Rule           | How                                 |\n| --------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| Open issues are still relevant    | `stale-issues` | Review open issues                  |\n| Labels are consistent             | `stale-issues` | Check for orphaned labels           |\n| Milestones are up to date         | `stale-issues` | Verify milestone assignments        |\n| `untested` issues track real gaps | `stale-issues` | Cross-ref with actual test coverage |\n\n### 3. Branches (MEDIUM)\n\n| Check                  | Rule             | How                                 |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| Stale remote branches  | `stale-branches` | Branches not touched in 2+ weeks    |\n| Merged but not deleted | `stale-branches` | Branches already merged to dev/main |\n| Worktrees still needed | `stale-branches` | Check `.handoffs/` for active tasks |\n\n### 4. Repo Structure (LOW)\n\n| Check                       | Rule              | How                                  |\n| --------------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Empty or unused directories | `stale-structure` | `find` for empty dirs                |\n| Orphaned files              | `stale-structure` | Files not imported anywhere          |\n| Config drift                | `stale-structure` | package.json scripts, tsconfig paths |\n\n## Output Format\n\n```markdown\n## Staleness Report - [date]\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [STALE] `docs/foo.md` — References removed component `Bar` (line 42)\n- [OK] `docs/data-model.md` — Matches current schema\n- [UPDATE NEEDED] `spec/matching.md` — Missing new location_mode dimension\n\n### Issues\n\n- [STALE] #N — \"Title\" — No activity in 30 days, may be resolved\n- [CLOSE] #N — \"Title\" — Resolved by PR #M but not closed\n- [UPDATE] #N — \"Title\" — Scope changed, description needs refresh\n\n### Branches\n\n- [DELETE] `feat/old-feature` — Merged 3 weeks ago, not deleted\n- [STALE] `fix/something` — Last commit 4 weeks ago, no PR\n\n### Structure\n\n- [EMPTY] `src/components/voice/` — All files removed in redesign\n- [ORPHAN] `scripts/check-credits.sh` — References deleted doc\n\n### Summary\n\n- Stale items: N\n- Actions needed: N\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:24:25.436Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Maintenance Agents needing periodic repository health checks and documentation freshness analysis.","zh":"适合需要定期存储库健康检查和文档新鲜度分析的代码维护代理。","ja":"周期的なリポジトリのヘルスチェックやドキュメントの新鮮度分析が必要なコードメンテナンスエージェントに適しています。","ko":"주기적인 저장소 상태 체크 및 문서 신선도 분석이 필요한 코드 유지 보수 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Mantenimiento de Código que necesitan controles periódicos de salud del repositorio y análisis de frescura de la documentación.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Maintenance de Code nécessitant des vérifications périodiques de la santé du référentiel et une analyse de fraîcheur de la documentation.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Wartungsagenten, die regelmäßige Repository-Health-Checks und Analysen der Dokumentationsfrische benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Manutenção de Código que necessitam de verificações periódicas de saúde do repositório e análise de frescor da documentação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по техническому обслуживанию кода, которым требуются периодические проверки здоровья репозитория и анализ свежести документации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل صيانة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى فحص صحة المخزن الدوري وتحليل свежة الوثائق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ensure codebase consistency and accuracy by performing weekly staleness checks, verifying documentation freshness, and validating repo structure using protocols like GitHub API, and file formats like Markdown.","zh":"通过执行每周陈旧度检查、验证文档新鲜度和使用GitHub API等协议以及Markdown等文件格式验证仓库结构，赋予代理确保代码库一致性和准确性的能力。","ja":"GitHub APIなどのプロトコルやMarkdownなどのファイル形式を使用して、毎週の古さチェック、ドキュメントの新鮮度の検証、リポジトリ構造の検証を行うことで、コードベースの整合性と正確性を確保するエージェントの能力を提供します。","ko":"GitHub API와 같은 프로토콜 및 Markdown와 같은 파일 형식을 사용하여 주간陈旧성 확인, 문서 신선도 확인 및 저장소 구조 확인을 통해 코드베이스 일관성 및 정확성을 보장하는 에이전트의 능력을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a garantizar la coherencia y precisión del código base mediante la realización de controles semanales de obsolescencia, verificando la frescura de la documentación y validando la estructura del repositorio utilizando protocolos como GitHub API y formatos de archivo como Markdown.","fr":"Permet aux agents de garantir la cohérence et l''exactitude du code base en effectuant des vérifications hebdomadaires de l''obsolescence, en vérifiant la fraîcheur de la documentation et en validant la structure du référentiel en utilisant des protocoles comme GitHub API et des formats de fichier comme Markdown.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Konsistenz und Genauigkeit des Codebases sicherzustellen, indem sie wöchentliche Überprüfungen auf Veraltetheit durchführen, die Frische der Dokumentation überprüfen und die Repository-Struktur mithilfe von Protokollen wie GitHub API und Dateiformaten wie Markdown validieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a garantir a consistência e precisão da base de código, realizando verificações semanais de obsolescência, verificando a frescura da documentação e validando a estrutura do repositório usando protocolos como GitHub API e formatos de arquivo como Markdown.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить последовательность и точность кодовой базы, выполняя еженедельные проверки на устаревание, проверяя свежесть документации и проверяя структуру репозитория с использованием протоколов, таких как GitHub API, и форматов файлов, таких как Markdown.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على ضمان اتحاد و دقة قاعدة الشفرة من خلال أداء فحوصات أسبوعية للتعفن ، و التحقق من свежة الوثائق ، و التحقق من هيكل المستودع باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل واجهة برمجة تطبيقات GitHub و صيغ الملفات مثل Markdown."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating weekly repository health checks","Validating documentation freshness before major releases","Debugging inconsistencies in repo structure after milestone completion"],"zh":["自动执行每周存储库健康检查","在主要版本发布前验证文档新鲜度","完成里程碑后调试存储库结构中的不一致性"],"ja":["毎週のリポジトリのヘルスチェックを自動化する","主要なリリースの前にドキュメントの新鮮度を検証する","マイルストーンを完了した後にリポジトリ構造の不一致をデバッグする"],"ko":["주간 저장소 상태 체크 자동화","주요 버전 릴리스 전에 문서 신선도 확인","마일스톤 완료 후 저장소 구조의 불일치 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar controles semanales de salud del repositorio","Validar la frescura de la documentación antes de los lanzamientos importantes","Depurar inconsistencias en la estructura del repositorio después de la finalización de un hito"],"fr":["Automatiser les vérifications hebdomadaires de la santé du référentiel","Valider la fraîcheur de la documentation avant les versions majeures","Déboguer les incohérences dans la structure du référentiel après l''achèvement d''un jalon"],"de":["Automatisieren von wöchentlichen Repository-Health-Checks","Überprüfen der Dokumentationsfrische vor größeren Releases","Fehlerbehebung von Inkonsistenzen in der Repository-Struktur nach dem Abschluss eines Meilensteins"],"pt":["Automatizar verificações semanais de saúde do repositório","Validar a frescura da documentação antes dos principais lançamentos","Depurar inconsistências na estrutura do repositório após a conclusão de marcos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать еженедельные проверки здоровья репозитория","Проверять свежесть документации перед основными выпусками","Отлаживать несоответствия в структуре репозитория после завершения вех"],"ar":["تأتمتة فحوصات صحية المستودع الأسبوعية","التحقق من鲜ة الوثائق قبل الإصدارات الرئيسية","تصحيح أخطاء في هيكل المستودع بعد إكمال الحجر الزاوية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires repository access and permissions","Limited to weekly or milestone-based checks","Dependent on contributor onboarding for maximum effectiveness"],"zh":["需要存储库访问和权限","仅限于每周或里程碑基于检查","依赖于贡献者入职以达到最大有效性"],"ja":["リポジトリへのアクセスと権限が必要","週次またはマイルストーンベースのチェックのみに限定される","最大の効果を達成するにはコントリビューターのオンボーディングに依存する"],"ko":["저장소 액세스 및 권한 필요","주간 또는 마일스톤 기반 확인만으로 제한","최대 효ิภาพ을 달성하려면 기여자의 입사에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso y permisos al repositorio","Limitado a controles semanales o basados en hitos","Dependiente de la incorporación de contribuyentes para una eficacia máxima"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès et des autorisations au référentiel","Limité aux vérifications hebdomadaires ou basées sur des jalons","Dépend de l''intégration des contributeurs pour une efficacité maximale"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff und Berechtigungen auf das Repository","Begrenzt auf wöchentliche oder meilensteinbasierte Überprüfungen","Abhängig von der Einbindung der Mitwirkenden für eine maximale Effektivität"],"pt":["Requer acesso e permissões do repositório","Limitado a verificações semanais ou baseadas em marcos","Dependente da integração de contribuidores para eficácia máxima"],"ru":["Требует доступа и разрешений репозитория","Ограничен еженедельными или основанными на вехах проверками","Зависит от интеграции участников для максимальной эффективности"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول والسماحيات للمستودع","محدود بالفحوصات الأسبوعية أو القائمة على الحجر الزاوية","يعتمد على دمج المساهمين لتحقيق أقصى فعالية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('fbosch/dotfiles/gh-pr-feedback', 'community', 'fbosch', 'dotfiles', 'fbosch/dotfiles', 'gh-pr-feedback', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z', '2026-02-18T13:24:07.756Z', NULL, '{"id":"fbosch/dotfiles/gh-pr-feedback","name":"gh-pr-feedback","description":{"zh":"Gh PR Feedback是一种工具，帮助开发者从GitHub PR审查中提取有价值的反馈信息","ja":"Gh PR Feedbackは、GitHub PRレビューから有益なフィードバックを抽出するためのツールです","ko":"Gh PR Feedback는 GitHub PR 리뷰에서 유용한 피드백을 추출하는 도구입니다","es":"El agente de habilidad gh-pr-feedback extrae comentarios de revisión de PR de GitHub y los presenta con rutas de archivos y rangos de líneas","fr":"L''agent de compétence gh-pr-feedback extrait des commentaires de révision de PR GitHub et les présente avec des chemins de fichiers et des plages de lignes","de":"Der gh-pr-feedback-Skill-Agent extrahiert GitHub-PR-Überprüfungsfeedback und präsentiert es mit Dateipfaden und Zeilenbereichen","pt":"O Gh PR Feedback é uma ferramenta que extrai feedback ação de revisões do GitHub PR, apresentando-o com caminhos de arquivo e intervalos de linha.","ru":"Gh PR Feedback — это инструмент, который извлекает обратную связь из обзоров GitHub PR, представляя ее с путями файлов и диапазонами строк.","ar":"Gh PR Feedback هو أداة لاستخراج ملاحظات المراجعة من مراجعات GitHub PR، وتقديمها مع مسارات الملفات ونطاقات الأسطر.","en":"🗂️ Configurations for macOS, WSL and Linux"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"GitHub PR反馈工具 - Gh PR Feedback","ja":"GitHub PRフィードバックツール - Gh PR Feedback","ko":"GitHub PR 피드백 도구 - Gh PR Feedback","es":"Retorna comentarios de PR de GitHub","fr":"Obtenez des commentaires de PR GitHub","de":"Erhalten Sie GitHub-PR-Feedback","pt":"Gh PR Feedback: Ferramenta de Extração de Feedback","ru":"Gh PR Feedback: Инструмент для извлечения обратной связи","ar":"Gh PR Feedback: أداة استخراج ملاحظات المراجعة","en":"gh-pr-feedback"},"description":{"zh":"Gh PR Feedback是一种工具，帮助开发者从GitHub PR审查中提取有价值的反馈信息","ja":"Gh PR Feedbackは、GitHub PRレビューから有益なフィードバックを抽出するためのツールです","ko":"Gh PR Feedback는 GitHub PR 리뷰에서 유용한 피드백을 추출하는 도구입니다","es":"El agente de habilidad gh-pr-feedback extrae comentarios de revisión de PR de GitHub y los presenta con rutas de archivos y rangos de líneas","fr":"L''agent de compétence gh-pr-feedback extrait des commentaires de révision de PR GitHub et les présente avec des chemins de fichiers et des plages de lignes","de":"Der gh-pr-feedback-Skill-Agent extrahiert GitHub-PR-Überprüfungsfeedback und präsentiert es mit Dateipfaden und Zeilenbereichen","pt":"O Gh PR Feedback é uma ferramenta que extrai feedback ação de revisões do GitHub PR, apresentando-o com caminhos de arquivo e intervalos de linha.","ru":"Gh PR Feedback — это инструмент, который извлекает обратную связь из обзоров GitHub PR, представляя ее с путями файлов и диапазонами строк.","ar":"Gh PR Feedback هو أداة لاستخراج ملاحظات المراجعة من مراجعات GitHub PR، وتقديمها مع مسارات الملفات ونطاقات الأسطر.","en":"🗂️ Configurations for macOS, WSL and Linux"},"definition":{"en":"🗂️ Configurations for macOS, WSL and Linux"},"features":{"zh":["从GitHub PR审查中提取可行的反馈","以文件路径和行范围呈现反馈","支持PR URL、直接审查链接和评论链接","可定制的配置选项"],"ja":["GitHub PRレビューからアクション可能なフィードバックを抽出","ファイルパスと行範囲でフィードバックを提示","PR URL、直接レビューリンク、コメントリンクをサポート","カスタマイズ可能な設定オプション"],"ko":["GitHub PR 리뷰에서 작업 가능한 피드백을 추출","파일 경로와 줄 범위로 피드백을 표시","PR URL, 직접 리뷰 링크, 댓글 링크를 지원","사용자 정의 가능한 설정 옵션"],"es":["Extrae comentarios de revisión de PR de GitHub","Presenta comentarios con rutas de archivos y rangos de líneas","Admite URLs de PR, revisiones y comentarios","Permite la extracción de comentarios de revisión de PR de GitHub de manera efectiva"],"fr":["Extrait des commentaires de révision de PR GitHub","Présente des commentaires avec des chemins de fichiers et des plages de lignes","Prend en charge les URL de PR, de révision et de commentaire","Permet l''extraction efficace de commentaires de révision de PR GitHub"],"de":["Extrahiert GitHub-PR-Überprüfungsfeedback","Präsentiert Feedback mit Dateipfaden und Zeilenbereichen","Unterstützt PR-URLs, Überprüfungen und Kommentare","Ermöglicht die effiziente Extraktion von GitHub-PR-Überprüfungsfeedback"],"pt":["Extração de feedback ação de revisões do GitHub PR","Apresentação de feedback com caminhos de arquivo e intervalos de linha","Suporte a URLs de PR, revisões e threads","Identificação de proprietário, repositório e número de PR"],"ru":["Извлечение обратной связи из обзоров GitHub PR","Представление обратной связи с путями файлов и диапазонами строк","Поддержка URL-адресов PR, обзоров и потоков","Определение владельца, репозитория и номера PR"],"ar":["استخراج ملاحظات المراجعة من مراجعات GitHub PR","تقديم ملاحظات المراجعة مع مسارات الملفات ونطاقات الأسطر","دعم للعناوين URL للـ PR والمراجعات والمناقشات","تحديد المالك والمستودع ورقم الـ PR"]},"keywords":{"zh":["GitHub PR反馈","Gh PR Feedback","代码审查工具","开发者工具","GitHub集成"],"ja":["GitHub PRフィードバック","Gh PR Feedback","コードレビューツール","開発者ツール","GitHub統合"],"ko":["GitHub PR 피드백","Gh PR Feedback","코드 리뷰 도구","개발자 도구","GitHub 통합"],"es":["github pr feedback","comentarios de revisión de pr","extracción de comentarios","rutas de archivos y rangos de líneas","flujo de trabajo de desarrollo","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["github pr feedback","commentaires de révision de pr","extraction de commentaires","chemins de fichiers et plages de lignes","flux de travail de développement","outils de développement"],"de":["github pr feedback","github-pr-überprüfungsfeedback","extraktion von kommentaren","dateipfade und zeilenbereiche","entwicklungsworkflow","entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Gh PR Feedback","GitHub PR","Extração de feedback","Revisões do GitHub","Desenvolvimento de software","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Gh PR Feedback","GitHub PR","Извлечение обратной связи","Обзоры GitHub","Разработка программного обеспечения","Инструменты разработки"],"ar":["Gh PR Feedback","GitHub PR","استخراج ملاحظات المراجعة","مراجعات GitHub","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"fbosch","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"fbosch/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"gh-pr-feedback","description":"Extract actionable feedback from GitHub pull request reviews and review comments using the gh CLI. Use when asked to read PR feedback, review threads, or actionable items from a PR link/number, and produce a line-referenced list that includes the full feedback text and an end question about turning it into a todo list or reference file.","bodyPreview":"# Gh PR Feedback\n\nExtract actionable feedback from a GitHub PR review and present it with file paths and line ranges.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the PR\n    - If user provides a PR URL, extract owner/repo/number.\n    - If user provides a direct review or thread link (e.g., `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/pull/<number>#pullrequestreview-<review_id>` or `#discussion_r<comment_id>`), extract owner/repo/number and the review or comment id for targeted fetching.\n    - If user provides just a number,","body":"# Gh PR Feedback\n\nExtract actionable feedback from a GitHub PR review and present it with file paths and line ranges.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the PR\n    - If user provides a PR URL, extract owner/repo/number.\n    - If user provides a direct review or thread link (e.g., `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/pull/<number>#pullrequestreview-<review_id>` or `#discussion_r<comment_id>`), extract owner/repo/number and the review or comment id for targeted fetching.\n    - If user provides just a number, assume the current repo and confirm by fetching PR details.\n    - If no PR is provided, infer from current branch name using GitHub MCP tools or `gh pr view --json number,url`.\n    - If the user provides an opencode tool-output transcript or file that already contains parsed review comments, treat it as the primary source and avoid re-fetching via `gh api` unless fields are missing.\n    - Include all comments by default, including informational and non-actionable comments (except excluded automated summaries), and label them as informational when needed.\n\n2. Fetch review metadata\n   - Use `gh pr view <number> --json number,title,url` for context.\n   - If a review URL is provided, fetch it with `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<number>/reviews/<review_id>`.\n   - If a direct review link is provided, confirm the review id matches and use it to scope comments.\n\n3. Fetch review comments\n    - Use `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<number>/comments --paginate`.\n    - If targeting a specific review, filter by `pull_request_review_id`.\n    - If targeting a specific thread/comment id from `#discussion_r<comment_id>`, filter to that comment and any replies in its thread.\n   - Reconstruct threads by grouping comments using `in_reply_to_id` and include the root comment with all replies.\n   - For each thread, read the full discussion before extracting feedback.\n    - Fetch general PR comments only when the user explicitly asks for them or when no inline review comment covers the same issue: `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<number>/comments --paginate`.\n   - If a parser script is provided (for example in an opencode tool-output path), run it first and use its output to populate thread groups and comment fields.\n   - For opencode tool-output JSON, use `scripts/parse-review-comments.py` to normalize thread groups before summarizing.\n     - Example: `python scripts/parse-review-comments.py /path/to/tool-output.json`\n\n4. Summarize actionable feedback\n    - For each comment, capture:\n      - `path` and `line` or `start_line`/`line` if present\n      - The core actionable request or concern\n      - Whether the comment is outdated or on a deleted/renamed file\n      - De-duplicate repeated points.\n      - Include the full feedback text from the reviewer; do not shorten or condense it.\n      - Identify similar feedback across reviewers and note it as corroboration (e.g., “also raised by @user2”).\n      - For automated agent comments that include long analysis chains or tool logs, exclude the analysis/log sections and only keep the actionable feedback or fix request itself.\n      - For automated overview summaries (e.g., Copilot PR overview) that do not request changes, treat them as non-actionable and exclude them.\n      - If a comment mixes background summary with actionable requests, keep only the actionable portion and preserve original wording.\n      - Preserve original markdown formatting within actionable excerpts (code blocks, links, emphasis) when present.\n      - Render code suggestions inside fenced code blocks (```) to preserve readability.\n      - When the same issue is raised by multiple comments, merge them after severity ordering into a single item and note that it was mentioned by multiple authors (e.g., \"Mentioned by Copilot and CodeRabbit\").\n\n## Prioritization mindset\n\n- Prefer user-impacting issues over stylistic or internal refactors.\n- When two items are similar severity, surface the one with broader blast radius first.\n   - If a comment is informational only, note it as non-actionable.\n   - Prefer review comments (inline) over general PR comments when both exist for the same issue.\n   - If multiple reviewers conflict, prioritize request-changes over comments and note the conflict explicitly.\n   - Exclude resolved threads and comments; only include current actionable feedback.\n\n## Output format\n\n- Use a flat bullet list\n- Each bullet should include: `path:line-range` + full feedback text\n- If a file/line is missing, use `path:unknown`\n- Do not include links in the output; the PR URL is enough context.\n- Order by severity if clear (request‑changes > should‑fix > nit), then by file path\n- If severity is unclear, group by reviewer role (maintainers > collaborators > external) and then by file path\n- Preserve the reviewer’s wording when it is a direct request\n- Do not output resolved threads at all\n- For outdated threads, append `(outdated)` to the bullet\n- Keep code fences inside the bullet so list structure stays intact.\n- Decision rules:\n   - If resolved, exclude.\n   - If outdated and unresolved, include and append `(outdated)`.\n   - If line/path missing, use `path:unknown`.\n   - For duplicates with different line ranges, use common sense based on the feedback at hand.\n   - Do not merge conflicting requests; keep them separate and flag the conflict.\n- Example bullet with code suggestion:\n  - `src/app.ts:42` Please handle empty input before parsing.\n    ```ts\n    if (input.trim().length == 0) {\n      return null;\n    }\n    ```\n- Example informational-only bullet:\n  - `src/app.ts:12` Informational: This change looks good; no action needed.\n- End by calling the `question` tool (do not print a plain-text `Question:` block) with:\n  - Header: `PR feedback next step`\n  - Question: `What should I do with this feedback?`\n  - Options (keep labels stable):\n    - `Apply fixes now`\n    - `Create a todo list here`\n    - `Write a markdown checklist file`\n    - `Keep as-is (no follow-up action)`\n  - Use single-select (`multiple: false`) and allow custom input.\n  - If there are conflicting requests, add a heads-up sentence before the final question.\n  - If writing a reference file, write a Markdown file with checkbox list items so progress can be tracked.\n  - Example reference file format:\n    - `# PR Feedback`\n    - `- [ ] src/app.ts:42 Handle empty input before parsing.`\n\n## Notes\n\n- Prefer the GitHub MCP tools when available; fall back to `gh` CLI JSON APIs.\n- Mention explicitly in the response when GitHub MCP tools were used.\n- Keep summaries verbatim; do not modify or condense the feedback content.\n- If any context is missing (owner/repo), ask for it only after trying to infer from current git remote.\n- Helper scripts:\n  - `scripts/inspect-review-json.py` prints structure and key fields.\n  - `scripts/parse-review-comments.py` outputs thread-grouped JSON.\n  - `scripts/list-review-comments.py` prints comments with key fields.\n - GitHub MCP tool mapping:\n   - Identify PR / metadata: `github_pull_request_read` (method: `get`).\n   - Review metadata: `github_pull_request_read` (method: `get_reviews`).\n   - Review comments (inline): `github_pull_request_read` (method: `get_review_comments`).\n   - General PR comments: `github_pull_request_read` (method: `get_comments`).\n   - PR files (for context/paths): `github_pull_request_read` (method: `get_files`).\n\n## Never\n\n- Never paraphrase a direct fix request unless it improves clarity without changing meaning; accuracy beats polish.\n- Never include agent analysis chains, tool logs, or execution transcripts in the output; only keep the actionable feedback.\n- Never include automated overview summaries that contain no actionable requests.\n- Never include non-actionable background summaries when a comment also contains an explicit action.\n- Never drop file/line context when it exists; the location is essential for action.\n- Never merge unrelated comments into one bullet; keep review intent separable.\n- Never omit outdated‑comment status when it is flagged in the review data; it prevents wasted effort.\n- Never include resolved threads; user has already acted on them.\n- Never treat outdated-but-open threads as resolved; include them and mark as `(outdated)`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:24:07.756Z","qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('deferred/dotfiles/chezmoi', 'community', 'deferred', 'dotfiles', 'deferred/dotfiles', 'chezmoi', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z', '2026-02-18T13:24:05.206Z', NULL, '{"id":"deferred/dotfiles/chezmoi","name":"chezmoi","description":{"zh":"chezmoi 是一个配置文件管理工具，使用 Git 仓库来管理和同步配置文件","ja":"chezmoi はドットファイルマネージャーです。Git リポジトリを使用して設定ファイルを管理および同期します","ko":"chezmoi는 설정 파일 관리자로 Git仓库를 사용하여 설정 파일을 관리하고同步합니다","es":"chezmoi es una herramienta de gestión de dotfiles que utiliza un repositorio Git para mantener tu entorno de desarrollo organizado.","fr":"chezmoi est un outil de gestion de dotfiles qui utilise un référentiel Git pour maintenir votre environnement de développement organisé.","de":"chezmoi ist ein Tool zur Verwaltung von Dotfiles, das ein Git-Repository verwendet, um Ihr Entwicklungsumfeld organisiert zu halten.","pt":"O chezmoi é uma ferramenta de gerenciamento de dotfiles que utiliza um repositório Git para armazenar configurações.","ru":"chezmoi - это инструмент для управления конфигурационными файлами, который использует репозиторий Git для хранения настроек.","ar":"chezmoi هو أداة لإدارة ملفات النقاط التي تستخدم مستودع Git لتخزين الإعدادات.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"chezmoi - 配置文件管理工具","ja":"chezmoi - ドットファイルマネージャー","ko":"chezmoi - 설정 파일 관리자","es":"chezmoi: Administrador de Dotfiles","fr":"chezmoi : Gestionnaire de Dotfiles","de":"chezmoi: Dotfiles-Manager","pt":"chezmoi: Gerenciador de Dotfiles","ru":"chezmoi: Менеджер конфигурационных файлов","ar":"chezmoi: مدير ملفات النقاط","en":"chezmoi"},"description":{"zh":"chezmoi 是一个配置文件管理工具，使用 Git 仓库来管理和同步配置文件","ja":"chezmoi はドットファイルマネージャーです。Git リポジトリを使用して設定ファイルを管理および同期します","ko":"chezmoi는 설정 파일 관리자로 Git仓库를 사용하여 설정 파일을 관리하고同步합니다","es":"chezmoi es una herramienta de gestión de dotfiles que utiliza un repositorio Git para mantener tu entorno de desarrollo organizado.","fr":"chezmoi est un outil de gestion de dotfiles qui utilise un référentiel Git pour maintenir votre environnement de développement organisé.","de":"chezmoi ist ein Tool zur Verwaltung von Dotfiles, das ein Git-Repository verwendet, um Ihr Entwicklungsumfeld organisiert zu halten.","pt":"O chezmoi é uma ferramenta de gerenciamento de dotfiles que utiliza um repositório Git para armazenar configurações.","ru":"chezmoi - это инструмент для управления конфигурационными файлами, который использует репозиторий Git для хранения настроек.","ar":"chezmoi هو أداة لإدارة ملفات النقاط التي تستخدم مستودع Git لتخزين الإعدادات.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用 Git 仓库来管理配置文件","支持文件元数据（权限、加密、模板行为）","自动同步配置文件","支持多种配置文件格式","命令行界面"],"ja":["Git リポジトリを使用して設定ファイルを管理","ファイルメタデータ（パーミッション、暗号化、テンプレート動作）をサポート","設定ファイルを自動同期","複数の設定ファイル形式をサポート","コマンドラインインターフェース"],"ko":["Git仓库를 사용하여 설정 파일을 관리","파일 메타데이터(권한, 암호화, 템플릿 동작) 지원","설정 파일을 자동으로 동기화","다양한 설정 파일 형식을 지원","명령줄 인터페이스"],"es":["Gestión de dotfiles mediante un repositorio Git","Compatibilidad con plantillas y metadatos","Aplicación de la configuración al directorio de inicio","Soporte para permisos y cifrado","Personalización a través de un archivo de configuración"],"fr":["Gestion des dotfiles via un référentiel Git","Compatibilité avec les modèles et les métadonnées","Application de la configuration au répertoire de démarrage","Prise en charge des autorisations et du chiffrement","Personnalisation via un fichier de configuration"],"de":["Verwaltung von Dotfiles über ein Git-Repository","Kompatibilität mit Vorlagen und Metadaten","Anwendung der Konfiguration auf das Startverzeichnis","Unterstützung für Berechtigungen und Verschlüsselung","Anpassung über eine Konfigurationsdatei"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de dotfiles","Repositório Git para configurações","Suporte a metadados de arquivos","Modelo de estado de origem e destino","Suporte a templates e criptografia"],"ru":["Управление конфигурационными файлами","Репозиторий Git для настроек","Поддержка метаданных файлов","Модель исходного и целевого состояния","Поддержка шаблонов и шифрования"],"ar":["إدارة ملفات النقاط","مستودع Git لإعدادات","دعم بيانات وصف الملفات","نموذج حالة المصدر والوجهة","دعم القوالب والتشفير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["chezmoi","配置文件管理","Git 仓库","文件元数据","自动同步","命令行界面"],"ja":["chezmoi","ドットファイルマネージャー","Git リポジトリ","ファイルメタデータ","自動同期","コマンドラインインターフェース"],"ko":["chezmoi","설정 파일 관리","Git倉库","파일 메타데이터","자동 동기화","명령줄 인터페이스"],"es":["chezmoi","dotfiles","gestión de dotfiles","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","git","repositorio git","configuración de entorno"],"fr":["chezmoi","dotfiles","gestion de dotfiles","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","git","référentiel git","configuration de l''environnement"],"de":["chezmoi","dotfiles","verwaltung von dotfiles","software-entwicklung","entwicklungstools","git","git-repository","konfiguration des umfelds"],"pt":["chezmoi","gerenciamento de dotfiles","configuração de sistema","repositório Git","metadados de arquivos","modelo de estado","templates","criptografia"],"ru":["chezmoi","управление конфигурационными файлами","настройка системы","репозиторий Git","метаданные файлов","модель состояния","шаблоны","шифрование"],"ar":["chezmoi","إدارة ملفات النقاط","إعداد نظام","مستودع Git","بيانات وصف الملفات","نموذج حالة","قوالب","تشفير"]}},"owner":"deferred","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"deferred/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"chezmoi","description":"Manage dotfiles with chezmoi. Use when running chezmoi CLI commands, creating or editing chezmoi-managed files, debugging chezmoi issues, writing chezmoi templates, or working with chezmoi source state in any way.","bodyPreview":"# chezmoi - Dotfiles Manager\n\n## Core Model\n\nchezmoi uses a **source state** (git repo at `~/.local/share/chezmoi`) that is computed into a **target state** and applied to the **destination** (`$HOME`). File metadata (permissions, encryption, template behavior) is encoded in source file names via prefixes and suffixes.\n\n## Source Directory Structure\n\n```\n~/.local/share/chezmoi/           # source directory (git repo)\n├── .chezmoi.toml.tmpl            # config template (prompts during init)\n├── .","body":"# chezmoi - Dotfiles Manager\n\n## Core Model\n\nchezmoi uses a **source state** (git repo at `~/.local/share/chezmoi`) that is computed into a **target state** and applied to the **destination** (`$HOME`). File metadata (permissions, encryption, template behavior) is encoded in source file names via prefixes and suffixes.\n\n## Source Directory Structure\n\n```\n~/.local/share/chezmoi/           # source directory (git repo)\n├── .chezmoi.toml.tmpl            # config template (prompts during init)\n├── .chezmoidata.toml              # custom template data\n├── .chezmoidata/                  # additional data files (lexical order)\n├── .chezmoiexternal.toml          # external files/archives\n├── .chezmoiexternals/             # additional external declarations\n├── .chezmoiignore                 # ignore patterns (supports templates)\n├── .chezmoiremove                 # patterns of files to remove on apply\n├── .chezmoitemplates/             # partial templates for {{ template \"name\" }}\n├── .chezmoiscripts/               # scripts directory (organizational)\n├── .chezmoiversion                # minimum required chezmoi version\n├── .chezmoiroot                   # redirect source root within repo\n├── dot_zshrc                      # → ~/.zshrc\n├── private_dot_ssh/               # → ~/.ssh/ (mode 0700)\n├── executable_dot_local/bin/foo   # → ~/.local/bin/foo (+x)\n└── run_onchange_before_install.sh.tmpl  # run script\n```\n\n## File Naming Quick Reference\n\nEncode target file attributes using prefixes (order matters) and suffixes:\n\n| Prefix | Effect |\n|---|---|\n| `dot_` | Leading `.` in target name |\n| `private_` | `0600` file / `0700` dir |\n| `readonly_` | Remove write permissions |\n| `executable_` | Add execute bit |\n| `encrypted_` | Encrypted in source |\n| `empty_` | Keep file even if empty |\n| `exact_` | (dirs) Remove unmanaged children |\n| `create_` | Only create if missing |\n| `modify_` | Script that modifies existing file (stdin = current contents) |\n| `remove_` | Remove target |\n| `symlink_` | Create symlink |\n| `run_` | Execute as script |\n| `once_` / `onchange_` | Script frequency |\n| `before_` / `after_` | Script phase |\n| `literal_` | Stop parsing prefixes |\n\n| Suffix | Effect |\n|---|---|\n| `.tmpl` | Process as Go template |\n| `.literal` | Stop parsing suffixes |\n\nFor full prefix ordering rules by target type, see [naming-conventions.md](references/naming-conventions.md).\n\n## Templates\n\nFiles with `.tmpl` suffix or inside `.chezmoitemplates/` are processed as Go `text/template` with sprig functions.\n\n```gohtml\n{{- if eq .chezmoi.os \"darwin\" }}\nexport BROWSER=\"open\"\n{{- else }}\nexport BROWSER=\"xdg-open\"\n{{- end }}\n```\n\nKey variables: `.chezmoi.os`, `.chezmoi.arch`, `.chezmoi.hostname`, `.chezmoi.username`, `.chezmoi.homeDir`\n\nCustom data defined in `[data]` config section or `.chezmoidata.*` files.\n\nFor complete template syntax, variables, and functions, see [templating.md](references/templating.md).\n\n## Externals\n\nDeclare external files/archives in `.chezmoiexternal.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[\".oh-my-zsh\"]\n    type = \"archive\"\n    url = \"https://github.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/archive/master.tar.gz\"\n    exact = true\n    stripComponents = 1\n    refreshPeriod = \"168h\"\n```\n\nTypes: `file`, `archive`, `archive-file`, `git-repo`. For all options, see [externals.md](references/externals.md).\n\n## Scripts\n\nName scripts with `run_` prefix plus optional frequency and phase modifiers:\n\n```\nrun_before_install.sh              # every apply, before other changes\nrun_once_after_setup.sh            # once ever, after changes\nrun_onchange_before_brew.sh.tmpl   # when content changes, before, templated\n```\n\nScripts can be templates — useful for OS-conditional execution:\n\n```bash\n{{ if eq .chezmoi.os \"darwin\" -}}\n#!/bin/bash\nbrew install ripgrep\n{{ end -}}\n```\n\n## .chezmoiignore\n\nGitignore-style patterns with template support for conditional ignoring:\n\n```\nREADME.md\n{{ if ne .chezmoi.os \"darwin\" }}\n.config/karabiner\nLibrary\n{{ end }}\n```\n\n## Encryption\n\nConfigure in `chezmoi.toml`, add files with `chezmoi add --encrypt`:\n\n```toml\nencryption = \"age\"\n[age]\n    identity = \"~/.config/chezmoi/key.txt\"\n    recipient = \"age1...\"\n```\n\n## Password Managers\n\nUse template functions to retrieve secrets (never stored in repo):\n\n```gohtml\n{{ onepasswordRead \"op://vault/item/field\" }}\n{{ pass \"path/to/secret\" }}\n{{ (bitwarden \"item-id\").login.password }}\n{{ keyring \"service\" \"user\" }}\n```\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n```bash\nchezmoi add ~/.config/foo        # add file to source state\nchezmoi add --encrypt ~/.ssh/key # add encrypted\nchezmoi add --template ~/.git*   # add as template\nchezmoi edit ~/.zshrc            # edit source, optionally auto-apply\nchezmoi diff                     # preview pending changes\nchezmoi apply                    # apply source → destination\nchezmoi update                   # git pull + apply\nchezmoi re-add                   # sync destination changes back to source\nchezmoi chattr +executable file  # change source attributes\n```\n\nFor all commands, see [commands.md](references/commands.md). For config file reference, see [configuration.md](references/configuration.md).\n\n## Reference Files\n\n- [Naming Conventions](references/naming-conventions.md) - Prefix ordering rules by target type, complete examples\n- [Templating](references/templating.md) - Go template syntax, built-in variables, sprig functions, password managers\n- [Commands](references/commands.md) - All chezmoi commands with usage\n- [Configuration](references/configuration.md) - Config file structure, all sections and variables\n- [Externals](references/externals.md) - `.chezmoiexternal.toml` types, options, examples\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:24:05.206Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Configuration Management Agents requiring automated dotfile synchronization and templating","zh":"适用于需要自动化点文件同步和模板的配置管理代理的理想选择","ja":"自動化されたドットファイルの同期とテンプレートが必要な構成管理エージェントに最適","ko":"자동화된 도트 파일 동기화 및 템플릿이 필요한 구성 관리 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de administración de configuración que requieren sincronización automática de archivos de configuración y plantillas","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de gestion de configuration nécessitant une synchronisation automatique des fichiers de configuration et des modèles","de":"Ideal für Konfigurationsmanagement-Agents, die eine automatisierte Synchronisierung von Dotfiles und Vorlagen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Configuração que exigem sincronização automática de dotfiles e modelagem","ru":"Идеально для агентов управления конфигурацией, требующих автоматической синхронизации dotfile и шаблонов","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة التكوين الذي يتطلب مزامنة dotfile وتقديم نموذج تلقائي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage dotfiles across systems using a git repository as the source state, applying file metadata and templating behaviors via prefixes and suffixes in source file names, and integrating with the destination directory via computed target states","zh":"赋予代理管理系统中的点文件的能力，使用git仓库作为源状态，通过源文件名中的前缀和后缀应用文件元数据和模板行为，并通过计算目标状态与目标目录集成","ja":"エージェントがシステム全体でドットファイルを管理する能力を与え、gitリポジトリをソース状態として使用し、ソースファイル名の中の接頭辞と接尾辞を介してファイルメタデータとテンプレートの動作を適用し、計算されたターゲット状態を介して宛先ディレクトリと統合する","ko":"에이전트가 시스템 전체에서 도트 파일을 관리할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 git 저장소를 원본 상태로 사용하고 소스 파일 이름中的 접두사와 접미사를 통해 파일 메타데이터와 템플릿 동작을 적용하고 계산된 대상 상태를 통해 대상 디렉토리와 통합","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar archivos de configuración en varios sistemas utilizando un repositorio git como estado de origen, aplicando metadatos de archivo y comportamientos de plantillas a través de prefijos y sufijos en los nombres de los archivos de origen, e integrándose con el directorio de destino a través de estados de destino calculados","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les fichiers de configuration sur plusieurs systèmes en utilisant un référentiel git comme état source, en appliquant des métadonnées de fichier et des comportements de modèles via des préfixes et des suffixes dans les noms de fichiers source, et en s''intégrant avec le répertoire de destination via des états cibles calculés","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Dotfiles über mehrere Systeme hinweg zu verwalten, indem sie ein Git-Repository als Quellzustand verwenden, Dateimetadaten und Vorlagenverhalten über Präfixe und Suffixe in den Quelldateinamen anwenden und sich über berechnete Zielzustände mit dem Zielverzeichnis integrieren","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar dotfiles em vários sistemas usando um repositório git como estado de origem, aplicando metadados de arquivo e comportamentos de modelagem via prefixos e sufixos nos nomes de arquivos de origem, e integrando-se com o diretório de destino por meio de estados de destino calculados","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять dotfile в различных системах, используя репозиторий git в качестве исходного состояния, применяя метаданные файлов и поведения шаблонов через префиксы и суффиксы в именах исходных файлов, и интегрируясь с целевым каталогом посредством рассчитанных целевых состояний","ar":"يمنح الوكيل إمكانية إدارة dotfiles عبر الأنظمة باستخدام مستودع git كمصدر للوضع، وتطبيق بيانات وصف الملف وسلوكيات القوالب من خلال الأسماء الأمامية والخلفية في أسماء الملفات الأصلية، والدمج مع الدليل الوجهة من خلال حالات الوجهة المحسوبة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating dotfile synchronization across multiple systems"," Templating configuration files with chezmoi''s template behavior","Managing file permissions and encryption through metadata encoding"],"zh":["跨多个系统自动化点文件同步","使用chezmoi的模板行为模板化配置文件","通过元数据编码管理文件权限和加密"],"ja":["複数のシステム全体でドットファイルの同期を自動化する","chezmoiのテンプレートの動作を使用してコンフィギュレーションファイルをテンプレート化する","メタデータのエンコードを介してファイルの権限と暗号化を管理する"],"ko":["여러 시스템에서 도트 파일 동기화를 자동화","chezmoi의 템플릿 동작을 사용하여 구성 파일을 템플릿화","메타데이터 인코딩을 통해 파일 권한 및 암호화를 관리"],"es":["Automatizar la sincronización de archivos de configuración en varios sistemas","Crear plantillas de archivos de configuración con el comportamiento de plantillas de chezmoi","Gestionar permisos y cifrado de archivos a través de la codificación de metadatos"],"fr":["Automatiser la synchronisation des fichiers de configuration sur plusieurs systèmes","Créer des modèles de fichiers de configuration avec le comportement de modèles de chezmoi","Gérer les autorisations et le chiffrement des fichiers via l''encodage des métadonnées"],"de":["Automatisieren der Synchronisierung von Dotfiles auf mehreren Systemen","Erstellen von Konfigurationsdateivvorlagen mit dem Vorlagenverhalten von chezmoi","Verwalten von Dateiberechtigungen und Verschlüsselung durch Metadaten-Codierung"],"pt":["Automatizar a sincronização de dotfiles em vários sistemas","Modelar arquivos de configuração com o comportamento de modelo do chezmoi","Gerenciar permissões de arquivo e criptografia por meio de codificação de metadados"],"ru":["Автоматизировать синхронизацию dotfile в нескольких системах","Шаблонизировать файлы конфигурации с помощью поведения шаблонов chezmoi","Управлять разрешениями файлов и шифрованием посредством кодирования метаданных"],"ar":["توفير التزامن التلقائي لملفات dotfiles عبر الأنظمة المتعددة","تقديم نموذج لملفات التكوين بسلوك chezmoi","إدارة صلاحيات الملفات والتشفير من خلال ترميز البيانات الوصفية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git repository setup at ~/.local/share/chezmoi","Destination directory management limited to $HOME"],"zh":["需要在~/.local/share/chezmoi设置git仓库","目标目录管理仅限于$HOME"],"ja":["~/.local/share/chezmoiにgitリポジトリを設定する必要がある","宛先ディレクトリの管理は$HOMEに限定される"],"ko":["~/.local/share/chezmoi에 git 저장소를 설정해야 함","대상 디렉토리 관리는 $HOME로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la configuración de un repositorio git en ~/.local/share/chezmoi","La gestión del directorio de destino se limita a $HOME"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de référentiel git en ~/.local/share/chezmoi","La gestion du répertoire de destination est limitée à $HOME"],"de":["Benötigt die Einrichtung eines Git-Repositorys in ~/.local/share/chezmoi","Die Verwaltung des Zielverzeichnisses ist auf $HOME beschränkt"],"pt":["Exige configuração do repositório git em ~/.local/share/chezmoi","Gerenciamento do diretório de destino limitado a $HOME"],"ru":["Требует настройки репозитория git в ~/.local/share/chezmoi","Управление целевым каталогом ограничено $HOME"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مستودع git في ~/.local/share/chezmoi","إدارة الدليل الوجهة مقيدة بـ $HOME"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
