dad Commit para OpenZeppelin UI sigue el estándar Conventional Commits para commits","fr":"La compétence Commit pour OpenZeppelin UI suit la norme Conventional Commits pour les commits","de":"Die Commit-Fähigkeit für OpenZeppelin UI folgt dem Conventional Commits-Standard für Commits","pt":"O Commit Skill para OpenZeppelin UI é uma ferramenta para fazer commits de acordo com o padrão Conventional Commits.","ru":"Навык Commit для OpenZeppelin UI — это инструмент для создания коммитов в соответствии со стандартом Conventional Commits.","ar":"مهارة Commit ل OpenZeppelin UI هي أداة لإجراء عمليات Commit وفقًا لمعيار Commits التقليدية.","en":"OpenZeppelin UI - React components and utilities for blockchain applications"},"definition":{"en":"OpenZeppelin UI - React components and utilities for blockchain applications"},"features":{"zh":["标准化的代码提交格式","GPG 签名和预提交钩子","Conventional Commits 标准支持","全 shell 权限支持","预提交钩子运行保证"],"ja":["コードの提交形式の標準化","GPG 署名と事前コミットフック","Conventional Commits 標準のサポート","フルシェル権限のサポート","事前コミットフックの実行保証"],"ko":["코드 제출 형식의 표준화","GPG 서명 및 事前 제출 훅","Conventional Commits 표준 지원","전체 쉘 권한 지원","事前 제출 훅 실행 보장"],"es":["Seguimiento del estándar Conventional Commits","Firma GPG obligatoria para todos los commits","Ejecución de hooks de pre-compromiso","Formato de commit específico","Compatibilidad con OpenZeppelin UI"],"fr":["Suivi de la norme Conventional Commits","Signature GPG obligatoire pour tous les commits","Exécution des hooks de pré-compromis","Format de commit spécifique","Compatibilité avec OpenZeppelin UI"],"de":["Einhalten des Conventional Commits-Standards","Pflicht-GPG-Signatur für alle Commits","Ausführung von Pre-Commit-Hooks","Spezifisches Commit-Format","Kompatibilität mit OpenZeppelin UI"],"pt":["Executar commits fora do sandbox","Utilizar GPG signing","Executar pre-commit hooks","Formato de commit personalizado","Suporte ao padrão Conventional Commits"],"ru":["Выполнение коммитов вне sandbox","Использование подписи GPG","Выполнение хуков pre-commit","Пользовательский формат коммита","Поддержка стандарта Conventional Commits"],"ar":["تشغيل عمليات Commit خارج Sandbox","استخدام التوقيع GPG","تشغيل hooks pre-commit","تنسيق Commit مخصص","دعم معيار Commits التقليدية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenZeppelin UI","Commit 技术","代码提交","代码管理","GPG 签名","Conventional Commits","预提交钩子"],"ja":["OpenZeppelin UI","コミットスキル","コードの提交","コードの管理","GPG 署名","Conventional Commits","事前コミットフック"],"ko":["OpenZeppelin UI","커밋 기술","코드 제출","코드 관리","GPG 서명","Conventional Commits","事前 제출 훅"],"es":["Commit Skill","OpenZeppelin UI","Conventional Commits","GPG firma","pre-compromiso","formato de commit","desarrollo de blockchain","React components"],"fr":["Compétence Commit","OpenZeppelin UI","Conventional Commits","Signature GPG","pré-compromis","format de commit","développement de blockchain","composants React"],"de":["Commit-Fähigkeit","OpenZeppelin UI","Conventional Commits","GPG-Signatur","Pre-Commit","Commit-Format","Blockchain-Entwicklung","React-Komponenten"],"pt":["Commit Skill","OpenZeppelin UI","Conventional Commits","GPG signing","pre-commit hooks","formato de commit","desenvolvimento de blockchain","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Навык Commit","OpenZeppelin UI","Conventional Commits","Подпись GPG","хуки pre-commit","формат коммита","разработка блокчейна","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["مهارة Commit","OpenZeppelin UI","Commits التقليدية","التوقيع GPG","hooks pre-commit","تنسيق Commit","تطوير البلوكشين","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"OpenZeppelin","repo":"openzeppelin-ui","repoPath":"OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-ui","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit","description":"Creates commits following the monorepos Conventional Commits standard with proper GPG signing, scope selection, and pre-commit validation. Reminds about changesets for package changes. Use when creating commits, writing commit messages, or when the user asks to commit changes.","bodyPreview":"# Commit Skill for OpenZeppelin UI Monorepo\n\nThis skill guides committing changes following the project''s Conventional Commits standard.\n\n## Critical Requirements\n\n1. **Always run commits outside sandbox** - Full shell permissions required for GPG signing and pre-commit hooks\n2. **Never use `--no-gpg-sign`** - All commits must be GPG-signed\n3. **Never use `--no-verify`** - Pre-commit hooks must run\n\n## Commit Format\n\n```\n<type>(<scope>): <subject>\n\n[optional body]\n\n[optional footer(s)]\n```\n\n###","body":"# Commit Skill for OpenZeppelin UI Monorepo\n\nThis skill guides committing changes following the project''s Conventional Commits standard.\n\n## Critical Requirements\n\n1. **Always run commits outside sandbox** - Full shell permissions required for GPG signing and pre-commit hooks\n2. **Never use `--no-gpg-sign`** - All commits must be GPG-signed\n3. **Never use `--no-verify`** - Pre-commit hooks must run\n\n## Commit Format\n\n```\n<type>(<scope>): <subject>\n\n[optional body]\n\n[optional footer(s)]\n```\n\n### Rules\n\n| Rule               | Requirement                                                          |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Header max length  | 100 characters                                                       |\n| Subject case       | lowercase (never sentence-case, start-case, pascal-case, upper-case) |\n| Subject ending     | No period                                                            |\n| Scope              | **Required** (scope-empty is enforced)                               |\n| Body line length   | Max 100 characters                                                   |\n| Body leading blank | Required if body present                                             |\n\n## Commit Types\n\n| Type       | Description                                             |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `feat`     | New feature                                             |\n| `fix`      | Bug fix                                                 |\n| `docs`     | Documentation only                                      |\n| `style`    | Formatting, whitespace (no code change)                 |\n| `refactor` | Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature |\n| `perf`     | Performance improvement                                 |\n| `test`     | Adding or correcting tests                              |\n| `build`    | Build system or external dependencies                   |\n| `ci`       | CI configuration changes                                |\n| `chore`    | Other changes (not src or test)                         |\n| `revert`   | Reverts a previous commit                               |\n| `wip`      | Work in progress (avoid if possible)                    |\n\n## Allowed Scopes\n\nThe commitlint config enforces these scopes:\n\n| Scope        | Description               |\n| ------------ | ------------------------- |\n| `types`      | Type definitions package  |\n| `utils`      | Utility functions package |\n| `styles`     | Styles package            |\n| `components` | Components package        |\n| `renderer`   | Renderer package          |\n| `react`      | React integration package |\n| `storage`    | Storage package           |\n| `deps`       | Dependencies              |\n| `config`     | Configuration files       |\n| `ci`         | CI/CD configuration       |\n| `docs`       | Documentation             |\n| `tests`      | Test-related changes      |\n| `release`    | Release automation        |\n| `examples`   | Example applications      |\n| `common`     | Common/shared code        |\n| `spec`       | Specification documents   |\n\n## Commit Workflow\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stage changes\ngit add <files>\n\n# 2. Commit with HEREDOC (recommended for multi-line messages)\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\nfeat(components): add new contract widget\n\nImplements a reusable widget component for displaying\ncontract state with real-time updates.\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n## Changeset Reminder\n\n**Before committing changes to `packages/` directory, check if a changeset is needed.**\n\nA changeset is required when:\n\n- Adding features to published packages\n- Fixing bugs in published packages\n- Making breaking changes\n\nCheck for existing changesets:\n\n```bash\nls .changeset/*.md\n```\n\nIf no changeset exists for your changes, create one:\n\n```bash\npnpm changeset\n```\n\nPublished packages in this monorepo:\n\n- `@openzeppelin/ui-types`\n- `@openzeppelin/ui-utils`\n- `@openzeppelin/ui-styles`\n- `@openzeppelin/ui-components`\n- `@openzeppelin/ui-renderer`\n- `@openzeppelin/ui-react`\n- `@openzeppelin/ui-storage`\n\n## Pre-commit Hooks\n\nThe following checks run automatically on commit:\n\n1. **Formatting check**: Runs `pnpm format:check`\n2. **Commit message validation**: Runs commitlint\n\nIf pre-commit fails, fix the issues and commit again.\n\n## Pre-push Hooks\n\nBefore pushing, these checks run:\n\n1. **Formatting and linting**: Runs `pnpm fix-all`\n2. **Type checking**: Runs `pnpm typecheck`\n3. **Tests**: Runs `pnpm test`\n\nIf pre-push fails, fix the issues and push again.\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\nIndicate breaking changes with `!` after type/scope:\n\n```bash\nfeat(types)!: change network config interface\n```\n\nOr with a footer:\n\n```\nfeat(types): change network config interface\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: NetworkConfig interface now requires chainId property.\nAll consumers must update their configuration.\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### Sandbox Mode Errors\n\n**Symptom**: Commit fails with permission errors, GPG signing fails, or hooks don''t run.\n\n**Fix**: Run commit commands with full shell permissions (outside sandbox).\n\n### Invalid Scope\n\n**Symptom**: `scope-enum` error from commitlint.\n\n**Fix**: Use one of the allowed scopes above. If a new scope is justified, update `commitlint.config.js`.\n\n### Subject Case Error\n\n**Symptom**: `subject-case` error.\n\n**Fix**: Use lowercase for the entire subject:\n\n- Bad: `Add new feature`\n- Good: `add new feature`\n\n### Missing Scope\n\n**Symptom**: `scope-empty` error from commitlint.\n\n**Fix**: Always include a scope. Choose the most relevant package or category.\n\n## Examples\n\n```bash\n# Feature with package scope\nfeat(components): add network badge component\n\n# Fix with package scope\nfix(utils): correct address validation for checksums\n\n# Refactor with package scope\nrefactor(renderer): simplify form field rendering logic\n\n# Specification documents\ndocs(spec): add data model for extend example apps feature\n\n# Documentation\ndocs(examples): add wallet connection tutorial\n\n# Test changes\ntest(react): add unit tests for useWalletComponents hook\n\n# Dependencies update\nchore(deps): update vitest to v3.2.4\n\n# CI changes\nci(config): add coverage threshold checks\n\n# Release automation (auto-generated, usually ignored by commitlint)\nchore(release): version packages\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```bash\n# Stage and commit\ngit add . && git commit -m \"feat(components): add feature\"\n\n# Check commit format is valid\necho \"feat(components): add feature\" | npx commitlint\n\n# View recent commit formats for reference\ngit log --oneline -10\n\n# Amend last commit (only if not pushed!)\ngit commit --amend\n\n# Create changeset for package changes\npnpm changeset\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:26:16.795Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Version Control Agents requiring standardized commit formatting and GPG signing","zh":"适合需要标准化提交格式和GPG签名的版本控制代理","ja":"標準化されたコミット形式とGPG署名を必要とするバージョン管理エージェントに最適","ko":"표준화된 커밋 형식 및 GPG 서명이 필요한 버전 제어 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Control de Versiones que requieren un formato de compromiso estandarizado y firma GPG","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de contrôle de version nécessitant un format de commit standardisé et une signature GPG","de":"Ideal für Version-Control-Agents, die ein standardisiertes Commit-Format und eine GPG-Signatur erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Controle de Versão que requerem formatação de commit padronizada e assinatura GPG","ru":"Идеально для агентов контроля версий, требующих стандартизированного форматирования коммитов и подписи GPG","ar":"مثالية لموكلات التحكم في الإصدار التي تتطلب تنسيق إلتزام معياري وتوقيع GPG"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce Conventional Commits standards, ensuring all commits are GPG-signed and verified through pre-commit hooks, utilizing protocols like GPG for secure signing and maintaining a consistent commit format","zh":"赋予代理人执行标准提交规范的能力，确保所有提交都经过GPG签名和通过预提交钩子验证，利用GPG等协议进行安全签名并保持一致的提交格式","ja":"エージェントに従典的なコミット規格を実施する能力を与え、すべてのコミットがGPG署名され、事前コミットフックを介して検証されることを保証し、GPGなどのプロトコルを使用してセキュアな署名を行い、一貫したコミット形式を維持する","ko":"에이전트에 표준 커밋 규격을 강제하는 능력을 부여하여 모든 커밋이 GPG 서명되고 사전 커밋 후크를 통해 검증되도록 하며, GPG와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 보안 서명과 일관된 커밋 형식을 유지","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar los estándares de Commits Convencionales, asegurando que todos los commits estén firmados y verificados con GPG a través de ganchos pre-commit, utilizando protocolos como GPG para una firma segura y manteniendo un formato de commit consistente","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer les normes de Commits Conventionnels, en s''assurant que tous les commits sont signés et vérifiés avec GPG via des crochets pre-commit, en utilisant des protocoles comme GPG pour une signature sécurisée et en maintenant un format de commit cohérent","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Standards von Conventional Commits durchzusetzen, indem sichergestellt wird, dass alle Commits durch GPG signiert und über Pre-Commit-Hooks verifiziert werden, indem Protokolle wie GPG für eine sichere Signatur verwendet werden und ein konsistentes Commit-Format beibehalten wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor os padrões de Commits Convencionais, garantindo que todos os commits sejam assinados com GPG e verificados por meio de ganchos pré-commit, utilizando protocolos como GPG para assinatura segura e manter um formato de commit consistente","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов Конвенциональных Коммитов, гарантируя, что все коммиты подписаны с помощью GPG и верифицируются через предкоммит-хуки, используя протоколы như GPG для безопасной подписи и поддержания последовательного формата коммита","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من فرض معايير الإلتزامات التقليدية، مما يضمن أن يتم التوقيع على جميع الإلتزامات وتحققها من خلال مشابك ما قبل الإلتزام، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل GPG لتوقيع آمن والحفاظ على تنسيق إلتزام متسق"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit validation","Generating standardized commit messages","Ensuring GPG signing for secure commits"],"zh":["自动提交验证","生成标准化提交消息","确保GPG签名以实现安全提交"],"ja":["コミットの自動検証","標準化されたコミットメッセージの生成","セキュアなコミットのためのGPG署名の確保"],"ko":["자동 커밋 검증","표준화된 커밋 메시지 생성","보안 커밋을 위한 GPG 서명의 보장"],"es":["Automatización de la validación de commits","Generación de mensajes de commit estandarizados","Asegurando la firma GPG para commits seguros"],"fr":["Automatisation de la validation des commits","Génération de messages de commit standardisés","Assurer la signature GPG pour des commits sécurisés"],"de":["Automatisierung der Commit-Validierung","Erzeugung standardisierter Commit-Nachrichten","Sicherstellung der GPG-Signatur für sichere Commits"],"pt":["Automatizar a validação de commit","Gerar mensagens de commit padronizadas","Garantir assinatura GPG para commits seguros"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку коммита","Генерировать стандартизированные сообщения коммита","Обеспечивать подпись GPG для безопасных коммитов"],"ar":["أتمتة التحقق من الإلتزام","جعل رسائل الإلتزام معيارية","ضمان التوقيع GPG من أجل إلتزامات آمنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires full shell permissions","Must run outside sandbox environment","Never use --no-gpg-sign or --no-verify flags"],"zh":["需要完整的shell权限","必须在沙盒环境外运行","永远不能使用--no-gpg-sign或--no-verify标志"],"ja":["完全なシェル権限が必要","サンドボックス環境の外で実行する必要がある","--no-gpg-signまたは--no-verifyフラグを使用してはならない"],"ko":["완전한 쉘 권한이 필요","샌드박스 환경 외부에서 실행해야 함","--no-gpg-sign 또는 --no-verify 플래그를 사용할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere permisos de shell completos","Debe ejecutarse fuera del entorno de sandbox","Nunca utilice las opciones --no-gpg-sign o --no-verify"],"fr":["Nécessite des permissions de shell complètes","Doit s''exécuter en dehors de l''environnement de sandbox","Ne jamais utiliser les options --no-gpg-sign ou --no-verify"],"de":["Erfordert vollständige Shell-Berechtigungen","Muss außerhalb der Sandbox-Umgebung ausgeführt werden","Niemals die Optionen --no-gpg-sign oder --no-verify verwenden"],"pt":["Exige permissões de shell completo","Deve ser executado fora do ambiente de sandbox","Nunca use as flags --no-gpg-sign ou --no-verify"],"ru":["Требует полных разрешений shell","Должно запускаться вне среды sandbox","Никогда не используйте флаги --no-gpg-sign или --no-verify"],"ar":["يتطلب صلاحيات شل كاملة","يجب تشغيله خارج بيئة الرمل","أبداً لا تستخدم أعلام --no-gpg-sign أو --no-verify"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ewei068/pokestar/use-deact-hook', 'community', 'ewei068', 'pokestar', 'ewei068/pokestar', 'use-deact-hook', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z', '2026-02-18T13:26:16.766Z', NULL, '{"id":"ewei068/pokestar/use-deact-hook","name":"use-deact-hook","description":{"zh":"Deact Hook 是一种可重用的函数，用于 Deact 元素，具有与 React Hook 类似的功能","ja":"Deact Hook は Deact 要素で使用できる再利用可能な関数です","ko":"Deact Hook 는 Deact 요소에서 사용할 수 있는 재사용 가능한 함수입니다","es":"Deact Hooks son funciones reutilizables inspiradas en React Hooks. Aprende a utilizarlas para mejorar tus aplicaciones.","fr":"Deact Hooks sont des fonctions réutilisables inspirées de React Hooks. Découvrez comment les utiliser pour améliorer vos applications.","de":"Deact Hooks sind wiederverwendbare Funktionen, die von React Hooks inspiriert sind. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie verwenden können, um Ihre Anwendungen zu verbessern.","pt":"Os hooks Deact são funções reutilizáveis inspiradas nos hooks React. Eles devem ser invocados sempre na mesma ordem dentro de um componente.","ru":"Хуки Deact - это многоразовые функции, вдохновленные хуками React. Они должны вызываться всегда в одном и том же порядке внутри компонента.","ar":"دياكت هكس هو دوال قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام مستوحاة من هكس رياكت. يجب استدعاؤها دائمًا في نفس الترتيب داخل المكون","en":"Pokemon Gacha Discord Bot"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Deact Hook 使用指南","ja":"Deact Hook の使用方法","ko":"Deact Hook 사용 방법","es":"Uso de Deact Hooks para Desarrolladores","fr":"Utiliser Deact Hooks pour les Développeurs","de":"Deact Hooks für Entwickler verwenden","pt":"Hooks Deact: Guia para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Deact Hooks: Руководство для Разработчиков","ar":"دياكت هكس: دليل للمطورين","en":"use-deact-hook"},"description":{"zh":"Deact Hook 是一种可重用的函数，用于 Deact 元素，具有与 React Hook 类似的功能","ja":"Deact Hook は Deact 要素で使用できる再利用可能な関数です","ko":"Deact Hook 는 Deact 요소에서 사용할 수 있는 재사용 가능한 함수입니다","es":"Deact Hooks son funciones reutilizables inspiradas en React Hooks. Aprende a utilizarlas para mejorar tus aplicaciones.","fr":"Deact Hooks sont des fonctions réutilisables inspirées de React Hooks. Découvrez comment les utiliser pour améliorer vos applications.","de":"Deact Hooks sind wiederverwendbare Funktionen, die von React Hooks inspiriert sind. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie verwenden können, um Ihre Anwendungen zu verbes...","pt":"Os hooks Deact são funções reutilizáveis inspiradas nos hooks React. Eles devem ser invocados sempre na mesma ordem dentro de um componente.","ru":"Хуки Deact - это многоразовые функции, вдохновленные хуками React. Они должны вызываться всегда в одном и том же порядке внутри компонента.","ar":"دياكت هكس هو دوال قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام مستوحاة من هكس رياكت. يجب استدعاؤها دائمًا في نفس الترتيب داخل المكون","en":"Pokemon Gacha Discord Bot"},"definition":{"en":"Pokemon Gacha Discord Bot"},"features":{"zh":["useState","useRef","useMemo","支持 React-like Hooks","所有 Hook 需要 ref 作为最后一个参数"],"ja":["useState","useRef","useMemo","React-like Hooks をサポート","すべての Hook には ref が最後のパラメータとして必要"],"ko":["useState","useRef","useMemo","React-like Hook 지원","모든 Hook 에서 ref 가 마지막 매개변수로 필요"],"es":["Uso de useState con ref","Uso de useRef con ref","Uso de useMemo con ref","Diferencias clave con React","Hooks primitivos disponibles"],"fr":["Utilisation de useState avec ref","Utilisation de useRef avec ref","Utilisation de useMemo avec ref","Différences clés avec React","Hooks primitifs disponibles"],"de":["Verwendung von useState mit ref","Verwendung von useRef mit ref","Verwendung von useMemo mit ref","Wichtige Unterschiede zu React","Verfügbare Primitive Hooks"],"pt":["useState","useRef","useMemo","Reutilização de componentes","Eficiência de renderização","Compatibilidade com React"],"ru":["useState","useRef","useMemo","Многоразовость компонентов","Эффективность рендеринга","Совместимость с React"],"ar":["useState","useRef","useMemo","إعادة استخدام المكونات","فعالية العرض","التوافق مع رياكت"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Deact Hook","React Hook","useState","useRef","useMemo","Deact 开发","前端开发"],"ja":["Deact Hook","React Hook","useState","useRef","useMemo","Deact 開発","フロントエンド開発"],"ko":["Deact Hook","React Hook","useState","useRef","useMemo","Deact 개발","프론트엔드 개발"],"es":["Deact Hooks","React Hooks","Desarrollo de aplicaciones","Programación funcional","useState","useRef","useMemo"],"fr":["Deact Hooks","React Hooks","Développement d''applications","Programmation fonctionnelle","useState","useRef","useMemo"],"de":["Deact Hooks","React Hooks","Anwendungsentwicklung","Funktionale Programmierung","useState","useRef","useMemo"],"pt":["Deact Hooks","React Hooks","Desenvolvimento de componentes","Reutilização de código","Eficiência de renderização","Programação em JavaScript","Bibliotecas de front-end","Desenvolvedores web"],"ru":["Deact Hooks","React Hooks","Разработка компонентов","Многоразовость кода","Эффективность рендеринга","Программирование на JavaScript","Библиотеки фронтенда","Веб-разработчики"],"ar":["دياكت هكس","رياكت هكس","تطوير المكونات","إعادة استخدام الكود","فعالية العرض","برمجة جافا سكريبت","مكتبات واجهة المستخدم","مطورو الويب"]}},"owner":"ewei068","repo":"pokestar","repoPath":"ewei068/pokestar","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"use-deact-hook","description":"Use Deact hooks for state management, memoization, and side effects. Reference for all available hooks.","bodyPreview":"# Using Deact Hooks\n\nHooks are re-usable functions in Deact elements inspired by React hooks. Similarly to React hooks, they should always be invoked in the same order within a component.\n\n## Key Difference from React\n\n**All hooks require `ref` as the last parameter.**\n\n```javascript\n// React\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\n\n// Deact\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0, ref);\n```\n\n## Available Primative Hooks (refer to `deact.js`)\n\n### React-like hooks\n\n- `useState`\n- `useRef`\n- `useMemo","body":"# Using Deact Hooks\n\nHooks are re-usable functions in Deact elements inspired by React hooks. Similarly to React hooks, they should always be invoked in the same order within a component.\n\n## Key Difference from React\n\n**All hooks require `ref` as the last parameter.**\n\n```javascript\n// React\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0);\n\n// Deact\nconst [value, setValue] = useState(0, ref);\n```\n\n## Available Primative Hooks (refer to `deact.js`)\n\n### React-like hooks\n\n- `useState`\n- `useRef`\n- `useMemo`\n- `useCallback`\n\n### Awaited hooks: used to await asynchronous code like data fetching.\n\n```javascript\nconst userData = await useAwaitedMemo(() => fetchUser(userId), [userId], ref);\n```\n\n- `useAwaitedMemo`\n- `useAwaitedEffect`\n\n### useCallbackBinding\n\nBind a callback to Discord component interactions (buttons, select menus). Refer to the `deact-component-callback` skill on how to use.\n\n### useModalSubmitCallbackBinding\n\nHandle modal form submissions.\n\n```javascript\nconst onSubmitKey = useModalSubmitCallbackBinding(\n  (interaction, data) => {\n    const inputValue = interaction.fields.getTextInputValue(\"inputId\");\n    setFormValue(inputValue);\n  },\n  ref,\n  { defer: true },\n);\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Pagination State\n\n```javascript\nconst [page, setPage] = useState(1, ref);\n\nconst prevKey = useCallbackBinding(() => setPage((p) => p - 1), ref);\nconst nextKey = useCallbackBinding(() => setPage((p) => p + 1), ref);\n```\n\n### Toggle State\n\n```javascript\nconst [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false, ref);\n\nconst toggleKey = useCallbackBinding(() => setIsOpen((v) => !v), ref);\n```\n\n### Filtered Data\n\n```javascript\nconst [filter, setFilter] = useState({}, ref);\n\nconst filteredItems = useMemo(\n  () => items.filter((item) => matchesFilter(item, filter)),\n  [items, filter],\n  ref,\n);\n```\n\n### Data with Loading\n\n```javascript\nconst result = await useAwaitedMemo(() => fetchData(id), [id], ref);\n\nif (result.err) {\n  return { err: result.err };\n}\n\nconst data = result.data;\n```\n\n## Custom Hooks\n\nCustom hooks are created in `src/hooks` and can be used for more specific purposes. Refer to the `create-deact-hook` skill on creating a custom hook.\n\n## Dependency Arrays\n\nLike React, dependencies determine when hooks re-run:\n\n```javascript\n// Always recalculates (no deps = every render)\nuseMemo(() => compute(), [], ref);\n\n// Recalculates when a or b changes\nuseMemo(() => compute(a, b), [a, b], ref);\n```\n\n**Include all values used inside the callback that could change.**\n\n## Key Rules\n\n1. **Always pass `ref` as last argument**\n2. **Don''t call hooks conditionally** (same as React)\n3. **Hooks must be called in same order every render**\n4. **`await` async hooks (`useAwaitedMemo`, `useAwaitedEffect`)**\n5. **Use `defer: false` for callbacks that show modals**\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:26:16.766Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing reusable functions in Deact elements with Hooks like useState, useRef, and useMemo.","zh":"非常适合需要在 Deact 元素中使用可重用函数的前端代理，尤其是那些使用 useState、useRef 和 useMemo 等 Hooks 的代理。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントが Deact 要素で再利用可能な関数を使用する必要がある場合、特に useState、useRef、useMemo などの Hooks を使用する場合に最適です。","ko":"프론트엔드 에이전트가 Deact 요소에서 재사용 가능한 함수를 사용해야 하는 경우, 특히 useState, useRef, useMemo 등의 Hooks를 사용하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan funciones reutilizables en elementos Deact con Hooks como useState, useRef y useMemo.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin de fonctions réutilisables dans les éléments Deact avec des Hooks comme useState, useRef et useMemo.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die wiederverwendbare Funktionen in Deact-Elementen mit Hooks wie useState, useRef und useMemo benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de funções reutilizáveis em elementos Deact com Hooks como useState, useRef e useMemo.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которые нуждаются в переиспользуемых функциях в элементах Deact с крючками типа useState, useRef и useMemo.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الذي يحتاج إلى دوال قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام في عناصر Deact مع Hooks مثل useState و useRef و useMemo."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create reusable functions in Deact elements using Hooks like useState, useRef, and useMemo, all while ensuring proper invocation order and ref parameter inclusion, allowing for seamless integration with Discord bots and other Deact-based applications.","zh":"赋予代理创建 Deact 元素中可重用函数的能力，使用像 useState、useRef 和 useMemo 这样的 Hooks，并确保正确的调用顺序和 ref 参数的包含，从而实现与 Discord 机器人和其他基于 Deact 的应用程序的无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントが Deact 要素で再利用可能な関数を作成できるようにし、useState、useRef、useMemo などの Hooks を使用して、正しい呼び出し順序と ref パラメータの包含を保証し、Discord ボットやその他の Deact ベースのアプリケーションとの無縫な統合を可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 Deact 요소에서 재사용 가능한 함수를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, useState, useRef, useMemo 등의 Hooks를 사용하여 올바른 호출 순서와 ref 매개변수의 포함을 보장하여 Discord 봇 및 기타 Deact 기반 애플리케이션과 무결한 통합을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear funciones reutilizables en elementos Deact utilizando Hooks como useState, useRef y useMemo, al mismo tiempo que garantiza el orden de invocación correcto y la inclusión del parámetro ref, lo que permite una integración sin problemas con bots de Discord y otras aplicaciones basadas en Deact.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des fonctions réutilisables dans les éléments Deact en utilisant des Hooks comme useState, useRef et useMemo, tout en garantissant l''ordre d''invocation correct et l''inclusion du paramètre ref, ce qui permet une intégration transparente avec les bots Discord et d''autres applications basées sur Deact.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, wiederverwendbare Funktionen in Deact-Elementen mit Hooks wie useState, useRef und useMemo zu erstellen, während gleichzeitig die richtige Reihenfolge der Aufrufe und die Einbeziehung des Ref-Parameters sichergestellt werden, was eine nahtlose Integration mit Discord-Bots und anderen Deact-basierten Anwendungen ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar funções reutilizáveis em elementos Deact usando Hooks como useState, useRef e useMemo, garantindo a ordem de invocação correta e a inclusão do parâmetro ref, permitindo uma integração perfeita com bots do Discord e outras aplicações baseadas em Deact.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать переиспользуемые функции в элементах Deact с помощью крючков типа useState, useRef и useMemo, обеспечивая правильный порядок вызова и включение параметра ref, что позволяет обеспечить бесшовную интеграцию с ботами Discord и другими приложениями на основе Deact.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من إنشاء دوال قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام في عناصر Deact باستخدام Hooks مثل useState و useRef و useMemo، مع ضمان ترتيب الاستدعاء الصحيح وإدراج 매개 변수 المرجع، مما يسمح بالتكامل السلس مع bots Discord وتطبيقات Deact الأخرى."},"useCases":{"en":["Building reusable UI components with Deact Hooks","Creating Discord bots with dynamic, state-dependent interfaces","Optimizing Deact element rendering with useMemo"],"zh":["使用 Deact Hooks 构建可重用 UI 组件","创建具有动态、状态依赖界面的 Discord 机器人","使用 useMemo 优化 Deact 元素渲染"],"ja":["Deact Hooks を使用して再利用可能な UI コンポーネントを構築する","動的、状態依存のインターフェイスを持つ Discord ボットを作成する","useMemo を使用して Deact 要素のレンダリングを最適化する"],"ko":["Deact Hooks를 사용하여 재사용 가능한 UI 구성 요소를 구축하는 것","동적, 상태 의존 인터페이스를 갖는 Discord 봇을 생성하는 것","useMemo를 사용하여 Deact 요소의 렌더링을 최적화하는 것"],"es":["Construir componentes de interfaz de usuario reutilizables con Deact Hooks","Crear bots de Discord con interfaces dinámicas y dependientes del estado","Optimizar la representación de elementos Deact con useMemo"],"fr":["Créer des composants d''interface utilisateur réutilisables avec des Deact Hooks","Créer des bots Discord avec des interfaces dynamiques et dépendantes de l''état","Optimiser le rendu d''éléments Deact avec useMemo"],"de":["Erstellen von wiederverwendbaren Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit Deact-Hooks","Erstellen von Discord-Bots mit dynamischen, zustandsabhängigen Schnittstellen","Optimieren des Renderns von Deact-Elementen mit useMemo"],"pt":["Construir componentes de IU reutilizáveis com Hooks Deact","Criar bots do Discord com interfaces dinâmicas e dependentes de estado","Otimizar a renderização de elementos Deact com useMemo"],"ru":["Построение переиспользуемых компонентов пользовательского интерфейса с помощью крючков Deact","Создание ботов Discord с динамическими и зависящими от состояния интерфейсами","Оптимизация рендеринга элементов Deact с помощью useMemo"],"ar":["بناء مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام مع Hooks Deact","إنشاء bots Discord مع واجهات ديناميكية ومتعلقة بالحالة","تحسين جودة عرض عناصر Deact باستخدام useMemo"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Deact framework","All hooks must be invoked with a ref parameter"],"zh":["需要 Deact 框架","所有 Hooks 必须带有 ref 参数"],"ja":["Deact フレームワークが必要","すべての Hooks は ref パラメータを使用して呼び出さなければならない"],"ko":["Deact 프레임워크가 필요","모든 Hooks는 ref 매개변수를 사용하여 호출되어야 함"],"es":["Requiere el framework Deact","Todos los hooks deben invocarse con un parámetro ref"],"fr":["Nécessite le framework Deact","Tous les hooks doivent être invoqués avec un paramètre ref"],"de":["Benötigt das Deact-Framework","Alle Hooks müssen mit einem Ref-Parameter aufgerufen werden"],"pt":["Exige o framework Deact","Todos os hooks devem ser invocados com um parâmetro ref"],"ru":["Требует фреймворка Deact","Все крючки должны быть вызваны с параметром ref"],"ar":["يتطلب إطار Deact","يجب استدعاء جميع Hooks مع parameter المرجع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('aussiegingersnap/ai-project-start/project-setup', 'community', 'aussiegingersnap', 'ai-project-start', 'aussiegingersnap/ai-project-start', 'project-setup', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z', '2026-02-18T13:26:25.119Z', NULL, '{"id":"aussiegingersnap/ai-project-start/project-setup","name":"project-setup","description":{"zh":"项目设置技能提供交互式入门流程，帮助用户配置项目技术栈和技能","ja":"プロジェクト設定スキルは、インタラクティブな入門フローを提供し、ユーザーがプロジェクトの技術スタックとスキルを設定するのに役立ちます","ko":"프로젝트 설정 스킬은 인터랙티브 온보딩 흐름을 제공하여 사용자가 프로젝트 기술 스택과 스킬을 설정하는 데 도움을 줍니다","es":"La habilidad de configuración de proyecto es una herramienta interactiva para configurar nuevos proyectos","fr":"La compétence de configuration de projet est un outil interactif pour configurer les nouveaux projets","de":"Die Projekt-Einrichtungsfunktion ist ein interaktives Werkzeug zur Konfiguration neuer Projekte","pt":"A habilidade de configuração de projeto fornece um fluxo de integração interativo para novos projetos criados a partir do modelo de projeto ai-project-start.","ru":"Навык настройки проекта предоставляет интерактивный поток интеграции для новых проектов, созданных на основе модели проекта ai-project-start.","ar":"مهارة إعداد المشروع توفر تدفق تكامل تفاعلي للمشاريع الجديدة التي تم إنشاؤها من نموذج المشروع ai-project-start.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"项目设置技能 - 项目自动化配置","ja":"プロジェクト設定スキル - 自動化プロジェクト構成","ko":"프로젝트 설정 스킬 - 자동화 프로젝트 구성","es":"Configuración de Proyecto","fr":"Configuration de Projet","de":"Projekt Einrichtung","pt":"Configuração de Projeto - Fluxo de Integração para Desenv...","ru":"Настройка Проекта - Интерактивный Поток для Разработчиков","ar":"إعداد المشروع - تدفق التكامل التفاعلي للمطورين","en":"project-setup"},"description":{"zh":"项目设置技能提供交互式入门流程，帮助用户配置项目技术栈和技能","ja":"プロジェクト設定スキルは、インタラクティブな入門フローを提供し、ユーザーがプロジェクトの技術スタックとスキルを設定するのに役立ちます","ko":"프로젝트 설정 스킬은 인터랙티브 온보딩 흐름을 제공하여 사용자가 프로젝트 기술 스택과 스킬을 설정하는 데 도움을 줍니다","es":"La habilidad de configuración de proyecto es una herramienta interactiva para configurar nuevos proyectos","fr":"La compétence de configuration de projet est un outil interactif pour configurer les nouveaux projets","de":"Die Projekt-Einrichtungsfunktion ist ein interaktives Werkzeug zur Konfiguration neuer Projekte","pt":"A habilidade de configuração de projeto fornece um fluxo de integração interativo para novos projetos criados a partir do modelo de projeto ai-project-start.","ru":"Навык настройки проекта предоставляет интерактивный поток интеграции для новых проектов, созданных на основе модели проекта ai-project-start.","ar":"مهارة إعداد المشروع توفر تدفق تكامل تفاعلي للمشاريع الجديدة التي تم إنشاؤها من نموذج المشروع ai-project-start.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["交互式入门流程","自动配置项目技术栈","设置项目技能","支持多种项目模板","简化项目设置流程"],"ja":["インタラクティブな入門フロー","プロジェクトの技術スタックを自動的に構成","プロジェクトのスキルを設定","複数のプロジェクトテンプレートをサポート","プロジェクト設定プロセスを簡素化"],"ko":["인터랙티브 온보딩 흐름","프로젝트 기술 스택 자동 구성","프로젝트 스킬 설정","다양한 프로젝트 템플릿 지원","프로젝트 설정 proceso 단순화"],"es":["Flujo de configuración interactivo","Detección automática de nuevos proyectos","Configuración de la tecnología adecuada","Guía para los usuarios","Integración con plantillas de proyecto"],"fr":["Flux de configuration interactif","Détection automatique de nouveaux projets","Configuration de la technologie appropriée","Guide pour les utilisateurs","Intégration avec des modèles de projet"],"de":["Interaktiver Konfigurationsfluss","Automatische Erkennung neuer Projekte","Konfiguration der geeigneten Technologie","Benutzerhandbuch","Integration mit Projektvorlagen"],"pt":["Fluxo de integração interativo","Configuração de projeto personalizada","Detecção automática de novos projetos","Integração com o modelo de projeto ai-project-start","Guias de configuração de tecnologia","Suporte a desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Интерактивный поток интеграции","Пользовательская настройка проекта","Автоматическое обнаружение новых проектов","Интеграция с моделью проекта ai-project-start","Руководства по настройке технологии","Поддержка разработчиков"],"ar":["تدفق تكامل تفاعلي","إعداد مشروع مخصص","كشف автомاتيكي للمشاريع الجديدة","التكامل مع نموذج المشروع ai-project-start","دلائل إعداد التكنولوجيا","دعم المطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["项目设置技能","自动化配置","交互式入门流程","项目技术栈","项目技能","新项目设置"],"ja":["プロジェクト設定スキル","自動構成","インタラクティブな入門フロー","プロジェクトの技術スタック","プロジェクトのスキル","新しいプロジェクトの設定"],"ko":["프로젝트 설정 스킬","자동화 구성","인터랙티브 온보딩 흐름","프로젝트 기술 스택","프로젝트 스킬","새로운 프로젝트 설정"],"es":["configuración de proyecto","desarrollo de software","tecnología de proyecto","plantillas de proyecto","flujo de configuración","detección automática","guía para desarrolladores"],"fr":["configuration de projet","développement de logiciels","technologie de projet","modèles de projet","flux de configuration","détection automatique","guide pour les développeurs"],"de":["Projekt-Einrichtung","Software-Entwicklung","Projekt-Technologie","Projekt-Vorlagen","Konfigurationsfluss","automatische Erkennung","Handbuch für Entwickler"],"pt":["configuração de projeto","fluxo de integração","desenvolvedores","modelo de projeto","ai-project-start","tecnologia","projeto","integração","desenvolvimento"],"ru":["настройка проекта","поток интеграции","разработчики","модель проекта","ai-project-start","технология","проект","интеграция","разработка"],"ar":["إعداد مشروع","تدفق تكامل","مطورين","نموذج مشروع","ai-project-start","تكنولوجيا","مشروع","تكامل","تطوير"]}},"owner":"aussiegingersnap","repo":"ai-project-start","repoPath":"aussiegingersnap/ai-project-start","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.519Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"project-setup","description":"Interactive project setup for new repos using this template. Detects placeholder text in project.mdc, asks about tech stack, recommends skills, and configures the project. Trigger automatically when project.mdc contains [Project Name].","bodyPreview":"# Project Setup Skill\n\nInteractive onboarding flow for new projects created from the ai-project-start template. This skill guides users through configuring their project with the right tech stack and skills.\n\n## Trigger Condition\n\nThis skill should trigger automatically when:\n- `project.mdc` contains the placeholder `[Project Name]`\n\nOr when the user explicitly asks to set up their project.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Detection & Welcome\n\n### Check for New Project\n\nRead `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` and che","body":"# Project Setup Skill\n\nInteractive onboarding flow for new projects created from the ai-project-start template. This skill guides users through configuring their project with the right tech stack and skills.\n\n## Trigger Condition\n\nThis skill should trigger automatically when:\n- `project.mdc` contains the placeholder `[Project Name]`\n\nOr when the user explicitly asks to set up their project.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Detection & Welcome\n\n### Check for New Project\n\nRead `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` and check for placeholder text:\n\n```\n[Project Name]\n[One-line description of the project]\n[e.g., Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui]\n```\n\nIf placeholders exist, proceed with setup. If project appears configured, ask:\n> \"Your project.mdc appears to be configured. Would you like to reconfigure it, or is there something specific I can help with?\"\n\n### Welcome Message\n\n```\n👋 Welcome to your new project!\n\nLet''s get you set up. I''ll ask a few questions about what you''re building,\nthen recommend skills to import and configure your project.mdc file.\n\nThis takes about 2 minutes.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Gather Project Info\n\n### Ask Questions\n\nAsk these questions one at a time or use the AskQuestion tool:\n\n**1. Project Name**\n> What''s the name of your project?\n\n**2. Description**\n> In one sentence, what are you building?\n\n**3. Project Type**\n> What type of project is this?\n- Web App (Next.js)\n- API Only (NestJS)\n- Full Stack (Next.js + NestJS)\n- CLI Tool\n- Other\n\n**4. Dashboard Style** (if Web App or Full Stack)\n> Which dashboard layout do you want to start with?\n- SaaS Admin (sidebar nav, user management, billing pages)\n- Analytics (charts, metrics, data tables)\n- E-commerce (products, orders, inventory)\n- Minimal Shell (just auth + empty dashboard skeleton)\n\n**5. Database**\n> What database are you using?\n- PostgreSQL (Drizzle ORM)\n- PostgreSQL (Prisma ORM)\n- SQLite\n- None / External API only\n\n**6. Authentication**\n> How will you handle auth?\n- Better Auth\n- NextAuth\n- External auth service\n- None needed yet\n\n**7. Deployment**\n> Where will you deploy?\n- Railway\n- Vercel\n- AWS\n- Docker / Self-hosted\n- Not decided yet\n\n**8. State Management** (if Web App or Full Stack)\n> How will you manage frontend state?\n- Tanstack Query + Effector\n- Zustand\n- React state only\n\n**9. Task Tracking**\n> Do you use Linear for task tracking?\n- Yes\n- No / Other\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Recommend Skills\n\nBased on answers, recommend skills from the cursor-skills repo.\n\n### Skill Recommendation Matrix\n\n| Tech Choice | Recommended Skills |\n|-------------|-------------------|\n| Next.js | `nextjs-16`, `ui-shadcn-studio` |\n| NestJS | `nestjs` |\n| PostgreSQL + Drizzle | `db-postgres` |\n| PostgreSQL + Prisma | `db-prisma` |\n| Better Auth | `auth-better-auth` |\n| Railway | `infra-railway` |\n| Docker | `docker-local` |\n| REST API | `api-rest` |\n| Tanstack Query + Effector | `effector`, `state-management` |\n| Linear tasks | `linear` |\n| Any frontend project | `feature-build`, `ui-design-system`, `ui-shadcn-studio` |\n| Any project | `feature-build`, `documentation`, `versioning` |\n\n### Present Recommendations\n\n```markdown\n## Recommended Skills\n\nBased on your stack, I recommend importing these skills:\n\n**Core (always useful):**\n- `feature-build` - Complete feature development lifecycle\n- `documentation` - Project documentation standards\n- `versioning` - Semantic versioning with CHANGELOG\n\n**For your stack:**\n- `nextjs-16` - Next.js 16 patterns and conventions\n- `db-postgres` - PostgreSQL with Drizzle ORM\n- `effector` - Effector state management\n- `linear` - Linear issue tracking\n\n### How to Import Skills\n\n1. Open Cursor Settings (Cmd+Shift+J)\n2. Go to the **Rules** tab\n3. Click **Add Rule** → **Remote Rule (GitHub)**\n4. Enter: `https://github.com/aussiegingersnap/cursor-skills`\n5. Select the skills you want to import\n\nThe skills will be added to your `.cursor/skills/` directory.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Update project.mdc\n\n### Generate Updated Content\n\nReplace placeholders with gathered info:\n\n```markdown\n---\nalwaysApply: true\n---\n\n# {Project Name}\n\nNEVER EDIT MY ENV FILES FOR ME, ALWAYS GIVE ME DIRECT INSTRUCTIONS WITH EXAMPLES TO COPY ON WHAT TO EDIT\n\n## What We''re Building\n\n{Description}\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- **Frontend**: {Frontend stack}\n- **Backend**: {Backend stack if applicable}\n- **Database**: {Database choice}\n- **Auth**: {Auth choice}\n- **State**: {State management}\n- **Deploy**: {Deployment target}\n- **Skills**: Cursor native skills\n\n## Core Constraints\n\n- **KISS**: Simplest solution that works\n- **DRY**: Don''t repeat—types in code, schema in migrations, patterns in docs\n- {Any project-specific constraints}\n\n## Documentation\n\n| Doc | Purpose |\n|-----|---------|\n| [TASKS.md](../TASKS.md) | Current sprint + backlog |\n| [CHANGELOG.md](../CHANGELOG.md) | Progress updates |\n| [docs/architecture.md](../docs/architecture.md) | Technical patterns + decisions |\n\n## Git Standards\n\n**Conventional Commits**: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`\n\nTypes: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `chore`, `ci`, `build`, `revert`\n\n```bash\nfeat: add user authentication\nfix(api): handle null response\ndocs: update architecture patterns\n```\n\n**Security**:\n- ❌ Never commit `.env` files or secrets\n- ✅ Secrets in `.env.local` (gitignored)\n- ✅ `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix for client-safe vars\n\n## Environment\n\nSee `.env.example` for required variables.\n\n## Workflow\n\nWhen a Cursor plan is complete, provide a summary block for manual git commits:\n\n```\n### Done\n\n**Summary**: [Brief description of changes]\n\n**Commits** (ohmyzsh):\ngaa && gcmsg \"feat(scope): description\"\ngcmsg \"fix(scope): description\"\ngp\n```\n\nUser will copy/paste these commands. Lefthook validates commit format and blocks secrets.\n```\n\n### Confirm Before Writing\n\n> I''ll update your project.mdc with this configuration. Here''s a preview:\n> \n> [Show key fields]\n>\n> Does this look correct? (y/n)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Finalize Setup\n\n### Update Files\n\n1. **Update project.mdc** with gathered configuration\n2. **Update TASKS.md** with initial sprint items based on project type\n3. **Update README.md** with project name and description\n\n### Completion Message\n\n```markdown\n## Setup Complete! 🎉\n\nYour project is configured with:\n- **Project**: {Name}\n- **Stack**: {Summary}\n- **Skills**: {Count} recommended (import via Cursor Settings)\n\n### Next Steps\n\n1. Import recommended skills via Cursor Settings (Cmd+Shift+J → Rules)\n2. Configure your `.env.local` based on `.env.example`\n3. Start building! Use `/feature-build` to work on tasks\n\n### Quick Commands\n\n```bash\n# Start dev server\nnpm run dev\n\n# Git workflow (ohmyzsh)\ngaa && gcmsg \"feat(scope): description\"\ngp\n```\n\nHappy building!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### If User Skips Questions\n\nUse sensible defaults:\n- Project Type: Web App\n- Database: None (can add later)\n- Auth: None (can add later)\n- Deploy: Not decided\n- State: React state only\n\n### If Import Fails\n\nProvide manual import instructions:\n```bash\n# Clone cursor-skills and copy desired skills\ngit clone https://github.com/aussiegingersnap/cursor-skills /tmp/cursor-skills\ncp -r /tmp/cursor-skills/skills/{skill-name} .cursor/skills/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Minimal Setup Flow\n\nFor users who want fast setup:\n\n1. \"What''s your project name and one-line description?\"\n2. \"Web app, API, or full stack?\"\n3. Generate config with defaults\n4. List recommended skills\n5. Done\n\n### Full Setup Flow\n\nFor users who want complete configuration:\n\n1. All 8 questions\n2. Detailed skill recommendations with explanations\n3. Preview and confirm project.mdc\n4. Update all project files\n5. Detailed next steps\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:26:25.119Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for AI Project Management Agents that automate development workflows and technical onboarding.","zh":"适用于自动化开发工作流和技术入职的 AI 项目管理代理。","ja":"開発ワークフローとテクニカルオンボーディングを自動化する AI プロジェクト管理エージェントに不可欠。","ko":"개발 워크플ロー 및 기술 온보딩을 자동화하는 AI 프로젝트 관리 에이전트에 필수입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de gestión de proyectos de inteligencia artificial que automatizan flujos de trabajo de desarrollo y configuración técnica.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de gestion de projet d''intelligence artificielle qui automatisent les flux de travail de développement et la configuration technique.","de":"Wesentlich für KI-Projektmanagement-Agenten, die Entwicklungswerkflüsse und technische Onboarding-Aufgaben automatisieren.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Gestão de Projetos de IA que automatizam fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento e integração técnica.","ru":"Необходимо для Агентов управления проектами ИИ, которые автоматизируют рабочие процессы разработки и техническое введение в курс дела.","ar":"أساسي لوكلاء إدارة مشاريع الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يقومون بأتمتة سير عمل التطوير والدمج التقني."},"recommendation":{"en":"Activates an interactive onboarding flow when `project.mdc` contains the `[Project Name]` placeholder, guiding users through tech stack selection and skill configuration from the ai-project-start template. Automates project initialization by reading and validating `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` configuration files.","zh":"当 `project.mdc` 包含 `[Project Name]` 占位符时，激活交互式入职流程，引导用户完成从 ai-project-start 模板的技术栈选择和技能配置。通过读取和验证 `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` 配置文件来自动化项目初始化。","ja":" `project.mdc` に `[Project Name]` プレースホルダーが含まれている場合、交互的なオンボーディング フローをアクティブ化し、ユーザーを ai-project-start テンプレートからのテクノロジー スタックの選択とスキル構成に誘導します。 `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` 構成ファイルを読み取り、検証することで、プロジェクトの初期化を自動化します。","ko":" `project.mdc`에 `[Project Name]` 자리 표시자가 포함된 경우 인터랙티브 온보딩 흐름을 활성화하여 ai-project-start 템플릿의 기술 스택 선택 및 스킬 구성으로 사용자를 안내합니다. `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` 구성 파일을 읽고 유효성 검사를 통해 프로젝트 초기화를 자동화합니다.","es":"Activa un flujo de configuración interactivo cuando `project.mdc` contiene el marcador de posición `[Project Name]`, guiando a los usuarios a través de la selección de la pila tecnológica y la configuración de habilidades desde la plantilla ai-project-start. Automatiza la inicialización del proyecto leyendo y validando archivos de configuración `.cursor/rules/project.mdc`.","fr":"Active un flux de configuration interactif lorsque `project.mdc` contient le marqueur de position `[Project Name]`, guidant les utilisateurs à travers la sélection de la pile technologique et la configuration des compétences à partir du modèle ai-project-start. Automatise l''initialisation du projet en lisant et en validant les fichiers de configuration `.cursor/rules/project.mdc`.","de":"Aktiviert einen interaktiven Onboarding-Prozess, wenn `project.mdc` den Platzhalter `[Project Name]` enthält, und führt die Benutzer durch die Auswahl der Technologie-Stacks und die Konfiguration von Fähigkeiten aus der Vorlage ai-project-start. Automatisiert die Projekterstellung durch das Lesen und Validieren von `.cursor/rules/project.mdc`-Konfigurationsdateien.","pt":"Ativa um fluxo interativo de integração quando `project.mdc` contém o marcador `[Nome do Projeto]`, orientando os usuários na seleção do stack tecnológico e configuração de habilidades a partir do modelo ai-project-start. Automatiza a inicialização do projeto ao ler e validar arquivos de configuração `.cursor/rules/project.mdc`.","ru":"Активирует интерактивный процесс введения в курс дела, когда `project.mdc` содержит заполнитель `[Название проекта]`, направляя пользователей через выбор технологического стека и настройку навыков из шаблона ai-project-start. Автоматизирует инициализацию проекта путем чтения и проверки файлов конфигурации `.cursor/rules/project.mdc`.","ar":"يفعّل سير دمج تفاعلي عندما يحتوي ملف `project.mdc` على العنصر النائب `[اسم المشروع]`، directing users through tech stack selection and skill configuration from the ai-project-start template. يُمكّن أتمتة تهيئة المشروع من خلال قراءة والتحقق من صحة ملفات التكوين `.cursor/rules/project.mdc`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating project initialization workflows","Configuring tech stack selection from templates","Validating project.mdc configuration files","Guiding users through interactive onboarding"],"zh":["自动化项目初始化工作流","从模板配置技术栈选择","验证 project.mdc 配置文件","引导用户完成交互式入职"],"ja":["プロジェクト初期化ワークフローを自動化する","テンプレートからのテクノロジー スタックの選択を構成する","project.mdc 構成ファイルを検証する","ユーザーを交互的なオンボーディングに導く"],"ko":["프로젝트 초기화 워크플ロー 자동화","템플릿에서 기술 스택 선택 구성","project.mdc 구성 파일 유효성 검사","인터랙티브 온보딩을 통해 사용자 안내"],"es":["Automatizar flujos de trabajo de inicialización de proyectos","Configurar la selección de la pila tecnológica desde plantillas","Validar archivos de configuración project.mdc","Guía a los usuarios a través de la configuración interactiva"],"fr":["Automatiser les flux de travail d''initialisation de projet","Configurer la sélection de la pile technologique à partir de modèles","Valider les fichiers de configuration project.mdc","Guider les utilisateurs à travers la configuration interactive"],"de":["Automatisieren von Projekterstellungs-Workflows","Konfigurieren der Technologie-Stack-Auswahl aus Vorlagen","Validieren von project.mdc-Konfigurationsdateien","Führen der Benutzer durch die interaktive Konfiguration"],"pt":["Automatizando fluxos de trabalho de inicialização de projetos","Configurando a seleção do stack tecnológico a partir de modelos","Validando arquivos de configuração project.mdc","Orientando usuários através de uma integração interativa"],"ru":["Автоматизация рабочих процессов инициализации проекта","Настройка выбора технологического стека из шаблонов","Проверка файлов конфигурации project.mdc","Направление пользователей через интерактивное введение в курс дела"],"ar":["أتمتة سير عمل تهيئة المشروع","تكوين اختيار المكدس التقني من القوالب","التحقق من صحة ملفات تكوين project.mdc","توجيه المستخدمين خلال عملية دمج تفاعلية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires specific placeholder in project.mdc","Depends on ai-project-start template structure","Needs filesystem access to read configuration"],"zh":["需要 project.mdc 中的特定占位符","依赖于 ai-project-start 模板结构","需要文件系统访问来读取配置"],"ja":["project.mdc に特定のプレースホルダーが必要","ai-project-start テンプレート構造に依存する","構成を読み取るためにファイル システムへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["project.mdc에 특정 자리 표시자가 필요함","ai-project-start 템플릿 구조에 의존함","구성을 읽어들이기 위해 파일 시스템 접근이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere un marcador de posición específico en project.mdc","Depende de la estructura de la plantilla ai-project-start","Necesita acceso al sistema de archivos para leer la configuración"],"fr":["Nécessite un marqueur de position spécifique dans project.mdc","Dépend de la structure du modèle ai-project-start","A besoin d''un accès au système de fichiers pour lire la configuration"],"de":["Benötigt einen bestimmten Platzhalter in project.mdc","Hängt von der Struktur der Vorlage ai-project-start ab","Benötigt Dateizugriff, um die Konfiguration zu lesen"],"pt":["Requer um marcador específico no project.mdc","Depende da estrutura do modelo ai-project-start","Requer acesso ao sistema de arquivos para ler a configuração"],"ru":["Требует определенного заполнителя в project.mdc","Зависит от структуры шаблона ai-project-start","Требует доступ к файловой системе для чтения конфигурации"],"ar":["يتطلب عنصرًا نائبًا محددًا في project.mdc","يعتمد على هيكل قالب ai-project-start","يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام الملفات لقراءة التكوين"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('jonsdoesch87-ai/craft-beer-wizard/color-consistency-checker', 'community', 'jonsdoesch87-ai', 'craft-beer-wizard', 'jonsdoesch87-ai/craft-beer-wizard', 'color-consistency-checker', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z', '2026-02-18T13:26:58.435Z', NULL, '{"id":"jonsdoesch87-ai/craft-beer-wizard/color-consistency-checker","name":"color-consistency-checker","description":{"zh":"颜色一致性检查器是一种工具，用于检查应用程序中颜色的使用是否与定义的颜色方案一致","ja":"カラーコンシステンシーチェッカーは、定義されたカラースキームに従ってアプリケーションで使用されているカラーをチェックするツールです","ko":"색상 일관성 체커는 애플리케이션에서 정의된 색상 체계와 일치하는지 확인하는 도구입니다","pt":"O verificador de cores consistentes é uma ferramenta que ajuda a garantir a harmonia visual do seu projeto, verificando se as cores estão alinhadas com o esquema de cores definido.","ru":"Проверка последовательности цвета - это инструмент, который помогает обеспечить визуальную гармонию вашего проекта, проверяя, соответствуют ли цвета заданной цветовой схеме.","ar":"مدقق التماسك اللوني هو أداة تساعد على ضمان الانسجام البصري لمشروعك من خلال التحقق من أن الألوان تتماشى مع مخطط الألوان المحدد.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"颜色一致性检查器","ja":"カラーコンシステンシーチェッカー","ko":"색상 일관성 체커","pt":"Verificador de Cores Consistentes","ru":"Проверка последовательности цвета","ar":"مدقق متسق الألوان","en":"color-consistency-checker"},"description":{"zh":"颜色一致性检查器是一种工具，用于检查应用程序中颜色的使用是否与定义的颜色方案一致","ja":"カラーコンシステンシーチェッカーは、定義されたカラースキームに従ってアプリケーションで使用されているカラーをチェックするツールです","ko":"색상 일관성 체커는 애플리케이션에서 정의된 색상 체계와 일치하는지 확인하는 도구입니다","pt":"O verificador de cores consistentes é uma ferramenta que ajuda a garantir a harmonia visual do seu projeto, verificando se as cores estão alinhadas com o esq...","ru":"Проверка последовательности цвета - это инструмент, который помогает обеспечить визуальную гармонию вашего проекта, проверяя, соответствуют ли цвета заданной...","ar":"مدقق التماسك اللوني هو أداة تساعد على ضمان الانسجام البصري لمشروعك من خلال التحقق من أن الألوان تتماشى مع مخطط الألوان المحدد.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["检查颜色使用的一致性","支持自定义颜色方案","集成到Tailwind CSS中","自动检查颜色使用","提供详细的错误报告"],"ja":["カラー使用の一貫性をチェック","カスタムカラースキームをサポート","Tailwind CSSとの統合","自動でカラー使用をチェック","詳細なエラーレポートを提供"],"ko":["색상 사용의 일관성을 확인","사용자 정의 색상 체계 지원","Tailwind CSS와의 통합","자동 색상 사용 확인","세부적인 오류 보고서 제공"],"pt":["Verificação de cores consistentes com o esquema de cores definido","Definição de cores em tailwind.config.ts e app/globals.css","Uso de classes de cores personalizadas","Verificação de cores para botões, links e estados de hover","Garantia de harmonia visual em todo o projeto"],"ru":["Проверка последовательности цвета с заданной цветовой схемой","Определение цветов в tailwind.config.ts и app/globals.css","Использование пользовательских цветовых классов","Проверка цветов для кнопок, ссылок и состояний наведения","Обеспечение визуальной гармонии во всем проекте"],"ar":["التحقق من التماسك اللوني مع مخطط الألوان المحدد","تحديد الألوان في tailwind.config.ts و app/globals.css","استخدام فئات الألوان المخصصة","التحقق من الألوان للزر و الروابط و حالات التمرير","ضمان الانسجام البصري في جميع أنحاء المشروع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["颜色一致性检查","Tailwind CSS","颜色方案","一致性检查","颜色使用","应用程序开发"],"ja":["カラーコンシステンシーチェック","Tailwind CSS","カラースキーム","一貫性チェック","カラー使用","アプリケーション開発"],"ko":["색상 일관성 체크","Tailwind CSS","색상 체계","일관성 확인","색상 사용","애플리케이션 개발"],"pt":["verificador de cores consistentes","esquema de cores","tailwind config","globais css","cores personalizadas","harmonia visual"],"ru":["проверка последовательности цвета","цветовая схема","tailwind config","глобальные css","пользовательские цветовые классы","визуальная гармония"],"ar":["مدقق التماسك اللوني","مخطط الألوان","تكوين تايل ويند","سي اس اس عالمي","فئات الألوان المخصصة","الانسجام البصري"]}},"owner":"jonsdoesch87-ai","repo":"craft-beer-wizard","repoPath":"jonsdoesch87-ai/craft-beer-wizard","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"color-consistency-checker","description":"Prüft die Farbkonsistenz im Projekt. Findet hardcoded Hex-Farben die durch Tailwind-Klassen ersetzt werden sollten. Verwende diesen Skill bei Code-Reviews, nach UI-Änderungen, oder wenn der User nach einer Farbprüfung fragt.","bodyPreview":"# Color Consistency Checker\n\nPrüft ob Farben konsistent mit dem Farbschema verwendet werden.\n\n## Offizielles Farbschema\n\nDefiniert in `tailwind.config.ts` und `app/globals.css`:\n\n| Farbe | Hex | Tailwind-Klasse | Verwendung |\n|-------|-----|-----------------|------------|\n| Primary | `#FFBF00` | `primary` | Akzente, Buttons, Links |\n| Primary Hover | `#E5AC00` | `primary/90` | Hover-States |\n| Primary Foreground | `#1a1a1a` | `primary-foreground` | Text auf Primary |\n| Background | `#1a1a1a` | `","body":"# Color Consistency Checker\n\nPrüft ob Farben konsistent mit dem Farbschema verwendet werden.\n\n## Offizielles Farbschema\n\nDefiniert in `tailwind.config.ts` und `app/globals.css`:\n\n| Farbe | Hex | Tailwind-Klasse | Verwendung |\n|-------|-----|-----------------|------------|\n| Primary | `#FFBF00` | `primary` | Akzente, Buttons, Links |\n| Primary Hover | `#E5AC00` | `primary/90` | Hover-States |\n| Primary Foreground | `#1a1a1a` | `primary-foreground` | Text auf Primary |\n| Background | `#1a1a1a` | `background` | Hintergrund |\n| Foreground | `#ededed` | `foreground` | Text |\n| Secondary | `#2a2a2a` | `secondary` | Sekundäre Elemente |\n| Muted | `#2a2a2a` | `muted` | Gedämpfte Bereiche |\n| Muted Foreground | `#a0a0a0` | `muted-foreground` | Gedämpfter Text |\n| Border | `#3a3a3a` | `border` | Rahmen |\n| Destructive | `#ef4444` | `destructive` | Fehler, Löschen |\n| Success | `#4CBB17` | `success` | Erfolg |\n| Ring | `#FFBF00` | `ring` | Focus-Ring |\n\n## Häufige Probleme\n\n### 1. Hardcoded Hex statt Tailwind-Klasse\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Schlecht - hardcoded\nclassName=\"bg-[#FFBF00] text-black hover:bg-[#E5AC00]\"\nclassName=\"text-[#FFBF00]\"\nclassName=\"border-[#FFBF00]\"\n\n// ✅ Gut - Tailwind-Klassen\nclassName=\"bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90\"\nclassName=\"text-primary\"\nclassName=\"border-primary\"\n```\n\n### 2. Inkonsistente Hover-States\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Verschiedene Hover-Farben\nhover:bg-[#E5AC00]  // manchmal\nhover:bg-[#d4a000]  // manchmal anders\n\n// ✅ Konsistent\nhover:bg-primary/90\n```\n\n### 3. Hardcoded Grautöne\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Hardcoded\nbg-[#1a1a1a]\ntext-[#ededed]\nborder-[#3a3a3a]\n\n// ✅ Semantic\nbg-background\ntext-foreground\nborder-border\n```\n\n## Prüfungs-Workflow\n\n### Schritt 1: Finde hardcoded Farben\n\n```bash\n# Alle Hex-Farben in TSX/TS Dateien\nrg ''#[0-9A-Fa-f]{6}'' --type ts --type tsx -g ''!*.json''\n\n# Spezifisch Primary-Farbe\nrg ''#FFBF00|#ffbf00'' --type ts --type tsx\n\n# Bracket-Notation (Tailwind arbitrary values)\nrg ''\\[#[0-9A-Fa-f]{6}\\]'' --type ts --type tsx\n```\n\n### Schritt 2: Kategorisiere die Funde\n\n| Kategorie | Aktion |\n|-----------|--------|\n| `#FFBF00` in className | → `primary` |\n| `#E5AC00` in hover | → `primary/90` |\n| `#1a1a1a` Background | → `background` |\n| `#ededed` Text | → `foreground` |\n| `#3a3a3a` Border | → `border` |\n| `#ef4444` Error | → `destructive` |\n| `#4CBB17` Success | → `success` |\n| Andere Hex-Werte | → Prüfen ob notwendig |\n\n### Schritt 3: Ausnahmen identifizieren\n\nDiese hardcoded Farben sind **OK**:\n\n1. **EBC/SRM Bierfarben** in `RecipeCard.tsx`:\n   ```tsx\n   // Diese sind dynamisch berechnet!\n   if (srm < 4) return \"#F8F5D4\"; // Pale Straw\n   if (srm < 7) return \"#F3F993\"; // Gold\n   ```\n\n2. **Print Styles** in `RecipeCard.tsx`:\n   ```tsx\n   // Print braucht andere Farben\n   border-bottom: 2px solid #FFBF00;\n   ```\n\n3. **OG Images** in `app/api/og/`:\n   ```tsx\n   // Generierte Bilder, kein Tailwind\n   ```\n\n## Report-Format\n\n```markdown\n## Farbkonsistenz-Prüfung\n\n### 🔴 Kritisch (hardcoded Primary)\n| Datei | Zeile | Aktuell | Vorschlag |\n|-------|-------|---------|-----------|\n| Navbar.tsx | 42 | `bg-[#FFBF00]` | `bg-primary` |\n\n### 🟡 Empfohlen (andere hardcoded)\n| Datei | Zeile | Aktuell | Vorschlag |\n|-------|-------|---------|-----------|\n| Footer.tsx | 15 | `text-[#a0a0a0]` | `text-muted-foreground` |\n\n### ✅ Ausnahmen (OK)\n- RecipeCard.tsx: EBC Farben (dynamisch berechnet)\n- api/og/route.tsx: OG Image Generation\n```\n\n## Bekannte Dateien mit vielen Hardcoded Farben\n\nDiese Dateien haben besonders viele hardcoded Farben:\n\n- `app/cellar/page.tsx` - 13 Stellen\n- `components/RecipeCard.tsx` - 82 Stellen (viele OK wegen Print/EBC)\n- `components/BrewSession.tsx` - 110 Stellen\n- `components/WizardStep2.tsx` - 6 Stellen\n- `components/Navbar.tsx` - 22 Stellen\n\n## Ersetzungs-Regeln\n\n### Button Primary\n```tsx\n// ❌ Vorher\n<Button className=\"bg-[#FFBF00] text-black hover:bg-[#E5AC00]\">\n\n// ✅ Nachher\n<Button className=\"bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90\">\n```\n\n### Text Primary\n```tsx\n// ❌ Vorher\n<span className=\"text-[#FFBF00]\">\n\n// ✅ Nachher\n<span className=\"text-primary\">\n```\n\n### Tab Active State\n```tsx\n// ❌ Vorher\nclassName=\"data-[state=active]:bg-[#FFBF00] data-[state=active]:text-black\"\n\n// ✅ Nachher\nclassName=\"data-[state=active]:bg-primary data-[state=active]:text-primary-foreground\"\n```\n\n### Star/Rating\n```tsx\n// ❌ Vorher\nclassName={rating ? \"text-[#FFBF00] fill-[#FFBF00]\" : \"text-zinc-600\"}\n\n// ✅ Nachher\nclassName={rating ? \"text-primary fill-primary\" : \"text-muted-foreground\"}\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:26:58.435Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing precise color palette management and consistency checks in Tailwind CSS configurations.","zh":"非常适合需要在Tailwind CSS配置中进行精确色彩板管理和一致性检查的前端代理。","ja":"Tailwind CSSの設定で正確なカラーパレット管理と一貫性の確認が必要なフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Tailwind CSS 구성에서 정확한 색상 팔레트 관리 및 일관성 확인이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan un manejo de paleta de colores preciso y comprobaciones de coherencia en configuraciones de Tailwind CSS.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend nécessitant une gestion de palette de couleurs précise et des vérifications de cohérence dans les configurations de Tailwind CSS.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die eine präzise Farbpalettenverwaltung und Konsistenzprüfungen in Tailwind-CSS-Konfigurationen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de gerenciamento de paleta de cores preciso e verificações de consistência em configurações do Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Идеально подходит для фронтенд-агентов, которым требуется точное управление цветовой палитрой и проверки согласованности в конфигурациях Tailwind CSS.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأماميين الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة دقيقة للpalette الألوان والتحقق من الاتساق في إعدادات Tailwind CSS."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce color consistency across web applications using Tailwind classes and hex codes defined in `tailwind.config.ts` and `app/globals.css`, ensuring uniform branding and visual identity.","zh":"赋予代理执行跨Web应用程序的色彩一致性，使用在`tailwind.config.ts`和`app/globals.css`中定义的Tailwind类和十六进制代码，确保统一的品牌和视觉身份。","ja":"`tailwind.config.ts`と`app/globals.css`に定義されたTailwindクラスと16進数コードを使用して、Webアプリケーション全体で色の一貫性を保つことが代理者に可能になり、統一されたブランドと視覚的アイデンティティが保証されます。","ko":"`tailwind.config.ts`와 `app/globals.css`에 정의된 Tailwind 클래스 및 16진수 코드를 사용하여 웹 애플리케이션 전반에서 색상 일관성을 유지할 수 있는 에이전트를赋予하여, 통일된 브랜드 및 시각적 정체성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a hacer cumplir la coherencia de color en aplicaciones web utilizando clases de Tailwind y códigos hex definidos en `tailwind.config.ts` y `app/globals.css`, garantizando una marca y una identidad visual uniformes.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''imposer une cohérence des couleurs dans les applications web en utilisant des classes Tailwind et des codes hex définis dans `tailwind.config.ts` et `app/globals.css`, garantissant une marque et une identité visuelle uniformes.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Farbkonsequenz in Webanwendungen durchzusetzen, indem sie Tailwind-Klassen und Hex-Codes verwenden, die in `tailwind.config.ts` und `app/globals.css` definiert sind, und somit eine einheitliche Marke und visuelle Identität sicherstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor a consistência de cores em aplicativos web usando classes Tailwind e códigos hex definidos em `tailwind.config.ts` e `app/globals.css`, garantindo marcação e identidade visual uniformes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать согласованность цветов на веб-приложениях с использованием классов Tailwind и шестнадцатеричных кодов, определенных в `tailwind.config.ts` и `app/globals.css`, обеспечивая единообразную брендинг и визуальную идентичность.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من فرض الاتساق اللوني في التطبيقات الويب باستخدام فصول Tailwind وأكواد السداسي عشر المحددة في `tailwind.config.ts` و `app/globals.css` ، مما يضمن التسمية والتطابق البصري الموحد."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating hex code usage against the official color scheme","Automating checks for consistent Tailwind class applications","Debugging color inconsistencies in web application UI components"],"zh":["验证十六进制代码的使用是否符合官方颜色方案","自动检查一致的Tailwind类应用","调试Web应用程序UI组件中的颜色不一致"],"ja":["公式のカラースキームに対する16進数コードの使用を検証する","一貫したTailwindクラスの適用を自動的にチェックする","WebアプリケーションのUIコンポーネントにおける色の一貫性をデバッグする"],"ko":["공식 색상 구성표에 대한 16진수 코드 사용을 검증","일관된 Tailwind 클래스 적용을 자동으로 확인","웹 애플리케이션 UI 구성 요소의 색상 불일치를 디버깅"],"es":["Validar el uso de códigos hex contra el esquema de color oficial","Automatizar comprobaciones para aplicaciones consistentes de clases Tailwind","Depurar inconsistencias de color en componentes de la interfaz de usuario de la aplicación web"],"fr":["Valider l''utilisation de codes hex contre le schéma de couleur officiel","Automatiser les vérifications pour des applications cohérentes de classes Tailwind","Déboguer les incohérences de couleur dans les composants de l''interface utilisateur de l''application web"],"de":["Überprüfen der Verwendung von Hex-Codes gegen das offizielle Farbschema","Automatisieren von Prüfungen für konsistente Tailwind-Klassen-Anwendungen","Fehlerbehebung bei Farbinconsistenzen in Benutzeroberflächen-Komponenten von Webanwendungen"],"pt":["Validar o uso de códigos hex contra o esquema de cores oficial","Automatizar verificações para aplicações consistentes de classes Tailwind","Depurar inconsistências de cores em componentes de interface do usuário de aplicativos web"],"ru":["Проверка использования шестнадцатеричных кодов против официальной цветовой схемы","Автоматизация проверок согласованного применения классов Tailwind","Отладка несоответствий цветов в компонентах интерфейса пользователя веб-приложений"],"ar":["التحقق من استخدام أكواد السداسي عشر مقابل مخطط الألوان الرسمي","تأتمتة الفحوصات لتحديد التطبيقات المتناسقة للفصول Tailwind","تصحيح الأخطاء في عدم الاتساق اللوني في مكونات واجهة المستخدم للتطبيقات الويب"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `tailwind.config.ts` and `app/globals.css` files","Limited to Tailwind CSS framework","Dependent on predefined color schema definitions"],"zh":["需要访问`tailwind.config.ts`和`app/globals.css`文件","仅限于Tailwind CSS框架","依赖于预定义的颜色方案定义"],"ja":["`tailwind.config.ts`と`app/globals.css`ファイルへのアクセスが必要","Tailwind CSSフレームワークのみに限定される","事前に定義されたカラースキームの定義に依存する"],"ko":["`tailwind.config.ts`와 `app/globals.css` 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요","Tailwind CSS 프레임워크만으로 제한","사전 정의된 색상 구성표 정의에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a los archivos `tailwind.config.ts` y `app/globals.css`","Limitado al marco de trabajo de Tailwind CSS","Dependiente de definiciones de esquemas de color preestablecidas"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux fichiers `tailwind.config.ts` et `app/globals.css`","Limité au framework Tailwind CSS","Dépendant des définitions de schémas de couleur prédéfinies"],"de":["Erfordert den Zugriff auf die Dateien `tailwind.config.ts` und `app/globals.css`","Begrenzt auf das Tailwind-CSS-Framework","Abhängig von vordefinierten Farbschemadefinitionen"],"pt":["Exige acesso aos arquivos `tailwind.config.ts` e `app/globals.css`","Limitado ao framework Tailwind CSS","Dependente de definições de esquema de cores predefinidas"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлам `tailwind.config.ts` и `app/globals.css`","Ограничен фреймворком Tailwind CSS","Зависит от предопределенных определений цветовой схемы"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الملفات `tailwind.config.ts` و `app/globals.css`","محدود بإطار العمل Tailwind CSS","يعتمد على تعريفات مخطط الألوان المحددة مسبقًا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('langfuse/skills/skill-creator', 'community', 'langfuse', 'skills', 'langfuse/skills', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z', '2026-02-18T13:26:36.493Z', NULL, '{"id":"langfuse/skills/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"技能创建器是一种 AI 代理技能，用于创建有效的技能，提供专业知识和工作流程","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、Langfuse AI エージェントの能力を拡張するためのスキルを作成する AI エージェント スキルです","ko":"스킬 생성기는 Langfuse AI 에이전트의 능력을 확장하는 스킬을 생성하는 AI 에이전트 스킬입니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite crear paquetes modulares y personalizados para Claude","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un outil pour les développeurs qui permet de créer des packages modulaires et personnalisés pour Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeitscreator ist ein Tool für Entwickler, das die Erstellung von modularen und maßgeschneiderten Paketen für Claude ermöglicht","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para a criação de habilidades eficazes, permitindo que os desenvolvedores estendam as capacidades do Claude.","ru":"Skill Creator предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, позволяя разработчикам расширить возможности Claude.","ar":"Skill Creator يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، مما يسمح للمطورين بتوسيع قدرات Claude.","en":"AI agent skills for Langfuse"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"技能创建器 - Langfuse AI 代理技能","ja":"スキルクリエーター - Langfuse AI エージェントスキル","ko":"스킬 생성기 - Langfuse AI 에이전트 스킬","es":"Creador de habilidades para desarrolladores","fr":"Créateur de compétences pour développeurs","de":"Fähigkeitscreator für Entwickler","pt":"Criador de Habilidades para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Создатель Навыков для Разработчиков","ar":"منشئ المهارات للمانحين","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"技能创建器是一种 AI 代理技能，用于创建有效的技能，提供专业知识和工作流程","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、Langfuse AI エージェントの能力を拡張するためのスキルを作成する AI エージェント スキルです","ko":"스킬 생성기는 Langfuse AI 에이전트의 능력을 확장하는 스킬을 생성하는 AI 에이전트 스킬입니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite crear paquetes modulares y personalizados para Claude","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un outil pour les développeurs qui permet de créer des packages modulaires et personnalisés pour Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeitscreator ist ein Tool für Entwickler, das die Erstellung von modularen und maßgeschneiderten Paketen für Claude ermöglicht","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para a criação de habilidades eficazes, permitindo que os desenvolvedores estendam as capacidades do Claude.","ru":"Skill Creator предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, позволяя разработчикам расширить возможности Claude.","ar":"Skill Creator يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، مما يسمح للمطورين بتوسيع قدرات Claude.","en":"AI agent skills for Langfuse"},"definition":{"en":"AI agent skills for Langfuse"},"features":{"zh":["提供专业知识和工作流程","扩展 Langfuse AI 代理的能力","创建有效的技能","支持多种工作流程","提供模块化和自包含的包","增强 Claude 的能力"],"ja":["専門知識とワークフローを提供","Langfuse AI エージェントの能力を拡張","効果的なスキルを作成","複数のワークフローをサポート","モジュラーで自己完結したパッケージを提供","Claude の能力を強化"],"ko":["전문 지식과 워크플로우 제공","Langfuse AI 에이전트의 능력을 확장","효과적인 스킬 생성","다중 워크플로우 지원","모듈화되고 자기 포함된 패키지 제공","Claude 의 능력을 강화"],"es":["Creación de flujos de trabajo personalizados","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude","Paquetes modulares y autocontenidos","Guías de incorporación para dominios específicos","Herramientas especializadas para desarrolladores","Integración con la plataforma Langfuse"],"fr":["Création de flux de travail personnalisés","Étendre les capacités de Claude","Packages modulaires et autocontenus","Guides d''intégration pour des domaines spécifiques","Outils spécialisés pour les développeurs","Intégration avec la plateforme Langfuse"],"de":["Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Workflows","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete","Einbindungsguides für spezifische Domänen","Spezialisierte Tools für Entwickler","Integration mit der Langfuse-Plattform"],"pt":["Habilidades personalizadas","Fluxos de trabalho especializados","Conhecimento procedural","Ferramentas de domínio específico","Guia de início rápido"],"ru":["Пользовательские навыки","Специализированные рабочие процессы","Процедурные знания","Инструменты для конкретных доменов","Гид по быстрому началу"],"ar":["مهارات مخصصة","سير عمل متخصص","معرفة إجرائية","أدوات مجال معينة","دليل البدء السريع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建器","AI 代理技能","Langfuse","专业知识","工作流程","Claude","模块化","自己包含"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","AI エージェント スキル","Langfuse","専門知識","ワークフロー","Claude","モジュラー","自己完結"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","AI 에이전트 스킬","Langfuse","전문 지식","워크플로우","Claude","모듈화","자기 포함"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","Claude","Langfuse","desarrolladores","paquetes modulares","flujos de trabajo personalizados","ampliación de capacidades","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","Claude","Langfuse","développeurs","packages modulaires","flux de travail personnalisés","étendre les capacités","outils de développement"],"de":["Fähigkeitscreator","Fähigkeitsentwicklung","Claude","Langfuse","Entwickler","modulare Pakete","benutzerdefinierte Workflows","Fähigkeitserweiterung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de habilidades","criação de habilidades","Langfuse","Claude","agentes AI","desenvolvedores","navegador de habilidades"],"ru":["разработка навыков","создание навыков","Langfuse","Claude","агенты ИИ","разработчики","навигатор навыков"],"ar":["تطوير المهارات","إنشاء المهارات","Langfuse","Claude","عملاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","المطورون","متصفح المهارات"]}},"owner":"langfuse","repo":"skills","repoPath":"langfuse/skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:26:36.493Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions through modular skills","zh":"非常适合像Claude这样需要专业知识并通过模块化技能扩展工作流程的AI智能体","ja":"Claudeのような専門知識を必要とし、モジュール型スキルを通じてワークフローを拡張するAIエージェントに最適です","ko":"전문 지식과 모듈형 스킬을 통해 워크플로우 확장이 필요한 Claude와 같은 AI 에이전트에 완벽하게 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude que necesitan conocimiento especializado y extensiones de flujo de trabajo mediante habilidades modulares","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude nécessitant des connaissances spécialisées et des extensions de flux de travail via des compétences modulaires","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agenten wie Claude, die spezialisiertes Wissen und Workflow-Erweiterungen durch modulare Skills benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como o Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho através de habilidades modulares","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-агентов, таких как Claude, которым требуется специализированные знания и расширения рабочих процессов через модульные навыки","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude الذين يحتاجون إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيع سير العمل من خلال المهارات المعيارية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, providing specialized workflows, and tools, utilizing modular self-contained packages that extend capabilities","zh":"使智能体能够转变为具备程序性知识的专业实体，通过模块化独立功能包扩展能力，提供专业化工作流程和工具","ja":"手続き型知識を備えた専門エンティティへとエージェントを変革し、機能を拡張するモジュール型の自己完結型パッケージを利用して、専門的なワークフローとツールを提供します","ko":"모듈형 독립 패키지를 활용하여 능력을 확장하고 전문 워크플로우와 도구를 제공하며, 절차적 지식을 갖춘 전문 엔티티로 에이전트를 변환할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes transformarse en entidades especializadas equipadas con conocimiento procedimental, proporcionando flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, utilizando paquetes modulares autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en entités spécialisées équipées de connaissances procédurales, fournissant des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, utilisant des packages modulaires autonomes qui étendent les capacités","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Einheiten zu verwandeln, die mit prozeduralem Wissen ausgestattet sind, spezialisierte Workflows und Werkzeuge bereitstellen und modulare, eigenständige Pakete nutzen, die die Fähigkeiten erweitern","pt":"Capacita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento processual, fornecendo fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas especializadas, utilizando pacotes modulares autônomos que estendem as capacidades","ru":"Позволяет агентам превращаться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, предоставляя специализированные рабочие процессы и инструменты, используя модульные автономные пакеты, расширяющие возможности","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من التحول إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بمعرفة إجرائية، وتوفير سير عمل وأدوات متخصصة، باستخدام حزم معيارية مستقلة قائمة بذاتها توسع القدرات"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating modular skills for domain-specific tasks","Extending agent capabilities with specialized knowledge","Developing procedural onboarding guides for unique workflows"],"zh":["为特定领域任务创建模块化技能","使用专业知识扩展智能体能力","为独特工作流程开发程序性入门指南"],"ja":["ドメイン固有タスクのためのモジュール型スキルの作成","専門知識によるエージェント機能の拡張","独自のワークフローのための手続き型オンボーディングガイドの開発"],"ko":["도메인 특화 작업을 위한 모듈형 스킬 생성","전문 지식으로 에이전트 능력 확장","고유한 워크플로우를 위한 절차적 온보딩 가이드 개발"],"es":["Creación de habilidades modulares para tareas específicas de dominio","Extensión de las capacidades del agente con conocimiento especializado","Desarrollo de guías de incorporación procedimentales para flujos de trabajo únicos"],"fr":["Création de compétences modulaires pour des tâches spécifiques à un domaine","Extension des capacités des agents avec des connaissances spécialisées","Développement de guides d''intégration procéduraux pour des flux de travail uniques"],"de":["Erstellung modularer Skills für domänenspezifische Aufgaben","Erweiterung der Agenten-Fähigkeiten mit spezialisiertem Wissen","Entwicklung prozeduraler Onboarding-Leitfäden für einzigartige Workflows"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades modulares para tarefas específicas de domínio","Extensão das capacidades do agente com conhecimento especializado","Desenvolvimento de guias de integração processual para fluxos de trabalho únicos"],"ru":["Создание модульных навыков для задач конкретной предметной области","Расширение возможностей агента со специализированными знаниями","Разработка процедурных руководств по адаптации для уникальных рабочих процессов"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات معيارية لمهام محددة في المجال","توسيع قدرات الوكيل بمعرفة متخصصة","تطوير أدلات إرشادية إجرائية لسير العمل الفريدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Langfuse compatibility","Specialized knowledge for specific domains or tasks required"],"zh":["需要与Langfuse兼容","需要特定领域或任务的专业知识"],"ja":["Langfuseとの互換性が必要","特定ドメインまたはタスクに対する専門知識が必要"],"ko":["Langfuse 호환성 필요","특정 도메인 또는 작업에 대한 전문 지식 필요"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con Langfuse","Se requiere conocimiento especializado para dominios o tareas específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compatibilité Langfuse","Connaissances spécialisées pour des domaines ou tâches spécifiques requises"],"de":["Erfor