 erreurs de formule, en conservant les formats et les styles existants","de":"Der xlsx-Skill stellt die Erstellung von Excel-Dateien ohne Formelfehler sicher, wobei bestehende Formate und Stile erhalten bleiben","pt":"O xlsx é um conjunto de diretrizes para criar arquivos Excel perfeitos, sem erros de fórmula e preservando os modelos existentes","ru":"xlsx - это набор руководств для создания идеальных Excel-файлов, без ошибок формул и с сохранением существующих шаблонов","ar":"xlsx هو مجموعة من الإرشادات لإنشاء ملفات إكسل مثالية، بدون أخطاء في الصيغ وحفظ القوالب الحالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["零公式错误","保留现有模板","金融模型色彩编码","确保文件格式和样式的一致性","支持多种 Excel 文件类型"],"ja":["零フォーミュラエラー","既存テンプレートの保存","金融モデル色コード","ファイル形式とスタイルの一貫性の確保","複数の Excel ファイル形式のサポート"],"ko":["0개의 수식 오류","기존 템플릿 유지","금융 모델 색상 코드","파일 형식과 스타일의 일관성 보장","다양한 Excel 파일 형식 지원"],"es":["Cero errores de fórmula","Conservación de formatos existentes","Compatibilidad con modelos financieros","Color coding para una mejor visualización","Preservación de estilos y convenciones existentes"],"fr":["Pas d''erreurs de formule","Conservation des formats existants","Compatibilité avec les modèles financiers","Color coding pour une meilleure visualisation","Préservation des styles et des conventions existants"],"de":["Keine Formelfehler","Bewahrung bestehender Formate","Kompatibilität mit Finanzmodellen","Farbcodierung für eine bessere Visualisierung","Bewahrung bestehender Stile und Konventionen"],"pt":["Sem erros de fórmula","Preservação de modelos existentes","Coloração de células","Manutenção de convenções de formatação","Suporte a modelos financeiros","Compatibilidade com arquivos Excel"],"ru":["Без ошибок формул","Сохранение существующих шаблонов","Цветовая кодировка ячеек","Сохранение конвенций форматирования","Поддержка финансовых моделей","Совместимость с Excel-файлами"],"ar":["بدون أخطاء في الصيغ","الحفاظ على القوالب الحالية","التلوين الخلوي","الحفاظ على اتفاقيات التنسيق","دعم النماذج المالية","التوافق مع ملفات إكسل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["xlsx 技术规范","Excel 文件质量","零公式错误","保留现有模板","金融模型","色彩编码","文件格式一致性"],"ja":["xlsx 技術仕様","Excel ファイル品質","零フォーミュラエラー","既存テンプレートの保存","金融モデル","色コード","ファイル形式の一貫性"],"ko":["xlsx 기술 사양","Excel 파일 품질","0개의 수식 오류","기존 템플릿 유지","금융 모델","색상 코드","파일 형식 일관성"],"es":["xlsx","archivos Excel","errores de fórmula","modelos financieros","color coding","formatos existentes","estilos y convenciones"],"fr":["xlsx","fichiers Excel","erreurs de formule","modèles financiers","color coding","formats existants","styles et conventions"],"de":["xlsx","Excel-Dateien","Formelfehler","Finanzmodelle","Farbcodierung","bestehende Formate","Stile und Konventionen"],"pt":["xlsx","arquivos excel","erros de fórmula","modelos financeiros","coloração de células","preservação de modelos","desenvolvimento de excel","otimização de excel","criação de arquivos excel"],"ru":["xlsx","Excel-файлы","ошибки формул","финансовые модели","цветовая кодировка ячеек","сохранение шаблонов","разработка Excel","оптимизация Excel","создание Excel-файлов"],"ar":["xlsx","ملفات إكسل","أخطاء الصيغ","النماذج المالية","التلوين الخلوي","الحفاظ على القوالب","تنمية إكسل","تحسين إكسل","إنشاء ملفات إكسل"]}},"owner":"sudat","repo":"req-manager","repoPath":"sudat/req-manager","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"xlsx","description":"Comprehensive spreadsheet creation, editing, and analysis with support for formulas, formatting, data analysis, and visualization. When Claude needs to work with spreadsheets (.xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, .tsv, etc) for: (1) Creating new spreadsheets with formulas and formatting, (2) Reading or analyzing data, (3) Modify existing spreadsheets while preserving formulas, (4) Data analysis and visualization in spreadsheets, or (5) Recalculating formulas","bodyPreview":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding S","body":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding Standards\nUnless otherwise stated by the user or existing template\n\n#### Industry-Standard Color Conventions\n- **Blue text (RGB: 0,0,255)**: Hardcoded inputs, and numbers users will change for scenarios\n- **Black text (RGB: 0,0,0)**: ALL formulas and calculations\n- **Green text (RGB: 0,128,0)**: Links pulling from other worksheets within same workbook\n- **Red text (RGB: 255,0,0)**: External links to other files\n- **Yellow background (RGB: 255,255,0)**: Key assumptions needing attention or cells that need to be updated\n\n### Number Formatting Standards\n\n#### Required Format Rules\n- **Years**: Format as text strings (e.g., \"2024\" not \"2,024\")\n- **Currency**: Use $#,##0 format; ALWAYS specify units in headers (\"Revenue ($mm)\")\n- **Zeros**: Use number formatting to make all zeros \"-\", including percentages (e.g., \"$#,##0;($#,##0);-\")\n- **Percentages**: Default to 0.0% format (one decimal)\n- **Multiples**: Format as 0.0x for valuation multiples (EV/EBITDA, P/E)\n- **Negative numbers**: Use parentheses (123) not minus -123\n\n### Formula Construction Rules\n\n#### Assumptions Placement\n- Place ALL assumptions (growth rates, margins, multiples, etc.) in separate assumption cells\n- Use cell references instead of hardcoded values in formulas\n- Example: Use =B5*(1+$B$6) instead of =B5*1.05\n\n#### Formula Error Prevention\n- Verify all cell references are correct\n- Check for off-by-one errors in ranges\n- Ensure consistent formulas across all projection periods\n- Test with edge cases (zero values, negative numbers)\n- Verify no unintended circular references\n\n#### Documentation Requirements for Hardcodes\n- Comment or in cells beside (if end of table). Format: \"Source: [System/Document], [Date], [Specific Reference], [URL if applicable]\"\n- Examples:\n  - \"Source: Company 10-K, FY2024, Page 45, Revenue Note, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Company 10-Q, Q2 2025, Exhibit 99.1, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Bloomberg Terminal, 8/15/2025, AAPL US Equity\"\n  - \"Source: FactSet, 8/20/2025, Consensus Estimates Screen\"\n\n# XLSX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA user may ask you to create, edit, or analyze the contents of an .xlsx file. You have different tools and workflows available for different tasks.\n\n## Important Requirements\n\n**LibreOffice Required for Formula Recalculation**: You can assume LibreOffice is installed for recalculating formula values using the `recalc.py` script. The script automatically configures LibreOffice on first run\n\n## Reading and analyzing data\n\n### Data analysis with pandas\nFor data analysis, visualization, and basic operations, use **pandas** which provides powerful data manipulation capabilities:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read Excel\ndf = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'')  # Default: first sheet\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', sheet_name=None)  # All sheets as dict\n\n# Analyze\ndf.head()      # Preview data\ndf.info()      # Column info\ndf.describe()  # Statistics\n\n# Write Excel\ndf.to_excel(''output.xlsx'', index=False)\n```\n\n## Excel File Workflows\n\n## CRITICAL: Use Formulas, Not Hardcoded Values\n\n**Always use Excel formulas instead of calculating values in Python and hardcoding them.** This ensures the spreadsheet remains dynamic and updateable.\n\n### ❌ WRONG - Hardcoding Calculated Values\n```python\n# Bad: Calculating in Python and hardcoding result\ntotal = df[''Sales''].sum()\nsheet[''B10''] = total  # Hardcodes 5000\n\n# Bad: Computing growth rate in Python\ngrowth = (df.iloc[-1][''Revenue''] - df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']) / df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']\nsheet[''C5''] = growth  # Hardcodes 0.15\n\n# Bad: Python calculation for average\navg = sum(values) / len(values)\nsheet[''D20''] = avg  # Hardcodes 42.5\n```\n\n### ✅ CORRECT - Using Excel Formulas\n```python\n# Good: Let Excel calculate the sum\nsheet[''B10''] = ''=SUM(B2:B9)''\n\n# Good: Growth rate as Excel formula\nsheet[''C5''] = ''=(C4-C2)/C2''\n\n# Good: Average using Excel function\nsheet[''D20''] = ''=AVERAGE(D2:D19)''\n```\n\nThis applies to ALL calculations - totals, percentages, ratios, differences, etc. The spreadsheet should be able to recalculate when source data changes.\n\n## Common Workflow\n1. **Choose tool**: pandas for data, openpyxl for formulas/formatting\n2. **Create/Load**: Create new workbook or load existing file\n3. **Modify**: Add/edit data, formulas, and formatting\n4. **Save**: Write to file\n5. **Recalculate formulas (MANDATORY IF USING FORMULAS)**: Use the recalc.py script\n   ```bash\n   python recalc.py output.xlsx\n   ```\n6. **Verify and fix any errors**: \n   - The script returns JSON with error details\n   - If `status` is `errors_found`, check `error_summary` for specific error types and locations\n   - Fix the identified errors and recalculate again\n   - Common errors to fix:\n     - `#REF!`: Invalid cell references\n     - `#DIV/0!`: Division by zero\n     - `#VALUE!`: Wrong data type in formula\n     - `#NAME?`: Unrecognized formula name\n\n### Creating new Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl for formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, PatternFill, Alignment\n\nwb = Workbook()\nsheet = wb.active\n\n# Add data\nsheet[''A1''] = ''Hello''\nsheet[''B1''] = ''World''\nsheet.append([''Row'', ''of'', ''data''])\n\n# Add formula\nsheet[''B2''] = ''=SUM(A1:A10)''\n\n# Formatting\nsheet[''A1''].font = Font(bold=True, color=''FF0000'')\nsheet[''A1''].fill = PatternFill(''solid'', start_color=''FFFF00'')\nsheet[''A1''].alignment = Alignment(horizontal=''center'')\n\n# Column width\nsheet.column_dimensions[''A''].width = 20\n\nwb.save(''output.xlsx'')\n```\n\n### Editing existing Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl to preserve formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\n\n# Load existing file\nwb = load_workbook(''existing.xlsx'')\nsheet = wb.active  # or wb[''SheetName''] for specific sheet\n\n# Working with multiple sheets\nfor sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n    sheet = wb[sheet_name]\n    print(f\"Sheet: {sheet_name}\")\n\n# Modify cells\nsheet[''A1''] = ''New Value''\nsheet.insert_rows(2)  # Insert row at position 2\nsheet.delete_cols(3)  # Delete column 3\n\n# Add new sheet\nnew_sheet = wb.create_sheet(''NewSheet'')\nnew_sheet[''A1''] = ''Data''\n\nwb.save(''modified.xlsx'')\n```\n\n## Recalculating formulas\n\nExcel files created or modified by openpyxl contain formulas as strings but not calculated values. Use the provided `recalc.py` script to recalculate formulas:\n\n```bash\npython recalc.py <excel_file> [timeout_seconds]\n```\n\nExample:\n```bash\npython recalc.py output.xlsx 30\n```\n\nThe script:\n- Automatically sets up LibreOffice macro on first run\n- Recalculates all formulas in all sheets\n- Scans ALL cells for Excel errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, etc.)\n- Returns JSON with detailed error locations and counts\n- Works on both Linux and macOS\n\n## Formula Verification Checklist\n\nQuick checks to ensure formulas work correctly:\n\n### Essential Verification\n- [ ] **Test 2-3 sample references**: Verify they pull correct values before building full model\n- [ ] **Column mapping**: Confirm Excel columns match (e.g., column 64 = BL, not BK)\n- [ ] **Row offset**: Remember Excel rows are 1-indexed (DataFrame row 5 = Excel row 6)\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n- [ ] **NaN handling**: Check for null values with `pd.notna()`\n- [ ] **Far-right columns**: FY data often in columns 50+ \n- [ ] **Multiple matches**: Search all occurrences, not just first\n- [ ] **Division by zero**: Check denominators before using `/` in formulas (#DIV/0!)\n- [ ] **Wrong references**: Verify all cell references point to intended cells (#REF!)\n- [ ] **Cross-sheet references**: Use correct format (Sheet1!A1) for linking sheets\n\n### Formula Testing Strategy\n- [ ] **Start small**: Test formulas on 2-3 cells before applying broadly\n- [ ] **Verify dependencies**: Check all cells referenced in formulas exist\n- [ ] **Test edge cases**: Include zero, negative, and very large values\n\n### Interpreting recalc.py Output\nThe script returns JSON with error details:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",           // or \"errors_found\"\n  \"total_errors\": 0,              // Total error count\n  \"total_formulas\": 42,           // Number of formulas in file\n  \"error_summary\": {              // Only present if errors found\n    \"#REF!\": {\n      \"count\": 2,\n      \"locations\": [\"Sheet1!B5\", \"Sheet1!C10\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Library Selection\n- **pandas**: Best for data analysis, bulk operations, and simple data export\n- **openpyxl**: Best for complex formatting, formulas, and Excel-specific features\n\n### Working with openpyxl\n- Cell indices are 1-based (row=1, column=1 refers to cell A1)\n- Use `data_only=True` to read calculated values: `load_workbook(''file.xlsx'', data_only=True)`\n- **Warning**: If opened with `data_only=True` and saved, formulas are replaced with values and permanently lost\n- For large files: Use `read_only=True` for reading or `write_only=True` for writing\n- Formulas are preserved but not evaluated - use recalc.py to update values\n\n### Working with pandas\n- Specify data types to avoid inference issues: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', dtype={''id'': str})`\n- For large files, read specific columns: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', usecols=[''A'', ''C'', ''E''])`\n- Handle dates properly: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', parse_dates=[''date_column''])`\n\n## Code Style Guidelines\n**IMPORTANT**: When generating Python code for Excel operations:\n- Write minimal, concise Python code without unnecessary comments\n- Avoid verbose variable names and redundant operations\n- Avoid unnecessary print statements\n\n**For Excel files themselves**:\n- Add comments to cells with complex formulas or important assumptions\n- Document data sources for hardcoded values\n- Include notes for key calculations and model sections"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:28:00.130Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Data Analysis Agents requiring precise Excel file manipulation and formula error handling.","zh":"适合需要精确Excel文件操作和公式错误处理的数据分析代理。","ja":"正確なExcelファイル操作と式のエラーハンドリングを必要とするデータ分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"정확한 Excel 파일 조작 및 수식 오류 처리가 필요한 데이터 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de datos que requieren una manipulación precisa de archivos de Excel y un manejo de errores de fórmulas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de données nécessitant une manipulation précise de fichiers Excel et une gestion d''erreurs de formules.","de":"Ideal für Data-Analytics-Agents, die eine präzise Excel-Dateimanipulation und eine Formel-Fehlerbehandlung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Dados que exigem manipulação precisa de arquivos do Excel e tratamento de erros de fórmulas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, требующих точной манипуляции файлами Excel и обработки ошибок формул.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء تحليل البيانات التي تتطلب التعامل الدقيق مع ملفات إكسل ومعالجة أخطاء الصيغ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate and modify Excel files with zero formula errors, preserving existing templates and conventions, and utilizing specific formatting and color coding protocols like color coding for financial models.","zh":"赋予代理生成和修改Excel文件的能力，确保零公式错误，保留现有的模板和约定，并利用特定的格式和颜色编码协议，如金融模型的颜色编码。","ja":"エージェントがゼロの式エラーでExcelファイルを生成および変更できるようにし、既存のテンプレートと規約を保持し、特定のフォーマットと色コードプロトコル（例：財務モデル用の色コード）を利用できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 영 수식 오류로 Excel 파일을 생성 및 수정할 수 있도록 하며, 기존 템플릿 및 규칙을 유지하고, 특정 형식 및 색상 코드 프로토콜(예: 재무 모델을 위한 색상 코드)을 활용할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes generar y modificar archivos de Excel con cero errores de fórmulas, preservando plantillas y convenciones existentes, y utilizando protocolos de formato y codificación de colores específicos como la codificación de colores para modelos financieros.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer et de modifier des fichiers Excel avec zéro erreur de formules, en préservant les modèles et les conventions existants, et en utilisant des protocoles de formatage et de codage de couleurs spécifiques comme la codification des couleurs pour les modèles financiers.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Excel-Dateien mit null Formelfehlern zu generieren und zu modifizieren, wobei bestehende Vorlagen und Konventionen erhalten bleiben und spezifische Formattierungs- und Farbcodierungsprotokolle wie Farbcodierung für Finanzmodelle verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita agentes a gerar e modificar arquivos do Excel com zero erros de fórmulas, preservando modelos e convenções existentes, e utilizando protocolos de formatação e codificação de cores específicos, como codificação de cores para modelos financeiros.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать и изменять файлы Excel с нулевым количеством ошибок формул, сохраняя существующие шаблоны и соглашения, и используя конкретные форматы и протоколы кодирования цвета, такие как кодирование цвета для финансовых моделей.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء و تعديل ملفات إكسل مع عدم وجود أخطاء في الصيغ، والحفاظ على القوالب والتقاليد الموجودة، واستخدام بروتوكولات تنسيق وترميز الألوان المحددة، مثل ترميز الألوان لنماذج مالية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Excel file updates with exact format matching","Debugging formula errors in complex Excel models","Generating financial reports with precise color coding"],"zh":["自动执行Excel文件更新以匹配确切格式","调试复杂Excel模型中的公式错误","生成具有精确颜色编码的财务报告"],"ja":["正確なフォーマットを一致させるためのExcelファイルの自動更新","複雑なExcelモデルの式エラーのデバッグ","正確な色コードを使用した財務報告書の生成"],"ko":["정确한 형식을 일치시키기 위한 Excel 파일 자동 업데이트","복잡한 Excel 모델의 수식 오류 디버깅","정확한 색상 코드를 사용한 재무 보고서 생성"],"es":["Automatizar actualizaciones de archivos de Excel con coincidencia de formato exacta","Depurar errores de fórmulas en modelos de Excel complejos","Generar informes financieros con codificación de colores precisa"],"fr":["Automatiser les mises à jour de fichiers Excel avec une correspondance de format exacte","Déboguer les erreurs de formules dans les modèles Excel complexes","Générer des rapports financiers avec une codification des couleurs précise"],"de":["Automatisieren von Excel-Datei-Aktualisierungen mit exakter Formatübereinstimmung","Fehlerbehebung in komplexen Excel-Modellen","Generieren von Finanzberichten mit präziser Farbcodierung"],"pt":["Automatizar atualizações de arquivos do Excel com correspondência de formato exata","Depurar erros de fórmulas em modelos do Excel complexos","Gerar relatórios financeiros com codificação de cores precisa"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обновления файлов Excel с точным совпадением формата","Отладить ошибки формул в сложных моделях Excel","Генерировать финансовые отчеты с точным кодированием цвета"],"ar":["أتمتة تحديث ملفات إكسل مع مطابقة تنسيق دقيقة","تصحيح أخطاء الصيغ في نماذج إكسل معقدة","إنشاء تقارير مالية مع ترميز ألوان دقيق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires exact template matching and preservation","Must handle formula errors like #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","Limited to Excel file format (.xlsx)"],"zh":["需要确切的模板匹配和保留","必须处理公式错误，如#REF！、#DIV/0！、#VALUE！、#N/A、#NAME？","仅限于Excel文件格式(.xlsx)"],"ja":["正確なテンプレートのマッチングと保存が必要","#REF！、#DIV/0！、#VALUE！、#N/A、#NAME？などの式エラーを処理する必要がある","Excelファイル形式(.xlsx)のみに限定"],"ko":["정확한 템플릿 일치 및 보존이 필요","#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME? 등의 수식 오류를 처리해야 함","Excel 파일 형식(.xlsx)만 해당"],"es":["Requiere una coincidencia y preservación de plantillas exactas","Debe manejar errores de fórmulas como #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","Limitado al formato de archivo de Excel (.xlsx)"],"fr":["Nécessite une correspondance et une préservation de modèles exacts","Doit gérer les erreurs de formules comme #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","Limité au format de fichier Excel (.xlsx)"],"de":["Benötigt eine exakte Vorlagenübereinstimmung und -erhaltung","Muss Formelfehler wie #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME? handhaben","Beschränkt auf Excel-Dateiformat (.xlsx)"],"pt":["Exige correspondência de modelo exata e preservação","Deve lidar com erros de fórmulas como #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","Limitado ao formato de arquivo do Excel (.xlsx)"],"ru":["Требует точного соответствия шаблона и сохранения","Должен обрабатывать ошибки формул, такие как #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","Ограничен форматом файла Excel (.xlsx)"],"ar":["يتطلب مطابقة قالب دقيقة والحفاظ عليها","يجب التعامل مع أخطاء الصيغ مثل #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?","محدود بتنسيق ملف إكسل (.xlsx)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
