 de melhores práticas da Vercel para React e Next.js oferece 57 regras para otimizar o desempenho.","ru":"Руководство по лучшим практикам Vercel для React и Next.js содержит 57 правил для оптимизации производительности.","ar":"دليل أفضل الممارسات لفيرسل لرياكت ونكست.جس يوفر 57 قاعدة لتحسين الأداء.","en":"Taxes"},"definition":{"en":"Taxes"},"features":{"zh":["57","8","React","Next.js","",""],"ja":["57","8","React","Next.js","",""],"ko":["57","8","React","Next.js","",""],"es":["57 reglas para optimizar el rendimiento","8 categorías para una mejor organización","Guía para la refactorización automática","Optimización de la carga de datos","Mejora del rendimiento de las aplicaciones React y Next.js"],"fr":["57 règles pour optimiser les performances","8 catégories pour une meilleure organisation","Guide pour la refactoring automatisée","Optimisation du chargement des données","Amélioration des performances des applications React et Next.js"],"de":["57 Regeln zur Leistungsoptimierung","8 Kategorien für eine bessere Organisation","Leitfaden für die automatisierte Refactoring","Optimierung der Datenladung","Verbesserung der Leistung von React- und Next.js-Anwendungen"],"pt":["57 regras para otimizar o desempenho","8 categorias para priorizar o impacto","Guia para refatoração automática e geração de código","Otimização para React e Next.js","Melhoria do desempenho da aplicação"],"ru":["57 правил для оптимизации производительности","8 категорий для приоритизации влияния","Руководство для автоматической рефакторинга и генерации кода","Оптимизация для React и Next.js","Повышение производительности приложения"],"ar":["57 قاعدة لتحسين الأداء","8 فئات لتحديد الأولوية للتأثير","دليل لإعادة هيكلة التطبيق وتوليد الشفرة","تحسين أداء رياكت ونكست.جس","تحسين أداء التطبيق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Vercel React","React","Next.js","","React","Next.js"],"ja":["Vercel React","React","Next.js","","React","Next.js"],"ko":["Vercel React","React","Next.js","","React","Next.js"],"es":["Vercel React","mejores prácticas","optimización de rendimiento","React","Next.js","desarrollo web","rendimiento de aplicaciones"],"fr":["Vercel React","meilleures pratiques","optimisation des performances","React","Next.js","développement web","performances des applications"],"de":["Vercel React","Best Practices","Leistungsoptimierung","React","Next.js","Webentwicklung","Anwendungsleistung"],"pt":["Vercel React","Melhores práticas React","Otimização de desempenho React","Next.js","Desenvolvimento web","React performance optimization"],"ru":["Vercel React","Лучшие практики React","Оптимизация производительности React","Next.js","Веб-разработка","React производительность оптимизация"],"ar":["فيرسل رياكت","أفضل الممارسات لرياكت","تحسين أداء رياكت","نكست.جس","تطوير الويب","تحسين أداء رياكت"]}},"owner":"IdkwhatImD0ing","repo":"Taxes","repoPath":"IdkwhatImD0ing/Taxes","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vercel-react-best-practices","description":"React and Next.js performance optimization guidelines from Vercel Engineering. This skill should be used when writing, reviewing, or refactoring React/Next.js code to ensure optimal performance patterns. Triggers on tasks involving React components, Next.js pages, data fetching, bundle optimization, or performance improvements.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Vercel React Best Practices\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for React and Next.js applications, maintained by Vercel. Contains 57 rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated refactoring and code generation.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n- Writing new React components or Next.js pages\n- Implementing data fetching (client or server-side)\n- Reviewing code for performance issues\n- Refactoring existing React/Next.js code\n- Optimizing bundl","body":"# Vercel React Best Practices\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for React and Next.js applications, maintained by Vercel. Contains 57 rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated refactoring and code generation.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n- Writing new React components or Next.js pages\n- Implementing data fetching (client or server-side)\n- Reviewing code for performance issues\n- Refactoring existing React/Next.js code\n- Optimizing bundle size or load times\n\n## Rule Categories by Priority\n\n| Priority | Category | Impact | Prefix |\n|----------|----------|--------|--------|\n| 1 | Eliminating Waterfalls | CRITICAL | `async-` |\n| 2 | Bundle Size Optimization | CRITICAL | `bundle-` |\n| 3 | Server-Side Performance | HIGH | `server-` |\n| 4 | Client-Side Data Fetching | MEDIUM-HIGH | `client-` |\n| 5 | Re-render Optimization | MEDIUM | `rerender-` |\n| 6 | Rendering Performance | MEDIUM | `rendering-` |\n| 7 | JavaScript Performance | LOW-MEDIUM | `js-` |\n| 8 | Advanced Patterns | LOW | `advanced-` |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### 1. Eliminating Waterfalls (CRITICAL)\n\n- `async-defer-await` - Move await into branches where actually used\n- `async-parallel` - Use Promise.all() for independent operations\n- `async-dependencies` - Use better-all for partial dependencies\n- `async-api-routes` - Start promises early, await late in API routes\n- `async-suspense-boundaries` - Use Suspense to stream content\n\n### 2. Bundle Size Optimization (CRITICAL)\n\n- `bundle-barrel-imports` - Import directly, avoid barrel files\n- `bundle-dynamic-imports` - Use next/dynamic for heavy components\n- `bundle-defer-third-party` - Load analytics/logging after hydration\n- `bundle-conditional` - Load modules only when feature is activated\n- `bundle-preload` - Preload on hover/focus for perceived speed\n\n### 3. Server-Side Performance (HIGH)\n\n- `server-auth-actions` - Authenticate server actions like API routes\n- `server-cache-react` - Use React.cache() for per-request deduplication\n- `server-cache-lru` - Use LRU cache for cross-request caching\n- `server-dedup-props` - Avoid duplicate serialization in RSC props\n- `server-serialization` - Minimize data passed to client components\n- `server-parallel-fetching` - Restructure components to parallelize fetches\n- `server-after-nonblocking` - Use after() for non-blocking operations\n\n### 4. Client-Side Data Fetching (MEDIUM-HIGH)\n\n- `client-swr-dedup` - Use SWR for automatic request deduplication\n- `client-event-listeners` - Deduplicate global event listeners\n- `client-passive-event-listeners` - Use passive listeners for scroll\n- `client-localstorage-schema` - Version and minimize localStorage data\n\n### 5. Re-render Optimization (MEDIUM)\n\n- `rerender-defer-reads` - Don''t subscribe to state only used in callbacks\n- `rerender-memo` - Extract expensive work into memoized components\n- `rerender-memo-with-default-value` - Hoist default non-primitive props\n- `rerender-dependencies` - Use primitive dependencies in effects\n- `rerender-derived-state` - Subscribe to derived booleans, not raw values\n- `rerender-derived-state-no-effect` - Derive state during render, not effects\n- `rerender-functional-setstate` - Use functional setState for stable callbacks\n- `rerender-lazy-state-init` - Pass function to useState for expensive values\n- `rerender-simple-expression-in-memo` - Avoid memo for simple primitives\n- `rerender-move-effect-to-event` - Put interaction logic in event handlers\n- `rerender-transitions` - Use startTransition for non-urgent updates\n- `rerender-use-ref-transient-values` - Use refs for transient frequent values\n\n### 6. Rendering Performance (MEDIUM)\n\n- `rendering-animate-svg-wrapper` - Animate div wrapper, not SVG element\n- `rendering-content-visibility` - Use content-visibility for long lists\n- `rendering-hoist-jsx` - Extract static JSX outside components\n- `rendering-svg-precision` - Reduce SVG coordinate precision\n- `rendering-hydration-no-flicker` - Use inline script for client-only data\n- `rendering-hydration-suppress-warning` - Suppress expected mismatches\n- `rendering-activity` - Use Activity component for show/hide\n- `rendering-conditional-render` - Use ternary, not && for conditionals\n- `rendering-usetransition-loading` - Prefer useTransition for loading state\n\n### 7. JavaScript Performance (LOW-MEDIUM)\n\n- `js-batch-dom-css` - Group CSS changes via classes or cssText\n- `js-index-maps` - Build Map for repeated lookups\n- `js-cache-property-access` - Cache object properties in loops\n- `js-cache-function-results` - Cache function results in module-level Map\n- `js-cache-storage` - Cache localStorage/sessionStorage reads\n- `js-combine-iterations` - Combine multiple filter/map into one loop\n- `js-length-check-first` - Check array length before expensive comparison\n- `js-early-exit` - Return early from functions\n- `js-hoist-regexp` - Hoist RegExp creation outside loops\n- `js-min-max-loop` - Use loop for min/max instead of sort\n- `js-set-map-lookups` - Use Set/Map for O(1) lookups\n- `js-tosorted-immutable` - Use toSorted() for immutability\n\n### 8. Advanced Patterns (LOW)\n\n- `advanced-event-handler-refs` - Store event handlers in refs\n- `advanced-init-once` - Initialize app once per app load\n- `advanced-use-latest` - useLatest for stable callback refs\n\n## How to Use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and code examples:\n\n```\nrules/async-parallel.md\nrules/bundle-barrel-imports.md\n```\n\nEach rule file contains:\n- Brief explanation of why it matters\n- Incorrect code example with explanation\n- Correct code example with explanation\n- Additional context and references\n\n## Full Compiled Document\n\nFor the complete guide with all rules expanded: `AGENTS.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:27:28.691Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents specializing in React and Next.js applications needing automated performance optimization and code refactoring.","zh":"非常适合专门从事 React 和 Next.js 应用程序的前端代理，需要自动性能优化和代码重构。","ja":"React と Next.js アプリケーションに自動パフォーマンス最適化とコードリファクタリングが必要なフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。","ko":"React 및 Next.js 애플리케이션에 자동 성능 최적화 및 코드 리팩터링이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de frontend especializados en aplicaciones React y Next.js que necesitan optimización automática del rendimiento y refactorización de código.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de frontend spécialisés dans les applications React et Next.js nécessitant une optimisation automatique des performances et une refactoring de code.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die auf React- und Next.js-Anwendungen spezialisiert sind und eine automatisierte Leistungsoptimierung und Code-Refactoring benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend especializados em aplicações React e Next.js que necessitam de otimização de desempenho automática e refatoração de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, специализирующихся на приложениях React и Next.js, требующих автоматической оптимизации производительности и рефакторинга кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية المتخصص في تطبيقات React و Next.js التي تحتاج إلى تحسين أداء تلقائي وإعادة هيكلة الكود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement 57 prioritized rules across 8 categories for React and Next.js, streamlining automated refactoring, code generation, and performance optimization, leveraging Vercel''s comprehensive guidelines for client and server-side data fetching and bundling.","zh":"赋予代理实现 57 个优先规则，跨越 8 个类别，用于 React 和 Next.js，简化自动重构、代码生成和性能优化，利用 Vercel 的客户端和服务器端数据获取和打包的全面指南。","ja":"エージェントが 57 の優先ルールを実装できるようにし、React と Next.js にわたる 8 つのカテゴリで自動リファクタリング、コード生成、パフォーマンス最適化を簡素化し、Vercel のクライアントサイドとサーバーサイドのデータ取得とバンドルのための包括的なガイドラインを活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 57개의 우선 규칙을 구현할 수 있도록 하여 React 및 Next.js에 걸쳐 8개의 카테고리에서 자동 리팩터링, 코드 생성 및 성능 최적화를 단순화하며 Vercel의 클라이언트 측 및 서버 측 데이터 가져오기 및 번들링을 위한 포괄적인 가이드라인을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar 57 reglas priorizadas en 8 categorías para React y Next.js, simplificando la refactorización automatizada, la generación de código y la optimización del rendimiento, aprovechando las directrices completas de Vercel para la recuperación y empaquetado de datos del lado del cliente y del servidor.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre 57 règles priorisées dans 8 catégories pour React et Next.js, simplifiant ainsi la refactoring automatique, la génération de code et l''optimisation des performances, en exploitant les directives complètes de Vercel pour la récupération et le regroupement de données côté client et côté serveur.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, 57 priorisierte Regeln in 8 Kategorien für React und Next.js umzusetzen, wodurch die automatisierte Refactoring, Codegenerierung und Leistungsoptimierung vereinfacht werden, indem die umfassenden Richtlinien von Vercel für Client- und Server-seitiges Datenabrufen und Bündeln genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar 57 regras prioritárias em 8 categorias para React e Next.js, simplificando a refatoração automatizada, geração de código e otimização de desempenho, aproveitando as diretrizes abrangentes da Vercel para coleta e empacotamento de dados do cliente e do servidor.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать 57 приоритизированных правил в 8 категориях для React и Next.js, оптимизируя автоматическую рефакторинг, генерацию кода и оптимизацию производительности, используя комплексные рекомендации Vercel для получения и пакетирования данных клиента и сервера.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ 57 قاعدة مصنفة في 8 فئات لتطبيقات React و Next.js، مما يُبسّط إعادة الهيكلة التلقائية وتوليد الكود و تحسين الأداء، مستفيداً من إرشادات Vercel الشاملة لاسترجاع البيانات وتحضيرها على جانبي العميل والخادم."},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring existing React and Next.js code for improved performance","Automating code reviews for performance issues and security vulnerabilities","Optimizing bundling and data fetching for faster application load times"],"zh":["重构现有的 React 和 Next.js 代码以提高性能","自动化代码审查以发现性能问题和安全漏洞","优化包装和数据获取以实现更快的应用程序加载时间"],"ja":["パフォーマンスの向上のために既存の React と Next.js コードをリファクタリングする","パフォーマンスの問題とセキュリティの脆弱性を発見するためのコードレビューの自動化","より速いアプリケーションの読み込み時間を実現するためのバンドルとデータ取得の最適化"],"ko":["성능 개선을 위해 기존 React 및 Next.js 코드를 리팩터링하는 것","성능 문제 및 보안 취약성을 발견하기 위한 코드 리뷰 자동화","더 빠른 애플리케이션 로드 시간을实现하기 위한 번들링 및 데이터 가져오기 최적화"],"es":["Reestructuración de código React y Next.js existente para mejorar el rendimiento","Automatización de revisiones de código para problemas de rendimiento y vulnerabilidades de seguridad","Optimización de empaquetado y recuperación de datos para tiempos de carga de aplicaciones más rápidos"],"fr":["Réorganisation du code React et Next.js existant pour améliorer les performances","Automatisation des examens de code pour les problèmes de performances et les vulnérabilités de sécurité","Optimisation du regroupement et de la récupération de données pour des temps de chargement d''applications plus rapides"],"de":["Umstrukturierung von bestehendem React- und Next.js-Code für verbesserte Leistung","Automatisierung von Code-Überprüfungen für Leistungsprobleme und Sicherheitslücken","Optimierung von Bündelung und Datenabruf für schnellere Ladezeiten von Anwendungen"],"pt":["Refatoração de código React e Next.js existente para melhorar o desempenho","Automatização de revisões de código para problemas de desempenho e vulnerabilidades de segurança","Otimização do empacotamento e coleta de dados para tempos de carregamento de aplicativos mais rápidos"],"ru":["Рефакторинг существующего кода React и Next.js для улучшения производительности","Автоматизация обзоров кода для проблем производительности и уязвимостей безопасности","Оптимизация пакетирования и получения данных для более быстрой загрузки приложений"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة الكود الموجود لتطبيقات React و Next.js لتحسين الأداء","تأتميم مراجعة الكود لتحديد مشاكل الأداء وثغرات الأمان","تحسين تحميل وتحضير البيانات لتحقيق أوقات تحميل للتطبيقات أسرع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of React and Next.js","Limited to applications hosted on Vercel","May require manual review of automated refactoring suggestions"],"zh":["需要 React 和 Next.js 的知识","仅限于托管在 Vercel 上的应用程序","可能需要手动审查自动重构建议"],"ja":["React と Next.js の知識が必要","Vercel でホストされているアプリケーションに限定される","自動リファクタリングの提案の手動レビューが必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["React 및 Next.js에 대한 지식이 필요합니다.","Vercel에서 호스팅하는 애플리케이션으로 제한됩니다.","자동 리팩터링 제안의 수동 검토가 필요할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de React y Next.js","Limitado a aplicaciones alojadas en Vercel","Puede requerir una revisión manual de las sugerencias de refactorización automatizada"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en React et Next.js","Limité aux applications hébergées sur Vercel","Peut nécessiter un examen manuel des suggestions de refactoring automatisé"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse in React und Next.js","Begrenzt auf auf Vercel gehostete Anwendungen","Kann eine manuelle Überprüfung der Vorschläge zur automatisierten Refactoring erfordern"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de React e Next.js","Limitado a aplicações hospedadas na Vercel","Pode exigir revisão manual de sugestões de refatoração automatizada"],"ru":["Требует знания React и Next.js","Ограничен для приложений, размещенных на Vercel","Может потребовать ручного обзора предложений автоматического рефакторинга"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بتطبيقات React و Next.js","محدود للتطبيقات المضيفة على منصة Vercel","يمكن أن يتطلب مراجعة يدوية لاقتراحات إعادة الهيكلة التلقائية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cacr92/WeReply/xlsx', 'community', 'cacr92', 'WeReply', 'cacr92/WeReply', 'xlsx', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z', '2026-02-18T13:27:58.556Z', NULL, '{"id":"cacr92/WeReply/xlsx","name":"xlsx","description":{"zh":"xlsx工具是一种Excel自动化工具，帮助开发者自动化Excel处理，确保零公式错误，保留现有模板格式","ja":"xlsxツールはExcelの自動化ツールで、開発者がExcelの処理を自動化するのに役立ちます","ko":"xlsx 도구는 엑셀 자동화 도구로, 개발자가 엑셀 처리를 자동화하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"xlsx es una herramienta de automatización de respuestas para Excel que garantiza la entrega de archivos con cero errores de fórmula y conserva los formatos existentes","fr":"xlsx est un outil d''automatisation de réponses pour Excel qui garantit la livraison de fichiers avec zéro erreur de formule et conserve les formats existants","de":"xlsx ist ein Tool für die Automatisierung von Antworten in Excel, das die Lieferung von Dateien mit null Formelfehlern und unter Beibehaltung bestehender Formate gewährleistet","pt":"O assistente de resposta automática xlsx é uma ferramenta para desenvolvedores que necessitam de modelagem financeira e preservação de templates.","ru":"Автоматический помощник ответов xlsx - это инструмент для разработчиков, которым необходимы финансовое моделирование и сохранение шаблонов.","ar":"مساعد الإجابة الآلي xlsx هو أداة للمطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى نمذجة مالية وتنسيق قوالب.","en":"微信聊天自动回复助手"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Excel自动化工具-xlsx","ja":"Excel自動化ツール-xlsx","ko":"엑셀 자동화 도구-xlsx","es":"Excel xlsx: Herramienta de automatización de respuestas","fr":"xlsx Excel : Outil d''automatisation de réponses","de":"xlsx Excel: Tool für die Automatisierung von Antworten","pt":"Assistente de Resposta Automática xlsx","ru":"Автоматический помощник ответов xlsx","ar":"مساعد الإجابة الآلي xlsx","en":"xlsx"},"description":{"zh":"xlsx工具是一种Excel自动化工具，帮助开发者自动化Excel处理，确保零公式错误，保留现有模板格式","ja":"xlsxツールはExcelの自動化ツールで、開発者がExcelの処理を自動化するのに役立ちます","ko":"xlsx 도구는 엑셀 자동화 도구로, 개발자가 엑셀 처리를 자동화하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"xlsx es una herramienta de automatización de respuestas para Excel que garantiza la entrega de archivos con cero errores de fórmula y conserva los formatos e...","fr":"xlsx est un outil d''automatisation de réponses pour Excel qui garantit la livraison de fichiers avec zéro erreur de formule et conserve les formats existants","de":"xlsx ist ein Tool für die Automatisierung von Antworten in Excel, das die Lieferung von Dateien mit null Formelfehlern und unter Beibehaltung bestehender For...","pt":"O assistente de resposta automática xlsx é uma ferramenta para desenvolvedores que necessitam de modelagem financeira e preservação de templates.","ru":"Автоматический помощник ответов xlsx - это инструмент для разработчиков, которым необходимы финансовое моделирование и сохранение шаблонов.","ar":"مساعد الإجابة الآلي xlsx هو أداة للمطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى نمذجة مالية وتنسيق قوالب.","en":"微信聊天自动回复助手"},"definition":{"en":"微信聊天自动回复助手"},"features":{"zh":["零公式错误","保留现有模板格式","自动化Excel处理","支持财务模型","颜色编码支持","确保数据准确性"],"ja":["零の式エラー","既存のテンプレート形式を保持","Excelの処理を自動化","財務モデルのサポート","色コードのサポート","データの正確性を確保"],"ko":["영 수식 오류","기존 템플릿 형식을 유지","엑셀 처리를 자동화","재무 모델 지원","색상 코드 지원","데이터 정확성을 보장"],"es":["Cero errores de fórmula","Conservación de formatos existentes","Compatibilidad con modelos financieros","Codificación de colores","Actualización de plantillas con precisión","Entrega de archivos con eficiencia"],"fr":["Zéro erreur de formule","Conservation des formats existants","Compatibilité avec les modèles financiers","Codage de couleurs","Mise à jour de modèles avec précision","Livraison de fichiers avec efficacité"],"de":["Null Formelfehler","Beibehaltung bestehender Formate","Kompatibilität mit Finanzmodellen","Farbcodierung","Aktualisierung von Vorlagen mit Präzision","Lieferung von Dateien mit Effizienz"],"pt":["Modelagem financeira","Preservação de templates","Sem erros de fórmula","Padronização de formatos","Compatibilidade com arquivos Excel"],"ru":["Финансовое моделирование","Сохранение шаблонов","Отсутствие ошибок формул","Стандартизация форматов","Совместимость с файлами Excel"],"ar":["النمذجة المالية","الاحتفاظ بالقوالب","بدون أخطاء الصيغ","تنسيق أنماط موحدة","توافق مع ملفات Excel"]},"keywords":{"zh":["xlsx工具","Excel自动化","零公式错误","保留现有模板格式","财务模型","颜色编码","数据准确性","开发者工具"],"ja":["xlsxツール","Excel自動化","零の式エラー","既存のテンプレート形式を保持","財務モデルのサポート","色コードのサポート","データの正確性","開発者ツール"],"ko":["xlsx 도구","엑셀 자동화","영 수식 오류","기존 템플릿 형식을 유지","재무 모델 지원","색상 코드 지원","데이터 정확성","개발자 도구"],"es":["xlsx","automatización de respuestas","Excel","cero errores de fórmula","conservación de formatos","modelos financieros","codificación de colores","desarrollo de software","herramientas de productividad"],"fr":["xlsx","automatisation de réponses","Excel","zéro erreur de formule","conservation de formats","modèles financiers","codage de couleurs","développement de logiciels","outils de productivité"],"de":["xlsx","Automatisierung von Antworten","Excel","null Formelfehler","Beibehaltung von Formaten","Finanzmodelle","Farbcodierung","Softwareentwicklung","Produktivitätstools"],"pt":["xlsx","assistente de resposta automática","modelagem financeira","preservação de templates","desenvolvedores","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","arquivos Excel"],"ru":["xlsx","автоматический помощник ответов","финансовое моделирование","сохранение шаблонов","разработчики","инструменты разработки","файлы Excel"],"ar":["xlsx","مساعد الإجابة الآلي","النمذجة المالية","الاحتفاظ بالقوالب","المطورين","أدوات التطوير","ملفات Excel"]}},"owner":"cacr92","repo":"WeReply","repoPath":"cacr92/WeReply","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"xlsx","description":"Comprehensive spreadsheet creation, editing, and analysis with support for formulas, formatting, data analysis, and visualization. When Claude needs to work with spreadsheets (.xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, .tsv, etc) for: (1) Creating new spreadsheets with formulas and formatting, (2) Reading or analyzing data, (3) Modify existing spreadsheets while preserving formulas, (4) Data analysis and visualization in spreadsheets, or (5) Recalculating formulas","bodyPreview":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding S","body":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding Standards\nUnless otherwise stated by the user or existing template\n\n#### Industry-Standard Color Conventions\n- **Blue text (RGB: 0,0,255)**: Hardcoded inputs, and numbers users will change for scenarios\n- **Black text (RGB: 0,0,0)**: ALL formulas and calculations\n- **Green text (RGB: 0,128,0)**: Links pulling from other worksheets within same workbook\n- **Red text (RGB: 255,0,0)**: External links to other files\n- **Yellow background (RGB: 255,255,0)**: Key assumptions needing attention or cells that need to be updated\n\n### Number Formatting Standards\n\n#### Required Format Rules\n- **Years**: Format as text strings (e.g., \"2024\" not \"2,024\")\n- **Currency**: Use $#,##0 format; ALWAYS specify units in headers (\"Revenue ($mm)\")\n- **Zeros**: Use number formatting to make all zeros \"-\", including percentages (e.g., \"$#,##0;($#,##0);-\")\n- **Percentages**: Default to 0.0% format (one decimal)\n- **Multiples**: Format as 0.0x for valuation multiples (EV/EBITDA, P/E)\n- **Negative numbers**: Use parentheses (123) not minus -123\n\n### Formula Construction Rules\n\n#### Assumptions Placement\n- Place ALL assumptions (growth rates, margins, multiples, etc.) in separate assumption cells\n- Use cell references instead of hardcoded values in formulas\n- Example: Use =B5*(1+$B$6) instead of =B5*1.05\n\n#### Formula Error Prevention\n- Verify all cell references are correct\n- Check for off-by-one errors in ranges\n- Ensure consistent formulas across all projection periods\n- Test with edge cases (zero values, negative numbers)\n- Verify no unintended circular references\n\n#### Documentation Requirements for Hardcodes\n- Comment or in cells beside (if end of table). Format: \"Source: [System/Document], [Date], [Specific Reference], [URL if applicable]\"\n- Examples:\n  - \"Source: Company 10-K, FY2024, Page 45, Revenue Note, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Company 10-Q, Q2 2025, Exhibit 99.1, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Bloomberg Terminal, 8/15/2025, AAPL US Equity\"\n  - \"Source: FactSet, 8/20/2025, Consensus Estimates Screen\"\n\n# XLSX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA user may ask you to create, edit, or analyze the contents of an .xlsx file. You have different tools and workflows available for different tasks.\n\n## Important Requirements\n\n**LibreOffice Required for Formula Recalculation**: You can assume LibreOffice is installed for recalculating formula values using the `recalc.py` script. The script automatically configures LibreOffice on first run\n\n## Reading and analyzing data\n\n### Data analysis with pandas\nFor data analysis, visualization, and basic operations, use **pandas** which provides powerful data manipulation capabilities:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read Excel\ndf = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'')  # Default: first sheet\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', sheet_name=None)  # All sheets as dict\n\n# Analyze\ndf.head()      # Preview data\ndf.info()      # Column info\ndf.describe()  # Statistics\n\n# Write Excel\ndf.to_excel(''output.xlsx'', index=False)\n```\n\n## Excel File Workflows\n\n## CRITICAL: Use Formulas, Not Hardcoded Values\n\n**Always use Excel formulas instead of calculating values in Python and hardcoding them.** This ensures the spreadsheet remains dynamic and updateable.\n\n### ❌ WRONG - Hardcoding Calculated Values\n```python\n# Bad: Calculating in Python and hardcoding result\ntotal = df[''Sales''].sum()\nsheet[''B10''] = total  # Hardcodes 5000\n\n# Bad: Computing growth rate in Python\ngrowth = (df.iloc[-1][''Revenue''] - df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']) / df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']\nsheet[''C5''] = growth  # Hardcodes 0.15\n\n# Bad: Python calculation for average\navg = sum(values) / len(values)\nsheet[''D20''] = avg  # Hardcodes 42.5\n```\n\n### ✅ CORRECT - Using Excel Formulas\n```python\n# Good: Let Excel calculate the sum\nsheet[''B10''] = ''=SUM(B2:B9)''\n\n# Good: Growth rate as Excel formula\nsheet[''C5''] = ''=(C4-C2)/C2''\n\n# Good: Average using Excel function\nsheet[''D20''] = ''=AVERAGE(D2:D19)''\n```\n\nThis applies to ALL calculations - totals, percentages, ratios, differences, etc. The spreadsheet should be able to recalculate when source data changes.\n\n## Common Workflow\n1. **Choose tool**: pandas for data, openpyxl for formulas/formatting\n2. **Create/Load**: Create new workbook or load existing file\n3. **Modify**: Add/edit data, formulas, and formatting\n4. **Save**: Write to file\n5. **Recalculate formulas (MANDATORY IF USING FORMULAS)**: Use the recalc.py script\n   ```bash\n   python recalc.py output.xlsx\n   ```\n6. **Verify and fix any errors**: \n   - The script returns JSON with error details\n   - If `status` is `errors_found`, check `error_summary` for specific error types and locations\n   - Fix the identified errors and recalculate again\n   - Common errors to fix:\n     - `#REF!`: Invalid cell references\n     - `#DIV/0!`: Division by zero\n     - `#VALUE!`: Wrong data type in formula\n     - `#NAME?`: Unrecognized formula name\n\n### Creating new Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl for formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, PatternFill, Alignment\n\nwb = Workbook()\nsheet = wb.active\n\n# Add data\nsheet[''A1''] = ''Hello''\nsheet[''B1''] = ''World''\nsheet.append([''Row'', ''of'', ''data''])\n\n# Add formula\nsheet[''B2''] = ''=SUM(A1:A10)''\n\n# Formatting\nsheet[''A1''].font = Font(bold=True, color=''FF0000'')\nsheet[''A1''].fill = PatternFill(''solid'', start_color=''FFFF00'')\nsheet[''A1''].alignment = Alignment(horizontal=''center'')\n\n# Column width\nsheet.column_dimensions[''A''].width = 20\n\nwb.save(''output.xlsx'')\n```\n\n### Editing existing Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl to preserve formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\n\n# Load existing file\nwb = load_workbook(''existing.xlsx'')\nsheet = wb.active  # or wb[''SheetName''] for specific sheet\n\n# Working with multiple sheets\nfor sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n    sheet = wb[sheet_name]\n    print(f\"Sheet: {sheet_name}\")\n\n# Modify cells\nsheet[''A1''] = ''New Value''\nsheet.insert_rows(2)  # Insert row at position 2\nsheet.delete_cols(3)  # Delete column 3\n\n# Add new sheet\nnew_sheet = wb.create_sheet(''NewSheet'')\nnew_sheet[''A1''] = ''Data''\n\nwb.save(''modified.xlsx'')\n```\n\n## Recalculating formulas\n\nExcel files created or modified by openpyxl contain formulas as strings but not calculated values. Use the provided `recalc.py` script to recalculate formulas:\n\n```bash\npython recalc.py <excel_file> [timeout_seconds]\n```\n\nExample:\n```bash\npython recalc.py output.xlsx 30\n```\n\nThe script:\n- Automatically sets up LibreOffice macro on first run\n- Recalculates all formulas in all sheets\n- Scans ALL cells for Excel errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, etc.)\n- Returns JSON with detailed error locations and counts\n- Works on both Linux and macOS\n\n## Formula Verification Checklist\n\nQuick checks to ensure formulas work correctly:\n\n### Essential Verification\n- [ ] **Test 2-3 sample references**: Verify they pull correct values before building full model\n- [ ] **Column mapping**: Confirm Excel columns match (e.g., column 64 = BL, not BK)\n- [ ] **Row offset**: Remember Excel rows are 1-indexed (DataFrame row 5 = Excel row 6)\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n- [ ] **NaN handling**: Check for null values with `pd.notna()`\n- [ ] **Far-right columns**: FY data often in columns 50+ \n- [ ] **Multiple matches**: Search all occurrences, not just first\n- [ ] **Division by zero**: Check denominators before using `/` in formulas (#DIV/0!)\n- [ ] **Wrong references**: Verify all cell references point to intended cells (#REF!)\n- [ ] **Cross-sheet references**: Use correct format (Sheet1!A1) for linking sheets\n\n### Formula Testing Strategy\n- [ ] **Start small**: Test formulas on 2-3 cells before applying broadly\n- [ ] **Verify dependencies**: Check all cells referenced in formulas exist\n- [ ] **Test edge cases**: Include zero, negative, and very large values\n\n### Interpreting recalc.py Output\nThe script returns JSON with error details:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",           // or \"errors_found\"\n  \"total_errors\": 0,              // Total error count\n  \"total_formulas\": 42,           // Number of formulas in file\n  \"error_summary\": {              // Only present if errors found\n    \"#REF!\": {\n      \"count\": 2,\n      \"locations\": [\"Sheet1!B5\", \"Sheet1!C10\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Library Selection\n- **pandas**: Best for data analysis, bulk operations, and simple data export\n- **openpyxl**: Best for complex formatting, formulas, and Excel-specific features\n\n### Working with openpyxl\n- Cell indices are 1-based (row=1, column=1 refers to cell A1)\n- Use `data_only=True` to read calculated values: `load_workbook(''file.xlsx'', data_only=True)`\n- **Warning**: If opened with `data_only=True` and saved, formulas are replaced with values and permanently lost\n- For large files: Use `read_only=True` for reading or `write_only=True` for writing\n- Formulas are preserved but not evaluated - use recalc.py to update values\n\n### Working with pandas\n- Specify data types to avoid inference issues: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', dtype={''id'': str})`\n- For large files, read specific columns: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', usecols=[''A'', ''C'', ''E''])`\n- Handle dates properly: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', parse_dates=[''date_column''])`\n\n## Code Style Guidelines\n**IMPORTANT**: When generating Python code for Excel operations:\n- Write minimal, concise Python code without unnecessary comments\n- Avoid verbose variable names and redundant operations\n- Avoid unnecessary print statements\n\n**For Excel files themselves**:\n- Add comments to cells with complex formulas or important assumptions\n- Document data sources for hardcoded values\n- Include notes for key calculations and model sections"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:27:58.556Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing precise Excel file manipulation and formula error handling.","zh":"非常适合需要精确 Excel 文件操作和公式错误处理的数据分析代理。","ja":"データ分析エージェントが正確なExcelファイル操作と式のエラーハンドリングを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"데이터 분석 에이전트가 정확한 Excel 파일 조작 및 수식 오류 처리가 필요한 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan una manipulación precisa de archivos de Excel y control de errores de fórmulas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données ayant besoin d''une manipulation précise de fichiers Excel et d''une gestion d''erreurs de formules.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die eine präzise Excel-Dateimanipulation und Formel-fehlerbehandlung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de manipulação precisa de arquivos do Excel e tratamento de erros de fórmulas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, которым требуется точная манипуляция файлами Excel и обработка ошибок формул.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل البيانات الذي يحتاج إلى تعامل دقيق مع ملفات إكسيل ومعالجة أخطاء الصيغ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and manage Excel files with zero formula errors, preserving existing templates and conventions, and utilizing color coding standards for financial models, all while maintaining compatibility with various Excel file formats and versions.","zh":"使代理能够创建和管理 Excel 文件，零公式错误，保留现有的模板和约定，并利用颜色编码标准进行财务建模，同时保持与各种 Excel 文件格式和版本的兼容性。","ja":"エージェントがゼロの式エラーでExcelファイルを作成および管理できるようにし、既存のテンプレートや規約を保ち、財務モデルの色付け規格を利用し、さまざまなExcelファイル形式やバージョンとの互換性を維持します。","ko":"에이전트가 영 수식 오류로 Excel 파일을 생성 및 관리할 수 있게 하며, 기존 템플릿 및 규약을 보존하고, 재무 모델의 색상 코딩 표준을 활용하며, 다양한 Excel 파일 형식 및 버전에 대한 호환성을 유지합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear y gestionar archivos de Excel con cero errores de fórmulas, preservando plantillas y convenciones existentes, y utilizando estándares de codificación de colores para modelos financieros, todo mientras mantiene la compatibilidad con varios formatos y versiones de archivos de Excel.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de gérer des fichiers Excel avec zéro erreur de formules, en préservant les modèles et les conventions existants, et en utilisant des normes de codage de couleurs pour les modèles financiers, le tout en maintenant la compatibilité avec divers formats et versions de fichiers Excel.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Excel-Dateien mit null Formelfehlern zu erstellen und zu verwalten, indem bestehende Vorlagen und Konventionen erhalten bleiben und Farbcodierungsstandards für Finanzmodelle verwendet werden, während die Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Excel-Dateiformaten und -Versionen aufrechterhalten wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e gerenciar arquivos do Excel com zero erros de fórmulas, preservando modelos e convenções existentes, e utilizando padrões de codificação de cores para modelos financeiros, tudo isso mantendo a compatibilidade com vários formatos e versões de arquivos do Excel.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и управлять файлами Excel с нулевыми ошибками формул, сохраняя существующие шаблоны и соглашения, и используя стандарты цветового кодирования для финансовых моделей, все это при сохранении совместимости с различными форматами и версиями файлов Excel.","ar":"يسمح للعميل بإنشاء وتحديث ملفات إكسيل بدون أخطاء صيغ، مع الحفاظ على القوالب والتقاليد الحالية، واستخدام معايير الترميز اللوني للنماذج المالية، مع الحفاظ على التوافق مع مختلف صيغ ونسخ ملفات إكسيل."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Excel file updates with zero formula errors","Generating financial models with color coding standards","Preserving existing template formats and conventions during file modifications"],"zh":["自动化 Excel 文件更新，零公式错误","使用颜色编码标准生成财务模型","在文件修改过程中保留现有的模板格式和约定"],"ja":["ゼロの式エラーでExcelファイルを自動更新する","財務モデルの色付け規格を使用して生成する","ファイルの変更中に既存のテンプレート形式や規約を保つ"],"ko":["영 수식 오류로 Excel 파일을 자동 업데이트하는 것","재무 모델의 색상 코딩 표준을 사용하여 생성하는 것","파일 수정 중에 기존 템플릿 형식 및 규약을 보존하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar actualizaciones de archivos de Excel con cero errores de fórmulas","Generar modelos financieros con estándares de codificación de colores","Preservar formatos y convenciones de plantillas existentes durante las modificaciones de archivos"],"fr":["Automatiser les mises à jour de fichiers Excel avec zéro erreur de formules","Générer des modèles financiers avec des normes de codage de couleurs","Préserver les formats et les conventions de modèles existants lors des modifications de fichiers"],"de":["Automatisierung von Excel-Datei-Aktualisierungen mit null Formelfehlern","Erstellung von Finanzmodellen mit Farbcodierungsstandards","Erhaltung bestehender Vorlagenformate und -konventionen während Dateimodifikationen"],"pt":["Automatizar atualizações de arquivos do Excel com zero erros de fórmulas","Gerar modelos financeiros com padrões de codificação de cores","Preservar formatos e convenções de modelos existentes durante modificações de arquivos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обновления файлов Excel с нулевыми ошибками формул","Генерировать финансовые модели со стандартами цветового кодирования","Сохранять форматы и соглашения существующих шаблонов при изменении файлов"],"ar":["تحديث ملفات إكسيل تلقائيًا بدون أخطاء صيغ","إنشاء نماذج مالية باستخدام معايير الترميز اللوني","الحفاظ على صيغ وتقاليد القوالب الحالية أثناء تحديث الملفات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires exact matching of existing format, style, and conventions","Must avoid imposing standardized formatting on files with established patterns"],"zh":["需要现有格式、样式和约定的完全匹配","避免对已建立模式的文件施加标准化格式"],"ja":["既存の形式、スタイル、規約の完全な一致が必要","既存のパターンを持つファイルに標準化された形式を課すことを避ける"],"ko":["기존 형식, 스타일, 규약의 완전한 일치가 필요","既存의 패턴을 가진 파일에 표준화된 형식을 강요하는 것을 피함"],"es":["Requiere una coincidencia exacta del formato, estilo y convenciones existentes","Debe evitar imponer un formato estandarizado en archivos con patrones establecidos"],"fr":["Nécessite une correspondance exacte du format, du style et des conventions existants","Doit éviter d''imposer un formatage standardisé sur des fichiers avec des modèles établis"],"de":["Erfordert eine exakte Übereinstimmung des bestehenden Formats, Stils und der Konventionen","Sollte die Aufdrängung einer standardisierten Formatierung auf Dateien mit etablierten Mustern vermeiden"],"pt":["Requer correspondência exata do formato, estilo e convenções existentes","Deve evitar impor formatação padronizada em arquivos com padrões estabelecidos"],"ru":["Требует точного совпадения существующего формата, стиля и соглашений","Должен избегать навязывания стандартизированного форматирования файлам с установленными шаблонами"],"ar":["يتطلب مطابقة دقيقة للتنسيق والنمط والتقاليد الحالية","يجب تجنب فرض تنسيق معياري على الملفات ذات الأنماط الموحدة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
