cel 파일에 수식 오류가 없고 기존 템플릿의 형식과 스타일이 유지되는 것을 요구합니다","es":"La creación de modelos financieros en xlsx requiere precisión y atención al detalle. Aprende a evitar errores de fórmula y a preservar los formatos existentes","fr":"La création de modèles financiers xlsx nécessite précision et attention aux détails. Apprenez à éviter les erreurs de formule et à préserver les formats exis...","de":"Die Erstellung von Finanzmodellen in xlsx erfordert Präzision und Aufmerksamkeit für Details. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Formelfehler vermeiden und bestehende For...","pt":"Desenvolva modelos Excel com zero erros de fórmula e preserve os templates existentes","ru":"Разработайте модели Excel с нулевыми ошибками формул и сохраните существующие шаблоны","ar":"طور نماذج إكسل بدون أخطاء في الصيغ واحفظ القوالب الحالية","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["零公式错误","保留现有模板","金融模型颜色编码","确保一致性","提高文件质量","简化文件修改"],"ja":["ゼロの式エラー","既存のテンプレートの保存","財務モデルの色付け","一貫性の確保","ファイル品質の向上","ファイル修正の簡素化"],"ko":["제로 수식 오류","기존 템플릿 유지","금융 모델 색상 코딩","일관성 보장","파일 품질 향상","파일 수정 간소화"],"es":["Creación de modelos financieros sin errores de fórmula","Preservación de formatos existentes","Color coding para una mejor visualización","Compatibilidad con Excel","Evitación de errores de fórmula como #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"fr":["Création de modèles financiers sans erreurs de formule","Préservation des formats existants","Color coding pour une meilleure visualisation","Compatibilité avec Excel","Évitement des erreurs de formule comme #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"de":["Erstellung von Finanzmodellen ohne Formelfehler","Erhaltung bestehender Formate","Color coding für eine bessere Visualisierung","Kompatibilität mit Excel","Vermeidung von Formelfehlern wie #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?"],"pt":["Zero erros de fórmula","Preservação de templates existentes","Color Coding para modelos financeiros","Compatibilidade com AesopIDE","Antigravity-inspired UI"],"ru":["Нулевые ошибки формул","Сохранение существующих шаблонов","Color Coding для финансовых моделей","Совместимость с AesopIDE","Интерфейс, вдохновленный Antigravity"],"ar":["بدون أخطاء في الصيغ","حفظ القوالب الحالية","تلوين للنماذج المالية","التوافق مع AesopIDE","واجهة مستوحاة من Antigravity"]},"keywords":{"zh":["XLSX 技术规范","Excel 文件质量","金融模型","颜色编码","一致性","文件修改","技术要求"],"ja":["XLSX 技術仕様","Excel ファイル品質","財務モデルの色付け","一貫性","ファイル修正","技術要件"],"ko":["XLSX 기술 사양","Excel 파일 품질","금융 모델 색상 코딩","일관성","파일 수정","기술 요구 사항"],"es":["xlsx","modelos financieros","creación de archivos Excel","evitación de errores de fórmula","preservación de formatos existentes","color coding","compatibilidad con Excel"],"fr":["xlsx","modèles financiers","création de fichiers Excel","évitement des erreurs de formule","préservation des formats existants","color coding","compatibilité avec Excel"],"de":["xlsx","Finanzmodelle","Erstellung von Excel-Dateien","Vermeidung von Formelfehlern","Erhaltung bestehender Formate","Color coding","Kompatibilität mit Excel"],"pt":["xlsx","modelos excel","zero erros de fórmula","preservação de templates","desenvolvimento de modelos","AesopIDE","Antigravity-inspired UI"],"ru":["xlsx","модели Excel","нулевые ошибки формул","сохранение шаблонов","разработка моделей","AesopIDE","Интерфейс, вдохновленный Antigravity"],"ar":["xlsx","نماذج إكسل","بدون أخطاء في الصيغ","حفظ القوالب","تطوير النماذج","AesopIDE","واجهة مستوحاة من Antigravity"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"xlsx","description":"Comprehensive spreadsheet creation, editing, and analysis with support for formulas, formatting, data analysis, and visualization. When Claude needs to work with spreadsheets (.xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, .tsv, etc) for: (1) Creating new spreadsheets with formulas and formatting, (2) Reading or analyzing data, (3) Modify existing spreadsheets while preserving formulas, (4) Data analysis and visualization in spreadsheets, or (5) Recalculating formulas","bodyPreview":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding S","body":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding Standards\nUnless otherwise stated by the user or existing template\n\n#### Industry-Standard Color Conventions\n- **Blue text (RGB: 0,0,255)**: Hardcoded inputs, and numbers users will change for scenarios\n- **Black text (RGB: 0,0,0)**: ALL formulas and calculations\n- **Green text (RGB: 0,128,0)**: Links pulling from other worksheets within same workbook\n- **Red text (RGB: 255,0,0)**: External links to other files\n- **Yellow background (RGB: 255,255,0)**: Key assumptions needing attention or cells that need to be updated\n\n### Number Formatting Standards\n\n#### Required Format Rules\n- **Years**: Format as text strings (e.g., \"2024\" not \"2,024\")\n- **Currency**: Use $#,##0 format; ALWAYS specify units in headers (\"Revenue ($mm)\")\n- **Zeros**: Use number formatting to make all zeros \"-\", including percentages (e.g., \"$#,##0;($#,##0);-\")\n- **Percentages**: Default to 0.0% format (one decimal)\n- **Multiples**: Format as 0.0x for valuation multiples (EV/EBITDA, P/E)\n- **Negative numbers**: Use parentheses (123) not minus -123\n\n### Formula Construction Rules\n\n#### Assumptions Placement\n- Place ALL assumptions (growth rates, margins, multiples, etc.) in separate assumption cells\n- Use cell references instead of hardcoded values in formulas\n- Example: Use =B5*(1+$B$6) instead of =B5*1.05\n\n#### Formula Error Prevention\n- Verify all cell references are correct\n- Check for off-by-one errors in ranges\n- Ensure consistent formulas across all projection periods\n- Test with edge cases (zero values, negative numbers)\n- Verify no unintended circular references\n\n#### Documentation Requirements for Hardcodes\n- Comment or in cells beside (if end of table). Format: \"Source: [System/Document], [Date], [Specific Reference], [URL if applicable]\"\n- Examples:\n  - \"Source: Company 10-K, FY2024, Page 45, Revenue Note, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Company 10-Q, Q2 2025, Exhibit 99.1, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Bloomberg Terminal, 8/15/2025, AAPL US Equity\"\n  - \"Source: FactSet, 8/20/2025, Consensus Estimates Screen\"\n\n# XLSX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA user may ask you to create, edit, or analyze the contents of an .xlsx file. You have different tools and workflows available for different tasks.\n\n## Important Requirements\n\n**LibreOffice Required for Formula Recalculation**: You can assume LibreOffice is installed for recalculating formula values using the `recalc.py` script. The script automatically configures LibreOffice on first run\n\n## Reading and analyzing data\n\n### Data analysis with pandas\nFor data analysis, visualization, and basic operations, use **pandas** which provides powerful data manipulation capabilities:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read Excel\ndf = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'')  # Default: first sheet\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', sheet_name=None)  # All sheets as dict\n\n# Analyze\ndf.head()      # Preview data\ndf.info()      # Column info\ndf.describe()  # Statistics\n\n# Write Excel\ndf.to_excel(''output.xlsx'', index=False)\n```\n\n## Excel File Workflows\n\n## CRITICAL: Use Formulas, Not Hardcoded Values\n\n**Always use Excel formulas instead of calculating values in Python and hardcoding them.** This ensures the spreadsheet remains dynamic and updateable.\n\n### ❌ WRONG - Hardcoding Calculated Values\n```python\n# Bad: Calculating in Python and hardcoding result\ntotal = df[''Sales''].sum()\nsheet[''B10''] = total  # Hardcodes 5000\n\n# Bad: Computing growth rate in Python\ngrowth = (df.iloc[-1][''Revenue''] - df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']) / df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']\nsheet[''C5''] = growth  # Hardcodes 0.15\n\n# Bad: Python calculation for average\navg = sum(values) / len(values)\nsheet[''D20''] = avg  # Hardcodes 42.5\n```\n\n### ✅ CORRECT - Using Excel Formulas\n```python\n# Good: Let Excel calculate the sum\nsheet[''B10''] = ''=SUM(B2:B9)''\n\n# Good: Growth rate as Excel formula\nsheet[''C5''] = ''=(C4-C2)/C2''\n\n# Good: Average using Excel function\nsheet[''D20''] = ''=AVERAGE(D2:D19)''\n```\n\nThis applies to ALL calculations - totals, percentages, ratios, differences, etc. The spreadsheet should be able to recalculate when source data changes.\n\n## Common Workflow\n1. **Choose tool**: pandas for data, openpyxl for formulas/formatting\n2. **Create/Load**: Create new workbook or load existing file\n3. **Modify**: Add/edit data, formulas, and formatting\n4. **Save**: Write to file\n5. **Recalculate formulas (MANDATORY IF USING FORMULAS)**: Use the recalc.py script\n   ```bash\n   python recalc.py output.xlsx\n   ```\n6. **Verify and fix any errors**: \n   - The script returns JSON with error details\n   - If `status` is `errors_found`, check `error_summary` for specific error types and locations\n   - Fix the identified errors and recalculate again\n   - Common errors to fix:\n     - `#REF!`: Invalid cell references\n     - `#DIV/0!`: Division by zero\n     - `#VALUE!`: Wrong data type in formula\n     - `#NAME?`: Unrecognized formula name\n\n### Creating new Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl for formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, PatternFill, Alignment\n\nwb = Workbook()\nsheet = wb.active\n\n# Add data\nsheet[''A1''] = ''Hello''\nsheet[''B1''] = ''World''\nsheet.append([''Row'', ''of'', ''data''])\n\n# Add formula\nsheet[''B2''] = ''=SUM(A1:A10)''\n\n# Formatting\nsheet[''A1''].font = Font(bold=True, color=''FF0000'')\nsheet[''A1''].fill = PatternFill(''solid'', start_color=''FFFF00'')\nsheet[''A1''].alignment = Alignment(horizontal=''center'')\n\n# Column width\nsheet.column_dimensions[''A''].width = 20\n\nwb.save(''output.xlsx'')\n```\n\n### Editing existing Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl to preserve formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\n\n# Load existing file\nwb = load_workbook(''existing.xlsx'')\nsheet = wb.active  # or wb[''SheetName''] for specific sheet\n\n# Working with multiple sheets\nfor sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n    sheet = wb[sheet_name]\n    print(f\"Sheet: {sheet_name}\")\n\n# Modify cells\nsheet[''A1''] = ''New Value''\nsheet.insert_rows(2)  # Insert row at position 2\nsheet.delete_cols(3)  # Delete column 3\n\n# Add new sheet\nnew_sheet = wb.create_sheet(''NewSheet'')\nnew_sheet[''A1''] = ''Data''\n\nwb.save(''modified.xlsx'')\n```\n\n## Recalculating formulas\n\nExcel files created or modified by openpyxl contain formulas as strings but not calculated values. Use the provided `recalc.py` script to recalculate formulas:\n\n```bash\npython recalc.py <excel_file> [timeout_seconds]\n```\n\nExample:\n```bash\npython recalc.py output.xlsx 30\n```\n\nThe script:\n- Automatically sets up LibreOffice macro on first run\n- Recalculates all formulas in all sheets\n- Scans ALL cells for Excel errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, etc.)\n- Returns JSON with detailed error locations and counts\n- Works on both Linux and macOS\n\n## Formula Verification Checklist\n\nQuick checks to ensure formulas work correctly:\n\n### Essential Verification\n- [ ] **Test 2-3 sample references**: Verify they pull correct values before building full model\n- [ ] **Column mapping**: Confirm Excel columns match (e.g., column 64 = BL, not BK)\n- [ ] **Row offset**: Remember Excel rows are 1-indexed (DataFrame row 5 = Excel row 6)\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n- [ ] **NaN handling**: Check for null values with `pd.notna()`\n- [ ] **Far-right columns**: FY data often in columns 50+ \n- [ ] **Multiple matches**: Search all occurrences, not just first\n- [ ] **Division by zero**: Check denominators before using `/` in formulas (#DIV/0!)\n- [ ] **Wrong references**: Verify all cell references point to intended cells (#REF!)\n- [ ] **Cross-sheet references**: Use correct format (Sheet1!A1) for linking sheets\n\n### Formula Testing Strategy\n- [ ] **Start small**: Test formulas on 2-3 cells before applying broadly\n- [ ] **Verify dependencies**: Check all cells referenced in formulas exist\n- [ ] **Test edge cases**: Include zero, negative, and very large values\n\n### Interpreting recalc.py Output\nThe script returns JSON with error details:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",           // or \"errors_found\"\n  \"total_errors\": 0,              // Total error count\n  \"total_formulas\": 42,           // Number of formulas in file\n  \"error_summary\": {              // Only present if errors found\n    \"#REF!\": {\n      \"count\": 2,\n      \"locations\": [\"Sheet1!B5\", \"Sheet1!C10\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Library Selection\n- **pandas**: Best for data analysis, bulk operations, and simple data export\n- **openpyxl**: Best for complex formatting, formulas, and Excel-specific features\n\n### Working with openpyxl\n- Cell indices are 1-based (row=1, column=1 refers to cell A1)\n- Use `data_only=True` to read calculated values: `load_workbook(''file.xlsx'', data_only=True)`\n- **Warning**: If opened with `data_only=True` and saved, formulas are replaced with values and permanently lost\n- For large files: Use `read_only=True` for reading or `write_only=True` for writing\n- Formulas are preserved but not evaluated - use recalc.py to update values\n\n### Working with pandas\n- Specify data types to avoid inference issues: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', dtype={''id'': str})`\n- For large files, read specific columns: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', usecols=[''A'', ''C'', ''E''])`\n- Handle dates properly: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', parse_dates=[''date_column''])`\n\n## Code Style Guidelines\n**IMPORTANT**: When generating Python code for Excel operations:\n- Write minimal, concise Python code without unnecessary comments\n- Avoid verbose variable names and redundant operations\n- Avoid unnecessary print statements\n\n**For Excel files themselves**:\n- Add comments to cells with complex formulas or important assumptions\n- Document data sources for hardcoded values\n- Include notes for key calculations and model sections"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:28:31.887Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing precise Excel file manipulation and formula error handling.","zh":"适合需要精确 Excel 文件操作和公式错误处理的数据分析代理。","ja":"正確なExcelファイル操作と数式エラーハンドリングが必要なデータ分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"정확한 Excel 파일 조작과 수식 오류 처리가 필요한 데이터 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan una manipulación precisa de archivos de Excel y control de errores de fórmulas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données nécessitant une manipulation précise de fichiers Excel et une gestion des erreurs de formules.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die eine präzise Excel-Dateimanipulation und Formel-Fehlerbehandlung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de manipulação precisa de arquivos do Excel e tratamento de erros de fórmulas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, требующих точного манипулирования файлами Excel и обработки ошибок формул.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء تحليل البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى تعامل دقيق مع ملفات إكسل ومعالجة أخطاء الصيغ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate error-free Excel models with zero formula errors, preserving existing template conventions and utilizing color coding standards, all while ensuring compatibility with various Excel file formats.","zh":"赋予代理生成零公式错误的Excel模型的能力，保留现有的模板约定，利用颜色编码标准，并确保与各种Excel文件格式兼容。","ja":"ゼロの数式エラーでExcelモデルを生成するエージェントを可能にし、既存のテンプレートの規約を保持し、色付けの標準を利用し、さまざまなExcelファイル形式との互換性を確保します。","ko":"제로 수식 오류로 Excel 모델을 생성할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, 기존 템플릿 규약을 유지하고, 색상 코딩 표준을 활용하며, 다양한 Excel 파일 형식과 호환성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar modelos de Excel sin errores, con cero errores de fórmulas, preservando las convenciones de plantilla existentes y utilizando estándares de codificación de colores, todo mientras se garantiza la compatibilidad con varios formatos de archivo de Excel.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des modèles Excel sans erreurs, avec zéro erreur de formules, en préservant les conventions de modèle de template existantes et en utilisant des normes de codage de couleurs, le tout en garantissant la compatibilité avec différents formats de fichiers Excel.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, fehlerfreie Excel-Modelle mit null Formelfehlern zu generieren, indem bestehende Vorlagenkonventionen erhalten und Farbcodierungsstandards verwendet werden, während die Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Excel-Dateiformaten gewährleistet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar modelos do Excel sem erros, com zero erros de fórmulas, preservando as convenções de modelos de template existentes e utilizando padrões de codificação de cores, garantindo compatibilidade com vários formatos de arquivos do Excel.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать модели Excel без ошибок, с нулевым количеством ошибок формул, сохраняя существующие конвенции шаблонов и используя стандарты цветового кодирования, обеспечивая совместимость с различными форматами файлов Excel.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنتاج نماذج إكسل خالية من الأخطاء، مع صفر أخطاء في الصيغ، مع الحفاظ على الاتفاقيات الحالية لقوالب النماذج واستخدام معايير الترميز اللوني، وضمان التوافق مع تنسيقات ملفات إكسل المختلفة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Excel template updates with exact format matching","Debugging formula errors in complex financial models","Generating color-coded Excel reports for data visualization"],"zh":["使用精确格式匹配自动更新 Excel 模板","调试复杂财务模型中的公式错误","生成彩色编码的 Excel 报表以进行数据可视化"],"ja":["正確なフォーマットマッチングを使用してExcelテンプレートを自動更新する","複雑な財務モデルの数式エラーをデバッグする","データの視覚化のためのカラーコード付きExcelレポートを生成する"],"ko":["정확한 형식 일치를 사용하여 Excel 템플릿을 자동으로 업데이트함","복잡한 재무 모델의 수식 오류를 디버깅함","데이터 시각화를 위한 색상 코딩이 된 Excel 보고서를 생성함"],"es":["Automatización de actualizaciones de plantillas de Excel con coincidencia de formato exacta","Depuración de errores de fórmulas en modelos financieros complejos","Generación de informes de Excel codificados por colores para visualización de datos"],"fr":["Automatisation de la mise à jour des modèles Excel avec une correspondance de format exacte","Débogage des erreurs de formules dans des modèles financiers complexes","Génération de rapports Excel codés en couleur pour la visualisation de données"],"de":["Automatisierung von Excel-Vorlagen-Updates mit exakter Formatübereinstimmung","Fehlerbehebung in komplexen Finanzmodellen","Generierung von farbcodierten Excel-Berichten für Datenvisualisierung"],"pt":["Automatizar atualizações de modelos do Excel com correspondência de formato exata","Depurar erros de fórmulas em modelos financeiros complexos","Gerar relatórios do Excel coloridos para visualização de dados"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обновления шаблонов Excel с точным совпадением формата","Отлаживать ошибки формул в сложных финансовых моделях","Генерировать цветные отчеты Excel для визуализации данных"],"ar":["توفير تحديثات آلية لقوالب إكسل مع مطابقة دقيقة للتنسيق","تصحيح أخطاء الصيغ في النماذج المالية المعقدة","إنتاج تقارير إكسل ملونة لتصور البيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires exact matching of existing template conventions","Zero formula errors required in delivered Excel models"],"zh":["需要现有的模板约定进行精确匹配","交付的 Excel 模型中需要零公式错误"],"ja":["既存のテンプレートの規約との正確なマッチングが必要","提供されたExcelモデルにはゼロの数式エラーが必要"],"ko":["기존 템플릿 규약과 정확한 일치가 필요함","제공된 Excel 모델에는 제로 수식 오류가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere una coincidencia exacta de las convenciones de plantilla existentes","Se requieren cero errores de fórmulas en los modelos de Excel entregados"],"fr":["Nécessite une correspondance exacte des conventions de modèle de template existantes","Des erreurs de formules nulles sont requises dans les modèles Excel livrés"],"de":["Erfordert eine exakte Übereinstimmung mit bestehenden Vorlagenkonventionen","Null Formelfehler sind in den gelieferten Excel-Modellen erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige correspondência exata das convenções de modelos de template existentes","Requer zero erros de fórmulas nos modelos do Excel entregues"],"ru":["Требует точного совпадения существующих конвенций шаблонов","Требует нулевого количества ошибок формул в поставляемых моделях Excel"],"ar":["يتطلب مطابقة دقيقة للاتفاقيات الحالية لقوالب النماذج","يتطلب صفر أخطاء في الصيغ في نماذج إكسل المسلّمة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
