ules clairs et des répertoires maintenables","de":"Entwerfen Sie gut organisierte Python-Projekte mit klaren Modulen und wartbaren Verzeichnissen","pt":"Desenvolva projetos Python organizados com módulos claros e diretórios mantenhaíveis.","ru":"Разрабатывайте проекты Python с четкой организацией модулей и поддерживаемыми директориями.","ar":"ابني مشاريع بايثون منظمة مع وحدات واضحة ومسموحات قابلة للصيانة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["明确的模块边界","可维护的目录结构","显式的公共接口","测试文件组织"],"ja":["明確なモジュール境界","保守可能なディレクトリ構造","明示的なパブリックインターフェース","テストファイルの組織"],"ko":["명확한 모듈 경계","유지 보수 가능한 디렉토리 구조","명시적인 공공 인터페이스","테스트 파일 구성"],"es":["Diseño de módulos claros","Definición de interfaces públicas","Estructuras de directorios mantenibles","Organización de proyectos nuevos y existentes","Decisión entre estructuras de directorios planas y anidadas"],"fr":["Conception de modules clairs","Définition d''interfaces publiques","Structures de répertoires maintenables","Organisation de projets nouveaux et existants","Décision entre structures de répertoires plates et imbriquées"],"de":["Entwurf von klaren Modulen","Definition von öffentlichen Schnittstellen","Wartbare Verzeichnisstrukturen","Organisation von neuen und bestehenden Projekten","Entscheidung zwischen flachen und verschachtelten Verzeichnisstrukturen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de projetos Python organizados","Definição de interfaces públicas com `__all__`","Estrutura de diretórios plana ou aninhada","Testes de unidade e integração","Manutenção de código legível e sustentável","Melhoria da descoberta e previsibilidade do código"],"ru":["Разработка организованных проектов Python","Определение публичных интерфейсов с `__all__`","Плоская или вложенная структура директорий","Юнит-тесты и интеграционные тесты","Поддержание читаемого и поддерживаемого кода","Улучшение обнаружения и предсказуемости кода"],"ar":["بناء مشاريع بايثون منظمة","تحديد واجهات عامة باستخدام `__all__`","هيكل مسموح بالدليل المسطح أو المتداخل","اختبارات الوحدة والتكامل","صيانة الكود المقروء والقابل للصيانة","تحسين الكشف والتنبؤ بالكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python 项目结构","模块架构","目录结构","公共接口","测试文件","代码组织"],"ja":["Python プロジェクト構造","モジュールアーキテクチャ","ディレクトリ構造","パブリックインターフェース","テストファイル","コード組織"],"ko":["파이썬 프로젝트 구조","모듈 아키텍처","디렉토리 구조","공공 인터페이스","테스트 파일","코드 구성"],"es":["estructura de proyecto python","diseño de módulos","interfaces públicas","estructuras de directorios","organización de proyectos","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["structure de projet python","conception de modules","interfaces publiques","structures de répertoires","organisation de projets","développement de logiciels"],"de":["python-projektstruktur","entwurf von modulen","öffentliche schnittstellen","verzeichnisstrukturen","projektorganisation","softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["estrutura de projeto python","desenvolvimento de software","programação python","módulos python","diretórios python","testes de unidade","manutenção de código","legibilidade de código","sustentabilidade de código"],"ru":["структура проекта python","разработка программного обеспечения","программирование на python","модули python","директории python","юнит-тесты","поддержка кода","читаемость кода","поддерживаемость кода"],"ar":["هيكل مشروع بايثون","تطوير البرمجيات","برمجة بايثون","وحدات بايثون","مسموحات بايثون","اختبارات الوحدة","صيانة الكود","قراءة الكود","صيانة الكود"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-project-structure","description":"Python project organization, module architecture, and public API design. Use when setting up new projects, organizing modules, defining public interfaces with __all__, or planning directory layouts.","bodyPreview":"# Python Project Structure & Module Architecture\n\nDesign well-organized Python projects with clear module boundaries, explicit public interfaces, and maintainable directory structures. Good organization makes code discoverable and changes predictable.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Starting a new Python project from scratch\n- Reorganizing an existing codebase for clarity\n- Defining module public APIs with `__all__`\n- Deciding between flat and nested directory structures\n- Determining test file pl","body":"# Python Project Structure & Module Architecture\n\nDesign well-organized Python projects with clear module boundaries, explicit public interfaces, and maintainable directory structures. Good organization makes code discoverable and changes predictable.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Starting a new Python project from scratch\n- Reorganizing an existing codebase for clarity\n- Defining module public APIs with `__all__`\n- Deciding between flat and nested directory structures\n- Determining test file placement strategies\n- Creating reusable library packages\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Module Cohesion\n\nGroup related code that changes together. A module should have a single, clear purpose.\n\n### 2. Explicit Interfaces\n\nDefine what''s public with `__all__`. Everything not listed is an internal implementation detail.\n\n### 3. Flat Hierarchies\n\nPrefer shallow directory structures. Add depth only for genuine sub-domains.\n\n### 4. Consistent Conventions\n\nApply naming and organization patterns uniformly across the project.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```\nmyproject/\n├── src/\n│   └── myproject/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── services/\n│       ├── models/\n│       └── api/\n├── tests/\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── README.md\n```\n\n## Fundamental Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: One Concept Per File\n\nEach file should focus on a single concept or closely related set of functions. Consider splitting when a file:\n\n- Handles multiple unrelated responsibilities\n- Grows beyond 300-500 lines (varies by complexity)\n- Contains classes that change for different reasons\n\n```python\n# Good: Focused files\n# user_service.py - User business logic\n# user_repository.py - User data access\n# user_models.py - User data structures\n\n# Avoid: Kitchen sink files\n# user.py - Contains service, repository, models, utilities...\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Explicit Public APIs with `__all__`\n\nDefine the public interface for every module. Unlisted members are internal implementation details.\n\n```python\n# mypackage/services/__init__.py\nfrom .user_service import UserService\nfrom .order_service import OrderService\nfrom .exceptions import ServiceError, ValidationError\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"UserService\",\n    \"OrderService\",\n    \"ServiceError\",\n    \"ValidationError\",\n]\n\n# Internal helpers remain private by omission\n# from .internal_helpers import _validate_input  # Not exported\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Flat Directory Structure\n\nPrefer minimal nesting. Deep hierarchies make imports verbose and navigation difficult.\n\n```\n# Preferred: Flat structure\nproject/\n├── api/\n│   ├── routes.py\n│   └── middleware.py\n├── services/\n│   ├── user_service.py\n│   └── order_service.py\n├── models/\n│   ├── user.py\n│   └── order.py\n└── utils/\n    └── validation.py\n\n# Avoid: Deep nesting\nproject/core/internal/services/impl/user/\n```\n\nAdd sub-packages only when there''s a genuine sub-domain requiring isolation.\n\n### Pattern 4: Test File Organization\n\nChoose one approach and apply it consistently throughout the project.\n\n**Option A: Colocated Tests**\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── user_service.py\n├── test_user_service.py\n├── order_service.py\n└── test_order_service.py\n```\n\nBenefits: Tests live next to the code they verify. Easy to see coverage gaps.\n\n**Option B: Parallel Test Directory**\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── services/\n│   ├── user_service.py\n│   └── order_service.py\ntests/\n├── services/\n│   ├── test_user_service.py\n│   └── test_order_service.py\n```\n\nBenefits: Clean separation between production and test code. Standard for larger projects.\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Pattern 5: Package Initialization\n\nUse `__init__.py` to provide a clean public interface for package consumers.\n\n```python\n# mypackage/__init__.py\n\"\"\"MyPackage - A library for doing useful things.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .core import MainClass, HelperClass\nfrom .exceptions import PackageError, ConfigError\nfrom .config import Settings\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"MainClass\",\n    \"HelperClass\",\n    \"PackageError\",\n    \"ConfigError\",\n    \"Settings\",\n]\n\n__version__ = \"1.0.0\"\n```\n\nConsumers can then import directly from the package:\n\n```python\nfrom mypackage import MainClass, Settings\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Layered Architecture\n\nOrganize code by architectural layer for clear separation of concerns.\n\n```\nmyapp/\n├── api/           # HTTP handlers, request/response\n│   ├── routes/\n│   └── middleware/\n├── services/      # Business logic\n├── repositories/  # Data access\n├── models/        # Domain entities\n├── schemas/       # API schemas (Pydantic)\n└── config/        # Configuration\n```\n\nEach layer should only depend on layers below it, never above.\n\n### Pattern 7: Domain-Driven Structure\n\nFor complex applications, organize by business domain rather than technical layer.\n\n```\necommerce/\n├── users/\n│   ├── models.py\n│   ├── services.py\n│   ├── repository.py\n│   └── api.py\n├── orders/\n│   ├── models.py\n│   ├── services.py\n│   ├── repository.py\n│   └── api.py\n└── shared/\n    ├── database.py\n    └── exceptions.py\n```\n\n## File and Module Naming\n\n### Conventions\n\n- Use `snake_case` for all file and module names: `user_repository.py`\n- Avoid abbreviations that obscure meaning: `user_repository.py` not `usr_repo.py`\n- Match class names to file names: `UserService` in `user_service.py`\n\n### Import Style\n\nUse absolute imports for clarity and reliability:\n\n```python\n# Preferred: Absolute imports\nfrom myproject.services import UserService\nfrom myproject.models import User\n\n# Avoid: Relative imports\nfrom ..services import UserService\nfrom . import models\n```\n\nRelative imports can break when modules are moved or reorganized.\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Keep files focused** - One concept per file, consider splitting at 300-500 lines (varies by complexity)\n2. **Define `__all__` explicitly** - Make public interfaces clear\n3. **Prefer flat structures** - Add depth only for genuine sub-domains\n4. **Use absolute imports** - More reliable and clearer\n5. **Be consistent** - Apply patterns uniformly across the project\n6. **Match names to content** - File names should describe their purpose\n7. **Separate concerns** - Keep layers distinct and dependencies flowing one direction\n8. **Document your structure** - Include a README explaining the organization\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:30:05.636Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring best practices in Python project organization and module architecture","zh":"适合需要 Python 项目组织和模块架构最佳实践的代码分析代理","ja":"Python プロジェクトの組織化とモジュールアーキテクチャのベストプラクティスを必要とするコード分析エージェントに最適","ko":"파이썬 프로젝트 조직과 모듈 아키텍처의 모범 사례가 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren las mejores prácticas en la organización de proyectos y arquitectura de módulos de Python","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant les meilleures pratiques dans l''organisation de projets et l''architecture de modules Python","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die beste Praktiken in der Python-Projektorganisation und Modularchitektur erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem boas práticas na organização de projetos Python e arquitetura de módulos","ru":"Идеально для Агентов Анализа Кодов, требующих лучших практик в организации проектов Python и архитектуры модулей","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يتطلب أفضل الممارسات في تنظيم مشاريع بايثون وهندسة الوحدات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design well-organized Python projects with clear module boundaries, explicit public interfaces using `__all__`, and maintainable directory structures, making code discoverable and changes predictable","zh":"赋予代理设计良好组织的 Python 项目的能力，具有清晰的模块边界、使用 `__all__` 的显式公共接口和可维护的目录结构，使代码可发现和变化可预测","ja":"エージェントが明確なモジュール境界、`__all__` を使用した明示的なパブリックインターフェイス、および保守可能なディレクトリ構造を持つ Python プロジェクトを設計できるようにし、コードを発見可能にし、変更を予測可能にする","ko":"에이전트가 명확한 모듈 경계, `__all__`를 사용한 명시적인 공개 인터페이스 및 유지 보수 가능한 디렉토리 구조를 갖는 파이썬 프로젝트를 설계할 수 있도록 하여 코드를 발견 가능하게 하고 변경을 예측 가능하게 함","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar proyectos de Python bien organizados con límites de módulos claros, interfaces públicas explícitas utilizando `__all__` y estructuras de directorios mantenibles, lo que hace que el código sea descubrible y los cambios sean predecibles","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des projets Python bien organisés avec des limites de modules claires, des interfaces publiques explicites utilisant `__all__` et des structures de répertoires maintenables, ce qui rend le code découvrable et les modifications prévisibles","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, gut organisierte Python-Projekte mit klaren Modulgrenzen, expliziten öffentlichen Schnittstellen unter Verwendung von `__all__` und wartbaren Verzeichnisstrukturen zu entwerfen, wodurch der Code auffindbar und Änderungen vorhersehbar werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar projetos Python bem organizados com limites de módulos claros, interfaces públicas explícitas usando `__all__` e estruturas de diretório mantidas, tornando o código descobrível e as alterações previsíveis","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать хорошо организованные проекты Python с четкими границами модулей, явными публичными интерфейсами с использованием `__all__` и поддерживаемыми структурами каталогов, что делает код открытым и изменения предсказуемыми","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية تصميم مشاريع بايثون منظمة جيدًا مع حدود وحدات واضحة وواجهات عامة صريحة باستخدام `__all__` وهيكل دليل قابل للصيانة ، مما يجعل الشفرة قابلة للكشف والتغييرات قابلة للتوقع"},"useCases":{"en":["Organizing new Python projects from scratch","Reorganizing existing codebases for clarity","Defining module public APIs","Determining optimal directory structures"],"zh":["从头开始组织新的 Python 项目","重新组织现有的代码库以提高清晰度","定义模块的公共 API","确定最佳的目录结构"],"ja":["新しい Python プロジェクトを一から整理する","既存のコードベースを再構成して明確性を高める","モジュールのパブリック API を定義する","最適なディレクトリ構造を決定する"],"ko":["새로운 파이썬 프로젝트를 처음부터 조직화","기존 코드베이스를 재구성하여 명확성을 높임","모듈의 공개 API를 정의","최적의 디렉토리 구조를 결정"],"es":["Organizar nuevos proyectos de Python desde cero","Reorganizar las bases de código existentes para mayor claridad","Definir APIs públicas de módulos","Determinar estructuras de directorios óptimas"],"fr":["Organiser de nouveaux projets Python à partir de zéro","Réorganiser les bases de code existantes pour plus de clarté","Définir les API publiques de modules","Déterminer les structures de répertoires optimales"],"de":["Neue Python-Projekte von Grund auf organisieren","Bestehende Codebasen für bessere Klarheit neu organisieren","Öffentliche Modul-APIs definieren","Optimale Verzeichnisstrukturen bestimmen"],"pt":["Organizar novos projetos Python do zero","Reorganizar codebases existentes para clareza","Definir APIs públicas de módulos","Determinar estruturas de diretório ótimas"],"ru":["Организация новых проектов Python с нуля","Перестановка существующих кодовых баз для ясности","Определение публичных API-модулей","Определение оптимальных структур каталогов"],"ar":["تنظيم مشاريع بايثون جديدة من الصفر","إعادة تنظيم قواعد الشفرة الحالية للوضوح","تحديد واجهات برمجة تطبيقات عامة للوحدات","تحديد هياكل دليل مثالية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python project setup","Limited to Python projects only"],"zh":["需要 Python 项目设置","仅限 Python 项目"],"ja":["Python プロジェクトの設定が必要","Python プロジェクトのみに限定"],"ko":["파이썬 프로젝트 설정이 필요","파이썬 프로젝트에만 한정"],"es":["Requiere configuración de proyecto de Python","Limitado solo a proyectos de Python"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de projet Python","Limité uniquement aux projets Python"],"de":["Benötigt Python-Projektsetup","Begrenzt auf Python-Projekte nur"],"pt":["Exige configuração de projeto Python","Limitado a projetos Python apenas"],"ru":["Требует настройки проекта Python","Ограничен только проектами Python"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مشروع بايثون","محدود بمشاريع بايثون فقط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
