],"pt":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","Sistemas escaláveis","Sistemas mantenedores","Arquitetura de backend"],"ru":["Чистая Архитектура","Шестиугольная Архитектура","Дизайн, ориентированный на домен","Масштабируемые системы","Поддерживаемые системы","Архитектура backend"],"ar":["هندسة نظيفة","هندسة سداسية","تصميم مثير للموضوع","أنظمة قابلة للتوسعة","أنظمة قابلة للصيانة","هندسة الخلفية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["后端架构模式","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","软件架构","系统设计","可维护性","可测试性","可扩展性"],"ja":["バックエンドアーキテクチャパターン","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ","システム設計","メンテナンス可能","テスト可能","スケーラブル"],"ko":["백엔드 아키텍처 패턴","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","소프트웨어 아키텍처","시스템 설계","유지 보수 가능","테스트 가능","확장 가능"],"es":["patrones de arquitectura","arquitectura de backend","clean architecture","domain-driven design","hexagonal architecture","sistemas mantenibles","sistemas escalables","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["modèles d''architecture","architecture de backend","clean architecture","domain-driven design","hexagonal architecture","systèmes maintenables","systèmes évolutifs","développement de logiciels"],"de":["architekturmuster","backend-architektur","clean architecture","domain-driven design","hexagonal architecture","wartbare systeme","skalierbare systeme","software-entwicklung"],"pt":["padrões de arquitetura de backend","arquitetura de software","desenvolvimento de software","sistemas escaláveis","sistemas mantenedores","clean architecture","hexagonal architecture","domain-driven design"],"ru":["шаблоны архитектуры backend","архитектура программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения","масштабируемые системы","поддерживаемые системы","чистая архитектура","шестиугольная архитектура","дизайн, ориентированный на домен"],"ar":["أنماط هندسة الخلفية","هندسة البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات","أنظمة قابلة للتوسعة","أنظمة قابلة للصيانة","هندسة نظيفة","هندسة سداسية","تصميم مثير للموضوع"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"architecture-patterns","description":"Implement proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design. Use when architecting complex backend systems or refactoring existing applications for better maintainability.","bodyPreview":"# Architecture Patterns\n\nMaster proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design to build maintainable, testable, and scalable systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new backend systems from scratch\n- Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability\n- Establishing architecture standards for your team\n- Migrating from tightly coupled to loosely coupled architectures\n- Implementing domain-driven design princ","body":"# Architecture Patterns\n\nMaster proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design to build maintainable, testable, and scalable systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new backend systems from scratch\n- Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability\n- Establishing architecture standards for your team\n- Migrating from tightly coupled to loosely coupled architectures\n- Implementing domain-driven design principles\n- Creating testable and mockable codebases\n- Planning microservices decomposition\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Clean Architecture (Uncle Bob)\n\n**Layers (dependency flows inward):**\n\n- **Entities**: Core business models\n- **Use Cases**: Application business rules\n- **Interface Adapters**: Controllers, presenters, gateways\n- **Frameworks & Drivers**: UI, database, external services\n\n**Key Principles:**\n\n- Dependencies point inward\n- Inner layers know nothing about outer layers\n- Business logic independent of frameworks\n- Testable without UI, database, or external services\n\n### 2. Hexagonal Architecture (Ports and Adapters)\n\n**Components:**\n\n- **Domain Core**: Business logic\n- **Ports**: Interfaces defining interactions\n- **Adapters**: Implementations of ports (database, REST, message queue)\n\n**Benefits:**\n\n- Swap implementations easily (mock for testing)\n- Technology-agnostic core\n- Clear separation of concerns\n\n### 3. Domain-Driven Design (DDD)\n\n**Strategic Patterns:**\n\n- **Bounded Contexts**: Separate models for different domains\n- **Context Mapping**: How contexts relate\n- **Ubiquitous Language**: Shared terminology\n\n**Tactical Patterns:**\n\n- **Entities**: Objects with identity\n- **Value Objects**: Immutable objects defined by attributes\n- **Aggregates**: Consistency boundaries\n- **Repositories**: Data access abstraction\n- **Domain Events**: Things that happened\n\n## Clean Architecture Pattern\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\napp/\n├── domain/           # Entities & business rules\n│   ├── entities/\n│   │   ├── user.py\n│   │   └── order.py\n│   ├── value_objects/\n│   │   ├── email.py\n│   │   └── money.py\n│   └── interfaces/   # Abstract interfaces\n│       ├── user_repository.py\n│       └── payment_gateway.py\n├── use_cases/        # Application business rules\n│   ├── create_user.py\n│   ├── process_order.py\n│   └── send_notification.py\n├── adapters/         # Interface implementations\n│   ├── repositories/\n│   │   ├── postgres_user_repository.py\n│   │   └── redis_cache_repository.py\n│   ├── controllers/\n│   │   └── user_controller.py\n│   └── gateways/\n│       ├── stripe_payment_gateway.py\n│       └── sendgrid_email_gateway.py\n└── infrastructure/   # Framework & external concerns\n    ├── database.py\n    ├── config.py\n    └── logging.py\n```\n\n### Implementation Example\n\n```python\n# domain/entities/user.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass\nclass User:\n    \"\"\"Core user entity - no framework dependencies.\"\"\"\n    id: str\n    email: str\n    name: str\n    created_at: datetime\n    is_active: bool = True\n\n    def deactivate(self):\n        \"\"\"Business rule: deactivating user.\"\"\"\n        self.is_active = False\n\n    def can_place_order(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Business rule: active users can order.\"\"\"\n        return self.is_active\n\n# domain/interfaces/user_repository.py\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\n\nclass IUserRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Port: defines contract, no implementation.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def find_by_id(self, user_id: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def find_by_email(self, email: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def save(self, user: User) -> User:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def delete(self, user_id: str) -> bool:\n        pass\n\n# use_cases/create_user.py\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\nfrom domain.interfaces.user_repository import IUserRepository\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport uuid\n\n@dataclass\nclass CreateUserRequest:\n    email: str\n    name: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass CreateUserResponse:\n    user: User\n    success: bool\n    error: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass CreateUserUseCase:\n    \"\"\"Use case: orchestrates business logic.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, user_repository: IUserRepository):\n        self.user_repository = user_repository\n\n    async def execute(self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> CreateUserResponse:\n        # Business validation\n        existing = await self.user_repository.find_by_email(request.email)\n        if existing:\n            return CreateUserResponse(\n                user=None,\n                success=False,\n                error=\"Email already exists\"\n            )\n\n        # Create entity\n        user = User(\n            id=str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            email=request.email,\n            name=request.name,\n            created_at=datetime.now(),\n            is_active=True\n        )\n\n        # Persist\n        saved_user = await self.user_repository.save(user)\n\n        return CreateUserResponse(\n            user=saved_user,\n            success=True\n        )\n\n# adapters/repositories/postgres_user_repository.py\nfrom domain.interfaces.user_repository import IUserRepository\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\nfrom typing import Optional\nimport asyncpg\n\nclass PostgresUserRepository(IUserRepository):\n    \"\"\"Adapter: PostgreSQL implementation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, pool: asyncpg.Pool):\n        self.pool = pool\n\n    async def find_by_id(self, user_id: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\", user_id\n            )\n            return self._to_entity(row) if row else None\n\n    async def find_by_email(self, email: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1\", email\n            )\n            return self._to_entity(row) if row else None\n\n    async def save(self, user: User) -> User:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            await conn.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at, is_active)\n                VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n                ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE\n                SET email = $2, name = $3, is_active = $5\n                \"\"\",\n                user.id, user.email, user.name, user.created_at, user.is_active\n            )\n            return user\n\n    async def delete(self, user_id: str) -> bool:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            result = await conn.execute(\n                \"DELETE FROM users WHERE id = $1\", user_id\n            )\n            return result == \"DELETE 1\"\n\n    def _to_entity(self, row) -> User:\n        \"\"\"Map database row to entity.\"\"\"\n        return User(\n            id=row[\"id\"],\n            email=row[\"email\"],\n            name=row[\"name\"],\n            created_at=row[\"created_at\"],\n            is_active=row[\"is_active\"]\n        )\n\n# adapters/controllers/user_controller.py\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException\nfrom use_cases.create_user import CreateUserUseCase, CreateUserRequest\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\nclass CreateUserDTO(BaseModel):\n    email: str\n    name: str\n\n@router.post(\"/users\")\nasync def create_user(\n    dto: CreateUserDTO,\n    use_case: CreateUserUseCase = Depends(get_create_user_use_case)\n):\n    \"\"\"Controller: handles HTTP concerns only.\"\"\"\n    request = CreateUserRequest(email=dto.email, name=dto.name)\n    response = await use_case.execute(request)\n\n    if not response.success:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=response.error)\n\n    return {\"user\": response.user}\n```\n\n## Hexagonal Architecture Pattern\n\n```python\n# Core domain (hexagon center)\nclass OrderService:\n    \"\"\"Domain service - no infrastructure dependencies.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        order_repository: OrderRepositoryPort,\n        payment_gateway: PaymentGatewayPort,\n        notification_service: NotificationPort\n    ):\n        self.orders = order_repository\n        self.payments = payment_gateway\n        self.notifications = notification_service\n\n    async def place_order(self, order: Order) -> OrderResult:\n        # Business logic\n        if not order.is_valid():\n            return OrderResult(success=False, error=\"Invalid order\")\n\n        # Use ports (interfaces)\n        payment = await self.payments.charge(\n            amount=order.total,\n            customer=order.customer_id\n        )\n\n        if not payment.success:\n            return OrderResult(success=False, error=\"Payment failed\")\n\n        order.mark_as_paid()\n        saved_order = await self.orders.save(order)\n\n        await self.notifications.send(\n            to=order.customer_email,\n            subject=\"Order confirmed\",\n            body=f\"Order {order.id} confirmed\"\n        )\n\n        return OrderResult(success=True, order=saved_order)\n\n# Ports (interfaces)\nclass OrderRepositoryPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def save(self, order: Order) -> Order:\n        pass\n\nclass PaymentGatewayPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        pass\n\nclass NotificationPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def send(self, to: str, subject: str, body: str):\n        pass\n\n# Adapters (implementations)\nclass StripePaymentAdapter(PaymentGatewayPort):\n    \"\"\"Primary adapter: connects to Stripe API.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, api_key: str):\n        self.stripe = stripe\n        self.stripe.api_key = api_key\n\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        try:\n            charge = self.stripe.Charge.create(\n                amount=amount.cents,\n                currency=amount.currency,\n                customer=customer\n            )\n            return PaymentResult(success=True, transaction_id=charge.id)\n        except stripe.error.CardError as e:\n            return PaymentResult(success=False, error=str(e))\n\nclass MockPaymentAdapter(PaymentGatewayPort):\n    \"\"\"Test adapter: no external dependencies.\"\"\"\n\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        return PaymentResult(success=True, transaction_id=\"mock-123\")\n```\n\n## Domain-Driven Design Pattern\n\n```python\n# Value Objects (immutable)\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Email:\n    \"\"\"Value object: validated email.\"\"\"\n    value: str\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        if \"@\" not in self.value:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid email\")\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Money:\n    \"\"\"Value object: amount with currency.\"\"\"\n    amount: int  # cents\n    currency: str\n\n    def add(self, other: \"Money\") -> \"Money\":\n        if self.currency != other.currency:\n            raise ValueError(\"Currency mismatch\")\n        return Money(self.amount + other.amount, self.currency)\n\n# Entities (with identity)\nclass Order:\n    \"\"\"Entity: has identity, mutable state.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, id: str, customer: Customer):\n        self.id = id\n        self.customer = customer\n        self.items: List[OrderItem] = []\n        self.status = OrderStatus.PENDING\n        self._events: List[DomainEvent] = []\n\n    def add_item(self, product: Product, quantity: int):\n        \"\"\"Business logic in entity.\"\"\"\n        item = OrderItem(product, quantity)\n        self.items.append(item)\n        self._events.append(ItemAddedEvent(self.id, item))\n\n    def total(self) -> Money:\n        \"\"\"Calculated property.\"\"\"\n        return sum(item.subtotal() for item in self.items)\n\n    def submit(self):\n        \"\"\"State transition with business rules.\"\"\"\n        if not self.items:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot submit empty order\")\n        if self.status != OrderStatus.PENDING:\n            raise ValueError(\"Order already submitted\")\n\n        self.status = OrderStatus.SUBMITTED\n        self._events.append(OrderSubmittedEvent(self.id))\n\n# Aggregates (consistency boundary)\nclass Customer:\n    \"\"\"Aggregate root: controls access to entities.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, id: str, email: Email):\n        self.id = id\n        self.email = email\n        self._addresses: List[Address] = []\n        self._orders: List[str] = []  # Order IDs, not full objects\n\n    def add_address(self, address: Address):\n        \"\"\"Aggregate enforces invariants.\"\"\"\n        if len(self._addresses) >= 5:\n            raise ValueError(\"Maximum 5 addresses allowed\")\n        self._addresses.append(address)\n\n    @property\n    def primary_address(self) -> Optional[Address]:\n        return next((a for a in self._addresses if a.is_primary), None)\n\n# Domain Events\n@dataclass\nclass OrderSubmittedEvent:\n    order_id: str\n    occurred_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.now)\n\n# Repository (aggregate persistence)\nclass OrderRepository:\n    \"\"\"Repository: persist/retrieve aggregates.\"\"\"\n\n    async def find_by_id(self, order_id: str) -> Optional[Order]:\n        \"\"\"Reconstitute aggregate from storage.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    async def save(self, order: Order):\n        \"\"\"Persist aggregate and publish events.\"\"\"\n        await self._persist(order)\n        await self._publish_events(order._events)\n        order._events.clear()\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/clean-architecture-guide.md**: Detailed layer breakdown\n- **references/hexagonal-architecture-guide.md**: Ports and adapters patterns\n- **references/ddd-tactical-patterns.md**: Entities, value objects, aggregates\n- **assets/clean-architecture-template/**: Complete project structure\n- **assets/ddd-examples/**: Domain modeling examples\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Dependency Rule**: Dependencies always point inward\n2. **Interface Segregation**: Small, focused interfaces\n3. **Business Logic in Domain**: Keep frameworks out of core\n4. **Test Independence**: Core testable without infrastructure\n5. **Bounded Contexts**: Clear domain boundaries\n6. **Ubiquitous Language**: Consistent terminology\n7. **Thin Controllers**: Delegate to use cases\n8. **Rich Domain Models**: Behavior with data\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Anemic Domain**: Entities with only data, no behavior\n- **Framework Coupling**: Business logic depends on frameworks\n- **Fat Controllers**: Business logic in controllers\n- **Repository Leakage**: Exposing ORM objects\n- **Missing Abstractions**: Concrete dependencies in core\n- **Over-Engineering**: Clean architecture for simple CRUD\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:30:35.064Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Software Development Agents requiring expertise in Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design for scalable system development.","zh":"适合需要精通 Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture 和 Domain-Driven Design 的软件开发代理，以实现可扩展的系统开发。","ja":"Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture、Domain-Driven Design に精通していることが求められるソフトウェア開発エージェントに最適で、拡張可能なシステム開発が可能です。","ko":"Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture 및 Domain-Driven Design 에 대한 전문 지식이 필요한 소프트웨어 개발 에이전트에게 적합하여 확장 가능한 시스템 개발을 위한 것입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo de software que requieren experiencia en Arquitectura Limpia, Arquitectura Hexagonal y Diseño Dirigido por Dominio para el desarrollo de sistemas escalables.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement de logiciels nécessitant une expertise en Architecture Propre, Architecture Hexagonale et Conception Pilotée par le Domaine pour le développement de systèmes évolutifs.","de":"Ideal für Software-Entwicklungsagenten, die Expertenwissen in Clean Architecture, Hexagonaler Architektur und Domain-Driven Design für die Entwicklung von skalierbaren Systemen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Software que requerem especialização em Arquitetura Limpa, Arquitetura Hexagonal e Projeto Dirigido por Domínio para o desenvolvimento de sistemas escaláveis.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по разработке программного обеспечения, требующих экспертизы в области Чистой Архитектуры, Гексагональной Архитектуры и Проектирования, Ориентированного на Домен, для разработки масштабируемых систем.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الذين يتطلبون خبرة في هندسة البرمجيات التي تتطلب خبرة في الهندسة المعمارية النظيفة والهندسة السداسية والتصميم الموجه بالمشكل لتنمية نظام قابل للتوسعة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design maintainable, testable, and scalable backend systems using proven architecture patterns, including Clean Architecture and Domain-Driven Design, facilitating the implementation of loosely coupled architectures and migration from monolithic applications.","zh":"赋予代理设计可维护、可测试和可扩展的后端系统的能力，使用经过验证的架构模式，包括 Clean Architecture 和 Domain-Driven Design，促进松散耦合架构的实现和从单体应用程序迁移。","ja":"Clean Architecture と Domain-Driven Design を含む検証済みのアーキテクチャパターンを使用して、保守可能なテスト可能な拡張可能なバックエンドシステムを設計するエージェントの能力を付与し、疎結合アーキテクチャの実装とモノリシックアプリケーションからの移行を促進します。","ko":"검증된 아키텍처 패턴을 사용하여 유지 보수 가능하고 테스트 가능하며 확장 가능한 백엔드 시스템을 설계할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하여 Clean Architecture 및 Domain-Driven Design를 포함하여 느슨하게 결합된 아키텍처의 구현 및 단일 응용 프로그램에서 마이그레이션을促進합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar sistemas de backend mantenibles, probables y escalables utilizando patrones de arquitectura comprobados, incluyendo Arquitectura Limpia y Diseño Dirigido por Dominio, facilitando la implementación de arquitecturas acopladas sueltas y la migración desde aplicaciones monolíticas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des systèmes backend maintenables, testables et évolutifs en utilisant des modèles d''architecture éprouvés, notamment l''Architecture Propre et la Conception Pilotée par le Domaine, facilitant la mise en œuvre d''architectures déchargées et la migration à partir d''applications monolithiques.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, wartbare, testbare und skalierbare Backendsysteme mithilfe bewährter Architekturmuster, einschließlich Clean Architecture und Domain-Driven Design, zu entwerfen, wodurch die Implementierung lose gekoppelter Architekturen und die Migration von monolithischen Anwendungen erleichtert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar sistemas de backend mantidos, testáveis e escaláveis usando padrões de arquitetura comprovados, incluindo Arquitetura Limpa e Projeto Dirigido por Domínio, facilitando a implementação de arquiteturas acopladas soltas e a migração de aplicações monolíticas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать поддерживаемые, тестируемые и масштабируемые системы бэкенда с помощью проверенных шаблонов архитектуры, включая Чистую Архитектуру и Проектирование, Ориентированное на Домен, что облегчает реализацию слабо связанных архитектур и миграцию из монолитных приложений.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تصميم أنظمة خلفية قابلة للصيانة وقابلة للاختبار وقابلة للتوسعة باستخدام أنماط معمارية مثبتة، بما في ذلك الهندسة المعمارية النظيفة والتصميم الموجه بالمشكل، مما يسهل تنفيذ الهندسة المعمارية المرتبطة بشكل فضفاض وانتقال التطبيقات أحادية القطعة."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing new backend systems from scratch with Clean Architecture","Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability using Hexagonal Architecture","Establishing architecture standards for development teams based on Domain-Driven Design principles"],"zh":["使用 Clean Architecture 从头开始设计新的后端系统","使用 Hexagonal Architecture 重构单体应用程序以提高可维护性","根据 Domain-Driven Design 原则为开发团队建立架构标准"],"ja":["Clean Architecture を使用して新しいバックエンドシステムを一から設計する","Hexagonal Architecture を使用してモノリシックアプリケーションをリファクタリングして保守性を高める","Domain-Driven Design の原則に基づいて開発チームのアーキテクチャスタンダードを確立する"],"ko":["Clean Architecture를 사용하여 새로운 백엔드 시스템을 처음부터 설계합니다.","Hexagonal Architecture를 사용하여 유지 보수성을 개선하기 위해 단일 응용 프로그램을 리팩토링합니다.","Domain-Driven Design 원칙에 따라 개발 팀을 위한 아키텍처 표준을 설정합니다."],"es":["Diseñar nuevos sistemas de backend desde cero con Arquitectura Limpia","Reestructurar aplicaciones monolíticas para una mejor mantenibilidad utilizando Arquitectura Hexagonal","Establecer estándares de arquitectura para equipos de desarrollo basados en principios de Diseño Dirigido por Dominio"],"fr":["Concevoir de nouveaux systèmes backend à partir de zéro avec l''Architecture Propre","Réaménager des applications monolithiques pour une meilleure maintenabilité en utilisant l''Architecture Hexagonale","Établir des normes d''architecture pour les équipes de développement basées sur les principes de Conception Pilotée par le Domaine"],"de":["Neue Backendsysteme von Grund auf mit Clean Architecture entwerfen","Monolithische Anwendungen für eine bessere Wartbarkeit mit Hilfe der Hexagonalen Architektur neu strukturieren","Architekturstandards für Entwicklungsteams auf Basis von Domain-Driven-Design-Prinzipien etablieren"],"pt":["Projetar novos sistemas de backend do zero com Arquitetura Limpa","Reestruturar aplicações monolíticas para melhor manutenção usando Arquitetura Hexagonal","Estabelecer padrões de arquitetura para equipes de desenvolvimento com base nos princípios do Projeto Dirigido por Domínio"],"ru":["Проектировать новые системы бэкенда с нуля с помощью Чистой Архитектуры","Рефакторинг монолитных приложений для лучшей поддерживаемости с помощью Гексагональной Архитектуры","Устанавливать архитектурные стандарты для команд разработки на основе принципов Проектирования, Ориентированного на Домен"],"ar":["تصميم أنظمة خلفية جديدة من الصفر باستخدام الهندسة المعمارية النظيفة","إعادة هيكلة التطبيقات أحادية القطعة لتحسين الصيانة باستخدام الهندسة المعمارية السداسية","تحديد معايير هندسية لمجموعات التطوير بناءً على مبادئ التصميم الموجه بالمشكل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires expertise in software development and architecture","Limited to backend system development","May require additional knowledge for implementation in specific programming languages or frameworks"],"zh":["需要软件开发和架构方面的专业知识","仅限于后端系统开发","可能需要额外的知识来实现特定的编程语言或框架"],"ja":["ソフトウェア開発およびアーキテクチャに関する専門知識が必要","バックエンドシステム開発のみに限定される","特定のプログラミング言語またはフレームワークの実装には追加の知識が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["소프트웨어 개발 및 아키텍처 분야의 전문 지식이 필요합니다.","백엔드 시스템 개발에만 제한됩니다.","특정 프로그래밍 언어 또는 프레임워크의 구현을 위해서는 추가적인 지식이 필요할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere experiencia en desarrollo de software y arquitectura","Limitado al desarrollo de sistemas de backend","Puede requerir conocimientos adicionales para la implementación en lenguajes de programación o marcos específicos"],"fr":["Nécessite une expertise en développement de logiciels et en architecture","Limité au développement de systèmes backend","Peut nécessiter des connaissances supplémentaires pour la mise en œuvre dans des langages de programmation ou des cadres spécifiques"],"de":["Erfordert Expertenwissen in Softwareentwicklung und Architektur","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von Backendsystemen","Kann zusätzliches Wissen für die Implementierung in bestimmten Programmiersprachen oder Frameworks erfordern"],"pt":["Requer especialização em desenvolvimento de software e arquitetura","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de sistemas de backend","Pode requerer conhecimento adicional para implementação em linguagens de programação ou estruturas específicas"],"ru":["Требует экспертизы в области разработки программного обеспечения и архитектуры","Ограничен разработкой систем бэкенда","Может потребовать дополнительных знаний для реализации в конкретных языках программирования или фреймворках"],"ar":["يتطلب خبرة في مجال هندسة البرمجيات والهندسة المعمارية","محدود بالتنمية الأنظمة الخلفية","يمكن أن يتطلب معارف إضافية للتنفيذ بلغات برمجة أو إطارات عمل معينة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ryolambert/kiro-wiz/kiro-agent-schema', 'community', 'ryolambert', 'kiro-wiz', 'ryolambert/kiro-wiz', 'kiro-agent-schema', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z', '2026-02-18T13:30:11.391Z', NULL, '{"id":"ryolambert/kiro-wiz/kiro-agent-schema","name":"kiro-agent-schema","description":{"zh":"Kiro Agent 配置模式是一种 JSON 格式的配置文件，用于定义 Agent 的属性和行为","ja":"Kiro エージェント構成スキーマは、エージェントの属性と動作を定義する JSON 形式の構成ファイルです","ko":"키로 에이전트 구성 스키마는 에이전트의 속성과 행동을 정의하는 JSON 형식의 구성 파일입니다","es":"El esquema de configuración de Kiro Agent permite personalizar tus agentes con facilidad. Configura tus agentes con nuestro esquema","fr":"Le schéma de configuration de Kiro Agent permet de personnaliser vos agents avec facilité. Configurez vos agents avec notre schéma","de":"Das Konfigurationsschema von Kiro Agent ermöglicht es, Ihre Agenten leicht anzupassen. Konfigurieren Sie Ihre Agenten mit unserem Schema","pt":"O esquema de configuração do Kiro Agent é um arquivo JSON que define as configurações do agente, incluindo nome, descrição e ferramentas disponíveis.","ru":"Схема конфигурации Kiro Agent - это файл JSON, который определяет настройки агента, включая имя, описание и доступные инструменты.","ar":"مخطط تعريف الوكيل Kiro هو ملف JSON يحدد إعدادات الوكيل، بما في ذلك الاسم والوصف والأدوات المتاحة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Kiro Agent 配置模式","ja":"Kiro エージェント構成スキーマ","ko":"키로 에이전트 구성 스키마","es":"Esquema de configuración de Kiro Agent","fr":"Schéma de configuration de Kiro Agent","de":"Kiro-Agent-Konfigurationsschema","pt":"Esquema de Configuração do Kiro Agent","ru":"Схема конфигурации Kiro Agent","ar":"مخطط تعريف الوكيل Kiro","en":"kiro-agent-schema"},"description":{"zh":"Kiro Agent 配置模式是一种 JSON 格式的配置文件，用于定义 Agent 的属性和行为","ja":"Kiro エージェント構成スキーマは、エージェントの属性と動作を定義する JSON 形式の構成ファイルです","ko":"키로 에이전트 구성 스키마는 에이전트의 속성과 행동을 정의하는 JSON 형식의 구성 파일입니다","es":"El esquema de configuración de Kiro Agent permite personalizar tus agentes con facilidad. Configura tus agentes con nuestro esquema","fr":"Le schéma de configuration de Kiro Agent permet de personnaliser vos agents avec facilité. Configurez vos agents avec notre schéma","de":"Das Konfigurationsschema von Kiro Agent ermöglicht es, Ihre Agenten leicht anzupassen. Konfigurieren Sie Ihre Agenten mit unserem Schema","pt":"O esquema de configuração do Kiro Agent é um arquivo JSON que define as configurações do agente, incluindo nome, descrição e ferramentas disponíveis.","ru":"Схема конфигурации Kiro Agent - это файл JSON, который определяет настройки агента, включая имя, описание и доступные инструменты.","ar":"مخطط تعريف الوكيل Kiro هو ملف JSON يحدد إعدادات الوكيل، بما في ذلك الاسم والوصف والأدوات المتاحة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持本地和全局配置文件","定义 Agent 的名称和描述","指定系统提示和工具","支持文件路径和内联提示"],"ja":["ローカルとグローバル構成ファイルをサポート","エージェントの名前と説明を定義","システムプロンプトとツールを指定","ファイルパスとインラインプロンプトをサポート"],"ko":["로컬과 글로벌 구성 파일 지원","에이전트의 이름과 설명 정의","시스템 프롬프트와 툴 지정","파일 경로와 인라인 프롬프트 지원"],"es":["Configuración de agentes personalizados","Esquema de configuración flexible","Soporte para herramientas y promts","Configuración local y global","Priorización de configuración local"],"fr":["Configuration d''agents personnalisés","Schéma de configuration flexible","Prise en charge d''outils et de promts","Configuration locale et globale","Priorisation de la configuration locale"],"de":["Konfiguration von benutzerdefinierten Agenten","Flexibles Konfigurationsschema","Unterstützung für Tools und Prompts","Lokale und globale Konfiguration","Priorisierung der lokalen Konfiguration"],"pt":["Definição de nome e descrição do agente","Especificação de ferramentas disponíveis","Configuração de prompt do sistema","Suporte a arquivos de configuração local e global","Precedência de configuração local sobre global"],"ru":["Определение имени и описания агента","Указание доступных инструментов","Настройка системного промпта","Поддержка локальных и глобальных файлов конфигурации","Приоритет локальной конфигурации над глобальной"],"ar":["تحديد اسم ووصف الوكيل","تحديد الأدوات المتاحة","تكوين سؤال النظام","دعم ملفات التكوين المحلية والعالمية","السماح للتكوين المحلي بال優 tiên على التكوين العالمي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kiro Agent","配置模式","JSON 配置","Agent 属性","开发效率","配置文件"],"ja":["Kiro エージェント","構成スキーマ","JSON 構成","エージェント属性","開発効率","構成ファイル"],"ko":["키로 에이전트","구성 스키마","JSON 구성","에이전트 속성","개발 효율성","구성 파일"],"es":["Kiro Agent","esquema de configuración","configuración de agentes","personalización de agentes","herramientas de desarrollo","prompts de sistema"],"fr":["Kiro Agent","schéma de configuration","configuration d''agents","personnalisation d''agents","outils de développement","prompts de système"],"de":["Kiro Agent","Konfigurationsschema","Konfiguration von Agenten","Anpassung von Agenten","Entwicklungstools","Systemprompts"],"pt":["Kiro Agent","esquema de configuração","arquivo JSON","desenvolvedores","ferramentas","configuração de sistema","prompt do sistema","arquivos de configuração"],"ru":["Kiro Agent","схема конфигурации","файл JSON","разработчики","инструменты","настройка системы","системный промпт","файлы конфигурации"],"ar":["الوكيل Kiro","مخطط التكوين","ملف JSON","المطورون","الأدوات","تكوين النظام","سؤال النظام","ملفات التكوين"]}},"owner":"ryolambert","repo":"kiro-wiz","repoPath":"ryolambert/kiro-wiz","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kiro-agent-schema","description":"Complete Kiro agent configuration schema reference. Use when creating or modifying agent JSON configs.","bodyPreview":"# Kiro Agent Configuration Schema\n\n## File Location\n- Local: `.kiro/agents/<name>.json`\n- Global: `~/.kiro/agents/<name>.json`\n- Local takes precedence over global with same name\n\n## Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\n| name | string | yes | Agent identifier |\n| description | string | no | Human-readable description |\n| prompt | string | no | System prompt (inline or `file:///path`) |\n| tools | array | no | Available tool names |\n| allowed","body":"# Kiro Agent Configuration Schema\n\n## File Location\n- Local: `.kiro/agents/<name>.json`\n- Global: `~/.kiro/agents/<name>.json`\n- Local takes precedence over global with same name\n\n## Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\n| name | string | yes | Agent identifier |\n| description | string | no | Human-readable description |\n| prompt | string | no | System prompt (inline or `file:///path`) |\n| tools | array | no | Available tool names |\n| allowedTools | array | no | Auto-approved tools (supports wildcards) |\n| toolsSettings | object | no | Per-tool configuration |\n| resources | array | no | Context files (`file://` and `skill://` URIs) |\n| hooks | object | no | Commands at trigger points |\n| mcpServers | object | no | MCP server configurations |\n| toolAliases | object | no | Remap tool names |\n| model | string | no | Model ID override |\n| keyboardShortcut | string | no | Keyboard shortcut (e.g., `ctrl+shift+a`) |\n| welcomeMessage | string | no | Message shown on agent switch |\n| useLegacyMcpJson | boolean | no | Include legacy MCP configs |\n\n## Tool Names\nBuilt-in: `fs_read`, `fs_write`, `execute_bash`, `grep`, `glob`, `code`, `use_aws`, `introspect`, `knowledge`, `thinking`, `todo_list`, `delegate`\n\n## allowedTools Patterns\n- Exact: `\"fs_read\"`\n- Wildcard: `\"fs_*\"`, `\"*_bash\"`\n- MCP tool: `\"@server/tool_name\"`, `\"@server/read_*\"`\n- All MCP: `\"@server\"`\n- All built-in: `\"@builtin\"`\n\n## Hook Triggers\n- `agentSpawn` — agent initializes\n- `userPromptSubmit` — user sends message\n- `preToolUse` — before tool (supports `matcher`)\n- `postToolUse` — after tool (supports `matcher`)\n- `stop` — assistant finishes\n\n## Resources URI Schemes\n- `file://path` — always loaded\n- `skill://path` — progressively loaded (requires YAML frontmatter)\n- Both support glob patterns\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:30:11.391Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Configuration-Driven Agents requiring structured, multi-location schema management.","zh":"适用于需要结构化、多位置模式管理的配置驱动代理。","ja":"構成駆動型エージェントが構造化された、マルチロケーションのスキーマ管理を必要とする場合に不可欠です。","ko":"구성 드리븐 에이전트가 구조화된 다중 위치 스키마 관리를 필요로 하는 경우에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para Agentes Dirigidos por Configuración que requieren gestión de esquemas estructurados y multilocalización.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents Dirigés par Configuration nécessitant une gestion de schémas structurés et multilocalisés.","de":"Wesentlich für konfigurationsgesteuerte Agenten, die eine strukturierte, mehrörtliche Schemaverwaltung erfordern.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes Dirigidos por Configuração que exigem gerenciamento de esquema estruturado e multi-localização.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов, управляемых конфигурацией, требующих структурированного управления схемами в нескольких местах.","ar":"ضروري للوكلاء الموجهين بالتكوين الذين يتطلبون إدارة مخططات متعددة المواقع ومنظمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables hierarchical agent configuration management with local (.kiro/agents/) overriding global (~/.kiro/agents/) definitions. Provides structured schema validation for agent identity (name), behavior (prompt), and capabilities (tools) through JSON-based configuration files.","zh":"实现了层次化的代理配置管理，局部(.kiro/agents/)配置覆盖全局(~/.kiro/agents/)定义。通过基于JSON的配置文件，为代理身份（名称）、行为（提示）和能力（工具）提供了结构化的模式验证。","ja":"階層型エージェント構成管理を可能にし、ローカル(.kiro/agents/)の設定がグローバル(~/.kiro/agents/)の定義を上書きする。JSONベースの構成ファイルを介して、エージェントのID（名前）、動作（プロンプト）、および機能（ツール）に対する構造化されたスキーマの検証を提供する。","ko":"계층화된 에이전트 구성 관리를 가능하게 하며, 로컬(.kiro/agents/) 구성이 글로벌(~/.kiro/agents/) 정의를 덮어쓴다. JSON 기반의 구성 파일을 통해 에이전트의 ID(이름), 동작(프롬프트), 기능(도구)에 대한 구조화된 스키마 유효성을 제공한다.","es":"Habilita la gestión jerárquica de la configuración de los agentes con anulación local (.kiro/agents/) de las definiciones globales (~/.kiro/agents/). Proporciona una validación de esquema estructurado para la identidad del agente (nombre), el comportamiento (prompt) y las capacidades (herramientas) a través de archivos de configuración basados en JSON.","fr":"Permet la gestion hiérarchique de la configuration des agents avec écrasement local (.kiro/agents/) des définitions globales (~/.kiro/agents/). Fournit une validation de schéma structuré pour l''identité de l''agent (nom), le comportement (prompt) et les capacités (outils) via des fichiers de configuration basés sur JSON.","de":"Ermöglicht die hierarchische Konfigurationsverwaltung von Agenten mit lokaler Überschreibung (.kiro/agents/) von globalen Definitionen (~/.kiro/agents/). Bietet eine strukturierte Schemavalidierung für die Agentenidentität (Name), das Verhalten (Prompt) und die Fähigkeiten (Werkzeuge) über JSON-basierte Konfigurationsdateien.","pt":"Permite o gerenciamento hierárquico de configuração de agente com configurações locais (/.kiro/agents/) que sobrepõem as definições globais (~/.kiro/agents/). Fornece validação de esquema estruturada para identidade de agente (nome), comportamento (prompt) e capacidades (ferramentas) por meio de arquivos de configuração baseados em JSON.","ru":"Позволяет выполнять иерархическое управление конфигурацией агентов с локальными настройками (/.kiro/agents/), переопределяющими глобальные настройки (~/.kiro/agents/). Обеспечивает структурированную валидацию схемы для идентификатора агента (имя), поведения (промпт) и возможностей (инструменты) через файлы конфигурации на основе JSON.","ar":"تمكن من إدارة تكوين الوكيل الهيكلي مع الإعدادات المحلية (/.kiro/agents/) التي تتجاوز التعريفات العالمية (~/.kiro/agents/). يوفر التحقق من مخطط منظم للتعريف الوكيل (الاسم)، السلوك (التحفيز) والقدرات (أدوات) من خلال ملفات التكوين القائمة على JSON."},"useCases":{"en":["Managing agent deployment configurations","Overriding global agent settings per-project","Validating agent schema compliance"],"zh":["管理代理部署配置","覆盖每个项目的全局代理设置","验证代理模式合规性"],"ja":["エージェントのデプロイ構成を管理する","各プロジェクトごとにグローバルエージェント設定を上書きする","エージェントのスキーマのコンプライアンスを検証する"],"ko":["에이전트 배포 구성 관리","각 프로젝트별 글로벌 에이전트 설정 덮어쓰기","에이전트 스키마 준수 사항 검증"],"es":["Gestión de configuraciones de implementación de agentes","Anulación de la configuración global de los agentes por proyecto","Validación de la conformidad del esquema del agente"],"fr":["Gestion des configurations de déploiement des agents","Écrasement des paramètres d''agent globaux par projet","Validation de la conformité du schéma de l''agent"],"de":["Verwaltung von Agenten-Implementierungskonfigurationen","Überschreibung der globalen Agenten-Einstellungen pro Projekt","Validierung der Konformität des Agenten-Schemas"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de configurações de implantação de agente","Sobrescrição de configurações globais de agente por projeto","Validação da conformidade do esquema do agente"],"ru":["Управление конфигурациями развертывания агентов","Переопределение глобальных настроек агентов для каждого проекта","Проверка соответствия схемы агента"],"ar":["إدارة تكوينات نشر الوكيل","تجاوز إعدادات الوكيل العالمية لكل مشروع","التحقق من تطابق مخطط الوكيل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires filesystem access for configuration loading","Local configuration takes precedence over global","JSON schema validation required"],"zh":["需要文件系统访问以加载配置","本地配置优先于全局配置","需要JSON模式验证"],"ja":["構成の読み込みにはファイルシステムへのアクセスが必要","ローカルの構成がグローバルの構成を上書きする","JSONスキーマの検証が必要"],"ko":["구성 로딩을 위해 파일 시스템 액세스가 필요","로컬 구성이 글로벌 구성보다 우선","JSON 스키마 유효성이 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso al sistema de archivos para la carga de la configuración","La configuración local tiene prioridad sobre la configuración global","Se requiere validación de esquema JSON"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au système de fichiers pour le chargement de la configuration","La configuration locale prime sur la configuration globale","Une validation de schéma JSON est requise"],"de":["Benötigt Dateisystemzugriff für das Laden der Konfiguration","Lokale Konfiguration hat Vorrang vor der globalen Konfiguration","JSON-Schemavalidierung ist erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao sistema de arquivos para carregar configurações","A configuração local tem precedência sobre a configuração global","Validação de esquema JSON é necessária"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файловой системе для загрузки конфигураций","Локальная конфигурация имеет приоритет над глобальной конфигурацией","Требуется валидация схемы JSON"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام الملفات لتحميل التكوينات","التكوين المحلي له الأسبقية على التكوين العالمي","التحقق من صحة مخطط JSON مطلوب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
