读写责任分离的软件架构模式，能够提高读写性能和可扩展性","ja":"CQRSは、読み書きの責任を分離するソフトウェアアーキテクチャパターンであり、読み書きのパフォーマンスとスケーラビリティを向上させることができる","ko":"CQRS는 읽기/쓰기 책임을 분리하는 소프트웨어 아키텍처 패턴으로 읽기/쓰기 성능 및 확장성을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"Guía completa para implementar CQRS, separando preocupaciones de lectura y escritura, escalando lecturas de forma independiente y optimizando escenarios de c...","fr":"Guide complet pour mettre en œuvre CQRS, en séparant les préoccupations de lecture et d''écriture, en faisant évoluer les lectures de manière indépendante et ...","de":"Umfassende Anleitung zur Implementierung von CQRS, um Lese- und Schreibbelange zu trennen, Lesevorgänge unabhängig zu skalieren und komplexe Abfrageszenarien...","pt":"O CQRS é um padrão de arquitetura que separa as preocupações de leitura e escrita, melhorando a escalabilidade e o desempenho","ru":"CQRS — это шаблон архитектуры, который отделяет проблемы чтения и записи, улучшая масштабируемость и производительность","ar":"CQRS هو نمط αρχيتектуре يفصل بين اهتمامات القراءة والكتابة، مما يحسن قابلية توسيع النظام وأدائه","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["将读写责任分离","提高读写性能","优化复杂查询场景","支持事件源系统","提高可扩展性"],"ja":["読み書きの責任を分離","読み書きのパフォーマンスを向上","複雑なクエリーシナリオを最適化","イベントソーシングシステムをサポート","スケーラビリティを向上"],"ko":["읽기/쓰기 책임을 분리","읽기/쓰기 성능을 향상","복잡한 쿼리 시나리오를 최적화","이벤트 소싱 시스템을 지원","확장성을 향상"],"es":["Separación de preocupaciones de lectura y escritura","Escalado de lecturas de forma independiente","Optimización de escenarios de consulta complejos","Creación de sistemas con fuentes de eventos","Requisitos de informes de alto rendimiento"],"fr":["Séparation des préoccupations de lecture et d''écriture","Faire évoluer les lectures de manière indépendante","Optimisation des scénarios de requête complexes","Création de systèmes à sources d''événements","Exigences de rapports de haute performance"],"de":["Trennung von Lese- und Schreibbelangen","Unabhängiges Skalieren von Lesevorgängen","Optimierung komplexer Abfrageszenarien","Erstellung von ereignisgesteuerten Systemen","Anforderungen an Hochleistungsberichte"],"pt":["Separação de preocupações de leitura e escrita","Escalabilidade de leituras independentemente de escritas","Construção de sistemas baseados em eventos","Otimização de cenários de consulta complexos","Modelos de dados de leitura e escrita diferentes"],"ru":["Отделение проблем чтения и записи","Масштабируемость чтения независимо от записи","Строительство систем на основе событий","Оптимизация сложных сценариев запросов","Разные модели данных для чтения и записи"],"ar":["فصل بين اهتمامات القراءة والكتابة","توسيع قابلية القراءة独立ًا عن الكتابة","بناء أنظمة قائمة على الأحداث","تحسين سيناريوهات الاستعلام المعقدة","نماذج بيانات مختلفة للقراءة والكتابة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CQRS","软件架构","读写分离","性能优化","可扩展性","事件源系统","复杂查询"],"ja":["CQRS","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ","読み書きの分離","パフォーマンス最適化","スケーラビリティ","イベントソーシングシステム","複雑なクエリー"],"ko":["CQRS","소프트웨어 아키텍처","읽기/쓰기 분리","성능 최적화","확장성","이벤트 소싱 시스템","복잡한 쿼리"],"es":["CQRS","Arquitectura de software","Patrones de diseño","Escalabilidad","Flexibilidad","Sistemas de fuentes de eventos","Informes de alto rendimiento"],"fr":["CQRS","Architecture logicielle","Modèles de conception","Évolutivité","Flexibilité","Systèmes à sources d''événements","Rapports de haute performance"],"de":["CQRS","Software-Architektur","Entwurfsmuster","Skalierbarkeit","Flexibilität","Ereignisgesteuerte Systeme","Hochleistungsberichte"],"pt":["CQRS","Padrão de arquitetura","Escalabilidade","Desempenho","Sistemas baseados em eventos","Otimização de consultas"],"ru":["CQRS","Шаблон архитектуры","Масштабируемость","Производительность","Системы на основе событий","Оптимизация запросов"],"ar":["CQRS","نمط ΑρχيتECTURE","قابلية توسيع","أداء","أنظمة قائمة على الأحداث","تحسين الاستعلام"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cqrs-implementation","description":"Implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation for scalable architectures. Use when separating read and write models, optimizing query performance, or building event-sourced systems.","bodyPreview":"# CQRS Implementation\n\nComprehensive guide to implementing CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Separating read and write concerns\n- Scaling reads independently from writes\n- Building event-sourced systems\n- Optimizing complex query scenarios\n- Different read/write data models needed\n- High-performance reporting requirements\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. CQRS Architecture\n\n```\n                    ┌─────────────┐\n                    │   Client    │","body":"# CQRS Implementation\n\nComprehensive guide to implementing CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Separating read and write concerns\n- Scaling reads independently from writes\n- Building event-sourced systems\n- Optimizing complex query scenarios\n- Different read/write data models needed\n- High-performance reporting requirements\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. CQRS Architecture\n\n```\n                    ┌─────────────┐\n                    │   Client    │\n                    └──────┬──────┘\n                           │\n              ┌────────────┴────────────┐\n              │                         │\n              ▼                         ▼\n       ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐\n       │  Commands   │          │   Queries   │\n       │    API      │          │    API      │\n       └──────┬──────┘          └──────┬──────┘\n              │                         │\n              ▼                         ▼\n       ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐\n       │  Command    │          │   Query     │\n       │  Handlers   │          │  Handlers   │\n       └──────┬──────┘          └──────┬──────┘\n              │                         │\n              ▼                         ▼\n       ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐\n       │   Write     │─────────►│    Read     │\n       │   Model     │  Events  │   Model     │\n       └─────────────┘          └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### 2. Key Components\n\n| Component           | Responsibility                  |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| **Command**         | Intent to change state          |\n| **Command Handler** | Validates and executes commands |\n| **Event**           | Record of state change          |\n| **Query**           | Request for data                |\n| **Query Handler**   | Retrieves data from read model  |\n| **Projector**       | Updates read model from events  |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Command Infrastructure\n\n```python\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import TypeVar, Generic, Dict, Any, Type\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport uuid\n\n# Command base\n@dataclass\nclass Command:\n    command_id: str = None\n    timestamp: datetime = None\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        self.command_id = self.command_id or str(uuid.uuid4())\n        self.timestamp = self.timestamp or datetime.utcnow()\n\n\n# Concrete commands\n@dataclass\nclass CreateOrder(Command):\n    customer_id: str\n    items: list\n    shipping_address: dict\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass AddOrderItem(Command):\n    order_id: str\n    product_id: str\n    quantity: int\n    price: float\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass CancelOrder(Command):\n    order_id: str\n    reason: str\n\n\n# Command handler base\nT = TypeVar(''T'', bound=Command)\n\nclass CommandHandler(ABC, Generic[T]):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def handle(self, command: T) -> Any:\n        pass\n\n\n# Command bus\nclass CommandBus:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._handlers: Dict[Type[Command], CommandHandler] = {}\n\n    def register(self, command_type: Type[Command], handler: CommandHandler):\n        self._handlers[command_type] = handler\n\n    async def dispatch(self, command: Command) -> Any:\n        handler = self._handlers.get(type(command))\n        if not handler:\n            raise ValueError(f\"No handler for {type(command).__name__}\")\n        return await handler.handle(command)\n\n\n# Command handler implementation\nclass CreateOrderHandler(CommandHandler[CreateOrder]):\n    def __init__(self, order_repository, event_store):\n        self.order_repository = order_repository\n        self.event_store = event_store\n\n    async def handle(self, command: CreateOrder) -> str:\n        # Validate\n        if not command.items:\n            raise ValueError(\"Order must have at least one item\")\n\n        # Create aggregate\n        order = Order.create(\n            customer_id=command.customer_id,\n            items=command.items,\n            shipping_address=command.shipping_address\n        )\n\n        # Persist events\n        await self.event_store.append_events(\n            stream_id=f\"Order-{order.id}\",\n            stream_type=\"Order\",\n            events=order.uncommitted_events\n        )\n\n        return order.id\n```\n\n### Template 2: Query Infrastructure\n\n```python\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import TypeVar, Generic, List, Optional\n\n# Query base\n@dataclass\nclass Query:\n    pass\n\n\n# Concrete queries\n@dataclass\nclass GetOrderById(Query):\n    order_id: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass GetCustomerOrders(Query):\n    customer_id: str\n    status: Optional[str] = None\n    page: int = 1\n    page_size: int = 20\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass SearchOrders(Query):\n    query: str\n    filters: dict = None\n    sort_by: str = \"created_at\"\n    sort_order: str = \"desc\"\n\n\n# Query result types\n@dataclass\nclass OrderView:\n    order_id: str\n    customer_id: str\n    status: str\n    total_amount: float\n    item_count: int\n    created_at: datetime\n    shipped_at: Optional[datetime] = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass PaginatedResult(Generic[T]):\n    items: List[T]\n    total: int\n    page: int\n    page_size: int\n\n    @property\n    def total_pages(self) -> int:\n        return (self.total + self.page_size - 1) // self.page_size\n\n\n# Query handler base\nT = TypeVar(''T'', bound=Query)\nR = TypeVar(''R'')\n\nclass QueryHandler(ABC, Generic[T, R]):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def handle(self, query: T) -> R:\n        pass\n\n\n# Query bus\nclass QueryBus:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._handlers: Dict[Type[Query], QueryHandler] = {}\n\n    def register(self, query_type: Type[Query], handler: QueryHandler):\n        self._handlers[query_type] = handler\n\n    async def dispatch(self, query: Query) -> Any:\n        handler = self._handlers.get(type(query))\n        if not handler:\n            raise ValueError(f\"No handler for {type(query).__name__}\")\n        return await handler.handle(query)\n\n\n# Query handler implementation\nclass GetOrderByIdHandler(QueryHandler[GetOrderById, Optional[OrderView]]):\n    def __init__(self, read_db):\n        self.read_db = read_db\n\n    async def handle(self, query: GetOrderById) -> Optional[OrderView]:\n        async with self.read_db.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"\"\"\n                SELECT order_id, customer_id, status, total_amount,\n                       item_count, created_at, shipped_at\n                FROM order_views\n                WHERE order_id = $1\n                \"\"\",\n                query.order_id\n            )\n            if row:\n                return OrderView(**dict(row))\n            return None\n\n\nclass GetCustomerOrdersHandler(QueryHandler[GetCustomerOrders, PaginatedResult[OrderView]]):\n    def __init__(self, read_db):\n        self.read_db = read_db\n\n    async def handle(self, query: GetCustomerOrders) -> PaginatedResult[OrderView]:\n        async with self.read_db.acquire() as conn:\n            # Build query with optional status filter\n            where_clause = \"customer_id = $1\"\n            params = [query.customer_id]\n\n            if query.status:\n                where_clause += \" AND status = $2\"\n                params.append(query.status)\n\n            # Get total count\n            total = await conn.fetchval(\n                f\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM order_views WHERE {where_clause}\",\n                *params\n            )\n\n            # Get paginated results\n            offset = (query.page - 1) * query.page_size\n            rows = await conn.fetch(\n                f\"\"\"\n                SELECT order_id, customer_id, status, total_amount,\n                       item_count, created_at, shipped_at\n                FROM order_views\n                WHERE {where_clause}\n                ORDER BY created_at DESC\n                LIMIT ${len(params) + 1} OFFSET ${len(params) + 2}\n                \"\"\",\n                *params, query.page_size, offset\n            )\n\n            return PaginatedResult(\n                items=[OrderView(**dict(row)) for row in rows],\n                total=total,\n                page=query.page,\n                page_size=query.page_size\n            )\n```\n\n### Template 3: FastAPI CQRS Application\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# Request/Response models\nclass CreateOrderRequest(BaseModel):\n    customer_id: str\n    items: List[dict]\n    shipping_address: dict\n\n\nclass OrderResponse(BaseModel):\n    order_id: str\n    customer_id: str\n    status: str\n    total_amount: float\n    item_count: int\n    created_at: datetime\n\n\n# Dependency injection\ndef get_command_bus() -> CommandBus:\n    return app.state.command_bus\n\n\ndef get_query_bus() -> QueryBus:\n    return app.state.query_bus\n\n\n# Command endpoints (POST, PUT, DELETE)\n@app.post(\"/orders\", response_model=dict)\nasync def create_order(\n    request: CreateOrderRequest,\n    command_bus: CommandBus = Depends(get_command_bus)\n):\n    command = CreateOrder(\n        customer_id=request.customer_id,\n        items=request.items,\n        shipping_address=request.shipping_address\n    )\n    order_id = await command_bus.dispatch(command)\n    return {\"order_id\": order_id}\n\n\n@app.post(\"/orders/{order_id}/items\")\nasync def add_item(\n    order_id: str,\n    product_id: str,\n    quantity: int,\n    price: float,\n    command_bus: CommandBus = Depends(get_command_bus)\n):\n    command = AddOrderItem(\n        order_id=order_id,\n        product_id=product_id,\n        quantity=quantity,\n        price=price\n    )\n    await command_bus.dispatch(command)\n    return {\"status\": \"item_added\"}\n\n\n@app.delete(\"/orders/{order_id}\")\nasync def cancel_order(\n    order_id: str,\n    reason: str,\n    command_bus: CommandBus = Depends(get_command_bus)\n):\n    command = CancelOrder(order_id=order_id, reason=reason)\n    await command_bus.dispatch(command)\n    return {\"status\": \"cancelled\"}\n\n\n# Query endpoints (GET)\n@app.get(\"/orders/{order_id}\", response_model=OrderResponse)\nasync def get_order(\n    order_id: str,\n    query_bus: QueryBus = Depends(get_query_bus)\n):\n    query = GetOrderById(order_id=order_id)\n    result = await query_bus.dispatch(query)\n    if not result:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Order not found\")\n    return result\n\n\n@app.get(\"/customers/{customer_id}/orders\")\nasync def get_customer_orders(\n    customer_id: str,\n    status: Optional[str] = None,\n    page: int = 1,\n    page_size: int = 20,\n    query_bus: QueryBus = Depends(get_query_bus)\n):\n    query = GetCustomerOrders(\n        customer_id=customer_id,\n        status=status,\n        page=page,\n        page_size=page_size\n    )\n    return await query_bus.dispatch(query)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/orders/search\")\nasync def search_orders(\n    q: str,\n    sort_by: str = \"created_at\",\n    query_bus: QueryBus = Depends(get_query_bus)\n):\n    query = SearchOrders(query=q, sort_by=sort_by)\n    return await query_bus.dispatch(query)\n```\n\n### Template 4: Read Model Synchronization\n\n```python\nclass ReadModelSynchronizer:\n    \"\"\"Keeps read models in sync with events.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, event_store, read_db, projections: List[Projection]):\n        self.event_store = event_store\n        self.read_db = read_db\n        self.projections = {p.name: p for p in projections}\n\n    async def run(self):\n        \"\"\"Continuously sync read models.\"\"\"\n        while True:\n            for name, projection in self.projections.items():\n                await self._sync_projection(projection)\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n\n    async def _sync_projection(self, projection: Projection):\n        checkpoint = await self._get_checkpoint(projection.name)\n\n        events = await self.event_store.read_all(\n            from_position=checkpoint,\n            limit=100\n        )\n\n        for event in events:\n            if event.event_type in projection.handles():\n                try:\n                    await projection.apply(event)\n                except Exception as e:\n                    # Log error, possibly retry or skip\n                    logger.error(f\"Projection error: {e}\")\n                    continue\n\n            await self._save_checkpoint(projection.name, event.global_position)\n\n    async def rebuild_projection(self, projection_name: str):\n        \"\"\"Rebuild a projection from scratch.\"\"\"\n        projection = self.projections[projection_name]\n\n        # Clear existing data\n        await projection.clear()\n\n        # Reset checkpoint\n        await self._save_checkpoint(projection_name, 0)\n\n        # Rebuild\n        while True:\n            checkpoint = await self._get_checkpoint(projection_name)\n            events = await self.event_store.read_all(checkpoint, 1000)\n\n            if not events:\n                break\n\n            for event in events:\n                if event.event_type in projection.handles():\n                    await projection.apply(event)\n\n            await self._save_checkpoint(\n                projection_name,\n                events[-1].global_position\n            )\n```\n\n### Template 5: Eventual Consistency Handling\n\n```python\nclass ConsistentQueryHandler:\n    \"\"\"Query handler that can wait for consistency.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, read_db, event_store):\n        self.read_db = read_db\n        self.event_store = event_store\n\n    async def query_after_command(\n        self,\n        query: Query,\n        expected_version: int,\n        stream_id: str,\n        timeout: float = 5.0\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Execute query, ensuring read model is at expected version.\n        Used for read-your-writes consistency.\n        \"\"\"\n        start_time = time.time()\n\n        while time.time() - start_time < timeout:\n            # Check if read model is caught up\n            projection_version = await self._get_projection_version(stream_id)\n\n            if projection_version >= expected_version:\n                return await self.execute_query(query)\n\n            # Wait a bit and retry\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n\n        # Timeout - return stale data with warning\n        return {\n            \"data\": await self.execute_query(query),\n            \"_warning\": \"Data may be stale\"\n        }\n\n    async def _get_projection_version(self, stream_id: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Get the last processed event version for a stream.\"\"\"\n        async with self.read_db.acquire() as conn:\n            return await conn.fetchval(\n                \"SELECT last_event_version FROM projection_state WHERE stream_id = $1\",\n                stream_id\n            ) or 0\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Separate command and query models** - Different needs\n- **Use eventual consistency** - Accept propagation delay\n- **Validate in command handlers** - Before state change\n- **Denormalize read models** - Optimize for queries\n- **Version your events** - For schema evolution\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t query in commands** - Use only for writes\n- **Don''t couple read/write schemas** - Independent evolution\n- **Don''t over-engineer** - Start simple\n- **Don''t ignore consistency SLAs** - Define acceptable lag\n\n## Resources\n\n- [CQRS Pattern](https://martinfowler.com/bliki/CQRS.html)\n- [Microsoft CQRS Guidance](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/cqrs)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:30:47.107Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Architecture Agents requiring advanced event-sourced system design and scalability through Command Query Responsibility Segregation patterns.","zh":"Ideal for Architecture Agents requiring advanced event-sourced system design and scalability through Command Query Responsibility Segregation patterns.","ja":"Ideal for Architecture Agents requiring advanced event-sourced system design and scalability through Command Query Responsibility Segregation patterns.","ko":"Ideal for Architecture Agents requiring advanced event-sourced system design and scalability through Command Query Responsibility Segregation patterns.","es":"Ideal para agentes de arquitectura que requieren un diseño de sistema avanzado con origen de eventos y escalabilidad a través de patrones de segregación de responsabilidad de consulta de comando.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''architecture nécessitant une conception de système avancée à base d''événements et une évolutivité via des modèles de ségrégation de responsabilité de requête de commande.","de":"Ideal für Architekturagenten, die ein fortschrittliches Systemdesign mit Ereignisquellen und Skalierbarkeit durch Befehlsabfrage-Verantwortungssegregationsmuster erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Arquitetura que requerem design de sistema avançado baseado em eventos e escalabilidade por meio de padrões de Segregação de Responsabilidade de Consulta de Comando.","ru":"Идеально для агентов архитектуры, требующих передового проектирования системы на основе событий и масштабируемости посредством паттернов сегрегации ответственности запроса команды.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الهندسة المعمارية التي تتطلب تصميم نظام متقدم مصدر الأحداث وزيادة القدرة من خلال أنماط فصل مسؤولية الاستعلام بالأوامر."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement CQRS architecture, enabling the separation of read and write concerns, scaling reads independently from writes, and optimizing complex query scenarios using event-sourced systems and different read/write data models.","zh":"Empowers agents to implement CQRS architecture, enabling the separation of read and write concerns, scaling reads independently from writes, and optimizing complex query scenarios using event-sourced systems and different read/write data models.","ja":"Empowers agents to implement CQRS architecture, enabling the separation of read and write concerns, scaling reads independently from writes, and optimizing complex query scenarios using event-sourced systems and different read/write data models.","ko":"Empowers agents to implement CQRS architecture, enabling the separation of read and write concerns, scaling reads independently from writes, and optimizing complex query scenarios using event-sourced systems and different read/write data models.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar la arquitectura CQRS, lo que permite la separación de las preocupaciones de lectura y escritura, la escalada de lecturas de forma independiente a las escrituras y la optimización de escenarios de consultas complejas mediante sistemas con origen de eventos y diferentes modelos de datos de lectura y escritura.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre l''architecture CQRS, permettant la séparation des préoccupations de lecture et d''écriture, la mise à l''échelle des lectures de manière indépendante des écritures et l''optimisation de scénarios de requêtes complexes à l''aide de systèmes à base d''événements et de différents modèles de données de lecture et d''écriture.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die CQRS-Architektur zu implementieren, wodurch die Trennung von Lese- und Schreibbelangen, die Skalierung von Lesevorgängen unabhängig von Schreibvorgängen und die Optimierung komplexer Abfrageszenarien mithilfe ereignisbasierter Systeme und unterschiedlicher Lese-/Schreibdatenmodelle ermöglicht wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar a arquitetura CQRS, permitindo a separação de preocupações de leitura e gravação, dimensionamento de leituras de forma independente das gravações e otimização de cenários de consulta complexos usando sistemas baseados em eventos e diferentes modelos de dados de leitura e gravação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать архитектуру CQRS, позволяя разделять проблемы чтения и записи, масштабировать чтение независимо от записи и оптимизировать сложные сценарии запросов с помощью систем на основе событий и разных моделей чтения/записи данных.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تنفيذ هندسة CQRS، مما يسمح بفصل مشاكل القراءة والكتابة وتوسيع نطاق القراءة بشكل مستقل عن الكتابة وتنظيم سيناريوهات الاستعلام المعقدة باستخدام الأنظمة المصدر للأحداث ونماذج بيانات القراءة والكتابة المختلفة."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing event-sourced systems for auditing and logging","Scaling database reads for high-performance reporting requirements","Optimizing complex query scenarios in microservices architecture"],"zh":["Implementing event-sourced systems for auditing and logging","Scaling database reads for high-performance reporting requirements","Optimizing complex query scenarios in microservices architecture"],"ja":["Implementing event-sourced systems for auditing and logging","Scaling database reads for high-performance reporting requirements","Optimizing complex query scenarios in microservices architecture"],"ko":["Implementing event-sourced systems for auditing and logging","Scaling database reads for high-performance reporting requirements","Optimizing complex query scenarios in microservices architecture"],"es":["Implementación de sistemas con origen de eventos para auditoría y registro","Escalada de lecturas de bases de datos para requisitos de informes de alto rendimiento","Optimización de escenarios de consultas complejas en arquitectura de microservicios"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de systèmes à base d''événements pour l''audit et la journalisation","Mise à l''échelle des lectures de bases de données pour les exigences de rapports à haute performance","Optimisation de scénarios de requêtes complexes dans l''architecture de microservices"],"de":["Implementierung ereignisbasierter Systeme für Auditing und Protokollierung","Skalierung von Datenbanklesungen für Hochleistungs-Berichterstellungsanforderungen","Optimierung komplexer Abfrageszenarien in Mikrodienstarchitekturen"],"pt":["Implementar sistemas baseados em eventos para auditoria e registro","Dimensionar leituras de banco de dados para requisitos de relatórios de alto desempenho","Otimizar cenários de consulta complexos em arquitetura de microsserviços"],"ru":["Реализация систем на основе событий для аудита и журналирования","Масштабирование чтения базы данных для требований отчетов с высоким уровнем производительности","Оптимизация сложных сценариев запросов в микросервисной архитектуре"],"ar":["تنفيذ أنظمة مصدر للأحداث لتسجيل المراجعة والسجل","توسيع نطاق قراءة قاعدة البيانات لمتطلبات تقارير الأداء العالي","تحسين سيناريوهات الاستعلام المعقدة في هندسة الخدمات الدقيقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of domain-driven design and event sourcing","May add complexity to system architecture"],"zh":["Requires understanding of domain-driven design and event sourcing","May add complexity to system architecture"],"ja":["Requires understanding of domain-driven design and event sourcing","May add complexity to system architecture"],"ko":["Requires understanding of domain-driven design and event sourcing","May add complexity to system architecture"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de diseño orientado a dominio y origen de eventos","Puede agregar complejidad a la arquitectura del sistema"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la conception orientée vers le domaine et de l''origine des événements","Peut ajouter de la complexité à l''architecture du système"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für domänengetriebenes Design und Ereignisquellen","Kann die Komplexität der Systemarchitektur erhöhen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de design dirigido por domínio e fonte de eventos","Pode adicionar complexidade à arquitetura do sistema"],"ru":["Требует понимания проектирования, управляемого доменом, и источника событий","Может добавить сложность к архитектуре системы"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم التصميم الموجه بالنطاق ومصدر الأحداث","يمكن أن يزيد من تعقيد هندسة النظام"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
