es","Application de la théorie des jeux"],"de":["Entwurf von Kernschleifen","Prinzipien des Spiele-Designs","Spiel-Muster","Schaffung von ansprechenden Spiel-Erlebnissen","Anwendung der Spieltheorie"],"pt":["Princípios de design de jogos","Pensamento de design para jogos envolventes","Ciclo de jogo core","Exemplos de gêneros de jogos","Loop de 30 segundos para jogos divertidos","Design de recompensa e feedback"],"ru":["Принципы дизайна игр","Дизайн-мышление для увлекательных игр","Основной игровой цикл","Примеры жанров игр","30-секундный цикл для увлекательных игр","Дизайн наград и обратной связи"],"ar":["مبادئ تصميم الألعاب","التفكير التصميمي للألعاب الجذابة","دورة اللعب الأساسية","أمثلة لأنواع الألعاب","دورة لعب 30 ثانية للألعاب الممتعة","تصميم المكافأة والتعكس"]},"keywords":{"zh":["游戏设计工具","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode","游戏设计原则","核心循环设计"],"ja":["ゲームデザインツール","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode","ゲームデザイン原則","コアループ設計"],"ko":["게임 디자인 도구","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode","게임 디자인 원칙","코어 루프 디자인"],"es":["diseño de juegos","principios de diseño de juegos","patrones de juego","teoría de juegos","experiencias de juego","juegos emocionales","juegos atractivos"],"fr":["conception de jeux","principes de conception de jeux","modèles de jeu","théorie des jeux","expériences de jeu","jeux émotionnels","jeux engageants"],"de":["Spiele-Design","Prinzipien des Spiele-Designs","Spiel-Muster","Spieltheorie","Spiel-Erlebnisse","emotionale Spiele","ansprechende Spiele"],"pt":["game design","design de jogos","princípios de design","jogos envolventes","design thinking","ciclo de jogo","gêneros de jogos","loop de 30 segundos"],"ru":["дизайн игр","принципы дизайна","увлекательные игры","дизайн-мышление","основной игровой цикл","жанры игр","30-секундный цикл","игровой дизайн"],"ar":["تصميم الألعاب","مبادئ التصميم","الألعاب الجذابة","التفكير التصميمي","دورة اللعب الأساسية","أنواع الألعاب","دورة لعب 30 ثانية","تصميم اللعب"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"game-design","description":"Game design principles. GDD structure, balancing, player psychology, progression.","bodyPreview":"# Game Design Principles\n\n> Design thinking for engaging games.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Loop Design\n\n### The 30-Second Test\n\n```\nEvery game needs a fun 30-second loop:\n1. ACTION → Player does something\n2. FEEDBACK → Game responds\n3. REWARD → Player feels good\n4. REPEAT\n```\n\n### Loop Examples\n\n| Genre | Core Loop |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Platformer | Run → Jump → Land → Collect |\n| Shooter | Aim → Shoot → Kill → Loot |\n| Puzzle | Observe → Think → Solve → Advance |\n| RPG | Explore → Fight → Level → Gea","body":"# Game Design Principles\n\n> Design thinking for engaging games.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Loop Design\n\n### The 30-Second Test\n\n```\nEvery game needs a fun 30-second loop:\n1. ACTION → Player does something\n2. FEEDBACK → Game responds\n3. REWARD → Player feels good\n4. REPEAT\n```\n\n### Loop Examples\n\n| Genre | Core Loop |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Platformer | Run → Jump → Land → Collect |\n| Shooter | Aim → Shoot → Kill → Loot |\n| Puzzle | Observe → Think → Solve → Advance |\n| RPG | Explore → Fight → Level → Gear |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Game Design Document (GDD)\n\n### Essential Sections\n\n| Section | Content |\n|---------|---------|\n| **Pitch** | One-sentence description |\n| **Core Loop** | 30-second gameplay |\n| **Mechanics** | How systems work |\n| **Progression** | How player advances |\n| **Art Style** | Visual direction |\n| **Audio** | Sound direction |\n\n### Principles\n\n- Keep it living (update regularly)\n- Visuals help communicate\n- Less is more (start small)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Player Psychology\n\n### Motivation Types\n\n| Type | Driven By |\n|------|-----------|\n| **Achiever** | Goals, completion |\n| **Explorer** | Discovery, secrets |\n| **Socializer** | Interaction, community |\n| **Killer** | Competition, dominance |\n\n### Reward Schedules\n\n| Schedule | Effect | Use |\n|----------|--------|-----|\n| **Fixed** | Predictable | Milestone rewards |\n| **Variable** | Addictive | Loot drops |\n| **Ratio** | Effort-based | Grind games |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Difficulty Balancing\n\n### Flow State\n\n```\nToo Hard → Frustration → Quit\nToo Easy → Boredom → Quit\nJust Right → Flow → Engagement\n```\n\n### Balancing Strategies\n\n| Strategy | How |\n|----------|-----|\n| **Dynamic** | Adjust to player skill |\n| **Selection** | Let player choose |\n| **Accessibility** | Options for all |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Progression Design\n\n### Progression Types\n\n| Type | Example |\n|------|---------|\n| **Skill** | Player gets better |\n| **Power** | Character gets stronger |\n| **Content** | New areas unlock |\n| **Story** | Narrative advances |\n\n### Pacing Principles\n\n- Early wins (hook quickly)\n- Gradually increase challenge\n- Rest beats between intensity\n- Meaningful choices\n\n---\n\n## 6. Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ Don''t | ✅ Do |\n|----------|-------|\n| Design in isolation | Playtest constantly |\n| Polish before fun | Prototype first |\n| Force one way to play | Allow player expression |\n| Punish excessively | Reward progress |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Fun is discovered through iteration, not designed on paper.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:31:07.509Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor and Claude Code seeking to create engaging game experiences through core loop design and design thinking principles.","zh":"适合像 Cursor 和 Claude Code 这样的 AI 代理，旨在通过核心循环设计和设计思维原则创建吸引人的游戏体验。","ja":"Cursor や Claude Code のような AI エージェントに適しており、コアループ設計とデザイン思考原則を通じて魅力的ゲーム体験を作成することを目指しています。","ko":"Cursor 와 Claude Code 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 핵심 루프 디자인과 디자인 사고 원리를 통해 매력적인 게임 경험을 만들고자 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor y Claude Code que buscan crear experiencias de juego atractivas a través del diseño de la bucle central y los principios de pensamiento de diseño.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor et Claude Code qui cherchent à créer des expériences de jeu engageantes via la conception de la boucle centrale et les principes de pensée de conception.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor und Claude Code, die anspruchsvolle Spieleerlebnisse durch Kernschleifendesign und Design-Denksprüche erstellen möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor e Claude Code que buscam criar experiências de jogos envolventes por meio do design do loop central e princípios de design thinking.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor и Claude Code, стремящихся создавать увлекательные игровые trải nghiệm посредством проектирования основного цикла и принципов дизайн-мышления.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Claude Code الذين يسعون إلى إنشاء تجارب ألعاب مثيرة بالتصميم الدوري الأساسي ومبادئ التفكير التصميمي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft addictive game mechanics using the 30-second test framework, incorporating action, feedback, reward, and repeat loops, while leveraging genre-specific core loop examples such as platformer, shooter, puzzle, and RPG designs.","zh":"使代理能够使用 30 秒测试框架创建上瘾的游戏机制，结合动作、反馈、奖励和重复循环，同时利用特定类型的核心循环示例，例如平台游戏、射击游戏、益智游戏和 RPG 设计。","ja":"エージェントが 30 秒テストフレームワークを使用して、アクション、フィードバック、報酬、リピートループを組み込んだ中毒性のあるゲームメカニズムを作成できるようにし、プラットフォーマー、シューティング、パズル、RPG デザインなどのジャンル固有のコアループの例を利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 30초 테스트 프레임워크를 사용하여 행동, 피드백, 보상 및 반복 루프를 결합한 중독성 있는 게임 메커니즘을 만들 수 있도록 하며, 플랫폼 게임, 슈팅 게임, 퍼즐 게임 및 RPG 디자인과 같은 장르별 핵심 루프 예를 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear mecánicas de juego adictivas utilizando el marco de trabajo de prueba de 30 segundos, incorporando acción, retroalimentación, recompensa y bucles de repetición, al mismo tiempo que aprovecha ejemplos de bucle central específicos del género como diseños de plataformas, disparos, rompecabezas y RPG.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des mécaniques de jeu addictives en utilisant le cadre de travail de test de 30 secondes, en incorporant l''action, la rétroaction, la récompense et les boucles de répétition, tout en exploitant des exemples de boucle centrale spécifiques au genre tels que les conceptions de plateformes, de tir, de puzzle et de RPG.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, süchtig machende Spielmechaniken unter Verwendung des 30-Sekunden-Test-Frameworks zu erstellen, indem es Aktion, Feedback, Belohnung und Wiederholungsschleifen integriert, während es gleichzeitig genre-spezifische Kernschleifen-Beispiele wie Plattform-, Shooter-, Puzzle- und RPG-Designs nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar mecânicas de jogo viciantes usando a estrutura de teste de 30 segundos, incorporando ação, feedback, recompensa e loops de repetição, aproveitando exemplos de loop central específicos do gênero, como projetos de plataforma, tiro, quebra-cabeça e RPG.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать увлекательные игровые механики с использованием рамки 30-секундного теста, включающей действие, обратную связь, награду и повторяющиеся циклы, используя примеры основного цикла, специфичные для жанра, такие как платформер, шутер, головоломка и дизайн RPG.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من تصميم ميكانيكا ألعاب مدمنة باستخدام إطار الاختبار لمدة 30 ثانية، ودمج العمل والتعليقات والمكافأة ودوائر التكرار، والاستفادة من أمثلة الحلقات الأساسية المحددة لنوع اللعبة، مثل تصميم المنصة وتصميم إطلاق النار وألغاز وتصميم RPG."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing immersive core loops for platformer games","Creating engaging shooter mechanics with feedback and reward systems","Developing puzzle games with observe-think-solve-advance core loops","Building RPGs with explore-fight-level-gear gameplay"],"zh":["为平台游戏设计沉浸式核心循环","使用反馈和奖励系统创建吸引人的射击游戏机制","开发具有观察-思考-解决-推进核心循环的益智游戏","构建具有探索-战斗-升级-装备游戏性的 RPG"],"ja":["プラットフォーマーゲームの没入型コアループを設計する","フィードバックと報酬システムを使用して魅力的シューティングゲームメカニズムを作成する","観察-思考-解決-進歩のコアループを備えたパズルゲームを開発する","探索-戦闘-レベル-ギアのゲーム性を持つ RPG を構築する"],"ko":["플랫폼 게임을 위한 몰입형 핵심 ループ 디자인","피드백 및 보상 시스템을 사용하여 매력적인 슈팅 게임 메커니즘 생성","관찰-思考-해결-진행 핵심 루프를 갖춘 퍼즐 게임 개발","탐험-전투-레벨-장비 게임성을 갖춘 RPG 구축"],"es":["Diseñar bucles centrales inmersivos para juegos de plataformas","Crear mecánicas de disparos atractivas con sistemas de retroalimentación y recompensa","Desarrollar juegos de rompecabezas con bucles centrales de observar-pensar-resolver-avanzar","Crear RPG con juego de explorar-luchar-nivel-armar"],"fr":["Concevoir des boucles centrales immersives pour les jeux de plateformes","Créer des mécaniques de tir engageantes avec des systèmes de rétroaction et de récompense","Développer des jeux de puzzle avec des boucles centrales d''observer-penser-résoudre-progresser","Construire des RPG avec un gameplay d''explorer-combattre-niveau-équiper"],"de":["Entwicklung von immersiven Kernschleifen für Plattformspiele","Erstellung von süchtig machenden Shooter-Mechaniken mit Feedback- und Belohnungssystemen","Entwicklung von Puzzle-Spielen mit beobachten-denken-lösen-voranschreiten-Kernschleifen","Erstellung von RPGs mit erkunden-kämpfen-leveln-ausrüsten-Spielmechanik"],"pt":["Projeto de loops centrais imersivos para jogos de plataforma","Criação de mecânicas de tiro envolventes com sistemas de feedback e recompensa","Desenvolvimento de jogos de quebra-cabeça com loops centrais de observar-pensar-resolver-avançar","Construção de RPGs com jogabilidade de explorar-lutar-nivelar-equipar"],"ru":["Проектирование погружающих основых циклов для платформенных игр","Создание увлекательных механик шутера с системами обратной связи и награды","Разработка игр-головоломок с основными циклами наблюдать-думать-решать-идти дальше","Строительство RPG с игровым процессом исследовать-драть-получать уровень-экипировать"],"ar":["تصميم الحلقات المركزية الغامرة لألعاب المنصة","إنشاء ميكانيكا إطلاق النار المثيرة مع أنظمة التعليقات والمكافأة","تطوير ألعاب ألغاز مع الحلقات المركزية لمشاهدة-تفكير-حل-تقدم","بناء RPGs مع لعبة استكشاف-قتال-مستوى-معدات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of game design principles","Limited to game development context"],"zh":["需要了解游戏设计原则","仅限游戏开发背景"],"ja":["ゲームデザイン原則の理解が必要","ゲーム開発のコンテキストに限定される"],"ko":["게임 디자인 원리의 이해가 필요","게임 개발 컨텍스트에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de diseño de juegos","Limitado al contexto de desarrollo de juegos"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de conception de jeux","Limité au contexte de développement de jeux"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis von Spiel-Design-Prinzipien","Begrenzt auf den Kontext der Spielentwicklung"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de design de jogos","Limitado ao contexto de desenvolvimento de jogos"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов дизайна игр","Ограничен контекстом разработки игр"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تصميم الألعاب","محدود سياق تطوير الألعاب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/backend-dev-guidelines', 'community', 'yashvinthan', 'DuskSpendr', 'yashvinthan/DuskSpendr', 'backend-dev-guidelines', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z', '2026-02-18T13:31:47.632Z', NULL, '{"id":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/backend-dev-guidelines","name":"backend-dev-guidelines","description":{"zh":"Langfuse 后端开发指南提供了使用 Next.js 14、tRPC、BullMQ 和 TypeScript 模式的最佳实践，帮助开发者建立一致的代码风格","ja":"Langfuse のバックエンド開発ガイドラインは、Next.js 14、tRPC、BullMQ、TypeScript パターンのベストプラクティスを提供し、開発者が一貫したコードスタイルを確立するのに役立ちます","ko":"Langfuse 백엔드 개발 가이드라인은 Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ, TypeScript 패턴의 최적화된 방법을 제공하여 개발자가 일관된 코드 스타일을 구축하도록 도와줍니다","es":"Establece la consistencia y las mejores prácticas en el desarrollo backend de Langfuse con Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ y TypeScript. Aprende a crear y modificar routers y procedimientos tRPC, endpoints de API públicos y consumidores y productores de cola BullMQ","fr":"Établissez la cohérence et les meilleures pratiques dans le développement backend de Langfuse avec Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ et TypeScript. Découvrez comment créer et modifier des routeurs et des procédures tRPC, des points de terminaison d''API publics et des consommateurs et producteurs de file d...","de":"Stellen Sie die Konsistenz und Best Practices im Backend-Entwicklung von Langfuse mit Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ und TypeScript sicher. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie tRPC-Router und -Prozeduren, öffentliche API-Endpunkte und BullMQ-Verbraucher und -Produzenten erstellen und ändern","pt":"Este guia fornece diretrizes para desenvolvimento de backend com Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ e TypeScript, garantindo a consistência e as melhores práticas em projetos de backend.","ru":"Это руководство предоставляет рекомендации для разработки бэкенда с использованием Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ и TypeScript, гарантируя последовательность и лучшие практики в проектах бэкенда.","ar":"يوفر هذا الدليل إرشادات لتطوير الخلفية باستخدام Next.js 14 و tRPC و BullMQ و TypeScript، مما يضمن الإ nhấtية والأفضل الممكنة في مشاريع الخلفية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"后端开发指南 - Langfuse 最佳实践","ja":"バックエンド開発ガイドライン - Langfuse のベストプラクティス","ko":"백엔드 개발 가이드라인 - Langfuse 최적화","es":"Pautas de Desarrollo Backend para Langfuse","fr":"Guidelines de Développement Backend pour Langfuse","de":"Richtlinien für Backend-Entwicklung bei Langfuse","pt":"Diretrizes de Desenvolvimento Backend","ru":"Руководство по разработке бэкенда","ar":"إرشادات تطوير الخلفية","en":"backend-dev-guidelines"},"description":{"zh":"Langfuse 后端开发指南提供了使用 Next.js 14、tRPC、BullMQ 和 TypeScript 模式的最佳实践，帮助开发者建立一致的代码风格","ja":"Langfuse のバックエンド開発ガイドラインは、Next.js 14、tRPC、BullMQ、TypeScript パターンのベストプラクティスを提供し、開発者が一貫したコードスタイルを確立するのに役立ちます","ko":"Langfuse 백엔드 개발 가이드라인은 Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ, TypeScript 패턴의 최적화된 방법을 제공하여 개발자가 일관된 코드 스타일을 구축하도록 도와줍니다","es":"Establece la consistencia y las mejores prácticas en el desarrollo backend de Langfuse con Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ y TypeScript. Aprende a crear y modificar...","fr":"Établissez la cohérence et les meilleures pratiques dans le développement backend de Langfuse avec Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ et TypeScript. Découvrez comment ...","de":"Stellen Sie die Konsistenz und Best Practices im Backend-Entwicklung von Langfuse mit Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ und TypeScript sicher. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie t...","pt":"Este guia fornece diretrizes para desenvolvimento de backend com Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ e TypeScript, garantindo a consistência e as melhores práticas em p...","ru":"Это руководство предоставляет рекомендации для разработки бэкенда с использованием Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ и TypeScript, гарантируя последовательность и луч...","ar":"يوفر هذا الدليل إرشادات لتطوير الخلفية باستخدام Next.js 14 و tRPC و BullMQ و TypeScript، مما يضمن الإ nhấtية والأفضل الممكنة في مشاريع الخلفية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用 Next.js 14 构建一致的后端代码","tRPC 和 REST API 的最佳实践","BullMQ 队列消费者和生产者的使用指南","TypeScript 模式和类型安全","业务逻辑服务的构建"],"ja":["Next.js 14 を使用した一貫したバックエンドコードの構築","tRPC と REST API のベストプラクティス","BullMQ キューのコンシューマーとプロデューサーの使用方法","TypeScript パターンと型安全","ビジネスロジックサービスを構築"],"ko":["Next.js 14를 사용하여 일관된 백엔드 코드를 구축","tRPC와 REST API의 최적화된 방법","BullMQ 큐의 소비자와 생산자의 사용 방법","TypeScript 패턴과 타입 안전","비즈니스 로직 서비스를 구축"],"es":["Establece la consistencia en el desarrollo backend","Mejoras en la creación y modificación de routers y procedimientos tRPC","Creación y modificación de endpoints de API públicos","Uso de BullMQ para la gestión de colas","Integración con Next.js 14 y TypeScript"],"fr":["Établit la cohérence dans le développement backend","Améliorations dans la création et la modification de routeurs et de procédures tRPC","Création et modification de points de terminaison d''API publics","Utilisation de BullMQ pour la gestion de files d''attente","Intégration avec Next.js 14 et TypeScript"],"de":["Sichert die Konsistenz im Backend-Entwicklung","Verbesserungen bei der Erstellung und Änderung von tRPC-Routern und -Prozeduren","Erstellung und Änderung von öffentlichen API-Endpunkten","Verwendung von BullMQ für die Verwaltung von Warteschlangen","Integration mit Next.js 14 und TypeScript"],"pt":["Estabelece a consistência em projetos de backend","Fornece as melhores práticas para desenvolvimento de backend","Suporta Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ e TypeScript","Melhora a qualidade e a manutenção de projetos de backend","Automatiza a ativação em projetos de backend"],"ru":["Устанавливает последовательность в проектах бэкенда","Предоставляет лучшие практики для разработки бэкенда","Поддерживает Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ и TypeScript","Улучшает качество и обслуживание проектов бэкенда","Автоматизирует активацию в проектах бэкенда"],"ar":["يوفر الإ nhấtية في مشاريع الخلفية","يقدم الأفضل الممكنة لتطوير الخلفية","يدعم Next.js 14 و tRPC و BullMQ و TypeScript","يحسن الجودة والصيانة في مشاريع الخلفية","يتم تنشيطه تلقائيا في مشاريع الخلفية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["后端开发指南","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","后端开发最佳实践","一致的代码风格","REST API","业务逻辑服务"],"ja":["バックエンド開発ガイドライン","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","バックエンド開発ベストプラクティス","一貫したコードスタイル","REST API","ビジネスロジックサービス"],"ko":["백엔드 개발 가이드라인","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","백엔드 개발 최적화","일관된 코드 스타일","REST API","비즈니스 로직 서비스"],"es":["desarrollo backend","Langfuse","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","pautas de desarrollo","mejores prácticas","consistencia en el desarrollo"],"fr":["développement backend","Langfuse","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","guidelines de développement","meilleures pratiques","cohérence dans le développement"],"de":["Backend-Entwicklung","Langfuse","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","Richtlinien für die Entwicklung","Best Practices","Konsistenz im Entwicklung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento backend","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","diretrizes de desenvolvimento","melhores práticas","consistência em projetos"],"ru":["разработка бэкенда","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","руководство по разработке","лучшие практики","последовательность в проектах"],"ar":["تطوير الخلفية","Next.js 14","tRPC","BullMQ","TypeScript","إرشادات التطوير","الأفضل الممكنة","الإ nhấtية في المشاريع"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"backend-dev-guidelines","description":"Comprehensive backend development guide for Langfuses Next.js 14/tRPC/Express/TypeScript monorepo. Use when creating tRPC routers, public API endpoints, BullMQ queue processors, services, or working with tRPC procedures, Next.js API routes, Prisma database access, ClickHouse analytics queries, Redis queues, OpenTelemetry instrumentation, Zod v4 validation, env.mjs configuration, tenant isolation patterns, or async patterns. Covers layered architecture (tRPC procedures → services, queue processors → services), dual database system (PostgreSQL + ClickHouse), projectId filtering for multi-tenant isolation, traceException error handling, observability patterns, and testing strategies (Jest for web, vitest for worker).","bodyPreview":"# Backend Development Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nEstablish consistency and best practices across Langfuse''s backend packages (web, worker, packages/shared) using Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ, and TypeScript patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nAutomatically activates when working on:\n\n- Creating or modifying tRPC routers and procedures\n- Creating or modifying public API endpoints (REST)\n- Creating or modifying BullMQ queue consumers and producers\n- Building services with business logic\n- Authenticatin","body":"# Backend Development Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nEstablish consistency and best practices across Langfuse''s backend packages (web, worker, packages/shared) using Next.js 14, tRPC, BullMQ, and TypeScript patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nAutomatically activates when working on:\n\n- Creating or modifying tRPC routers and procedures\n- Creating or modifying public API endpoints (REST)\n- Creating or modifying BullMQ queue consumers and producers\n- Building services with business logic\n- Authenticating API requests\n- Accessing resources based on entitlements\n- Implementing middleware (tRPC, NextAuth, public API)\n- Database operations with Prisma (PostgreSQL) or ClickHouse\n- Observability with OpenTelemetry, DataDog, logger, and traceException\n- Input validation with Zod v4\n- Environment configuration from env variables\n- Backend testing and refactoring\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### UI: New tRPC Feature Checklist (Web)\n\n- [ ] **Router**: Define in `features/[feature]/server/*Router.ts`\n- [ ] **Procedures**: Use appropriate procedure type (protected, public)\n- [ ] **Authentication**: Use JWT authorization via middlewares.\n- [ ] **Entitlement check**: Access resources based on resource and role\n- [ ] **Validation**: Zod v4 schema for input\n- [ ] **Service**: Business logic in service file\n- [ ] **Error handling**: Use traceException wrapper\n- [ ] **Tests**: Unit + integration tests in `__tests__/`\n- [ ] **Config**: Access via env.mjs\n\n### SDKs: New Public API Endpoint Checklist (Web)\n\n- [ ] **Route file**: Create in `pages/api/public/`\n- [ ] **Wrapper**: Use `withMiddlewares` + `createAuthedProjectAPIRoute`\n- [ ] **Types**: Define in `features/public-api/types/`\n- [ ] **Authentication**: Authorization via basic auth\n- [ ] **Validation**: Zod schemas for query/body/response\n- [ ] **Versioning**: Versioning in API path and Zod schemas for query/body/response\n- [ ] **Tests**: Add end-to-end test in `__tests__/async/`\n\n### New Queue Processor Checklist (Worker)\n\n- [ ] **Processor**: Create in `worker/src/queues/`\n- [ ] **Queue types**: Create queue types in `packages/shared/src/server/queues`\n- [ ] **Service**: Business logic in `features/` or `worker/src/features/`\n- [ ] **Error handling**: Distinguish between errors which should fail queue processing and errors which should result in a succeeded event.\n- [ ] **Queue registration**: Add to WorkerManager in app.ts\n- [ ] **Tests**: Add vitest tests in worker\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n### Layered Architecture\n\n```\n# Web Package (Next.js 14)\n\n┌─ tRPC API ──────────────────┐   ┌── Public REST API ──────────┐\n│                             │   │                             │\n│  HTTP Request               │   │  HTTP Request               │\n│      ↓                      │   │      ↓                      │\n│  tRPC Procedure             │   │  withMiddlewares +          │\n│  (protectedProjectProcedure)│   │  createAuthedProjectAPIRoute│\n│      ↓                      │   │      ↓                      │\n│  Service (business logic)   │   │  Service (business logic)   │\n│      ↓                      │   │      ↓                      │\n│  Prisma / ClickHouse        │   │  Prisma / ClickHouse        │\n│                             │   │                             │\n└─────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────────┘\n                 ↓\n            [optional]: Publish to Redis BullMQ queue\n                 ↓\n┌─ Worker Package (Express) ──────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                                             │\n│  BullMQ Queue Job                                           │\n│      ↓                                                      │\n│  Queue Processor (handles job)                              │\n│      ↓                                                      │\n│  Service (business logic)                                   │\n│      ↓                                                      │\n│  Prisma / ClickHouse                                        │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Key Principles:**\n\n- **Web**: tRPC procedures for UI OR public API routes for SDKs → Services → Database\n- **Worker**: Queue processors → Services → Database\n- **packages/shared**: Shared code for Web and Worker\n\nSee [architecture-overview.md](architecture-overview.md) for complete details.\n\n---\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n### Web Package (`/web/`)\n\n```\nweb/src/\n├── features/                # Feature-organized code\n│   ├── [feature-name]/\n│   │   ├── server/          # Backend logic\n│   │   │   ├── *Router.ts   # tRPC router\n│   │   │   └── service.ts   # Business logic\n│   │   ├── components/      # React components\n│   │   └── types/           # Feature types\n├── server/\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── routers/         # tRPC routers\n│   │   ├── trpc.ts          # tRPC setup & middleware\n│   │   └── root.ts          # Main router\n│   ├── auth.ts              # NextAuth.js config\n│   └── db.ts                # Database client\n├── pages/\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── public/          # Public REST APIs\n│   │   └── trpc/            # tRPC endpoint\n│   └── [routes].tsx         # Next.js pages\n├── __tests__/               # Jest tests\n│   └── async/               # Integration tests\n├── instrumentation.ts       # OpenTelemetry (FIRST IMPORT)\n└── env.mjs                  # Environment config\n```\n\n### Worker Package (`/worker/`)\n\n```\nworker/src/\n├── queues/                  # BullMQ processors\n│   ├── evalQueue.ts\n│   ├── ingestionQueue.ts\n│   └── workerManager.ts\n├── features/                # Business logic\n│   └── [feature]/\n│       └── service.ts\n├── instrumentation.ts       # OpenTelemetry (FIRST IMPORT)\n├── app.ts                   # Express setup + queue registration\n├── env.ts                   # Environment config\n└── index.ts                 # Server start\n```\n\n### Shared Package (`/packages/shared/`)\n\n```\nshared/src/\n├── server/                  # Server utilities\n│   ├── auth/                # Authentication helpers\n│   ├── clickhouse/          # ClickHouse client & schema\n│   ├── instrumentation/     # OpenTelemetry helpers\n│   ├── llm/                 # LLM integration utilities\n│   ├── redis/               # Redis queues & cache\n│   ├── repositories/        # Data repositories\n│   ├── services/            # Shared services\n│   ├── utils/               # Server utilities\n│   ├── logger.ts\n│   └── queues.ts\n├── encryption/              # Encryption utilities\n├── features/                # Feature-specific code\n├── tableDefinitions/        # Table schemas\n├── utils/                   # Shared utilities\n├── constants.ts\n├── db.ts                    # Prisma client\n├── env.ts                   # Environment config\n└── index.ts                 # Main exports\n```\n\n**Import Paths (package.json exports):**\n\nThe shared package exposes specific import paths for different use cases:\n\n| Import Path                                | Maps To                           | Use For                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@langfuse/shared`                         | `dist/src/index.js`               | General types, schemas, utilities, constants                    |\n| `@langfuse/shared/src/db`                  | `dist/src/db.js`                  | Prisma client and database types                                |\n| `@langfuse/shared/src/server`              | `dist/src/server/index.js`        | Server-side utilities (queues, auth, services, instrumentation) |\n| `@langfuse/shared/src/server/auth/apiKeys` | `dist/src/server/auth/apiKeys.js` | API key management utilities                                    |\n| `@langfuse/shared/encryption`              | `dist/src/encryption/index.js`    | Encryption and signature utilities                              |\n\n**Usage Examples:**\n\n```typescript\n// General imports - types, schemas, constants, interfaces\nimport {\n  CloudConfigSchema,\n  StringNoHTML,\n  AnnotationQueueObjectType,\n  type APIScoreV2,\n  type ColumnDefinition,\n  Role,\n} from \"@langfuse/shared\";\n\n// Database - Prisma client and types\nimport { prisma, Prisma, JobExecutionStatus } from \"@langfuse/shared/src/db\";\nimport { type DB as Database } from \"@langfuse/shared\";\n\n// Server utilities - queues, services, auth, instrumentation\nimport {\n  logger,\n  instrumentAsync,\n  traceException,\n  redis,\n  getTracesTable,\n  StorageService,\n  sendMembershipInvitationEmail,\n  invalidateApiKeysForProject,\n  recordIncrement,\n  recordHistogram,\n} from \"@langfuse/shared/src/server\";\n\n// API key management (specific path)\nimport { createAndAddApiKeysToDb } from \"@langfuse/shared/src/server/auth/apiKeys\";\n\n// Encryption utilities\nimport { encrypt, decrypt, sign, verify } from \"@langfuse/shared/encryption\";\n```\n\n**What Goes Where:**\n\nThe shared package provides types, utilities, and server code used by both web and worker packages. It has **5 export paths** that control frontend vs backend access:\n\n| Import Path                                | Usage                 | What''s Included                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@langfuse/shared`                         | ✅ Frontend + Backend | Prisma types, Zod schemas, constants, table definitions, domain models, utilities  |\n| `@langfuse/shared/src/db`                  | 🔒 Backend only       | Prisma client instance                                                             |\n| `@langfuse/shared/src/server`              | 🔒 Backend only       | Services, repositories, queues, auth, ClickHouse, LLM integration, instrumentation |\n| `@langfuse/shared/src/server/auth/apiKeys` | 🔒 Backend only       | API key management (separated to avoid circular deps)                              |\n| `@langfuse/shared/encryption`              | 🔒 Backend only       | Database field encryption/decryption                                               |\n\n**Naming Conventions:**\n\n- tRPC Routers: `camelCaseRouter.ts` - `datasetRouter.ts`\n- Services: `service.ts` in feature directory\n- Queue Processors: `camelCaseQueue.ts` - `evalQueue.ts`\n- Public APIs: `kebab-case.ts` - `dataset-items.ts`\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. tRPC Procedures Delegate to Services\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ NEVER: Business logic in procedures\nexport const traceRouter = createTRPCRouter({\n  byId: protectedProjectProcedure\n    .input(z.object({ traceId: z.string() }))\n    .query(async ({ input, ctx }) => {\n      // 200 lines of logic here\n    }),\n});\n\n// ✅ ALWAYS: Delegate to service\nexport const traceRouter = createTRPCRouter({\n  byId: protectedProjectProcedure\n    .input(z.object({ traceId: z.string() }))\n    .query(async ({ input, ctx }) => {\n      return await getTraceById(input.traceId);\n    }),\n});\n```\n\n### 2. Access Config via env.mjs, NEVER process.env\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ NEVER (except in env.mjs itself)\nconst dbUrl = process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n\n// ✅ ALWAYS\nimport { env } from \"@/src/env.mjs\";\nconst dbUrl = env.DATABASE_URL;\n```\n\n### 3. Validate ALL Input with Zod v4\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from \"zod/v4\";\n\nconst schema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  projectId: z.string(),\n});\nconst validated = schema.parse(input);\n```\n\n### 4. Services Use Prisma Directly for Simple CRUD or Repositories for Complex Queries\n\n```typescript\n// Services use Prisma directly for simple CRUD\nimport { prisma } from \"@langfuse/shared/src/db\";\n\nconst dataset = await prisma.dataset.findUnique({\n  where: { id: datasetId, projectId }, // Always filter by projectId for tenant isolation\n});\n\n// Or use repositories for complex queries (traces, observations, scores)\nimport { getTracesTable } from \"@langfuse/shared/src/server\";\n\nconst traces = await getTracesTable({\n  projectId,\n  filter: [...],\n  limit: 1000,\n});\n```\n\n### 6. Observability: OpenTelemetry + DataDog (Not Sentry for Backend)\n\n**Langfuse uses OpenTelemetry for backend observability, with traces and logs sent to DataDog.**\n\n```typescript\n// Import observability utilities\nimport {\n  logger,          // Winston logger with OpenTelemetry/DataDog context\n  traceException,  // Record exceptions to OpenTelemetry spans\n  instrumentAsync, // Create instrumented spans\n} from \"@langfuse/shared/src/server\";\n\n// Structured logging (includes trace_id, span_id, dd.trace_id)\nlogger.info(\"Processing dataset\", { datasetId, projectId });\nlogger.error(\"Failed to create dataset\", { error: err.message });\n\n// Record exceptions to OpenTelemetry (sent to DataDog)\ntry {\n  await operation();\n} catch (error) {\n  traceException(error); // Records to current span\n  throw error;\n}\n\n// Instrument critical operations (all API routes auto-instrumented)\nconst result = await instrumentAsync(\n  { name: \"dataset.create\" },\n  async (span) => {\n    span.setAttributes({ datasetId, projectId });\n    // Operation here\n    return dataset;\n  },\n);\n```\n\n**Note**: Frontend uses Sentry, but backend (tRPC, API routes, services, worker) uses OpenTelemetry + DataDog.\n\n### 7. Comprehensive Testing Required\n\nWrite tests for all new features and bug fixes. See [testing-guide.md](resources/testing-guide.md) for detailed examples.\n\n**Test Types:**\n\n| Type        | Framework | Location                                | Purpose                      |\n| ----------- | --------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Integration | Jest      | `web/src/__tests__/async/`              | Full API endpoint testing    |\n| tRPC        | Jest      | `web/src/__tests__/async/`              | tRPC procedures with auth    |\n| Service     | Jest      | `web/src/__tests__/async/repositories/` | Repository/service functions |\n| Worker      | Vitest    | `worker/src/__tests__/`                 | Queue processors & streams   |\n\n**Quick Examples:**\n\n```typescript\n// Integration Test (Public API)\nconst res = await makeZodVerifiedAPICall(\n  PostDatasetsV1Response, \"POST\", \"/api/public/datasets\",\n  { name: \"test-dataset\" }, auth\n);\nexpect(res.status).toBe(200);\n\n// tRPC Test\nconst { caller } = await prepare(); // Creates session + caller\nconst response = await caller.automations.getAutomations({ projectId });\nexpect(response).toHaveLength(1);\n\n// Service Test\nconst result = await getObservationsWithModelDataFromEventsTable({\n  projectId, filter: [...], limit: 1000, offset: 0\n});\nexpect(result.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n\n// Worker Test (vitest)\nconst stream = await getObservationStream({ projectId, filter: [] });\nconst rows = [];\nfor await (const chunk of stream) rows.push(chunk);\nexpect(rows).toHaveLength(2);\n```\n\n**Key Principles:**\n\n- Use unique IDs (`randomUUID()`) to avoid test interference\n- Clean up test data or use unique project IDs\n- Tests must be independent and runnable in any order\n- Never use `pruneDatabase` in tests\n\n### 8. Always Filter by projectId for Tenant Isolation\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ CORRECT: Filter by projectId for tenant isolation\nconst trace = await prisma.trace.findUnique({\n  where: { id: traceId, projectId }, // Required for multi-tenant data isolation\n});\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: ClickHouse queries also require projectId\nconst traces = await queryClickhouse({\n  query: `\n    SELECT * FROM traces\n    WHERE project_id = {projectId: String}\n    AND timestamp >= {startTime: DateTime64(3)}\n  `,\n  params: { projectId, startTime },\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Imports\n\n```typescript\n// tRPC (Web)\nimport { z } from \"zod/v4\";\nimport {\n  createTRPCRouter,\n  protectedProjectProcedure,\n} from \"@/src/server/api/trpc\";\nimport { TRPCError } from \"@trpc/server\";\n\n// Database\nimport { prisma } from \"@langfuse/shared/src/db\";\nimport type { Prisma } from \"@prisma/client\";\n\n// ClickHouse\nimport {\n  queryClickhouse,\n  queryClickhouseStream,\n  upsertClickhouse,\n} from \"@langfuse/shared/src/server\";\n\n// Observability - OpenTelemetry + DataDog (NOT Sentry for backend)\nimport {\n  logger,          // Winston logger with OTEL/DataDog trace context\n  traceException,  // Record exceptions to OpenTelemetry spans\n  instrumentAsync, // Create instrumented spans for operations\n} from \"@langfuse/shared/src/server\";\n\n// Config\nimport { env } from \"@/src/env.mjs\"; // web\n// or\nimport { env } from \"./env\"; // worker\n\n// Public API (Web)\nimport { withMiddlewares } from \"@/src/features/public-api/server/withMiddlewares\";\nimport { createAuthedProjectAPIRoute } from \"@/src/features/public-api/server/createAuthedProjectAPIRoute\";\n\n// Queue Processing (Worker)\nimport { Job } from \"bullmq\";\nimport { QueueName, TQueueJobTypes } from \"@langfuse/shared/src/server\";\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### HTTP Status Codes\n\n| Code | Use Case     |\n| ---- | ------------ |\n| 200  | Success      |\n| 201  | Created      |\n| 400  | Bad Request  |\n| 401  | Unauthorized |\n| 403  | Forbidden    |\n| 404  | Not Found    |\n| 500  | Server Error |\n\n### Example Features to Reference\n\nReference existing Langfuse features for implementation patterns:\n- **Datasets** (`web/src/features/datasets/`) - Complete feature with tRPC router, public API, and service\n- **Prompts** (`web/src/features/prompts/`) - Feature with versioning and templates\n- **Evaluations** (`web/src/features/evals/`) - Complex feature with worker integration\n- **Public API** (`web/src/features/public-api/`) - Middleware and route patterns\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n❌ Business logic in routes/procedures\n❌ Direct process.env usage (always use env.mjs/env.ts)\n❌ Missing error handling\n❌ No input validation (always use Zod v4)\n❌ Missing projectId filter on tenant-scoped queries\n❌ console.log instead of logger/traceException (OpenTelemetry)\n\n---\n\n## Navigation Guide\n\n| Need to...                | Read this                                                    |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Understand architecture   | [architecture-overview.md](resources/architecture-overview.md)         |\n| Create routes/controllers | [routing-and-controllers.md](resources/routing-and-controllers.md)     |\n| Organize business logic   | [services-and-repositories.md](resources/services-and-repositories.md) |\n| Create middleware         | [middleware-guide.md](resources/middleware-guide.md)                   |\n| Database access           | [database-patterns.md](resources/database-patterns.md)                 |\n| Manage config             | [configuration.md](resources/configuration.md)                         |\n| Write tests               | [testing-guide.md](resources/testing-guide.md)                         |\n\n---\n\n## Resource Files\n\n### [architecture-overview.md](resources/architecture-overview.md)\n\nThree-layer architecture (tRPC/Public API → Services → Data Access), request lifecycle for tRPC/Public API/Worker, Next.js 14 directory structure, dual database system (PostgreSQL + ClickHouse), separation of concerns, repository pattern for complex queries\n\n### [routing-and-controllers.md](resources/routing-and-controllers.md)\n\nNext.js file-based routing, tRPC router patterns, Public REST API routes, layered architecture (Entry Points → Services → Repositories → Database), service layer organization, anti-patterns to avoid\n\n### [services-and-repositories.md](resources/services-and-repositories.md)\n\nService layer overview, dependency injection patterns, singleton patterns, repository pattern for data access, service design principles, caching strategies, testing services\n\n### [middleware-guide.md](resources/middleware-guide.md)\n\ntRPC middleware (withErrorHandling, withOtelInstrumentation, enforceUserIsAuthed), seven tRPC procedure types (publicProcedure, authenticatedProcedure, protectedProjectProcedure, etc.), Public API middleware (withMiddlewares, createAuthedProjectAPIRoute), authentication patterns (NextAuth for tRPC, Basic Auth for Public API)\n\n### [database-patterns.md](resources/database-patterns.md)\n\nDual database architecture (PostgreSQL via Prisma + ClickHouse via direct client), PostgreSQL CRUD operations, ClickHouse query patterns (queryClickhouse, queryClickhouseStream, upsertClickhouse), repository pattern for complex queries, tenant isolation with projectId filtering, when to use which database\n\n### [configuration.md](resources/configuration.md)\n\nEnvironment variable validation with Zod, package-specific configs (web/env.mjs with t3-oss/env-nextjs, worker/env.ts, shared/env.ts), NEXT_PUBLIC_LANGFUSE_CLOUD_REGION usage, LANGFUSE_EE_LICENSE_KEY for enterprise features, best practices for env management\n\n### [testing-guide.md](resources/testing-guide.md)\n\nIntegration tests (Public API with makeZodVerifiedAPICall), tRPC tests (createInnerTRPCContext, appRouter.createCaller), service-level tests (repository/service functions), worker tests (vitest with streams), test isolation principles, running tests (Jest for web, vitest for worker)\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **database-verification** - Verify column names and schema consistency\n- **skill-developer** - Meta-skill for creating and managing skills\n\n---\n\n**Skill Status**: COMPLETE ✅\n**Line Count**: ~540 lines\n**Progressive Disclosure**: 7 resource files ✅\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:31:47.632Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for TypeScript-focused Backend Agents working with Next.js 14, tRPC, and BullMQ ecosystems.","zh":"非常适合专注于TypeScript的后端智能体，并与Next.js 14、tRPC和BullMQ生态系统协同工作。","ja":"TypeScriptに焦点を当てたバックエンドエージェントで、Next.js 14、tRPC、BullMQエコシステムを扱う場合に理想的です。","ko":"Next.js 14, tRPC 및 BullMQ 생태계와 함께 작업하는 TypeScript 중심의 백엔드 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de backend centrados en TypeScript que trabajan con los ecosistemas de Next.js 14, tRPC y BullMQ.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents backend axés sur TypeScript travaillant avec les écosystèmes Next.js 14, tRPC et BullMQ.","de":"Ideal für TypeScript-fokussierte Backend-Agents, die mit den Ökosystemen Next.js 14, tRPC und BullMQ arbeiten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Backend focados em TypeScript que trabalham com os ecossistemas Next.js 14, tRPC e BullMQ.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов бэкенда, ориентированных на TypeScript, работающих с экосистемами Next.js 14, tRPC и BullMQ.","ar":"مثالي لعميل خلفي يركز على TypeScript يعمل مع بيئات Next.js 14 و tRPC و BullMQ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables consistent implementation of tRPC routers, REST API endpoints, and BullMQ queue producers/consumers following Langfuse''s established patterns. Provides structured guidance for authentication flows and business logic services in TypeScript environments.","zh":"能够按照Langfuse既定模式，一致性地实现tRPC路由器、REST API端点和BullMQ队列生产者/消费者。为TypeScript环境中的身份验证流程和业务逻辑服务提供结构化指导。","ja":"Langfuseの確立されたパターンに従って、tRPCルーター、REST APIエンドポイント、BullMQキューのプロデューサー/コンシューマーを一貫して実装できます。TypeScript環境における認証フローとビジネスロジックサービスの構造化されたガイダンスを提供します。","ko":"Langfuse의 확립된 패턴에 따라 tRPC 라우터, REST API 엔드포인트 및 BullMQ 큐 생산자/소비자를 일관되게 구현할 수 있게 합니다. TypeScript 환경에서 인증 흐름 및 비즈니스 로직 서비스에 대한 구조화된 지침을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite la implementación consistente de routers tRPC, endpoints de API REST y productores/consumidores de colas BullMQ siguiendo los patrones establecidos de Langfuse. Proporciona orientación estructurada para flujos de autenticación y servicios de lógica de negocio en entornos TypeScript.","fr":"Permet une mise en œuvre cohérente des routeurs tRPC, des points de terminaison d''API REST et des producteurs/consommateurs de files d''attente BullMQ suivant les modèles établis de Langfuse. Fournit des conseils structurés pour les flux d''authentification et les services de logique métier dans les environnements TypeScript.","de":"Ermöglicht eine konsistente Implementierung von tRPC-Routern, REST-API-Endpunkten und BullMQ-Warteschlangen-Producern/Consumern nach den etablierten Mustern von Langfuse. Bietet strukturierte Anleitung für Authentifizierungsabläufe und Geschäftslogik-Dienste in TypeScript-Umgebungen.","pt":"Permite a implementação consistente de roteadores tRPC, pontos de extremidade de API REST e produtores/consumidores de fila BullMQ, seguindo os padrões estabelecidos pela Langfuse. Fornece orientação estruturada para fluxos de autenticação e serviços de lógica de negócios em ambientes TypeScript.","ru":"Позволяет обеспечить последовательную реализацию маршрутизаторов tRPC, конечных точек REST API и производителей/потребителей очереди BullMQ, следующих устоявшимся шаблонам Langfuse. Предоставляет структурированное руководство для потоков аутентификации и сервисов бизнес-логики в средах TypeScript.","ar":"تمكن من تنفيذ متسق لموجهات tRPC ونقاط نهاية API REST و منتجي/مستهلكي fila BullMQ ، متابعة الأنماط المثبتة من Langfuse. يوفر توجيهًا منظمًا لتدفقات التحقق وخدمات منطق الأعمال في بيئات TypeScript."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating tRPC routers and procedures","Modifying BullMQ queue consumers and producers","Building authentication services","Developing REST API endpoints","Implementing business logic services"],"zh":["创建tRPC路由器和过程","修改BullMQ队列消费者和生产者","构建身份验证服务","开发REST API端点","实现业务逻辑服务"],"ja":["tRPCルーターとプロシージャの作成","BullMQキューのコンシューマーとプロデューサーの変更","認証サービスの構築","REST APIエンドポイントの開発","ビジネスロジックサービスの実装"],"ko":["tRPC 라우터 및 프로시저 생성","BullMQ 큐 소비자 및 생산자 수정","인증 서비스 구축","REST API 엔드포인트 개발","비즈니스 로직 서비스 구현"],"es":["Creación de routers y procedimientos tRPC","Modificación de consumidores y productores de colas BullMQ","Construcción de servicios de autenticación","Desarrollo de endpoints de API REST","Implementación de servicios de lógica de negocio"],"fr":["Création de routeurs et procédures tRPC","Modification des consommateurs et producteurs de files d''attente BullMQ","Construction de services d''authentification","Développement de points de terminaison d''API REST","Mise en œuvre de services de logique métier"],"de":["Erstellung von tRPC-Routern und Prozeduren","Modifikation von BullMQ-Warteschlangen-Consumern und -Producern","Aufbau von Authentifizierungsdiensten","Entwicklung von REST-API-Endpunkten","Implementierung von Geschäftslogik-Diensten"],"pt":["Criação de roteadores e procedimentos tRPC","Modificação de consumidores e produtores de fila BullMQ","Construção de serviços de autenticação","Desenvolvimento de pontos de extremidade de API REST","Implementação de serviços de lógica de negócios"],"ru":["Создание маршрутизаторов и процедур tRPC","Модификация потребителей и производителей очереди BullMQ","Строительство сервисов аутентификации","Разработка конечных точек REST API","Реализация сервисов бизнес-логики"],"ar":["