ones con registros estructurados, métricas y trazas para depurar problemas de producción de manera efec...","fr":"L''observabilité Python permet d''instrumenter des applications avec des journaux structurés, des métriques et des traces pour déboguer les problèmes de produc...","de":"Die Python-Observability ermöglicht das Instrumentieren von Anwendungen mit strukturierten Protokollen, Metriken und Ablaufverfolgungen, um Produktionsproble...","pt":"Instrumente aplicativos Python com logs estruturados, métricas e rastreamento para resolver problemas de produção de forma eficaz","ru":"Инструментируйте приложения Python структурированными журналами, метриками и трассировкой для эффективного решения проблем производства","ar":"أداة تطبيقات بيثون بسجلات هيكلية ومقاييس وتحديد الموقع لحل مشاكل الإنتاج بفعالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Python","Prometheus","ID","","API"],"ja":["Python","Prometheus","ID","","API"],"ko":["Python","Prometheus","ID","","API"],"es":["Registro estructurado de aplicaciones","Colección de métricas con Prometheus","Configuración de trazas distribuidas entre servicios","Propagación de IDs de correlación a través de cadenas de solicitudes","Depuración de problemas de producción","Creación de paneles de observabilidad"],"fr":["Journalisation structurée des applications","Collecte de métriques avec Prometheus","Configuration de traçage distribué entre les services","Propagation des ID de corrélation à travers les chaînes de requêtes","Débogage des problèmes de production","Création de tableaux de bord d''observabilité"],"de":["Strukturierte Protokollierung von Anwendungen","Metriken-Sammlung mit Prometheus","Einrichtung von verteilter Ablaufverfolgung zwischen Diensten","Weiterleitung von Korrelations-IDs durch Anfrageketten","Fehlersuche bei Produktionsproblemen","Erstellung von Observability-Dashboards"],"pt":["Adicionando logs estruturados aos aplicativos","Implementando coleta de métricas com Prometheus","Configurando rastreamento distribuído entre serviços","Propagando IDs de correlação por meio de cadeias de solicitação","Depurando problemas de produção","Construindo painéis de observabilidade"],"ru":["Добавление структурированных журналов в приложения","Реализация сбора метрик с Prometheus","Настройка распределенного трассирования между сервисами","Пропагация идентификаторов корреляции через цепочки запросов","Отладка проблем производства","Создание панелей наблюдаемости"],"ar":["إضافة سجلات هيكلية إلى التطبيقات","تنفيذ جمع المقاييس مع بروميثيوس","تهيئة تحديد الموقع المنتشر بين الخدمات","انتشار معرّفات الارتباط عبر سلاسل الطلب","تصحيح أخطاء الإنتاج","بناء لوحات مراقبة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python","Prometheus","ID","API","Python","logging"],"ja":["Python","Prometheus","ID","API","Python","logging"],"ko":["Python","Prometheus","ID","API","Python","logging"],"es":["observabilidad python","monitoreo de aplicaciones","depuración de producción","registros estructurados","métricas con prometheus","trazas distribuidas","ids de correlación","paneles de observabilidad"],"fr":["observabilité python","surveillance d''applications","débogage de production","journaux structurés","métriques avec prometheus","traçage distribué","ids de corrélation","tableaux de bord d''observabilité"],"de":["python-observability","anwendungsüberwachung","fehlersuche in der produktion","strukturierte protokolle","metriken mit prometheus","verteilte ablaufverfolgung","korrelations-ids","observability-dashboards"],"pt":["Observabilidade Python","Logs estruturados","Métricas","Rastreamento","Depuração de produção","Painéis de observabilidade","Prometheus"," IDs de correlação"],"ru":["Наблюдаемость Python","Структурированные журналы","Метрики","Трассировка","Отладка производства","Панели наблюдаемости","Prometheus","Идентификаторы корреляции"],"ar":["مراقبة بيثون","سجلات هيكلية","مقاييس","تحديد الموقع","تصحيح أخطاء الإنتاج","لوحات مراقبة","بروميثيوس","معرّفات الارتباط"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.520Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-observability","description":"Python observability patterns including structured logging, metrics, and distributed tracing. Use when adding logging, implementing metrics collection, setting up tracing, or debugging production systems.","bodyPreview":"# Python Observability\n\nInstrument Python applications with structured logs, metrics, and traces. When something breaks in production, you need to answer \"what, where, and why\" without deploying new code.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Adding structured logging to applications\n- Implementing metrics collection with Prometheus\n- Setting up distributed tracing across services\n- Propagating correlation IDs through request chains\n- Debugging production issues\n- Building observability dashboards\n\n## C","body":"# Python Observability\n\nInstrument Python applications with structured logs, metrics, and traces. When something breaks in production, you need to answer \"what, where, and why\" without deploying new code.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Adding structured logging to applications\n- Implementing metrics collection with Prometheus\n- Setting up distributed tracing across services\n- Propagating correlation IDs through request chains\n- Debugging production issues\n- Building observability dashboards\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Structured Logging\n\nEmit logs as JSON with consistent fields for production environments. Machine-readable logs enable powerful queries and alerts. For local development, consider human-readable formats.\n\n### 2. The Four Golden Signals\n\nTrack latency, traffic, errors, and saturation for every service boundary.\n\n### 3. Correlation IDs\n\nThread a unique ID through all logs and spans for a single request, enabling end-to-end tracing.\n\n### 4. Bounded Cardinality\n\nKeep metric label values bounded. Unbounded labels (like user IDs) explode storage costs.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```python\nimport structlog\n\nstructlog.configure(\n    processors=[\n        structlog.processors.TimeStamper(fmt=\"iso\"),\n        structlog.processors.JSONRenderer(),\n    ],\n)\n\nlogger = structlog.get_logger()\nlogger.info(\"Request processed\", user_id=\"123\", duration_ms=45)\n```\n\n## Fundamental Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Structured Logging with Structlog\n\nConfigure structlog for JSON output with consistent fields.\n\n```python\nimport logging\nimport structlog\n\ndef configure_logging(log_level: str = \"INFO\") -> None:\n    \"\"\"Configure structured logging for the application.\"\"\"\n    structlog.configure(\n        processors=[\n            structlog.contextvars.merge_contextvars,\n            structlog.processors.add_log_level,\n            structlog.processors.TimeStamper(fmt=\"iso\"),\n            structlog.processors.StackInfoRenderer(),\n            structlog.processors.format_exc_info,\n            structlog.processors.JSONRenderer(),\n        ],\n        wrapper_class=structlog.make_filtering_bound_logger(\n            getattr(logging, log_level.upper())\n        ),\n        context_class=dict,\n        logger_factory=structlog.PrintLoggerFactory(),\n        cache_logger_on_first_use=True,\n    )\n\n# Initialize at application startup\nconfigure_logging(\"INFO\")\nlogger = structlog.get_logger()\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Consistent Log Fields\n\nEvery log entry should include standard fields for filtering and correlation.\n\n```python\nimport structlog\nfrom contextvars import ContextVar\n\n# Store correlation ID in context\ncorrelation_id: ContextVar[str] = ContextVar(\"correlation_id\", default=\"\")\n\nlogger = structlog.get_logger()\n\ndef process_request(request: Request) -> Response:\n    \"\"\"Process request with structured logging.\"\"\"\n    logger.info(\n        \"Request received\",\n        correlation_id=correlation_id.get(),\n        method=request.method,\n        path=request.path,\n        user_id=request.user_id,\n    )\n\n    try:\n        result = handle_request(request)\n        logger.info(\n            \"Request completed\",\n            correlation_id=correlation_id.get(),\n            status_code=200,\n            duration_ms=elapsed,\n        )\n        return result\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(\n            \"Request failed\",\n            correlation_id=correlation_id.get(),\n            error_type=type(e).__name__,\n            error_message=str(e),\n        )\n        raise\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Semantic Log Levels\n\nUse log levels consistently across the application.\n\n| Level | Purpose | Examples |\n|-------|---------|----------|\n| `DEBUG` | Development diagnostics | Variable values, internal state |\n| `INFO` | Request lifecycle, operations | Request start/end, job completion |\n| `WARNING` | Recoverable anomalies | Retry attempts, fallback used |\n| `ERROR` | Failures needing attention | Exceptions, service unavailable |\n\n```python\n# DEBUG: Detailed internal information\nlogger.debug(\"Cache lookup\", key=cache_key, hit=cache_hit)\n\n# INFO: Normal operational events\nlogger.info(\"Order created\", order_id=order.id, total=order.total)\n\n# WARNING: Abnormal but handled situations\nlogger.warning(\n    \"Rate limit approaching\",\n    current_rate=950,\n    limit=1000,\n    reset_seconds=30,\n)\n\n# ERROR: Failures requiring investigation\nlogger.error(\n    \"Payment processing failed\",\n    order_id=order.id,\n    error=str(e),\n    payment_provider=\"stripe\",\n)\n```\n\nNever log expected behavior at `ERROR`. A user entering a wrong password is `INFO`, not `ERROR`.\n\n### Pattern 4: Correlation ID Propagation\n\nGenerate a unique ID at ingress and thread it through all operations.\n\n```python\nfrom contextvars import ContextVar\nimport uuid\nimport structlog\n\ncorrelation_id: ContextVar[str] = ContextVar(\"correlation_id\", default=\"\")\n\ndef set_correlation_id(cid: str | None = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Set correlation ID for current context.\"\"\"\n    cid = cid or str(uuid.uuid4())\n    correlation_id.set(cid)\n    structlog.contextvars.bind_contextvars(correlation_id=cid)\n    return cid\n\n# FastAPI middleware example\nfrom fastapi import Request\n\nasync def correlation_middleware(request: Request, call_next):\n    \"\"\"Middleware to set and propagate correlation ID.\"\"\"\n    # Use incoming header or generate new\n    cid = request.headers.get(\"X-Correlation-ID\") or str(uuid.uuid4())\n    set_correlation_id(cid)\n\n    response = await call_next(request)\n    response.headers[\"X-Correlation-ID\"] = cid\n    return response\n```\n\nPropagate to outbound requests:\n\n```python\nimport httpx\n\nasync def call_downstream_service(endpoint: str, data: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Call downstream service with correlation ID.\"\"\"\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient() as client:\n        response = await client.post(\n            endpoint,\n            json=data,\n            headers={\"X-Correlation-ID\": correlation_id.get()},\n        )\n        return response.json()\n```\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Pattern 5: The Four Golden Signals with Prometheus\n\nTrack these metrics for every service boundary:\n\n```python\nfrom prometheus_client import Counter, Histogram, Gauge\n\n# Latency: How long requests take\nREQUEST_LATENCY = Histogram(\n    \"http_request_duration_seconds\",\n    \"Request latency in seconds\",\n    [\"method\", \"endpoint\", \"status\"],\n    buckets=[0.01, 0.025, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2.5, 5, 10],\n)\n\n# Traffic: Request rate\nREQUEST_COUNT = Counter(\n    \"http_requests_total\",\n    \"Total HTTP requests\",\n    [\"method\", \"endpoint\", \"status\"],\n)\n\n# Errors: Error rate\nERROR_COUNT = Counter(\n    \"http_errors_total\",\n    \"Total HTTP errors\",\n    [\"method\", \"endpoint\", \"error_type\"],\n)\n\n# Saturation: Resource utilization\nDB_POOL_USAGE = Gauge(\n    \"db_connection_pool_used\",\n    \"Number of database connections in use\",\n)\n```\n\nInstrument your endpoints:\n\n```python\nimport time\nfrom functools import wraps\n\ndef track_request(func):\n    \"\"\"Decorator to track request metrics.\"\"\"\n    @wraps(func)\n    async def wrapper(request: Request, *args, **kwargs):\n        method = request.method\n        endpoint = request.url.path\n        start = time.perf_counter()\n\n        try:\n            response = await func(request, *args, **kwargs)\n            status = str(response.status_code)\n            return response\n        except Exception as e:\n            status = \"500\"\n            ERROR_COUNT.labels(\n                method=method,\n                endpoint=endpoint,\n                error_type=type(e).__name__,\n            ).inc()\n            raise\n        finally:\n            duration = time.perf_counter() - start\n            REQUEST_COUNT.labels(method=method, endpoint=endpoint, status=status).inc()\n            REQUEST_LATENCY.labels(method=method, endpoint=endpoint, status=status).observe(duration)\n\n    return wrapper\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Bounded Cardinality\n\nAvoid labels with unbounded values to prevent metric explosion.\n\n```python\n# BAD: User ID has potentially millions of values\nREQUEST_COUNT.labels(method=\"GET\", user_id=user.id)  # Don''t do this!\n\n# GOOD: Bounded values only\nREQUEST_COUNT.labels(method=\"GET\", endpoint=\"/users\", status=\"200\")\n\n# If you need per-user metrics, use a different approach:\n# - Log the user_id and query logs\n# - Use a separate analytics system\n# - Bucket users by type/tier\nREQUEST_COUNT.labels(\n    method=\"GET\",\n    endpoint=\"/users\",\n    user_tier=\"premium\",  # Bounded set of values\n)\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: Timed Operations with Context Manager\n\nCreate a reusable timing context manager for operations.\n\n```python\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nimport time\nimport structlog\n\nlogger = structlog.get_logger()\n\n@contextmanager\ndef timed_operation(name: str, **extra_fields):\n    \"\"\"Context manager for timing and logging operations.\"\"\"\n    start = time.perf_counter()\n    logger.debug(\"Operation started\", operation=name, **extra_fields)\n\n    try:\n        yield\n    except Exception as e:\n        elapsed_ms = (time.perf_counter() - start) * 1000\n        logger.error(\n            \"Operation failed\",\n            operation=name,\n            duration_ms=round(elapsed_ms, 2),\n            error=str(e),\n            **extra_fields,\n        )\n        raise\n    else:\n        elapsed_ms = (time.perf_counter() - start) * 1000\n        logger.info(\n            \"Operation completed\",\n            operation=name,\n            duration_ms=round(elapsed_ms, 2),\n            **extra_fields,\n        )\n\n# Usage\nwith timed_operation(\"fetch_user_orders\", user_id=user.id):\n    orders = await order_repository.get_by_user(user.id)\n```\n\n### Pattern 8: OpenTelemetry Tracing\n\nSet up distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry.\n\n**Note:** OpenTelemetry is actively evolving. Check the [official Python documentation](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/languages/python/) for the latest API patterns and best practices.\n\n```python\nfrom opentelemetry import trace\nfrom opentelemetry.sdk.trace import TracerProvider\nfrom opentelemetry.sdk.trace.export import BatchSpanProcessor\nfrom opentelemetry.exporter.otlp.proto.grpc.trace_exporter import OTLPSpanExporter\n\ndef configure_tracing(service_name: str, otlp_endpoint: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Configure OpenTelemetry tracing.\"\"\"\n    provider = TracerProvider()\n    processor = BatchSpanProcessor(OTLPSpanExporter(endpoint=otlp_endpoint))\n    provider.add_span_processor(processor)\n    trace.set_tracer_provider(provider)\n\ntracer = trace.get_tracer(__name__)\n\nasync def process_order(order_id: str) -> Order:\n    \"\"\"Process order with tracing.\"\"\"\n    with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"process_order\") as span:\n        span.set_attribute(\"order.id\", order_id)\n\n        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"validate_order\"):\n            validate_order(order_id)\n\n        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"charge_payment\"):\n            charge_payment(order_id)\n\n        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"send_confirmation\"):\n            send_confirmation(order_id)\n\n        return order\n```\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Use structured logging** - JSON logs with consistent fields\n2. **Propagate correlation IDs** - Thread through all requests and logs\n3. **Track the four golden signals** - Latency, traffic, errors, saturation\n4. **Bound label cardinality** - Never use unbounded values as metric labels\n5. **Log at appropriate levels** - Don''t cry wolf with ERROR\n6. **Include context** - User ID, request ID, operation name in logs\n7. **Use context managers** - Consistent timing and error handling\n8. **Separate concerns** - Observability code shouldn''t pollute business logic\n9. **Test your observability** - Verify logs and metrics in integration tests\n10. **Set up alerts** - Metrics are useless without alerting\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:31:39.351Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Python Development Agents requiring production debugging capabilities without code redeployment.","zh":"Essential for Python Development Agents requiring production debugging capabilities without code redeployment.","ja":"Essential for Python Development Agents requiring production debugging capabilities without code redeployment.","ko":"Essential for Python Development Agents requiring production debugging capabilities without code redeployment.","es":"Esencial para agentes de desarrollo de Python que requieren capacidades de depuración de producción sin redeployar el código.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de développement Python nécessitant des capacités de débogage de production sans redéploiement de code.","de":"Wesentlich für Python-Entwicklungsagenten, die Produktions-Debugging-Funktionen ohne Code-Neuverteilung erfordern.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de capacidades de depuração em produção sem reimplementação de código.","ru":"Необходим для агентов разработки на Python, которым требуются возможности отладки в рабочей среде без повторного развертывания кода.","ar":"أساسي لوكلاء تطوير بايثون الذين يتطلبون قدرات تصحيح الأخطاء في بيئة الإنتاج دون إعادة نشر الكود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables comprehensive observability through structured logging, Prometheus metrics collection, and distributed tracing with correlation ID propagation across service boundaries. Provides immediate visibility into production issues by instrumenting applications without code changes.","zh":"Enables comprehensive observability through structured logging, Prometheus metrics collection, and distributed tracing with correlation ID propagation across service boundaries. Provides immediate visibility into production issues by instrumenting applications without code changes.","ja":"Enables comprehensive observability through structured logging, Prometheus metrics collection, and distributed tracing with correlation ID propagation across service boundaries. Provides immediate visibility into production issues by instrumenting applications without code changes.","ko":"Enables comprehensive observability through structured logging, Prometheus metrics collection, and distributed tracing with correlation ID propagation across service boundaries. Provides immediate visibility into production issues by instrumenting applications without code changes.","es":"Permite una observabilidad integral a través de la registración estructurada, la recolección de métricas de Prometheus y el seguimiento distribuido con propagación de ID de correlación a través de los límites del servicio. Proporciona visibilidad inmediata en los problemas de producción al instrumentar aplicaciones sin cambios de código.","fr":"Permet une observabilité complète grâce à la journalisation structurée, à la collecte de métriques Prometheus et au suivi distribué avec propagation d''ID de corrélation à travers les limites de service. Fournit une visibilité immédiate sur les problèmes de production en instrumentant les applications sans modifications de code.","de":"Ermöglicht umfassende Beobachtbarkeit durch strukturierte Protokollierung, Prometheus-Metrik-Sammlung und verteilter Nachverfolgung mit Korrelations-ID-Weiterleitung über Dienstgrenzen hinweg. Bietet sofortige Einblicke in Produktionsprobleme, indem Anwendungen ohne Codeänderungen instrumentiert werden.","pt":"Permite observabilidade abrangente por meio de registro estruturado de logs, coleta de métricas do Prometheus e rastreamento distribuído com propagação de ID de correlação entre os limites dos serviços. Fornece visibilidade imediata de problemas em produção instrumentando aplicações sem alterações de código.","ru":"Обеспечивает комплексную наблюдательность за счет структурированного логирования, сбора метрик Prometheus и распределенной трассировки с распространением идентификатора корреляции через границы сервисов. Обеспечивает немедленную видимость проблем в рабочей среде за счет инструментирования приложений без изменения кода.","ar":"يمكن من المراقبة الشاملة من خلال التسجيل المنظم، وجمع مقاييس Prometheus، والتتبع الموزع مع نشر معرّف الارتباط عبر حدود الخدمات. يوفر رؤية فورية للمشاكل في بيئة الإنتاج من خلال أداة التطبيقات دون تغييرات في الكود."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging production issues in real-time","Implementing metrics collection with Prometheus","Setting up distributed tracing across microservices","Propagating correlation IDs through request chains","Building observability dashboards from instrumented data"],"zh":["Debugging production issues in real-time","Implementing metrics collection with Prometheus","Setting up distributed tracing across microservices","Propagating correlation IDs through request chains","Building observability dashboards from instrumented data"],"ja":["Debugging production issues in real-time","Implementing metrics collection with Prometheus","Setting up distributed tracing across microservices","Propagating correlation IDs through request chains","Building observability dashboards from instrumented data"],"ko":["Debugging production issues in real-time","Implementing metrics collection with Prometheus","Setting up distributed tracing across microservices","Propagating correlation IDs through request chains","Building observability dashboards from instrumented data"],"es":["Depuración de problemas de producción en tiempo real","Implementación de la recolección de métricas con Prometheus","Configuración del seguimiento distribuido entre microservicios","Propagación de ID de correlación a través de cadenas de solicitudes","Creación de paneles de observabilidad a partir de datos instrumentados"],"fr":["Débogage des problèmes de production en temps réel","Mise en œuvre de la collecte de métriques avec Prometheus","Configuration du suivi distribué entre microservices","Propagation d''ID de corrélation à travers les chaînes de requêtes","Création de tableaux de bord d''observabilité à partir de données instrumentées"],"de":["Debugging von Produktionsproblemen in Echtzeit","Implementierung der Metrik-Sammlung mit Prometheus","Einrichtung der verteilten Nachverfolgung zwischen Mikrodiensten","Weiterleitung von Korrelations-IDs über Anforderungsketten hinweg","Erstellung von Beobachtungs-Dashboards aus instrumentierten Daten"],"pt":["Depuração de problemas em produção em tempo real","Implementação de coleta de métricas com Prometheus","Configuração de rastreamento distribuído em microsserviços","Propagação de IDs de correlação através de cadeias de solicitação","Criação de painéis de observabilidade a partir de dados instrumentados"],"ru":["Отладка проблем в рабочей среде в реальном времени","Внедрение сбора метрик с помощью Prometheus","Настройка распределенной трассировки в микросервисах","Распространение идентификаторов корреляции по цепочкам запросов","Создание панелей наблюдения на основе инструментированных данных"],"ar":["تصحيح المشاكل في بيئة الإنتاج في الوقت الفعلي","تنفيذ جمع المقاييس باستخدام Prometheus","إعداد التتبع الموزع عبر الخدمات المصغرة","نشر معرّفات الارتباط عبر سلاسل الطلبات","بناء لوحات مراقبة من البيانات المأدوأة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Python applications only","Requires application instrumentation","Dependent on Prometheus for metrics collection","Needs trace storage backend for distributed tracing"],"zh":["Python applications only","Requires application instrumentation","Dependent on Prometheus for metrics collection","Needs trace storage backend for distributed tracing"],"ja":["Python applications only","Requires application instrumentation","Dependent on Prometheus for metrics collection","Needs trace storage backend for distributed tracing"],"ko":["Python applications only","Requires application instrumentation","Dependent on Prometheus for metrics collection","Needs trace storage backend for distributed tracing"],"es":["Solo aplicaciones de Python","Requiere instrumentación de aplicaciones","Dependiente de Prometheus para la recolección de métricas","Necesita un backend de almacenamiento de seguimiento para el seguimiento distribuido"],"fr":["Applications Python uniquement","Nécessite l''instrumentation d''applications","Dépendante de Prometheus pour la collecte de métriques","Nécessite un backend de stockage de suivi pour le suivi distribué"],"de":["Nur Python-Anwendungen","Benötigt Anwendungs-Instrumentierung","Abhängig von Prometheus für Metrik-Sammlung","Benötigt einen Nachverfolgungs-Speicher-Backend für verteilte Nachverfolgung"],"pt":["Apenas aplicações Python","Requer instrumentação da aplicação","Dependente do Prometheus para coleta de métricas","Necessita de um backend de armazenamento de traços para rastreamento distribuído"],"ru":["Только приложения Python","Требует инструментирования приложения","Зависит от Prometheus для сбора метрик","Требует бэкенд для хранения трассировок для распределенной трассировки"],"ar":["تطبيقات بايثون فقط","يتطلب أداة التطبيق","يعتمد على Prometheus لجمع المقاييس","يحتاج إلى خلفية لتخزين التتبع للتتبع الموزع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
