bir y responder a comentarios de revisión de código.","fr":"La révision de code nécessite une évaluation technique, et non une performance émotionnelle. Apprenez à recevoir et à répondre aux commentaires de révision d...","de":"Die Code-Review erfordert eine technische Bewertung, nicht eine emotionale Leistung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Code-Review-Feedback erhalten und beantworten.","pt":"Recepção de revisão de código é um processo que exige avaliação técnica, não desempenho emocional. Verifique antes de implementar e pergunte antes de assumir.","ru":"Прием код-ревью - это процесс, требующий технической оценки, а не эмоционального выступления. Верифицируйте перед реализацией и спрашивайте перед предположен...","ar":"استقبال مراجعة الكود هو عملية تتطلب تقييم تقني، وليس أداء عاطفي. التحقق قبل التنفيذ وسؤال قبل افتراض.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["读取反馈","理解要求","验证代码","评估技术","响应反馈"],"ja":["フィードバックの読み取り","要件の理解","コードの検証","技術の評価","フィードバックの返信"],"ko":["피드백 수신","요구사항 이해","코드 검증","기술 평가","피드백 응답"],"es":["Verificación antes de implementación","Preguntar antes de asumir","Prioridad a la corrección técnica","Evaluación técnica del código","Respuesta efectiva a comentarios"],"fr":["Vérification avant mise en œuvre","Demander avant de supposer","Priorité à la correction technique","Évaluation technique du code","Réponse efficace aux commentaires"],"de":["Verifizierung vor Implementierung","Fragen vor Annahme","Priorität für technische Korrektheit","Technische Bewertung des Codes","Effektive Beantwortung von Kommentaren"],"pt":["Leitura completa do feedback","Verificação da exigência","Verificação contra a realidade do código","Avaliação da correção técnica","Resposta técnica"],"ru":["Полное чтение отзывов","Проверка требования","Проверка против реальности кода","Оценка технической правильности","Технический ответ"],"ar":["قراءة كاملة لتعليقات","التحقق من المتطلبات","التحقق ضد واقع الكود","تقييم الصحة الفنية","استجابة فنية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码反馈","技术评估","代码质量","开发最佳实践","代码审查流程"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コードフィードバック","技術評価","コード品質","開発ベストプラクティス","コードレビューのプロセス"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 피드백","기술 평가","코드 품질","개발 최적화","코드 리뷰 프로세스"],"es":["revisión de código","recepción de comentarios","evaluación técnica","desarrollo de software","mejora del código","principios de revisión de código"],"fr":["révision de code","réception de commentaires","évaluation technique","développement de logiciels","amélioration du code","principes de révision de code"],"de":["Code-Review","Erhalt von Feedback","technische Bewertung","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Verbesserung","Prinzipien der Code-Review"],"pt":["revisão de código","colaboração em equipe","desenvolvimento de software","recepção de feedback","avaliação técnica","programação"],"ru":["код-ревью","командная работа","разработка программного обеспечения","прием отзывов","техническая оценка","программирование"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","العمل الجماعي","تطوير البرمجيات","استقبال التعليقات","التقييم الفني","البرمجة"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.521Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"receiving-code-review","description":"Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response Pattern\n\n```\nWHEN receiving code review feedback:\n\n1. READ: Complete feedback without reacting\n2. UNDERSTAND: Restate requirement in own words (or ask)\n3. VERIFY: Check against codebase reality\n4. EVALUATE: Technically sound for THIS codebase?\n5. RESPOND: Techni","body":"# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response Pattern\n\n```\nWHEN receiving code review feedback:\n\n1. READ: Complete feedback without reacting\n2. UNDERSTAND: Restate requirement in own words (or ask)\n3. VERIFY: Check against codebase reality\n4. EVALUATE: Technically sound for THIS codebase?\n5. RESPOND: Technical acknowledgment or reasoned pushback\n6. IMPLEMENT: One item at a time, test each\n```\n\n## Forbidden Responses\n\n**NEVER:**\n- \"You''re absolutely right!\" (explicit CLAUDE.md violation)\n- \"Great point!\" / \"Excellent feedback!\" (performative)\n- \"Let me implement that now\" (before verification)\n\n**INSTEAD:**\n- Restate the technical requirement\n- Ask clarifying questions\n- Push back with technical reasoning if wrong\n- Just start working (actions > words)\n\n## Handling Unclear Feedback\n\n```\nIF any item is unclear:\n  STOP - do not implement anything yet\n  ASK for clarification on unclear items\n\nWHY: Items may be related. Partial understanding = wrong implementation.\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n\n❌ WRONG: Implement 1,2,3,6 now, ask about 4,5 later\n✅ RIGHT: \"I understand items 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before proceeding.\"\n```\n\n## Source-Specific Handling\n\n### From your human partner\n- **Trusted** - implement after understanding\n- **Still ask** if scope unclear\n- **No performative agreement**\n- **Skip to action** or technical acknowledgment\n\n### From External Reviewers\n```\nBEFORE implementing:\n  1. Check: Technically correct for THIS codebase?\n  2. Check: Breaks existing functionality?\n  3. Check: Reason for current implementation?\n  4. Check: Works on all platforms/versions?\n  5. Check: Does reviewer understand full context?\n\nIF suggestion seems wrong:\n  Push back with technical reasoning\n\nIF can''t easily verify:\n  Say so: \"I can''t verify this without [X]. Should I [investigate/ask/proceed]?\"\n\nIF conflicts with your human partner''s prior decisions:\n  Stop and discuss with your human partner first\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"External feedback - be skeptical, but check carefully\"\n\n## YAGNI Check for \"Professional\" Features\n\n```\nIF reviewer suggests \"implementing properly\":\n  grep codebase for actual usage\n\n  IF unused: \"This endpoint isn''t called. Remove it (YAGNI)?\"\n  IF used: Then implement properly\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"You and reviewer both report to me. If we don''t need this feature, don''t add it.\"\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n```\nFOR multi-item feedback:\n  1. Clarify anything unclear FIRST\n  2. Then implement in this order:\n     - Blocking issues (breaks, security)\n     - Simple fixes (typos, imports)\n     - Complex fixes (refactoring, logic)\n  3. Test each fix individually\n  4. Verify no regressions\n```\n\n## When To Push Back\n\nPush back when:\n- Suggestion breaks existing functionality\n- Reviewer lacks full context\n- Violates YAGNI (unused feature)\n- Technically incorrect for this stack\n- Legacy/compatibility reasons exist\n- Conflicts with your human partner''s architectural decisions\n\n**How to push back:**\n- Use technical reasoning, not defensiveness\n- Ask specific questions\n- Reference working tests/code\n- Involve your human partner if architectural\n\n**Signal if uncomfortable pushing back out loud:** \"Strange things are afoot at the Circle K\"\n\n## Acknowledging Correct Feedback\n\nWhen feedback IS correct:\n```\n✅ \"Fixed. [Brief description of what changed]\"\n✅ \"Good catch - [specific issue]. Fixed in [location].\"\n✅ [Just fix it and show in the code]\n\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right!\"\n❌ \"Great point!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for catching that!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for [anything]\"\n❌ ANY gratitude expression\n```\n\n**Why no thanks:** Actions speak. Just fix it. The code itself shows you heard the feedback.\n\n**If you catch yourself about to write \"Thanks\":** DELETE IT. State the fix instead.\n\n## Gracefully Correcting Your Pushback\n\nIf you pushed back and were wrong:\n```\n✅ \"You were right - I checked [X] and it does [Y]. Implementing now.\"\n✅ \"Verified this and you''re correct. My initial understanding was wrong because [reason]. Fixing.\"\n\n❌ Long apology\n❌ Defending why you pushed back\n❌ Over-explaining\n```\n\nState the correction factually and move on.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| Performative agreement | State requirement or just act |\n| Blind implementation | Verify against codebase first |\n| Batch without testing | One at a time, test each |\n| Assuming reviewer is right | Check if breaks things |\n| Avoiding pushback | Technical correctness > comfort |\n| Partial implementation | Clarify all items first |\n| Can''t verify, proceed anyway | State limitation, ask for direction |\n\n## Real Examples\n\n**Performative Agreement (Bad):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right! Let me remove that...\"\n```\n\n**Technical Verification (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n✅ \"Checking... build target is 10.15+, this API needs 13+. Need legacy for backward compat. Current impl has wrong bundle ID - fix it or drop pre-13 support?\"\n```\n\n**YAGNI (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Implement proper metrics tracking with database, date filters, CSV export\"\n✅ \"Grepped codebase - nothing calls this endpoint. Remove it (YAGNI)? Or is there usage I''m missing?\"\n```\n\n**Unclear Item (Good):**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix items 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n✅ \"Understand 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before implementing.\"\n```\n\n## GitHub Thread Replies\n\nWhen replying to inline review comments on GitHub, reply in the comment thread (`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{pr}/comments/{id}/replies`), not as a top-level PR comment.\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**External feedback = suggestions to evaluate, not orders to follow.**\n\nVerify. Question. Then implement.\n\nNo performative agreement. Technical rigor always.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:37:06.381Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Collaborative Coding Agents needing structured code review reception and technical evaluation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化代码审查接收和技术评估能力的协作编码代理。","ja":"構造化されたコードレビューの受信と技術評価機能を必要とするコラボレーティブコーディングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"구조화된 코드 리뷰 수신 및 기술 평가 기능이 필요한 협업 코딩 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Codificación Colaborativa que necesitan una recepción de revisión de código estructurada y capacidades de evaluación técnica.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Codage Collaboratif ayant besoin d''une réception de revue de code structurée et de capacités d''évaluation technique.","de":"Perfekt für kollaborative Codierungsagenten, die eine strukturierte Code-Review-Rezeption und technische Bewertungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Codificação Colaborativa que necessitam de recepção de revisão de código estruturada e capacidades de avaliação técnica.","ru":"Идеально подходит для коллаборативных агентов кодирования, которым необходима структурированная проверка кода и техническая оценка.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الترميز التعاونية التي تحتاج إلى استقبال مراجعة الكود المنظّمة وقدرات التقييم الفني."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to technically evaluate codebase reality, verify requirements, and respond with technically sound feedback using protocols like restating requirements and checking against codebase reality.","zh":"赋予代理技术评估代码库现实、验证需求并使用类似重新陈述需求和检查代码库现实的协议以技术上合理的反馈做出响应的能力。","ja":"エージェントにコードベースの現実を技術的に評価し、要件を検証し、要件の再提示やコードベースの現実との照合などのプロトコルを使用して技術的に妥当なフィードバックで応答する機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트에 코드베이스 현실을 기술적으로 평가하고 요구 사항을 검증하며 요구 사항 재陈述 및 코드베이스 현실 확인과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 기술적으로 합리적인 피드백으로 응답하는 능력을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a evaluar técnicamente la realidad de la base de código, verificar los requisitos y responder con comentarios técnicamente sólidos utilizando protocolos como la reiteración de los requisitos y la verificación contra la realidad de la base de código.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''évaluer techniquement la réalité de la base de code, de vérifier les exigences et de répondre avec des commentaires techniquement solides en utilisant des protocoles tels que la réitération des exigences et la vérification contre la réalité de la base de code.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Realität der Codebasis technisch zu bewerten, Anforderungen zu überprüfen und mit technisch fundierten Feedback zu antworten, indem Protokolle wie die Wiederholung der Anforderungen und die Überprüfung gegen die Realität der Codebasis verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a avaliar tecnicamente a realidade do código, verificar os requisitos e responder com feedback tecnicamente sólido usando protocolos como reafirmar os requisitos e verificar contra a realidade do código.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью технически оценить реальность кодовой базы, проверить требования и ответить технически обоснованными отзывами, используя протоколы, такие как повторное заявление требований и проверка против реальности кодовой базы.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تقييم الواقع الفني للكود، والتحقق من المتطلبات والاستجابة بملاحظات فنية مدروسة باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل إعادة صياغة المتطلبات والتحقق مقابل واقع الكود."},"useCases":{"en":["Evaluating code submissions for technical correctness","Responding to code review feedback with clarity","Verifying codebase requirements before implementation"],"zh":["用于评估代码提交的技术正确性","用清晰度响应代码审查反馈","在实现之前验证代码库需求"],"ja":["コード提出の技術的正しさを評価するために","コードレビューフィードバックに明確性で応答する","実装前にコードベースの要件を検証する"],"ko":["기술적 정확성을 가진 코드 제출을 평가하기위한","코드 리뷰 피드백에 명확성을 가진 응답","구현 전에 코드베이스 요구 사항을 검증하기위한"],"es":["Evaluación de envíos de código para corrección técnica","Respuesta a comentarios de revisión de código con claridad","Verificación de los requisitos de la base de código antes de la implementación"],"fr":["Évaluation des soumissions de code pour la correction technique","Réponse aux commentaires de revue de code avec clarté","Vérification des exigences de la base de code avant la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Bewertung von Code-Eingaben auf technische Richtigkeit","Antworten auf Code-Review-Feedback mit Klarheit","Überprüfung der Codebasis-Anforderungen vor der Implementierung"],"pt":["Avaliar submissões de código para correção técnica","Responder a feedback de revisão de código com clareza","Verificar requisitos da base de código antes da implementação"],"ru":["Оценка представлений кода на техническую правильность","Ответ на обратную связь по коду с ясностью","Проверка требований кодовой базы перед реализацией"],"ar":["تقييم إرسال الكود لصحة فنية","الاستجابة لتعليقات مراجعة الكود بوضوح","التحقق من متطلبات قاعدة الكود قبل التنفيذ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of technical code review principles","Assumes presence of a codebase for verification"],"zh":["需要了解技术代码审查原则","假设代码库存在以便验证"],"ja":["技術的なコードレビューの原則を理解する必要がある","コードベースが存在することを前提として検証する"],"ko":["기술적인 코드 리뷰 원칙을 이해해야함","코드베이스가 존재한다는 가정하에 검증"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de revisión de código técnica","Supone la presencia de una base de código para la verificación"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de revue de code technique","Suppose la présence d''une base de code pour la vérification"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Grundsätze der technischen Code-Review","Geht von der Anwesenheit einer Codebasis für die Überprüfung aus"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de revisão de código técnica","Pressupõe a presença de uma base de código para verificação"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов технической проверки кода","Предполагает наличие кодовой базы для верификации"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ مراجعة الكود الفني","يفترض وجود قاعدة كود للتحقق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
