cribir smart contracts seguros y optimizados. Aprende a prevenir vulnerabilidades y a implementar patrones de desarro...","fr":"Maîtriser la sécurité de Solidity pour écrire des smart contracts sécurisés et optimisés. Apprenez à prévenir les vulnérabilités et à implémenter des modèles...","de":"Meistern Sie die Solidity-Sicherheit, um sichere und optimierte Smart Contracts zu schreiben. Lernen Sie, wie Sie Schwachstellen vermeiden und sichere Entwic...","pt":"Domine as melhores práticas de segurança em Solidity para desenvolver contratos inteligentes seguros e prevenir vulnerabilidades.","ru":"Освойте лучшие практики безопасности Solidity, чтобы разработать безопасные умные контракты и предотвратить уязвимости.","ar":"استمتع بأفضل الممارسات لأمان سوليدتي لتطوير العقود الذكية الآمنة ومنع الثغرات.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Solidity "," ","DeFi ","Reentrancy"," ","gas "],"ja":["Solidity","","DeFi","Reentrancy","","gas"],"ko":["Solidity "," ","DeFi "," "," ","gas "],"es":["Mejores prácticas para la seguridad de smart contracts","Prevención de vulnerabilidades como reentrancy y overflow","Implementación de patrones de desarrollo seguros","Optimización del uso de gas","Preparación de contratos para auditorías profesionales","Comprensión de vectores de ataque comunes"],"fr":["Meilleures pratiques pour la sécurité des smart contracts","Prévention des vulnérabilités telles que la réentrance et le débordement","Implémentation de modèles de développement sécurisés","Optimisation de l''utilisation de gaz","Préparation de contrats pour des audits professionnels","Compréhension des vecteurs d''attaque courants"],"de":["Best Practices für die Sicherheit von Smart Contracts","Vermeidung von Schwachstellen wie Reentrancy und Überlauf","Implementierung sicherer Entwicklungsmodelle","Optimierung des Gasverbrauchs","Vorbereitung von Verträgen für professionelle Audits","Verständnis häufiger Angriffvektoren"],"pt":["Prevenção de reentrancy e overflow","Controle de acesso e autenticação","Otimização do uso de gás","Análise de vulnerabilidades e auditoria","Desenvolvimento de contratos inteligentes seguros","Implementação de protocolos DeFi seguros"],"ru":["Предотвращение повторного входа и переполнения","Контроль доступа и аутентификация","Оптимизация использования газа","Анализ уязвимостей и аудит","Разработка безопасных умных контрактов","Реализация безопасных протоколов DeFi"],"ar":["منع إعادة الدخول والفيضان","مراقبة الوصول والتحقق","تحسين استخدام الغاز","تحليل الثغرات والتدقيق","تطوير العقود الذكية الآمنة","تنفيذ بروتوكولات دي في آمنة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Solidity"," ","DeFi","Reentrancy"," ","gas "," ","Smart Contract"," "],"ja":["Solidity","","DeFi","Reentrancy","","gas","","Smart Contract",""],"ko":["Solidity"," ","DeFi"," "," ","gas "," ","Smart Contract"," "],"es":["seguridad de Solidity","smart contracts seguros","mejores prácticas de seguridad","prevención de vulnerabilidades","optimización de gas","auditorías de seguridad","desarrollo de blockchain","seguridad de DeFi"],"fr":["sécurité de Solidity","smart contracts sécurisés","meilleures pratiques de sécurité","prévention des vulnérabilités","optimisation de gaz","audits de sécurité","développement de blockchain","sécurité de DeFi"],"de":["Solidity-Sicherheit","sichere Smart Contracts","Sicherheitsbest Practices","Schwachstellenvermeidung","Gasoptimierung","Sicherheitsaudits","Blockchain-Entwicklung","DeFi-Sicherheit"],"pt":["segurança em solidity","desenvolvimento de contratos inteligentes","prevenção de vulnerabilidades","otimização de gás","auditoria de contratos","protocolos DeFi seguros","melhores práticas de segurança","desenvolvimento de blockchain","segurança de contratos inteligentes"],"ru":["безопасность solidity","разработка умных контрактов","предотвращение уязвимостей","оптимизация газа","аудит контрактов","безопасные протоколы DeFi","лучшие практики безопасности","разработка блокчейна","безопасность умных контрактов"],"ar":["أمان سوليدتي","تطوير العقود الذكية","منع الثغرات","تحسين الغاز","تدقيق العقود","بروتوكولات دي في آمنة","أفضل الممارسات لأمان","تطوير البلوكشين","أمان العقود الذكية"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.521Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"solidity-security","description":"Master smart contract security best practices to prevent common vulnerabilities and implement secure Solidity patterns. Use when writing smart contracts, auditing existing contracts, or implementing security measures for blockchain applications.","bodyPreview":"# Solidity Security\n\nMaster smart contract security best practices, vulnerability prevention, and secure Solidity development patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing secure smart contracts\n- Auditing existing contracts for vulnerabilities\n- Implementing secure DeFi protocols\n- Preventing reentrancy, overflow, and access control issues\n- Optimizing gas usage while maintaining security\n- Preparing contracts for professional audits\n- Understanding common attack vectors\n\n## Critical Vulnerab","body":"# Solidity Security\n\nMaster smart contract security best practices, vulnerability prevention, and secure Solidity development patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing secure smart contracts\n- Auditing existing contracts for vulnerabilities\n- Implementing secure DeFi protocols\n- Preventing reentrancy, overflow, and access control issues\n- Optimizing gas usage while maintaining security\n- Preparing contracts for professional audits\n- Understanding common attack vectors\n\n## Critical Vulnerabilities\n\n### 1. Reentrancy\n\nAttacker calls back into your contract before state is updated.\n\n**Vulnerable Code:**\n\n```solidity\n// VULNERABLE TO REENTRANCY\ncontract VulnerableBank {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    function withdraw() public {\n        uint256 amount = balances[msg.sender];\n\n        // DANGER: External call before state update\n        (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}(\"\");\n        require(success);\n\n        balances[msg.sender] = 0;  // Too late!\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Secure Pattern (Checks-Effects-Interactions):**\n\n```solidity\ncontract SecureBank {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    function withdraw() public {\n        uint256 amount = balances[msg.sender];\n        require(amount > 0, \"Insufficient balance\");\n\n        // EFFECTS: Update state BEFORE external call\n        balances[msg.sender] = 0;\n\n        // INTERACTIONS: External call last\n        (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}(\"\");\n        require(success, \"Transfer failed\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Alternative: ReentrancyGuard**\n\n```solidity\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/security/ReentrancyGuard.sol\";\n\ncontract SecureBank is ReentrancyGuard {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    function withdraw() public nonReentrant {\n        uint256 amount = balances[msg.sender];\n        require(amount > 0, \"Insufficient balance\");\n\n        balances[msg.sender] = 0;\n\n        (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}(\"\");\n        require(success, \"Transfer failed\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Integer Overflow/Underflow\n\n**Vulnerable Code (Solidity < 0.8.0):**\n\n```solidity\n// VULNERABLE\ncontract VulnerableToken {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public {\n        // No overflow check - can wrap around\n        balances[msg.sender] -= amount;  // Can underflow!\n        balances[to] += amount;          // Can overflow!\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Secure Pattern (Solidity >= 0.8.0):**\n\n```solidity\n// Solidity 0.8+ has built-in overflow/underflow checks\ncontract SecureToken {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public {\n        // Automatically reverts on overflow/underflow\n        balances[msg.sender] -= amount;\n        balances[to] += amount;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**For Solidity < 0.8.0, use SafeMath:**\n\n```solidity\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/math/SafeMath.sol\";\n\ncontract SecureToken {\n    using SafeMath for uint256;\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public {\n        balances[msg.sender] = balances[msg.sender].sub(amount);\n        balances[to] = balances[to].add(amount);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Access Control\n\n**Vulnerable Code:**\n\n```solidity\n// VULNERABLE: Anyone can call critical functions\ncontract VulnerableContract {\n    address public owner;\n\n    function withdraw(uint256 amount) public {\n        // No access control!\n        payable(msg.sender).transfer(amount);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Secure Pattern:**\n\n```solidity\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/access/Ownable.sol\";\n\ncontract SecureContract is Ownable {\n    function withdraw(uint256 amount) public onlyOwner {\n        payable(owner()).transfer(amount);\n    }\n}\n\n// Or implement custom role-based access\ncontract RoleBasedContract {\n    mapping(address => bool) public admins;\n\n    modifier onlyAdmin() {\n        require(admins[msg.sender], \"Not an admin\");\n        _;\n    }\n\n    function criticalFunction() public onlyAdmin {\n        // Protected function\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Front-Running\n\n**Vulnerable:**\n\n```solidity\n// VULNERABLE TO FRONT-RUNNING\ncontract VulnerableDEX {\n    function swap(uint256 amount, uint256 minOutput) public {\n        // Attacker sees this in mempool and front-runs\n        uint256 output = calculateOutput(amount);\n        require(output >= minOutput, \"Slippage too high\");\n        // Perform swap\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Mitigation:**\n\n```solidity\ncontract SecureDEX {\n    mapping(bytes32 => bool) public usedCommitments;\n\n    // Step 1: Commit to trade\n    function commitTrade(bytes32 commitment) public {\n        usedCommitments[commitment] = true;\n    }\n\n    // Step 2: Reveal trade (next block)\n    function revealTrade(\n        uint256 amount,\n        uint256 minOutput,\n        bytes32 secret\n    ) public {\n        bytes32 commitment = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\n            msg.sender, amount, minOutput, secret\n        ));\n        require(usedCommitments[commitment], \"Invalid commitment\");\n        // Perform swap\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\n### Checks-Effects-Interactions Pattern\n\n```solidity\ncontract SecurePattern {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    function withdraw(uint256 amount) public {\n        // 1. CHECKS: Validate conditions\n        require(amount <= balances[msg.sender], \"Insufficient balance\");\n        require(amount > 0, \"Amount must be positive\");\n\n        // 2. EFFECTS: Update state\n        balances[msg.sender] -= amount;\n\n        // 3. INTERACTIONS: External calls last\n        (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}(\"\");\n        require(success, \"Transfer failed\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pull Over Push Pattern\n\n```solidity\n// Prefer this (pull)\ncontract SecurePayment {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public pendingWithdrawals;\n\n    function recordPayment(address recipient, uint256 amount) internal {\n        pendingWithdrawals[recipient] += amount;\n    }\n\n    function withdraw() public {\n        uint256 amount = pendingWithdrawals[msg.sender];\n        require(amount > 0, \"Nothing to withdraw\");\n\n        pendingWithdrawals[msg.sender] = 0;\n        payable(msg.sender).transfer(amount);\n    }\n}\n\n// Over this (push)\ncontract RiskyPayment {\n    function distributePayments(address[] memory recipients, uint256[] memory amounts) public {\n        for (uint i = 0; i < recipients.length; i++) {\n            // If any transfer fails, entire batch fails\n            payable(recipients[i]).transfer(amounts[i]);\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Input Validation\n\n```solidity\ncontract SecureContract {\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public {\n        // Validate inputs\n        require(to != address(0), \"Invalid recipient\");\n        require(to != address(this), \"Cannot send to contract\");\n        require(amount > 0, \"Amount must be positive\");\n        require(amount <= balances[msg.sender], \"Insufficient balance\");\n\n        // Proceed with transfer\n        balances[msg.sender] -= amount;\n        balances[to] += amount;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Emergency Stop (Circuit Breaker)\n\n```solidity\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/security/Pausable.sol\";\n\ncontract EmergencyStop is Pausable, Ownable {\n    function criticalFunction() public whenNotPaused {\n        // Function logic\n    }\n\n    function emergencyStop() public onlyOwner {\n        _pause();\n    }\n\n    function resume() public onlyOwner {\n        _unpause();\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Gas Optimization\n\n### Use `uint256` Instead of Smaller Types\n\n```solidity\n// More gas efficient\ncontract GasEfficient {\n    uint256 public value;  // Optimal\n\n    function set(uint256 _value) public {\n        value = _value;\n    }\n}\n\n// Less efficient\ncontract GasInefficient {\n    uint8 public value;  // Still uses 256-bit slot\n\n    function set(uint8 _value) public {\n        value = _value;  // Extra gas for type conversion\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pack Storage Variables\n\n```solidity\n// Gas efficient (3 variables in 1 slot)\ncontract PackedStorage {\n    uint128 public a;  // Slot 0\n    uint64 public b;   // Slot 0\n    uint64 public c;   // Slot 0\n    uint256 public d;  // Slot 1\n}\n\n// Gas inefficient (each variable in separate slot)\ncontract UnpackedStorage {\n    uint256 public a;  // Slot 0\n    uint256 public b;  // Slot 1\n    uint256 public c;  // Slot 2\n    uint256 public d;  // Slot 3\n}\n```\n\n### Use `calldata` Instead of `memory` for Function Arguments\n\n```solidity\ncontract GasOptimized {\n    // More gas efficient\n    function processData(uint256[] calldata data) public pure returns (uint256) {\n        return data[0];\n    }\n\n    // Less efficient\n    function processDataMemory(uint256[] memory data) public pure returns (uint256) {\n        return data[0];\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Use Events for Data Storage (When Appropriate)\n\n```solidity\ncontract EventStorage {\n    // Emitting events is cheaper than storage\n    event DataStored(address indexed user, uint256 indexed id, bytes data);\n\n    function storeData(uint256 id, bytes calldata data) public {\n        emit DataStored(msg.sender, id, data);\n        // Don''t store in contract storage unless needed\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Common Vulnerabilities Checklist\n\n```solidity\n// Security Checklist Contract\ncontract SecurityChecklist {\n    /**\n     * [ ] Reentrancy protection (ReentrancyGuard or CEI pattern)\n     * [ ] Integer overflow/underflow (Solidity 0.8+ or SafeMath)\n     * [ ] Access control (Ownable, roles, modifiers)\n     * [ ] Input validation (require statements)\n     * [ ] Front-running mitigation (commit-reveal if applicable)\n     * [ ] Gas optimization (packed storage, calldata)\n     * [ ] Emergency stop mechanism (Pausable)\n     * [ ] Pull over push pattern for payments\n     * [ ] No delegatecall to untrusted contracts\n     * [ ] No tx.origin for authentication (use msg.sender)\n     * [ ] Proper event emission\n     * [ ] External calls at end of function\n     * [ ] Check return values of external calls\n     * [ ] No hardcoded addresses\n     * [ ] Upgrade mechanism (if proxy pattern)\n     */\n}\n```\n\n## Testing for Security\n\n```javascript\n// Hardhat test example\nconst { expect } = require(\"chai\");\nconst { ethers } = require(\"hardhat\");\n\ndescribe(\"Security Tests\", function () {\n  it(\"Should prevent reentrancy attack\", async function () {\n    const [attacker] = await ethers.getSigners();\n\n    const VictimBank = await ethers.getContractFactory(\"SecureBank\");\n    const bank = await VictimBank.deploy();\n\n    const Attacker = await ethers.getContractFactory(\"ReentrancyAttacker\");\n    const attackerContract = await Attacker.deploy(bank.address);\n\n    // Deposit funds\n    await bank.deposit({ value: ethers.utils.parseEther(\"10\") });\n\n    // Attempt reentrancy attack\n    await expect(\n      attackerContract.attack({ value: ethers.utils.parseEther(\"1\") }),\n    ).to.be.revertedWith(\"ReentrancyGuard: reentrant call\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"Should prevent integer overflow\", async function () {\n    const Token = await ethers.getContractFactory(\"SecureToken\");\n    const token = await Token.deploy();\n\n    // Attempt overflow\n    await expect(token.transfer(attacker.address, ethers.constants.MaxUint256))\n      .to.be.reverted;\n  });\n\n  it(\"Should enforce access control\", async function () {\n    const [owner, attacker] = await ethers.getSigners();\n\n    const Contract = await ethers.getContractFactory(\"SecureContract\");\n    const contract = await Contract.deploy();\n\n    // Attempt unauthorized withdrawal\n    await expect(contract.connect(attacker).withdraw(100)).to.be.revertedWith(\n      \"Ownable: caller is not the owner\",\n    );\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Audit Preparation\n\n```solidity\ncontract WellDocumentedContract {\n    /**\n     * @title Well Documented Contract\n     * @dev Example of proper documentation for audits\n     * @notice This contract handles user deposits and withdrawals\n     */\n\n    /// @notice Mapping of user balances\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;\n\n    /**\n     * @dev Deposits ETH into the contract\n     * @notice Anyone can deposit funds\n     */\n    function deposit() public payable {\n        require(msg.value > 0, \"Must send ETH\");\n        balances[msg.sender] += msg.value;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @dev Withdraws user''s balance\n     * @notice Follows CEI pattern to prevent reentrancy\n     * @param amount Amount to withdraw in wei\n     */\n    function withdraw(uint256 amount) public {\n        // CHECKS\n        require(amount <= balances[msg.sender], \"Insufficient balance\");\n\n        // EFFECTS\n        balances[msg.sender] -= amount;\n\n        // INTERACTIONS\n        (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}(\"\");\n        require(success, \"Transfer failed\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/reentrancy.md**: Comprehensive reentrancy prevention\n- **references/access-control.md**: Role-based access patterns\n- **references/overflow-underflow.md**: SafeMath and integer safety\n- **references/gas-optimization.md**: Gas saving techniques\n- **references/vulnerability-patterns.md**: Common vulnerability catalog\n- **assets/solidity-contracts-templates.sol**: Secure contract templates\n- **assets/security-checklist.md**: Pre-audit checklist\n- **scripts/analyze-contract.sh**: Static analysis tools\n\n## Tools for Security Analysis\n\n- **Slither**: Static analysis tool\n- **Mythril**: Security analysis tool\n- **Echidna**: Fuzzing tool\n- **Manticore**: Symbolic execution\n- **Securify**: Automated security scanner\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n1. **Using `tx.origin` for Authentication**: Use `msg.sender` instead\n2. **Unchecked External Calls**: Always check return values\n3. **Delegatecall to Untrusted Contracts**: Can hijack your contract\n4. **Floating Pragma**: Pin to specific Solidity version\n5. **Missing Events**: Emit events for state changes\n6. **Excessive Gas in Loops**: Can hit block gas limit\n7. **No Upgrade Path**: Consider proxy patterns if upgrades needed\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:38:12.416Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Blockchain Agents focused on Ethereum smart contract development needing advanced Solidity security auditing and vulnerability prevention capabilities.","zh":"适用于专注于以太坊智能合约开发并需要高级Solidity安全审计和漏洞防御能力的区块链代理。","ja":"イーサリアムスマートコントラクト開発に焦点を当てたブロックチェーンエージェントに適しています。高度なSolidityのセキュリティ監査と脆弱性防止機能が必要です。","ko":"이더리움 스마트 계약 개발에 중점을 둔 블록체인 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 고급 솔리디티 보안 감사 및 취약점 방지 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de Blockchain centrados en el desarrollo de contratos inteligentes de Ethereum que necesitan capacidades de auditoría de seguridad de Solidity avanzadas y prevención de vulnerabilidades.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de Blockchain axés sur le développement de contrats intelligents Ethereum nécessitant des capacités de sécurité avancées d''audit de Solidity et de prévention des vulnérabilités.","de":"Ideal für Blockchain-Agents, die auf die Entwicklung von Ethereum-Smart-Verträgen spezialisiert sind und erweiterte Solidity-Sicherheitsprüf- und Schwachstellenvermeidungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Blockchain focados no desenvolvimento de contratos inteligentes Ethereum que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de auditoria de segurança Solidity e prevenção de vulnerabilidades.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов блокчейна, ориентированных на разработку умных контрактов Ethereum, требующих продвинутых возможностей аудита безопасности Solidity и предотвращения уязвимостей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل البلوكشين الذي يركز على تطوير عقود إيثريوم الذكية التي تحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لتدقيق أمان سوليدتي وتحذير من نقاط الضعف."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement secure DeFi protocols, prevent reentrancy and overflow issues, and optimize gas usage while maintaining security, leveraging Solidity best practices and common attack vector knowledge.","zh":"赋予代理实现安全的DeFi协议、防止重入和溢出问题、优化gas使用同时保持安全性，利用Solidity最佳实践和常见攻击向量知识。","ja":"エージェントがセキュアなDeFiプロトコルを実装し、リエントリやオーバーフロー問題を防ぎ、ガスの使用を最適化しながらセキュリティを維持することを可能にします。Solidityのベストプラクティスと一般的な攻撃ベクトルの知識を活用してください。","ko":"에이전트가 안전한 DeFi 프로토콜을 구현하고 재진입 및 오버플로 문제를 방지하며 가스 사용을 최적화하면서 보안을 유지할 수 있도록 합니다. 솔리디티의 모범 사례와 일반적인 공격 벡터 지식을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar protocolos DeFi seguros, prevenir problemas de reentrada y desbordamiento, y optimizar el uso de gas manteniendo la seguridad, aprovechando las mejores prácticas de Solidity y el conocimiento de los vectores de ataque comunes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des protocoles DeFi sécurisés, de prévenir les problèmes de réentrance et de débordement, et d''optimiser l''utilisation de gaz tout en maintenant la sécurité, en exploitant les meilleures pratiques de Solidity et la connaissance des vecteurs d''attaque courants.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, sichere DeFi-Protokolle umzusetzen, Probleme mit erneuter Eingabe und Überlauf zu verhindern und die Gasnutzung zu optimieren, während die Sicherheit aufrechterhalten wird, indem Solidity-Best-Practices und Kenntnisse über gängige Angriffvektoren genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar protocolos DeFi seguros, prevenir problemas de reentrância e overflow, e otimizar o uso de gás enquanto mantém a segurança, utilizando as melhores práticas de Solidity e conhecimento de vetores de ataque comuns.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать безопасные протоколы DeFi, предотвращать проблемы повторного входа и переполнения, а также оптимизировать использование газа при сохранении безопасности, используя лучшие практики Solidity и знания об общих векторах атак.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ بروتوكولات دي في آمنة ومنع مشاكل إعادة الدخول والفيض، وتحسين استخدام الغاز مع الحفاظ على الأمان، باستخدام أفضل الممارسات لسوليدتي ومعرفة المتجهات الشائعة للهجوم."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing existing smart contracts for security vulnerabilities","Implementing access control and secure data storage in smart contracts","Preventing common attack vectors such as reentrancy and front-running"],"zh":["审计现有的智能合约以发现安全漏洞","在智能合约中实现访问控制和安全数据存储","防止常见的攻击向量，例如重入和抢跑"],"ja":["既存のスマートコントラクトのセキュリティ脆弱性を監査する","スマートコントラクトでアクセス制御とセキュアなデータストレージを実装する","一般的な攻撃ベクトル（リエントリ、フロントランニングなど）を防止する"],"ko":["기존 스마트 계약의 보안 취약성을 감사하는 것","스마트 계약에서 액세스 제어 및 보안 데이터 저장소를 구현하는 것","일반적인 공격 벡터(재진입, 프론트 러닝 등)를 방지하는 것"],"es":["Auditoría de contratos inteligentes existentes para vulnerabilidades de seguridad","Implementación de control de acceso y almacenamiento de datos seguro en contratos inteligentes","Prevención de vectores de ataque comunes como la reentrada y el front-running"],"fr":["Auditorat de contrats intelligents existants pour les vulnérabilités de sécurité","Mise en œuvre du contrôle d''accès et du stockage de données sécurisé dans les contrats intelligents","Prévention des vecteurs d''attaque courants tels que la réentrance et le front-running"],"de":["Prüfung bestehender Smart-Verträge auf Sicherheitsschwachstellen","Implementierung von Zugriffskontrolle und sicherer Datenspeicherung in Smart-Verträgen","Verhinderung gängiger Angriffvektoren wie erneuter Eingabe und Front-Running"],"pt":["Auditoria de contratos inteligentes existentes para vulnerabilidades de segurança","Implementação de controle de acesso e armazenamento de dados seguro em contratos inteligentes","Prevenção de vetores de ataque comuns, como reentrância e front-running"],"ru":["Аудит существующих умных контрактов на уязвимости безопасности","Реализация контроля доступа и безопасного хранения данных в умных контрактах","Предотвращение общих векторов атак, таких как повторный вход и фронт-раннинг"],"ar":["تدقيق العقود الذكية الحالية على نقاط الضعف الأمنية","تنفيذ سيطرة الوصول وتخزين البيانات الآمن في العقود الذكية","منع متجهات الهجوم الشائعة مثل إعادة الدخول والسباق إلى الأمام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Solidity and Ethereum smart contract development","Limited to Ethereum-based blockchain applications"],"zh":["需要Solidity和以太坊智能合约开发的知识","仅限以太坊为基础的区块链应用"],"ja":["Solidityとイーサリアムスマートコントラクト開発の知識が必要","イーサリアムベースのブロックチェーンアプリケーションに限定"],"ko":["솔리디티 및 이더리움 스마트 계약 개발에 대한 지식이 필요합니다.","이더리움 기반 블록체인 애플리케이션으로 제한됩니다."],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de Solidity y desarrollo de contratos inteligentes de Ethereum","Limitado a aplicaciones de blockchain basadas en Ethereum"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en Solidity et en développement de contrats intelligents Ethereum","Limité aux applications de blockchain basées sur Ethereum"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse in Solidity und Ethereum-Smart-Vertrag-Entwicklung","Begrenzt auf Ethereum-basierte Blockchain-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de Solidity e desenvolvimento de contratos inteligentes Ethereum","Limitado a aplicações de blockchain baseadas em Ethereum"],"ru":["Требует знания Solidity и разработки умных контрактов Ethereum","Ограничен для приложений блокчейна на основе Ethereum"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة سوليدتي وتطوير عقود إيثريوم الذكية","محدود للتطبيقات البلوكشين المبنية على إيثريوم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
