 es crucial para organizar características, errores y refactoreo en Conductor. Aprende a crear y gestionar pistas de manera efectiva","fr":"La gestion de pistes est cruciale pour organiser les fonctionnalités, les bogues et les refactoreos dans Conductor. Découvrez comment créer et gérer des pist...","de":"Das Track-Management ist entscheidend für die Organisation von Funktionen, Fehlern und Refactoreos in Conductor. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Tracks effektiv erstel...","pt":"O gerenciamento de faixas é um processo crucial para organizar recursos, bugs e refatorações no Conductor.","ru":"Управление треками является важным процессом для организации функций, ошибок и рефакторинга в Conductor.","ar":"إدارة المسارات هي عملية حاسمة لتنظيم الميزات والأخطاء وإعادة الهيكلة في Conductor.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["创建新功能、错误或重构轨道","编写或审查spec.md文件","创建或更新plan.md文件","管理轨道生命周期","理解轨道状态标记和约定","使用tracks.md文件"],"ja":["新しい機能、バグ、またはリファクタリングトラックの作成","spec.mdファイルの作成またはレビュー","plan.mdファイルの作成または更新","トラックライフサイクルの管理","トラックステータスマーカーと規約の理解","tracks.mdファイルの使用"],"ko":["새로운 기능, 버그 또는 리팩터링 트랙 생성","spec.md 파일 작성 또는 검토","plan.md 파일 생성 또는 업데이트","트랙 生命周期 관리","트랙 상태 마커 및 규약 이해","tracks.md 파일 사용"],"es":["Creación de pistas para características, errores y refactoreo","Gestión del ciclo de vida de las pistas","Comprensión de los indicadores de estado de las pistas","Creación y actualización de archivos spec.md y plan.md","Trabajo con archivos tracks.md","Organización de características, errores y refactoreo"],"fr":["Création de pistes pour les fonctionnalités, les bogues et les refactoreos","Gestion du cycle de vie des pistes","Compréhension des indicateurs d''état des pistes","Création et mise à jour des fichiers spec.md et plan.md","Travail avec les fichiers tracks.md","Organisation des fonctionnalités, des bogues et des refactoreos"],"de":["Erstellung von Tracks für Funktionen, Fehler und Refactoreos","Verwaltung des Lebenszyklus von Tracks","Verständnis der Statusindikatoren von Tracks","Erstellung und Aktualisierung von Dateien spec.md und plan.md","Arbeit mit Dateien tracks.md","Organisation von Funktionen, Fehlern und Refactoreos"],"pt":["Criação de novas faixas de recursos, bugs ou refatorações","Gerenciamento do ciclo de vida da faixa","Entendimento de marcadores de status e convenções","Trabalho com arquivos spec.md e plan.md","Gerenciamento de faixas do início ao fim","Organização de recursos, bugs e refatorações"],"ru":["Создание новых треков функций, ошибок или рефакторинга","Управление жизненным циклом трека","Понимание маркеров статуса и конвенций","Работа с файлами spec.md и plan.md","Управление треками от начала до конца","Организация функций, ошибок и рефакторинга"],"ar":["إنشاء مسارات جديدة للميزات والأخطاء وإعادة الهيكلة","إدارة دورة حياة المسار","فهم علامات الحالة والاتفاقيات","العمل مع الملفات spec.md و plan.md","إدارة المسارات من البداية إلى النهاية","تنظيم الميزات والأخطاء وإعادة الهيكلة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["跟踪管理","Conductor","轨道管理","功能开发","错误修复","重构"],"ja":["トラック管理","Conductor","トラックマネジメント","機能開発","バグ修正","リファクタリング"],"ko":["트랙 관리","Conductor","트랙 관리","기능 개발","버그 수정","리팩터링"],"es":["gestión de pistas","Conductor","características","errores","refactoreo","ciclo de vida de las pistas","indicadores de estado de las pistas","spec.md","plan.md","tracks.md"],"fr":["gestion de pistes","Conductor","fonctionnalités","bogues","refactoreos","cycle de vie des pistes","indicateurs d''état des pistes","spec.md","plan.md","tracks.md"],"de":["Track-Management","Conductor","Funktionen","Fehler","Refactoreos","Lebenszyklus von Tracks","Statusindikatoren von Tracks","spec.md","plan.md","tracks.md"],"pt":["gerenciamento de faixas","Conductor","desenvolvedores","ciclo de vida da faixa","marcadores de status","spec.md","plan.md","organização de recursos"],"ru":["управление треками","Conductor","разработчики","жизненный цикл трека","маркеры статуса","spec.md","plan.md","организация функций"],"ar":["إدارة المسارات","Conductor","مطورين","دورة حياة المسار","علامات الحالة","spec.md","plan.md","تنظيم الميزات"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.521Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"track-management","description":"Use this skill when creating, managing, or working with Conductor tracks - the logical work units for features, bugs, and refactors. Applies to spec.md, plan.md, and track lifecycle operations.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Track Management\n\nGuide for creating, managing, and completing Conductor tracks - the logical work units that organize features, bugs, and refactors through specification, planning, and implementation phases.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating new feature, bug, or refactor tracks\n- Writing or reviewing spec.md files\n- Creating or updating plan.md files\n- Managing track lifecycle from creation to completion\n- Understanding track status markers and conventions\n- Working with the tracks.md re","body":"# Track Management\n\nGuide for creating, managing, and completing Conductor tracks - the logical work units that organize features, bugs, and refactors through specification, planning, and implementation phases.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating new feature, bug, or refactor tracks\n- Writing or reviewing spec.md files\n- Creating or updating plan.md files\n- Managing track lifecycle from creation to completion\n- Understanding track status markers and conventions\n- Working with the tracks.md registry\n- Interpreting or updating track metadata\n\n## Track Concept\n\nA track is a logical work unit that encapsulates a complete piece of work. Each track has:\n\n- A unique identifier\n- A specification defining requirements\n- A phased plan breaking work into tasks\n- Metadata tracking status and progress\n\nTracks provide semantic organization for work, enabling:\n\n- Clear scope boundaries\n- Progress tracking\n- Git-aware operations (revert by track)\n- Team coordination\n\n## Track Types\n\n### feature\n\nNew functionality or capabilities. Use for:\n\n- New user-facing features\n- New API endpoints\n- New integrations\n- Significant enhancements\n\n### bug\n\nDefect fixes. Use for:\n\n- Incorrect behavior\n- Error conditions\n- Performance regressions\n- Security vulnerabilities\n\n### chore\n\nMaintenance and housekeeping. Use for:\n\n- Dependency updates\n- Configuration changes\n- Documentation updates\n- Cleanup tasks\n\n### refactor\n\nCode improvement without behavior change. Use for:\n\n- Code restructuring\n- Pattern adoption\n- Technical debt reduction\n- Performance optimization (same behavior, better performance)\n\n## Track ID Format\n\nTrack IDs follow the pattern: `{shortname}_{YYYYMMDD}`\n\n- **shortname**: 2-4 word kebab-case description (e.g., `user-auth`, `api-rate-limit`)\n- **YYYYMMDD**: Creation date in ISO format\n\nExamples:\n\n- `user-auth_20250115`\n- `fix-login-error_20250115`\n- `upgrade-deps_20250115`\n- `refactor-api-client_20250115`\n\n## Track Lifecycle\n\n### 1. Creation (newTrack)\n\n**Define Requirements**\n\n1. Gather requirements through interactive Q&A\n2. Identify acceptance criteria\n3. Determine scope boundaries\n4. Identify dependencies\n\n**Generate Specification**\n\n1. Create `spec.md` with structured requirements\n2. Document functional and non-functional requirements\n3. Define acceptance criteria\n4. List dependencies and constraints\n\n**Generate Plan**\n\n1. Create `plan.md` with phased task breakdown\n2. Organize tasks into logical phases\n3. Add verification tasks after phases\n4. Estimate effort and complexity\n\n**Register Track**\n\n1. Add entry to `tracks.md` registry\n2. Create track directory structure\n3. Generate `metadata.json`\n4. Create track `index.md`\n\n### 2. Implementation\n\n**Execute Tasks**\n\n1. Select next pending task from plan\n2. Mark task as in-progress\n3. Implement following workflow (TDD)\n4. Mark task complete with commit SHA\n\n**Update Status**\n\n1. Update task markers in plan.md\n2. Record commit SHAs for traceability\n3. Update phase progress\n4. Update track status in tracks.md\n\n**Verify Progress**\n\n1. Complete verification tasks\n2. Wait for checkpoint approval\n3. Record checkpoint commits\n\n### 3. Completion\n\n**Sync Documentation**\n\n1. Update product.md if features added\n2. Update tech-stack.md if dependencies changed\n3. Verify all acceptance criteria met\n\n**Archive or Delete**\n\n1. Mark track as completed in tracks.md\n2. Record completion date\n3. Archive or retain track directory\n\n## Specification (spec.md) Structure\n\n```markdown\n# {Track Title}\n\n## Overview\n\nBrief description of what this track accomplishes and why.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1: {Requirement Name}\n\nDescription of the functional requirement.\n\n- Acceptance: How to verify this requirement is met\n\n### FR-2: {Requirement Name}\n\n...\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### NFR-1: {Requirement Name}\n\nDescription of the non-functional requirement (performance, security, etc.)\n\n- Target: Specific measurable target\n- Verification: How to test\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Criterion 1: Specific, testable condition\n- [ ] Criterion 2: Specific, testable condition\n- [ ] Criterion 3: Specific, testable condition\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n\n- Explicitly included items\n- Features to implement\n- Components to modify\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Explicitly excluded items\n- Future considerations\n- Related but separate work\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Internal\n\n- Other tracks or components this depends on\n- Required context artifacts\n\n### External\n\n- Third-party services or APIs\n- External dependencies\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\n| Risk             | Impact          | Mitigation          |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | ------------------- |\n| Risk description | High/Medium/Low | Mitigation strategy |\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- [ ] Question that needs resolution\n- [x] Resolved question - Answer\n```\n\n## Plan (plan.md) Structure\n\n```markdown\n# Implementation Plan: {Track Title}\n\nTrack ID: `{track-id}`\nCreated: YYYY-MM-DD\nStatus: pending | in-progress | completed\n\n## Overview\n\nBrief description of implementation approach.\n\n## Phase 1: {Phase Name}\n\n### Tasks\n\n- [ ] **Task 1.1**: Task description\n  - Sub-task or detail\n  - Sub-task or detail\n- [ ] **Task 1.2**: Task description\n- [ ] **Task 1.3**: Task description\n\n### Verification\n\n- [ ] **Verify 1.1**: Verification step for phase\n\n## Phase 2: {Phase Name}\n\n### Tasks\n\n- [ ] **Task 2.1**: Task description\n- [ ] **Task 2.2**: Task description\n\n### Verification\n\n- [ ] **Verify 2.1**: Verification step for phase\n\n## Phase 3: Finalization\n\n### Tasks\n\n- [ ] **Task 3.1**: Update documentation\n- [ ] **Task 3.2**: Final integration test\n\n### Verification\n\n- [ ] **Verify 3.1**: All acceptance criteria met\n\n## Checkpoints\n\n| Phase   | Checkpoint SHA | Date | Status  |\n| ------- | -------------- | ---- | ------- |\n| Phase 1 |                |      | pending |\n| Phase 2 |                |      | pending |\n| Phase 3 |                |      | pending |\n```\n\n## Status Marker Conventions\n\nUse consistent markers in plan.md:\n\n| Marker | Meaning     | Usage                       |\n| ------ | ----------- | --------------------------- |\n| `[ ]`  | Pending     | Task not started            |\n| `[~]`  | In Progress | Currently being worked      |\n| `[x]`  | Complete    | Task finished (include SHA) |\n| `[-]`  | Skipped     | Intentionally not done      |\n| `[!]`  | Blocked     | Waiting on dependency       |\n\nExample:\n\n```markdown\n- [x] **Task 1.1**: Set up database schema `abc1234`\n- [~] **Task 1.2**: Implement user model\n- [ ] **Task 1.3**: Add validation logic\n- [!] **Task 1.4**: Integrate auth service (blocked: waiting for API key)\n- [-] **Task 1.5**: Legacy migration (skipped: not needed)\n```\n\n## Track Registry (tracks.md) Format\n\n```markdown\n# Track Registry\n\n## Active Tracks\n\n| Track ID                                         | Type    | Status      | Phase | Started    | Assignee   |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ------- | ----------- | ----- | ---------- | ---------- |\n| [user-auth_20250115](tracks/user-auth_20250115/) | feature | in-progress | 2/3   | 2025-01-15 | @developer |\n| [fix-login_20250114](tracks/fix-login_20250114/) | bug     | pending     | 0/2   | 2025-01-14 | -          |\n\n## Completed Tracks\n\n| Track ID                                       | Type  | Completed  | Duration |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ---------- | -------- |\n| [setup-ci_20250110](tracks/setup-ci_20250110/) | chore | 2025-01-12 | 2 days   |\n\n## Archived Tracks\n\n| Track ID                                             | Reason     | Archived   |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ---------- |\n| [old-feature_20241201](tracks/old-feature_20241201/) | Superseded | 2025-01-05 |\n```\n\n## Metadata (metadata.json) Fields\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"user-auth_20250115\",\n  \"title\": \"User Authentication System\",\n  \"type\": \"feature\",\n  \"status\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"priority\": \"high\",\n  \"created\": \"2025-01-15T10:30:00Z\",\n  \"updated\": \"2025-01-15T14:45:00Z\",\n  \"started\": \"2025-01-15T11:00:00Z\",\n  \"completed\": null,\n  \"assignee\": \"@developer\",\n  \"phases\": {\n    \"total\": 3,\n    \"current\": 2,\n    \"completed\": 1\n  },\n  \"tasks\": {\n    \"total\": 12,\n    \"completed\": 5,\n    \"in_progress\": 1,\n    \"pending\": 6\n  },\n  \"checkpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"phase\": 1,\n      \"sha\": \"abc1234\",\n      \"date\": \"2025-01-15T13:00:00Z\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dependencies\": [],\n  \"tags\": [\"auth\", \"security\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Track Operations\n\n### Creating a Track\n\n1. Run `/conductor:new-track`\n2. Answer interactive questions\n3. Review generated spec.md\n4. Review generated plan.md\n5. Confirm track creation\n\n### Starting Implementation\n\n1. Read spec.md and plan.md\n2. Verify context artifacts are current\n3. Mark first task as `[~]`\n4. Begin TDD workflow\n\n### Completing a Phase\n\n1. Ensure all phase tasks are `[x]`\n2. Complete verification tasks\n3. Wait for checkpoint approval\n4. Record checkpoint SHA\n5. Proceed to next phase\n\n### Completing a Track\n\n1. Verify all phases complete\n2. Verify all acceptance criteria met\n3. Update product.md if needed\n4. Mark track completed in tracks.md\n5. Update metadata.json\n\n### Reverting a Track\n\n1. Run `/conductor:revert`\n2. Select track to revert\n3. Choose granularity (track/phase/task)\n4. Confirm revert operation\n5. Update status markers\n\n## Handling Track Dependencies\n\n### Identifying Dependencies\n\nDuring track creation, identify:\n\n- **Hard dependencies**: Must complete before this track can start\n- **Soft dependencies**: Can proceed in parallel but may affect integration\n- **External dependencies**: Third-party services, APIs, or team decisions\n\n### Documenting Dependencies\n\nIn spec.md, list dependencies with:\n\n- Dependency type (hard/soft/external)\n- Current status (available/pending/blocked)\n- Resolution path (what needs to happen)\n\n### Managing Blocked Tracks\n\nWhen a track is blocked:\n\n1. Mark blocked tasks with `[!]` and reason\n2. Update tracks.md status\n3. Document blocker in metadata.json\n4. Consider creating dependency track if needed\n\n## Track Sizing Guidelines\n\n### Right-Sized Tracks\n\nAim for tracks that:\n\n- Complete in 1-5 days of work\n- Have 2-4 phases\n- Contain 8-20 tasks total\n- Deliver a coherent, testable unit\n\n### Too Large\n\nSigns a track is too large:\n\n- More than 5 phases\n- More than 25 tasks\n- Multiple unrelated features\n- Estimated duration > 1 week\n\nSolution: Split into multiple tracks with clear boundaries.\n\n### Too Small\n\nSigns a track is too small:\n\n- Single phase with 1-2 tasks\n- No meaningful verification needed\n- Could be a sub-task of another track\n- Less than a few hours of work\n\nSolution: Combine with related work or handle as part of existing track.\n\n## Specification Quality Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing spec.md, verify:\n\n### Requirements Quality\n\n- [ ] Each requirement has clear acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Requirements are testable\n- [ ] Requirements are independent (can verify separately)\n- [ ] No ambiguous language (\"should be fast\" → \"response < 200ms\")\n\n### Scope Clarity\n\n- [ ] In-scope items are specific\n- [ ] Out-of-scope items prevent scope creep\n- [ ] Boundaries are clear to implementer\n\n### Dependencies Identified\n\n- [ ] All internal dependencies listed\n- [ ] External dependencies have owners/contacts\n- [ ] Dependency status is current\n\n### Risks Addressed\n\n- [ ] Major risks identified\n- [ ] Impact assessment realistic\n- [ ] Mitigations are actionable\n\n## Plan Quality Checklist\n\nBefore starting implementation, verify plan.md:\n\n### Task Quality\n\n- [ ] Tasks are atomic (one logical action)\n- [ ] Tasks are independently verifiable\n- [ ] Task descriptions are clear\n- [ ] Sub-tasks provide helpful detail\n\n### Phase Organization\n\n- [ ] Phases group related tasks\n- [ ] Each phase delivers something testable\n- [ ] Verification tasks after each phase\n- [ ] Phases build on each other logically\n\n### Completeness\n\n- [ ] All spec requirements have corresponding tasks\n- [ ] Documentation tasks included\n- [ ] Testing tasks included\n- [ ] Integration tasks included\n\n## Common Track Patterns\n\n### Feature Track Pattern\n\n```\nPhase 1: Foundation\n- Data models\n- Database migrations\n- Basic API structure\n\nPhase 2: Core Logic\n- Business logic implementation\n- Input validation\n- Error handling\n\nPhase 3: Integration\n- UI integration\n- API documentation\n- End-to-end tests\n```\n\n### Bug Fix Track Pattern\n\n```\nPhase 1: Reproduction\n- Write failing test capturing bug\n- Document reproduction steps\n\nPhase 2: Fix\n- Implement fix\n- Verify test passes\n- Check for regressions\n\nPhase 3: Verification\n- Manual verification\n- Update documentation if needed\n```\n\n### Refactor Track Pattern\n\n```\nPhase 1: Preparation\n- Add characterization tests\n- Document current behavior\n\nPhase 2: Refactoring\n- Apply changes incrementally\n- Maintain green tests throughout\n\nPhase 3: Cleanup\n- Remove dead code\n- Update documentation\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **One track, one concern**: Keep tracks focused on a single logical change\n2. **Small phases**: Break work into phases of 3-5 tasks maximum\n3. **Verification after phases**: Always include verification tasks\n4. **Update markers immediately**: Mark task status as you work\n5. **Record SHAs**: Always note commit SHAs for completed tasks\n6. **Review specs before planning**: Ensure spec is complete before creating plan\n7. **Link dependencies**: Explicitly note track dependencies\n8. **Archive, don''t delete**: Preserve completed tracks for reference\n9. **Size appropriately**: Keep tracks between 1-5 days of work\n10. **Clear acceptance criteria**: Every requirement must be testable\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:37:58.933Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring structured project management, particularly those working with Conductor tracks and spec.md files.","zh":"适合需要结构化项目管理的开发代理，特别是那些使用 Conductor 跟踪和 spec.md 文件的代理。","ja":"Conductor トラックや spec.md ファイルを使用する開発エージェントが構造化されたプロジェクト管理を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"Conductor 트랙 및 spec.md 파일을 사용하는 개발 에이전트가 구조화된 프로젝트 관리를 필요로 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una gestión de proyectos estructurada, particularmente aquellos que trabajan con pistas de Conductor y archivos spec.md.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une gestion de projet structurée, en particulier ceux qui travaillent avec des pistes Conductor et des fichiers spec.md.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsagenten, die eine strukturierte Projektverwaltung benötigen, insbesondere solche, die mit Conductor-Tracks und spec.md-Dateien arbeiten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem gestão estruturada de projetos, particularmente aqueles que trabalham com tracks do Conductor e arquivos spec.md.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих структурированного управления проектами, особенно для тех, кто работает с треками Conductor и файлами spec.md.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الذين يتطلبون إدارة مشاريع منظمة، وخاصة أولئك الذين يعملون مع مسارات Conductor وملفات spec.md."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage track lifecycles from creation to completion, utilizing track status markers and conventions, and working with tracks.md files to organize features, bugs, and refactors through specification, planning, and implementation phases.","zh":"赋予代理从创建到完成管理跟踪生命周期的能力，利用跟踪状态标记和约定，并使用 tracks.md 文件在规范、规划和实施阶段组织功能、错误和重构。","ja":"エージェントが作成から完了までのトラックライフサイクルを管理できるようにし、トラックステータスマーカーと規約を使用し、specification、planning、実装の各段階で機能、バグ、リファクタリングを tracks.md ファイルで組織できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 생성에서 완료까지의 트랙 생애주기를 관리할 수 있도록 하며, 트랙 상태 마커와 규약을 사용하며, tracks.md 파일을 사용하여 사양, 계획, 구현 단계에서 기능, 버그 및 리팩토링을 조직합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes gestionar los ciclos de vida de las pistas desde la creación hasta la finalización, utilizando marcadores de estado de pista y convenciones, y trabajando con archivos tracks.md para organizar características, errores y refactorizaciones a través de fases de especificación, planificación e implementación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les cycles de vie des pistes de la création à la completion, en utilisant des marqueurs d''état de piste et des conventions, et en travaillant avec des fichiers tracks.md pour organiser les fonctionnalités, les bogues et les refactorisations à travers les phases de spécification, de planification et de mise en œuvre.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Lebenszyklen von Tracks von der Erstellung bis zur Fertigstellung zu verwalten, indem sie Track-Statusmarker und -konventionen verwenden und mit tracks.md-Dateien zusammenarbeiten, um Funktionen, Fehler und Refaktorisierungen durch Spezifikations-, Planungs- und Implementierungsphasen zu organisieren.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a gerenciar ciclos de vida de tracks desde a criação até a conclusão, utilizando marcadores de status de track e convenções, e trabalhando com arquivos tracks.md para organizar funcionalidades, bugs e refatorações através das fases de especificação, planeamento e implementação.","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять жизненным циклом треков от создания до завершения, используя маркеры статуса треков и соглашения, а также работая с файлами tracks.md для организации функций, ошибок и рефакторингов через этапы спецификации, планирования и реализации.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة دورة حياة المسارات من الإنشاء إلى الانتهاء، باستخدام علامات حالة المسار والأعراف، والعمل مع ملفات tracks.md لتنظيم الميزات والأخطاء وإعادة الهيكلة خلال مراحل المواصفات والتخطيط والتنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating and managing new feature, bug, or refactor tracks","Automating spec.md file reviews and updates","Streamlining plan.md file creation and synchronization"],"zh":["创建和管理新的功能、错误或重构跟踪","自动化 spec.md 文件审查和更新","简化 plan.md 文件创建和同步"],"ja":["新しい機能、バグ、またはリファクタリングトラックの作成と管理","spec.md ファイルのレビューと更新の自動化","plan.md ファイルの作成と同期の簡素化"],"ko":["새로운 기능, 버그 또는 리팩토링 트랙의 생성 및 관리","spec.md 파일의 검토 및 업데이트 자동화","plan.md 파일의 생성 및 동기화 단순화"],"es":["Crear y gestionar nuevas pistas de características, errores o refactorizaciones","Automatizar las revisiones y actualizaciones de archivos spec.md","Optimizar la creación y sincronización de archivos plan.md"],"fr":["Créer et gérer de nouvelles pistes de fonctionnalités, de bogues ou de refactorisations","Automatiser les révisions et les mises à jour des fichiers spec.md","Optimiser la création et la synchronisation des fichiers plan.md"],"de":["Erstellen und Verwalten neuer Tracks für Funktionen, Fehler oder Refaktorisierungen","Automatisieren von Überprüfungen und Aktualisierungen von spec.md-Dateien","Optimieren der Erstellung und Synchronisation von plan.md-Dateien"],"pt":["Criar e gerir tracks de novas funcionalidades, bugs ou refatorações","Automatizar revisões e atualizações de ficheiros spec.md","Simplificar a criação e sincronização de ficheiros plan.md"],"ru":["Создание и управление новыми треками функций, ошибок или рефакторинга","Автоматизация проверок и обновлений файлов spec.md","Упрощение создания и синхронизации файлов plan.md"],"ar":["إنشاء وإدارة مسارات الميزات الجديدة أو الأخطاء أو إعادة الهيكلة","أتمتة مراجعات وتحديثات ملفات spec.md","تبسيط إنشاء ومزامنة ملفات plan.md"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Conductor track management conventions","Limited to projects using spec.md and plan.md files","Track management capabilities restricted to Conductor tracks"],"zh":["需要了解 Conductor 跟踪管理约定","仅限使用 spec.md 和 plan.md 文件的项目","跟踪管理功能仅限 Conductor 跟踪"],"ja":["Conductor トラック管理規約の理解が必要","spec.md ファイルと plan.md ファイルを使用するプロジェクトのみに限定","トラック管理機能は Conductor トラックのみに制限"],"ko":["Conductor 트랙 관리 규약의 이해가 필요","spec.md 파일 및 plan.md 파일을 사용하는 프로젝트에만 제한","트랙 관리 기능은 Conductor 트랙에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las convenciones de gestión de pistas de Conductor","Limitado a proyectos que utilizan archivos spec.md y plan.md","Las capacidades de gestión de pistas están restringidas a pistas de Conductor"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des conventions de gestion de pistes Conductor","Limité aux projets utilisant des fichiers spec.md et plan.md","Les capacités de gestion de pistes sont restreintes aux pistes Conductor"],"de":["Benötigt ein Verständnis der Konventionen für die Trackverwaltung von Conductor","Begrenzt auf Projekte, die spec.md- und plan.md-Dateien verwenden","Die Trackverwaltungsfunktionen sind auf Conductor-Tracks beschränkt"],"pt":["Requer compreensão das convenções de gestão de tracks do Conductor","Limitado a projetos que utilizam ficheiros spec.md e plan.md","Capacidades de gestão de tracks restritas a tracks do Conductor"],"ru":["Требует понимания соглашений по управлению треками Conductor","Ограничено проектами, использующими файлы spec.md и plan.md","Возможности управления треками ограничены треками Conductor"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم أعراف إدارة مسارات Conductor","يقتصر على المشاريع التي تستخدم ملفات spec.md و plan.md","قدرات إدارة المسارات تقتصر على مسارات Conductor"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/brainstorming', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'brainstorming', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.521Z', '2026-02-18T13:38:23.799Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/brainstorming","name":"brainstorming","description":{"zh":"脑暴技能帮助开发者将想法转化为完整的设计和规格","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキルは、開発者がアイデアを完全な設計と仕様に変えるのに役立ちます","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 개발자가 아이디어를 완전한 디자인과 사양으로 전환하는 데 도움을 줍니다","es":"El proceso de brainstorming te ayuda a convertir ideas en diseños y especificaciones completas","fr":"Le processus de brainstorming vous aide à convertir des idées en conceptions et spécifications complètes","de":"Der Brainstorming-Prozess hilft Ihnen, Ideen in vollständige Designs und Spezifikationen umzusetzen","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica colaborativa para desenvolver ideias em projetos. Ele envolve entender o contexto do projeto e refinar a ideia por meio de diálogos naturais","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это совместный метод разработки идей в проектах. Он включает понимание контекста проекта и уточнение идеи посредством естественного диалога","ar":"عمليات الإبداع هي تقنية تعاونية لتطوير الأفكار في المشاريع. تتضمن فهم سياق المشروع وتحسين الفكرة من خلال حوارات طبيعية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"协同脑暴设计","ja":"アイデアをデザインに","ko":"아이디어를 디자인으로","es":"Generación de ideas y diseños colaborativos","fr":"Génération d''idées et de conceptions collaboratives","de":"Kollaboratives Ideen- und Designs-Generieren","pt":"Brainstorming: Desenvolva Ideias em Projetos","ru":"Мозговой штурм: разработка идей в проектах","ar":"عمليات إبداعية: تحويل الأفكار إلى تصاميم","en":"brainstorming"},"description":{"zh":"脑暴技能帮助开发者将想法转化为完整的设计和规格","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキルは、開発者がアイデアを完全な設計と仕様に変えるのに役立ちます","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 개발자가 아이디어를 완전한 디자인과 사양으로 전환하는 데 도움을 줍니다","es":"El proceso de brainstorming te ayuda a convertir ideas en diseños y especificaciones completas","fr":"Le processus de brainstorming vous aide à convertir des idées en conceptions et spécifications complètes","de":"Der Brainstorming-Prozess hilft Ihnen, Ideen in vollständige Designs und Spezifikationen umzusetzen","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica colaborativa para desenvolver ideias em projetos. Ele envolve entender o contexto do projeto e refinar a ideia por meio de diál...","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это совместный метод разработки идей в проектах. Он включает понимание контекста проекта и уточнение идеи посредством естественного диалога","ar":"عمليات الإبداع هي تقنية تعاونية لتطوير الأفكار في المشاريع. تتضمن فهم سياق المشروع وتحسين الفكرة من خلال حوارات طبيعية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["理解项目背景","自然协作对话","分段呈现设计","实时反馈","完善设计"],"ja":["プロジェクトの背景を理解","自然なコラボレーションのダイアログ","設計を小さなセクションで提示","リアルタイムのフィードバック","設計を完成させる"],"ko":["프로젝트 배경 이해","자연스러운 협업 대화","디자인을 작은 섹션으로 제시","실시간 피드백","디자인 완성"],"es":["Colaboración natural y diálogo","Refinamiento de ideas a través de preguntas","Presentación de diseños en secciones","Revisión y ajuste de diseños","Generación de especificaciones completas"],"fr":["Collaboration naturelle et dialogue","Affinement des idées à travers des questions","Présentation des conceptions en sections","Révision et ajustement des conceptions","Génération de spécifications complètes"],"de":["Natürliche Kollaboration und Dialog","Verfeinerung von Ideen durch Fragen","Präsentation von Designs in Abschnitten","Überprüfung und Anpassung von Designs","Erstellung von vollständigen Spezifikationen"],"pt":["Entendimento do contexto do projeto","Refinamento da ideia por meio de diálogos","Desenvolvimento de designs e specs","Colaboração natural e iterativa","Revisão e ajuste contínuo"],"ru":["Понимание контекста проекта","Уточнение идеи посредством диалога","Разработка дизайна и спецификаций","Естественное и итеративное сотрудничество","Постоянный обзор и корректировка"],"ar":["فهم سياق المشروع","تحسين الفكرة من خلال الحوار","تطوير التصاميم والمواصفات","التعاون الطبيعي والتكراري","المراجعة والتكيف المستمر"]},"keywords":{"zh":["脑暴设计","协作对话","设计开发","项目管理","软件开发","产品设计"],"ja":["ブレインストーミング設計","コラボレーションのダイアログ","設計開発","プロジェクト管理","ソフトウェア開発","製品設計"],"ko":["브레인스토밍 디자인","협업 대화","디자인 개발","프로젝트 관리","소프트웨어 개발","제품 디자인"],"es":["brainstorming","diseño colaborativo","generación de ideas","desarrollo de proyectos","colaboración en equipo","innovación y creatividad"],"fr":["brainstorming","conception collaborative","génération d''idées","développement de projets","collaboration d''équipe","innovation et créativité"],"de":["brainstorming","kollaboratives Design","Ideen-Generierung","Projektentwicklung","Team-Kollaboration","Innovation und Kreativität"],"pt":["brainstorming para desenvolvedores","desenvolvimento de ideias","colaboração em projetos","design e specs","diálogo natural","refinamento de ideias"],"ru":["мозговой штурм для разработчиков","разработка идей","сотрудничество в проектах","дизайн и спецификации","естественный диалог","уточнение идей"],"ar":["عمليات إبداعية للمطورين","تطوير الأفكار","التعاون في المشاريع","التصاميم والمواصفات","الحوار الطبيعي","تحسين الأفكار"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.521Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation.","bodyPreview":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, d","body":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, docs, recent commits)\n- Ask questions one at a time to refine the idea\n- Prefer multiple choice questions when possible, but open-ended is fine too\n- Only one question per message - if a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple questions\n- Focus on understanding: purpose, constraints, success criteria\n\n**Exploring approaches:**\n- Propose 2-3 different approaches with trade-offs\n- Present options conversationally with your recommendation and reasoning\n- Lead with your recommended option and explain why\n\n**Presenting the design:**\n- Once you believe you understand what you''re building, present the design\n- Break it into sections of 200-300 words\n- Ask after each section whether it looks right so far\n- Cover: architecture, components, data flow, error handling, testing\n- Be ready to go back and clarify if something doesn''t make sense\n\n## After the Design\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Write the validated design to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md`\n- Use elements-of-style:writing-clearly-and-concisely skill if available\n- Commit the design document to git\n\n**Implementation (if continuing):**\n- Ask: \"Ready to set up for implementation?\"\n- Use superpowers:using-git-worktrees to create isolated workspace\n- Use superpowers:writing-plans to create detailed implementation plan\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- **One question at a time** - Don''t overwhelm with multiple questions\n- **Multiple choice preferred** - Easier to answer than open-ended when possible\n- **YAGNI ruthlessly** - Remove unnecessary features from all designs\n- **Explore alternatives** - Always propose 2-3 approaches before settling\n- **Incremental validation** - Present design in sections, validate each\n- **Be flexible** - Go back and clarify when something doesn''t make sense\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:38:23.799Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Collaborative Agents needing advanced natural language processing capabilities for idea refinement and design specification.","zh":"非常适合需要先进自然语言处理能力以进行想法细化和设计规范制定的协作型智能体。","ja":"アイデアの洗練と設計仕様のための高度な自然言語処理能力を必要とする協働エージェントに最適です。","ko":"아이디어 구체화 및 설계 명세를 위한 고급 자연어 처리 기능이 필요한 협업 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes colaborativos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de procesamiento de lenguaje natural para la refinación de ideas y la especificación de diseños.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents collaboratifs ayant besoin de capacités avancées de traitement du langage naturel pour l''affinement des idées et la spécification de la conception.","de":"Perfekt für kollaborierende Agenten, die erweiterte natürliche Sprachverarbeitungsfähigkeiten für die Verfeinerung von Ideen und die Designspezifikation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Colaborativos que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de processamento de linguagem natural para refinamento de ideias e especificação de design.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Коллаборативных Агентов, которым требуются продвинутые возможности обработки естественного языка для усовершенствования идей и спецификации дизайна.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التعاونيين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة في معالجة اللغة الطبيعية لتحسين الأفكار وتصميم المواصفات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to engage in collaborative dialogue, refining ideas through iterative questioning and presenting designs in manageable sections, utilizing natural language understanding and generation capabilities.","zh":"使智能体能够参与协作对话，通过迭代式提问细化想法，并以可管理部分呈现设计方案，利用自然语言理解和生成能力。","ja":"自然言語理解と生成能力を活用し、反復的な質問を通じてアイデアを洗練し、管理可能なセクションで設計を提示する協働対話にエージェントを参加させます。","ko":"자연어 이해 및 생성 기능을 활용하여 반복적인 질의를 통해 아이디어를 구체화하고 관리 가능한 섹션으로 설계를 제시하는 협업 대화에 에이전트가 참여할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a participar en diálogos colaborativos, refinando ideas a través de preguntas iterativas y presentando diseños en secciones manejables, utilizando capacidades de comprensión y generación de lenguaje natural.","fr":"Permet aux agents de s''engager dans des dialogues collaboratifs, en affinant les idées par des questions itératives et en présentant les conceptions en sections gérables, en utilisant les capacités de compréhension et de génération de langage naturel.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, an kollaborativen Dialogen teilzunehmen, Ideen durch iterative Fragen zu verfeinern und Entwürfe in handhabbaren Abschnitten vorzustellen, indem sie Fähigkeiten zur Verständigung und Generierung natürlicher Sprache nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se engajarem em diálogos colaborativos, refinando ideias por meio de questionamentos iterativos e apresentando projetos em seções gerenciáveis, utilizando capacidades de compreensão e geração de linguagem natural.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью участвовать в коллаборативном диалоге, усовершенствовании идей посредством итеративного вопросования и представлении дизайна в управляемых разделах, используя возможности понимания и генерации естественного языка.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على المشاركة في حوار تعاوني، وتصفية الأفكار من خلال أسئلة متكررة وعرض التصاميم في أقسام قابلة للإدارة، باستخدام قدرات فهم اللغة الطبيعية وتوليدها."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining project ideas through collaborative questioning","Generating design specifications from natural language inputs","Iteratively presenting and refining design sections"],"zh":["通过协作提问细化项目想法","根据自然语言输入生成设计规范","迭代式呈现和细化设计部分"],"ja":["協働的な質問を通じたプロジェクトアイデアの洗練","自然言語入力からの設計仕様の生成","反復的な設計セクションの提示と洗練"],"ko":["협업 질의를 통한 프로젝트 아이디어 구체화","자연어 입력으로부터 설계 명세 생성","반복적인 설계 섹션 제시 및 구체화"],"es":["Perfeccionar ideas de proyecto a través de preguntas colaborativas","Generar especificaciones de diseño a partir de entradas de lenguaje natural","Presentar y perfeccionar secciones de diseño de manera iterativa"],"fr":["Affiner les idées de projet par des questions collaboratives","Générer des spécifications de conception à partir d''entrées de langage naturel","Présenter et affiner des sections de conception de manière itérative"],"de":["Projektideen durch kollaborative Fragen verfeinern","Entwurfspezifikationen aus natürlichen Spracheneingaben generieren","Entwurfsabschnitte iterativ präsentieren und verfeinern"],"pt":["Refinamento de ideias de projeto por meio de questionamentos colaborativos","Geração de especificações de design a partir de entradas de linguagem natural","Apresentação e refinamento iterativo de seções de design"],"ru":["Усовершенствование идей проекта посредством коллаборативного вопросования","Генерация спецификаций дизайна из входных данных естественного языка","Итеративное представление и усовершенствование разделов дизайна"],"ar":["تحسين أفكار المشروع من خلال أسئلة تعاونية","توليد مواصفات التصميم من مدخلات اللغة الطبيعية","عرض وتحسين أقسام التصميم بشكل متكرر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires natural language understanding and generation capabilities","Dependent on project context and available files or data"],"zh":["需要自然语言理解和生成能力","依赖于项目上下文和可用文件或数据"],"ja":["自然言語理解と生成能力が必要","プロジェクトのコンテキストと利用可能なファイルまたはデータに依存"],"ko":["자연어 이해 및 생성 기능 필요","프로젝트 컨텍스트 및 사용 가능한 파일 또는 데이터에 의존"],"es":["Requiere capacidades de comprensión y generación de lenguaje natural","Depende del contexto del proyecto y de los archivos o datos disponibles"],"fr":["Nécessite des capacités de compréhension et de génération de langage naturel","Dépend du contexte du projet et des fichiers ou données disponibles"],"de":["Benötigt Fähigkeiten zur Verständigung und Generierung natürlicher Sprache","Hängt vom Projektzusammenhang und den verfügbaren Dateien oder Daten ab"],"pt":["Exige capacidades de compreensão e geração de linguagem natural","Dependente do contexto do projeto e dos arquivos ou dados disponíveis"],"ru":["Требует возможностей понимания и генерации естественного языка","Зависит от контекста проекта и доступных файлов или данных"],"ar":["يتطلب قدرات فهم اللغة الطبيعية وتوليدها","يعتمد على سياق المشروع والملفات أو البيانات المتاحة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
