ricas de receita","Eficiência de crescimento","Gestão de caixa","Análise de unidades econômicas","Otimização de métricas para captação de recursos","Excelência operacional"],"ru":["Метрики выручки","Эффективность роста","Управление денежными средствами","Анализ экономических единиц","Оптимизация метрик для привлечения средств","Операционное совершенство"],"ar":["مقاييس الإيرادات","كفاءة النمو","إدارة السيولة النقدية","تحليل الوحدات الاقتصادية","أتمتة مقاييس لجلب الأموال","الكمال التشغيلي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["启动指标框架","启动业务模型","关键绩效指标","成长效率","现金管理","运用优位性","筹资能力"],"ja":["スタートアップメトリクスフレームワーク","スタートアップビジネスモデル","重要なパフォーマンス指標","成長効率","キャッシュマネジメント","運用の優位性","資金調達能力"],"ko":["스타트업 메트릭스 프레임워크","스타트업 비즈니스 모델","핵심 성과 지표","성장 효율성","현금 관리","운용의 우위성","자금 조달 능력"],"es":["métricas de startup","MRR","eficiencia del crecimiento","gestión del efectivo","economía de unidades","recaudación de fondos","excelencia operativa"],"fr":["métriques de startup","MRR","efficacité de la croissance","gestion de la trésorerie","économie des unités","collecte de fonds","excellence opérationnelle"],"de":["Startup-Metriken","MRR","Wachstumseffizienz","Bargeldmanagement","Einheitökonomie","Geldbeschaffung","betriebliche Exzellenz"],"pt":["métricas de startup","rastreamento de métricas","otimização de desempenho","receita mensal recorrente","eficiência de crescimento","gestão de caixa","análise de unidades econômicas","captação de recursos"],"ru":["метрики стартапа","отслеживание метрик","оптимизация эффективности","месячный рекуррентный доход","эффективность роста","управление денежными средствами","анализ экономических единиц","привлечение средств"],"ar":["مقاييس الشركات الناشئة","تتبع المقاييس","أتمتة الأداء","إيرادات شهرية متكررة","كفاءة النمو","إدارة السيولة النقدية","تحليل الوحدات الاقتصادية","جلب الأموال"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.521Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"startup-metrics-framework","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks about key startup metrics, SaaS metrics, CAC and LTV, unit economics, burn multiple, rule of 40, marketplace metrics, or requests guidance on tracking and optimizing business performance metrics.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Startup Metrics Framework\n\nComprehensive guide to tracking, calculating, and optimizing key performance metrics for different startup business models from seed through Series A.\n\n## Overview\n\nTrack the right metrics at the right stage. Focus on unit economics, growth efficiency, and cash management metrics that matter for fundraising and operational excellence.\n\n## Universal Startup Metrics\n\n### Revenue Metrics\n\n**MRR (Monthly Recurring Revenue)**\n\n```\nMRR = Σ (Active Subscriptions × Monthly P","body":"# Startup Metrics Framework\n\nComprehensive guide to tracking, calculating, and optimizing key performance metrics for different startup business models from seed through Series A.\n\n## Overview\n\nTrack the right metrics at the right stage. Focus on unit economics, growth efficiency, and cash management metrics that matter for fundraising and operational excellence.\n\n## Universal Startup Metrics\n\n### Revenue Metrics\n\n**MRR (Monthly Recurring Revenue)**\n\n```\nMRR = Σ (Active Subscriptions × Monthly Price)\n```\n\n**ARR (Annual Recurring Revenue)**\n\n```\nARR = MRR × 12\n```\n\n**Growth Rate**\n\n```\nMoM Growth = (This Month MRR - Last Month MRR) / Last Month MRR\nYoY Growth = (This Year ARR - Last Year ARR) / Last Year ARR\n```\n\n**Target Benchmarks:**\n\n- Seed stage: 15-20% MoM growth\n- Series A: 10-15% MoM growth, 3-5x YoY\n- Series B+: 100%+ YoY (Rule of 40)\n\n### Unit Economics\n\n**CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost)**\n\n```\nCAC = Total S&M Spend / New Customers Acquired\n```\n\nInclude: Sales salaries, marketing spend, tools, overhead\n\n**LTV (Lifetime Value)**\n\n```\nLTV = ARPU × Gross Margin% × (1 / Churn Rate)\n```\n\nSimplified:\n\n```\nLTV = ARPU × Average Customer Lifetime × Gross Margin%\n```\n\n**LTV:CAC Ratio**\n\n```\nLTV:CAC = LTV / CAC\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- LTV:CAC > 3.0 = Healthy\n- LTV:CAC 1.0-3.0 = Needs improvement\n- LTV:CAC < 1.0 = Unsustainable\n\n**CAC Payback Period**\n\n```\nCAC Payback = CAC / (ARPU × Gross Margin%)\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- < 12 months = Excellent\n- 12-18 months = Good\n- > 24 months = Concerning\n\n### Cash Efficiency Metrics\n\n**Burn Rate**\n\n```\nMonthly Burn = Monthly Revenue - Monthly Expenses\n```\n\nNegative burn = losing money (typical early-stage)\n\n**Runway**\n\n```\nRunway (months) = Cash Balance / Monthly Burn Rate\n```\n\n**Target:** Always maintain 12-18 months runway\n\n**Burn Multiple**\n\n```\nBurn Multiple = Net Burn / Net New ARR\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- < 1.0 = Exceptional efficiency\n- 1.0-1.5 = Good\n- 1.5-2.0 = Acceptable\n- > 2.0 = Inefficient\n\nLower is better (spending less to generate ARR)\n\n## SaaS Metrics\n\n### Revenue Composition\n\n**New MRR**\nNew customers × ARPU\n\n**Expansion MRR**\nUpsells and cross-sells from existing customers\n\n**Contraction MRR**\nDowngrades from existing customers\n\n**Churned MRR**\nLost customers\n\n**Net New MRR Formula:**\n\n```\nNet New MRR = New MRR + Expansion MRR - Contraction MRR - Churned MRR\n```\n\n### Retention Metrics\n\n**Logo Retention**\n\n```\nLogo Retention = (Customers End - New Customers) / Customers Start\n```\n\n**Dollar Retention (NDR - Net Dollar Retention)**\n\n```\nNDR = (ARR Start + Expansion - Contraction - Churn) / ARR Start\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- NDR > 120% = Best-in-class\n- NDR 100-120% = Good\n- NDR < 100% = Needs work\n\n**Gross Retention**\n\n```\nGross Retention = (ARR Start - Churn - Contraction) / ARR Start\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- > 90% = Excellent\n- 85-90% = Good\n- < 85% = Concerning\n\n### SaaS-Specific Metrics\n\n**Magic Number**\n\n```\nMagic Number = Net New ARR (quarter) / S&M Spend (prior quarter)\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- > 0.75 = Efficient, ready to scale\n- 0.5-0.75 = Moderate efficiency\n- < 0.5 = Inefficient, don''t scale yet\n\n**Rule of 40**\n\n```\nRule of 40 = Revenue Growth Rate% + Profit Margin%\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- > 40% = Excellent\n- 20-40% = Acceptable\n- < 20% = Needs improvement\n\n**Example:**\n50% growth + (10%) margin = 40% ✓\n\n**Quick Ratio**\n\n```\nQuick Ratio = (New MRR + Expansion MRR) / (Churned MRR + Contraction MRR)\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- > 4.0 = Healthy growth\n- 2.0-4.0 = Moderate\n- < 2.0 = Churn problem\n\n## Marketplace Metrics\n\n### GMV (Gross Merchandise Value)\n\n**Total Transaction Volume:**\n\n```\nGMV = Σ (Transaction Value)\n```\n\n**Growth Rate:**\n\n```\nGMV Growth Rate = (Current Period GMV - Prior Period GMV) / Prior Period GMV\n```\n\n**Target:** 20%+ MoM early-stage\n\n### Take Rate\n\n```\nTake Rate = Net Revenue / GMV\n```\n\n**Typical Ranges:**\n\n- Payment processors: 2-3%\n- E-commerce marketplaces: 10-20%\n- Service marketplaces: 15-25%\n- High-value B2B: 5-15%\n\n### Marketplace Liquidity\n\n**Time to Transaction**\nHow long from listing to sale/match?\n\n**Fill Rate**\n% of requests that result in transaction\n\n**Repeat Rate**\n% of users who transact multiple times\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- Fill rate > 80% = Strong liquidity\n- Repeat rate > 60% = Strong retention\n\n### Marketplace Balance\n\n**Supply/Demand Ratio:**\nTrack relative growth of supply and demand sides.\n\n**Warning Signs:**\n\n- Too much supply: Low fill rates, frustrated suppliers\n- Too much demand: Long wait times, frustrated customers\n\n**Goal:** Balanced growth (1:1 ratio ideal, but varies by model)\n\n## Consumer/Mobile Metrics\n\n### Engagement Metrics\n\n**DAU (Daily Active Users)**\nUnique users active each day\n\n**MAU (Monthly Active Users)**\nUnique users active each month\n\n**DAU/MAU Ratio**\n\n```\nDAU/MAU = DAU / MAU\n```\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- > 50% = Exceptional (daily habit)\n- 20-50% = Good\n- < 20% = Weak engagement\n\n**Session Frequency**\nAverage sessions per user per day/week\n\n**Session Duration**\nAverage time spent per session\n\n### Retention Curves\n\n**Day 1 Retention:** % users who return next day\n**Day 7 Retention:** % users active 7 days after signup\n**Day 30 Retention:** % users active 30 days after signup\n\n**Benchmarks (Day 30):**\n\n- > 40% = Excellent\n- 25-40% = Good\n- < 25% = Weak\n\n**Retention Curve Shape:**\n\n- Flattening curve = good (users becoming habitual)\n- Steep decline = poor product-market fit\n\n### Viral Coefficient (K-Factor)\n\n```\nK-Factor = Invites per User × Invite Conversion Rate\n```\n\n**Example:**\n10 invites/user × 20% conversion = 2.0 K-factor\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n- K > 1.0 = Viral growth\n- K = 0.5-1.0 = Strong referrals\n- K < 0.5 = Weak virality\n\n## B2B Metrics\n\n### Sales Efficiency\n\n**Win Rate**\n\n```\nWin Rate = Deals Won / Total Opportunities\n```\n\n**Target:** 20-30% for new sales team, 30-40% mature\n\n**Sales Cycle Length**\nAverage days from opportunity to close\n\n**Shorter is better:**\n\n- SMB: 30-60 days\n- Mid-market: 60-120 days\n- Enterprise: 120-270 days\n\n**Average Contract Value (ACV)**\n\n```\nACV = Total Contract Value / Contract Length (years)\n```\n\n### Pipeline Metrics\n\n**Pipeline Coverage**\n\n```\nPipeline Coverage = Total Pipeline Value / Quota\n```\n\n**Target:** 3-5x coverage (3-5x pipeline needed to hit quota)\n\n**Conversion Rates by Stage:**\n\n- Lead → Opportunity: 10-20%\n- Opportunity → Demo: 50-70%\n- Demo → Proposal: 30-50%\n- Proposal → Close: 20-40%\n\n## Metrics by Stage\n\n### Pre-Seed (Product-Market Fit)\n\n**Focus Metrics:**\n\n1. Active users growth\n2. User retention (Day 7, Day 30)\n3. Core engagement (sessions, features used)\n4. Qualitative feedback (NPS, interviews)\n\n**Don''t worry about:**\n\n- Revenue (may be zero)\n- CAC (not optimizing yet)\n- Unit economics\n\n### Seed ($500K-$2M ARR)\n\n**Focus Metrics:**\n\n1. MRR growth rate (15-20% MoM)\n2. CAC and LTV (establish baseline)\n3. Gross retention (> 85%)\n4. Core product engagement\n\n**Start tracking:**\n\n- Sales efficiency\n- Burn rate and runway\n\n### Series A ($2M-$10M ARR)\n\n**Focus Metrics:**\n\n1. ARR growth (3-5x YoY)\n2. Unit economics (LTV:CAC > 3, payback < 18 months)\n3. Net dollar retention (> 100%)\n4. Burn multiple (< 2.0)\n5. Magic number (> 0.5)\n\n**Mature tracking:**\n\n- Rule of 40\n- Sales efficiency\n- Pipeline coverage\n\n## Metric Tracking Best Practices\n\n### Data Infrastructure\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n- Single source of truth (analytics platform)\n- Real-time or daily updates\n- Automated calculations\n- Historical tracking\n\n**Tools:**\n\n- Mixpanel, Amplitude (product analytics)\n- ChartMogul, Baremetrics (SaaS metrics)\n- Looker, Tableau (BI dashboards)\n\n### Reporting Cadence\n\n**Daily:**\n\n- MRR, active users\n- Sign-ups, conversions\n\n**Weekly:**\n\n- Growth rates\n- Retention cohorts\n- Sales pipeline\n\n**Monthly:**\n\n- Full metric suite\n- Board reporting\n- Investor updates\n\n**Quarterly:**\n\n- Trend analysis\n- Benchmarking\n- Strategy review\n\n### Common Mistakes\n\n**Mistake 1: Vanity Metrics**\nDon''t focus on:\n\n- Total users (without retention)\n- Page views (without engagement)\n- Downloads (without activation)\n\nFocus on actionable metrics tied to value.\n\n**Mistake 2: Too Many Metrics**\nTrack 5-7 core metrics intensely, not 50 loosely.\n\n**Mistake 3: Ignoring Unit Economics**\nCAC and LTV are critical even at seed stage.\n\n**Mistake 4: Not Segmenting**\nBreak down metrics by customer segment, channel, cohort.\n\n**Mistake 5: Gaming Metrics**\nOptimize for real business outcomes, not dashboard numbers.\n\n## Investor Metrics\n\n### What VCs Want to See\n\n**Seed Round:**\n\n- MRR growth rate\n- User retention\n- Early unit economics\n- Product engagement\n\n**Series A:**\n\n- ARR and growth rate\n- CAC payback < 18 months\n- LTV:CAC > 3.0\n- Net dollar retention > 100%\n- Burn multiple < 2.0\n\n**Series B+:**\n\n- Rule of 40 > 40%\n- Efficient growth (magic number)\n- Path to profitability\n- Market leadership metrics\n\n### Metric Presentation\n\n**Dashboard Format:**\n\n```\nCurrent MRR: $250K (↑ 18% MoM)\nARR: $3.0M (↑ 280% YoY)\nCAC: $1,200 | LTV: $4,800 | LTV:CAC = 4.0x\nNDR: 112% | Logo Retention: 92%\nBurn: $180K/mo | Runway: 18 months\n```\n\n**Include:**\n\n- Current value\n- Growth rate or trend\n- Context (target, benchmark)\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Reference Files\n\n- **`references/metric-definitions.md`** - Complete definitions and formulas for 50+ metrics\n- **`references/benchmarks-by-stage.md`** - Target ranges for each metric by company stage\n- **`references/calculation-examples.md`** - Step-by-step calculation examples\n\n### Example Files\n\n- **`examples/saas-metrics-dashboard.md`** - Complete metrics suite for B2B SaaS company\n- **`examples/marketplace-metrics.md`** - Marketplace-specific metrics with examples\n- **`examples/investor-metrics-deck.md`** - How to present metrics for fundraising\n\n## Quick Start\n\nTo implement startup metrics framework:\n\n1. **Identify business model** - SaaS, marketplace, consumer, B2B\n2. **Choose 5-7 core metrics** - Based on stage and model\n3. **Establish tracking** - Set up analytics and dashboards\n4. **Calculate unit economics** - CAC, LTV, payback\n5. **Set targets** - Use benchmarks for goals\n6. **Review regularly** - Weekly for core metrics\n7. **Share with team** - Align on goals and progress\n8. **Update investors** - Monthly/quarterly reporting\n\nFor detailed definitions, benchmarks, and examples, see `references/` and `examples/`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:39:31.633Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Business Intelligence Agents requiring advanced startup metrics analysis and visualization for fundraising and operational excellence.","zh":"适用于需要高级启动指标分析和可视化的商业智能代理，以实现筹资和运营卓越。","ja":"ビジネスインテリジェンスエージェントが高度な起動メトリクス分析および可視化を必要とする場合に最適です。基金調達および運用の優れたエージェントに。","ko":"고급 시작 메트릭 분석 및 시각화를 요구하는 비즈니스 인텔리전스 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 자금 조달 및 운영 우수성에 대한 에이전트입니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Inteligencia Empresarial que requieren análisis de métricas de inicio avanzadas y visualización para recaudación de fondos y excelencia operativa.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence commerciale nécessitant une analyse de métriques de démarrage avancée et une visualisation pour la collecte de fonds et l''excellence opérationnelle.","de":"Ideal für Business-Intelligence-Agenten, die erweiterte Startmetrikenanalyse und Visualisierung für die Beschaffung von Mitteln und betriebliche Exzellenz benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Inteligência de Negócios que exigem análise avançada de métricas de inicialização e visualização para captação de recursos e excelência operacional.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов бизнес-интеллекта, требующих продвинутого анализа метрик запуска и визуализации для сбора средств и операционного совершенства.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء استخبارات الأعمال الذين يتطلبون تحليل متقدم لمرتكزات التشغيل ومؤشرات الأداء للتمويل والتميز التشغيلي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to track and calculate key performance metrics such as MRR, unit economics, and growth efficiency, utilizing data visualization libraries for informed decision-making and optimized cash management strategies.","zh":"赋予代理跟踪和计算关键绩效指标，例如月度经常性收入（MRR）、单位经济学和增长效率，利用数据可视化库进行明智的决策和优化的现金管理策略。","ja":"エージェントに、月々の定期収入（MRR）、ユニットエコノミクス、成長効率などの重要なパフォーマンスメトリクスを追跡して計算する力を与え、データ視覚化ライブラリを使用して情報に基づいた意思決定と最適化されたキャッシュ管理戦略を実現する。","ko":"에이전트가 월간 반복 수익(MRR), 단위 경제학 및 성장 효율성等의 주요 성과 지표를 추적하고 계산할 수 있도록하여 데이터 시각화 라이브러리를 사용하여 정보에 기반한 의사 결정과 최적화된 현금 관리 전략을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes realizar un seguimiento y calcular métricas de rendimiento clave como MRR, economía de unidades y eficiencia de crecimiento, utilizando bibliotecas de visualización de datos para la toma de decisiones informadas y estrategias de gestión de efectivo optimizadas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de suivre et de calculer des métriques de performance clés telles que MRR, économie d''unités et efficacité de croissance, en utilisant des bibliothèques de visualisation de données pour une prise de décision éclairée et des stratégies de gestion de trésorerie optimisées.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Schlüsselleistungsindikatoren wie MRR, Einheiteneonomie und Wachstumseffizienz zu verfolgen und zu berechnen, unter Nutzung von Datenvisualisierungsbibliotheken für eine fundierte Entscheidungsfindung und optimierte Bargeldmanagementstrategien.","pt":"Habilita agentes a rastrear e calcular métricas de desempenho-chave, como MRR, economia unitária e eficiência de crescimento, utilizando bibliotecas de visualização de dados para tomada de decisões informadas e estratégias de gestão de caixa otimizadas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отслеживать и рассчитывать ключевые показатели эффективности, такие как MRR, экономика единицы и эффективность роста, используя библиотеки визуализации данных для принятия обоснованных решений и оптимизированных стратегий управления денежными средствами.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تتبع وحساب مقاييس الأداء الرئيسية مثل إيرادات الشهر المتكرر (MRR) واقتصاد الوحدة وفعّالية النمو، مستخدمين مكتبات تمثيل البيانات لاتخاذ القرارات المُستنيرة واستراتيجيات الإدارة النقدية المُحسنة."},"useCases":{"en":["Calculating Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) for subscription-based startups","Analyzing unit economics for e-commerce businesses","Optimizing growth efficiency metrics for Series A fundraising"],"zh":["计算基于订阅的创业公司的月度经常性收入（MRR）","分析电子商务企业的单位经济学","优化为系列A筹资提供增长效率指标"],"ja":["サブスクリプションベースのスタートアップの月々の定期収入（MRR）を計算する","電子商取引ビジネスのユニットエコノミクスを分析する","シリーズAの資金調達のために成長効率メトリクスを最適化する"],"ko":["구독 기반 스타트업의 월간 반복 수익(MRR) 계산","전자상거래 비즈니스 단위 경제학 분석","시리즈 A 자금 조달을 위한 성장 효율성 지표 최적화"],"es":["Cálculo de la Recaudación Mensual Recurrente (MRR) para startups de suscripción","Análisis de la economía de unidades para empresas de comercio electrónico","Optimización de las métricas de eficiencia de crecimiento para la recaudación de fondos de Serie A"],"fr":["Calcul du Revenu Mensuel Récurrent (MRR) pour les startups à abonnement","Analyse de l''économie d''unités pour les entreprises de commerce électronique","Optimisation des métriques d''efficacité de croissance pour le financement de série A"],"de":["Berechnung des monatlichen wiederkehrenden Umsatzes (MRR) für Abonnement-Startups","Analyse der Einheiteneonomie für E-Commerce-Unternehmen","Optimierung der Wachstumseffizienzmetriken für die Finanzierungsrunde Series A"],"pt":["Calculando a Receita Mensal Recorrente (MRR) para startups baseadas em assinatura","Analisando a economia unitária para empresas de comércio eletrônico","Otimizando métricas de eficiência de crescimento para captação de recursos da Série A"],"ru":["Расчет ежемесячного повторяющегося дохода (MRR) для стартапов, основанных на подписке","Анализ экономики единицы для электронных коммерческих предприятий","Оптимизация показателей эффективности роста для сбора средств серии А"],"ar":["حساب الإيرادات الشهريّة المتكررة (MRR) لاستارتآب القائمة على الاشتراك","تحليل اقتصاد الوحدة لشركات التجارة الإلكترونية","تحسين مقاييس فعّالية النمو لجمع التمويل من السلسلة أ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of startup business models and key performance metrics","Focused on seed through Series A stage startups"],"zh":["需要了解启动商业模式和关键绩效指标的知识","专注于种子至系列A阶段的启动商业"],"ja":["起動ビジネスモデルと重要なパフォーマンスメトリクスの知識が必要","シードステージからシリーズAステージまでの起動ビジネスに焦点を当てている"],"ko":["启动 비즈니스 모델 및 주요 성과 지표에 대한 지식이 필요","시드 단계에서 시리즈 A 단계까지의 시작 비즈니스에 중점을 두고 있습니다"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de los modelos de negocio de las startups y los indicadores clave de rendimiento","Se centra en startups en etapa de semilla a Serie A"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des modèles d''entreprise de démarrage et des indicateurs clés de performance","Se concentre sur les startups en phase de semence à série A"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Geschäftsmodelle von Startups und der wichtigsten Leistungsindikatoren","Konzentriert sich auf Startups in der Saat- bis Series-A-Phase"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de modelos de negócios de startups e métricas de desempenho-chave","Focado em startups em estágio de semente até Série A"],"ru":["Требует знания моделей бизнеса стартапов и ключевых показателей эффективности","Ориентирован на стартапы на стадии семенного финансирования до серии А"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بنى 商ıcı و مقاييس الأداء الرئيسية لاستارتآب","مركز على استارتآب في مرحلة البذور حتى السلسلة أ"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
