ilot や Kiro などの開発ツールで使用できる形式に変換します","ko":"브레인스토밍 툴은 Antigravity IDE 설정을 GitHub Copilot 및 Kiro 등의 개발 도구에서 사용할 수 있는 형식으로 변환합니다","es":"La herramienta de brainstorming es una solución para convertir configuraciones de Agent, Skill y Workflows de Antigravity IDE a formatos compatibles con otro...","fr":"L''outil de brainstorming est une solution pour convertir les configurations d''Agent, de Skill et de Workflows d''Antigravity IDE en formats compatibles avec d...","de":"Das Brainstorming-Tool ist eine Lösung zur Konvertierung von Agent-, Skill- und Workflow-Konfigurationen von Antigravity IDE in Formate, die mit anderen Entw...","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro..."},"definition":{"en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"features":{"zh":["支持 Antigravity IDE 配置转换","兼容 GitHub Copilot、Cursor 等 IDE","兼容 Kiro、OpenCode 等 CLI","简化开发流程","提高开发效率"],"ja":["Antigravity IDE 設定を変換する機能","GitHub Copilot や Cursor などの IDE との互換性","Kiro や OpenCode などの CLI との互換性","開発プロセスの簡素化","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["Antigravity IDE 설정 변환 지원","GitHub Copilot 및 Cursor 등의 IDE와 호환","Kiro 및 OpenCode 등의 CLI와 호환","개발 프로세스 단순화","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Conversión de configuraciones de Antigravity IDE","Compatibilidad con GitHub Copilot y Cursor","Soporte para CLIs como Kiro y OpenCode","Herramienta de comunicación para solicitudes complejas","Protocolo de clarificación para solicitudes vagas"],"fr":["Conversion de configurations d''Antigravity IDE","Compatibilité avec GitHub Copilot et Cursor","Support pour les CLIs comme Kiro et OpenCode","Outil de communication pour les demandes complexes","Protocole de clarification pour les demandes vagues"],"de":["Konvertierung von Antigravity IDE-Konfigurationen","Kompatibilität mit GitHub Copilot und Cursor","Unterstützung für CLIs wie Kiro und OpenCode","Kommunikationswerkzeug für komplexe Anfragen","Klärungsprotokoll für vage Anfragen"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Brainstorming 工具","Antigravity IDE","配置转换","GitHub Copilot","Kiro","开发工具","配置兼容性","开发流程"],"ja":["ブレインストーミングツール","Antigravity IDE","設定変換","GitHub Copilot","Kiro","開発ツール","設定互換性","開発プロセス"],"ko":["브레인스토밍 툴","Antigravity IDE","설정 변환","GitHub Copilot","Kiro","개발 도구","설정 호환성","개발 프로세스"],"es":["brainstorming","conversión de configuraciones","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["brainstorming","conversion de configurations","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["Brainstorming","Konvertierung von Konfigurationen","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"Socratic questioning protocol + user communication. MANDATORY for complex requests, new features, or unclear requirements. Includes progress reporting and error handling.","bodyPreview":"# Brainstorming & Communication Protocol\n\n> **MANDATORY:** Use for complex/vague requests, new features, updates.\n\n---\n\n## 🛑 SOCRATIC GATE (ENFORCEMENT)\n\n### When to Trigger\n\n| Pattern | Action |\n|---------|--------|\n| \"Build/Create/Make [thing]\" without details | 🛑 ASK 3 questions |\n| Complex feature or architecture | 🛑 Clarify before implementing |\n| Update/change request | 🛑 Confirm scope |\n| Vague requirements | 🛑 Ask purpose, users, constraints |\n\n### 🚫 MANDATORY: 3 Questions Before I","body":"# Brainstorming & Communication Protocol\n\n> **MANDATORY:** Use for complex/vague requests, new features, updates.\n\n---\n\n## 🛑 SOCRATIC GATE (ENFORCEMENT)\n\n### When to Trigger\n\n| Pattern | Action |\n|---------|--------|\n| \"Build/Create/Make [thing]\" without details | 🛑 ASK 3 questions |\n| Complex feature or architecture | 🛑 Clarify before implementing |\n| Update/change request | 🛑 Confirm scope |\n| Vague requirements | 🛑 Ask purpose, users, constraints |\n\n### 🚫 MANDATORY: 3 Questions Before Implementation\n\n1. **STOP** - Do NOT start coding\n2. **ASK** - Minimum 3 questions:\n   - 🎯 Purpose: What problem are you solving?\n   - 👥 Users: Who will use this?\n   - 📦 Scope: Must-have vs nice-to-have?\n3. **WAIT** - Get response before proceeding\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Dynamic Question Generation\n\n**⛔ NEVER use static templates.** Read `dynamic-questioning.md` for principles.\n\n### Core Principles\n\n| Principle | Meaning |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Questions Reveal Consequences** | Each question connects to an architectural decision |\n| **Context Before Content** | Understand greenfield/feature/refactor/debug context first |\n| **Minimum Viable Questions** | Each question must eliminate implementation paths |\n| **Generate Data, Not Assumptions** | Don''t guess—ask with trade-offs |\n\n### Question Generation Process\n\n```\n1. Parse request → Extract domain, features, scale indicators\n2. Identify decision points → Blocking vs. deferable\n3. Generate questions → Priority: P0 (blocking) > P1 (high-leverage) > P2 (nice-to-have)\n4. Format with trade-offs → What, Why, Options, Default\n```\n\n### Question Format (MANDATORY)\n\n```markdown\n### [PRIORITY] **[DECISION POINT]**\n\n**Question:** [Clear question]\n\n**Why This Matters:**\n- [Architectural consequence]\n- [Affects: cost/complexity/timeline/scale]\n\n**Options:**\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Best For |\n|--------|------|------|----------|\n| A | [+] | [-] | [Use case] |\n\n**If Not Specified:** [Default + rationale]\n```\n\n**For detailed domain-specific question banks and algorithms**, see: `dynamic-questioning.md`\n\n---\n\n## Progress Reporting (PRINCIPLE-BASED)\n\n**PRINCIPLE:** Transparency builds trust. Status must be visible and actionable.\n\n### Status Board Format\n\n| Agent | Status | Current Task | Progress |\n|-------|--------|--------------|----------|\n| [Agent Name] | ✅🔄⏳❌⚠️ | [Task description] | [% or count] |\n\n### Status Icons\n\n| Icon | Meaning | Usage |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| ✅ | Completed | Task finished successfully |\n| 🔄 | Running | Currently executing |\n| ⏳ | Waiting | Blocked, waiting for dependency |\n| ❌ | Error | Failed, needs attention |\n| ⚠️ | Warning | Potential issue, not blocking |\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling (PRINCIPLE-BASED)\n\n**PRINCIPLE:** Errors are opportunities for clear communication.\n\n### Error Response Pattern\n\n```\n1. Acknowledge the error\n2. Explain what happened (user-friendly)\n3. Offer specific solutions with trade-offs\n4. Ask user to choose or provide alternative\n```\n\n### Error Categories\n\n| Category | Response Strategy |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| **Port Conflict** | Offer alternative port or close existing |\n| **Dependency Missing** | Auto-install or ask permission |\n| **Build Failure** | Show specific error + suggested fix |\n| **Unclear Error** | Ask for specifics: screenshot, console output |\n\n---\n\n## Completion Message (PRINCIPLE-BASED)\n\n**PRINCIPLE:** Celebrate success, guide next steps.\n\n### Completion Structure\n\n```\n1. Success confirmation (celebrate briefly)\n2. Summary of what was done (concrete)\n3. How to verify/test (actionable)\n4. Next steps suggestion (proactive)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Communication Principles\n\n| Principle | Implementation |\n|-----------|----------------|\n| **Concise** | No unnecessary details, get to point |\n| **Visual** | Use emojis (✅🔄⏳❌) for quick scanning |\n| **Specific** | \"~2 minutes\" not \"wait a bit\" |\n| **Alternatives** | Offer multiple paths when stuck |\n| **Proactive** | Suggest next step after completion |\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns (AVOID)\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why |\n|--------------|-----|\n| Jumping to solutions before understanding | Wastes time on wrong problem |\n| Assuming requirements without asking | Creates wrong output |\n| Over-engineering first version | Delays value delivery |\n| Ignoring constraints | Creates unusable solutions |\n| \"I think\" phrases | Uncertainty → Ask instead |\n\n---\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:41:20.969Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring structured communication protocols for complex requests","zh":"适用于对话式 AI 代理，如 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT，需要结构化的通信协议来处理复杂的请求","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの会話型 AI エージェントに適しており、複雑なリクエストに構造化された通信プロトコルが必要","ko":"클라우드 코드 및 오토 GPT와 같은 대화형 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 구조화된 통신 프로토콜이 필요한 복잡한 요청","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Conversacional como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren protocolos de comunicación estructurados para solicitudes complejas","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA conversationnels comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des protocoles de communication structurés pour des demandes complexes","de":"Ideal für Conversational-AI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die strukturierte Kommunikationsprotokolle für komplexe Anfragen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Conversacional como Claude Code e AutoGPT que exigem protocolos de comunicação estruturados para solicitações complexas","ru":"Идеально подходит для Конверсационных ИИ-агентов, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих структурированных протоколов связи для сложных запросов","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المحادثي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذي يتطلب بروتوكولات اتصال منظمة لطلبات معقدة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate vague requirements through Socratic questioning, ensuring clarity before implementation, and utilizing protocols like SOCRATIC GATE for efficient communication","zh":"使代理能够通过苏格拉底式提问来应对模糊的需求，确保在实施前明确，并利用诸如 SOCRATIC GATE 之类的协议进行高效的通信","ja":"エージェントがソクラテス式の質問を通じて漠然とした要件に対処し、実装前に明確性を確保し、SOCRATIC GATEなどのプロトコルを使用して効率的なコミュニケーションを行うことができる","ko":"에이전트가 소크라테스식 질문을 통해 모호한 요구 사항에 대처하여 구현 전에 명확성을 보장하며, SOCRATIC GATE와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 효율적인 통신을 활성화","es":"Permite a los agentes navegar por requisitos vagos a través de preguntas socráticas, asegurando la claridad antes de la implementación y utilizando protocolos como SOCRATIC GATE para una comunicación eficiente","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer dans les exigences vagues grâce à des questions socratiques, en assurant la clarté avant la mise en œuvre et en utilisant des protocoles comme SOCRATIC GATE pour une communication efficace","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, ungenaue Anforderungen durch sokratische Fragen zu navigieren, um Klarheit vor der Implementierung sicherzustellen und Protokolle wie SOCRATIC GATE für eine effiziente Kommunikation zu nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a navegar em requisitos vagos por meio de questionamento socrático, garantindo clareza antes da implementação e utilizando protocolos como SOCRATIC GATE para comunicação eficiente","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью ориентироваться в неясных требованиях посредством сократического вопроса, обеспечивающего ясность до реализации и использующего протоколы, такие как SOCRATIC GATE, для эффективной связи","ar":"يُمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التنقل في المتطلبات الغامضة من خلال الأسئلة السقراطية، وضمان الوضوح قبل التنفيذ، واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل SOCRATIC GATE للاتصال الفعال"},"useCases":{"en":["Clarifying complex feature requests through systematic questioning","Confirming scope for update or change requests to prevent misimplementation","Analyzing purpose, users, and constraints for features with vague requirements"],"zh":["通过系统化的问题来阐明复杂的功能请求","确认更新或更改请求的范围，以防止误实现","分析具有模糊需求的功能的目的、用户和约束"],"ja":["体系的な質問を通じて複雑な機能リクエストを明確化する","更新または変更リクエストの範囲を確認して誤った実装を防ぐ","目的、ユーザー、制約などの要素を分析して、曖昧な要件を持つ機能をより明確にする"],"ko":["체계적인 질문을 통해 복잡한 기능 요청을 명확히 함","업데이트 또는 변경 요청의 범위를 확인하여 잘못된 구현을 방지","目的, 사용자, 제약 조건 등을 분석하여 모호한 요구 사항을 가진 기능에 대한 목적을 명확히 함"],"es":["Clarificar solicitudes de características complejas a través de un cuestionamiento sistemático","Confirmar el alcance de las solicitudes de actualización o cambio para prevenir una mala implementación","Analizar el propósito, los usuarios y las restricciones para características con requisitos vagos"],"fr":["Clarifier les demandes de fonctionnalités complexes grâce à un questionnement systématique","Confirmer la portée des demandes de mise à jour ou de modification pour prévenir une mauvaise mise en œuvre","Analyser le but, les utilisateurs et les contraintes pour les fonctionnalités ayant des exigences vagues"],"de":["Komplexe Funktionsanforderungen durch systematisches Fragen klären","Den Umfang von Aktualisierungs- oder Änderungsanfragen bestätigen, um eine Fehlimplementierung zu vermeiden","Zweck, Benutzer und Einschränkungen für Funktionen mit ungenauen Anforderungen analysieren"],"pt":["Esclarecimento de solicitações de recursos complexos por meio de questionamento sistemático","Confirmação do escopo para solicitações de atualização ou alteração para prevenir implementação incorreta","Análise do propósito, dos usuários e das restrições para recursos com requisitos vagos"],"ru":["Уточнение сложных запросов функций посредством систематического вопроса","Подтверждение объема для запросов обновления или изменения для предотвращения неправильной реализации","Анализ цели, пользователей и ограничений для функций с неясными требованиями"],"ar":["توضيح طلبات الميزات المعقدة من خلال الاستفهام المنظم","تأكيد النطاق لطلبات التحديث أو التغيير لمنع التنفيذ الخاطئ","تحليل الغرض والمستخدمين والقيود للميزات ذات المتطلبات الغامضة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with compatible IDEs and CLIs","Mandatory use for complex or vague requests may slow initial response times"],"zh":["需要与兼容的 IDE 和 CLI 集成","对于复杂或模糊的请求，强制使用可能会减慢初始响应时间"],"ja":["対応した IDE および CLI と統合する必要がある","複雑または漠然としたリクエストの場合は、必須の使用により初期応答時間が遅くなる可能性がある"],"ko":["호환되는 IDE 및 CLI와의 통합이 필요","복잡하거나 모호한 요청의 경우, 강제 사용으로 초기 응답 시간이 느려질 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere integración con IDE y CLI compatibles","El uso obligatorio para solicitudes complejas o vagas puede ralentizar los tiempos de respuesta iniciales"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec des IDE et des CLI compatibles","L''utilisation obligatoire pour les demandes complexes ou vagues peut ralentir les temps de réponse initiaux"],"de":["Benötigt eine Integration mit kompatiblen IDEs und CLIs","Der verpflichtende Einsatz für komplexe oder ungenaue Anfragen kann die anfänglichen Antwortzeiten verlangsamen"],"pt":["Exige integração com IDEs e CLIs compatíveis","Uso obrigatório para solicitações complexas ou vagas pode reduzir os tempos de resposta iniciais"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с совместимыми IDE и CLI","Обязательное использование для сложных или неясных запросов может减нить первоначальные времена ответа"],"ar":["يتطلب التكامل مع بيئات التطوير المتكاملة وواجهات سطر الأوامر المتوافقة","استخدام إلزامي لطلبات معقدة أو غامضة قد يؤدي إلى تباطؤ أوقات الاستجابة الأولية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/linkerd-patterns', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'linkerd-patterns', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z', '2026-02-18T13:41:13.133Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/linkerd-patterns","name":"linkerd-patterns","description":{"zh":"Linkerd Patterns是轻量级服务网格解决方案，提供自动mTLS、流量分割、服务配置文件等功能","ja":"Linkerd Patternsは軽量級サービスメッシュソリューションで、自動mTLS、トラフィックスプリット、サービスプロファイルなどを提供します","ko":"Linkerd Patterns는 경량 서비스 메시 솔루션으로, 자동 mTLS, 트래픽 분할, 서비스 프로파일 등을 제공합니다","es":"Linkerd es un service mesh ligero y seguro para Kubernetes que ofrece patrones de producción para una implementación efectiva","fr":"Linkerd est un service mesh léger et sécurisé pour Kubernetes qui propose des modèles de production pour une mise en œuvre efficace","de":"Linkerd ist ein leichtes und sicheres Service Mesh für Kubernetes, das Produktionsmuster für eine effektive Implementierung bietet","pt":"Linkerd é uma service mesh leve e segura para Kubernetes, que fornece padrões de produção para implementar mTLS, divisões de tráfego e perfis de serviço","ru":"Linkerd - это легкая и безопасная service mesh для Kubernetes, которая предоставляет шаблоны производительности для реализации mTLS, разделения трафика и профилей служб","ar":"Linkerd هي شبكة الخدمة الخفيفة والأمنية لكوبيرنتس، توفر أنماط الإنتاج لتنفيذ mTLS وتقسيمات Movement وملفات تعريف الخدمة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Linkerd Patterns - 轻量级服务网格解决方案","ja":"Linkerd Patterns - 軽量級サービスメッシュソリューション","ko":"Linkerd Patterns - 경량 서비스 메시 솔루션","es":"Patrones de Linkerd para Service Mesh","fr":"Modèles Linkerd pour Service Mesh","de":"Linkerd-Muster für Service Mesh","pt":"Padrões Linkerd: Service Mesh Leve e Seguro","ru":"Шаблоны Linkerd: Легкая и Безопасная Service Mesh","ar":"أنماط Linkerd: شبكة الخدمة الخفيفة والأمنية","en":"linkerd-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"Linkerd Patterns是轻量级服务网格解决方案，提供自动mTLS、流量分割、服务配置文件等功能","ja":"Linkerd Patternsは軽量級サービスメッシュソリューションで、自動mTLS、トラフィックスプリット、サービスプロファイルなどを提供します","ko":"Linkerd Patterns는 경량 서비스 메시 솔루션으로, 자동 mTLS, 트래픽 분할, 서비스 프로파일 등을 제공합니다","es":"Linkerd es un service mesh ligero y seguro para Kubernetes que ofrece patrones de producción para una implementación efectiva","fr":"Linkerd est un service mesh léger et sécurisé pour Kubernetes qui propose des modèles de production pour une mise en œuvre efficace","de":"Linkerd ist ein leichtes und sicheres Service Mesh für Kubernetes, das Produktionsmuster für eine effektive Implementierung bietet","pt":"Linkerd é uma service mesh leve e segura para Kubernetes, que fornece padrões de produção para implementar mTLS, divisões de tráfego e perfis de serviço","ru":"Linkerd - это легкая и безопасная service mesh для Kubernetes, которая предоставляет шаблоны производительности для реализации mTLS, разделения трафика и про...","ar":"Linkerd هي شبكة الخدمة الخفيفة والأمنية لكوبيرنتس، توفر أنماط الإنتاج لتنفيذ mTLS وتقسيمات Movement وملفات تعريف الخدمة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动mTLS","流量分割","服务配置文件","重试和超时","多集群服务网格"],"ja":["自動mTLS","トラフィックスプリット","サービスプロファイル","リトライとタイムアウト","マルチクラスターサービスメッシュ"],"ko":["자동 mTLS","트래픽 분할","서비스 프로파일","재시도와 타임아웃","멀티 클러스터 서비스 메시"],"es":["Implementación de mTLS automático","Configuración de tráfico para despliegues canarios","Perfiles de servicio para métricas por ruta","Reintentos y tiempos de espera","Service mesh multi-cluster"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de mTLS automatique","Configuration du trafic pour les déploiements canari","Profils de service pour les métriques par route","Réessais et délais d''attente","Service mesh multi-cluster"],"de":["Implementierung von automatischem mTLS","Konfiguration des Datenverkehrs für Canary-Deployments","Service-Profile für Route-Metriken","Wiederholungen und Timeouts","Multi-Cluster-Service-Mesh"],"pt":["Implementação automática de mTLS","Divisões de tráfego para implantações canary","Perfis de serviço para métricas por rota","Retentativas e temporizadores","Service mesh multi-cluster"],"ru":["Автоматическая реализация mTLS","Разделение трафика для канареечных развертываний","Профили служб для метрик по маршруту","Повторные попытки и таймауты","Мульти-кластерная service mesh"],"ar":["تنفيذ تلقائي ل mTLS","تقسيمات حركة المرور لتنفيذ الكركي","ملفات تعريف الخدمة لمقاييس المسار","محاولات إعادة وتأخير","شبكة الخدمة متعددة العنقود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Linkerd Patterns","轻量级服务网格","自动mTLS","流量分割","服务配置文件","Kubernetes"],"ja":["Linkerd Patterns","軽量級サービスメッシュ","自動mTLS","トラフィックスプリット","サービスプロファイル","Kubernetes"],"ko":["Linkerd Patterns","경량 서비스 메시","자동 mTLS","트래픽 분할","서비스 프로파일","Kubernetes"],"es":["Linkerd","service mesh","Kubernetes","mTLS","despliegues canarios","métricas por ruta","reintentos","tiempos de espera","service mesh multi-cluster"],"fr":["Linkerd","service mesh","Kubernetes","mTLS","déploiements canari","métriques par route","réessais","délais d''attente","service mesh multi-cluster"],"de":["Linkerd","Service Mesh","Kubernetes","mTLS","Canary-Deployments","Route-Metriken","Wiederholungen","Timeouts","Multi-Cluster-Service-Mesh"],"pt":["Linkerd","service mesh","Kubernetes","mTLS","segurança","escalabilidade","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Linkerd","service mesh","Kubernetes","mTLS","безопасность","масштабируемость","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["Linkerd","شبكة الخدمة","كوبيرنتس","mTLS","الأمن","التوسع","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"linkerd-patterns","description":"Implement Linkerd service mesh patterns for lightweight, security-focused service mesh deployments. Use when setting up Linkerd, configuring traffic policies, or implementing zero-trust networking with minimal overhead.","bodyPreview":"# Linkerd Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for Linkerd service mesh - the lightweight, security-first service mesh for Kubernetes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up a lightweight service mesh\n- Implementing automatic mTLS\n- Configuring traffic splits for canary deployments\n- Setting up service profiles for per-route metrics\n- Implementing retries and timeouts\n- Multi-cluster service mesh\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Linkerd Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│","body":"# Linkerd Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for Linkerd service mesh - the lightweight, security-first service mesh for Kubernetes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up a lightweight service mesh\n- Implementing automatic mTLS\n- Configuring traffic splits for canary deployments\n- Setting up service profiles for per-route metrics\n- Implementing retries and timeouts\n- Multi-cluster service mesh\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Linkerd Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                Control Plane                 │\n│  ┌─────────┐ ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ │\n│  │ destiny │ │ identity │ │ proxy-inject │ │\n│  └─────────┘ └──────────┘ └──────────────┘ │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                      │\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 Data Plane                   │\n│  ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐             │\n│  │proxy│────│proxy│────│proxy│             │\n│  └─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘             │\n│     │           │           │               │\n│  ┌──┴──┐    ┌──┴──┐    ┌──┴──┐            │\n│  │ app │    │ app │    │ app │            │\n│  └─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘            │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 2. Key Resources\n\n| Resource                | Purpose                              |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| **ServiceProfile**      | Per-route metrics, retries, timeouts |\n| **TrafficSplit**        | Canary deployments, A/B testing      |\n| **Server**              | Define server-side policies          |\n| **ServerAuthorization** | Access control policies              |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Mesh Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install CLI\ncurl --proto ''=https'' --tlsv1.2 -sSfL https://run.linkerd.io/install | sh\n\n# Validate cluster\nlinkerd check --pre\n\n# Install CRDs\nlinkerd install --crds | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Install control plane\nlinkerd install | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Verify installation\nlinkerd check\n\n# Install viz extension (optional)\nlinkerd viz install | kubectl apply -f -\n```\n\n### Template 2: Inject Namespace\n\n```yaml\n# Automatic injection for namespace\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Namespace\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\n  annotations:\n    linkerd.io/inject: enabled\n---\n# Or inject specific deployment\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\n  annotations:\n    linkerd.io/inject: enabled\nspec:\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      annotations:\n        linkerd.io/inject: enabled\n```\n\n### Template 3: Service Profile with Retries\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: linkerd.io/v1alpha2\nkind: ServiceProfile\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service.my-namespace.svc.cluster.local\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  routes:\n    - name: GET /api/users\n      condition:\n        method: GET\n        pathRegex: /api/users\n      responseClasses:\n        - condition:\n            status:\n              min: 500\n              max: 599\n          isFailure: true\n      isRetryable: true\n    - name: POST /api/users\n      condition:\n        method: POST\n        pathRegex: /api/users\n      # POST not retryable by default\n      isRetryable: false\n    - name: GET /api/users/{id}\n      condition:\n        method: GET\n        pathRegex: /api/users/[^/]+\n      timeout: 5s\n      isRetryable: true\n  retryBudget:\n    retryRatio: 0.2\n    minRetriesPerSecond: 10\n    ttl: 10s\n```\n\n### Template 4: Traffic Split (Canary)\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: split.smi-spec.io/v1alpha1\nkind: TrafficSplit\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service-canary\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  service: my-service\n  backends:\n    - service: my-service-stable\n      weight: 900m # 90%\n    - service: my-service-canary\n      weight: 100m # 10%\n```\n\n### Template 5: Server Authorization Policy\n\n```yaml\n# Define the server\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta1\nkind: Server\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service-http\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  podSelector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: my-service\n  port: http\n  proxyProtocol: HTTP/1\n---\n# Allow traffic from specific clients\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta1\nkind: ServerAuthorization\nmetadata:\n  name: allow-frontend\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  server:\n    name: my-service-http\n  client:\n    meshTLS:\n      serviceAccounts:\n        - name: frontend\n          namespace: my-namespace\n---\n# Allow unauthenticated traffic (e.g., from ingress)\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta1\nkind: ServerAuthorization\nmetadata:\n  name: allow-ingress\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  server:\n    name: my-service-http\n  client:\n    unauthenticated: true\n    networks:\n      - cidr: 10.0.0.0/8\n```\n\n### Template 6: HTTPRoute for Advanced Routing\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta2\nkind: HTTPRoute\nmetadata:\n  name: my-route\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  parentRefs:\n    - name: my-service\n      kind: Service\n      group: core\n      port: 8080\n  rules:\n    - matches:\n        - path:\n            type: PathPrefix\n            value: /api/v2\n        - headers:\n            - name: x-api-version\n              value: v2\n      backendRefs:\n        - name: my-service-v2\n          port: 8080\n    - matches:\n        - path:\n            type: PathPrefix\n            value: /api\n      backendRefs:\n        - name: my-service-v1\n          port: 8080\n```\n\n### Template 7: Multi-cluster Setup\n\n```bash\n# On each cluster, install with cluster credentials\nlinkerd multicluster install | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Link clusters\nlinkerd multicluster link --cluster-name west \\\n  --api-server-address https://west.example.com:6443 \\\n  | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Export a service to other clusters\nkubectl label svc/my-service mirror.linkerd.io/exported=true\n\n# Verify cross-cluster connectivity\nlinkerd multicluster check\nlinkerd multicluster gateways\n```\n\n## Monitoring Commands\n\n```bash\n# Live traffic view\nlinkerd viz top deploy/my-app\n\n# Per-route metrics\nlinkerd viz routes deploy/my-app\n\n# Check proxy status\nlinkerd viz stat deploy -n my-namespace\n\n# View service dependencies\nlinkerd viz edges deploy -n my-namespace\n\n# Dashboard\nlinkerd viz dashboard\n```\n\n## Debugging\n\n```bash\n# Check injection status\nlinkerd check --proxy -n my-namespace\n\n# View proxy logs\nkubectl logs deploy/my-app -c linkerd-proxy\n\n# Debug identity/TLS\nlinkerd identity -n my-namespace\n\n# Tap traffic (live)\nlinkerd viz tap deploy/my-app --to deploy/my-backend\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Enable mTLS everywhere** - It''s automatic with Linkerd\n- **Use ServiceProfiles** - Get per-route metrics and retries\n- **Set retry budgets** - Prevent retry storms\n- **Monitor golden metrics** - Success rate, latency, throughput\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t skip check** - Always run `linkerd check` after changes\n- **Don''t over-configure** - Linkerd defaults are sensible\n- **Don''t ignore ServiceProfiles** - They unlock advanced features\n- **Don''t forget timeouts** - Set appropriate values per route\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Linkerd Documentation](https://linkerd.io/2.14/overview/)\n- [Service Profiles](https://linkerd.io/2.14/features/service-profiles/)\n- [Authorization Policy](https://linkerd.io/2.14/features/server-policy/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:41:13.133Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Kubernetes Agents needing lightweight service mesh integration with automatic mTLS and traffic management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要轻量级服务网格集成的Kubernetes代理，具有自动mTLS和流量管理功能。","ja":"Kubernetesエージェントが軽量のサービスメッシュ統合を必要とする場合に最適で、自動mTLSとトラフィック管理機能を備えています。","ko":"자동 mTLS 및 트래픽 관리 기능을 갖춘 경량 서비스 메시 통합이 필요한 Kubernetes 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de Kubernetes que necesitan una integración de malla de servicio ligera con capacidades de mTLS automático y gestión de tráfico.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Kubernetes nécessitant une intégration de mesh de service légère avec des capacités de mTLS automatique et de gestion de trafic.","de":"Perfekt für Kubernetes-Agents, die eine leichte Service-Mesh-Integration mit automatischem mTLS und Traffikmanagement-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes Kubernetes que necessitam de integração de malha de serviço leve com mTLS automático e capacidades de gerenciamento de tráfego.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Kubernetes, которым требуется легкая интеграция сервисной сетки с автоматическим mTLS и возможностями управления трафиком.","ar":"مثالي لعميل Kubernetes الذي يحتاج إلى دمج شبكة خدمة خفيفة الوزن مع مTLS تلقائي وقدرات إدارة المرور."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement secure and scalable service mesh patterns using Linkerd, including automatic mTLS, traffic splits for canary deployments, and service profiles for per-route metrics, leveraging Kubernetes for multi-cluster service mesh configurations.","zh":"赋予代理实现安全可扩展的服务网格模式的能力，使用Linkerd，包括自动mTLS、用于金丝雀部署和A/B测试的流量分割，以及用于每条路由指标的服务配置文件，利用Kubernetes进行多集群服务网格配置。","ja":"Linkerdを使用して、自動mTLS、カナリアデプロイとA/Bテストのためのトラフィック分割、ルートごとのメトリクスの詳細なサービスプロファイルなどの、安全でスケーラブルなサービスメッシュパターンを実装するエージェントの能力を提供し、Kubernetesを使用してマルチクラスターサービスメッシュ構成を実現します。","ko":"Linkerd를 사용하여 자동 mTLS, 카나리 배포 및 A/B 테스트를 위한 트래픽 분할, 루트별 메트릭スの 자세한 서비스 프로파일 등을 포함하여 안전하고 확장 가능한 서비스 메시 패턴을 구현할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하며, Kubernetes를 사용하여 멀티 클러스터 서비스 메시 구성도 가능합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar patrones de malla de servicio seguros y escalables utilizando Linkerd, incluyendo mTLS automático, divisiones de tráfico para implementaciones de canario y perfiles de servicio para métricas por ruta, aprovechando Kubernetes para configuraciones de malla de servicio multi-cluster.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des modèles de mesh de service sécurisés et évolutifs à l''aide de Linkerd, notamment le mTLS automatique, les divisions de trafic pour les déploiements canari et les profils de service pour les métriques par route, en exploitant Kubernetes pour les configurations de mesh de service multi-cluster.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, sichere und skalierbare Service-Mesh-Muster mit Linkerd zu implementieren, einschließlich automatischem mTLS, Traffiksplitten für Canary-Deployments und Service-Profilen für pro-Routen-Metriken, wobei Kubernetes für Multi-Cluster-Service-Mesh-Konfigurationen genutzt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar padrões de malha de serviço seguros e escaláveis usando Linkerd, incluindo mTLS automático, divisões de tráfego para implantações canary e perfis de serviço para métricas por rota, aproveitando o Kubernetes para configurações de malha de serviço multi-cluster.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать безопасные и масштабируемые шаблоны сервисной сетки с помощью Linkerd, включая автоматический mTLS, разделение трафика для канареечных развертываний и профили сервисов для метрик на уровне маршрута, используя Kubernetes для конфигураций сервисной сетки в нескольких кластерах.","ar":"تمكين العميل من تنفيذ أنماط شبكة خدمة آمنة ومقابلة باستخدام Linkerd، بما في ذلك مTLS تلقائي وتقسيمات حركة المرور لتنصيب الطيور المحاكية وملفات تعريف الخدمة لأدوات指 Метрик لكل مسار، واستخدام Kubernetes لإعدادات شبكة الخدمة متعددة الكلستر."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing automatic mTLS for secure service communication","Configuring traffic splits for canary deployments and A/B testing","Setting up service profiles for detailed per-route metrics and monitoring"],"zh":["实现服务通信的自动mTLS安全","配置金丝雀部署和A/B测试的流量分割","设置服务配置文件以获取每条路由的详细指标和监控"],"ja":["サービス通信のための自動mTLSのセキュリティを実現する","カナリアデプロイとA/Bテストのためのトラフィック分割を構成する","詳細なルートごとのメトリクスとモニタリングのためのサービスプロファイルを設定する"],"ko":["서비스 통신을 위한 자동 mTLS 보안 구현","카나리 배포 및 A/B 테스트를 위한 트래픽 분할 구성"," 자세한 루트별 메트릭스 및 모니터링을 위한 서비스 프로파일 설정"],"es":["Implementar mTLS automático para una comunicación de servicio segura","Configurar divisiones de tráfico para implementaciones de canario y pruebas A/B","Configurar perfiles de servicio para métricas detalladas por ruta y monitoreo"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre un mTLS automatique pour une communication de service sécurisée","Configurer les divisions de trafic pour les déploiements canari et les tests A/B","Configurer les profils de service pour des métriques détaillées par route et un monitoreo"],"de":["Automatisches mTLS für sichere Dienstkommunikation implementieren","Traffiksplitten für Canary-Deployments und A/B-Tests konfigurieren","Service-Profile für detaillierte pro-Routen-Metriken und Überwachung einrichten"],"pt":["Implementando mTLS automático para comunicação de serviço segura","Configurando divisões de tráfego para implantações canary e testes A/B","Configurando perfis de serviço para métricas detalhadas por rota e monitoramento"],"ru":["Реализация автоматического mTLS для безопасной коммуникации сервисов","Настройка разделения трафика для канареечных развертываний и тестирования A/B","Настройка профилей сервисов для подробных метрик на уровне маршрута и мониторинга"],"ar":["تنفيذ مTLS تلقائي للاتصال الآمن بخدمة","التكوين تقسيمات حركة المرور لتنصيب الطيور المحاكية واختبارات A/B","إعداد ملفات تعريف الخدمة لأدوات指 Метрик لكل مسار وتحديد أداء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Kubernetes environment","Limited to Linkerd service mesh","Dependent on Kubernetes cluster configuration and networking policies"],"zh":["需要Kubernetes环境","仅限Linkerd服务网格","依赖Kubernetes集群配置和网络策略"],"ja":["Kubernetes環境を必要とする","Linkerdサービスメッシュのみに限定される","Kubernetesクラスタ構成とネットワークポリシーに依存する"],"ko":["Kubernetes 환경 필요","Linkerd 서비스 메시만 제한됨","Kubernetes 클러스터 구성 및 네트워크 정책에 의존"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de Kubernetes","Limitado a la malla de servicio Linkerd","Dependiente de la configuración del clúster de Kubernetes y las políticas de red"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Kubernetes","Limité au mesh de service Linkerd","Dépend de la configuration du cluster Kubernetes et des politiques de réseau"],"de":["Benötigt eine Kubernetes-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf das Linkerd-Service-Mesh","Abhängig von der Konfiguration des Kubernetes-Clusters und den Netzwerkrichtlinien"],"pt":["Exige ambiente Kubernetes","Limitado à malha de serviço Linkerd","Dependente da configuração do cluster Kubernetes e das políticas de rede"],"ru":["Требует среды Kubernetes","Ограничен сервисной сеткой Linkerd","Зависит от конфигурации кластера Kubernetes и сетевых политик"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Kubernetes","محدود بشبكة الخدمة Linkerd","يعتمد على تكوين الكلستر Kubernetes وسياسات الشبكة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
