ation de tests","playwright python"],"de":["Webanwendungstests","Python Playwright","Hilfs-Skripte","Verwaltung des Lebenszyklus des Servers","Entwicklung von Webanwendungen","Testing von Webanwendungen","Automatisierung von Tests","playwright python"],"pt":["teste de aplicativos web","python playwright","teste de aplicativos web locais","gerenciamento do ciclo de vida do servidor","scripts de ajuda","desenvolvimento web","teste de software","automatização de testes"],"ru":["тестирование веб-приложений","python playwright","тестирование локальных веб-приложений","управление жизненным циклом сервера","вспомогательные скрипты","веб-разработка","тестирование программного обеспечения","автоматизация тестирования"],"ar":["اختبار تطبيقات الويب","python playwright","اختبار تطبيقات الويب المحلية","إدارة دورة حياة الخادم","سكريبتات مساعدة","تطوير الويب","اختبار البرمجيات","أتمتة الاختبار"]}},"owner":"rongma1sheng","repo":"kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","repoPath":"rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"webapp-testing","description":"Toolkit for interacting with and testing local web applications using Playwright. Supports verifying frontend functionality, debugging UI behavior, capturing browser screenshots, and viewing browser logs.","bodyPreview":"# Web Application Testing\n\nTo test local web applications, write native Python Playwright scripts.\n\n**Helper Scripts Available**:\n- `scripts/with_server.py` - Manages server lifecycle (supports multiple servers)\n\n**Always run scripts with `--help` first** to see usage. DO NOT read the source until you try running the script first and find that a customized solution is abslutely necessary. These scripts can be very large and thus pollute your context window. They exist to be called directly as bl","body":"# Web Application Testing\n\nTo test local web applications, write native Python Playwright scripts.\n\n**Helper Scripts Available**:\n- `scripts/with_server.py` - Manages server lifecycle (supports multiple servers)\n\n**Always run scripts with `--help` first** to see usage. DO NOT read the source until you try running the script first and find that a customized solution is abslutely necessary. These scripts can be very large and thus pollute your context window. They exist to be called directly as black-box scripts rather than ingested into your context window.\n\n## Decision Tree: Choosing Your Approach\n\n```\nUser task → Is it static HTML?\n    ├─ Yes → Read HTML file directly to identify selectors\n    │         ├─ Success → Write Playwright script using selectors\n    │         └─ Fails/Incomplete → Treat as dynamic (below)\n    │\n    └─ No (dynamic webapp) → Is the server already running?\n        ├─ No → Run: python scripts/with_server.py --help\n        │        Then use the helper + write simplified Playwright script\n        │\n        └─ Yes → Reconnaissance-then-action:\n            1. Navigate and wait for networkidle\n            2. Take screenshot or inspect DOM\n            3. Identify selectors from rendered state\n            4. Execute actions with discovered selectors\n```\n\n## Example: Using with_server.py\n\nTo start a server, run `--help` first, then use the helper:\n\n**Single server:**\n```bash\npython scripts/with_server.py --server \"npm run dev\" --port 5173 -- python your_automation.py\n```\n\n**Multiple servers (e.g., backend + frontend):**\n```bash\npython scripts/with_server.py \\\n  --server \"cd backend && python server.py\" --port 3000 \\\n  --server \"cd frontend && npm run dev\" --port 5173 \\\n  -- python your_automation.py\n```\n\nTo create an automation script, include only Playwright logic (servers are managed automatically):\n```python\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True) # Always launch chromium in headless mode\n    page = browser.new_page()\n    page.goto(''http://localhost:5173'') # Server already running and ready\n    page.wait_for_load_state(''networkidle'') # CRITICAL: Wait for JS to execute\n    # ... your automation logic\n    browser.close()\n```\n\n## Reconnaissance-Then-Action Pattern\n\n1. **Inspect rendered DOM**:\n   ```python\n   page.screenshot(path=''/tmp/inspect.png'', full_page=True)\n   content = page.content()\n   page.locator(''button'').all()\n   ```\n\n2. **Identify selectors** from inspection results\n\n3. **Execute actions** using discovered selectors\n\n## Common Pitfall\n\n❌ **Don''t** inspect the DOM before waiting for `networkidle` on dynamic apps\n✅ **Do** wait for `page.wait_for_load_state(''networkidle'')` before inspection\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- **Use bundled scripts as black boxes** - To accomplish a task, consider whether one of the scripts available in `scripts/` can help. These scripts handle common, complex workflows reliably without cluttering the context window. Use `--help` to see usage, then invoke directly. \n- Use `sync_playwright()` for synchronous scripts\n- Always close the browser when done\n- Use descriptive selectors: `text=`, `role=`, CSS selectors, or IDs\n- Add appropriate waits: `page.wait_for_selector()` or `page.wait_for_timeout()`\n\n## Reference Files\n\n- **examples/** - Examples showing common patterns:\n  - `element_discovery.py` - Discovering buttons, links, and inputs on a page\n  - `static_html_automation.py` - Using file:// URLs for local HTML\n  - `console_logging.py` - Capturing console logs during automation"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:43:46.969Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Testing Agents needing native Python Playwright scripts for local web application testing.","zh":"适用于需要使用本机 Python Playwright 脚本进行本地 Web 应用程序测试的测试代理。","ja":"ローカル Web アプリケーションのテストにネイティブ Python Playwright スクリプトを必要とするテスト エージェントに適しています。","ko":"로컬 웹 애플리케이션 테스트에 네이티브 Python Playwright 스크립트가 필요한 테스트 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de prueba que necesitan scripts de Python Playwright nativos para pruebas de aplicaciones web locales.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de test nécessitant des scripts Python Playwright natifs pour les tests d''applications web locales.","de":"Perfekt für Testagenten, die native Python-Playwright-Skripte für lokale Webanwendungstests benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Teste que necessitam de scripts Python Playwright nativos para testes de aplicações web locais.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов тестирования, которым требуются родные скрипты Python Playwright для локального тестирования веб-приложений.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التجريبيين الذين يحتاجون إلى نصوص برمجة بايثون بلاي رايت الأصلية لاختبار تطبيقات الويب المحلية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage server lifecycles and execute tests using Python Playwright, supporting multiple servers via scripts like `with_server.py`, and leveraging command-line flags like `--help` for usage guidance.","zh":"赋予代理管理服务器生命周期并使用 Python Playwright 执行测试的能力，支持通过脚本（如 `with_server.py`）管理多个服务器，并利用命令行标志（如 `--help`）获取使用指南。","ja":"エージェントにサーバーのライフサイクルを管理し、Python Playwright を使用してテストを実行する機能を提供します。複数のサーバーをスクリプト（例： `with_server.py`）で管理し、コマンドライン フラグ（例： `--help`）で使用方法のガイダンスを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 서버 수명 주기를 관리하고 Python Playwright를 사용하여 테스트를 실행할 수 있는 능력을 제공하며, 스크립트(예: `with_server.py`)를 통해 여러 서버를 지원하고, 명령줄 플래그(예: `--help`)를 통해 사용 지침을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes gestionar los ciclos de vida del servidor y ejecutar pruebas utilizando Python Playwright, admitiendo múltiples servidores a través de scripts como `with_server.py`, y aprovechando las opciones de línea de comandos como `--help` para obtener orientación sobre el uso.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les cycles de vie du serveur et d''exécuter des tests en utilisant Python Playwright, en prenant en charge plusieurs serveurs via des scripts tels que `with_server.py`, et en exploitant les options de ligne de commande comme `--help` pour obtenir des conseils d''utilisation.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Serverlebenszyklen zu verwalten und Tests mit Python Playwright auszuführen, wobei mehrere Server über Skripte wie `with_server.py` unterstützt werden und Befehlszeilenoptionen wie `--help` für die Nutzungshinweise genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar ciclos de vida do servidor e executar testes usando Python Playwright, suportando vários servidores por meio de scripts como `with_server.py`, e aproveitando flags de linha de comando como `--help` para orientação de uso.","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять жизненным циклом сервера и выполнять тесты с помощью Python Playwright, поддерживая несколько серверов через скрипты типа `with_server.py` и использует флаги командной строки типа `--help` для руководства по использованию.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إدارة دورة حياة الخادم وتشغيل الاختبارات باستخدام بايثون بلاي رايت، ودعم الخوادم المتعددة من خلال سكريبتات مثل `with_server.py` ، واستخدام أعلام سطر الأوامر مثل `--help` لتوجيه الاستخدام."},"useCases":{"en":["Testing local web applications","Managing server lifecycles for multiple servers","Generating test scripts with Python Playwright"],"zh":["测试本地 Web 应用程序","管理多个服务器的服务器生命周期","使用 Python Playwright 生成测试脚本"],"ja":["ローカル Web アプリケーションのテスト","複数のサーバーのサーバー ライフサイクルを管理","Python Playwright を使用してテスト スクリプトを生成"],"ko":["로컬 웹 애플리케이션 테스트","여러 서버의 서버 수명 주기 관리","Python Playwright를 사용하여 테스트 스크립트 생성"],"es":["Pruebas de aplicaciones web locales","Gestión de ciclos de vida del servidor para múltiples servidores","Generación de scripts de prueba con Python Playwright"],"fr":["Tests d''applications web locales","Gestion des cycles de vie du serveur pour plusieurs serveurs","Génération de scripts de test avec Python Playwright"],"de":["Lokale Webanwendungstests","Verwaltung von Serverlebenszyklen für mehrere Server","Generierung von Testskripten mit Python Playwright"],"pt":["Testar aplicações web locais","Gerenciar ciclos de vida do servidor para vários servidores","Gerar scripts de teste com Python Playwright"],"ru":["Тестировать локальные веб-приложения","Управлять жизненным циклом сервера для нескольких серверов","Генерировать скрипты тестирования с помощью Python Playwright"],"ar":["اختبار تطبيقات الويب المحلية","إدارة دورة حياة الخادم لعدة خوادم","إنشاء سكريبتات اختبار باستخدام بايثون بلاي رايت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment","Native Python Playwright scripts necessary","Must run scripts with `--help` first"],"zh":["需要 Python 环境","需要本机 Python Playwright 脚本","必须先运行带有 `--help` 的脚本"],"ja":["Python 環境が必要","ネイティブ Python Playwright スクリプトが必要","スクリプトを `--help` で実行する必要がある"],"ko":["Python 환경이 필요합니다.","네이티브 Python Playwright 스크립트가 필요합니다.","스크립트를 `--help`로 실행해야 합니다."],"es":["Requiere entorno de Python","Se necesitan scripts de Python Playwright nativos","Debe ejecutar scripts con `--help` primero"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python","Des scripts Python Playwright natifs sont nécessaires","Doit exécuter les scripts avec `--help` en premier"],"de":["Benötigt Python-Umgebung","Native Python-Playwright-Skripte erforderlich","Muss Skripte mit `--help` ausführen"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python","Scripts Python Playwright nativos necessários","Deve executar scripts com `--help` primeiro"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python","Необходимы родные скрипты Python Playwright","Скрипты должны быть запущены с `--help` в первую очередь"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة بايثون","يتطلب سكريبتات بايثون بلاي رايت الأصلية","يجب تشغيل السكريبتات مع `--help` أولا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit/verification-before-completion', 'community', 'dwalleck', 'kiro-starter-kit', 'dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit', 'verification-before-completion', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z', '2026-02-18T13:43:46.147Z', NULL, '{"id":"dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit/verification-before-completion","name":"verification-before-completion","description":{"zh":"验证前完成是一种开发原则，强调在声明工作完成前必须进行验证，确保开发质量和效率。","ja":"完了前に検証は、作業を完了したと主張する前に検証を行う必要性を強調する開発原則です。","ko":"완료 전 검증은 작업을 완료했다고 주장하기 전에 검증을 수행해야 한다는 개발 원칙을 강조합니다.","es":"La verificación antes de completar es un principio fundamental en el desarrollo. Asegúrate de tener evidencia antes de hacer reclamos","fr":"La vérification avant achèvement est un principe fondamental du développement. Assurez-vous d''avoir des preuves avant de faire des réclamations","de":"Die Verifizierung vor Abschluss ist ein grundlegendes Prinzip in der Entwicklung. Stellen Sie sicher, dass Sie Beweise haben, bevor Sie Ansprüche erheben","pt":"A verificação antes da conclusão é um princípio fundamental que assegura a integridade do trabalho, evitando alegações infundadas.","ru":"Верификация до завершения является основным принципом, обеспечивающим целостность работы, предотвращая необоснованные заявления.","ar":"التحقق قبل الاستكمال هو مبدأ أساسي يضمن سلامة العمل، ويمنع المطالبات غير المبررة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"验证前完成 - 高效开发的核心原则","ja":"完了前に検証 - 効率的な開発の基本原則","ko":"완료 전 검증 - 효율적인 개발의 핵심 원칙","es":"Verificación antes de completar: principios de desarrollo","fr":"Vérification avant achèvement : principes de développement","de":"Verifizierung vor Abschluss: Entwicklungsprinzipien","pt":"Verificação Antes da Conclusão: Princípio Fundamental","ru":"Верификация до Завершения: Основной Принцип","ar":"التحقق قبل الاستكمال: مبدأ أساسي","en":"verification-before-completion"},"description":{"zh":"验证前完成是一种开发原则，强调在声明工作完成前必须进行验证，确保开发质量和效率。","ja":"完了前に検証は、作業を完了したと主張する前に検証を行う必要性を強調する開発原則です。","ko":"완료 전 검증은 작업을 완료했다고 주장하기 전에 검증을 수행해야 한다는 개발 원칙을 강조합니다.","es":"La verificación antes de completar es un principio fundamental en el desarrollo. Asegúrate de tener evidencia antes de hacer reclamos","fr":"La vérification avant achèvement est un principe fondamental du développement. Assurez-vous d''avoir des preuves avant de faire des réclamations","de":"Die Verifizierung vor Abschluss ist ein grundlegendes Prinzip in der Entwicklung. Stellen Sie sicher, dass Sie Beweise haben, bevor Sie Ansprüche erheben","pt":"A verificação antes da conclusão é um princípio fundamental que assegura a integridade do trabalho, evitando alegações infundadas.","ru":"Верификация до завершения является основным принципом, обеспечивающим целостность работы, предотвращая необоснованные заявления.","ar":"التحقق قبل الاستكمال هو مبدأ أساسي يضمن سلامة العمل، ويمنع المطالبات غير المبررة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["强调验证在开发过程中的重要性","确保开发质量和效率","禁止未经验证的完成声明","提供验证证据","提高开发团队的责任感"],"ja":["開発プロセスにおける検証の重要性を強調","開発品質と効率を確保","検証なしの完了宣言を禁止","検証結果を提供","開発チームの責任感を高める"],"ko":["개발 프로세스에서 검증의 중요성을 강조","개발 품질과 효율성을 확보","검증 없이 완료를 선언하는 것을 금지","검증 결과를 제공","개발 팀의 책임감을 높임"],"es":["Requiere evidencia fresca para verificar el estado del proyecto","Evita reclamos falsos de finalización","Mejora la eficiencia y la honestidad en el desarrollo","Establece un principio claro para el desarrollo","Ayuda a prevenir errores y problemas en el proyecto"],"fr":["Exige des preuves fraîches pour vérifier l''état du projet","Évite les réclamations fausses d''achèvement","Améliore l''efficacité et l''honnêteté dans le développement","Établit un principe clair pour le développement","Aide à prévenir les erreurs et les problèmes dans le projet"],"de":["Erfordert frische Beweise, um den Status des Projekts zu überprüfen","Verhindert falsche Ansprüche auf Abschluss","Verbessert die Effizienz und Ehrlichkeit in der Entwicklung","Legt ein klares Prinzip für die Entwicklung fest","Hilft, Fehler und Probleme im Projekt zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Garantia de integridade do trabalho","Prevenção de alegações infundadas","Melhoria da eficiência","Redução de erros","Aumento da confiabilidade"],"ru":["Гарантия целостности работы","Предотвращение необоснованных заявлений","Улучшение эффективности","Снижение ошибок","Повышение надежности"],"ar":["ضمان سلامة العمل","منع المطالبات غير المبررة","تحسين الكفاءة","تقليل الأخطاء","زيادة الموثوقية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["验证前完成","开发原则","开发质量","开发效率","验证证据","开发团队","责任感"],"ja":["完了前に検証","開発原則","開発品質","開発効率","検証結果","開発チーム","責任感"],"ko":["완료 전 검증","개발 원칙","개발 품질","개발 효율","검증 결과","개발 팀","책임감"],"es":["verificación antes de completar","principios de desarrollo","eficiencia en el desarrollo","honestidad en el desarrollo","evidencia en el desarrollo","desarrollo de software","pruebas de software"],"fr":["vérification avant achèvement","principes de développement","efficacité dans le développement","honnêteté dans le développement","preuves dans le développement","développement de logiciels","tests de logiciels"],"de":["Verifizierung vor Abschluss","Entwicklungsprinzipien","Effizienz in der Entwicklung","Ehrlichkeit in der Entwicklung","Beweise in der Entwicklung","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Tests"],"pt":["verificação antes da conclusão","princípio fundamental","integridade do trabalho","eficiência","confiabilidade","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["верификация до завершения","основной принцип","целостность работы","эффективность","надежность","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التحقق قبل الاستكمال","مبدأ أساسي","سلامة العمل","كفاءة","موثوقية","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"dwalleck","repo":"kiro-starter-kit","repoPath":"dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"verification-before-completion","description":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always","bodyPreview":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing sati","body":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing satisfaction:\n\n1. IDENTIFY: What command proves this claim?\n2. RUN: Execute the FULL command (fresh, complete)\n3. READ: Full output, check exit code, count failures\n4. VERIFY: Does output confirm the claim?\n   - If NO: State actual status with evidence\n   - If YES: State claim WITH evidence\n5. ONLY THEN: Make the claim\n\nSkip any step = lying, not verifying\n```\n\n## Common Failures\n\n| Claim | Requires | Not Sufficient |\n|-------|----------|----------------|\n| Tests pass | Test command output: 0 failures | Previous run, \"should pass\" |\n| Linter clean | Linter output: 0 errors | Partial check, extrapolation |\n| Build succeeds | Build command: exit 0 | Linter passing, logs look good |\n| Bug fixed | Test original symptom: passes | Code changed, assumed fixed |\n| Regression test works | Red-green cycle verified | Test passes once |\n| Agent completed | VCS diff shows changes | Agent reports \"success\" |\n| Requirements met | Line-by-line checklist | Tests passing |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP\n\n- Using \"should\", \"probably\", \"seems to\"\n- Expressing satisfaction before verification (\"Great!\", \"Perfect!\", \"Done!\", etc.)\n- About to commit/push/PR without verification\n- Trusting agent success reports\n- Relying on partial verification\n- Thinking \"just this once\"\n- Tired and wanting work over\n- **ANY wording implying success without having run verification**\n\n## Rationalization Prevention\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Should work now\" | RUN the verification |\n| \"I''m confident\" | Confidence ≠ evidence |\n| \"Just this once\" | No exceptions |\n| \"Linter passed\" | Linter ≠ compiler |\n| \"Agent said success\" | Verify independently |\n| \"I''m tired\" | Exhaustion ≠ excuse |\n| \"Partial check is enough\" | Partial proves nothing |\n| \"Different words so rule doesn''t apply\" | Spirit over letter |\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n**Tests:**\n```\n✅ [Run test command] [See: 34/34 pass] \"All tests pass\"\n❌ \"Should pass now\" / \"Looks correct\"\n```\n\n**Regression tests (TDD Red-Green):**\n```\n✅ Write → Run (pass) → Revert fix → Run (MUST FAIL) → Restore → Run (pass)\n❌ \"I''ve written a regression test\" (without red-green verification)\n```\n\n**Build:**\n```\n✅ [Run build] [See: exit 0] \"Build passes\"\n❌ \"Linter passed\" (linter doesn''t check compilation)\n```\n\n**Requirements:**\n```\n✅ Re-read plan → Create checklist → Verify each → Report gaps or completion\n❌ \"Tests pass, phase complete\"\n```\n\n**Agent delegation:**\n```\n✅ Agent reports success → Check VCS diff → Verify changes → Report actual state\n❌ Trust agent report\n```\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nFrom 24 failure memories:\n- your human partner said \"I don''t believe you\" - trust broken\n- Undefined functions shipped - would crash\n- Missing requirements shipped - incomplete features\n- Time wasted on false completion → redirect → rework\n- Violates: \"Honesty is a core value. If you lie, you''ll be replaced.\"\n\n## When To Apply\n\n**ALWAYS before:**\n- ANY variation of success/completion claims\n- ANY expression of satisfaction\n- ANY positive statement about work state\n- Committing, PR creation, task completion\n- Moving to next task\n- Delegating to agents\n\n**Rule applies to:**\n- Exact phrases\n- Paraphrases and synonyms\n- Implications of success\n- ANY communication suggesting completion/correctness\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**No shortcuts for verification.**\n\nRun the command. Read the output. THEN claim the result.\n\nThis is non-negotiable.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:43:46.147Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Precision-Oriented Agents requiring rigorous validation and verification protocols","zh":"非常适合需要严格验证和核实协议的面向精确的代理","ja":"厳密な検証および検証プロトコルを必要とする精度志向のエージェントに最適","ko":"정밀한 검증 및 검사 프로토콜을 요구하는 정밀도 지향 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes con orientación a la precisión que requieren protocolos rigurosos de validación y verificación","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur la précision nécessitant des protocoles rigoureux de validation et de vérification","de":"Perfekt für präzisionsorientierte Agenten, die strenge Validierungs- und Verifizierungsprotokolle erfordern","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes com Orientação para Precisão que requerem protocolos rigorosos de validação e verificação","ru":"Идеально подходит для ориентированных на точность агентов, требующих строгих протоколов проверки и верификации","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المتجهين إلى الدقة الذين يتطلبون بروتوكولات صارمة للتحقق والتحقق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce the core principle of evidence before claims, ensuring integrity and accuracy through fresh verification evidence, adhering to the Iron Law of no completion claims without verification","zh":"赋予代理人以证据为先的核心原则，确保通过新鲜验证证据的完整性和准确性，遵守无验证即无完成的铁律","ja":"エージェントに証拠を優先するコア原則を実施させ、検証証拠を通じて完全性と正確性を確保することで、検証なしの完了は認められないという鉄の法則に従う","ko":"에이전트가 증거를 먼저 확인하는 핵심 원칙을 강화하여 신선한 검증 증거를 통해完整성과 정확성을 보장하고, 검증 없이 완료는 인정되지 않는다는 철의 법칙을 준수","es":"Habilita a los agentes a hacer cumplir el principio fundamental de la evidencia antes de las reclamaciones, garantizando la integridad y la precisión a través de evidencia de verificación fresca, ajustándose a la Ley de Hierro de no reclamaciones de finalización sin verificación","fr":"Permet aux agents de faire respecter le principe fondamental de la preuve avant les allégations, garantissant l''intégrité et la précision grâce à des preuves de vérification fraîches, conformément à la Loi de Fer de pas de réclamations de completion sans vérification","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, das Kernprinzip der Beweise vor den Ansprüchen durchzusetzen, die Integrität und Genauigkeit durch frische Verifizierungsbeweise sicherzustellen, indem sie sich an das Eisernes Gesetz von keinen Fertigstellungsansprüchen ohne Verifizierung halten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor o princípio fundamental de evidências antes de reivindicações, garantindo integridade e precisão por meio de evidências de verificação frescas, aderindo à Lei de Ferro de que não há reivindicações de conclusão sem verificação","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить соблюдение основного принципа доказательств до заявлений, гарантируя целостность и точность посредством свежих доказательств проверки, придерживаясь Железного Закона о том, что не существует заявлений о завершении без проверки","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على فرض المبدأ الأساسي للأدلة قبل المطالبات، وضمان السلامة والدقة من خلال أدلة التحقق الطازجة، والالتزام بقانون الحديد الذي لا يوجد به مطالب بإكمال بدون التحقق"},"useCases":{"en":["Validating task completion with fresh evidence","Enforcing the Iron Law in workflow automation","Debugging false completion claims"],"zh":["使用新鲜证据验证任务完成","在工作流自动化中强制执行铁律","调试虚假完成主张"],"ja":["新しい証拠を使用してタスクの完了を検証する","ワークフロー自動化で鉄の法則を強制する","偽の完了主張のデバッグ"],"ko":["신선한 증거를 사용하여 작업 완성을 검증","워크플로 자동화에서 철의 법칙을 강제","가짜 완료 주장의 디버깅"],"es":["Validar la finalización de tareas con evidencia fresca","Hacer cumplir la Ley de Hierro en la automatización de flujos de trabajo","Depurar reclamaciones falsas de finalización"],"fr":["Valider la completion de tâches avec des preuves fraîches","Faire respecter la Loi de Fer dans l''automatisation des flux de travail","Déboguer les allégations fausses de completion"],"de":["Die Vervollständigung von Aufgaben mit frischen Beweisen überprüfen","Das Eisernes Gesetz in der Workflow-Automatisierung durchsetzen","Falsche Fertigstellungsansprüche debuggen"],"pt":["Validar a conclusão de tarefas com evidências frescas","Impor a Lei de Ferro na automação de fluxos de trabalho","Depurar reivindicações de conclusão falsas"],"ru":["Проверка завершения задач с помощью свежих доказательств","Применение Железного Закона в автоматизации рабочих процессов","Отладка ложных заявлений о завершении"],"ar":["التحقق من إكمال المهام مع أدلة طازجة","تطبيق قانون الحديد في أتمتة سير العمل","تصحيح مطالب إكمال كاذبة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires strict adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the rule is considered a violation of the spirit of the rule"],"zh":["需要严格遵守铁律","违反规则的字面意义被认为是违反规则的精神"],"ja":["鉄の法則に厳格に従う必要がある","規則の文字通りに違反することは規則の精神に違反することとみなされる"],"ko":["철의 법칙을 엄격히 준수해야 함","규칙의 문자를 위반하는 것은 규칙의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주됨"],"es":["Requiere una estricta adherencia a la Ley de Hierro","Violación de la letra de la regla se considera una violación del espíritu de la regla"],"fr":["Requiert une stricte adhésion à la Loi de Fer","La violation de la lettre de la règle est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit de la règle"],"de":["Erfordert eine strikte Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes","Verletzung des Buchstabens der Regel gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Regel"],"pt":["Exige adesão estrita à Lei de Ferro","Violar a letra da regra é considerado uma violação do espírito da regra"],"ru":["Требует строгого соблюдения Железного Закона","Нарушение буквы правила считается нарушением духа правила"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع صارم لقانون الحديد","الانتهاك حرفيًا لقاعدة هو اعتبر انتهاكًا لروح القاعدة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant/brand-guidelines', 'community', 'rongma1sheng', 'kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant', 'rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant', 'brand-guidelines', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z', '2026-02-18T13:43:50.684Z', NULL, '{"id":"rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant/brand-guidelines","name":"brand-guidelines","description":{"zh":"Anthropic 品牌风格指南提供了品牌身份、颜色、字体和视觉设计的资源","ja":"Anthropic ブランドスタイリングは、ブランドアイデンティティ、色、フォント、視覚デザインのリソースを提供","ko":"Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링은 브랜드 아이덴티티, 색상, 글꼴 및 시각적 디자인의 리소스를 제공","es":"La guía de marca Anthropic proporciona acceso a recursos de identidad y estilo de marca, incluyendo colores, tipografía y diseño visual.","fr":"La ligne directrice de marque Anthropic fournit un accès aux ressources d''identité et de style de marque, y compris les couleurs, la typographie et le design visuel.","de":"Die Markenrichtlinien von Anthropic bieten Zugang zu Ressourcen für Markenidentität und -stil, einschließlich Farben, Typografie und visuellem Design.","pt":"As diretrizes de marca da Anthropic fornecem recursos de identidade e estilo visual para desenvolvedores","ru":"Руководство по бренду Anthropic предоставляет разработчикам ресурсы для идентичности и визуального стиля","ar":"إرشادات العلامة التجارية لشركة Anthropic توفر للمطورين موارد الهوية والتصميم المرئي","en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"品牌指南 - Anthropic 品牌风格指南","ja":"ブランドガイドライン - Anthropic ブランドスタイリング","ko":"브랜드 가이드라인 - Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링","es":"Pautas de marca Anthropic - Recursos de identidad visual","fr":"Lignes directrices de marque Anthropic - Ressources d''ide...","de":"Anthropic Markenrichtlinien - Ressourcen für visuelle Ide...","pt":"Diretrizes de Marca Anthropic","ru":"Руководство по бренду Anthropic","ar":"إرشادات العلامة التجارية لشركة Anthropic","en":"brand-guidelines"},"description":{"zh":"Anthropic 品牌风格指南提供了品牌身份、颜色、字体和视觉设计的资源","ja":"Anthropic ブランドスタイリングは、ブランドアイデンティティ、色、フォント、視覚デザインのリソースを提供","ko":"Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링은 브랜드 아이덴티티, 색상, 글꼴 및 시각적 디자인의 리소스를 제공","es":"La guía de marca Anthropic proporciona acceso a recursos de identidad y estilo de marca, incluyendo colores, tipografía y diseño visual.","fr":"La ligne directrice de marque Anthropic fournit un accès aux ressources d''identité et de style de marque, y compris les couleurs, la typographie et le design...","de":"Die Markenrichtlinien von Anthropic bieten Zugang zu Ressourcen für Markenidentität und -stil, einschließlich Farben, Typografie und visuellem Design.","pt":"As diretrizes de marca da Anthropic fornecem recursos de identidade e estilo visual para desenvolvedores","ru":"Руководство по бренду Anthropic предоставляет разработчикам ресурсы для идентичности и визуального стиля","ar":"إرشادات العلامة التجارية لشركة Anthropic توفر للمطورين موارد الهوية والتصميم المرئي","en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"definition":{"en":"🤖 Kiro智能开发助手 - AI驱动的开发支持系统"},"features":{"zh":["品牌颜色","字体样式","视觉设计","品牌风格指南","Anthropic 品牌身份"],"ja":["ブランドカラー","フォントスタイル","視覚デザイン","ブランドスタイリングガイドライン","Anthropic ブランドアイデンティティ"],"ko":["브랜드 색상","글꼴 스타일","시각적 디자인","브랜드 스타일링 가이드라인","Anthropic 브랜드 아이덴티티"],"es":["Colores de marca personalizados","Tipografía y diseño visual","Recursos de identidad de marca","Estilo de marca consistente","Guía de diseño visual"],"fr":["Couleurs de marque personnalisées","Typographie et design visuel","Ressources d''identité de marque","Style de marque cohérent","Guide de design visuel"],"de":["Maßgeschneiderte Markenfarben","Typografie und visuelles Design","Ressourcen für Markenidentität","Konsistentes Markenimage","Leitfaden für visuelles Design"],"pt":["Cores principais: Dark, Light e Mid Gray","Tipografia e formatação visual","Recursos de estilo e design","Guia de identidade de marca","Recursos de desenvolvimento para designers e desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Основные цвета: Dark, Light и Mid Gray","Типография и визуальная форматировка","Ресурсы стиля и дизайна","Руководство по идентичности бренда","Ресурсы для разработчиков и дизайнеров"],"ar":["الألوان الرئيسية: الداكن والفاتح والرمادي المتوسط","الطباعة والتنسيق المرئي","مصادر الأسلوب والتصميم","دليل الهوية التجارية","مصادر التطوير لمصممي و مطوري التطبيقات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["品牌指南","Anthropic 品牌风格","品牌身份","视觉设计","颜色","字体","品牌风格指南"],"ja":["ブランドガイドライン","Anthropic ブランドスタイリング","ブランドアイデンティティ","視覚デザイン","色","フォント","ブランドスタイリングガイドライン"],"ko":["브랜드 가이드라인","Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링","브랜드 아이덴티티","시각적 디자인","색상","글꼴","브랜드 스타일링 가이드라인"],"es":["pautas de marca","identidad visual","colores de marca","tipografía","diseño visual","marca anthropic","recursos de marca","estilo de marca","guía de diseño"],"fr":["lignes directrices de marque","identité visuelle","couleurs de marque","typographie","design visuel","marque anthropic","ressources de marque","style de marque","guide de design"],"de":["markenrichtlinien","visuelle identität","markenfarben","typografie","visuelles design","anthropic marke","markenressourcen","markenimage","designleitfaden"],"pt":["diretrizes de marca","identidade visual","desenvolvimento de software","design de interface","tipografia","cores da marca","estilo de marca","guias de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["руководство по бренду","визуальная идентичность","разработка программного обеспечения","дизайн интерфейса","типография","цвета бренда","стиль бренда","руководства для разработчиков"],"ar":["إرشادات العلامة التجارية","الهوية المرئية","تطوير البرمجيات","تصميم الواجهة","الطباعة","ألوان العلامة التجارية","أسلوب العلامة التجارية","دلائل المطورين"]}},"owner":"rongma1sheng","repo":"kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","repoPath":"rongma1sheng/kiro-intelligent-dev-assistant","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brand-guidelines","description":"Applies Anthropics official brand colors and typography to any sort of artifact that may benefit from having Anthropics look-and-feel. Use it when brand colors or style guidelines, visual formatting, or company design standards apply.","bodyPreview":"# Anthropic Brand Styling\n\n## Overview\n\nTo access Anthropic''s official brand identity and style resources, use this skill.\n\n**Keywords**: branding, corporate identity, visual identity, post-processing, styling, brand colors, typography, Anthropic brand, visual formatting, visual design\n\n## Brand Guidelines\n\n### Colors\n\n**Main Colors:**\n\n- Dark: `#141413` - Primary text and dark backgrounds\n- Light: `#faf9f5` - Light backgrounds and text on dark\n- Mid Gray: `#b0aea5` - Secondary elements\n- Light","body":"# Anthropic Brand Styling\n\n## Overview\n\nTo access Anthropic''s official brand identity and style resources, use this skill.\n\n**Keywords**: branding, corporate identity, visual identity, post-processing, styling, brand colors, typography, Anthropic brand, visual formatting, visual design\n\n## Brand Guidelines\n\n### Colors\n\n**Main Colors:**\n\n- Dark: `#141413` - Primary text and dark backgrounds\n- Light: `#faf9f5` - Light backgrounds and text on dark\n- Mid Gray: `#b0aea5` - Secondary elements\n- Light Gray: `#e8e6dc` - Subtle backgrounds\n\n**Accent Colors:**\n\n- Orange: `#d97757` - Primary accent\n- Blue: `#6a9bcc` - Secondary accent\n- Green: `#788c5d` - Tertiary accent\n\n### Typography\n\n- **Headings**: Poppins (with Arial fallback)\n- **Body Text**: Lora (with Georgia fallback)\n- **Note**: Fonts should be pre-installed in your environment for best results\n\n## Features\n\n### Smart Font Application\n\n- Applies Poppins font to headings (24pt and larger)\n- Applies Lora font to body text\n- Automatically falls back to Arial/Georgia if custom fonts unavailable\n- Preserves readability across all systems\n\n### Text Styling\n\n- Headings (24pt+): Poppins font\n- Body text: Lora font\n- Smart color selection based on background\n- Preserves text hierarchy and formatting\n\n### Shape and Accent Colors\n\n- Non-text shapes use accent colors\n- Cycles through orange, blue, and green accents\n- Maintains visual interest while staying on-brand\n\n## Technical Details\n\n### Font Management\n\n- Uses system-installed Poppins and Lora fonts when available\n- Provides automatic fallback to Arial (headings) and Georgia (body)\n- No font installation required - works with existing system fonts\n- For best results, pre-install Poppins and Lora fonts in your environment\n\n### Color Application\n\n- Uses RGB color values for precise brand matching\n- Applied via python-pptx''s RGBColor class\n- Maintains color fidelity across different systems\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:43:50.684Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Design-focused Agents requiring precise brand styling and visual identity implementation.","zh":"适合需要精确品牌样式和视觉身份实现的设计导向代理。","ja":"デザイン志向のエージェントが正確なブランドスタイリングと視覚的アイデンティティの実装を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"정확한 브랜드 스타일링 및 시각적 정체성 구현이 필요한 디자인 중심 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes enfocados en diseño que requieren un estilo de marca y una identidad visual precisos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents axés sur la conception nécessitant un style de marque et une identité visuelle précis.","de":"Ideal für designorientierte Agenten, die eine präzise Markenstyling und visuelle Identitätsimplementierung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes focados em Design que exigem estilização de marca precisa e implementação de identidade visual.","ru":"Идеально для агентов, ориентированных на дизайн, требующих точного брендирования и реализации визуальной идентичности.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الوسيط المتخصص في التصميم الذي يتطلب تنسيق علامة تجارية دقيقًا وتطبيقًا للهوية البصرية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce consistent branding across platforms using Anthropic''s official brand colors, typography, and visual formatting guidelines, ensuring adherence to specific styles like #141413 for primary text and dark backgrounds.","zh":"赋予代理商在各个平台上使用Anthropic的官方品牌颜色、字体和视觉格式指南强制执行一致的品牌推广，确保遵守特定的样式，如#141413用于主文本和深色背景。","ja":"Anthropicの公式ブランドカラー、タイポグラフィ、視覚的なフォーマットガイドラインを使用して、エージェントがプラットフォーム全体で一貫したブランド化を強制することを可能にし、#141413のような主なテキストとダークバックグラウンドの特定のスタイルへの準拠を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 Anthropic의 공식 브랜드 색상, 타이포그래피 및 시각적 형식 지침을 사용하여 모든 플랫폼에서 일관된 브랜딩을 강제 적용할 수 있도록 하며, #141413과 같은 주요 텍스트 및 다크 배경의 특정 스타일을 준수합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar una marca coherente en varias plataformas utilizando los colores de marca oficiales de Anthropic, la tipografía y las pautas de formato visual, asegurando el cumplimiento de estilos específicos como #141413 para texto principal y fondos oscuros.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer une marque cohérente sur plusieurs plateformes en utilisant les couleurs de marque officielles d''Anthropic, la typographie et les lignes directrices de formatage visuel, en garantissant le respect de styles spécifiques comme #141413 pour le texte principal et les arrières-plans sombres.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, eine konsistente Markenidentität auf verschiedenen Plattformen durchzusetzen, indem sie die offiziellen Markenfarben, Typografie und visuellen Formatierungsrichtlinien von Anthropic verwenden, um die Einhaltung spezifischer Stile wie #141413 für Primärtext und dunkle Hintergründe sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor marcação consistente em várias plataformas usando as cores oficiais da marca Anthropic, a tipografia e as diretrizes de formatação visual, garantindo a adesão a estilos específicos como #141413 para texto primário e fundos escuros.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить последовательное брендирование на различных платформах с использованием официальных бренд-цветов Anthropic, типографики и руководящих принципов визуального форматирования, обеспечивая соблюдение определенных стилей, таких как #141413 для основного текста и темных фонов.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من فرض التسمية التجارية المتسقة عبر منصات متعددة باستخدام ألوان العلامة التجارية الرسمية لشركة Anthropic والطباعة والتنسيق البصري الإرشادي، مما يضمن الالتزام بالأساليب المحددة مثل #141413 لنص رئيسي وخلفيات مظلمة."},"useCases":{"en":["Applying Anthropic brand guidelines to new marketing materials","Generating consistent visual identities for web and mobile applications","Validating brand color schemes against Anthropic''s main colors"],"zh":["将Anthropic品牌指南应用于新的营销材料","为Web和移动应用程序生成一致的视觉身份","将品牌颜色方案验证为Anthropic的主色"],"ja":["新しいマーケティング資料にAnthropicのブランドガイドラインを適用する","Webおよびモバイルアプリケーションに一貫した視覚的なアイデンティティを生成する","ブランドカラースキームをAnthropicのメインカラーと比較検証する"],"ko":["新的 마케팅 자료에 Anthropic 브랜드 가이드ライン을 적용하는 것","웹 및 모바일 애플리케이션에 일관된 시각적 정체성을 생성하는 것","브랜드 색상 스키마를 Anthropic의 주요 색상과 비교 검증하는 것"],"es":["Aplicar las pautas de marca de Anthropic a nuevos materiales de marketing","Generar identidades visuales coherentes para aplicaciones web y móviles","Validar esquemas de color de marca contra los colores principales de Anthropic"],"fr":["Appliquer les lignes directrices de marque d''Anthropic à de nouveaux matériaux de marketing","Générer des identités visuelles cohérentes pour les applications Web et mobiles","Valider les schémas de couleur de marque par rapport aux couleurs principales d''Anthropic"],"de":["Die Markenrichtlinien von Anthropic auf neue Marketingmaterialien anwenden","Konsistente visuelle Identitäten für Web- und Mobile-Anwendungen generieren","Markenfarbschemata gegen die Hauptfarben von Anthropic validieren"],"pt":["Aplicar diretrizes de marca Anthropic a novos materiais de marketing","Gerar identidades visuais consistentes para aplicativos web e móveis","Validar esquemas de cores de marca contra as cores principais da Anthropic"],"ru":["Применение руководящих принципов бренда Anthropic к новым материалам маркетинга","Генерация последовательных визуальных идентичностей для веб- и мобильных приложений","Проверка схем цветов бренда с основными цветами Anthropic"],"ar":["تطبيق إرشادات العلامة التجارية لشركة Anthropic على مواد تسويقية جديدة","генерация هويات بصرية متسقة لتطبيقات الويب والأجهزة المحمولة","التحقق من مخططات ألوان العلامة التجارية مقابل الألوان الرئيسية لشركة Anthropic"]},"limitations":{"en":["Limited to Anthropic''s brand identity and style resources","Requires understanding of color codes and typography"],"zh":["仅限于Anthropic的品牌身份和样式资源","需要对颜色代码和字体有所了解"],"ja":["Anthropicのブランドアイデンティティとスタイルリソースのみに限定される","カラーコードとタイポグラフィに関する知識が必要"],"ko":["Anthropic의 브랜드 정체성 및 스타일 리소스만으로 제한됨","색상 코드 및 타이포그래피에 대한 지식이 필요함"],"es":["Limitado a los recursos de identidad y estilo de marca de Anthropic","Requiere comprensión de códigos de color y tipografía"],"fr":["Limité aux ressources d''identité et de style de marque d''Anthropic","Nécessite une compréhension des codes de couleur et de la typographie"],"de":["Begrenzt auf die Identitäts- und Stilressourcen von Anthropic","Benötigt Verständnis von Farbcodes und Typografie"],"pt":["Limitado à identidade e recursos de estilo da marca Anthropic","Exige compreensão de códigos de cor e tipografia"],"ru":["Ограничен идентичностью и ресурсами стиля бренда Anthropic","Требует понимания кодов цвета и типографики"],"ar":["محدود بهوية شركة Anthropic وأسلوب الموارد","يتطلب فهم أكواد الألوان والطباعة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/fastapi-templates', 'community', 'yashvinthan', 'DuskSpendr', 'yashvinthan/DuskSpendr', 'fastapi-templates', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z', '2026-02-18T13:44:04.567Z', NULL, '{"id":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/fastapi-templates","name":"fastapi-templates","description":{"zh":"FastAPI项目模板，提供生产就绪的项目结构，包括异步模式、依赖注入、中间件和最佳实践","ja":"FastAPIプロジェクトテンプレート、プロダクションレディのプロジェクト構造を提供します。非同期パターン、依存性注入、中間件、ベストプラクティスなどを含みます","ko":"FastAPI 프로젝트 템플릿, 프로덕션 레디 프로젝트 구조를 제공합니다. 비동기 패턴, 의존성 주입, 미들웨어 및 최선의实践을 포함합니다","es":"Plantillas de proyecto FastAPI listas para producción con patrones asíncronos y mejores prácticas para construir API de alto rendimiento","fr":"Modèles de projet FastAPI prêts pour la production avec des modèles asynchrones et les meilleures pratiques pour construire des API hautement performantes","de":"Produktionsreife FastAPI-Projektvorlagen mit asynchronen Mustern und bewährten Methoden für den Bau hochleistungsstarker APIs","pt":"Os templates de projeto FastAPI fornecem estruturas de projeto prontas para produção com padrões assíncronos e injeção de dependência para construir APIs de alto desempenho.","ru":"Шаблоны проекта FastAPI предоставляют готовые структуры проектов для продукции с асинхронными шаблонами и внедрением зависимостей для построения высокопроизводительных API.","ar":"قوالب مشروع FastAPI توفر هياكل مشروع جاهزة للإنتاج مع الأنماط غير المتزامنة وإدارة التبعيات لبناء واجهات برمجة تطبيقات عالية الأداء.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"FastAPI模板 - 构建高性能API","ja":"FastAPIテンプレート - ハイパフォーマンスAPIの構築","ko":"FastAPI 템플릿 - 고성능 API 구축","es":"Plantillas de FastAPI para proyectos de alto rendimiento","fr":"Modèles de projet FastAPI pour des API hautement performa...","de":"FastAPI-Vorlagen für hochleistungsstarke Projekte","pt":"FastAPI Templates: Estruturas de Projeto Prontas para Pro...","ru":"Шаблоны FastAPI: Готовые Структуры Проектов для Продукции","ar":"قوالب FastAPI: هياكل مشروع جاهزة للإنتاج","en":"fastapi-templates"},"description":{"zh":"FastAPI项目模板，提供生产就绪的项目结构，包括异步模式、依赖注入、中间件和最佳实践","ja":"FastAPIプロジェクトテンプレート、プロダクションレディのプロジェクト構造を提供します。非同期パターン、依存性注入、中間件、ベストプラクティスなどを含みます","ko":"FastAPI 프로젝트 템플릿, 프로덕션 레디 프로젝트 구조를 제공합니다. 비동기 패턴, 의존성 주입, 미들웨어 및 최선의实践을 포함합니다","es":"Plantillas de proyecto FastAPI listas para producción con patrones asíncronos y mejores prácticas para construir API de alto rendimiento","fr":"Modèles de projet FastAPI prêts pour la production avec des modèles asynchrones et les meilleures pratiques pour construire des API hautement performantes","de":"Produktionsreife FastAPI-Projektvorlagen mit asynchronen Mustern und bewährten Methoden für den Bau hochleistungsstarker APIs","pt":"Os templates de projeto FastAPI fornecem estruturas de projeto prontas para produção com padrões assíncronos e injeção de dependência para construir APIs de ...","ru":"Шаблоны проекта FastAPI предоставляют готовые структуры проектов для продукции с асинхронными шаблонами и внедрением зависимостей для построения высокопроизв...","ar":"قوالب مشروع FastAPI توفر هياكل مشروع جاهزة للإنتاج مع الأنماط غير المتزامنة وإدارة التبعيات لبناء واجهات برمجة تطبيقات عالية الأداء.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["异步REST API","依赖注入","中间件","生产就绪的项目结构","PostgreSQL和MongoDB支持"],"ja":["非同期REST API","依存性注入","中間件","プロダクションレディのプロジェクト構造","PostgreSQLとMongoDBのサポート"],"ko":["비동기 REST API","의존성 주입","미들웨어","프로덕션 레디 프로젝트 구조","PostgreSQL 및 MongoDB 지원"],"es":["Estructuras de proyecto listas para producción","Patrones asíncronos para API de alto rendimiento","Inyección de dependencias para una mayor flexibilidad","Middleware para una mayor seguridad y escalabilidad","Mejores prácticas para la construcción de API"],"fr":["Structures de projet prêtes pour la production","Modèles asynchrones pour des API hautement performantes","Injection de dépendances pour une plus grande flexibilité","Middleware pour une plus grande sécurité et évolutivité","Meilleures pratiques pour la construction d''API"],"de":["Produktionsreife Projektstrukturen","Asynchrone Muster für hochleistungsstarke APIs","Abhängigkeitsinjektion für eine größere Flexibilität","Middleware für eine größere Sicherheit und Skalierbarkeit","Bewährte Methoden für den Bau von APIs"],"pt":["Estruturas de projeto prontas para produção","Padrões assíncronos para construir APIs de alto desempenho","Injeção de dependência para gerenciar dependências","Middleware para manipular requisições e respostas","Suporte a bancos de dados como PostgreSQL e MongoDB"],"ru":["Готовые структуры проектов для продукции","Асинхронные шаблоны для построения высокопроизводительных API","Внедрение зависимостей для управления зависимостями","Middleware для манипулирования запросами и ответами","Поддержка баз данных, таких как PostgreSQL и MongoDB"],"ar":["هياكل مشروع جاهزة للإنتاج","الأنماط غير المتزامنة لبناء واجهات برمجة تطبيقات عالية الأداء","إدارة التبعيات للتحكم في التبعيات","برامج الوسيط للتحكم في الطلبات والاستجابات","دعم قواعد البيانات مثل PostgreSQL و MongoDB"]},"keywords":{"zh":["FastAPI","高性能API","异步REST API","依赖注入","中间件","PostgreSQL","MongoDB"],"ja":["FastAPI","ハイパフォーマンスAPI","非同期REST API","依存性注入","中間件","PostgreSQL","MongoDB"],"ko":["FastAPI","고성능 API","비동기 REST API","의존성 주입","미들웨어","PostgreSQL","MongoDB"],"es":["FastAPI","plantillas de proyecto","API de alto rendimiento","patrones asíncronos","inyección de dependencias","middleware","mejores prácticas","Python","desarrollo de API"],"fr":["FastAPI","modèles de projet","API hautement performantes","modèles asynchrones","injection de dépendances","middleware","meilleures pratiques","Python","développement d''API"],"de":["FastAPI","Projektvorlagen","hochleistungsstarke APIs","asynchrone Muster","Abhängigkeitsinjektion","Middleware","bewährte Methoden","Python","API-Entwicklung"],"pt":["FastAPI","Templates de projeto","APIs de alto desempenho","Padrões assíncronos","Injeção de dependência","Middleware","PostgreSQL","MongoDB"],"ru":["FastAPI","Шаблоны проекта","Высокопроизводительные API","Асинхронные шаблоны","Внедрение зависимостей","Middleware","PostgreSQL","MongoDB"],"ar":["FastAPI","قوالب مشروع","واجهات برمجة تطبيقات عالية الأداء","الأنماط غير المتزامنة","إدارة التبعيات","برامج الوسيط","PostgreSQL","MongoDB"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fastapi-templates","description":"Create production-ready FastAPI projects with async patterns, dependency injection, and comprehensive error handling. Use when building new FastAPI applications or setting up backend API projects.","bodyPreview":"# FastAPI Project Templates\n\nProduction-ready FastAPI project structures with async patterns, dependency injection, middleware, and best practices for building high-performance APIs.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Starting new FastAPI projects from scratch\n- Implementing async REST APIs with Python\n- Building high-performance web services and microservices\n- Creating async applications with PostgreSQL, MongoDB\n- Setting up API projects with proper structure and testing\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. P","body":"# FastAPI Project Templates\n\nProduction-ready FastAPI project structures with async patterns, dependency injection, middleware, and best practices for building high-performance APIs.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Starting new FastAPI projects from scratch\n- Implementing async REST APIs with Python\n- Building high-performance web services and microservices\n- Creating async applications with PostgreSQL, MongoDB\n- Setting up API projects with proper structure and testing\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Project Structure\n\n**Recommended Layout:**\n\n```\napp/\n├── api/                    # API routes\n│   ├── v1/\n│   │   ├── endpoints/\n│   │   │   ├── users.py\n│   │   │   ├── auth.py\n│   │   │   └── items.py\n│   │   └── router.py\n│   └── dependencies.py     # Shared dependencies\n├── core/                   # Core configuration\n│   ├── config.py\n│   ├── security.py\n│   └── database.py\n├── models/                 # Database models\n│   ├── user.py\n│   └── item.py\n├── schemas/                # Pydantic schemas\n│   ├── user.py\n│   └── item.py\n├── services/               # Business logic\n│   ├── user_service.py\n│   └── auth_service.py\n├── repositories/           # Data access\n│   ├── user_repository.py\n│   └── item_repository.py\n└── main.py                 # Application entry\n```\n\n### 2. Dependency Injection\n\nFastAPI''s built-in DI system using `Depends`:\n\n- Database session management\n- Authentication/authorization\n- Shared business logic\n- Configuration injection\n\n### 3. Async Patterns\n\nProper async/await usage:\n\n- Async route handlers\n- Async database operations\n- Async background tasks\n- Async middleware\n\n## Implementation Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Complete FastAPI Application\n\n```python\n# main.py\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Depends\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    \"\"\"Application lifespan events.\"\"\"\n    # Startup\n    await database.connect()\n    yield\n    # Shutdown\n    await database.disconnect()\n\napp = FastAPI(\n    title=\"API Template\",\n    version=\"1.0.0\",\n    lifespan=lifespan\n)\n\n# CORS middleware\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=[\"*\"],\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n\n# Include routers\nfrom app.api.v1.router import api_router\napp.include_router(api_router, prefix=\"/api/v1\")\n\n# core/config.py\nfrom pydantic_settings import BaseSettings\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\nclass Settings(BaseSettings):\n    \"\"\"Application settings.\"\"\"\n    DATABASE_URL: str\n    SECRET_KEY: str\n    ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES: int = 30\n    API_V1_STR: str = \"/api/v1\"\n\n    class Config:\n        env_file = \".env\"\n\n@lru_cache()\ndef get_settings() -> Settings:\n    return Settings()\n\n# core/database.py\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import create_async_engine, AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\nfrom app.core.config import get_settings\n\nsettings = get_settings()\n\nengine = create_async_engine(\n    settings.DATABASE_URL,\n    echo=True,\n    future=True\n)\n\nAsyncSessionLocal = sessionmaker(\n    engine,\n    class_=AsyncSession,\n    expire_on_commit=False\n)\n\nBase = declarative_base()\n\nasync def get_db() -> AsyncSession:\n    \"\"\"Dependency for database session.\"\"\"\n    async with AsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n        try:\n            yield session\n            await session.commit()\n        except Exception:\n            await session.rollback()\n            raise\n        finally:\n            await session.close()\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: CRUD Repository Pattern\n\n```python\n# repositories/base_repository.py\nfrom typing import Generic, TypeVar, Type, Optional, List\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nModelType = TypeVar(\"ModelType\")\nCreateSchemaType = TypeVar(\"CreateSchemaType\", bound=BaseModel)\nUpdateSchemaType = TypeVar(\"UpdateSchemaType\", bound=BaseModel)\n\nclass BaseRepository(Generic[ModelType, CreateSchemaType, UpdateSchemaType]):\n    \"\"\"Base repository for CRUD operations.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, model: Type[ModelType]):\n        self.model = model\n\n    async def get(self, db: AsyncSession, id: int) -> Optional[ModelType]:\n        \"\"\"Get by ID.\"\"\"\n        result = await db.execute(\n            select(self.model).where(self.model.id == id)\n        )\n        return result.scalars().first()\n\n    async def get_multi(\n        self,\n        db: AsyncSession,\n        skip: int = 0,\n        limit: int = 100\n    ) -> List[ModelType]:\n        \"\"\"Get multiple records.\"\"\"\n        result = await db.execute(\n            select(self.model).offset(skip).limit(limit)\n        )\n        return result.scalars().all()\n\n    async def create(\n        self,\n        db: AsyncSession,\n        obj_in: CreateSchemaType\n    ) -> ModelType:\n        \"\"\"Create new record.\"\"\"\n        db_obj = self.model(**obj_in.dict())\n        db.add(db_obj)\n        await db.flush()\n        await db.refresh(db_obj)\n        return db_obj\n\n    async def update(\n        self,\n        db: AsyncSession,\n        db_obj: ModelType,\n        obj_in: UpdateSchemaType\n    ) -> ModelType:\n        \"\"\"Update record.\"\"\"\n        update_data = obj_in.dict(exclude_unset=True)\n        for field, value in update_data.items():\n            setattr(db_obj, field, value)\n        await db.flush()\n        await db.refresh(db_obj)\n        return db_obj\n\n    async def delete(self, db: AsyncSession, id: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Delete record.\"\"\"\n        obj = await self.get(db, id)\n        if obj:\n            await db.delete(obj)\n            return True\n        return False\n\n# repositories/user_repository.py\nfrom app.repositories.base_repository import BaseRepository\nfrom app.models.user import User\nfrom app.schemas.user import UserCreate, UserUpdate\n\nclass UserRepository(BaseRepository[User, UserCreate, UserUpdate]):\n    \"\"\"User-specific repository.\"\"\"\n\n    async def get_by_email(self, db: AsyncSession, email: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        \"\"\"Get user by email.\"\"\"\n        result = await db.execute(\n            select(User).where(User.email == email)\n        )\n        return result.scalars().first()\n\n    async def is_active(self, db: AsyncSession, user_id: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if user is active.\"\"\"\n        user = await self.get(db, user_id)\n        return user.is_active if user else False\n\nuser_repository = UserRepository(User)\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Service Layer\n\n```python\n# services/user_service.py\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\nfrom app.repositories.user_repository import user_repository\nfrom app.schemas.user import UserCreate, UserUpdate, User\nfrom app.core.security import get_password_hash, verify_password\n\nclass UserService:\n    \"\"\"Business logic for users.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.repository = user_repository\n\n    async def create_user(\n        self,\n        db: AsyncSession,\n        user_in: UserCreate\n    ) -> User:\n        \"\"\"Create new user with hashed password.\"\"\"\n        # Check if email exists\n        existing = await self.repository.get_by_email(db, user_in.email)\n        if existing:\n            raise ValueError(\"Email already registered\")\n\n        # Hash password\n        user_in_dict = user_in.dict()\n        user_in_dict[\"hashed_password\"] = get_password_hash(user_in_dict.pop(\"password\"))\n\n        # Create user\n        user = await self.repository.create(db, UserCreate(**user_in_dict))\n        return user\n\n    async def authenticate(\n        self,\n        db: AsyncSession,\n        email: str,\n        password: str\n    ) -> Optional[User]:\n        \"\"\"Authenticate user.\"\"\"\n        user = await self.repository.get_by_email(db, email)\n        if not user:\n            return None\n        if not verify_password(password, user.hashed_password):\n            return None\n        return user\n\n    async def update_user(\n        self,\n        db: AsyncSession,\n        user_id: int,\n        user_in: UserUpdate\n    ) -> Optional[User]:\n        \"\"\"Update user.\"\"\"\n        user = await self.repository.get(db, user_id)\n        if not user:\n            return None\n\n        if user_in.password:\n            user_in_dict = user_in.dict(exclude_unset=True)\n            user_in_dict[\"hashed_password\"] = get_password_hash(\n                user_in_dict.pop(\"password\")\n            )\n            user_in = UserUpdate(**user_in_dict)\n\n        return await self.repository.update(db, user, user_in)\n\nuser_service = UserService()\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: API Endpoints with Dependencies\n\n```python\n# api/v1/endpoints/users.py\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException, status\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom app.core.database import get_db\nfrom app.schemas.user import User, UserCreate, UserUpdate\nfrom app.services.user_service import user_service\nfrom app.api.dependencies import get_current_user\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\n@router.post(\"/\", response_model=User, status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)\nasync def create_user(\n    user_in: UserCreate,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)\n):\n    \"\"\"Create new user.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        user = await user_service.create_user(db, user_in)\n        return user\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e))\n\n@router.get(\"/me\", response_model=User)\nasync def read_current_user(\n    current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user)\n):\n    \"\"\"Get current user.\"\"\"\n    return current_user\n\n@router.get(\"/{user_id}\", response_model=User)\nasync def read_user(\n    user_id: int,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n    current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user)\n):\n    \"\"\"Get user by ID.\"\"\"\n    user = await user_service.repository.get(db, user_id)\n    if not user:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"User not found\")\n    return user\n\n@router.patch(\"/{user_id}\", response_model=User)\nasync def update_user(\n    user_id: int,\n    user_in: UserUpdate,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n    current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user)\n):\n    \"\"\"Update user.\"\"\"\n    if current_user.id != user_id:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail=\"Not authorized\")\n\n    user = await user_service.update_user(db, user_id, user_in)\n    if not user:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"User not found\")\n    return user\n\n@router.delete(\"/{user_id}\", status_code=status.HTTP_204_NO_CONTENT)\nasync def delete_user(\n    user_id: int,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n    current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user)\n):\n    \"\"\"Delete user.\"\"\"\n    if current_user.id != user_id:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail=\"Not authorized\")\n\n    deleted = await user_service.repository.delete(db, user_id)\n    if not deleted:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"User not found\")\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Authentication & Authorization\n\n```python\n# core/security.py\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom jose import JWTError, jwt\nfrom passlib.context import CryptContext\nfrom app.core.config import get_settings\n\nsettings = get_settings()\npwd_context = CryptContext(schemes=[\"bcrypt\"], deprecated=\"auto\")\n\nALGORITHM = \"HS256\"\n\ndef create_access_token(data: dict, expires_delta: Optional[timedelta] = None):\n    \"\"\"Create JWT access token.\"\"\"\n    to_encode = data.copy()\n    if expires_delta:\n        expire = datetime.utcnow() + expires_delta\n    else:\n        expire = datetime.utcnow() + timedelta(minutes=15)\n    to_encode.update({\"exp\": expire})\n    encoded_jwt = jwt.encode(to_encode, settings.SECRET_KEY, algorithm=ALGORITHM)\n    return encoded_jwt\n\ndef verify_password(plain_password: str, hashed_password: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Verify password against hash.\"\"\"\n    return pwd_context.verify(plain_password, hashed_password)\n\ndef get_password_hash(password: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Hash password.\"\"\"\n    return pwd_context.hash(password)\n\n# api/dependencies.py\nfrom fastapi import Depends, HTTPException, status\nfrom fastapi.security import OAuth2PasswordBearer\nfrom jose import JWTError, jwt\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\n\nfrom app.core.database import get_db\nfrom app.core.security import ALGORITHM\nfrom app.core.config import get_settings\nfrom app.repositories.user_repository import user_repository\n\noauth2_scheme = OAuth2PasswordBearer(tokenUrl=f\"{settings.API_V1_STR}/auth/login\")\n\nasync def get_current_user(\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n    token: str = Depends(oauth2_scheme)\n):\n    \"\"\"Get current authenticated user.\"\"\"\n    credentials_exception = HTTPException(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n        detail=\"Could not validate credentials\",\n        headers={\"WWW-Authenticate\": \"Bearer\"},\n    )\n\n    try:\n        payload = jwt.decode(token, settings.SECRET_KEY, algorithms=[ALGORITHM])\n        user_id: int = payload.get(\"sub\")\n        if user_id is None:\n            raise credentials_exception\n    except JWTError:\n        raise credentials_exception\n\n    user = await user_repository.get(db, user_id)\n    if user is None:\n        raise credentials_exception\n\n    return user\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n```python\n# tests/conftest.py\nimport pytest\nimport asyncio\nfrom httpx import AsyncClient\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import create_async_engine, AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\n\nfrom app.main import app\nfrom app.core.database import get_db, Base\n\nTEST_DATABASE_URL = \"sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:\"\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef event_loop():\n    loop = asyncio.get_event_loop_policy().new_event_loop()\n    yield loop\n    loop.close()\n\n@pytest.fixture\nasync def db_session():\n    engine = create_async_engine(TEST_DATABASE_URL, echo=True)\n    async with engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    AsyncSessionLocal = sessionmaker(\n        engine, class_=AsyncSession, expire_on_commit=False\n    )\n\n    async with AsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n        yield session\n\n@pytest.fixture\nasync def client(db_session):\n    async def override_get_db():\n        yield db_session\n\n    app.dependency_overrides[get_db] = override_get_db\n\n    async with AsyncClient(app=app, base_url=\"http://test\") as client:\n        yield client\n\n# tests/test_users.py\nimport pytest\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_create_user(client):\n    response = await client.post(\n        \"/api/v1/users/\",\n        json={\n            \"email\": \"test@example.com\",\n            \"password\": \"testpass123\",\n            \"name\": \"Test User\"\n        }\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 201\n    data = response.json()\n    assert data[\"email\"] == \"test@example.com\"\n    assert \"id\" in data\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/fastapi-architecture.md**: Detailed architecture guide\n- **references/async-best-practices.md**: Async/await patterns\n- **references/testing-strategies.md**: Comprehensive testing guide\n- **assets/project-template/**: Complete FastAPI project\n- **assets/docker-compose.yml**: Development environment setup\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Async All The Way**: Use async for database, external APIs\n2. **Dependency Injection**: Leverage FastAPI''s DI system\n3. **Repository Pattern**: Separate data access from business logic\n4. **Service Layer**: Keep business logic out of routes\n5. **Pydantic Schemas**: Strong typing for request/response\n6. **Error Handling**: Consistent error responses\n7. **Testing**: Test all layers independently\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Blocking Code in Async**: Using synchronous database drivers\n- **No Service Layer**: Business logic in route handlers\n- **Missing Type Hints**: Loses FastAPI''s benefits\n- **Ignoring Sessions**: Not properly managing database sessions\n- **No Testing**: Skipping integration tests\n- **Tight Coupling**: Direct database access in routes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:44:04.567Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for API Development Agents needing production-ready FastAPI project structures with async patterns and dependency injection.","zh":"Perfect for API Development Agents needing production-ready FastAPI project structures with async patterns and dependency injection.","ja":"Perfect for API Development Agents needing production-ready FastAPI project structures with async patterns and dependency injection.","ko":"Perfect for API Development Agents needing production-ready FastAPI project structures with async patterns and dependency injection.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de API que necesitan estructuras de proyectos de FastAPI listas para producción con patrones asíncronos y inyección de dependencias.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement d''API ayant besoin de structures de projets FastAPI prêtes pour la production avec des modèles asynchrones et une injection de dépendances.","de":"Perfekt für API-Entwicklungsagenten, die produktionsreife FastAPI-Projektstrukturen mit asynchronen Mustern und Abhängigkeitsinjektion benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de API que precisam de estruturas de projetos FastAPI prontas para produção com padrões assíncronos e injeção de dependência.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по разработке API, которым необходимы проекты FastAPI, готовые к производству, с асинхронными шаблонами и внедрением зависимостей.","ar":"مثالي لعميلة تطوير واجهة برمجة التطبيقات التي تحتاج إلى هياكل مشروع FastAPI جاهزة للإنتاج مع أنماط غير متزامنة وَحقن الاعتماديات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build high-performance APIs with async REST capabilities, leveraging Python and databases like PostgreSQL and MongoDB, while following best practices for testing and project structure.","zh":"Empowers agents to build high-performance APIs with async REST capabilities, leveraging Python and databases like PostgreSQL and MongoDB, while 