ブなコンポーネントにキーボードナビゲーションを追加する","フォーカス管理とフォーカストラッピングを実装する","適切なラベル付けのあるアクセシブルなフォームを作成する","動きの減少と高コントラストの設定をサポートする"],"ko":["WCAG 2.2 Level AA 또는 AAA 규정 준수를 구현","화면 읽기 소프트웨어가 접근할 수 있는 인터페이스를 구축","대화형 구성 요소에 키보드 탐색을 추가","초점 관리 및 초점 트래핑을 구현","적절한 레이블이 있는 접근 가능한 양식을 생성","움직임 감소 및 고대비 설정을 지원"],"es":["Implementación de la norma WCAG 2.2","Accesibilidad para lectores de pantalla","Navegación por teclado","Gestión de enfoque y trampa de enfoque","Formularios accesibles con etiquetas adecuadas","Compatibilidad con preferencias de movimiento reducido y contraste alto"],"fr":["Implémentation de la norme WCAG 2.2","Accessibilité pour les lecteurs d''écran","Navigation au clavier","Gestion de la mise au point et du piégeage de la mise au point","Formulaires accessibles avec des étiquettes appropriées","Compatibilité avec les préférences de mouvement réduit et de contraste élevé"],"de":["Implementierung der Norm WCAG 2.2","Barrierefreiheit für Bildschirmlesegeräte","Tastaturnavigation","Fokuskontrolle und Fokusfang","Barrierefreie Formulare mit geeigneten Beschriftungen","Kompatibilität mit reduzierter Bewegung und hohem Kontrast"]},"keywords":{"zh":["无障碍合规性","WCAG 2.2","屏幕阅读器","键盘导航","焦点管理","可访问表单","减少运动","高对比度"],"ja":["アクセシビリティコンプライアンス","WCAG 2.2","スクリーンリーダー","キーボードナビゲーション","フォーカス管理","アクセシブルなフォーム","動きの減少","高コントラスト"],"ko":["접근성 규정 준수","WCAG 2.2","화면 읽기 소프트웨어","키보드 탐색","초점 관리","접근 가능한 양식","움직임 감소","고대비"],"es":["accesibilidad web","WCAG 2.2","lectores de pantalla","navegación por teclado","gestión de enfoque","formularios accesibles","compatibilidad con discapacidades","experiencias inclusivas"],"fr":["accessibilité web","WCAG 2.2","lecteurs d''écran","navigation au clavier","gestion de la mise au point","formulaires accessibles","compatibilité avec les handicaps","expériences inclusives"],"de":["Barrierefreiheit im Web","WCAG 2.2","Bildschirmlesegeräte","Tastaturnavigation","Fokuskontrolle","barrierefreie Formulare","Kompatibilität mit Behinderungen","inklusive Erfahrungen"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.522Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"accessibility-compliance","description":"Implement WCAG 2.2 compliant interfaces with mobile accessibility, inclusive design patterns, and assistive technology support. Use when auditing accessibility, implementing ARIA patterns, building for screen readers, or ensuring inclusive user experiences.","bodyPreview":"# Accessibility Compliance\n\nMaster accessibility implementation to create inclusive experiences that work for everyone, including users with disabilities.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Implementing WCAG 2.2 Level AA or AAA compliance\n- Building screen reader accessible interfaces\n- Adding keyboard navigation to interactive components\n- Implementing focus management and focus trapping\n- Creating accessible forms with proper labeling\n- Supporting reduced motion and high contrast preferences\n- Buil","body":"# Accessibility Compliance\n\nMaster accessibility implementation to create inclusive experiences that work for everyone, including users with disabilities.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Implementing WCAG 2.2 Level AA or AAA compliance\n- Building screen reader accessible interfaces\n- Adding keyboard navigation to interactive components\n- Implementing focus management and focus trapping\n- Creating accessible forms with proper labeling\n- Supporting reduced motion and high contrast preferences\n- Building mobile accessibility features (iOS VoiceOver, Android TalkBack)\n- Conducting accessibility audits and fixing violations\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. WCAG 2.2 Guidelines\n\n- Perceivable: Content must be presentable in different ways\n- Operable: Interface must be navigable with keyboard and assistive tech\n- Understandable: Content and operation must be clear\n- Robust: Content must work with current and future assistive technologies\n\n### 2. ARIA Patterns\n\n- Roles: Define element purpose (button, dialog, navigation)\n- States: Indicate current condition (expanded, selected, disabled)\n- Properties: Describe relationships and additional info (labelledby, describedby)\n- Live regions: Announce dynamic content changes\n\n### 3. Keyboard Navigation\n\n- Focus order and tab sequence\n- Focus indicators and visible focus states\n- Keyboard shortcuts and hotkeys\n- Focus trapping for modals and dialogs\n\n### 4. Screen Reader Support\n\n- Semantic HTML structure\n- Alternative text for images\n- Proper heading hierarchy\n- Skip links and landmarks\n\n### 5. Mobile Accessibility\n\n- Touch target sizing (44x44dp minimum)\n- VoiceOver and TalkBack compatibility\n- Gesture alternatives\n- Dynamic Type support\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### WCAG 2.2 Success Criteria Checklist\n\n| Level | Criterion | Description                                          |\n| ----- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| A     | 1.1.1     | Non-text content has text alternatives               |\n| A     | 1.3.1     | Info and relationships programmatically determinable |\n| A     | 2.1.1     | All functionality keyboard accessible                |\n| A     | 2.4.1     | Skip to main content mechanism                       |\n| AA    | 1.4.3     | Contrast ratio 4.5:1 (text), 3:1 (large text)        |\n| AA    | 1.4.11    | Non-text contrast 3:1                                |\n| AA    | 2.4.7     | Focus visible                                        |\n| AA    | 2.5.8     | Target size minimum 24x24px (NEW in 2.2)             |\n| AAA   | 1.4.6     | Enhanced contrast 7:1                                |\n| AAA   | 2.5.5     | Target size minimum 44x44px                          |\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Accessible Button\n\n```tsx\ninterface ButtonProps extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {\n  variant?: \"primary\" | \"secondary\";\n  isLoading?: boolean;\n}\n\nfunction AccessibleButton({\n  children,\n  variant = \"primary\",\n  isLoading = false,\n  disabled,\n  ...props\n}: ButtonProps) {\n  return (\n    <button\n      // Disable when loading\n      disabled={disabled || isLoading}\n      // Announce loading state to screen readers\n      aria-busy={isLoading}\n      // Describe the button''s current state\n      aria-disabled={disabled || isLoading}\n      className={cn(\n        // Visible focus ring\n        \"focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-2\",\n        // Minimum touch target size (44x44px)\n        \"min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]\",\n        variant === \"primary\" && \"bg-primary text-primary-foreground\",\n        (disabled || isLoading) && \"opacity-50 cursor-not-allowed\",\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    >\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <>\n          <span className=\"sr-only\">Loading</span>\n          <Spinner aria-hidden=\"true\" />\n        </>\n      ) : (\n        children\n      )}\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Accessible Modal Dialog\n\n```tsx\nimport * as React from \"react\";\nimport { FocusTrap } from \"@headlessui/react\";\n\ninterface DialogProps {\n  isOpen: boolean;\n  onClose: () => void;\n  title: string;\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}\n\nfunction AccessibleDialog({ isOpen, onClose, title, children }: DialogProps) {\n  const titleId = React.useId();\n  const descriptionId = React.useId();\n\n  // Close on Escape key\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    const handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {\n      if (e.key === \"Escape\" && isOpen) {\n        onClose();\n      }\n    };\n    document.addEventListener(\"keydown\", handleKeyDown);\n    return () => document.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", handleKeyDown);\n  }, [isOpen, onClose]);\n\n  // Prevent body scroll when open\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    if (isOpen) {\n      document.body.style.overflow = \"hidden\";\n    }\n    return () => {\n      document.body.style.overflow = \"\";\n    };\n  }, [isOpen]);\n\n  if (!isOpen) return null;\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      role=\"dialog\"\n      aria-modal=\"true\"\n      aria-labelledby={titleId}\n      aria-describedby={descriptionId}\n    >\n      {/* Backdrop */}\n      <div\n        className=\"fixed inset-0 bg-black/50\"\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\n        onClick={onClose}\n      />\n\n      {/* Focus trap container */}\n      <FocusTrap>\n        <div className=\"fixed inset-0 flex items-center justify-center p-4\">\n          <div className=\"bg-background rounded-lg shadow-lg max-w-md w-full p-6\">\n            <h2 id={titleId} className=\"text-lg font-semibold\">\n              {title}\n            </h2>\n            <div id={descriptionId}>{children}</div>\n            <button\n              onClick={onClose}\n              className=\"absolute top-4 right-4\"\n              aria-label=\"Close dialog\"\n            >\n              <X className=\"h-4 w-4\" />\n            </button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </FocusTrap>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Accessible Form\n\n```tsx\nfunction AccessibleForm() {\n  const [errors, setErrors] = React.useState<Record<string, string>>({});\n\n  return (\n    <form aria-describedby=\"form-errors\" noValidate>\n      {/* Error summary for screen readers */}\n      {Object.keys(errors).length > 0 && (\n        <div\n          id=\"form-errors\"\n          role=\"alert\"\n          aria-live=\"assertive\"\n          className=\"bg-destructive/10 border border-destructive p-4 rounded-md mb-4\"\n        >\n          <h2 className=\"font-semibold text-destructive\">\n            Please fix the following errors:\n          </h2>\n          <ul className=\"list-disc list-inside mt-2\">\n            {Object.entries(errors).map(([field, message]) => (\n              <li key={field}>\n                <a href={`#${field}`} className=\"underline\">\n                  {message}\n                </a>\n              </li>\n            ))}\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Required field with error */}\n      <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n        <label htmlFor=\"email\" className=\"block font-medium\">\n          Email address\n          <span aria-hidden=\"true\" className=\"text-destructive ml-1\">\n            *\n          </span>\n          <span className=\"sr-only\">(required)</span>\n        </label>\n        <input\n          id=\"email\"\n          name=\"email\"\n          type=\"email\"\n          required\n          aria-required=\"true\"\n          aria-invalid={!!errors.email}\n          aria-describedby={errors.email ? \"email-error\" : \"email-hint\"}\n          className={cn(\n            \"w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-md\",\n            errors.email && \"border-destructive\",\n          )}\n        />\n        {errors.email ? (\n          <p id=\"email-error\" className=\"text-sm text-destructive\" role=\"alert\">\n            {errors.email}\n          </p>\n        ) : (\n          <p id=\"email-hint\" className=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n            We''ll never share your email.\n          </p>\n        )}\n      </div>\n\n      <button type=\"submit\" className=\"mt-4\">\n        Submit\n      </button>\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Skip Navigation Link\n\n```tsx\nfunction SkipLink() {\n  return (\n    <a\n      href=\"#main-content\"\n      className={cn(\n        // Hidden by default, visible on focus\n        \"sr-only focus:not-sr-only\",\n        \"focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-50\",\n        \"focus:bg-background focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:rounded-md\",\n        \"focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary\",\n      )}\n    >\n      Skip to main content\n    </a>\n  );\n}\n\n// In layout\nfunction Layout({ children }) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <SkipLink />\n      <header>...</header>\n      <nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\">...</nav>\n      <main id=\"main-content\" tabIndex={-1}>\n        {children}\n      </main>\n      <footer>...</footer>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Live Region for Announcements\n\n```tsx\nfunction useAnnounce() {\n  const [message, setMessage] = React.useState(\"\");\n\n  const announce = React.useCallback(\n    (text: string, priority: \"polite\" | \"assertive\" = \"polite\") => {\n      setMessage(\"\"); // Clear first to ensure re-announcement\n      setTimeout(() => setMessage(text), 100);\n    },\n    [],\n  );\n\n  const Announcer = () => (\n    <div\n      role=\"status\"\n      aria-live=\"polite\"\n      aria-atomic=\"true\"\n      className=\"sr-only\"\n    >\n      {message}\n    </div>\n  );\n\n  return { announce, Announcer };\n}\n\n// Usage\nfunction SearchResults({ results, isLoading }) {\n  const { announce, Announcer } = useAnnounce();\n\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    if (!isLoading && results) {\n      announce(`${results.length} results found`);\n    }\n  }, [results, isLoading, announce]);\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <Announcer />\n      <ul>{/* results */}</ul>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Color Contrast Requirements\n\n```typescript\n// Contrast ratio utilities\nfunction getContrastRatio(foreground: string, background: string): number {\n  const fgLuminance = getLuminance(foreground);\n  const bgLuminance = getLuminance(background);\n  const lighter = Math.max(fgLuminance, bgLuminance);\n  const darker = Math.min(fgLuminance, bgLuminance);\n  return (lighter + 0.05) / (darker + 0.05);\n}\n\n// WCAG requirements\nconst CONTRAST_REQUIREMENTS = {\n  // Normal text (<18pt or <14pt bold)\n  normalText: {\n    AA: 4.5,\n    AAA: 7,\n  },\n  // Large text (>=18pt or >=14pt bold)\n  largeText: {\n    AA: 3,\n    AAA: 4.5,\n  },\n  // UI components and graphics\n  uiComponents: {\n    AA: 3,\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use Semantic HTML**: Prefer native elements over ARIA when possible\n2. **Test with Real Users**: Include people with disabilities in user testing\n3. **Keyboard First**: Design interactions to work without a mouse\n4. **Don''t Disable Focus Styles**: Style them, don''t remove them\n5. **Provide Text Alternatives**: All non-text content needs descriptions\n6. **Support Zoom**: Content should work at 200% zoom\n7. **Announce Changes**: Use live regions for dynamic content\n8. **Respect Preferences**: Honor prefers-reduced-motion and prefers-contrast\n\n## Common Issues\n\n- **Missing alt text**: Images without descriptions\n- **Poor color contrast**: Text hard to read against background\n- **Keyboard traps**: Focus stuck in component\n- **Missing labels**: Form inputs without associated labels\n- **Auto-playing media**: Content that plays without user initiation\n- **Inaccessible custom controls**: Recreating native functionality poorly\n- **Missing skip links**: No way to bypass repetitive content\n- **Focus order issues**: Tab order doesn''t match visual order\n\n## Testing Tools\n\n- **Automated**: axe DevTools, WAVE, Lighthouse\n- **Manual**: VoiceOver (macOS/iOS), NVDA/JAWS (Windows), TalkBack (Android)\n- **Simulators**: NoCoffee (vision), Silktide (various disabilities)\n\n## Resources\n\n- [WCAG 2.2 Guidelines](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/)\n- [WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/)\n- [A11y Project Checklist](https://www.a11yproject.com/checklist/)\n- [Inclusive Components](https://inclusive-components.design/)\n- [Deque University](https://dequeuniversity.com/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:45:57.287Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents focused on creating inclusive web experiences, particularly those implementing WCAG 2.2 Level AA or AAA compliance.","zh":"适合专注于创建包容性网页体验的前端代理，特别是那些实施WCAG 2.2级别AA或AAA兼容性的代理。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントが、特にWCAG 2.2レベルAAまたはAAAのコンプライアンスを実装することに重点を置いた包括的なWebエクスペリエンスを作成するのに適しています。","ko":"프론트엔드 에이전트가 포괄적인 웹 경험을 생성하는 데 중점을 두고 특히 WCAG 2.2 레벨 AA 또는 AAA 컴플라이언스를 구현하는 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes frontend centrados en la creación de experiencias web inclusivas, particularmente aquellos que implementan la norma WCAG 2.2 Nivel AA o AAA.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents frontend axés sur la création d''expériences Web inclusives, en particulier ceux qui mettent en œuvre la norme WCAG 2.2 Niveau AA ou AAA.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agents, die sich auf die Erstellung von inklusiven Web-Erlebnissen konzentrieren, insbesondere solche, die die WCAG 2.2-Stufe AA oder AAA einhalten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Frontend que se concentram na criação de experiências web inclusivas, particularmente aqueles que implementam a conformidade com o nível AA ou AAA da WCAG 2.2.","ru":"Идеально для агентов фронтенда, ориентированных на создание инклюзивных веб-опытов, особенно тех, кто реализует соответствие уровню AA или AAA WCAG 2.2.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأماميين الذين يركزون على 创建 تجارب ويب شاملة، ولا سيما أولئك الذين ينفذون متطلبات التوافق مع مستوى AA أو AAA من إرشادات الويب المحسنة 2.2."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement screen reader accessible interfaces, add keyboard navigation, and manage focus trapping, while supporting reduced motion and high contrast preferences through proper labeling and accessibility features, leveraging standards like WCAG 2.2.","zh":"赋予代理实现屏幕阅读器可访问的接口、添加键盘导航和管理焦点捕获的能力，同时支持通过适当的标签和无障碍功能来减少动作和高对比度偏好，利用诸如WCAG 2.2的标准。","ja":"エージェントがスクリーンリーダーにアクセス可能なインターフェイスを実装したり、キーボードナビゲーションを追加したり、フォーカストラッピングを管理したりして、WCAG 2.2などの規格を利用して、適切なラベル付けとアクセシビリティ機能を通じて減少した動きと高コントラストの好みをサポートする能力を与えます。","ko":"에이전트가 화면 리더기에서 접근할 수 있는 인터페이스를 구현하거나 키보드 탐색을 추가하거나 포커스 트래핑을 관리하는 기능을 부여하고 적절한 레이블 지정 및 접근성 기능을 통해 줄어든 동작 및 고대비 선호도를 지원하는 동시에 WCAG 2.2와 같은 표준을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar interfaces accesibles para lectores de pantalla, agregar navegación por teclado y gestionar la trampa de enfoque, mientras apoyan preferencias de movimiento reducido y contraste alto a través de la etiquetado y características de accesibilidad adecuados, aprovechando estándares como WCAG 2.2.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des interfaces accessibles aux lecteurs d''écran, d''ajouter une navigation au clavier et de gérer le piégeage de focus, tout en soutenant les préférences de mouvement réduit et de contraste élevé grâce à un étiquetage et à des fonctionnalités d''accessibilité appropriés, en exploitant des normes comme WCAG 2.2.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Screen-Reader-Interfaces zu implementieren, Tastaturnavigation hinzuzufügen und Fokusfallen zu verwalten, während sie Präferenzen für reduzierte Bewegung und hohen Kontrast durch ordnungsgemäßes Labeling und Accessibility-Features unterstützen, indem sie Standards wie WCAG 2.2 nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar interfaces acessíveis ao leitor de tela, adicionar navegação por teclado e gerenciar armadilhas de foco, enquanto suporta preferências de movimento reduzido e alto contraste por meio de etiquetas e recursos de acessibilidade adequados, aproveitando padrões como a WCAG 2.2.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать интерфейсы, доступные для программ чтения с экрана, добавить навигацию с помощью клавиатуры и управлять фокусировкой, поддерживая при этом предпочтения снижения движения и высокого контраста посредством надлежащего маркирования и функций доступности, опираясь на стандарты типа WCAG 2.2.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنفيذ واجهات مستخدم قابلة للوصول إلى قارئ الشاشة، وإضافة التنقل باللوحة المفاتيحية، وإدارة فخاخ التركيز، مع دعم تفضيلات الحركة المنخفضة والتوتر العالي من خلال التسميات والميزات الإضافية لسهولة الوصول، واستخدام معايير مثل إرشادات الويب المحسنة 2.2."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing WCAG 2.2 Level AA or AAA compliance for web applications","Building screen reader accessible interfaces for interactive components","Adding keyboard navigation to enhance user experience","Creating accessible forms with proper labeling for improved usability"],"zh":["为Web应用程序实施WCAG 2.2级别AA或AAA兼容性","为交互式组件构建屏幕阅读器可访问的接口","添加键盘导航以增强用户体验","创建具有适当标签的可访问表单以提高可用性"],"ja":["WebアプリケーションにWCAG 2.2レベルAAまたはAAAのコンプライアンスを実装する","インタラクティブコンポーネントのためのスクリーンリーダーにアクセス可能なインターフェイスを構築する","キーボードナビゲーションを追加してユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させる","適切なラベル付けのあるアクセシブルフォームを作成して利便性を向上させる"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션에 WCAG 2.2 레벨 AA 또는 AAA 컴플라이언스를 구현하는 것","인터랙티브 컴포넌트를 위한 화면 리더기에서 접근할 수 있는 인터페이스를 구축하는 것","키보드 탐색을 추가하여 사용자 경험을 향상시키는 것","적절한 레이블 지정이 있는 접근 가능한 폼을 생성하여 사용성을 향상시키는 것"],"es":["Implementar la norma WCAG 2.2 Nivel AA o AAA para aplicaciones web","Crear interfaces accesibles para lectores de pantalla para componentes interactivos","Agregar navegación por teclado para mejorar la experiencia del usuario","Crear formularios accesibles con etiquetado adecuado para una mejor usabilidad"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre la norme WCAG 2.2 Niveau AA ou AAA pour les applications Web","Créer des interfaces accessibles aux lecteurs d''écran pour les composants interactifs","Ajouter une navigation au clavier pour améliorer l''expérience utilisateur","Créer des formulaires accessibles avec un étiquetage approprié pour une meilleure utilisabilité"],"de":["WCAG 2.2-Stufe AA oder AAA für Webanwendungen implementieren","Screen-Reader-Interfaces für interaktive Komponenten erstellen","Tastaturnavigation hinzufügen, um die Benutzererfahrung zu verbessern","Zugängliche Formulare mit ordnungsgemäßem Labeling für eine bessere Benutzbarkeit erstellen"],"pt":["Implementação da conformidade com o nível AA ou AAA da WCAG 2.2 para aplicações web","Criação de interfaces acessíveis ao leitor de tela para componentes interativos","Adição de navegação por teclado para melhorar a experiência do usuário","Criação de formulários acessíveis com etiquetas adequadas para melhorar a usabilidade"],"ru":["Реализация соответствия уровню AA или AAA WCAG 2.2 для веб-приложений","Создание интерфейсов, доступных для программ чтения с экрана, для интерактивных компонентов","Добавление навигации с помощью клавиатуры для улучшения пользовательского опыта","Создание доступных форм с надлежащим маркированием для улучшения удобства использования"],"ar":["تنفيذ متطلبات التوافق مع مستوى AA أو AAA من إرشادات الويب المحسنة 2.2 لتطبيقات الويب","إنشاء واجهات مستخدم قابلة للوصول إلى قارئ الشاشة لمكونات تفاعلية","إضافة التنقل باللوحة المفاتيحية لتحسين تجربة المستخدم","إنشاء استمارات قابلة للوصول مع تسميات مناسبة لتحسين سهولة الاستخدام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of accessibility guidelines and standards like WCAG 2.2","May need additional testing for screen reader compatibility","Dependent on the agent''s ability to parse and apply accessibility features in code"],"zh":["需要了解无障碍指南和标准，如WCAG 2.2","可能需要额外的测试以确保屏幕阅读器兼容性","依赖于代理在代码中解析和应用无障碍功能的能力"],"ja":["WCAG 2.2などのアクセシビリティガイドラインや規格の知識が必要","スクリーンリーダーの互換性を確保するために追加のテストが必要になる可能性がある","コードでアクセシビリティ機能を解析して適用するエージェントの能力に依存する"],"ko":["WCAG 2.2와 같은 접근성 지침 및 표준에 대한 지식이 필요함","화면 리더기 호환성을 보장하기 위해 추가 테스트가 필요할 수 있음","코드에서 접근성 기능을 파싱하고 적용하는 에이전트의 능력에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de las directrices y normas de accesibilidad como WCAG 2.2","Puede necesitar pruebas adicionales para la compatibilidad con el lector de pantalla","Depende de la capacidad del agente para analizar y aplicar características de accesibilidad en el código"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des lignes directrices et des normes d''accessibilité comme WCAG 2.2","Peut nécessiter des tests supplémentaires pour la compatibilité avec le lecteur d''écran","Dépend de la capacité de l''agent à analyser et à appliquer les fonctionnalités d''accessibilité dans le code"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Richtlinien und Standards für Accessibility wie WCAG 2.2","Benötigt möglicherweise zusätzliche Tests für die Kompatibilität mit Screenreadern","Hängt von der Fähigkeit des Agents ab, Accessibility-Features im Code zu analysieren und anzuwenden"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento das diretrizes e normas de acessibilidade, como a WCAG 2.2","Pode precisar de testes adicionais para garantir a compatibilidade com leitores de tela","Depende da capacidade do agente de analisar e aplicar recursos de acessibilidade no código"],"ru":["Требует знания руководств и стандартов доступности, таких как WCAG 2.2","Может потребовать дополнительного тестирования для обеспечения совместимости с программами чтения с экрана","Зависит от способности агента парсить и применять функции доступности в коде"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة الإرشادات والمعايير لسهولة الوصول، مثل إرشادات الويب المحسنة 2.2","يمكن أن يتطلب اختبارات إضافية لضمان التوافق مع برامج قراءة الشاشة","يعتمد على قدرة الوكيل على تحليل وتطبيق الميزات الإضافية لسهولة الوصول في الكود"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
