 моделей ценообразования"],"ar":["تحليل المنافسين","تحديد أسعار مخصصة","تحسين الإيرادات","مواءمة الأسعار مع استعداد الزبون لدفع الثمن","إنشاء نماذج تسعير قابلة للتحجيم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SaaS 定价","价格战略","客户支付意愿","竞争对手分析","价格优化","收入增长"],"ja":["SaaS の価格","価格戦略","顧客の支払い意欲","競合分析","価格最適化","収益増加"],"ko":["SaaS 가격","가격 전략","고객 지불 의견","경쟁사 분석","가격 최적화","수익 증가"],"es":["estrategia de precios SaaS","monetización SaaS","diseño de precios","valor único","voluntad de pago","optimización de precios"],"fr":["stratégie de tarification SaaS","monétisation SaaS","conception de prix","valeur unique","volonté de payer","optimisation des prix"],"de":["Preisstrategie SaaS","Monetisierung SaaS","Preisgestaltung","einzigartiger Wert","Zahlungsbereitschaft","Preisoptimierung"],"pt":["estratégia de preços SaaS","otimização de receita","preços personalizados","análise de concorrentes","alinhamento com a disposição do cliente em pagar","desenvolvimento de modelos de preços escaláveis"],"ru":["стратегия ценообразования SaaS","оптимизация дохода","индивидуальные цены","анализ конкурентов","согласование с готовностью клиента платить","разработка масштабируемых моделей ценообразования"],"ar":["استراتيجية التسعير السحابي","تحسين الإيرادات","أسعار مخصصة","تحليل المنافسين","مواءمة الأسعار مع استعداد الزبون لدفع الثمن","إنشاء نماذج تسعير قابلة للتحجيم"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pricing-strategy","description":"When the user wants help with pricing decisions, packaging, or monetization strategy. Also use when the user mentions pricing, pricing tiers, freemium, free trial, packaging, price increase, value metric, Van Westendorp, willingness to pay, or monetization. This skill covers pricing research, tier structure, and packaging strategy.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Pricing Strategy\n\nYou are an expert in SaaS pricing and monetization strategy. Your goal is to help design pricing that captures value, drives growth, and aligns with customer willingness to pay.\n\n## Before Starting\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Busines","body":"# Pricing Strategy\n\nYou are an expert in SaaS pricing and monetization strategy. Your goal is to help design pricing that captures value, drives growth, and aligns with customer willingness to pay.\n\n## Before Starting\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Business Context\n- What type of product? (SaaS, marketplace, e-commerce, service)\n- What''s your current pricing (if any)?\n- What''s your target market? (SMB, mid-market, enterprise)\n- What''s your go-to-market motion? (self-serve, sales-led, hybrid)\n\n### 2. Value & Competition\n- What''s the primary value you deliver?\n- What alternatives do customers consider?\n- How do competitors price?\n\n### 3. Current Performance\n- What''s your current conversion rate?\n- What''s your ARPU and churn rate?\n- Any feedback on pricing from customers/prospects?\n\n### 4. Goals\n- Optimizing for growth, revenue, or profitability?\n- Moving upmarket or expanding downmarket?\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Fundamentals\n\n### The Three Pricing Axes\n\n**1. Packaging** — What''s included at each tier?\n- Features, limits, support level\n- How tiers differ from each other\n\n**2. Pricing Metric** — What do you charge for?\n- Per user, per usage, flat fee\n- How price scales with value\n\n**3. Price Point** — How much do you charge?\n- The actual dollar amounts\n- Perceived value vs. cost\n\n### Value-Based Pricing\n\nPrice should be based on value delivered, not cost to serve:\n\n- **Customer''s perceived value** — The ceiling\n- **Your price** — Between alternatives and perceived value\n- **Next best alternative** — The floor for differentiation\n- **Your cost to serve** — Only a baseline, not the basis\n\n**Key insight:** Price between the next best alternative and perceived value.\n\n---\n\n## Value Metrics\n\n### What is a Value Metric?\n\nThe value metric is what you charge for—it should scale with the value customers receive.\n\n**Good value metrics:**\n- Align price with value delivered\n- Are easy to understand\n- Scale as customer grows\n- Are hard to game\n\n### Common Value Metrics\n\n| Metric | Best For | Example |\n|--------|----------|---------|\n| Per user/seat | Collaboration tools | Slack, Notion |\n| Per usage | Variable consumption | AWS, Twilio |\n| Per feature | Modular products | HubSpot add-ons |\n| Per contact/record | CRM, email tools | Mailchimp |\n| Per transaction | Payments, marketplaces | Stripe |\n| Flat fee | Simple products | Basecamp |\n\n### Choosing Your Value Metric\n\nAsk: \"As a customer uses more of [metric], do they get more value?\"\n- If yes → good value metric\n- If no → price doesn''t align with value\n\n---\n\n## Tier Structure Overview\n\n### Good-Better-Best Framework\n\n**Good tier (Entry):** Core features, limited usage, low price\n**Better tier (Recommended):** Full features, reasonable limits, anchor price\n**Best tier (Premium):** Everything, advanced features, 2-3x Better price\n\n### Tier Differentiation\n\n- **Feature gating** — Basic vs. advanced features\n- **Usage limits** — Same features, different limits\n- **Support level** — Email → Priority → Dedicated\n- **Access** — API, SSO, custom branding\n\n**For detailed tier structures and persona-based packaging**: See [references/tier-structure.md](references/tier-structure.md)\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Research\n\n### Van Westendorp Method\n\nFour questions that identify acceptable price range:\n1. Too expensive (wouldn''t consider)\n2. Too cheap (question quality)\n3. Expensive but might consider\n4. A bargain\n\nAnalyze intersections to find optimal pricing zone.\n\n### MaxDiff Analysis\n\nIdentifies which features customers value most:\n- Show sets of features\n- Ask: Most important? Least important?\n- Results inform tier packaging\n\n**For detailed research methods**: See [references/research-methods.md](references/research-methods.md)\n\n---\n\n## When to Raise Prices\n\n### Signs It''s Time\n\n**Market signals:**\n- Competitors have raised prices\n- Prospects don''t flinch at price\n- \"It''s so cheap!\" feedback\n\n**Business signals:**\n- Very high conversion rates (>40%)\n- Very low churn (<3% monthly)\n- Strong unit economics\n\n**Product signals:**\n- Significant value added since last pricing\n- Product more mature/stable\n\n### Price Increase Strategies\n\n1. **Grandfather existing** — New price for new customers only\n2. **Delayed increase** — Announce 3-6 months out\n3. **Tied to value** — Raise price but add features\n4. **Plan restructure** — Change plans entirely\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Page Best Practices\n\n### Above the Fold\n- Clear tier comparison table\n- Recommended tier highlighted\n- Monthly/annual toggle\n- Primary CTA for each tier\n\n### Common Elements\n- Feature comparison table\n- Who each tier is for\n- FAQ section\n- Annual discount callout (17-20%)\n- Money-back guarantee\n- Customer logos/trust signals\n\n### Pricing Psychology\n- **Anchoring:** Show higher-priced option first\n- **Decoy effect:** Middle tier should be best value\n- **Charm pricing:** $49 vs. $50 (for value-focused)\n- **Round pricing:** $50 vs. $49 (for premium)\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Checklist\n\n### Before Setting Prices\n- [ ] Defined target customer personas\n- [ ] Researched competitor pricing\n- [ ] Identified your value metric\n- [ ] Conducted willingness-to-pay research\n- [ ] Mapped features to tiers\n\n### Pricing Structure\n- [ ] Chosen number of tiers\n- [ ] Differentiated tiers clearly\n- [ ] Set price points based on research\n- [ ] Created annual discount strategy\n- [ ] Planned enterprise/custom tier\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What pricing research have you done?\n2. What''s your current ARPU and conversion rate?\n3. What''s your primary value metric?\n4. Who are your main pricing personas?\n5. Are you self-serve, sales-led, or hybrid?\n6. What pricing changes are you considering?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **page-cro**: For optimizing pricing page conversion\n- **copywriting**: For pricing page copy\n- **marketing-psychology**: For pricing psychology principles\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing pricing changes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:47:38.132Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for SaaS-focused AI Agents needing advanced pricing strategy and monetization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级定价策略和盈利能力的SaaS专注AI代理。","ja":"SaaSに焦点を当てた高度な価格戦略と収益化機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 가격 전략 및 수익화 기능이 필요한 SaaS 중심 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA centrados en SaaS que necesitan una estrategia de precios avanzada y capacidades de monetización.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA axés sur le SaaS ayant besoin d''une stratégie de tarification avancée et de capacités de monétisation.","de":"Perfekt für SaaS-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine fortschrittliche Preisstrategie und Monetisierungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA focados em SaaS que necessitam de estratégia de preços avançada e capacidades de monetização.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на SaaS, которые нуждаются в продвинутой стратегии ценообразования и возможностях монетизации.","ar":"مثالي لوفاء إيه إيه التي تركز على ساس وتحتاج إلى استراتيجية تسعير متقدمة وقدرات توليد إيرادات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design pricing that captures value, drives growth, and aligns with customer willingness to pay, utilizing product marketing context and SaaS pricing expertise, potentially integrating with file formats like `.md` for context gathering.","zh":"赋予代理设计能够捕获价值、驱动增长并与客户愿意支付的价格相符的定价，利用产品营销背景和SaaS定价专业知识，可能集成文件格式如`.md`进行背景收集。","ja":"エージェントは、製品マーケティングの背景とSaaSの価格設定の専門知識を利用して、価値を捉え、成長を促進し、顧客が支払う意欲と一致する価格を設計できるようになります。`.md`のようなファイル形式の統合も可能です。","ko":"에이전트는 제품 마케팅 환경 및 SaaS 가격 설정 전문 지식을 사용하여 가치를 포착하고 성장률을 높이고 고객이 지불할 의향과 일치하는 가격을 설계할 수 있습니다. `.md`와 같은 파일 형식의 통합도 가능합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar precios que capturan valor, impulsan el crecimiento y se alinean con la voluntad del cliente de pagar, utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos y la experiencia en precios de SaaS, potencialmente integrándose con formatos de archivo como `.md` para la recopilación de contexto.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des tarifs qui capturent la valeur, stimulent la croissance et s''alignent sur la volonté du client de payer, en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits et l''expertise en tarification SaaS, potentiellement en intégrant des formats de fichiers comme `.md` pour la collecte de contexte.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Preise zu entwerfen, die Wert erfassen, Wachstum vorantreiben und mit der Zahlungsbereitschaft des Kunden übereinstimmen, unter Verwendung des Produktmarketing-Kontexts und der SaaS-Preis-Expertise, potenziell integriert mit Dateiformaten wie `.md` für die Kontexterfassung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar preços que capturam valor, impulsionam o crescimento e alinham-se com a disposição do cliente em pagar, utilizando o contexto de marketing de produtos e a especialização em preços de SaaS, potencialmente integrando-se com formatos de arquivo como `.md` para coleta de contexto.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать ценообразование, которое захватывает стоимость, стимулирует рост и соответствует готовности клиента платить, используя контекст маркетинга продукта и экспертизу в области ценообразования SaaS, потенциально интегрируясь с форматами файлов, такими как `.md`, для сбора контекста.","ar":"تمكّن الوكالات من تصميم التسعير الذي يلتقط القيمة ويدفع النمو ويتوافق مع استعداد العميل لدفع الثمن، مستخدمًا سياق تسويق المنتج وخبرة تسعير ساس، ودمجها بشكل محتمل مع تنسيقات الملفات مثل `.md` لجمع السياق."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing customer willingness to pay for SaaS products","Designing pricing strategies that drive business growth","Aligning pricing with product marketing context for optimal monetization"],"zh":["分析SaaS产品的客户愿意支付的价格","设计能够驱动业务增长的定价策略","将定价与产品营销背景对齐以实现最佳的盈利"],"ja":["SaaS製品の顧客が支払う意欲を分析する","ビジネスの成長を促進する価格戦略を設計する","価格を製品マーケティングの背景と一致させて、最適な収益化を実現する"],"ko":["SaaS 제품의 고객이 지불할 의향을 분석한다","사업의 성장률을 높이는 가격 전략을 설계한다","가격을 제품 마케팅 환경과 일치시켜 최적의 수익화를 달성한다"],"es":["Análisis de la voluntad del cliente de pagar por productos SaaS","Diseño de estrategias de precios que impulsan el crecimiento empresarial","Alineación de precios con el contexto de marketing de productos para una monetización óptima"],"fr":["Analyse de la volonté du client de payer pour les produits SaaS","Conception de stratégies de tarification qui stimulent la croissance commerciale","Alignement des tarifs sur le contexte de marketing de produits pour une monétisation optimale"],"de":["Analyse der Zahlungsbereitschaft des Kunden für SaaS-Produkte","Entwurf von Preisstrategien, die Geschäftswachstum vorantreiben","Ausrichtung der Preise mit dem Produktmarketing-Kontext für eine optimale Monetisierung"],"pt":["Analisar a disposição do cliente em pagar por produtos SaaS","Projetar estratégias de preços que impulsionam o crescimento empresarial","Alinhar os preços com o contexto de marketing de produtos para monetização ótima"],"ru":["Анализ готовности клиента платить за продукты SaaS","Проектирование стратегий ценообразования, которые стимулируют бизнес-рост","Совмещение цен с контекстом маркетинга продукта для оптимальной монетизации"],"ar":["تحليل استعداد العميل لدفع ثمن منتجات ساس","تصم