pération d''événements","schémas de magasin d''événements"],"de":["Ereignisspeicher-Design","Anwendungen mit Ereignisquelle","Ereignis-Infrastruktur","benutzerdefinierter Ereignisspeicher","Ereignisspeicher-Technologien","Skalierbarkeit des Ereignisspeichers","Optimierung des Speicher- und Abrufverhaltens von Ereignissen","Ereignisrückgewinnung","Ereignisspeicher-Schemata"],"pt":["projeto de loja de eventos","aplicações orientadas a eventos","armazenamento de eventos","recuperação de eventos","tecnologias de loja de eventos","otimização de loja de eventos"],"ru":["проектирование хранилища событий","событийно-ориентированные приложения","хранение событий","извлечение событий","технологии хранилища событий","оптимизация хранилища событий"],"ar":["تصميم مخزن للأحداث","تطبيقات مصدر الأحداث","تخزين الأحداث","استرجاع الأحداث","تكنولوجيا مخزن للأحداث","تحسين مخزن للأحداث"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"event-store-design","description":"Design and implement event stores for event-sourced systems. Use when building event sourcing infrastructure, choosing event store technologies, or implementing event persistence patterns.","bodyPreview":"# Event Store Design\n\nComprehensive guide to designing event stores for event-sourced applications.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing event sourcing infrastructure\n- Choosing between event store technologies\n- Implementing custom event stores\n- Optimizing event storage and retrieval\n- Setting up event store schemas\n- Planning for event store scaling\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Event Store Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    Event Sto","body":"# Event Store Design\n\nComprehensive guide to designing event stores for event-sourced applications.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing event sourcing infrastructure\n- Choosing between event store technologies\n- Implementing custom event stores\n- Optimizing event storage and retrieval\n- Setting up event store schemas\n- Planning for event store scaling\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Event Store Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    Event Store                       │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐ │\n│  │   Stream 1   │  │   Stream 2   │  │   Stream 3   │ │\n│  │ (Aggregate)  │  │ (Aggregate)  │  │ (Aggregate)  │ │\n│  ├─────────────┤  ├─────────────┤  ├─────────────┤ │\n│  │ Event 1     │  │ Event 1     │  │ Event 1     │ │\n│  │ Event 2     │  │ Event 2     │  │ Event 2     │ │\n│  │ Event 3     │  │ ...         │  │ Event 3     │ │\n│  │ ...         │  │             │  │ Event 4     │ │\n│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘ │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Global Position: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5 → 6 → ...     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 2. Event Store Requirements\n\n| Requirement       | Description                        |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| **Append-only**   | Events are immutable, only appends |\n| **Ordered**       | Per-stream and global ordering     |\n| **Versioned**     | Optimistic concurrency control     |\n| **Subscriptions** | Real-time event notifications      |\n| **Idempotent**    | Handle duplicate writes safely     |\n\n## Technology Comparison\n\n| Technology       | Best For                  | Limitations                      |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| **EventStoreDB** | Pure event sourcing       | Single-purpose                   |\n| **PostgreSQL**   | Existing Postgres stack   | Manual implementation            |\n| **Kafka**        | High-throughput streaming | Not ideal for per-stream queries |\n| **DynamoDB**     | Serverless, AWS-native    | Query limitations                |\n| **Marten**       | .NET ecosystems           | .NET specific                    |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: PostgreSQL Event Store Schema\n\n```sql\n-- Events table\nCREATE TABLE events (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    stream_id VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    stream_type VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    event_type VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    event_data JSONB NOT NULL,\n    metadata JSONB DEFAULT ''{}'',\n    version BIGINT NOT NULL,\n    global_position BIGSERIAL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),\n\n    CONSTRAINT unique_stream_version UNIQUE (stream_id, version)\n);\n\n-- Index for stream queries\nCREATE INDEX idx_events_stream_id ON events(stream_id, version);\n\n-- Index for global subscription\nCREATE INDEX idx_events_global_position ON events(global_position);\n\n-- Index for event type queries\nCREATE INDEX idx_events_event_type ON events(event_type);\n\n-- Index for time-based queries\nCREATE INDEX idx_events_created_at ON events(created_at);\n\n-- Snapshots table\nCREATE TABLE snapshots (\n    stream_id VARCHAR(255) PRIMARY KEY,\n    stream_type VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    snapshot_data JSONB NOT NULL,\n    version BIGINT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- Subscriptions checkpoint table\nCREATE TABLE subscription_checkpoints (\n    subscription_id VARCHAR(255) PRIMARY KEY,\n    last_position BIGINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n```\n\n### Template 2: Python Event Store Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Any, Optional, List\nfrom uuid import UUID, uuid4\nimport json\nimport asyncpg\n\n@dataclass\nclass Event:\n    stream_id: str\n    event_type: str\n    data: dict\n    metadata: dict = field(default_factory=dict)\n    event_id: UUID = field(default_factory=uuid4)\n    version: Optional[int] = None\n    global_position: Optional[int] = None\n    created_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)\n\n\nclass EventStore:\n    def __init__(self, pool: asyncpg.Pool):\n        self.pool = pool\n\n    async def append_events(\n        self,\n        stream_id: str,\n        stream_type: str,\n        events: List[Event],\n        expected_version: Optional[int] = None\n    ) -> List[Event]:\n        \"\"\"Append events to a stream with optimistic concurrency.\"\"\"\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            async with conn.transaction():\n                # Check expected version\n                if expected_version is not None:\n                    current = await conn.fetchval(\n                        \"SELECT MAX(version) FROM events WHERE stream_id = $1\",\n                        stream_id\n                    )\n                    current = current or 0\n                    if current != expected_version:\n                        raise ConcurrencyError(\n                            f\"Expected version {expected_version}, got {current}\"\n                        )\n\n                # Get starting version\n                start_version = await conn.fetchval(\n                    \"SELECT COALESCE(MAX(version), 0) + 1 FROM events WHERE stream_id = $1\",\n                    stream_id\n                )\n\n                # Insert events\n                saved_events = []\n                for i, event in enumerate(events):\n                    event.version = start_version + i\n                    row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                        \"\"\"\n                        INSERT INTO events (id, stream_id, stream_type, event_type,\n                                          event_data, metadata, version, created_at)\n                        VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, $6, $7, $8)\n                        RETURNING global_position\n                        \"\"\",\n                        event.event_id,\n                        stream_id,\n                        stream_type,\n                        event.event_type,\n                        json.dumps(event.data),\n                        json.dumps(event.metadata),\n                        event.version,\n                        event.created_at\n                    )\n                    event.global_position = row[''global_position'']\n                    saved_events.append(event)\n\n                return saved_events\n\n    async def read_stream(\n        self,\n        stream_id: str,\n        from_version: int = 0,\n        limit: int = 1000\n    ) -> List[Event]:\n        \"\"\"Read events from a stream.\"\"\"\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            rows = await conn.fetch(\n                \"\"\"\n                SELECT id, stream_id, event_type, event_data, metadata,\n                       version, global_position, created_at\n                FROM events\n                WHERE stream_id = $1 AND version >= $2\n                ORDER BY version\n                LIMIT $3\n                \"\"\",\n                stream_id, from_version, limit\n            )\n            return [self._row_to_event(row) for row in rows]\n\n    async def read_all(\n        self,\n        from_position: int = 0,\n        limit: int = 1000\n    ) -> List[Event]:\n        \"\"\"Read all events globally.\"\"\"\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            rows = await conn.fetch(\n                \"\"\"\n                SELECT id, stream_id, event_type, event_data, metadata,\n                       version, global_position, created_at\n                FROM events\n                WHERE global_position > $1\n                ORDER BY global_position\n                LIMIT $2\n                \"\"\",\n                from_position, limit\n            )\n            return [self._row_to_event(row) for row in rows]\n\n    async def subscribe(\n        self,\n        subscription_id: str,\n        handler,\n        from_position: int = 0,\n        batch_size: int = 100\n    ):\n        \"\"\"Subscribe to all events from a position.\"\"\"\n        # Get checkpoint\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            checkpoint = await conn.fetchval(\n                \"\"\"\n                SELECT last_position FROM subscription_checkpoints\n                WHERE subscription_id = $1\n                \"\"\",\n                subscription_id\n            )\n            position = checkpoint or from_position\n\n        while True:\n            events = await self.read_all(position, batch_size)\n            if not events:\n                await asyncio.sleep(1)  # Poll interval\n                continue\n\n            for event in events:\n                await handler(event)\n                position = event.global_position\n\n            # Save checkpoint\n            async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n                await conn.execute(\n                    \"\"\"\n                    INSERT INTO subscription_checkpoints (subscription_id, last_position)\n                    VALUES ($1, $2)\n                    ON CONFLICT (subscription_id)\n                    DO UPDATE SET last_position = $2, updated_at = NOW()\n                    \"\"\",\n                    subscription_id, position\n                )\n\n    def _row_to_event(self, row) -> Event:\n        return Event(\n            event_id=row[''id''],\n            stream_id=row[''stream_id''],\n            event_type=row[''event_type''],\n            data=json.loads(row[''event_data'']),\n            metadata=json.loads(row[''metadata'']),\n            version=row[''version''],\n            global_position=row[''global_position''],\n            created_at=row[''created_at'']\n        )\n\n\nclass ConcurrencyError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when optimistic concurrency check fails.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n### Template 3: EventStoreDB Usage\n\n```python\nfrom esdbclient import EventStoreDBClient, NewEvent, StreamState\nimport json\n\n# Connect\nclient = EventStoreDBClient(uri=\"esdb://localhost:2113?tls=false\")\n\n# Append events\ndef append_events(stream_name: str, events: list, expected_revision=None):\n    new_events = [\n        NewEvent(\n            type=event[''type''],\n            data=json.dumps(event[''data'']).encode(),\n            metadata=json.dumps(event.get(''metadata'', {})).encode()\n        )\n        for event in events\n    ]\n\n    if expected_revision is None:\n        state = StreamState.ANY\n    elif expected_revision == -1:\n        state = StreamState.NO_STREAM\n    else:\n        state = expected_revision\n\n    return client.append_to_stream(\n        stream_name=stream_name,\n        events=new_events,\n        current_version=state\n    )\n\n# Read stream\ndef read_stream(stream_name: str, from_revision: int = 0):\n    events = client.get_stream(\n        stream_name=stream_name,\n        stream_position=from_revision\n    )\n    return [\n        {\n            ''type'': event.type,\n            ''data'': json.loads(event.data),\n            ''metadata'': json.loads(event.metadata) if event.metadata else {},\n            ''stream_position'': event.stream_position,\n            ''commit_position'': event.commit_position\n        }\n        for event in events\n    ]\n\n# Subscribe to all\nasync def subscribe_to_all(handler, from_position: int = 0):\n    subscription = client.subscribe_to_all(commit_position=from_position)\n    async for event in subscription:\n        await handler({\n            ''type'': event.type,\n            ''data'': json.loads(event.data),\n            ''stream_id'': event.stream_name,\n            ''position'': event.commit_position\n        })\n\n# Category projection ($ce-Category)\ndef read_category(category: str):\n    \"\"\"Read all events for a category using system projection.\"\"\"\n    return read_stream(f\"$ce-{category}\")\n```\n\n### Template 4: DynamoDB Event Store\n\n```python\nimport boto3\nfrom boto3.dynamodb.conditions import Key\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport json\nimport uuid\n\nclass DynamoEventStore:\n    def __init__(self, table_name: str):\n        self.dynamodb = boto3.resource(''dynamodb'')\n        self.table = self.dynamodb.Table(table_name)\n\n    def append_events(self, stream_id: str, events: list, expected_version: int = None):\n        \"\"\"Append events with conditional write for concurrency.\"\"\"\n        with self.table.batch_writer() as batch:\n            for i, event in enumerate(events):\n                version = (expected_version or 0) + i + 1\n                item = {\n                    ''PK'': f\"STREAM#{stream_id}\",\n                    ''SK'': f\"VERSION#{version:020d}\",\n                    ''GSI1PK'': ''EVENTS'',\n                    ''GSI1SK'': datetime.utcnow().isoformat(),\n                    ''event_id'': str(uuid.uuid4()),\n                    ''stream_id'': stream_id,\n                    ''event_type'': event[''type''],\n                    ''event_data'': json.dumps(event[''data'']),\n                    ''version'': version,\n                    ''created_at'': datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n                }\n                batch.put_item(Item=item)\n        return events\n\n    def read_stream(self, stream_id: str, from_version: int = 0):\n        \"\"\"Read events from a stream.\"\"\"\n        response = self.table.query(\n            KeyConditionExpression=Key(''PK'').eq(f\"STREAM#{stream_id}\") &\n                                  Key(''SK'').gte(f\"VERSION#{from_version:020d}\")\n        )\n        return [\n            {\n                ''event_type'': item[''event_type''],\n                ''data'': json.loads(item[''event_data'']),\n                ''version'': item[''version'']\n            }\n            for item in response[''Items'']\n        ]\n\n# Table definition (CloudFormation/Terraform)\n\"\"\"\nDynamoDB Table:\n  - PK (Partition Key): String\n  - SK (Sort Key): String\n  - GSI1PK, GSI1SK for global ordering\n\nCapacity: On-demand or provisioned based on throughput needs\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Use stream IDs that include aggregate type** - `Order-{uuid}`\n- **Include correlation/causation IDs** - For tracing\n- **Version events from day one** - Plan for schema evolution\n- **Implement idempotency** - Use event IDs for deduplication\n- **Index appropriately** - For your query patterns\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t update or delete events** - They''re immutable facts\n- **Don''t store large payloads** - Keep events small\n- **Don''t skip optimistic concurrency** - Prevents data corruption\n- **Don''t ignore backpressure** - Handle slow consumers\n\n## Resources\n\n- [EventStoreDB](https://www.eventstore.com/)\n- [Marten Events](https://martendb.io/events/)\n- [Event Sourcing Pattern](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/event-sourcing)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:47:18.011Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Architect Agents specializing in event-sourced applications needing optimized event store infrastructure design.","zh":"适用于专门从事事件源应用程序并需要优化事件存储基础设施设计的架构代理。","ja":"イベントソーシングアプリケーションに対する最適化されたイベントストアインフラストラクチャ設計を必要とするアーキテクトエージェントに適しています。","ko":"이벤트 소싱 애플리케이션에 최적화된 이벤트 저장소 인프라 설계가 필요한 아키텍트 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Arquitectura que se especializan en aplicaciones con origen de eventos y necesitan un diseño de infraestructura de almacenamiento de eventos optimizado.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''architecture spécialisés dans les applications à source d''événements nécessitant une conception d''infrastructure de stockage d''événements optimisée.","de":"Ideal für Architekturagenten, die auf ereignisquellbasierte Anwendungen spezialisiert sind und einen optimierten Ereignisspeicher-Infrastruktur-Design benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Arquitetos especializados em aplicações com event sourcing que necessitam de uma infraestrutura de armazenamento de eventos otimizada.","ru":"Идеально для Архитекторов-Агентов, специализирующихся на приложениях с событийно-ориентированной архитектурой, которым необходимо проектирование оптимизированной инфраструктуры хранилища событий.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء المهندسين المعماريين المتخصصين في التطبيقات المعتمدة على الأحداث (event-sourced) والذين يحتاجون إلى تصميم بنية تحتية مُحسنة لمستودع الأحداث."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design scalable event stores, choose between event store technologies, and optimize event storage and retrieval using event sourcing infrastructure and custom event stores, while planning for event store scaling and setting up event store schemas.","zh":"赋予代理设计可扩展的事件存储、在事件存储技术之间进行选择以及使用事件源基础设施和自定义事件存储优化事件存储和检索，同时规划事件存储扩展和设置事件存储模式。","ja":"エージェントがスケーラブルなイベントストアを設計し、イベントストアテクノロジーを選択し、イベントソーシングインフラストラクチャとカスタムイベントストアを使用してイベントの保存と取得を最適化し、イベントストアのスケーリングを計画し、イベントストアのスキーマを設定することを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 확장 가능한 이벤트 저장소를 설계하고 이벤트 저장소 기술을 선택하고 이벤트 소싱 인프라 및 사용자 지정 이벤트 저장소를 사용하여 이벤트 저장소 및 검색을 최적화하며 이벤트 저장소 확장 계획 및 이벤트 저장소 스키마 설정을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar almacenes de eventos escalables, elegir entre tecnologías de almacén de eventos y optimizar el almacenamiento y la recuperación de eventos utilizando la infraestructura de origen de eventos y almacenes de eventos personalizados, mientras planean la escalabilidad del almacén de eventos y configuran los esquemas del almacén de eventos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des magasins d''événements évolutifs, de choisir entre les technologies de stockage d''événements et d''optimiser le stockage et la récupération d''événements en utilisant l''infrastructure de source d''événements et les magasins d''événements personnalisés, tout en planifiant la mise à l''échelle du magasin d''événements et en configurant les schémas du magasin d''événements.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, skalierbare Ereignisspeicher zu entwerfen, zwischen Ereignisspeichertechnologien zu wählen und den Ereignisspeicher und die Ereignisrückgewinnung unter Verwendung der Ereignisquelleninfrastruktur und benutzerdefinierter Ereignisspeicher zu optimieren, während sie die Skalierbarkeit des Ereignisspeichers planen und die Schemata des Ereignisspeichers einrichten.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a projetar armazenamentos de eventos escaláveis, escolher entre tecnologias de armazenamento de eventos e otimizar o armazenamento e a recuperação de eventos usando infraestrutura de event sourcing e armazenamentos de eventos personalizados, enquanto planejam a escalabilidade do armazenamento de eventos e configuram esquemas de armazenamento de eventos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам проектировать масштабируемые хранилища событий, выбирать между технологиями хранения событий и оптимизировать хранение и извлечение событий с использованием инфраструктуры событийно-ориентированного проектирования и пользовательских хранилищ событий, одновременно планируя масштабирование хранилища событий и настраивая схемы хранилища событий.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من تصميم مستودعات أحداث قابلة للتوسع، والاختيار بين تقنيات مستودع الأحداث، وتحسين تخزين واسترجاع الأحداث باستخدام بنية event sourcing ومستودعات الأحداث المخصصة، مع التخطيط لتوسيع نطاق مستودع الأحداث وإعداد مخططات مستودع الأحداث."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing event sourcing infrastructure for high-volume applications","Implementing custom event stores for domain-specific use cases","Optimizing event storage and retrieval for improved query performance"],"zh":["为高容量应用程序设计事件源基础设施","为特定领域用例实现自定义事件存储","优化事件存储和检索以提高查询性能"],"ja":["ハイスループットアプリケーション用のイベントソーシングインフラストラクチャを設計する","ドメイン固有のユースケース用にカスタムイベントストアを実装する","クエリパフォーマンスの向上のためにイベントの保存と取得を最適化する"],"ko":["고容量 애플리케이션을 위한 이벤트 소싱 인프라 설계","도메인 특정 사용 사례를 위한 사용자 지정 이벤트 저장소 구현","쿼리 성능 향상을 위한 이벤트 저장소 및 검색 최적화"],"es":["Diseñar infraestructura de origen de eventos para aplicaciones de alto volumen","Implementar almacenes de eventos personalizados para casos de uso específicos del dominio","Optimizar el almacenamiento y la recuperación de eventos para mejorar el rendimiento de las consultas"],"fr":["Concevoir une infrastructure de source d''événements pour des applications à haut volume","Mettre en œuvre des magasins d''événements personnalisés pour des cas d''utilisation spécifiques au domaine","Optimiser le stockage et la récupération d''événements pour améliorer les performances des requêtes"],"de":["Entwerfen von Ereignisquelleninfrastruktur für Anwendungen mit hohem Volumen","Implementieren von benutzerdefinierten Ereignisspeichern für domänen-spezifische Anwendungsfälle","Optimieren des Ereignisspeichers und der Ereignisrückgewinnung für verbesserte Abfrageleistung"],"pt":["Projetar infraestrutura de event sourcing para aplicações de alto volume","Implementar armazenamentos de eventos personalizados para casos de uso específicos de domínio","Otimizar o armazenamento e recuperação de eventos para melhorar o desempenho de consultas"],"ru":["Проектирование инфраструктуры событийно-ориентированного проектирования для высоконагруженных приложений","Реализация пользовательских хранилищ событий для предметно-ориентированных случаев использования","Оптимизация хранения и извлечения событий для повышения производительности запросов"],"ar":["تصميم بنية تحتية لـ event sourcing للتطبيقات عالية الحجم","تنفيذ مستودعات أحداث مخصصة لحالات الاستخدام الخاصة بالنطاق (domain-specific)","تحسين تخزين واسترجاع الأحداث لتحسين أداء الاستعلامات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of event-sourced application architecture","Limited to event store design and implementation"],"zh":["需要事件源应用程序架构的知识","仅限事件存储设计和实现"],"ja":["イベントソーシングアプリケーションのアーキテクチャに関する知識が必要","イベントストアの設計と実装に限定される"],"ko":["이벤트 소싱 애플리케이션 아키텍처에 대한 지식이 필요","이벤트 저장소 설계 및 구현에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de la arquitectura de aplicaciones con origen de eventos","Limitado al diseño y la implementación de la infraestructura de almacenamiento de eventos"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en matière d''architecture d''applications à source d''événements","Limité à la conception et à la mise en œuvre de l''infrastructure de stockage d''événements"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Architektur von ereignisquellbasierten Anwendungen","Begrenzt auf das Design und die Implementierung der Ereignisspeicher-Infrastruktur"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento da arquitetura de aplicações com event sourcing","Limitado ao design e implementação de armazenamento de eventos"],"ru":["Требует знаний архитектуры приложений с событийно-ориентированным проектированием","Ограничено проектированием и реализацией хранилища событий"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة ببنية التطبيقات المعتمدة على الأحداث (event-sourced)","يقتصر على تصميم وتنفيذ مستودع الأحداث"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
