["Implantação automática de aplicações do Kubernetes","Configuração de políticas de sincronização automatizadas","Gerenciamento de implantações em vários clusters","Implementação de estratégias de entrega progressiva","Integração com ArgoCD e Flux CD"],"ru":["Автоматическое развертывание приложений Kubernetes","Настройка автоматических политик синхронизации","Управление развертыванием в нескольких кластерах","Реализация стратегий прогрессивной доставки","Интеграция с ArgoCD и Flux CD"],"ar":["نشر تلقائي لتطبيقات كوبيرنتس","تكوين سياسات التزامن التلقائية","إدارة النشر في عدة مستويات","تنفيذ استراتيجيات التسليم التدريجي","التكامل مع ArgoCD و Flux CD"]},"keywords":{"zh":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux","declarative","continuous delivery","自动化部署","多集群部署"],"ja":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux","宣言的","継続的デリバリー","自動化デプロイ","マルチクラスターデプロイ"],"ko":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux","선언적","지속적 전달","자동화 배포","다중 클러스터 배포"],"es":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux","despliegue automático","entrega continua","estrategias de entrega progresiva"],"fr":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux","déploiement automatique","livraison continue","stratégies de livraison progressive"],"de":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux","automatisierte Bereitstellung","kontinuierliche Lieferung","Strategien für progressive Lieferung"],"pt":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux CD","entrega contínua","implantação automática","gerenciamento de clusters"],"ru":["GitOps","Kubernetes","ArgoCD","Flux CD","непрерывная доставка","автоматическое развертывание","управление кластерами"],"ar":["جيتوبس","كوبيرنتس","ArgoCD","Flux CD","التسليم المستمر","النشر التلقائي","إدارة المستويات"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"gitops-workflow","description":"Implement GitOps workflows with ArgoCD and Flux for automated, declarative Kubernetes deployments with continuous reconciliation. Use when implementing GitOps practices, automating Kubernetes deployments, or setting up declarative infrastructure management.","bodyPreview":"# GitOps Workflow\n\nComplete guide to implementing GitOps workflows with ArgoCD and Flux for automated Kubernetes deployments.\n\n## Purpose\n\nImplement declarative, Git-based continuous delivery for Kubernetes using ArgoCD or Flux CD, following OpenGitOps principles.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Set up GitOps for Kubernetes clusters\n- Automate application deployments from Git\n- Implement progressive delivery strategies\n- Manage multi-cluster deployments\n- Configure automated sync policies\n- Set up","body":"# GitOps Workflow\n\nComplete guide to implementing GitOps workflows with ArgoCD and Flux for automated Kubernetes deployments.\n\n## Purpose\n\nImplement declarative, Git-based continuous delivery for Kubernetes using ArgoCD or Flux CD, following OpenGitOps principles.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Set up GitOps for Kubernetes clusters\n- Automate application deployments from Git\n- Implement progressive delivery strategies\n- Manage multi-cluster deployments\n- Configure automated sync policies\n- Set up secret management in GitOps\n\n## OpenGitOps Principles\n\n1. **Declarative** - Entire system described declaratively\n2. **Versioned and Immutable** - Desired state stored in Git\n3. **Pulled Automatically** - Software agents pull desired state\n4. **Continuously Reconciled** - Agents reconcile actual vs desired state\n\n## ArgoCD Setup\n\n### 1. Installation\n\n```bash\n# Create namespace\nkubectl create namespace argocd\n\n# Install ArgoCD\nkubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml\n\n# Get admin password\nkubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath=\"{.data.password}\" | base64 -d\n```\n\n**Reference:** See `references/argocd-setup.md` for detailed setup\n\n### 2. Repository Structure\n\n```\ngitops-repo/\n├── apps/\n│   ├── production/\n│   │   ├── app1/\n│   │   │   ├── kustomization.yaml\n│   │   │   └── deployment.yaml\n│   │   └── app2/\n│   └── staging/\n├── infrastructure/\n│   ├── ingress-nginx/\n│   ├── cert-manager/\n│   └── monitoring/\n└── argocd/\n    ├── applications/\n    └── projects/\n```\n\n### 3. Create Application\n\n```yaml\n# argocd/applications/my-app.yaml\napiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\nkind: Application\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\n  namespace: argocd\nspec:\n  project: default\n  source:\n    repoURL: https://github.com/org/gitops-repo\n    targetRevision: main\n    path: apps/production/my-app\n  destination:\n    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc\n    namespace: production\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      prune: true\n      selfHeal: true\n    syncOptions:\n      - CreateNamespace=true\n```\n\n### 4. App of Apps Pattern\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\nkind: Application\nmetadata:\n  name: applications\n  namespace: argocd\nspec:\n  project: default\n  source:\n    repoURL: https://github.com/org/gitops-repo\n    targetRevision: main\n    path: argocd/applications\n  destination:\n    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc\n    namespace: argocd\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated: {}\n```\n\n## Flux CD Setup\n\n### 1. Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install Flux CLI\ncurl -s https://fluxcd.io/install.sh | sudo bash\n\n# Bootstrap Flux\nflux bootstrap github \\\n  --owner=org \\\n  --repository=gitops-repo \\\n  --branch=main \\\n  --path=clusters/production \\\n  --personal\n```\n\n### 2. Create GitRepository\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: source.toolkit.fluxcd.io/v1\nkind: GitRepository\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\n  namespace: flux-system\nspec:\n  interval: 1m\n  url: https://github.com/org/my-app\n  ref:\n    branch: main\n```\n\n### 3. Create Kustomization\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/v1\nkind: Kustomization\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\n  namespace: flux-system\nspec:\n  interval: 5m\n  path: ./deploy\n  prune: true\n  sourceRef:\n    kind: GitRepository\n    name: my-app\n```\n\n## Sync Policies\n\n### Auto-Sync Configuration\n\n**ArgoCD:**\n\n```yaml\nsyncPolicy:\n  automated:\n    prune: true # Delete resources not in Git\n    selfHeal: true # Reconcile manual changes\n    allowEmpty: false\n  retry:\n    limit: 5\n    backoff:\n      duration: 5s\n      factor: 2\n      maxDuration: 3m\n```\n\n**Flux:**\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  interval: 1m\n  prune: true\n  wait: true\n  timeout: 5m\n```\n\n**Reference:** See `references/sync-policies.md`\n\n## Progressive Delivery\n\n### Canary Deployment with ArgoCD Rollouts\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\nkind: Rollout\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\nspec:\n  replicas: 5\n  strategy:\n    canary:\n      steps:\n        - setWeight: 20\n        - pause: { duration: 1m }\n        - setWeight: 50\n        - pause: { duration: 2m }\n        - setWeight: 100\n```\n\n### Blue-Green Deployment\n\n```yaml\nstrategy:\n  blueGreen:\n    activeService: my-app\n    previewService: my-app-preview\n    autoPromotionEnabled: false\n```\n\n## Secret Management\n\n### External Secrets Operator\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: external-secrets.io/v1beta1\nkind: ExternalSecret\nmetadata:\n  name: db-credentials\nspec:\n  refreshInterval: 1h\n  secretStoreRef:\n    name: aws-secrets-manager\n    kind: SecretStore\n  target:\n    name: db-credentials\n  data:\n    - secretKey: password\n      remoteRef:\n        key: prod/db/password\n```\n\n### Sealed Secrets\n\n```bash\n# Encrypt secret\nkubeseal --format yaml < secret.yaml > sealed-secret.yaml\n\n# Commit sealed-secret.yaml to Git\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use separate repos or branches** for different environments\n2. **Implement RBAC** for Git repositories\n3. **Enable notifications** for sync failures\n4. **Use health checks** for custom resources\n5. **Implement approval gates** for production\n6. **Keep secrets out of Git** (use External Secrets)\n7. **Use App of Apps pattern** for organization\n8. **Tag releases** for easy rollback\n9. **Monitor sync status** with alerts\n10. **Test changes** in staging first\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**Sync failures:**\n\n```bash\nargocd app get my-app\nargocd app sync my-app --prune\n```\n\n**Out of sync status:**\n\n```bash\nargocd app diff my-app\nargocd app sync my-app --force\n```\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- `k8s-manifest-generator` - For creating manifests\n- `helm-chart-scaffolding` - For packaging applications\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:48:30.299Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for DevOps Agents requiring automated Kubernetes deployments using GitOps workflows with ArgoCD and Flux","zh":"适用于需要使用 GitOps 工作流和 ArgoCD 以及 Flux 自动化 Kubernetes 部署的 DevOps 代理","ja":"ArgoCD および Flux を使用した GitOps ワークフローによる自動化された Kubernetes デプロイを必要とする DevOps エージェントに適しています","ko":"GitOps 워크플로와 ArgoCD 및 Flux를 사용하여 자동화된 Kubernetes 배포가 필요한 DevOps 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de DevOps que requieren despliegues automatizados de Kubernetes utilizando flujos de trabajo de GitOps con ArgoCD y Flux","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps nécessitant des déploiements Kubernetes automatisés en utilisant des flux de travail GitOps avec ArgoCD et Flux","de":"Ideal für DevOps-Agents, die automatisierte Kubernetes-Bereitstellungen unter Verwendung von GitOps-Workflows mit ArgoCD und Flux erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes DevOps que exigem implantações automatizadas do Kubernetes usando fluxos de trabalho GitOps com ArgoCD e Flux","ru":"Идеально для агентов DevOps, требующих автоматических развертываний Kubernetes с использованием рабочих процессов GitOps с ArgoCD и Flux","ar":"مثالي للموكلين DevOps الذين يتطلبون عمليات نشر Kubernetes آليّة باستخدام تدفقات عمل GitOps مع ArgoCD و Flux"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement declarative, Git-based continuous delivery for Kubernetes, following OpenGitOps principles, and automate application deployments from Git using protocols like ArgoCD and Flux CD","zh":"赋予代理实现声明式、基于 Git 的 Kubernetes 持续交付，遵循 OpenGitOps 原则，并使用 ArgoCD 和 Flux CD 等协议从 Git 自动化应用程序部署","ja":"OpenGitOps の原則に従い、ArgoCD および Flux CD などのプロトコルを使用して Git から自動的にアプリケーションをデプロイすることで、エージェントが宣言型の Git ベースの Kubernetes の継続的デリバリーを実装できるようにします","ko":"OpenGitOps 원칙을 따르고 ArgoCD 및 Flux CD 등의 프로토콜을 사용하여 Git에서 자동으로 애플리케이션을 배포함으로써 에이전트가 선언적 Git 기반 Kubernetes 지속적 전달을 구현할 수 있게 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar una entrega continua declarativa basada en Git para Kubernetes, siguiendo los principios de OpenGitOps, y automatizar los despliegues de aplicaciones desde Git utilizando protocolos como ArgoCD y Flux CD","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre une livraison continue déclarative basée sur Git pour Kubernetes, en suivant les principes d''OpenGitOps, et d''automatiser les déploiements d''applications à partir de Git en utilisant des protocoles tels qu''ArgoCD et Flux CD","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, eine deklarative, Git-basierte Continuous Delivery für Kubernetes umzusetzen, den OpenGitOps-Prinzipien folgend, und automatisiert Anwendungs-Bereitstellungen von Git aus, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie ArgoCD und Flux CD","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementarem entrega contínua baseada em Git, declarativa, para Kubernetes, seguindo os princípios do OpenGitOps, e automatizar implantações de aplicações do Git usando protocolos como ArgoCD e Flux CD","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать декларативную, основанную на Git, непрерывную доставку для Kubernetes, следуя принципам OpenGitOps, и автоматизировать развертывания приложений из Git, используя протоколы, такие как ArgoCD и Flux CD","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنفيذ تسليم مستمر إعلاني قائم على Git ل Kubernetes، متبعة مبادئ OpenGitOps، وتأتمة نشرات التطبيقات من Git باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل ArgoCD و Flux CD"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Kubernetes deployments from Git","Implementing progressive delivery strategies for multi-cluster environments","Configuring automated sync policies for consistent deployments"],"zh":["从 Git 自动化 Kubernetes 部署","为多集群环境实现渐进式交付策略","配置自动同步策略以实现一致的部署"],"ja":["Git から Kubernetes の自動デプロイ","マルチクラスター環境に対するプログレッシブデリバリ戦略の実施","一貫したデプロイを実現するための自動同期ポリシーの構成"],"ko":["Git에서 Kubernetes 자동 배포","다중 클러스터 환경을 위한 점진적 전달 전략 구현","일관된 배포를 위한 자동 동기화 정책 구성"],"es":["Automatizar despliegues de Kubernetes desde Git","Implementar estrategias de entrega progresiva para entornos de multi-cluster","Configurar políticas de sincronización automatizada para despliegues coherentes"],"fr":["Automatiser les déploiements Kubernetes à partir de Git","Mettre en œuvre des stratégies de livraison progressive pour des environnements multi-cluster","Configurer des stratégies de synchronisation automatique pour des déploiements cohérents"],"de":["Automatisierung von Kubernetes-Bereitstellungen von Git aus","Implementierung von schrittweisen Auslieferungsstrategien für Multi-Cluster-Umgebungen","Konfigurieren von automatisierten Synchronisationsrichtlinien für konsistente Bereitstellungen"],"pt":["Automatizar implantações do Kubernetes do Git","Implementar estratégias de entrega progressiva para ambientes de vários clusters","Configurar políticas de sincronização automatizadas para implantações consistentes"],"ru":["Автоматизировать развертывания Kubernetes из Git","Реализовать прогрессивные стратегии доставки для много-кластерных сред","Настроить автоматические политики синхронизации для согласованных развертываний"],"ar":["أتمتة عمليات نشر Kubernetes من Git","تنفيذ استراتيجيات التسليم التدريجي للبيئات متعددة الأузان","تكوين سياسات التزام آليّة لنشرات متسقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Kubernetes cluster setup","Limited to ArgoCD and Flux CD implementations","Dependent on OpenGitOps principles for workflow management"],"zh":["需要 Kubernetes 集群设置","仅限 ArgoCD 和 Flux CD 实现","依赖于 OpenGitOps 原则进行工作流管理"],"ja":["Kubernetes クラスターの設定が必要","ArgoCD および Flux CD の実装のみ","ワークフローの管理には OpenGitOps の原則に依存"],"ko":["Kubernetes 클러스터 설정이 필요","ArgoCD 및 Flux CD 구현에만 제한","워크플로우 관리에는 OpenGitOps 원칙에 의존"],"es":["Requiere configuración de clúster de Kubernetes","Limitado a implementaciones de ArgoCD y Flux CD","Dependiente de los principios de OpenGitOps para la gestión de flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de cluster Kubernetes","Limité aux implémentations d''ArgoCD et de Flux CD","Dépendant des principes d''OpenGitOps pour la gestion des flux de travail"],"de":["Benötigt eine Kubernetes-Cluster-Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf ArgoCD- und Flux-CD-Implementierungen","Abhängig von den OpenGitOps-Prinzipien für die Workflow-Verwaltung"],"pt":["Exige configuração do cluster do Kubernetes","Limitado a implementações do ArgoCD e Flux CD","Dependente dos princípios do OpenGitOps para gerenciamento de fluxos de trabalho"],"ru":["Требует настройки кластера Kubernetes","Ограничен реализациями ArgoCD и Flux CD","Зависит от принципов OpenGitOps для управления рабочими процессами"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد خوشة Kubernetes","محدود بتطبيقات ArgoCD و Flux CD","يعتمد على مبادئ OpenGitOps لإدارة تدفقات العمل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/database-schema-designer', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'database-schema-designer', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z', '2026-02-18T13:48:51.977Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/database-schema-designer","name":"database-schema-designer","description":{"zh":"数据库模式设计师帮助您创建生产就绪的数据库模式，内置最佳实践。只需描述您的数据模型，即可生成完整的SQL模式","ja":"データベーススキーマデザイナーは、ベストプラクティスを組み込んだ生産対応のデータベーススキーマを作成するのに役立ちます。データモデルを説明するだけで、完全なSQLスキーマが生成されます","ko":"데이터베이스 스키마 디자이너는 생산 준비가 완료된 데이터베이스 스키마를 생성하는 데 도움이 됩니다. 최고의 실践이 내장되어 있으며, 데이터 모델을 설명하기만 하면 전체 SQL 스키마가 생성됩니다.","es":"El diseñador de esquemas de base de datos crea esquemas de producción con las mejores prácticas. Describe tu modelo de datos y obtén un esquema SQL completo.","fr":"Le conceleur de schéma de base de données crée des schémas de production avec les meilleures pratiques. Décrivez votre modèle de données et obtenez un schéma SQL complet.","de":"Der Datenbank-Schema-Designer erstellt produktionsbereite Schemata mit integrierten Best Practices. Beschreiben Sie Ihr Datenmodell und erhalten Sie ein vollständiges SQL-Schema.","pt":"O Designer de Esquema de Banco de Dados ajuda a criar esquemas de banco de dados personalizados e prontos para produção.","ru":"Конструктор схемы базы данных помогает создавать индивидуальные схемы базы данных, готовые к производству.","ar":"مصمم مخطط قاعدة البيانات يساعد على إنشاء مخططات قواعد البيانات المخصصة والجاهزة للانتاج.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"数据库模式设计师 - 自动生成SQL模式","ja":"データベーススキーマデザイナー - 生SQLスキーマ生成","ko":"데이터베이스 스키마 디자이너 - 자동 SQL 스키마 생성","es":"Diseñador de Esquemas de Base de Datos","fr":"Conceleur de Schéma de Base de Données","de":"Datenbank-Schema-Designer","pt":"Designer de Esquema de Banco de Dados","ru":"Конструктор схемы базы данных","ar":"مصمم مخطط قاعدة البيانات","en":"database-schema-designer"},"description":{"zh":"数据库模式设计师帮助您创建生产就绪的数据库模式，内置最佳实践。只需描述您的数据模型，即可生成完整的SQL模式","ja":"データベーススキーマデザイナーは、ベストプラクティスを組み込んだ生産対応のデータベーススキーマを作成するのに役立ちます。データモデルを説明するだけで、完全なSQLスキーマが生成されます","ko":"데이터베이스 스키마 디자이너는 생산 준비가 완료된 데이터베이스 스키마를 생성하는 데 도움이 됩니다. 최고의 실践이 내장되어 있으며, 데이터 모델을 설명하기만 하면 전체 SQL 스키마가 생성됩니다.","es":"El diseñador de esquemas de base de datos crea esquemas de producción con las mejores prácticas. Describe tu modelo de datos y obtén un esquema SQL completo.","fr":"Le conceleur de schéma de base de données crée des schémas de production avec les meilleures pratiques. Décrivez votre modèle de données et obtenez un schéma...","de":"Der Datenbank-Schema-Designer erstellt produktionsbereite Schemata mit integrierten Best Practices. Beschreiben Sie Ihr Datenmodell und erhalten Sie ein voll...","pt":"O Designer de Esquema de Banco de Dados ajuda a criar esquemas de banco de dados personalizados e prontos para produção.","ru":"Конструктор схемы базы данных помогает создавать индивидуальные схемы базы данных, готовые к производству.","ar":"مصمم مخطط قاعدة البيانات يساعد على إنشاء مخططات قواعد البيانات المخصصة والجاهزة للانتاج.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["根据数据模型生成SQL模式","内置最佳实践","支持多种数据库管理系统","易于使用的界面","快速生成模式"],"ja":["データモデルに基づいてSQLスキーマを生成","ベストプラクティスを組み込む","複数のデータベース管理システムをサポート","使いやすいインターフェース","迅速にスキーマを生成"],"ko":["데이터 모델 기반으로 SQL 스키마 생성","최상의 실践을 내장","다중 데이터베이스 관리 시스템 지원","사용하기 쉬운 인터페이스","빠른 스키마 생성"],"es":["Crea esquemas de base de datos de producción","Integra las mejores prácticas","Soporta la descripción de modelos de datos","Genera esquemas SQL completos","Ideal para plataformas de comercio electrónico","Fácil de usar"],"fr":["Concevez des schémas de base de données de production","Intégrez les meilleures pratiques","Prend en charge la description de modèles de données","Générez des schémas SQL complets","Idéal pour les plateformes de commerce électronique","Facile à utiliser"],"de":["Erstellt produktionsbereite Datenbankschemata","Integriert Best Practices","Unterstützt die Beschreibung von Datenmodellen","Erzeugt vollständige SQL-Schemata","Ideal für E-Commerce-Plattformen","Einfach zu bedienen"],"pt":["Criação de esquemas de banco de dados personalizados","Incorporação de melhores práticas","Geração de esquemas SQL prontos para produção","Desenvolvimento de esquemas para plataformas de e-commerce","Suporte a múltiplos bancos de dados"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных схем базы данных","Встраивание лучших практик","Генерация схем SQL, готовых к производству","Разработка схем для платформ электронной коммерции","Поддержка нескольких баз данных"],"ar":["إنشاء مخططات قواعد البيانات المخصصة","دمج أفضل الممارسات","توليد مخططات SQL الجاهزة للانتاج","تطوير مخططات لمنصات التجارة الإلكترونية","دعم قواعد البيانات المتعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["数据库模式设计","SQL模式生成","生产就绪的数据库模式","数据模型","数据库管理系统","最佳实践"],"ja":["データベーススキーマ設計","SQLスキーマ生成","生産対応のデータベーススキーマ","データモデル","データベース管理システム","ベストプラクティス"],"ko":["데이터베이스 스키마 디자인","SQL 스키마 생성","생산 준비가 완료된 데이터베이스 스키마","데이터 모델","데이터베이스 관리 시스템","최상의 실践"],"es":["diseñador de esquemas de base de datos","esquemas de base de datos de producción","mejores prácticas","modelo de datos","esquema SQL","plataforma de comercio electrónico","desarrollo de bases de datos"],"fr":["conceleur de schéma de base de données","schémas de base de données de production","meilleures pratiques","modèle de données","schéma SQL","plateforme de commerce électronique","développement de bases de données"],"de":["Datenbank-Schema-Designer","produktionsbereite Datenbankschemata","Best Practices","Datenmodell","SQL-Schema","E-Commerce-Plattform","Datenbankentwicklung"],"pt":["designer de esquema de banco de dados","esquema de banco de dados","banco de dados","sql","desenvolvimento de software","plataformas de e-commerce"],"ru":["конструктор схемы базы данных","схема базы данных","база данных","sql","разработка программного обеспечения","платформы электронной коммерции"],"ar":["مصمم مخطط قاعدة البيانات","مخطط قاعدة البيانات","قاعدة البيانات","sql","تطوير البرمجيات","منصات التجارة الإلكترونية"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"database-schema-designer","description":"Design robust, scalable database schemas for SQL and NoSQL databases. Provides normalization guidelines, indexing strategies, migration patterns, constraint design, and performance optimization. Ensures data integrity, query performance, and maintainable data models.","bodyPreview":"# Database Schema Designer\n\nDesign production-ready database schemas with best practices built-in.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\nJust describe your data model:\n\n```\ndesign a schema for an e-commerce platform with users, products, orders\n```\n\nYou''ll get a complete SQL schema like:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  id BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,\n  email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  id BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,\n  use","body":"# Database Schema Designer\n\nDesign production-ready database schemas with best practices built-in.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\nJust describe your data model:\n\n```\ndesign a schema for an e-commerce platform with users, products, orders\n```\n\nYou''ll get a complete SQL schema like:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  id BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,\n  email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  id BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,\n  user_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n  total DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  INDEX idx_orders_user (user_id)\n);\n```\n\n**What to include in your request:**\n- Entities (users, products, orders)\n- Key relationships (users have orders, orders have items)\n- Scale hints (high-traffic, millions of records)\n- Database preference (SQL/NoSQL) - defaults to SQL if not specified\n\n---\n\n## Triggers\n\n| Trigger | Example |\n|---------|---------|\n| `design schema` | \"design a schema for user authentication\" |\n| `database design` | \"database design for multi-tenant SaaS\" |\n| `create tables` | \"create tables for a blog system\" |\n| `schema for` | \"schema for inventory management\" |\n| `model data` | \"model data for real-time analytics\" |\n| `I need a database` | \"I need a database for tracking orders\" |\n| `design NoSQL` | \"design NoSQL schema for product catalog\" |\n\n---\n\n## Key Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **Normalization** | Organizing data to reduce redundancy (1NF → 2NF → 3NF) |\n| **3NF** | Third Normal Form - no transitive dependencies between columns |\n| **OLTP** | Online Transaction Processing - write-heavy, needs normalization |\n| **OLAP** | Online Analytical Processing - read-heavy, benefits from denormalization |\n| **Foreign Key (FK)** | Column that references another table''s primary key |\n| **Index** | Data structure that speeds up queries (at cost of slower writes) |\n| **Access Pattern** | How your app reads/writes data (queries, joins, filters) |\n| **Denormalization** | Intentionally duplicating data to speed up reads |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Approach | Key Consideration |\n|------|----------|-------------------|\n| New schema | Normalize to 3NF first | Domain modeling over UI |\n| SQL vs NoSQL | Access patterns decide | Read/write ratio matters |\n| Primary keys | INT or UUID | UUID for distributed systems |\n| Foreign keys | Always constrain | ON DELETE strategy critical |\n| Indexes | FKs + WHERE columns | Column order matters |\n| Migrations | Always reversible | Backward compatible first |\n\n---\n\n## Process Overview\n\n```\nYour Data Requirements\n    |\n    v\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n| Phase 1: ANALYSIS                                   |\n| * Identify entities and relationships               |\n| * Determine access patterns (read vs write heavy)   |\n| * Choose SQL or NoSQL based on requirements         |\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n    |\n    v\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n| Phase 2: DESIGN                                     |\n| * Normalize to 3NF (SQL) or embed/reference (NoSQL) |\n| * Define primary keys and foreign keys              |\n| * Choose appropriate data types                     |\n| * Add constraints (UNIQUE, CHECK, NOT NULL)         |\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n    |\n    v\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n| Phase 3: OPTIMIZE                                   |\n| * Plan indexing strategy                            |\n| * Consider denormalization for read-heavy queries   |\n| * Add timestamps (created_at, updated_at)           |\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n    |\n    v\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n| Phase 4: MIGRATE                                    |\n| * Generate migration scripts (up + down)            |\n| * Ensure backward compatibility                     |\n| * Plan zero-downtime deployment                     |\n+-----------------------------------------------------+\n    |\n    v\nProduction-Ready Schema\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | When to Use | Action |\n|---------|-------------|--------|\n| `design schema for {domain}` | Starting fresh | Full schema generation |\n| `normalize {table}` | Fixing existing table | Apply normalization rules |\n| `add indexes for {table}` | Performance issues | Generate index strategy |\n| `migration for {change}` | Schema evolution | Create reversible migration |\n| `review schema` | Code review | Audit existing schema |\n\n**Workflow:** Start with `design schema` → iterate with `normalize` → optimize with `add indexes` → evolve with `migration`\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n| Principle | WHY | Implementation |\n|-----------|-----|----------------|\n| Model the Domain | UI changes, domain doesn''t | Entity names reflect business concepts |\n| Data Integrity First | Corruption is costly to fix | Constraints at database level |\n| Optimize for Access Pattern | Can''t optimize for both | OLTP: normalized, OLAP: denormalized |\n| Plan for Scale | Retrofitting is painful | Index strategy + partitioning plan |\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Avoid | Why | Instead |\n|-------|-----|---------|\n| VARCHAR(255) everywhere | Wastes storage, hides intent | Size appropriately per field |\n| FLOAT for money | Rounding errors | DECIMAL(10,2) |\n| Missing FK constraints | Orphaned data | Always define foreign keys |\n| No indexes on FKs | Slow JOINs | Index every foreign key |\n| Storing dates as strings | Can''t compare/sort | DATE, TIMESTAMP types |\n| SELECT * in queries | Fetches unnecessary data | Explicit column lists |\n| Non-reversible migrations | Can''t rollback | Always write DOWN migration |\n| Adding NOT NULL without default | Breaks existing rows | Add nullable, backfill, then constrain |\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nAfter designing a schema:\n\n- [ ] Every table has a primary key\n- [ ] All relationships have foreign key constraints\n- [ ] ON DELETE strategy defined for each FK\n- [ ] Indexes exist on all foreign keys\n- [ ] Indexes exist on frequently queried columns\n- [ ] Appropriate data types (DECIMAL for money, etc.)\n- [ ] NOT NULL on required fields\n- [ ] UNIQUE constraints where needed\n- [ ] CHECK constraints for validation\n- [ ] created_at and updated_at timestamps\n- [ ] Migration scripts are reversible\n- [ ] Tested on staging with production data\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Normalization (SQL)</strong></summary>\n\n### Normal Forms\n\n| Form | Rule | Violation Example |\n|------|------|-------------------|\n| **1NF** | Atomic values, no repeating groups | `product_ids = ''1,2,3''` |\n| **2NF** | 1NF + no partial dependencies | customer_name in order_items |\n| **3NF** | 2NF + no transitive dependencies | country derived from postal_code |\n\n### 1st Normal Form (1NF)\n\n```sql\n-- BAD: Multiple values in column\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  product_ids VARCHAR(255)  -- ''101,102,103''\n);\n\n-- GOOD: Separate table for items\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  customer_id INT\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE order_items (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  order_id INT REFERENCES orders(id),\n  product_id INT\n);\n```\n\n### 2nd Normal Form (2NF)\n\n```sql\n-- BAD: customer_name depends only on customer_id\nCREATE TABLE order_items (\n  order_id INT,\n  product_id INT,\n  customer_name VARCHAR(100),  -- Partial dependency!\n  PRIMARY KEY (order_id, product_id)\n);\n\n-- GOOD: Customer data in separate table\nCREATE TABLE customers (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name VARCHAR(100)\n);\n```\n\n### 3rd Normal Form (3NF)\n\n```sql\n-- BAD: country depends on postal_code\nCREATE TABLE customers (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  postal_code VARCHAR(10),\n  country VARCHAR(50)  -- Transitive dependency!\n);\n\n-- GOOD: Separate postal_codes table\nCREATE TABLE postal_codes (\n  code VARCHAR(10) PRIMARY KEY,\n  country VARCHAR(50)\n);\n```\n\n### When to Denormalize\n\n| Scenario | Denormalization Strategy |\n|----------|-------------------------|\n| Read-heavy reporting | Pre-calculated aggregates |\n| Expensive JOINs | Cached derived columns |\n| Analytics dashboards | Materialized views |\n\n```sql\n-- Denormalized for performance\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  customer_id INT,\n  total_amount DECIMAL(10,2),  -- Calculated\n  item_count INT               -- Calculated\n);\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Data Types</strong></summary>\n\n### String Types\n\n| Type | Use Case | Example |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| CHAR(n) | Fixed length | State codes, ISO dates |\n| VARCHAR(n) | Variable length | Names, emails |\n| TEXT | Long content | Articles, descriptions |\n\n```sql\n-- Good sizing\nemail VARCHAR(255)\nphone VARCHAR(20)\ncountry_code CHAR(2)\n```\n\n### Numeric Types\n\n| Type | Range | Use Case |\n|------|-------|----------|\n| TINYINT | -128 to 127 | Age, status codes |\n| SMALLINT | -32K to 32K | Quantities |\n| INT | -2.1B to 2.1B | IDs, counts |\n| BIGINT | Very large | Large IDs, timestamps |\n| DECIMAL(p,s) | Exact precision | Money |\n| FLOAT/DOUBLE | Approximate | Scientific data |\n\n```sql\n-- ALWAYS use DECIMAL for money\nprice DECIMAL(10, 2)  -- $99,999,999.99\n\n-- NEVER use FLOAT for money\nprice FLOAT  -- Rounding errors!\n```\n\n### Date/Time Types\n\n```sql\nDATE        -- 2025-10-31\nTIME        -- 14:30:00\nDATETIME    -- 2025-10-31 14:30:00\nTIMESTAMP   -- Auto timezone conversion\n\n-- Always store in UTC\ncreated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\nupdated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n```\n\n### Boolean\n\n```sql\n-- PostgreSQL\nis_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE\n\n-- MySQL\nis_active TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 1\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Indexing Strategy</strong></summary>\n\n### When to Create Indexes\n\n| Always Index | Reason |\n|--------------|--------|\n| Foreign keys | Speed up JOINs |\n| WHERE clause columns | Speed up filtering |\n| ORDER BY columns | Speed up sorting |\n| Unique constraints | Enforced uniqueness |\n\n```sql\n-- Foreign key index\nCREATE INDEX idx_orders_customer ON orders(customer_id);\n\n-- Query pattern index\nCREATE INDEX idx_orders_status_date ON orders(status, created_at);\n```\n\n### Index Types\n\n| Type | Best For | Example |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| B-Tree | Ranges, equality | `price > 100` |\n| Hash | Exact matches only | `email = ''x@y.com''` |\n| Full-text | Text search | `MATCH AGAINST` |\n| Partial | Subset of rows | `WHERE is_active = true` |\n\n### Composite Index Order\n\n```sql\nCREATE INDEX idx_customer_status ON orders(customer_id, status);\n\n-- Uses index (customer_id first)\nSELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 123;\nSELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 123 AND status = ''pending'';\n\n-- Does NOT use index (status alone)\nSELECT * FROM orders WHERE status = ''pending'';\n```\n\n**Rule:** Most selective column first, or column most queried alone.\n\n### Index Pitfalls\n\n| Pitfall | Problem | Solution |\n|---------|---------|----------|\n| Over-indexing | Slow writes | Only index what''s queried |\n| Wrong column order | Unused index | Match query patterns |\n| Missing FK indexes | Slow JOINs | Always index FKs |\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Constraints</strong></summary>\n\n### Primary Keys\n\n```sql\n-- Auto-increment (simple)\nid INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY\n\n-- UUID (distributed systems)\nid CHAR(36) PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT (UUID())\n\n-- Composite (junction tables)\nPRIMARY KEY (student_id, course_id)\n```\n\n### Foreign Keys\n\n```sql\nFOREIGN KEY (customer_id) REFERENCES customers(id)\n  ON DELETE CASCADE     -- Delete children with parent\n  ON DELETE RESTRICT    -- Prevent deletion if referenced\n  ON DELETE SET NULL    -- Set to NULL when parent deleted\n  ON UPDATE CASCADE     -- Update children when parent changes\n```\n\n| Strategy | Use When |\n|----------|----------|\n| CASCADE | Dependent data (order_items) |\n| RESTRICT | Important references (prevent accidents) |\n| SET NULL | Optional relationships |\n\n### Other Constraints\n\n```sql\n-- Unique\nemail VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL\n\n-- Composite unique\nUNIQUE (student_id, course_id)\n\n-- Check\nprice DECIMAL(10,2) CHECK (price >= 0)\ndiscount INT CHECK (discount BETWEEN 0 AND 100)\n\n-- Not null\nname VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Relationship Patterns</strong></summary>\n\n### One-to-Many\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  customer_id INT NOT NULL REFERENCES customers(id)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE order_items (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  order_id INT NOT NULL REFERENCES orders(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  product_id INT NOT NULL,\n  quantity INT NOT NULL\n);\n```\n\n### Many-to-Many\n\n```sql\n-- Junction table\nCREATE TABLE enrollments (\n  student_id INT REFERENCES students(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  course_id INT REFERENCES courses(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  enrolled_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (student_id, course_id)\n);\n```\n\n### Self-Referencing\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE employees (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n  manager_id INT REFERENCES employees(id)\n);\n```\n\n### Polymorphic\n\n```sql\n-- Approach 1: Separate FKs (stronger integrity)\nCREATE TABLE comments (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  content TEXT NOT NULL,\n  post_id INT REFERENCES posts(id),\n  photo_id INT REFERENCES photos(id),\n  CHECK (\n    (post_id IS NOT NULL AND photo_id IS NULL) OR\n    (post_id IS NULL AND photo_id IS NOT NULL)\n  )\n);\n\n-- Approach 2: Type + ID (flexible, weaker integrity)\nCREATE TABLE comments (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  content TEXT NOT NULL,\n  commentable_type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,\n  commentable_id INT NOT NULL\n);\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: NoSQL Design (MongoDB)</strong></summary>\n\n### Embedding vs Referencing\n\n| Factor | Embed | Reference |\n|--------|-------|-----------|\n| Access pattern | Read together | Read separately |\n| Relationship | 1:few | 1:many |\n| Document size | Small | Approaching 16MB |\n| Update frequency | Rarely | Frequently |\n\n### Embedded Document\n\n```json\n{\n  \"_id\": \"order_123\",\n  \"customer\": {\n    \"id\": \"cust_456\",\n    \"name\": \"Jane Smith\",\n    \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"\n  },\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"product_id\": \"prod_789\", \"quantity\": 2, \"price\": 29.99 }\n  ],\n  \"total\": 109.97\n}\n```\n\n### Referenced Document\n\n```json\n{\n  \"_id\": \"order_123\",\n  \"customer_id\": \"cust_456\",\n  \"item_ids\": [\"item_1\", \"item_2\"],\n  \"total\": 109.97\n}\n```\n\n### MongoDB Indexes\n\n```javascript\n// Single field\ndb.users.createIndex({ email: 1 }, { unique: true });\n\n// Composite\ndb.orders.createIndex({ customer_id: 1, created_at: -1 });\n\n// Text search\ndb.articles.createIndex({ title: \"text\", content: \"text\" });\n\n// Geospatial\ndb.stores.createIndex({ location: \"2dsphere\" });\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Migrations</strong></summary>\n\n### Migration Best Practices\n\n| Practice | WHY |\n|----------|-----|\n| Always reversible | Need to rollback |\n| Backward compatible | Zero-downtime deploys |\n| Schema before data | Separate concerns |\n| Test on staging | Catch issues early |\n\n### Adding a Column (Zero-Downtime)\n\n```sql\n-- Step 1: Add nullable column\nALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN phone VARCHAR(20);\n\n-- Step 2: Deploy code that writes to new column\n\n-- Step 3: Backfill existing rows\nUPDATE users SET phone = '''' WHERE phone IS NULL;\n\n-- Step 4: Make required (if needed)\nALTER TABLE users MODIFY phone VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL;\n```\n\n### Renaming a Column (Zero-Downtime)\n\n```sql\n-- Step 1: Add new column\nALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN email_address VARCHAR(255);\n\n-- Step 2: Copy data\nUPDATE users SET email_address = email;\n\n-- Step 3: Deploy code reading from new column\n-- Step 4: Deploy code writing to new column\n\n-- Step 5: Drop old column\nALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN email;\n```\n\n### Migration Template\n\n```sql\n-- Migration: YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql\n\n-- UP\nBEGIN;\nALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN phone VARCHAR(20);\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_phone ON users(phone);\nCOMMIT;\n\n-- DOWN\nBEGIN;\nDROP INDEX idx_users_phone ON users;\nALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN phone;\nCOMMIT;\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Performance Optimization</strong></summary>\n\n### Query Analysis\n\n```sql\nEXPLAIN SELECT * FROM orders\nWHERE customer_id = 123 AND status = ''pending'';\n```\n\n| Look For | Meaning |\n|----------|---------|\n| type: ALL | Full table scan (bad) |\n| type: ref | Index used (good) |\n| key: NULL | No index used |\n| rows: high | Many rows scanned |\n\n### N+1 Query Problem\n\n```python\n# BAD: N+1 queries\norders = db.query(\"SELECT * FROM orders\")\nfor order in orders:\n    customer = db.query(f\"SELECT * FROM customers WHERE id = {order.customer_id}\")\n\n# GOOD: Single JOIN\nresults = db.query(\"\"\"\n    SELECT orders.*, customers.name\n    FROM orders\n    JOIN customers ON orders.customer_id = customers.id\n\"\"\")\n```\n\n### Optimization Techniques\n\n| Technique | When to Use |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Add indexes | Slow WHERE/ORDER BY |\n| Denormalize | Expensive JOINs |\n| Pagination | Large result sets |\n| Caching | Repeated queries |\n| Read replicas | Read-heavy load |\n| Partitioning | Very large tables |\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n## Extension Points\n\n1. **Database-Specific Patterns:** Add MySQL vs PostgreSQL vs SQLite variations\n2. **Advanced Patterns:** Time-series, event sourcing, CQRS, multi-tenancy\n3. **ORM Integration:** TypeORM, Prisma, SQLAlchemy patterns\n4. **Monitoring:** Query performance tracking, slow query alerts\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:48:51.977Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing automated database schema creation with SQL best practices.","zh":"适合需要自动数据库架构创建和SQL最佳实践的数据分析代理。","ja":"データ分析エージェントが自動でデータベーススキーマを作成し、SQLベストプラクティスを使用する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"자동 데이터베이스 스키마 생성 및 SQL 모범 사례가 필요한 데이터 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de datos que necesitan la creación automática de esquemas de base de datos con las mejores prácticas de SQL.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données ayant besoin de la création automatisée de schémas de base de données avec les meilleures pratiques SQL.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die eine automatisierte Erstellung von Datenbank-Schemata mit SQL-Best-Practices benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que precisam de criação automática de esquema de banco de dados com as melhores práticas de SQL.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, которым требуется автоматическое создание схемы базы данных с использованием лучших практик SQL.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل البيانات الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء مخطط قاعدة البيانات تلقائيًا باستخدام أفضل الممارسات لغة الاستفسار البنيوي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate production-ready database schemas with complete SQL syntax, including table creation, indexing, and constraints, using SQL protocols and supporting various database management systems.","zh":"赋予代理生成生产就绪的数据库架构的能力，包括完整的SQL语法、表创建、索引和约束，使用SQL协议，并支持各种数据库管理系统。","ja":"エージェントが、完全なSQL構文、テーブル作成、インデックス、制約を含む、プロダクションレディのデータベーススキーマを生成できるようにし、SQLプロトコルを使用し、さまざまなデータベース管理システムをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 프로덕션 준비가 완료된 데이터베이스 스키마를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 이는 완전한 SQL 구문, 테이블 생성, 인덱싱 및 제약 조건을 포함하며 SQL 프로토콜을 사용하고 다양한 데이터베이스 관리 시스템을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar esquemas de base de datos listos para producción con sintaxis SQL completa, incluyendo la creación de tablas, indexación y restricciones, utilizando protocolos SQL y admitiendo varios sistemas de gestión de bases de datos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des schémas de base de données prêts pour la production avec une syntaxe SQL complète, y compris la création de tables, l''indexation et les contraintes, en utilisant les protocoles SQL et en prenant en charge divers systèmes de gestion de bases de données.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, produktionsreife Datenbank-Schemata mit vollständiger SQL-Syntax zu generieren, einschließlich Tabellenerstellung, Indexierung und Einschränkungen, unter Verwendung von SQL-Protokollen und Unterstützung verschiedener Datenbankmanagementsysteme.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar esquemas de banco de dados prontos para produção com sintaxe SQL completa, incluindo criação de tabelas, indexação e restrições, usando protocolos SQL e suportando vários sistemas de gerenciamento de bancos de dados.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать готовые к производству схемы баз данных с полной синтаксисом SQL, включая создание таблиц, индексирование и ограничения, используя протоколы SQL и поддерживая различные системы управления базами данных.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من إنشاء مخططات قاعدة البيانات جاهزة للإنتاج بأسلوب لغة الاستفسار البنيوي الكامل، بما في ذلك إنشاء الجداول والفهرسة والقيود، باستخدام بروتوكولات لغة الاستفسار البنيوي ودعم أنظمة إدارة قواعد البيانات المختلفة"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing schemas for e-commerce platforms","Creating database structures for user management systems","Generating SQL scripts for data warehousing"],"zh":["为电子商务平台设计架构","为用户管理系统创建数据库结构","为数据仓库生成SQL脚本"],"ja":["電子商取引プラットフォームのスキーマ設計","ユーザー管理システムのデータベース構造作成","データウェアハウスのSQLスクリプト生成"],"ko":["전자상거래 플랫폼을 위한 스키마 설계","사용자 관리 시스템을 위한 데이터베이스 구조 생성","데이터웨어하우스를 위한 SQL 스크립트 생성"],"es":["Diseñar esquemas para plataformas de comercio electrónico","Crear estructuras de base de datos para sistemas de gestión de usuarios","Generar scripts SQL para almacenamiento de datos"],"fr":["Concevoir des schémas pour les plateformes de commerce électronique","Créer des structures de base de données pour les systèmes de gestion des utilisateurs","Générer des scripts SQL pour l''entreposage de données"],"de":["Schemata für E-Commerce-Plattformen entwerfen","Datenbankstrukturen für Benutzerverwaltungssysteme erstellen","SQL-Skripte für Data-Warehousing generieren"],"pt":["Projetar esquemas para plataformas de comércio eletrônico","Criar estruturas de banco de dados para sistemas de gerenciamento de usuários","Gerar scripts SQL para armazenamento de dados"],"ru":["Проектирование схем для электронных коммерческих платформ","Создание структур баз данных для систем управления пользователями","Генерация скриптов SQL для хранилищ данных"],"ar":["تصميم مخططات لأنظمة التجارة الإلكترونية","إنشاء هياكل قاعدة البيانات لأنظمة إدارة المستخدمين","إنشاء نصوص لغة الاستفسار البنيوي لتحليل البيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires descriptive data model input","Limited to SQL-based database management systems"],"zh":["需要描述性数据模型输入","仅限于基于SQL的数据库管理系统"],"ja":["記述的なデータモデル入力が必要","SQLベースのデータベース管理システムのみ"],"ko":["설명적인 데이터 모델 입력이 필요함","SQL 기반 데이터베이스 관리 시스템만 지원"],"es":["Requiere una entrada de modelo de datos descriptivo","Limitado a sistemas de gestión de bases de datos basados en SQL"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée de modèle de données descriptif","Limité aux systèmes de gestion de bases de données basés sur SQL"],"de":["Benötigt eine beschreibende Eingabe des Datenmodells","Begrenzt auf SQL-basierte Datenbankmanagementsysteme"],"pt":["Requer entrada de modelo de dados descritivo","Limitado a sistemas de gerenciamento de bancos de dados baseados em SQL"],"ru":["Требуется ввод описательной модели данных","Ограничен системами управления базами данных на основе SQL"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال نموذج بيانات وصفية","محدود بنظم إدارة قواعد البيانات التي تعتمد على لغة الاستفسار البنيوي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
