patibilidad con React 18+/19 y Next.js 14+/15+","Actualizaciones mínimas de v5 a v6","Soporte para interfaces de usuario personalizadas"],"fr":["Message Parts Structure","Intégration avec Vercel AI SDK v6","Compatibilité avec React 18+/19 et Next.js 14+/15+","Mises à jour minimales de v5 à v6","Support pour les interfaces utilisateur personnalisées"],"de":["Message Parts Structure","Integration mit Vercel AI SDK v6","Kompatibilität mit React 18+/19 und Next.js 14+/15+","Minimale Updates von v5 auf v6","Unterstützung für benutzerdefinierte Benutzeroberflächen"],"pt":["React Hooks para interfaces de usuário AI-powered","Compatibilidade com Vercel AI SDK v6","Suporte a React 18+/19 e Next.js 14+/15+","Nova estrutura de partes de mensagens","Minimas alterações quebradoras de versão v5 → v6"],"ru":["Реакт-хуки для интерфейсов пользователя с поддержкой ИИ","Совместимость с Vercel AI SDK v6","Поддержка React 18+/19 и Next.js 14+/15+","Новая структура частей сообщений","Минимальные изменения, нарушающие версию v5 → v6"],"ar":["Hooks React لواجهات المستخدم المدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي","التوافق مع Vercel AI SDK v6","دعم React 18+/19 و Next.js 14+/15+","هيكل جديد للجزء الرسائل","التغييرات القليلة التي كسرت الإصدار v5 → v6"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI SDK UI","React","Vercel AI SDK","AI 驱动的用户界面","前端钩子","React 18+/19","Next.js 14+/15+"],"ja":["AI SDK UI","React","Vercel AI SDK","AI パワード UI","フロントエンド フック","React 18+/19","Next.js 14+/15+"],"ko":["AI SDK UI","React","Vercel AI SDK","AI 기반 사용자 인터페이스","프론트엔드 훅","React 18+/19","Next.js 14+/15+"],"es":["ai-sdk-ui","hooks de React","interfaces de usuario inteligentes","Vercel AI SDK v6","aprendizaje automático","desarrollo de software","React 18+/19","Next.js 14+/15+"],"fr":["ai-sdk-ui","hooks React","interfaces utilisateur intelligentes","Vercel AI SDK v6","apprentissage automatique","développement de logiciels","React 18+/19","Next.js 14+/15+"],"de":["ai-sdk-ui","React-Hooks","KI-basierte Benutzeroberflächen","Vercel AI SDK v6","maschinelles Lernen","Softwareentwicklung","React 18+/19","Next.js 14+/15+"],"pt":["AI SDK UI","React Hooks","Vercel AI SDK v6","Interfaces de usuário AI-powered","Desenvolvimento de software","Tecnologias de IA"],"ru":["AI SDK UI","Реакт-хуки","Vercel AI SDK v6","Интерфейсы пользователя с поддержкой ИИ","Разработка программного обеспечения","Технологии ИИ"],"ar":["AI SDK UI","Hooks React","Vercel AI SDK v6","واجهات المستخدم المدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير البرمجيات","تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ai-sdk-ui","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# AI SDK UI - Frontend React Hooks\n\nFrontend React hooks for AI-powered user interfaces with Vercel AI SDK v6.\n\n**Version**: AI SDK v6.0.42 (Stable)\n**Framework**: React 18+/19, Next.js 14+/15+\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n\n---\n\n## AI SDK v6 Stable (January 2026)\n\n**Status:** Stable Release\n**Latest:** ai@6.0.42, @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44, @ai-sdk/openai@3.0.7\n**Migration:** Minimal breaking changes from v5 → v6\n\n### New UI Features in v6\n\n**1. Message Parts Structure (Breaking Change)**\nIn v6, messa","body":"# AI SDK UI - Frontend React Hooks\n\nFrontend React hooks for AI-powered user interfaces with Vercel AI SDK v6.\n\n**Version**: AI SDK v6.0.42 (Stable)\n**Framework**: React 18+/19, Next.js 14+/15+\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n\n---\n\n## AI SDK v6 Stable (January 2026)\n\n**Status:** Stable Release\n**Latest:** ai@6.0.42, @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44, @ai-sdk/openai@3.0.7\n**Migration:** Minimal breaking changes from v5 → v6\n\n### New UI Features in v6\n\n**1. Message Parts Structure (Breaking Change)**\nIn v6, message content is now accessed via `.parts` array instead of `.content`:\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ v5 (OLD)\n{messages.map(m => (\n  <div key={m.id}>{m.content}</div>\n))}\n\n// ✅ v6 (NEW)\n{messages.map(m => (\n  <div key={m.id}>\n    {m.parts.map((part, i) => {\n      if (part.type === ''text'') return <span key={i}>{part.text}</span>;\n      if (part.type === ''tool-invocation'') return <ToolCall key={i} tool={part} />;\n      if (part.type === ''file'') return <FilePreview key={i} file={part} />;\n      return null;\n    })}\n  </div>\n))}\n```\n\n**Part Types:**\n- `text` - Text content with `.text` property\n- `tool-invocation` - Tool calls with `.toolName`, `.args`, `.result`\n- `file` - File attachments with `.mimeType`, `.data`\n- `reasoning` - Model reasoning (when available)\n- `source` - Source citations\n\n**3. Agent Integration**\nType-safe messaging with agents using `InferAgentUIMessage<typeof agent>`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat } from ''@ai-sdk/react'';\nimport type { InferAgentUIMessage } from ''ai'';\nimport { myAgent } from ''./agent'';\n\nexport default function AgentChat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat<InferAgentUIMessage<typeof myAgent>>({\n    api: ''/api/chat'',\n  });\n  // messages are now type-checked against agent schema\n}\n```\n\n**4. Tool Approval Workflows (Human-in-the-Loop)**\nRequest user confirmation before executing tools:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat } from ''@ai-sdk/react'';\nimport { useState } from ''react'';\n\nexport default function ChatWithApproval() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, addToolApprovalResponse } = useChat({\n    api: ''/api/chat'',\n  });\n\n  const handleApprove = (toolCallId: string) => {\n    addToolApprovalResponse({\n      toolCallId,\n      approved: true,  // or false to deny\n    });\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map(message => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.toolInvocations?.map(tool => (\n            tool.state === ''awaiting-approval'' && (\n              <div key={tool.toolCallId}>\n                <p>Approve tool call: {tool.toolName}?</p>\n                <button onClick={() => handleApprove(tool.toolCallId)}>\n                  Approve\n                </button>\n                <button onClick={() => addToolApprovalResponse({\n                  toolCallId: tool.toolCallId,\n                  approved: false\n                })}>\n                  Deny\n                </button>\n              </div>\n            )\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**5. Auto-Submit Capability**\nAutomatically continue conversation after handling approvals:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithApprovalResponses } from ''@ai-sdk/react'';\n\nexport default function AutoSubmitChat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    api: ''/api/chat'',\n    sendAutomaticallyWhen: lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithApprovalResponses,\n    // Automatically resubmit after all approval responses provided\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**6. Structured Output in Chat**\nGenerate structured data alongside tool calling (previously only available in `useObject`):\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat } from ''@ai-sdk/react'';\nimport { z } from ''zod'';\n\nconst schema = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  sentiment: z.enum([''positive'', ''neutral'', ''negative'']),\n});\n\nexport default function StructuredChat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    api: ''/api/chat'',\n    // Server can now stream structured output with chat messages\n  });\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## useChat Hook - v4 → v5 Breaking Changes\n\n**CRITICAL: useChat no longer manages input state in v5!**\n\n**v4 (OLD - DON''T USE):**\n```tsx\nconst { messages, input, handleInputChange, handleSubmit, append } = useChat();\n\n<form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>\n  <input value={input} onChange={handleInputChange} />\n</form>\n```\n\n**v5 (NEW - CORRECT):**\n```tsx\nconst { messages, sendMessage } = useChat();\nconst [input, setInput] = useState('''');\n\n<form onSubmit={(e) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  sendMessage({ content: input });\n  setInput('''');\n}}>\n  <input value={input} onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)} />\n</form>\n```\n\n**Summary of v5 Changes:**\n1. **Input management removed**: `input`, `handleInputChange`, `handleSubmit` no longer exist\n2. **`append()` → `sendMessage()`**: New method for sending messages\n3. **`onResponse` removed**: Use `onFinish` instead\n4. **`initialMessages` → controlled mode**: Use `messages` prop for full control\n5. **`maxSteps` removed**: Handle on server-side only\n\nSee `references/use-chat-migration.md` for complete migration guide.\n\n---\n\n## useAssistant Hook (Deprecated)\n\n> **⚠️ Deprecation Notice**: `useAssistant` is deprecated as of AI SDK v5. OpenAI Assistants API v2\n> will sunset on August 26, 2026. For new projects, use `useChat` with custom backend logic instead.\n> See the **openai-assistants** skill for migration guidance.\n\nInteract with OpenAI-compatible assistant APIs with automatic UI state management.\n\n**Import:**\n```tsx\nimport { useAssistant } from ''@ai-sdk/react'';\n```\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n```tsx\n''use client'';\nimport { useAssistant } from ''@ai-sdk/react'';\nimport { useState, FormEvent } from ''react'';\n\nexport default function AssistantChat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, error } = useAssistant({\n    api: ''/api/assistant'',\n  });\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('''');\n\n  const handleSubmit = (e: FormEvent) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    sendMessage({ content: input });\n    setInput('''');\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map(m => (\n        <div key={m.id}>\n          <strong>{m.role}:</strong> {m.content}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)}\n          disabled={isLoading}\n        />\n      </form>\n      {error && <div>{error.message}</div>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Building OpenAI Assistant-powered UIs\n- Managing assistant threads and runs\n- Streaming assistant responses with UI state management\n- File search and code interpreter integrations\n\nSee official docs for complete API reference: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/reference/ai-sdk-ui/use-assistant\n\n---\n\n## Top UI Errors & Solutions\n\nSee `references/top-ui-errors.md` for complete documentation. Quick reference:\n\n### 1. useChat Failed to Parse Stream\n\n**Error**: `SyntaxError: Unexpected token in JSON at position X`\n\n**Cause**: API route not returning proper stream format.\n\n**Solution**:\n```typescript\n// ✅ CORRECT\nreturn result.toDataStreamResponse();\n\n// ❌ WRONG\nreturn new Response(result.textStream);\n```\n\n### 2. useChat No Response\n\n**Cause**: API route not streaming correctly.\n\n**Solution**:\n```typescript\n// App Router - use toDataStreamResponse()\nexport async function POST(req: Request) {\n  const result = streamText({ /* ... */ });\n  return result.toDataStreamResponse(); // ✅\n}\n\n// Pages Router - use pipeDataStreamToResponse()\nexport default async function handler(req, res) {\n  const result = streamText({ /* ... */ });\n  return result.pipeDataStreamToResponse(res); // ✅\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Streaming Not Working When Deployed\n\n**Cause**: Deployment platform buffering responses.\n\n**Solution**: Vercel auto-detects streaming. Other platforms may need configuration.\n\n### 4. Stale Body Values with useChat\n\n**Cause**: `body` option captured at first render only.\n\n**Solution**:\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - body captured once\nconst { userId } = useUser();\nconst { messages } = useChat({\n  body: { userId },  // Stale!\n});\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - use controlled mode\nconst { userId } = useUser();\nconst { messages, sendMessage } = useChat();\n\nsendMessage({\n  content: input,\n  data: { userId },  // Fresh on each send\n});\n```\n\n### 5. React Maximum Update Depth\n\n**Cause**: Infinite loop in useEffect.\n\n**Solution**:\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG\nuseEffect(() => {\n  saveMessages(messages);\n}, [messages, saveMessages]); // saveMessages triggers re-render!\n\n// ✅ CORRECT\nuseEffect(() => {\n  saveMessages(messages);\n}, [messages]); // Only depend on messages\n```\n\nSee `references/top-ui-errors.md` for 13 more common errors (18 total documented).\n\n---\n\n## Streaming Best Practices\n\n### Performance\n\n**Always use streaming for better UX:**\n```tsx\n// ✅ GOOD - Streaming (shows tokens as they arrive)\nconst { messages } = useChat({ api: ''/api/chat'' });\n\n// ❌ BAD - Non-streaming (user waits for full response)\nconst response = await fetch(''/api/chat'', { method: ''POST'' });\n```\n\n### UX Patterns\n\n**Show loading states:**\n```tsx\n{isLoading && <div>AI is typing...</div>}\n```\n\n**Provide stop button:**\n```tsx\n{isLoading && <button onClick={stop}>Stop</button>}\n```\n\n**Auto-scroll to latest message:**\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  messagesEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: ''smooth'' });\n}, [messages]);\n```\n\n**Disable input while loading:**\n```tsx\n<input disabled={isLoading} />\n```\n\nSee `references/streaming-patterns.md` for comprehensive best practices.\n\n---\n\n## React Strict Mode Considerations\n\nReact Strict Mode intentionally double-invokes effects to catch bugs. When using `useChat` or `useCompletion` in effects (auto-resume, initial messages), guard against double execution to prevent duplicate API calls and token waste.\n\n**Problem:**\n```tsx\n''use client'';\nimport { useChat } from ''@ai-sdk/react'';\nimport { useEffect } from ''react'';\n\nexport default function Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, resumeStream } = useChat({\n    api: ''/api/chat'',\n    resume: true,\n  });\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // ❌ Triggers twice in strict mode → two concurrent streams\n    sendMessage({ content: ''Hello'' });\n    // or\n    resumeStream();\n  }, []);\n}\n```\n\n**Solution:**\n```tsx\n// ✅ Use ref to track execution\nimport { useRef } from ''react'';\n\nconst hasSentRef = useRef(false);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (hasSentRef.current) return;\n  hasSentRef.current = true;\n\n  sendMessage({ content: ''Hello'' });\n}, []);\n\n// For resumeStream specifically:\nconst hasResumedRef = useRef(false);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!autoResume || hasResumedRef.current || status === ''streaming'') return;\n  hasResumedRef.current = true;\n  resumeStream();\n}, [autoResume, resumeStream, status]);\n```\n\n**Why It Happens:** React Strict Mode double-invokes effects to surface side effects. The SDK doesn''t guard against concurrent requests, so both invocations create separate streams that fight for state updates.\n\n**Impact:** Duplicate messages, doubled token usage, race conditions causing TypeError: \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading ''state'')\".\n\n**Source:** [GitHub Issue #7891](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/7891), [Issue #6166](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/6166)\n\n---\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n### Use ai-sdk-ui When:\n- Building React chat interfaces\n- Implementing AI completions in UI\n- Streaming AI responses to frontend\n- Building Next.js AI applications\n- Handling chat message state\n- Displaying tool calls in UI\n- Managing file attachments with AI\n- Migrating from v4 to v5 (UI hooks)\n- Encountering useChat/useCompletion errors\n\n### Don''t Use When:\n- Need backend AI functionality → Use **ai-sdk-core** instead\n- Building non-React frontends (Svelte, Vue) → Check official docs\n- Need Generative UI / RSC → See https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-rsc\n- Building native apps → Different SDK required\n\n### Related Skills:\n- **ai-sdk-core** - Backend text generation, structured output, tools, agents\n- Compose both for full-stack AI applications\n\n---\n\n## Package Versions\n\n**Stable (v6 - Recommended):**\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"ai\": \"^6.0.8\",\n    \"@ai-sdk/react\": \"^3.0.6\",\n    \"@ai-sdk/openai\": \"^3.0.2\",\n    \"react\": \"^18.3.0\",\n    \"zod\": \"^3.24.2\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Legacy (v5):**\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"ai\": \"^5.0.99\",\n    \"@ai-sdk/react\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"@ai-sdk/openai\": \"^2.0.68\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Version Notes:**\n- AI SDK v6.0.6 (stable, Jan 2026) - recommended for new projects\n- AI SDK v5.x (legacy) - still supported but not receiving new features\n- React 18.3+ / React 19 supported\n- Next.js 14+/15+ recommended\n- Zod 3.24.2+ for schema validation\n\n---\n\n## Links to Official Documentation\n\n**Core UI Hooks:**\n- AI SDK UI Overview: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/overview\n- useChat: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/chatbot\n- useCompletion: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/completion\n- useObject: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/object-generation\n\n**Advanced Topics (Link Only):**\n- Generative UI (RSC): https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-rsc/overview\n- Stream Protocols: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/stream-protocols\n- Message Metadata: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/message-metadata\n\n**Next.js Integration:**\n- Next.js App Router: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/getting-started/nextjs-app-router\n- Next.js Pages Router: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/getting-started/nextjs-pages-router\n\n**Migration & Troubleshooting:**\n- v4→v5 Migration: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/migration-guides/migration-guide-5-0\n- Troubleshooting: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/troubleshooting\n- Common Issues: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/troubleshooting/common-issues\n\n**Vercel Deployment:**\n- Vercel Functions: https://vercel.com/docs/functions\n- Streaming on Vercel: https://vercel.com/docs/functions/streaming\n\n---\n\n## Templates\n\nThis skill includes the following templates in `templates/`:\n\n1. **use-chat-basic.tsx** - Basic chat with manual input (v5 pattern)\n2. **use-chat-tools.tsx** - Chat with tool calling UI rendering\n3. **use-chat-attachments.tsx** - File attachments support\n4. **use-completion-basic.tsx** - Basic text completion\n5. **use-object-streaming.tsx** - Streaming structured data\n6. **nextjs-chat-app-router.tsx** - Next.js App Router complete example\n7. **nextjs-chat-pages-router.tsx** - Next.js Pages Router complete example\n8. **nextjs-api-route.ts** - API route for both App and Pages Router\n9. **message-persistence.tsx** - Save/load chat history\n10. **custom-message-renderer.tsx** - Custom message components with markdown\n11. **package.json** - Dependencies template\n\n## Reference Documents\n\nSee `references/` for:\n\n- **use-chat-migration.md** - Complete v4→v5 migration guide\n- **streaming-patterns.md** - UI streaming best practices\n- **top-ui-errors.md** - 18 common UI errors with solutions\n- **nextjs-integration.md** - Next.js setup patterns\n- **links-to-official-docs.md** - Organized links to official docs\n\n---\n\n**Production Tested**: WordPress Auditor (https://wordpress-auditor.webfonts.workers.dev)\n**Last verified**: 2026-01-20 | **Skill version**: 3.1.0 | **Changes**: Updated to AI SDK v6.0.42 (+19 patches). Added React Strict Mode section. Expanded Issue #7 (stale body) with 3 workarounds. Added 6 new issues: TypeError with resume+onFinish (#13), concurrent sendMessage state corruption (#14), tool approval callback edge case (#15), ZodError on early stop (#16), convertToModelMessages tool approval bug (#17), undefined id infinite loop (#18). Error count: 12→18.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:49:33.150Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing advanced AI-powered user interface components with React and Vercel AI SDK integration.","zh":"非常适合需要高级AI驱动用户界面组件的前端代理，特别是那些需要与React和Vercel AI SDK集成的代理。","ja":"ReactおよびVercel AI SDKの統合が必要な高度なAI駆動のユーザーインターフェイスコンポーネントを必要とするフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。","ko":"리액트와 버셀 AI SDK 통합이 필요한 고급 AI 구동 사용자 인터페이스 구성 요소를 필요로 하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan componentes de interfaz de usuario avanzados con tecnología de inteligencia artificial integrados con React y SDK de Vercel AI.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin de composants d''interface utilisateur avancés avec technologie d''intelligence artificielle intégrés à React et au SDK Vercel AI.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die erweiterte Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit KI-Technologie benötigen, die in React und Vercel AI SDK integriert sind.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de componentes de interface do usuário avançados com tecnologia de inteligência artificial, integrados ao React e ao SDK de IA da Vercel.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым требуются продвинутые компоненты интерфейса пользователя с искусственным интеллектом, интегрированные с React и SDK ИИ Vercel.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية الذي يحتاج إلى مكونات متقدمة مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي مع تكنولوجيا React و SDK Vercel الاصطناعي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build intuitive AI-driven interfaces using React hooks, leveraging Vercel AI SDK v6 for seamless integration with Next.js and OpenAI APIs, while handling message parts structure and other UI features.","zh":"赋予代理构建直观的AI驱动界面使用React Hooks的能力，利用Vercel AI SDK v6实现与Next.js和OpenAI API的无缝集成，同时处理消息部分结构和其他UI功能。","ja":"エージェントがReact Hooksを使用して直感的なAI駆動のインターフェイスを構築する機能を提供し、Vercel AI SDK v6を使用してNext.jsおよびOpenAI APIとのシームレスな統合を実現し、メッセージパーツ構造やその他のUI機能を処理します。","ko":"리액트 훅을 사용하여 직관적인 AI 구동 인터페이스를 구축할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 제공하며, 버셀 AI SDK v6를 사용하여 넥스트 자스 및 오픈 AI API와의无缝한 통합을 구현하고, 메시지 부분 구조 및 기타 UI 기능을 처리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear interfaces intuitivas impulsadas por inteligencia artificial utilizando ganchos de React, aprovechando el SDK de Vercel AI v6 para una integración fluida con Next.js y las API de OpenAI, mientras maneja la estructura de partes de mensaje y otras características de la interfaz de usuario.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces intuitives alimentées par l''intelligence artificielle en utilisant des crochets React, en exploitant le SDK Vercel AI v6 pour une intégration fluide avec Next.js et les API OpenAI, tout en gérant la structure des parties de message et d''autres fonctionnalités de l''interface utilisateur.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, intuitive künstliche Intelligenz-getriebene Schnittstellen mit React-Hooks zu erstellen, indem es das Vercel AI SDK v6 für eine nahtlose Integration mit Next.js und OpenAI-APIs nutzt, während es die Nachrichtenteilstruktur und andere Benutzeroberflächenfunktionen handhabt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir interfaces intuitivas impulsionadas por IA, usando ganchos do React, aproveitando o SDK de IA da Vercel v6 para integração perfeita com Next.js e APIs do OpenAI, além de lidar com a estrutura de partes de mensagem e outros recursos de interface do usuário.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать интуитивно понятные интерфейсы, работающие на основе ИИ, с использованием крючков React, а также использует SDK ИИ Vercel v6 для бесшовной интеграции с Next.js и API OpenAI, обрабатывая структуру составных частей сообщения и другие функции интерфейса пользователя.","ar":"تمكين العميل من بناء واجهات مستخدم مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي باستخدام hooks من React، وتحقيق تكامل مثالي مع Next.js وواجهات برمجة التطبيقات OpenAI باستخدام SDK Vercel v6، بالإضافة إلى التعامل مع هيكل أجزاء الرسائل وغيرها من ميزات واجهة المستخدم."},"useCases":{"en":["Building AI-powered chat interfaces with message parts structure"," Integrating OpenAI APIs into React applications using @ai-sdk/openai","Migrating from AI SDK v5 to v6 with minimal breaking changes"],"zh":["构建具有消息部分结构的AI驱动聊天界面","使用@ai-sdk/openai将OpenAI API集成到React应用程序中","从AI SDK v5迁移到v6，尽量减少破坏性更改"],"ja":["メッセージパーツ構造を備えたAI駆動のチャットインターフェイスを構築する","@ai-sdk/openaiを使用してOpenAI APIをReactアプリケーションに統合する","AI SDK v5からv6への移行を実施し、破壊的な変更を最小限に抑える"],"ko":["메시지 부분 구조를 갖춘 AI 구동 채팅 인터페이스를 구축","@ai-sdk/openai를 사용하여 오픈 AI API를 리액트 애플리케이션에 통합","AI SDK v5에서 v6로 마이그레이션을 수행하여 破壊적인 변경을 최소화"],"es":["Creación de interfaces de chat impulsadas por inteligencia artificial con estructura de partes de mensaje","Integración de API de OpenAI en aplicaciones React con @ai-sdk/openai","Migración de AI SDK v5 a v6 con cambios mínimos de ruptura"],"fr":["Création d''interfaces de chat alimentées par l''intelligence artificielle avec structure de parties de message","Intégration des API OpenAI dans les applications React avec @ai-sdk/openai","Migration du SDK AI v5 à v6 avec des changements de rupture minimaux"],"de":["Erstellung von künstlicher Intelligenz-getriebenen Chat-Schnittstellen mit Nachrichtenteilstruktur","Integration von OpenAI-APIs in React-Anwendungen mit @ai-sdk/openai","Migration von AI SDK v5 zu v6 mit minimalen Umbauten"],"pt":["Construir interfaces de chat impulsionadas por IA com estrutura de partes de mensagem","Integrar APIs do OpenAI em aplicações React usando @ai-sdk/openai","Migrar do SDK de IA v5 para v6 com alterações mínimas de quebra"],"ru":["Создание интерфейсов чата на основе ИИ со структурой составных частей сообщения","Интеграция API OpenAI в приложения React с использованием @ai-sdk/openai","Миграция с SDK ИИ v5 на v6 с минимальными изменениями, нарушающими работу"],"ar":["بناء واجهات دردشة مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي مع هيكل أجزاء الرسائل","دمج واجهات برمجة التطبيقات OpenAI في تطبيقات React باستخدام @ai-sdk/openai","الانتقال من SDK الذكاء الاصطناعي v5 إلى v6 مع تغييرات كسرية قليلة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React 18+/19 and Next.js 14+/15+","Compatible with Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42 and @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"],"zh":["需要React 18+/19和Next.js 14+/15+","兼容Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42和@ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"],"ja":["React 18+/19およびNext.js 14+/15+が必要","Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42および@ai-sdk/react@3.0.44と互換性がある"],"ko":["리액트 18+/19 및 넥스트 자스 14+/15+가 필요","버셀 AI SDK v6.0.42 및 @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44와 호환"],"es":["Requiere React 18+/19 y Next.js 14+/15+","Compatible con Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42 y @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"],"fr":["Nécessite React 18+/19 et Next.js 14+/15+","Compatible avec le SDK Vercel AI v6.0.42 et @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"],"de":["Benötigt React 18+/19 und Next.js 14+/15+","Kompatibel mit Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42 und @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"],"pt":["Exige React 18+/19 e Next.js 14+/15+","Compatível com Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42 e @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"],"ru":["Требует React 18+/19 и Next.js 14+/15+","Совместим с Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42 и @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"],"ar":["يتطلب React 18+/19 و Next.js 14+/15+","متوافق مع Vercel AI SDK v6.0.42 و @ai-sdk/react@3.0.44"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/frontend-code-review', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'frontend-code-review', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z', '2026-02-18T13:49:08.960Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/frontend-code-review","name":"frontend-code-review","description":{"zh":"前端代码审查工具支持两种审查模式，帮助开发者确保代码质量","ja":"フロントエンドコードレビューツールは、2つのレビューモードをサポートしてコードの品質を確保する","ko":"프론트엔드 코드 리뷰 도구는 두 가지 리뷰 모드를 지원하여 코드 품질을 보장합니다","es":"La revisión de código frontend es una herramienta que inspecta y analiza el código para detectar violaciones y mejorar la calidad","fr":"La révision de code frontend est un outil qui inspecte et analyse le code pour détecter les violations et améliorer la qualité","de":"Die Frontend-Code-Überprüfung ist ein Tool, das den Code überprüft und analysiert, um Verletzungen zu erkennen und die Qualität zu verbessern","pt":"A revisão de código frontend é um processo que ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código. Nossa ferramenta oferece duas modalidades de revisão.","ru":"Проверка кода фронтенда - это процесс, который помогает обеспечить качество кода. Наша утилита предлагает два режима проверки.","ar":"مراجعة كود الجبهة هي عملية تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود. تُقدم أداتنا وضعين لمراجعة الكود.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"前端代码审查工具","ja":"フロントエンドコードレビューツール","ko":"프론트엔드 코드 리뷰 도구","es":"Revisión de código frontend","fr":"Révision de code frontend","de":"Frontend-Code-Überprüfung","pt":"Revisão de Código Frontend","ru":"Проверка Кодa Фронтенда","ar":"مراجعة كود الجبهة","en":"frontend-code-review"},"description":{"zh":"前端代码审查工具支持两种审查模式，帮助开发者确保代码质量","ja":"フロントエンドコードレビューツールは、2つのレビューモードをサポートしてコードの品質を確保する","ko":"프론트엔드 코드 리뷰 도구는 두 가지 리뷰 모드를 지원하여 코드 품질을 보장합니다","es":"La revisión de código frontend es una herramienta que inspecta y analiza el código para detectar violaciones y mejorar la calidad","fr":"La révision de code frontend est un outil qui inspecte et analyse le code pour détecter les violations et améliorer la qualité","de":"Die Frontend-Code-Überprüfung ist ein Tool, das den Code überprüft und analysiert, um Verletzungen zu erkennen und die Qualität zu verbessern","pt":"A revisão de código frontend é um processo que ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código. Nossa ferramenta oferece duas modalidades de revisão.","ru":"Проверка кода фронтенда - это процесс, который помогает обеспечить качество кода. Наша утилита предлагает два режима проверки.","ar":"مراجعة كود الجبهة هي عملية تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود. تُقدم أداتنا وضعين لمراجعة الكود.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持pending-change review和file-targeted review两种模式","自动检查代码中的常见问题","支持.tsx、.ts和.js文件","实时反馈代码质量问题","提高代码审查效率"],"ja":["pending-change reviewとfile-targeted reviewの2つのモードをサポート","コード内の一般的な問題を自動でチェック",".tsx、.ts、.jsファイルをサポート","コード品質の問題をリアルタイムでフィードバック","コードレビューの効率を向上"],"ko":["pending-change review와 file-targeted review 두 가지 모드 지원","코드 내의 일반적인 문제 자동 확인",".tsx, .ts, .js 파일 지원","코드 품질 문제 실시간 피드백","코드 리뷰 효율성 향상"],"es":["Revisión de código pendiente de cambios","Revisión de archivos específicos","Detección de violaciones de checklist","Análisis de calidad de código","Soporte para archivos .tsx, .ts y .js"],"fr":["Révision de code en attente de modifications","Révision de fichiers spécifiques","Détection de violations de checklist","Analyse de la qualité du code","Prise en charge des fichiers .tsx, .ts et .js"],"de":["Überprüfung von Code mit bevorstehenden Änderungen","Überprüfung von bestimmten Dateien","Erkennung von Verletzungen von Checklist","Analyse der Code-Qualität","Unterstützung für Dateien .tsx, .ts und .js"],"pt":["Revisão de código em diferentes modos","Verificação de violações de checklist","Análise de arquivos específicos","Suporte a arquivos .tsx, .ts e .js","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Проверка кода в разных режимах","Проверка нарушений чек-листа","Анализ конкретных файлов","Поддержка файлов .tsx, .ts и .js","Улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["مراجعة كود في وضعين مختلفين","تحقق من انتهاكات قائمة التحقق","تحليل الملفات المحددة","دعم الملفات .tsx و .ts و .js","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["前端代码审查","代码质量","自动化代码审查","pending-change review","file-targeted review","tsx","ts","js"],"ja":["フロントエンドコードレビュー","コード品質","自動コードレビュー","pending-change review","file-targeted review","tsx","ts","js"],"ko":["프론트엔드 코드 리뷰","코드 품질","自动화 코드 리뷰","pending-change review","file-targeted review","tsx","ts","js"],"es":["revisión de código frontend","análisis de código","calidad de código","checklist de código","frontend development","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["révision de code frontend","analyse de code","qualité de code","checklist de code","développement frontend","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Frontend-Code-Überprüfung","Code-Analyse","Code-Qualität","Checklist für Code","Frontend-Entwicklung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["revisão de código frontend","desenvolvimento web","qualidade de código","padrões de código","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","melhoria de código"],"ru":["проверка кода фронтенда","веб-разработка","качество кода","стандарты кода","инструменты разработки","улучшение кода"],"ar":["مراجعة كود الجبهة","تطوير الويب","جودة الكود","معايير الكود","أدوات التطوير","تحسين الكود"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-code-review","description":"Trigger when the user requests a review of frontend files (e.g., `.tsx`, `.ts`, `.js`). Support both pending-change reviews and focused file reviews while applying the checklist rules.","bodyPreview":"# Frontend Code Review\n\n## Intent\nUse this skill whenever the user asks to review frontend code (especially `.tsx`, `.ts`, or `.js` files). Support two review modes:\n\n1. **Pending-change review** – inspect staged/working-tree files slated for commit and flag checklist violations before submission.\n2. **File-targeted review** – review the specific file(s) the user names and report the relevant checklist findings.\n\nStick to the checklist below for every applicable file and mode.\n\n## Checklist\nSee","body":"# Frontend Code Review\n\n## Intent\nUse this skill whenever the user asks to review frontend code (especially `.tsx`, `.ts`, or `.js` files). Support two review modes:\n\n1. **Pending-change review** – inspect staged/working-tree files slated for commit and flag checklist violations before submission.\n2. **File-targeted review** – review the specific file(s) the user names and report the relevant checklist findings.\n\nStick to the checklist below for every applicable file and mode.\n\n## Checklist\nSee [references/code-quality.md](references/code-quality.md), [references/performance.md](references/performance.md), [references/business-logic.md](references/business-logic.md) for the living checklist split by category—treat it as the canonical set of rules to follow.\n\nFlag each rule violation with urgency metadata so future reviewers can prioritize fixes.\n\n## Review Process\n1. Open the relevant component/module. Gather lines that relate to class names, React Flow hooks, prop memoization, and styling.\n2. For each rule in the review point, note where the code deviates and capture a representative snippet.\n3. Compose the review section per the template below. Group violations first by **Urgent** flag, then by category order (Code Quality, Performance, Business Logic).\n\n## Required output\nWhen invoked, the response must exactly follow one of the two templates:\n\n### Template A (any findings)\n```\n# Code review\nFound <N> urgent issues need to be fixed:\n\n## 1 <brief description of bug>\nFilePath: <path> line <line>\n<relevant code snippet or pointer>\n\n\n### Suggested fix\n<brief description of suggested fix>\n\n---\n... (repeat for each urgent issue) ...\n\nFound <M> suggestions for improvement:\n\n## 1 <brief description of suggestion>\nFilePath: <path> line <line>\n<relevant code snippet or pointer>\n\n\n### Suggested fix\n<brief description of suggested fix>\n\n---\n\n... (repeat for each suggestion) ...\n```\n\nIf there are no urgent issues, omit that section. If there are no suggestions, omit that section.\n\nIf the issue number is more than 10, summarize as \"10+ urgent issues\" or \"10+ suggestions\" and just output the first 10 issues.\n\nDon''t compress the blank lines between sections; keep them as-is for readability.\n\nIf you use Template A (i.e., there are issues to fix) and at least one issue requires code changes, append a brief follow-up question after the structured output asking whether the user wants you to apply the suggested fix(es). For example: \"Would you like me to use the Suggested fix section to address these issues?\"\n\n### Template B (no issues)\n```\n## Code review\nNo issues found.\n```\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:49:08.960Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents specializing in frontend development with expertise in .tsx, .ts, and .js files","zh":"适用于专门从事前端开发的代码审查代理，尤其是精通 .tsx、.ts 和 .js 文件","ja":"フロントエンド開発を専門とするコードレビュー代理に適しています。特に、.tsx、.ts、.js ファイルを専門としています","ko":"프론트엔드 개발을 전문으로 하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 특히 .tsx, .ts, .js 파일에 전문적인 지식을 갖추고 있습니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que se especializan en desarrollo frontend con experiencia en archivos .tsx, .ts y .js","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code spécialisés dans le développement frontend avec une expertise dans les fichiers .tsx, .ts et .js","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agenten, die sich auf Frontend-Entwicklung mit Erfahrung in .tsx-, .ts- und .js-Dateien spezialisieren","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código especializados em desenvolvimento frontend com especialização em arquivos .tsx, .ts e .js","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-ревьюеров кода, специализирующихся на разработке frontend с опытом работы с файлами .tsx, .ts и .js","ar":"مثالي لويكلاء مراجعة الكود المتخصصين في تطوير الواجهة الأمامية مع الخبرة في ملفات .tsx و .ts و .js"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to inspect staged or specific frontend code files, flagging checklist violations before submission, and supporting both pending-change review and file-targeted review modes with precise feedback on .tsx, .ts, or .js files","zh":"赋予代理检查暂存或特定前端代码文件的能力，提交前标记清单违规，并支持待更改审查和文件目标审查模式，对 .tsx、.ts 或 .js 文件提供精确的反馈","ja":"エージェントがステージングされたフロントエンドコードファイルまたは特定のファイルを検査する機能を提供し、チェックリストの違反をフラグし、変更待ちのレビューとファイル対象のレビューモードをサポートし、.tsx、.ts、または .js ファイルに対して正確なフィードバックを提供する","ko":"에이전트가 暫存된 프론트엔드 코드 파일 또는 특정 파일을 검사하도록 허용하고, 제출 전 체크리스트 위반을 표시하며, 변경 대기 리뷰 및 파일 대상 리뷰 모드를 지원하며, .tsx, .ts 또는 .js 파일에 대한 정확한 피드백을 제공합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a inspeccionar archivos de código frontend puestos en escena o específicos, señalizando violaciones de la lista de verificación antes de la presentación, y soportando tanto el modo de revisión de cambios pendientes como el modo de revisión dirigida a archivos con comentarios precisos sobre archivos .tsx, .ts o .js","fr":"Permet aux agents d''inspecter des fichiers de code frontend mis en scène ou spécifiques, en signalant les violations de la liste de vérification avant la soumission, et en prenant en charge à la fois le mode de révision des modifications en attente et le mode de révision ciblée sur les fichiers avec des commentaires précis sur les fichiers .tsx, .ts ou .js","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, gestaffelten oder spezifischen Frontend-Code-Dateien zu untersuchen, Checklist-Verstöße vor der Einreichung zu kennzeichnen und sowohl den Warteschleifen-Review-Modus als auch den dateizielgerichteten Review-Modus mit präzisen Feedback zu .tsx-, .ts- oder .js-Dateien zu unterstützen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a inspecionar os arquivos de código frontend em estágio ou específicos, sinalizando violações de checklist antes da submissão, e suporta ambos os modos de revisão de alterações pendentes e revisão direcionada a arquivos com feedback preciso sobre arquivos .tsx, .ts ou .js","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять файлы frontend-кода на стадии или конкретные файлы, флагируя нарушения чек-листа до отправки, и поддерживает как режим проверки изменений, так и режим целенаправленной проверки файлов с точной обратной связью по файлам .tsx, .ts или .js","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من فحص ملفات كود الواجهة الأمامية الموضعية أو المحددة، وتحديد انتهاكات قائمة التحقق قبل الارسال، ودعم كلاً من طريقة مراجعة التغييرات المعلقة وطريقة المراجعة المستهدفة للملفات مع ملاحظات دقيقة حول ملفات .tsx و .ts و .js"},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing staged frontend code changes for checklist compliance","Inspecting specific .tsx, .ts, or .js files for adherence to coding standards","Flagging potential issues in frontend code before commit"],"zh":["审查暂存的前端代码更改以确保符合清单","检查特定的 .tsx、.ts 或 .js 文件以确保遵守编码标准","在提交前标记前端代码中的潜在问题"],"ja":["チェックリストへの準拠を確保するためにステージングされたフロントエンドコードの変更をレビューする","特定の .tsx、.ts、または .js ファイルをレビューしてコーディング規約への準拠を確認する","コミット前にフロントエンドコード内の潜在的な問題をフラグする"],"ko":["체크리스트 준수를 확인하기 위해 暫存된 프론트엔드 코드 변경을 리뷰하는 것","특정 .tsx, .ts 또는 .js 파일을 리뷰하여 코딩 표준 준수를 확인하는 것","커밋 전 프론트엔드 코드의 잠재적인 문제를 표시하는 것"],"es":["Revisar los cambios de código frontend puestos en escena para la conformidad con la lista de verificación","Inspeccionar archivos .tsx, .ts o .js específicos para la adherencia a los estándares de codificación","Señalarizar posibles problemas en el código frontend antes del compromiso"],"fr":["Réviser les modifications de code frontend mises en scène pour la conformité à la liste de vérification","Inspecter des fichiers .tsx, .ts ou .js spécifiques pour l''adhésion aux normes de codage","Signaler les problèmes potentiels dans le code frontend avant l''engagement"],"de":["Überprüfen der gestaffelten Frontend-Code-Änderungen auf die Konformität mit der Checklist","Untersuchen spezifischer .tsx-, .ts- oder .js-Dateien auf die Einhaltung der Codierungsstandards","Kennzeichnen von potenziellen Problemen im Frontend-Code vor dem Commit"],"pt":["Revisar alterações de código frontend em estágio para cumprimento do checklist","Inspecionar arquivos .tsx, .ts ou .js específicos para aderência aos padrões de codificação","Sinalizar problemas potenciais no código frontend antes do commit"],"ru":["Проверка изменений frontend-кода на стадии на соответствие чек-листу","Проверка конкретных файлов .tsx, .ts или .js на соответствие стандартам кодирования","Выявление потенциальных проблем в frontend-коде до фиксации"],"ar":["مراجعة تغييرات كود الواجهة الأمامية الموضعية لامتثال قائمة التحقق","فحص ملفات .tsx أو .ts أو .js المحددة لامتثال لمعايير البرمجة","تحديد المشاكل المحتملة في كود الواجهة الأمامية قبل الالتزام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Limited to frontend code review","Requires access to staged or specific files for review","Supports .tsx, .ts, and .js file formats"],"zh":["仅限于前端代码审查","需要访问暂存或特定文件进行审查","支持 .tsx、.ts 和 .js 文件格式"],"ja":["フロントエンドコードのレビューのみに限定されている","レビューするためにステージングされたファイルまたは特定のファイルへのアクセスが必要",".tsx、.ts、.js ファイル形式をサポート"],"ko":["프론트엔드 코드 리뷰에만 제한됨","리뷰를 위해 暫存된 파일 또는 특정 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요함",".tsx, .ts, .js 파일 형식만 지원"],"es":["Limitado a la revisión de código frontend","Requiere acceso a archivos puestos en escena o específicos para la revisión","Soporta formatos de archivo .tsx, .ts y .js"],"fr":["Limité à la révision de code frontend","Nécessite l''accès à des fichiers mis en scène ou spécifiques pour la révision","Prend en charge les formats de fichiers .tsx, .ts et .js"],"de":["Begrenzt auf die Code-Review von Frontend-Code","Benötigt den Zugriff auf gestaffelte oder spezifische Dateien für die Überprüfung","Unterstützt .tsx-, .ts- und .js-Dateiformate"],"pt":["Limitado à revisão de código frontend","Requer acesso a arquivos em estágio ou específicos para revisão","Suporta formatos de arquivo .tsx, .ts e .js"],"ru":["Ограничен проверкой frontend-кода","Требует доступа к файлам на стадии или конкретным файлам для проверки","Поддерживает форматы файлов .tsx, .ts и .js"],"ar":["محدود بمراجعة كود الواجهة الأمامية","يتطلب الوصول إلى الملفات الموضعية أو المحددة لمراجعتها","يدعم صيغ ملفات .tsx و .ts و .js"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/signup-flow-cro', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'signup-flow-cro', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z', '2026-02-18T13:50:07.130Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/signup-flow-cro","name":"signup-flow-cro","description":{"zh":"signup-flow-cro ","ja":"signup ","ko":"signup ","es":"El flujo de registro es crucial para el éxito de una aplicación. Nuestro experto en CRO ayuda a optimizar este proceso","fr":"Le flux d''inscription est crucial pour le succès d''une application. Notre expert en CRO aide à optimiser ce processus","de":"Der Registrierungsfluss ist entscheidend für den Erfolg einer Anwendung. Unser CRO-Experte hilft bei der Optimierung dieses Prozesses","pt":"Otimização do fluxo de cadastro para reduzir a fricção e aumentar as taxas de conclusão","ru":"Оптимизация потока регистрации для уменьшения трения и увеличения показателей завершения","ar":"تحسين تدفق التسجيل لتقليل الاحتكاك وزيادة معدلات الإكمال","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"signup-flow-cro ","ja":"Signup ","ko":"signup ","es":"Optimización de flujos de registro","fr":"Amélioration des flux d''inscription","de":"Optimierung von Registrierungsflüssen","pt":"Otimização de Fluxo de Cadastro","ru":"Оптимизация потока регистрации","ar":"تحسين تدفق التسجيل","en":"signup-flow-cro"},"description":{"zh":"signup-flow-cro ","ja":"signup ","ko":"signup ","es":"El flujo de registro es crucial para el éxito de una aplicación. Nuestro experto en CRO ayuda a optimizar este proceso","fr":"Le flux d''inscription est crucial pour le succès d''une application. Notre expert en CRO aide à optimiser ce processus","de":"Der Registrierungsfluss ist entscheidend für den Erfolg einer Anwendung. Unser CRO-Experte hilft bei der Optimierung dieses Prozesses","pt":"Otimização do fluxo de cadastro para reduzir a fricção e aumentar as taxas de conclusão","ru":"Оптимизация потока регистрации для уменьшения трения и увеличения показателей завершения","ar":"تحسين تدفق التسجيل لتقليل الاحتكاك وزيادة معدلات الإكمال","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["1. ","2. ","3. ","4. ","5. "],"ja":["1. ","2. ","3. ","4. ","5. "],"ko":["1. ","2. ","3. ","4. ","5. "],"es":["Análisis de flujos de registro","Recomendaciones de CRO","Optimización de formularios","Redución de la fricción","Mejora de las tasas de finalización"],"fr":["Analyse des flux d''inscription","Recommandations de CRO","Optimisation des formulaires","Réduction de la friction","Amélioration des taux d''achèvement"],"de":["Analyse von Registrierungsflüssen","CRO-Empfehlungen","Optimierung von Formularen","Reduzierung der Reibung","Verbesserung der Abschlussraten"],"pt":["Análise de fluxo de cadastro","Otimização de formulários","Redução da fricção","Aumento das taxas de conclusão","Melhoria da experiência do usuário"],"ru":["Анализ потока регистрации","Оптимизация форм","Уменьшение трения","Увеличение показателей завершения","Улучшение пользовательского опыта"],"ar":["تحليل تدفق التسجيل","تحسين الاستمارة","تقليل الاحتكاك","زيادة معدلات الإكمال","تحسين تجربة المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["signup","cro","","","",""],"ja":["signup","cro","","","",""],"ko":["signup","cro","","","",""],"es":["optimización de flujos de registro","CRO","flujos de registro","registros de usuario","formularios de registro","experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["amélioration des flux d''inscription","CRO","flux d''inscription","enregistrements d''utilisateurs","formulaires d''inscription","expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Optimierung von Registrierungsflüssen","CRO","Registrierungsflüsse","Benutzerregistrierungen","Registrierungsformulare","Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["otimização de fluxo de cadastro","CRO","fluxo de cadastro","redução da fricção","aumento das taxas de conclusão","melhoria da experiência do usuário"],"ru":["оптимизация потока регистрации","CRO","поток регистрации","уменьшение трения","увеличение показателей завершения","улучшение пользовательского опыта"],"ar":["تحسين تدفق التسجيل","CRO","تدفق التسجيل","تقليل الاحتكاك","زيادة معدلات الإكمال","تحسين تجربة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"signup-flow-cro","description":"When the user wants to optimize signup, registration, account creation, or trial activation flows. Also use when the user mentions signup conversions, registration friction, signup form optimization, free trial signup, reduce signup dropoff, or account creation flow. For post-signup onboarding, see onboarding-cro. For lead capture forms (not account creation), see form-cro.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Signup Flow CRO\n\nYou are an expert in optimizing signup and registration flows. Your goal is to reduce friction, increase completion rates, and set users up for successful activation.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Flow Type**","body":"# Signup Flow CRO\n\nYou are an expert in optimizing signup and registration flows. Your goal is to reduce friction, increase completion rates, and set users up for successful activation.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Flow Type**\n   - Free trial signup\n   - Freemium account creation\n   - Paid account creation\n   - Waitlist/early access signup\n   - B2B vs B2C\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - How many steps/screens?\n   - What fields are required?\n   - What''s the current completion rate?\n   - Where do users drop off?\n\n3. **Business Constraints**\n   - What data is genuinely needed at signup?\n   - Are there compliance requirements?\n   - What happens immediately after signup?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Minimize Required Fields\nEvery field reduces conversion. For each field, ask:\n- Do we absolutely need this before they can use the product?\n- Can we collect this later through progressive profiling?\n- Can we infer this from other data?\n\n**Typical field priority:**\n- Essential: Email (or phone), Password\n- Often needed: Name\n- Usually deferrable: Company, Role, Team size, Phone, Address\n\n### 2. Show Value Before Asking for Commitment\n- What can you show/give before requiring signup?\n- Can they experience the product before creating an account?\n- Reverse the order: value first, signup second\n\n### 3. Reduce Perceived Effort\n- Show progress if multi-step\n- Group related fields\n- Use smart defaults\n- Pre-fill when possible\n\n### 4. Remove Uncertainty\n- Clear expectations (\"Takes 30 seconds\")\n- Show what happens after signup\n- No surprises (hidden requirements, unexpected steps)\n\n---\n\n## Field-by-Field Optimization\n\n### Email Field\n- Single field (no email confirmation field)\n- Inline validation for format\n- Check for common typos (gmial.com → gmail.com)\n- Clear error messages\n\n### Password Field\n- Show password toggle (eye icon)\n- Show requirements upfront, not after failure\n- Consider passphrase hints for strength\n- Update requirement indicators in real-time\n\n**Better password UX:**\n- Allow paste (don''t disable)\n- Show strength meter instead of rigid rules\n- Consider passwordless options\n\n### Name Field\n- Single \"Full name\" field vs. First/Last split (test this)\n- Only require if immediately used (personalization)\n- Consider making optional\n\n### Social Auth Options\n- Place prominently (often higher conversion than email)\n- Show most relevant options for your audience\n  - B2C: Google, Apple, Facebook\n  - B2B: Google, Microsoft, SSO\n- Clear visual separation from email signup\n- Consider \"Sign up with Google\" as primary\n\n### Phone Number\n- Defer unless essential (SMS verification, calling leads)\n- If required, explain why\n- Use proper input type with country code handling\n- Format as they type\n\n### Company/Organization\n- Defer if possible\n- Auto-suggest as they type\n- Infer from email domain when possible\n\n### Use Case / Role Questions\n- Defer to onboarding if possible\n- If needed at signup, keep to one question\n- Use progressive disclosure (don''t show all options at once)\n\n---\n\n## Single-Step vs. Multi-Step\n\n### Single-Step Works When:\n- 3 or fewer fields\n- Simple B2C products\n- High-intent visitors (from ads, waitlist)\n\n### Multi-Step Works When:\n- More than 3-4 fields needed\n- Complex B2B products needing segmentation\n- You need to collect different types of info\n\n### Multi-Step Best Practices\n- Show progress indicator\n- Lead with easy questions (name, email)\n- Put harder questions later (after psychological commitment)\n- Each step should feel completable in seconds\n- Allow back navigation\n- Save progress (don''t lose data on refresh)\n\n**Progressive commitment pattern:**\n1. Email only (lowest barrier)\n2. Password + name\n3. Customization questions (optional)\n\n---\n\n## Trust and Friction Reduction\n\n### At the Form Level\n- \"No credit card required\" (if true)\n- \"Free forever\" or \"14-day free trial\"\n- Privacy note: \"We''ll never share your email\"\n- Security badges if relevant\n- Testimonial near signup form\n\n### Error Handling\n- Inline validation (not just on submit)\n- Specific error messages (\"Email already registered\" + recovery path)\n- Don''t clear the form on error\n- Focus on the problem field\n\n### Microcopy\n- Placeholder text: Use for examples, not labels\n- Labels: Always visible (not just placeholders)\n- Help text: Only when needed, placed close to field\n\n---\n\n## Mobile Signup Optimization\n\n- Larger touch targets (44px+ height)\n- Appropriate keyboard types (email, tel, etc.)\n- Autofill support\n- Reduce typing (social auth, pre-fill)\n- Single column layout\n- Sticky CTA button\n- Test with actual devices\n\n---\n\n## Post-Submit Experience\n\n### Success State\n- Clear confirmation\n- Immediate next step\n- If email verification required:\n  - Explain what to do\n  - Easy resend option\n  - Check spam reminder\n  - Option to change email if wrong\n\n### Verification Flows\n- Consider delaying verification until necessary\n- Magic link as alternative to password\n- Let users explore while awaiting verification\n- Clear re-engagement if verification stalls\n\n---\n\n## Measurement\n\n### Key Metrics\n- Form start rate (landed → started filling)\n- Form completion rate (started → submitted)\n- Field-level drop-off (which fields lose people)\n- Time to complete\n- Error rate by field\n- Mobile vs. desktop completion\n\n### What to Track\n- Each field interaction (focus, blur, error)\n- Step progression in multi-step\n- Social auth vs. email signup ratio\n- Time between steps\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Audit Findings\nFor each issue found:\n- **Issue**: What''s wrong\n- **Impact**: Why it matters (with estimated impact if possible)\n- **Fix**: Specific recommendation\n- **Priority**: High/Medium/Low\n\n### Recommended Changes\nOrganized by:\n1. Quick wins (same-day fixes)\n2. High-impact changes (week-level effort)\n3. Test hypotheses (things to A/B test)\n\n### Form Redesign (if requested)\n- Recommended field set with rationale\n- Field order\n- Copy for labels, placeholders, buttons, errors\n- Visual layout suggestions\n\n---\n\n## Common Signup Flow Patterns\n\n### B2B SaaS Trial\n1. Email + Password (or Google auth)\n2. Name + Company (optional: role)\n3. → Onboarding flow\n\n### B2C App\n1. Google/Apple auth OR Email\n2. → Product experience\n3. Profile completion later\n\n### Waitlist/Early Access\n1. Email only\n2. Optional: Role/use case question\n3. → Waitlist confirmation\n\n### E-commerce Account\n1. Guest checkout as default\n2. Account creation optional post-purchase\n3. OR Social auth with single click\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Ideas\n\n### Form Design Experiments\n\n**Layout & Structure**\n- Single-step vs. multi-step signup flow\n- Multi-step with progress bar vs. without\n- 1-column vs. 2-column field layout\n- Form embedded on page vs. separate signup page\n- Horizontal vs. vertical field alignment\n\n**Field Optimization**\n- Reduce to minimum fields (email + password only)\n- Add or remove phone number field\n- Single \"Name\" field vs. \"First/Last\" split\n- Add or remove company/organization field\n- Test required vs. optional field balance\n\n**Authentication Options**\n- Add SSO options (Google, Microsoft, GitHub, LinkedIn)\n- SSO prominent vs. email form prominent\n- Test which SSO options resonate (varies by audience)\n- SSO-only vs. SSO + email option\n\n**Visual Design**\n- Test button colors and sizes for CTA prominence\n- Plain background vs. product-related visuals\n- Test form container styling (card vs. minimal)\n- Mobile-optimized layout testing\n\n---\n\n### Copy & Messaging Experiments\n\n**Headlines & CTAs**\n- Test headline variations above signup form\n- CTA button text: \"Create Account\" vs. \"Start Free Trial\" vs. \"Get Started\"\n- Add clarity around trial length in CTA\n- Test value proposition emphasis in form header\n\n**Microcopy**\n- Field labels: minimal vs. descriptive\n- Placeholder text optimization\n- Error message clarity and tone\n- Password requirement display (upfront vs. on error)\n\n**Trust Elements**\n- Add social proof next to signup form\n- Test trust badges near form (security, compliance)\n- Add \"No credit card required\" messaging\n- Include privacy assurance copy\n\n---\n\n### Trial & Commitment Experiments\n\n**Free Trial Variations**\n- Credit card required vs. not required for trial\n- Test trial length impact (7 vs. 14 vs. 30 days)\n- Freemium vs. free trial model\n- Trial with limited features vs. full access\n\n**Friction Points**\n- Email verification required vs. delayed vs. removed\n- Test CAPTCHA impact on completion\n- Terms acceptance checkbox vs. implicit acceptance\n- Phone verification for high-value accounts\n\n---\n\n### Post-Submit Experiments\n\n- Clear next steps messaging after signup\n- Instant product access vs. email confirmation first\n- Personalized welcome message based on signup data\n- Auto-login after signup vs. require login\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What''s your current signup completion rate?\n2. Do you have field-level analytics on drop-off?\n3. What data is absolutely required before they can use the product?\n4. Are there compliance or verification requirements?\n5. What happens immediately after signup?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **onboarding-cro**: For optimizing what happens after signup\n- **form-cro**: For non-signup forms (lead capture, contact)\n- **page-cro**: For the landing page leading to signup\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing signup flow changes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:50:07.130Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversion Rate Optimization Agents focused on streamlining user registration processes.","zh":"适合专注于简化用户注册流程的转化率优化代理","ja":"ユーザー登録プロセスの最適化に焦点を当てたコンバージョンレート最適化エージェントに最適","ko":"사용자 등록 프로세스를 최적화하는 전환률 최적화 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de optimización de la tasa de conversión centrados en optimizar los procesos de registro de usuarios.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''optimisation du taux de conversion axés sur la rationalisation des processus d''inscription des utilisateurs.","de":"Ideal für Agenten zur Optimierung der Konvertierungsrate, die sich auf die Optimierung der Benutzerregistrierungsprozesse konzentrieren.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Otimização de Taxa de Conversão focados em otimizar processos de registro de usuário.","ru":"Идеально для агентов оптимизации коэффициента конверсии, ориентированных на оптимизацию процессов регистрации пользователей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحسين معدل التحويل الذي يركز على简ification عمليات التسجيل للمستخدمين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to analyze and optimize signup flows, reducing friction and increasing completion rates through data-driven recommendations, leveraging product marketing context and understanding of flow types.","zh":"赋予代理分析和优化注册流程的能力，通过数据驱动的建议减少摩擦，提高完成率，同时利用产品营销背景和流程类型的理解","ja":"エージェントがサインアップフローを分析および最適化する機能を提供し、データドリブンの推奨事項を利用してフリクションを減らし、完了率を向上させ、製品マーケティングコンテキストとフロータイプの理解を活用","ko":"에이전트가 회원가입 흐름을 분석하고 최적화하는 기능을 제공하여 데이터 주도 추천을 통해 마찰을 줄이고 완료率를提高하며, 제품 마케팅.context와 흐름 유형에 대한 이해를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a analizar y optimizar los flujos de registro, reduciendo la fricción y aumentando las tasas de finalización a través de recomendaciones basadas en datos, aprovechando el contexto de marketing de productos y la comprensión de los tipos de flujo.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser et d''optimiser les flux d''inscription, en réduisant les frictions et en augmentant les taux d''achèvement grâce à des recommandations basées sur les données, en exploitant le contexte de marketing de produits et la compréhension des types de flux.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Registrierungsflüsse zu analysieren und zu optimieren, die Reibung zu reduzieren und die Abschlussraten durch datengetriebene Empfehlungen zu erhöhen, die den Kontext des Produktmarketings und das Verständnis der Flusetypen nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a analisar e otimizar fluxos de inscrição, reduzindo a fricção e aumentando as taxas de conclusão por meio de recomendações baseadas em dados, utilizando o contexto de marketing de produtos e compreensão dos tipos de fluxo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью анализировать и оптимизировать потоки регистрации, снижая трение и увеличивая показатели завершения благодаря рекомендациям, основанным на данных, используя контекст маркетинга продукта и понимание типов потоков.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تحليل و تحسين dòng الإشارات، وتقليل الاحتكاك وزيادة معدلات الإكمال من خلال التوصيات القائمة على البيانات، باستخدام سياق تسويق المنتجات وفهم أنواع التدفقات."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing existing signup flows for friction points","Generating recommendations for flow optimization","Evaluating the impact of flow changes on user activation rates"],"zh":["分析现有的注册流程以查找摩擦点","生成流程优化的建议","评估流程更改对用户激活率的影响"],"ja":["既存のサインアップフローを分析してフリクションポイントを探す","フロー最適化のための推奨事項を生成する","フロー変更がユーザー有効化率に与える影響を評価する"],"ko":["기존의 회원가입 흐름을 분석하여 마찰점을 찾기","흐름 최적화를 위한 추천을 생성","흐름 변경이 사용자 활성화율에 미치는 영향을 평가"],"es":["Analizar flujos de registro existentes para identificar puntos de fricción","Generar recomendaciones para la optimización de flujos","Evaluar el impacto de los cambios en los flujos en las tasas de activación de los usuarios"],"fr":["Analyser les flux d''inscription existants pour identifier les points de friction","Générer des recommandations pour l''optimisation des flux","Évaluer l''impact des modifications des flux sur les taux d''activation des utilisateurs"],"de":["Analysieren bestehender Registrierungsflüsse auf Reibungspunkte","Erstellen von Empfehlungen für die Optimierung von Flüssen","Bewerten des Einflusses von Änderungen an den Flüssen auf die Aktivierungsrate der Benutzer"],"pt":["Analisar fluxos de inscrição existentes para pontos de fricção","Gerar recomendações para otimização de fluxo","Avaliar o impacto das alterações de fluxo nas taxas de ativação do usuário"],"ru":["Анализ существующих потоков регистрации для точек трения","Генерация рекомендаций для оптимизации потока","Оценка воздействия изменений потока на показатели активации пользователей"],"ar":["تحليل التدفقات الحالية للتسجيل لنتائج الاحتكاك","توليد التوصيات لتحسين التدفق","تقييم تأثير تغييرات التدفق على معدلات تفعيل المستخدمين"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to product marketing context","Limited to signup and registration flow optimization"],"zh":["需要访问产品营销背景","仅限注册和注册流程优化"],"ja":["製品マーケティングコンテキストへのアクセスが必要","サインアップおよび登録フロー最適化のみ"],"ko":["제품 마케팅.context에 대한 액세스가 필요","회원가입 및 등록 흐름 최적화만"],"es":["Requiere acceso al contexto de marketing de productos","Limitado a la optimización de flujos de registro y registro"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au contexte de marketing de produits","Limité à l''optimisation des flux d''inscription et d''enregistrement"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf den Kontext des Produktmarketings","Begrenzt auf die Optimierung von Registrierungs- und Anmeldeflüssen"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao contexto de marketing de produtos","Limitado à otimização de fluxo de inscrição e registro"],"ru":["Требует доступа к контексту маркетинга продукта","Ограничен оптимизацией потока регистрации и оформления"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى سياق تسويق المنتجات","محدود بتحسين dòng الإشارات والتسجيل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/frontend-design', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'frontend-design', 0, 0, 25, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z', '2026-02-18T13:50:03.553Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/frontend-design","name":"frontend-design","description":{"zh":"前端设计技能指南，帮助您创建独特的生产级界面，避免通用性设计","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキルガイドは、ユニークなプロダクションレベルのインターフェースを作成し、一般的なデザインを避けるのに役立ちます","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 스킬 가이드는 독특한 프로덕션 급 인터페이스를 생성하고 일반적인 디자인을 피하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Este skill permite crear interfaces de frontend personalizadas y de alta calidad, con atención al detalle y opciones creativas","fr":"Ce skill permet de créer des interfaces de frontend sur mesure et de haute qualité, avec attention au détail et options créatives","de":"Dieser Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten und hochwertigen Frontend-Oberflächen, mit besonderer Aufmerksamkeit für Details und kreative Optionen","pt":"Este guia de habilidades ajuda a criar interfaces frontend personalizadas e de alta qualidade, evitando estéticas genéricas. Implemente códigos funcionais com atenção aos detalhes estéticos.","ru":"Этот навык помогает создать уникальные и высококачественные интерфейсы frontend, избегая общих эстетических решений. Реализуйте рабочий код с исключительным вниманием к деталям.","ar":"يساعد هذا الدليل المهاري على إنشاء واجهات مستخدم أمامية فريدة وذات جودة عالية، وتجنب الجمال العام. قم بتنفيذ شفرات تعمل مع اهتمام استثنائي بالتفاصيل الجمالية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"前端设计技能 - 创建独特的生产级界面","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキル - ユニークなプロダクションレベルのインターフェースを作成","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 스킬 - 독특한 프로덕션 급 인터페이스 생성","es":"Diseño de frontend personalizado","fr":"Conception de frontend sur mesure","de":"Benutzerdefiniertes Frontend-Design","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Interfaces Frontend Personalizadas","ru":"Разработка уникальных интерфейсов frontend","ar":"تصميم واجهات المستخدم الأمامية الفريدة","en":"frontend-design"},"description":{"zh":"前端设计技能指南，帮助您创建独特的生产级界面，避免通用性设计","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキルガイドは、ユニークなプロダクションレベルのインターフェースを作成し、一般的なデザインを避けるのに役立ちます","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 스킬 가이드는 독특한 프로덕션 급 인터페이스를 생성하고 일반적인 디자인을 피하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Este skill permite crear interfaces de frontend personalizadas y de alta calidad, con atención al detalle y opciones creativas","fr":"Ce skill permet de créer des interfaces de frontend sur mesure et de haute qualité, avec attention au détail et options créatives","de":"Dieser Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten und hochwertigen Frontend-Oberflächen, mit besonderer Aufmerksamkeit für Details und kreative ...","pt":"Este guia de habilidades ajuda a criar interfaces frontend personalizadas e de alta qualidade, evitando estéticas genéricas. Implemente códigos funcionais co...","ru":"Этот навык помогает создать уникальные и высококачественные интерфейсы frontend, избегая общих эстетических решений. Реализуйте рабочий код с исключительным ...","ar":"يساعد هذا الدليل المهاري على إنشاء واجهات مستخدم أمامية فريدة وذات جودة عالية، وتجنب الجمال العام. قم بتنفيذ شفرات تعمل مع اهتمام استثنائي بالتفاصيل الجمالية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["创建独特的生产级界面","注重美学细节和创意选择","实现设计思维和代码实现","支持多种技术约束"],"ja":["ユニークなプロダクションレベルのインターフェースを作成","美的細部と創造的な選択に焦点を当て","デザイン思考とコード実装を実現","複数の技術的制約をサポート"],"ko":["독특한 프로덕션 급 인터페이스를 생성","미적 세부 사항과 창의적인 선택에 중점을 둡니다","디자인 사고와 코드 구현을 구현","다양한 기술적 제약을 지원"],"es":["Creación de interfaces de usuario personalizadas","Atención al detalle y opciones creativas","Implementación de código de producción de alta calidad","Diseño de componentes, páginas y aplicaciones","Consideración de contexto y restricciones técnicas"],"fr":["Création d''interfaces utilisateur sur mesure","Attention au détail et options créatives","Mise en œuvre de code de production de haute qualité","Conception de composants, pages et applications","Prise en compte du contexte et des contraintes techniques"],"de":["Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Benutzeroberflächen","Besondere Aufmerksamkeit für Details und kreative Optionen","Implementierung von hochwertigem Produktionscode","Entwurf von Komponenten, Seiten und Anwendungen","Berücksichtigung von Kontext und technischen Einschränkungen"],"pt":["Criação de interfaces personalizadas","Atenção aos detalhes estéticos","Implementação de códigos funcionais","Desenvolvimento de componentes e páginas","Consideração de contextos e restrições técnicas"],"ru":["Создание уникальных интерфейсов","Внимание к деталям","Реализация рабочего кода","Разработка компонентов и страниц","Учет контекста и технических ограничений"],"ar":["إنشاء واجهات مستخدم فريدة","الاهتمام بالتفاصيل الجمالية","تنفيذ شفرات تعمل","تطوير المكونات والصفحات","مراعاة السياق والقيود الفنية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["前端设计","生产级界面","独特设计","美学细节","创意选择","设计思维","代码实现"],"ja":["フロントエンドデザイン","プロダクションレベルのインターフェース","ユニークなデザイン","美的細部","創造的な選択","デザイン思考","コード実装"],"ko":["프론트엔드 디자인","프로덕션 급 인터페이스","독특한 디자인","미적 세부 사항","창의적인 선택","디자인 사고","코드 구현"],"es":["diseño de frontend","interfaces de usuario","desarrollo web","codificación","creación de aplicaciones","diseño de componentes","experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["conception de frontend","interfaces utilisateur","développement web","codage","création d''applications","conception de composants","expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Frontend-Design","Benutzeroberflächen","Webentwicklung","Codierung","Anwendungsentwicklung","Komponenten-Design","Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento frontend","interfaces personalizadas","design de interface","desenvolvimento web","código frontend","estética de interface"],"ru":["разработка frontend","уникальные интерфейсы","дизайн интерфейса","веб-разработка","коды frontend","эстетика интерфейса"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات المستخدم الأمامية","واجهات مستخدم فريدة","تصميم الواجهة","تطوير الويب","شفرات الأمامية","جمال واجهة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-design","description":"Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality. Use this skill when the user asks to build web components, pages, artifacts, posters, or applications (examples include websites, landing pages, dashboards, React components, HTML/CSS layouts, or when styling/beautifying any web UI). Generates creative, polished code and UI design that avoids generic AI aesthetics.","bodyPreview":"This skill guides creation of distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces that avoid generic \"AI slop\" aesthetics. Implement real working code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details and creative choices.\n\nThe user provides frontend requirements: a component, page, application, or interface to build. They may include context about the purpose, audience, or technical constraints.\n\n## Design Thinking\n\nBefore coding, understand the context and commit to a BOLD aesthetic direction:\n- *","body":"This skill guides creation of distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces that avoid generic \"AI slop\" aesthetics. Implement real working code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details and creative choices.\n\nThe user provides frontend requirements: a component, page, application, or interface to build. They may include context about the purpose, audience, or technical constraints.\n\n## Design Thinking\n\nBefore coding, understand the context and commit to a BOLD aesthetic direction:\n- **Purpose**: What problem does this interface solve? Who uses it?\n- **Tone**: Pick an extreme: brutally minimal, maximalist chaos, retro-futuristic, organic/natural, luxury/refined, playful/toy-like, editorial/magazine, brutalist/raw, art deco/geometric, soft/pastel, industrial/utilitarian, etc. There are so many flavors to choose from. Use these for inspiration but design one that is true to the aesthetic direction.\n- **Constraints**: Technical requirements (framework, performance, accessibility).\n- **Differentiation**: What makes this UNFORGETTABLE? What''s the one thing someone will remember?\n\n**CRITICAL**: Choose a clear conceptual direction and execute it with precision. Bold maximalism and refined minimalism both work - the key is intentionality, not intensity.\n\nThen implement working code (HTML/CSS/JS, React, Vue, etc.) that is:\n- Production-grade and functional\n- Visually striking and memorable\n- Cohesive with a clear aesthetic point-of-view\n- Meticulously refined in every detail\n\n## Frontend Aesthetics Guidelines\n\nFocus on:\n- **Typography**: Choose fonts that are beautiful, unique, and interesting. Avoid generic fonts like Arial and Inter; opt instead for distinctive choices that elevate the frontend''s aesthetics; unexpected, characterful font choices. Pair a distinctive display font with a refined body font.\n- **Color & Theme**: Commit to a cohesive aesthetic. Use CSS variables for consistency. Dominant colors with sharp accents outperform timid, evenly-distributed palettes.\n- **Motion**: Use animations for effects and micro-interactions. Prioritize CSS-only solutions for HTML. Use Motion library for React when available. Focus on high-impact moments: one well-orchestrated page load with staggered reveals (animation-delay) creates more delight than scattered micro-interactions. Use scroll-triggering and hover states that surprise.\n- **Spatial Composition**: Unexpected layouts. Asymmetry. Overlap. Diagonal flow. Grid-breaking elements. Generous negative space OR controlled density.\n- **Backgrounds & Visual Details**: Create atmosphere and depth rather than defaulting to solid colors. Add contextual effects and textures that match the overall aesthetic. Apply creative forms like gradient meshes, noise textures, geometric patterns, layered transparencies, dramatic shadows, decorative borders, custom cursors, and grain overlays.\n\nNEVER use generic AI-generated aesthetics like overused font families (Inter, Roboto, Arial, system fonts), cliched color schemes (particularly purple gradients on white backgrounds), predictable layouts and component patterns, and cookie-cutter design that lacks context-specific character.\n\nInterpret creatively and make unexpected choices that feel genuinely designed for the context. No design should be the same. Vary between light and dark themes, different fonts, different aesthetics. NEVER converge on common choices (Space Grotesk, for example) across generations.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Match implementation complexity to the aesthetic vision. Maximalist designs need elaborate code with extensive animations and effects. Minimalist or refined designs need restraint, precision, and careful attention to spacing, typography, and subtle details. Elegance comes from executing the vision well.\n\nRemember: Claude is capable of extraordinary creative work. Don''t hold back, show what can truly be created when thinking outside the box and committing fully to a distinctive vision.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:50:03.553Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Creative Coding Agents specializing in production-grade UI/UX with distinctive, non-generic aesthetics.","zh":"非常适合专注于生产级UI/UX的创意编码代理，具有独特的、非通用的美学风格。","ja":"プロダクショングレードのUI/UXに特化したクリエイティブコーディングエージェントに最適。独特で、汎用的な美学を持ったエージェント。","ko":"생산급 UI/UX를専門으로 하는 창의적 인코딩 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 독특하고 일반적이지 않은 미적 감각을 가진 에이전트입니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Codificación Creativa especializados en UI/UX de grado de producción con estéticas distintivas y no genéricas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Codage Créatif spécialisés dans les UI/UX de production de grade avec des esthétiques distinctives et non génériques.","de":"Perfekt für kreative Codierungsagenten, die auf produktionsreife UI/UX mit distinktiven, nicht generischen Ästhetik spezialisiert sind.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Programação Criativa especializados em UI/UX de nível de produção com estéticas distintas e não genéricas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для креативных кодирующих агентов, специализирующихся на UI/UX промышленного уровня с уникальной, нешаблонной эстетикой.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء البرمجة الإبداعية المتخصصة في واجهات المستخدم وتجربته من مستوى الإنتاج ذات الجماليات المميزة وغير العامة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement real working frontend code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details and bold creative choices, moving beyond generic ''AI slop'' interfaces. Provides guidance on design thinking, context analysis, and commitment to distinctive visual directions before coding execution.","zh":"赋予代理实现真正可行的前端代码的能力，具有对美学细节的异常关注和大胆的创意选择，超越了通用的''AI slop''接口。提供有关设计思维、上下文分析以及在编码执行之前对独特视觉方向的承诺的指导。","ja":"エージェントが実際に動作するフロントエンドコードを実装できる能力を与え、美的細節への異常な注意と大胆な創造的な選択肢を提供し、汎用的な''AI slop''インターフェイスを超越する。設計思考、コンテキスト分析、およびコーディング実行前に独自の視覚的な方向性へのコミットメントに関するガイダンスを提供する。","ko":"에이전트가 실제 작동하는 프론트엔드 코드를 구현할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, 미적 세부 사항에 대한 예외적인 주의와 대담한 창의적인 선택을 제공함으로써 일반적인 ''AI slop'' 인터페이스를 넘어서는 것. 디자인 사고, 컨텍스트 분석 및 코딩 실행 전에 고유한 시각적 방향에 대한 확약에 대한 가이드를 제공합니다.","es":"Empodera a los agentes para implementar código frontend real que funcione con una atención excepcional a los detalles estéticos y opciones creativas audaces, superando las interfaces genéricas de ''suciedad de IA''. Proporciona orientación sobre pensamiento de diseño, análisis de contexto y compromiso con direcciones visuales distintivas antes de la ejecución de codificación.","fr":"Autorise les agents à mettre en œuvre du code frontend réel fonctionnel avec une attention exceptionnelle aux détails esthétiques et des choix créatifs audacieux, allant au-delà des interfaces génériques de ''bouillie d''IA''. Fournit des conseils sur la pensée de conception, l''analyse de contexte et l''engagement envers des directions visuelles distinctives avant l''exécution de la codification.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, reales Frontend-Code mit außergewöhnlicher Aufmerksamkeit für ästhetische Details und kühne kreative Entscheidungen umzusetzen, über die generischen ''KI-Schlechte''-Schnittstellen hinausgehend. Bietet Anleitung zur Design-Denke, Kontextanalyse und Engagement für distinktive visuelle Richtungen vor der Codierungsausführung.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a implementar código frontend funcional com atenção excepcional aos detalhes estéticos e escolhas criativas ousadas, indo além das interfaces genéricas de ''lixo de IA''. Fornece orientação sobre design thinking, análise de contexto e comprometimento com direções visuais distintas antes da execução do código.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать реально работающий фронтенд-код с исключительным вниманием к эстетическим деталям и смелыми творческими решениями, выходя за рамки шаблонных интерфейсов ''ИИ-помоев''. Предоставляет руководство по дизайн-мышлению, анализу контекста и приверженности distinctive визуальным направлениям до выполнения кодирования.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ كود واجهة أمامية عاملة باهتمام استثنائي بالتفاصيل الجمالية والخيارات الإبداعية الجريئة، متجاوزًا واجهات ''قمامة الذكاء الاصطناعي'' العامة. يقدم إرشادات حول التفكير التصميمي، وتحليل السياق، والالتزام باتجاهات بصرية مميزة قبل تنفيذ البرمجة."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing production-grade component libraries","Creating distinctive hero sections with custom animations","Designing bold portfolio interfaces with unique aesthetics","Building creative landing pages with unconventional layouts"],"zh":["实现生产级组件库","创建具有自定义动画的独特英雄部分","设计具有独特美学的粗犷作品集接口","构建具有非传统布局的创意登陆页面"],"ja":["プロダクショングレードのコンポーネントライブラリの実装","カスタムアニメーションを備えた独特なヒーローセクションの作成","独自の美学を持ったボールドなポートフォリオインターフェイスの設計","非 truyền統的なレイアウトを備えたクリエイティブなランディングページの構築"],"ko":["생산급 컴포넌트 라이브러리의 구현","사용자 정의 애니메이션을 갖춘 독특한 영웅 섹션 생성","독특한 미학을 갖춘 대담한 포트폴리오 인터페이스 디자인","비전통적인 레이아웃을 갖춘 창의적인 랜딩 페이지 구축"],"es":["Implementar bibliotecas de componentes de grado de producción","Crear secciones de héroe distintivas con animaciones personalizadas","Diseñar interfaces de cartera audaces con estéticas únicas","Construir páginas de aterrizaje creativas con diseños no convencionales"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des bibliothèques de composants de production de grade","Créer des sections de héros distinctives avec des animations personnalisées","Concevoir des interfaces de portefeuille audacieuses avec des esthétiques uniques","Construire des pages d''atterrissage créatives avec des dispositions non conventionnelles"],"de":["Implementierung von produktionsreifen Komponentenbibliotheken","Erstellen von distinktiven Hero-Abschnitten mit benutzerdefinierten Animationen","Entwerfen von kühnen Portfolio-Schnittstellen mit einzigartigen Ästhetiken","Erstellung von kreativen Landingpages mit unkonventionellen Layouts"],"pt":["Implementação de bibliotecas de componentes de nível de produção","Criação de seções hero distintas com animações personalizadas","Design de interfaces de portfólio ousadas com estéticas únicas","Construção de páginas de destino criativas com layouts não convencionais"],"ru":["Внедрение библиотек компонентов промышленного уровня","Создание уникальных геро-секций с пользовательской анимацией","Проектирование смелых интерфейсов портфолио с уникальной эстетикой","Создание креативных целевых страниц с нетрадиционной компоновкой"],"ar":["تنفيذ مكتبات مكونات من مستوى الإنتاج","إنشاء أقسام رئيسية مميزة برسوم متحركة مخصصة","تصميم واجهات ملفات شخصية جريئة بجماليات فريدة","بناء صفحات هبوط إبداعية بتخطيطات غير تقليدية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clear frontend requirements and context from user","Needs specific aesthetic direction commitment before implementation","Focuses on distinctive designs rather than generic templates"],"zh":["需要用户提供明确的前端要求和上下文","需要在实施之前对美学方向进行具体的承诺","注重独特的设计而不是通用的模板"],"ja":["ユーザーからの明確なフロントエンド要件とコンテキストが必要","実装前に美的方向性への具体的なコミットメントが必要","独特なデザインに焦点を当て、汎用的なテンプレートではなく"],"ko":["사용자로부터 명확한 프론트엔드 요구 사항과 컨텍스트가 필요함","구현 전에 미적 방향에 대한 구체적인 확약이 필요함","독특한 디자인에 중점을 두고 일반적인 템플릿이 아닌"],"es":["Requiere requisitos y contexto de frontend claros por parte del usuario","Necesita un compromiso específico con la dirección estética antes de la implementación","Se centra en diseños distintivos en lugar de plantillas genéricas"],"fr":["Nécessite des exigences et un contexte de frontend clairs de la part de l''utilisateur","A besoin d''un engagement spécifique envers la direction esthétique avant la mise en œuvre","Se concentre sur des conceptions distinctives plutôt que sur des modèles génériques"],"de":["Benötigt klare Frontend-Anforderungen und Kontext von Seiten des Benutzers","Benötigt ein spezifisches Engagement für die ästhetische Richtung vor der Umsetzung","Konzentriert sich auf distinktive Designs anstelle von generischen Vorlagen"],"pt":["Requer requisitos claros de frontend e contexto do usuário","Necessita de um comprometimento com uma direção estética específica antes da implementação","Foca em designs distintos em vez de modelos genéricos"],"ru":["Требует четких требований к фронтенду и контекста от пользователя","Требует обязательного определения конкретного эстетического направления перед реализацией","Сосредоточен на уникальных дизайнах, а не на общих шаблонах"],"ar":["يتطلب متطلبات واضحة للواجهة الأمامية والسياق من المستخدم","يحتاج إلى التزام باتجاه جمالي محدد قبل التنفيذ","يركز على التصاميم المميزة بدلاً من القوالب العامة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":25}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/auto-animate', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'auto-animate', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z', '2026-02-18T13:49:39.136Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/auto-animate","name":"auto-animate","description":{"zh":"AutoAnimate是一个用于防止SSR错误的库，支持React、Vue、Solid、Svelte和Preact框架","ja":"AutoAnimateはSSRエラーを防ぐためのライブラリです。React、Vue、Solid、Svelte、Preactフレームワークをサポート","ko":"AutoAnimate는 SSR 오류를 예방하기 위한 라이브러리입니다. React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact 프레임워크를 지원합니다","es":"AutoAnimate es una biblioteca que permite animar elementos de forma automática. Esta guía te ayudará a prevenir errores al implementarla","fr":"AutoAnimate est une bibliothèque qui permet d''animer des éléments de manière automatique. Ce guide vous aidera à prévenir les erreurs lors de son implémentation","de":"AutoAnimate ist eine Bibliothek, die es ermöglicht, Elemente automatisch zu animieren. Diese Anleitung hilft Ihnen, Fehler bei der Implementierung zu vermeiden","pt":"O AutoAnimate é uma biblioteca que ajuda a prevenir erros de SSR em aplicações web. Aprenda a usá-la de forma eficaz em seus projetos.","ru":"AutoAnimate — это библиотека, которая помогает предотвратить ошибки SSR в веб-приложениях. Узнайте, как эффективно использовать ее в своих проектах.","ar":"AutoAnimate هي مكتبة تساعد على منع الأخطاء في تطبيقات الويب. تعلم كيفية استخدامها بفعالية في مشاريعك.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AutoAnimate - 防止SSR错误的指南","ja":"AutoAnimate - SSRエラー防止ガイド","ko":"AutoAnimate - SSR 오류 예방 가이드","es":"AutoAnimate: Guía de prevención de errores","fr":"AutoAnimate : Guide de prévention des erreurs","de":"AutoAnimate: Fehlervermeidungsanleitung","pt":"AutoAnimate: Guia de Prevenção de Erros para Desenvolvedores","ru":"AutoAnimate: Руководство по предотвращению ошибок для раз...","ar":"توجيهات AutoAnimate لتجنب الأخطاء لمطوري البرمجيات","en":"auto-animate"},"description":{"zh":"AutoAnimate是一个用于防止SSR错误的库，支持React、Vue、Solid、Svelte和Preact框架","ja":"AutoAnimateはSSRエラーを防ぐためのライブラリです。React、Vue、Solid、Svelte、Preactフレームワークをサポート","ko":"AutoAnimate는 SSR 오류를 예방하기 위한 라이브러리입니다. React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact 프레임워크를 지원합니다","es":"AutoAnimate es una biblioteca que permite animar elementos de forma automática. Esta guía te ayudará a prevenir errores al implementarla","fr":"AutoAnimate est une bibliothèque qui permet d''animer des éléments de manière automatique. Ce guide vous aidera à prévenir les erreurs lors de son implémentation","de":"AutoAnimate ist eine Bibliothek, die es ermöglicht, Elemente automatisch zu animieren. Diese Anleitung hilft Ihnen, Fehler bei der Implementierung zu vermeiden","pt":"O AutoAnimate é uma biblioteca que ajuda a prevenir erros de SSR em aplicações web. Aprenda a usá-la de forma eficaz em seus projetos.","ru":"AutoAnimate — это библиотека, которая помогает предотвратить ошибки SSR в веб-приложениях. Узнайте, как эффективно использовать ее в своих проектах.","ar":"AutoAnimate هي مكتبة تساعد على منع الأخطاء في تطبيقات الويب. تعلم كيفية استخدامها بفعالية في مشاريعك.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["防止SSR错误","支持React、Vue、Solid、Svelte和Preact框架","使用client-only导入防止SSR错误","支持Cloudflare Workers和Next.js"],"ja":["SSRエラーを防ぐ","React、Vue、Solid、Svelte、Preactフレームワークをサポート","クライアントのみのインポートを使用してSSRエラーを防ぐ","Cloudflare WorkersとNext.jsをサポート"],"ko":["SSR 오류 예방","React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact 프레임워크 지원","클라이언트 전용导入을 사용하여 SSR 오류 예방","Cloudflare Workers 및 Next.js 지원"],"es":["Compatibilidad con React, Vue, Solid, Svelte y Preact","Patrón de seguridad para Cloudflare Workers y Next.js","Implementación segura con client-only import","Actualizaciones automáticas de elementos","Soporte para SSR"],"fr":["Compatibilité avec React, Vue, Solid, Svelte et Preact","Modèle de sécurité pour Cloudflare Workers et Next.js","Implémentation sécurisée avec client-only import","Mises à jour automatiques d''éléments","Prise en charge de SSR"],"de":["Kompatibilität mit React, Vue, Solid, Svelte und Preact","Sicherheitsmuster für Cloudflare Workers und Next.js","Sichere Implementierung mit client-only Import","Automatische Aktualisierung von Elementen","Unterstützung für SSR"],"pt":["Suporte a React, Vue, Solid, Svelte e Preact","Prevenção de erros de SSR","Padrão de animação automática","Compatibilidade com Cloudflare Workers e Next.js","Uso fácil e intuitivo"],"ru":["Поддержка React, Vue, Solid, Svelte и Preact","Предотвращение ошибок SSR","Автоматический шаблон анимации","Совместимость с Cloudflare Workers и Next.js","Легкое и интуитивное использование"],"ar":["دعم React و Vue و Solid و Svelte و Preact","منع الأخطاء","نمط تلقائي للتحريك","التوافق مع Cloudflare Workers و Next.js","استخدام سهل و直-forward"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AutoAnimate","SSR错误","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js"],"ja":["AutoAnimate","SSRエラー","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js"],"ko":["AutoAnimate","SSR 오류","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js"],"es":["AutoAnimate","animación automática","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js","SSR"],"fr":["AutoAnimate","animation automatique","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js","SSR"],"de":["AutoAnimate","automatische Animation","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js","SSR"],"pt":["AutoAnimate","prevenção de erros","SSR","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js"],"ru":["AutoAnimate","предотвращение ошибок","SSR","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js"],"ar":["AutoAnimate","منع الأخطاء","SSR","React","Vue","Solid","Svelte","Preact","Cloudflare Workers","Next.js"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"auto-animate","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# AutoAnimate - Error Prevention Guide\n\n**Package**: @formkit/auto-animate@0.9.0 (current)\n**Frameworks**: React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-21\n\n---\n\n## SSR-Safe Pattern (Critical for Cloudflare Workers/Next.js)\n\n```tsx\n// Use client-only import to prevent SSR errors\nimport { useState, useEffect } from \"react\";\n\nexport function useAutoAnimateSafe<T extends HTMLElement>() {\n  const [parent, setParent] = useState<T | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (typeof window","body":"# AutoAnimate - Error Prevention Guide\n\n**Package**: @formkit/auto-animate@0.9.0 (current)\n**Frameworks**: React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-21\n\n---\n\n## SSR-Safe Pattern (Critical for Cloudflare Workers/Next.js)\n\n```tsx\n// Use client-only import to prevent SSR errors\nimport { useState, useEffect } from \"react\";\n\nexport function useAutoAnimateSafe<T extends HTMLElement>() {\n  const [parent, setParent] = useState<T | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (typeof window !== \"undefined\" && parent) {\n      import(\"@formkit/auto-animate\").then(({ default: autoAnimate }) => {\n        autoAnimate(parent);\n      });\n    }\n  }, [parent]);\n\n  return [parent, setParent] as const;\n}\n```\n\n**Why this matters**: Prevents Issue #1 (SSR/Next.js import errors). AutoAnimate uses DOM APIs not available on server.\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues Prevention (15 Documented Errors)\n\nThis skill prevents **15** documented issues:\n\n### Issue #1: SSR/Next.js Import Errors\n**Error**: \"Can''t import the named export ''useEffect'' from non EcmaScript module\"\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/55\n**Why It Happens**: AutoAnimate uses DOM APIs not available on server\n**Prevention**: Use dynamic imports (see `templates/vite-ssr-safe.tsx`)\n\n### Issue #2: Conditional Parent Rendering\n**Error**: Animations don''t work when parent is conditional\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/8\n**Why It Happens**: Ref can''t attach to non-existent element\n**Prevention**:\n\n**React Pattern**:\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong\n{showList && <ul ref={parent}>...</ul>}\n\n// ✅ Correct\n<ul ref={parent}>{showList && items.map(...)}</ul>\n```\n\n**Vue.js Pattern**:\n```vue\n<!-- ❌ Wrong - parent conditional -->\n<ul v-if=\"showList\" ref=\"parent\">\n  <li v-for=\"item in items\" :key=\"item.id\">{{ item.text }}</li>\n</ul>\n\n<!-- ✅ Correct - children conditional -->\n<ul ref=\"parent\">\n  <li v-if=\"showList\" v-for=\"item in items\" :key=\"item.id\">\n    {{ item.text }}\n  </li>\n</ul>\n```\n\n**Source**: React [Issue #8](https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/8), Vue [Issue #193](https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/193)\n\n### Issue #3: Missing Unique Keys\n**Error**: Items don''t animate correctly or flash\n**Source**: Official docs\n**Why It Happens**: React can''t track which items changed\n**Prevention**: Always use unique, stable keys (`key={item.id}`)\n\n### Issue #4: Flexbox Width and Shaking Issues\n**Error**: Elements snap to width instead of animating smoothly, or container shakes on remove\n**Source**: Official docs, [Issue #212](https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/212)\n**Why It Happens**: `flex-grow: 1` waits for surrounding content, causing timing issues\n**Prevention**: Use explicit width instead of flex-grow for animated elements\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong - causes shaking\n<ul ref={parent} style={{ display: ''flex'' }}>\n  {items.map(item => (\n    <li key={item.id} style={{ flex: ''1 1 auto'' }}>{item.text}</li>\n  ))}\n</ul>\n\n// ✅ Correct - fixed sizes\n<ul ref={parent} style={{ display: ''flex'', gap: ''1rem'' }}>\n  {items.map(item => (\n    <li\n      key={item.id}\n      style={{ minWidth: ''200px'', maxWidth: ''200px'' }}\n    >\n      {item.text}\n    </li>\n  ))}\n</ul>\n```\n\n**Maintainer Note**: justin-schroeder confirmed fixed sizes are required for flex containers\n\n### Issue #5: Table Row Display Issues\n**Error**: Table structure breaks when removing rows\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/7\n**Why It Happens**: Display: table-row conflicts with animations\n**Prevention**: Apply to `<tbody>` instead of individual rows, or use div-based layouts\n\n### Issue #6: Jest Testing Errors\n**Error**: \"Cannot find module ''@formkit/auto-animate/react''\"\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/29\n**Why It Happens**: Jest doesn''t resolve ESM exports correctly\n**Prevention**: Configure `moduleNameMapper` in jest.config.js\n\n### Issue #7: esbuild Compatibility\n**Error**: \"Path ''.'' not exported by package\"\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/36\n**Why It Happens**: ESM/CommonJS condition mismatch\n**Prevention**: Configure esbuild to handle ESM modules properly\n\n### Issue #8: CSS Position Side Effects\n**Error**: Layout breaks after adding AutoAnimate\n**Source**: Official docs\n**Why It Happens**: Parent automatically gets `position: relative`\n**Prevention**: Account for position change in CSS or set explicitly\n\n### Issue #9: Vue/Nuxt Registration Errors\n**Error**: \"Failed to resolve directive: auto-animate\"\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/43\n**Why It Happens**: Plugin not registered correctly\n**Prevention**: Proper plugin setup in Vue/Nuxt config (see references/)\n\n**Nuxt 3 Note**: Requires v0.8.2+ (April 2024). Earlier versions have ESM import issues fixed by Daniel Roe. See [Issue #199](https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/199)\n\n### Issue #10: Angular ESM Issues\n**Error**: Build fails with \"ESM-only package\"\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/72\n**Why It Happens**: CommonJS build environment\n**Prevention**: Configure ng-packagr for Angular Package Format\n\n### Issue #11: React 19 StrictMode Double-Call Bug\n**Error**: Child animations don''t work in React 19 StrictMode\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/232\n**Why It Happens**: StrictMode calls useEffect twice, triggering autoAnimate initialization twice\n**Prevention**: Use ref to track initialization\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong - breaks in StrictMode\nconst [parent] = useAutoAnimate();\n\n// ✅ Correct - prevents double initialization\nconst [parent] = useAutoAnimate();\nconst initialized = useRef(false);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (initialized.current) return;\n  initialized.current = true;\n}, []);\n```\n\n**Note**: React 19 enables StrictMode by default in development. This affects all React 19+ projects.\n\n### Issue #12: Broken Animation Outside Viewport\n**Error**: Animations broken when list is outside viewport\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/222\n**Why It Happens**: Chrome may not run Animation API for off-screen elements\n**Prevention**: Ensure parent is visible before applying autoAnimate\n\n```tsx\nconst isInViewport = (element) => {\n  const rect = element.getBoundingClientRect();\n  return rect.top >= 0 && rect.bottom <= window.innerHeight;\n};\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (parent.current && isInViewport(parent.current)) {\n    autoAnimate(parent.current);\n  }\n}, [parent]);\n```\n\n### Issue #13: Deleted Elements Overlay Existing Content\n**Error**: Removed items overlay other items during fade out\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/231\n**Why It Happens**: Exit animation maintains z-index, covering active content\n**Prevention**: Add explicit z-index handling\n\n```tsx\n// CSS workaround\n<style>{`\n  [data-auto-animate-target] {\n    z-index: -1 !important;\n  }\n`}</style>\n```\n\n### Issue #14: Cannot Disable During Drag & Drop\n**Error**: Calling enable(false) doesn''t prevent animations during drag\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/215\n**Why It Happens**: Disable doesn''t work reliably mid-drag\n**Prevention**: Conditionally remove ref during drag\n\n```tsx\nconst [isDragging, setIsDragging] = useState(false);\nconst [parent] = useAutoAnimate();\n\nreturn (\n  <ul ref={isDragging ? null : parent}>\n    {/* items */}\n  </ul>\n);\n```\n\n### Issue #15: CSS Transform Parent Position Bug\n**Error**: Items animate from wrong position after parent transform\n**Source**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/227\n**Why It Happens**: Items remember original position before transform\n**Prevention**: Delay autoAnimate until transform completes\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (showList && parent.current) {\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      autoAnimate(parent.current);\n    }, 300); // Match CSS transition duration\n  }\n}, [showList]);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Critical Rules (Error Prevention)\n\n### Always Do\n\n✅ **Use unique, stable keys** - `key={item.id}` not `key={index}`\n✅ **Keep parent in DOM** - Parent ref element always rendered\n✅ **Client-only for SSR** - Dynamic import for server environments\n✅ **Respect accessibility** - Keep `disrespectUserMotionPreference: false`\n✅ **Test with motion disabled** - Verify UI works without animations\n✅ **Use explicit width** - Avoid flex-grow on animated elements\n✅ **Apply to tbody for tables** - Not individual rows\n\n### Never Do\n\n❌ **Conditional parent** - `{show && <ul ref={parent}>}`\n❌ **Index as key** - `key={index}` breaks animations\n❌ **Ignore SSR** - Will break in Cloudflare Workers/Next.js\n❌ **Force animations** - `disrespectUserMotionPreference: true` breaks accessibility\n❌ **Animate tables directly** - Use tbody or div-based layout\n❌ **Skip unique keys** - Required for proper animation\n❌ **Complex animations** - Use Motion instead\n\n**Note**: AutoAnimate respects `prefers-reduced-motion` automatically (never disable this).\n\n---\n\n## Community Tips (Community-Sourced)\n\n> **Note**: These tips come from community discussions. Verify against your version.\n\n### Tip: Prevent Test Freezing with Mocked Package\n\n**Source**: [Issue #230](https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/230) | **Confidence**: MEDIUM\n**Applies to**: v0.8.2+\n\nTests may freeze for ~10 seconds when package is mocked. Add ResizeObserver mock:\n\n```typescript\n// jest.setup.js\nglobal.ResizeObserver = jest.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({\n  observe: jest.fn(),\n  unobserve: jest.fn(),\n  disconnect: jest.fn(),\n}));\n\n// __mocks__/@formkit/auto-animate.js\nconst autoAnimate = jest.fn(() => () => {});\nconst useAutoAnimate = jest.fn(() => [null, jest.fn(), jest.fn()]);\nmodule.exports = { default: autoAnimate, useAutoAnimate };\n```\n\n### Tip: Memory Leak Prevention\n\n**Source**: [Issue #180](https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate/issues/180) | **Confidence**: LOW\n**Applies to**: All versions\n\nFor long-lived SPAs, ensure proper cleanup:\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const cleanup = autoAnimate(parent.current);\n  return () => cleanup && cleanup();\n}, []);\n\n// useAutoAnimate hook handles cleanup automatically\nconst [parent] = useAutoAnimate(); // Preferred\n```\n\n---\n\n## Package Versions\n\n**Latest**: @formkit/auto-animate@0.9.0 (Sept 5, 2025)\n\n**Recent Releases**:\n- v0.9.0 (Sept 5, 2025) - Current stable\n- v0.8.2 (April 10, 2024) - Fixed Nuxt 3 ESM imports, ResizeObserver guard\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@formkit/auto-animate\": \"^0.9.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Framework Compatibility**: React 18+, Vue 3+, Solid, Svelte, Preact\n\n**Important**: For Nuxt 3 users, v0.8.2+ is required. Earlier versions have ESM import issues\n\n---\n\n## Official Documentation\n\n- **Official Site**: https://auto-animate.formkit.com\n- **GitHub**: https://github.com/formkit/auto-animate\n- **npm**: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@formkit/auto-animate\n- **React Docs**: https://auto-animate.formkit.com/react\n\n---\n\n## Templates & References\n\nSee bundled resources:\n- `templates/` - Copy-paste examples (SSR-safe, accordion, toast, forms)\n- `references/` - CSS conflicts, SSR patterns, library comparisons\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:49:39.136Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing seamless UI animations across React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, and Preact frameworks.","zh":"非常适合需要在 React、Vue、Solid、Svelte 和 Preact 框架中实现无缝 UI 动画的前端代理。","ja":"React、Vue、Solid、Svelte、Preact フレームワークでのシームレスな UI アニメーションが必要なフロントエンド エージェントに最適です。","ko":"React, Vue, Solid, Svelte 및 Preact 프레임워크에서 무결점 UI 애니메이션을 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan animaciones de UI sin problemas en los frameworks React, Vue, Solid, Svelte y Preact.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend nécessitant des animations d''interface utilisateur sans problème dans les frameworks React, Vue, Solid, Svelte et Preact.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die nahtlose UI-Animationen in den Frameworks React, Vue, Solid, Svelte und Preact benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de animações de UI sem interrupções em frameworks como React, Vue, Solid, Svelte e Preact.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым необходимы бесшовные анимации UI в фреймворках React, Vue, Solid, Svelte и Preact.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية الذي يحتاج إلى تحريك واجهة المستخدم الخالية من العيوب عبر إطارات React و Vue و Solid و Svelte و Preact."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to prevent SSR errors and ensure smooth animations using the @formkit/auto-animate package, leveraging client-only imports and the SSR-Safe pattern for compatibility with Cloudflare Workers and Next.js.","zh":"赋予代理防止 SSR 错误并使用 @formkit/auto-animate 包确保平滑动画的能力，利用客户端导入和 SSR 安全模式与 Cloudflare Workers 和 Next.js 兼容。","ja":"@formkit/auto-animate パッケージを使用して、SSR エラーを防ぎ、スムーズなアニメーションを実現するエージェントの能力を提供し、Cloudflare Workers および Next.js との互換性を確保するために、クライアントのみのインポートと SSR セーフ パターンを利用します。","ko":"@formkit/auto-animate 패키지를 사용하여 SSR 오류를 방지하고 부드러운 애니메이션을 보장하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하며, 클라우드 플레어 워커와 넥스트.js와의 호환성을 보장하기 위해 클라이언트 전용 가져오기와 SSR 안전 패턴을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes prevenir errores de SSR y garantizar animaciones suaves utilizando el paquete @formkit/auto-animate, aprovechando las importaciones solo para cliente y el patrón de seguridad SSR para la compatibilidad con Cloudflare Workers y Next.js.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''empêcher les erreurs de SSR et d''assurer des animations fluides en utilisant le paquet @formkit/auto-animate, en exploitant les imports client-seulement et le modèle de sécurité SSR pour la compatibilité avec Cloudflare Workers et Next.js.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, SSR-Fehler zu verhindern und eine reibungslose Animation sicherzustellen, indem sie das @formkit/auto-animate-Paket verwenden, das Client-only-Importe und das SSR-Safe-Muster für die Kompatibilität mit Cloudflare Workers und Next.js nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a prevenir erros de SSR e garantir animações suaves usando o pacote @formkit/auto-animate, aproveitando importações somente para cliente e o padrão SSR-Safe para compatibilidade com Cloudflare Workers e Next.js.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью предотвратить ошибки SSR и обеспечить плавные анимации с помощью пакета @formkit/auto-animate, используя импорты только для клиента и шаблон SSR-Safe для совместимости с Cloudflare Workers и Next.js.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من منع أخطاء SSR وضمان تشغيل حركات سلاسة باستخدام حزمة @formkit/auto-animate، واستخدام الاستيرادات فقط للعميل ونمط SSR-Safe لتوافق مع Cloudflare Workers و Next.js."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating UI animations for enhanced user experience","Debugging SSR errors in React and Vue applications","Implementing animations in Svelte and Preact projects with ease"],"zh":["为增强用户体验自动执行 UI 动画","调试 React 和 Vue 应用中的 SSR 错误","轻松在 Svelte 和 Preact 项目中实现动画"],"ja":["ユーザー体験の向上のために UI アニメーションを自動化する","React および Vue アプリケーションの SSR エラーをデバッグする","Svelte および Preact プロジェクトでアニメーションを簡単に実装する"],"ko":["개선된 사용자 경험을 위한 UI 애니메이션 자동화","React 및 Vue 애플리케이션의 SSR 오류 디버깅","Svelte 및 Preact 프로젝트에서 애니메이션을 쉽게 구현"],"es":["Automatizar las animaciones de UI para una experiencia de usuario mejorada","Depurar errores de SSR en aplicaciones React y Vue","Implementar animaciones en proyectos Svelte y Preact con facilidad"],"fr":["Automatiser les animations d''interface utilisateur pour une expérience utilisateur améliorée","Déboguer les erreurs de SSR dans les applications React et Vue","Mettre en œuvre des animations dans les projets Svelte et Preact avec facilité"],"de":["Automatisieren von UI-Animationen für eine verbesserte Benutzererfahrung","Debuggen von SSR-Fehlern in React- und Vue-Anwendungen","Einrichten von Animationen in Svelte- und Preact-Projekten mit Leichtigkeit"],"pt":["Automatizar animações de UI para experiência do usuário aprimorada","Depurar erros de SSR em aplicações React e Vue","Implementar animações em projetos Svelte e Preact com facilidade"],"ru":["Автоматизация анимаций UI для улучшения пользовательского опыта","Отладка ошибок SSR в приложениях React и Vue","Реализация анимаций в проектах Svelte и Preact с легкостью"],"ar":["تأتمة تحريك واجهة المستخدم لتحسين تجربة المستخدم","تصحيح أخطاء SSR في تطبيقات React و Vue","تنفيذ الحركات في مشاريع Svelte و Preact بسهولة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires client-side rendering","Compatibility issues may arise with older framework versions","Specific implementation required for Cloudflare Workers and Next.js"],"zh":["需要客户端渲染","可能与旧版本框架出现兼容性问题","Cloudflare Workers 和 Next.js 需要特定的实现"],"ja":["クライアント側のレンダリングが必要","古いバージョンのフレームワークと互換性の問題が発生する可能性がある","Cloudflare Workers および Next.js では特定の実装が必要"],"ko":["클라이언트 측 렌더링이 필요","구 버전 프레임워크와의 호환성 문제가 발생할 수 있음","클라우드 플레어 워커 및 넥스트.js에서는 특정 구현이 필요"],"es":["Requiere representación en el lado del cliente","Pueden surgir problemas de compatibilidad con versiones anteriores de los frameworks","Se requiere una implementación específica para Cloudflare Workers y Next.js"],"fr":["Nécessite un rendu sur le côté client","Des problèmes de compatibilité peuvent survenir avec les versions antérieures des frameworks","Une mise en œuvre spécifique est requise pour Cloudflare Workers et Next.js"],"de":["Benötigt Client-seitige Rendering","Kompatibilitätsprobleme können mit älteren Framework-Versionen auftreten","Eine spezifische Implementierung ist für Cloudflare Workers und Next.js erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer renderização do lado do cliente","Pode ocorrer problemas de compatibilidade com versões mais antigas do framework","Requer implementação específica para Cloudflare Workers e Next.js"],"ru":["Требуется рендеринг на стороне клиента","Могут возникнуть проблемы совместимости со старыми версиями фреймворка","Требуется специальная реализация для Cloudflare Workers и Next.js"],"ar":["يتطلب تحrick من جانب العميل","قد تظهر مشاكل في التوافق مع إصدارات الإطار القديمة","يتطلب تنفيذاً محدداً لعمال Cloudflare و Next.js"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/saga-orchestration', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'saga-orchestration', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z', '2026-02-18T13:50:14.488Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/saga-orchestration","name":"saga-orchestration","description":{"zh":"Saga 编排是一种用于管理分布式事务和长时间运行的业务流程的模式，确保数据一致性和可靠性","ja":"Saga オーケストレーションは、分散トランザクションと長時間実行されるビジネスプロセスを管理するためのパターンであり、データの一貫性と信頼性を保証します","ko":"사가 오케스트레이션은 분산 트랜잭션 및 장기 실행 비즈니스 프로세스를 관리하기 위한 패턴으로, 데이터 일관성 및 신뢰성을 보장합니다","es":"La orquestación de Saga es un patrón de diseño para gestionar transacciones distribuidas y procesos de negocio a largo plazo de manera eficiente","fr":"L''orchestration de Saga est un modèle de conception pour gérer les transactions distribuées et les processus métier à long terme de manière efficace","de":"Die Saga-Orchestrierung ist ein Entwurfsmuster zur effizienten Verwaltung verteilter Transaktionen und langfristiger Geschäftsprozesse","pt":"O padrão de orquestração de saga é uma abordagem para gerenciar transações distribuídas e processos de negócios de longa execução","ru":"Шаблон оркестровки саги - это подход к управлению распределенными транзакциями и долгосрочными бизнес-процессами","ar":"نمط أوركسترا ساجا هو نهج لتنسيق المعاملات الموزعة وعمليات الأعمال طويلة المدى","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Saga 编排：分布式事务管理","ja":"Saga オーケストレーション：分散トランザクション管理","ko":"사가 오케스트레이션: 분산 트랜잭션 관리","es":"Orquestación de Saga para Procesos de Negocio","fr":"Orchestration de Saga pour les Processus Métier","de":"Saga-Orchestrierung für Geschäftsprozesse","pt":"Orquestração de Saga: Padronização de Transações","ru":"Оркестровка Саги: Управление Распределенными Транзакциями","ar":"أوركسترا ساجا: تنسيق المعاملات الموزعة","en":"saga-orchestration"},"description":{"zh":"Saga 编排是一种用于管理分布式事务和长时间运行的业务流程的模式，确保数据一致性和可靠性","ja":"Saga オーケストレーションは、分散トランザクションと長時間実行されるビジネスプロセスを管理するためのパターンであり、データの一貫性と信頼性を保証します","ko":"사가 오케스트레이션은 분산 트랜잭션 및 장기 실행 비즈니스 프로세스를 관리하기 위한 패턴으로, 데이터 일관성 및 신뢰성을 보장합니다","es":"La orquestación de Saga es un patrón de diseño para gestionar transacciones distribuidas y procesos de negocio a largo plazo de manera eficiente","fr":"L''orchestration de Saga est un modèle de conception pour gérer les transactions distribuées et les processus métier à long terme de manière efficace","de":"Die Saga-Orchestrierung ist ein Entwurfsmuster zur effizienten Verwaltung verteilter Transaktionen und langfristiger Geschäftsprozesse","pt":"O padrão de orquestração de saga é uma abordagem para gerenciar transações distribuídas e processos de negócios de longa execução","ru":"Шаблон оркестровки саги - это подход к управлению распределенными транзакциями и долгосрочными бизнес-процессами","ar":"نمط أوركسترا ساجا هو نهج لتنسيق المعاملات الموزعة وعمليات الأعمال طويلة المدى","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["管理分布式事务","实现补偿事务","管理长时间运行的业务流程","处理分布式系统中的故障","构建订单履行过程","实现审批工作流"],"ja":["分散トランザクションの管理","補償トランザクションの実装","長時間実行されるビジネスプロセスの管理","分散システムにおける障害の処理","オーダーフラグメントプロセスの構築","承認ワークフローの実装"],"ko":["분산 트랜잭션 관리","보상 트랜잭션 구현","장기 실행 비즈니스 프로세스 관리","분산 시스템에서의 오류 처리","주문 이행 프로세스 구축","승인 워크플로 구현"],"es":["Gestión de transacciones distribuidas","Implementación de transacciones compensatorias","Gestión de procesos de negocio a largo plazo","Control de errores en sistemas distribuidos","Creación de procesos de cumplimiento de pedidos","Implementación de flujos de aprobación"],"fr":["Gestion des transactions distribuées","Mise en œuvre de transactions compensatoires","Gestion des processus métier à long terme","Gestion des erreurs dans les systèmes distribués","Création de processus de traitement de commandes","Mise en œuvre de flux d''approbation"],"de":["Verwaltung verteilter Transaktionen","Implementierung von Kompensations-transaktionen","Verwaltung langfristiger Geschäftsprozesse","Fehlerverwaltung in verteilten Systemen","Erstellung von Prozessen zur Auftragsabwicklung","Implementierung von Genehmigungsflüssen"],"pt":["Coordinar transações multi-serviço","Implementar transações compensatórias","Gerenciar fluxos de trabalho de negócios de longa execução","Tratar falhas em sistemas distribuídos","Construir processos de cumprimento de pedidos"],"ru":["Координировать многосервисные транзакции","Реализовывать компенсирующие транзакции","Управлять долгосрочными бизнес-процессами","Обрабатывать сбои в распределенных системах","Строить процессы выполнения заказов"],"ar":["تنسيق معاملات متعددة الخدمات","تنفيذ معاملات تعويض","إدارة عمليات الأعمال طويلة المدى","معالجة الأعطال في الأنظمة الموزعة","بناء عمليات تنفيذ الطلبات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Saga 编排","分布式事务","长时间运行的业务流程","补偿事务","分布式系统","订单履行","审批工作流"],"ja":["Saga オーケストレーション","分散トランザクション","長時間実行されるビジネスプロセス","補償トランザクション","分散システム","オーダーフラグメント","承認ワークフロー"],"ko":["사가 오케스트레이션","분산 트랜잭션","장기 실행 비즈니스 프로세스","보상 트랜잭션","분산 시스템","주문 이행","승인 워크플로"],"es":["orquestación de Saga","transacciones distribuidas","procesos de negocio a largo plazo","patrones de diseño","gestión de errores","sistemas distribuidos","arquitectura de software"],"fr":["orchestration de Saga","transactions distribuées","processus métier à long terme","modèles de conception","gestion des erreurs","systèmes distribués","architecture logicielle"],"de":["Saga-Orchestrierung","verteilte Transaktionen","langfristige Geschäftsprozesse","Entwurfsmuster","Fehlerverwaltung","verteilte Systeme","Software-Architektur"],"pt":["orquestração de saga","transações distribuídas","processos de negócios de longa execução","padrão de design","gerenciamento de transações","sistemas distribuídos"],"ru":["оркестровка саги","распределенные транзакции","долгосрочные бизнес-процессы","шаблон проектирования","управление транзакциями","распределенные системы"],"ar":["أوركسترا ساجا","معاملات موزعة","عمليات الأعمال طويلة المدى","نمط تصميم","إدارة المعاملات","أنظمة موزعة"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"saga-orchestration","description":"Implement saga patterns for distributed transactions and cross-aggregate workflows. Use when coordinating multi-step business processes, handling compensating transactions, or managing long-running workflows.","bodyPreview":"# Saga Orchestration\n\nPatterns for managing distributed transactions and long-running business processes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Coordinating multi-service transactions\n- Implementing compensating transactions\n- Managing long-running business workflows\n- Handling failures in distributed systems\n- Building order fulfillment processes\n- Implementing approval workflows\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Saga Types\n\n```\nChoreography                    Orchestration\n┌─────┐  ┌─────┐  ┌─────┐     ┌─────","body":"# Saga Orchestration\n\nPatterns for managing distributed transactions and long-running business processes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Coordinating multi-service transactions\n- Implementing compensating transactions\n- Managing long-running business workflows\n- Handling failures in distributed systems\n- Building order fulfillment processes\n- Implementing approval workflows\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Saga Types\n\n```\nChoreography                    Orchestration\n┌─────┐  ┌─────┐  ┌─────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│Svc A│─►│Svc B│─►│Svc C│     │ Orchestrator│\n└─────┘  └─────┘  └─────┘     └──────┬──────┘\n   │        │        │               │\n   ▼        ▼        ▼         ┌─────┼─────┐\n Event    Event    Event       ▼     ▼     ▼\n                            ┌────┐┌────┐┌────┐\n                            │Svc1││Svc2││Svc3│\n                            └────┘└────┘└────┘\n```\n\n### 2. Saga Execution States\n\n| State            | Description                    |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| **Started**      | Saga initiated                 |\n| **Pending**      | Waiting for step completion    |\n| **Compensating** | Rolling back due to failure    |\n| **Completed**    | All steps succeeded            |\n| **Failed**       | Saga failed after compensation |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Saga Orchestrator Base\n\n```python\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport uuid\n\nclass SagaState(Enum):\n    STARTED = \"started\"\n    PENDING = \"pending\"\n    COMPENSATING = \"compensating\"\n    COMPLETED = \"completed\"\n    FAILED = \"failed\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass SagaStep:\n    name: str\n    action: str\n    compensation: str\n    status: str = \"pending\"\n    result: Optional[Dict] = None\n    error: Optional[str] = None\n    executed_at: Optional[datetime] = None\n    compensated_at: Optional[datetime] = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Saga:\n    saga_id: str\n    saga_type: str\n    state: SagaState\n    data: Dict[str, Any]\n    steps: List[SagaStep]\n    current_step: int = 0\n    created_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)\n    updated_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)\n\n\nclass SagaOrchestrator(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Base class for saga orchestrators.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, saga_store, event_publisher):\n        self.saga_store = saga_store\n        self.event_publisher = event_publisher\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def define_steps(self, data: Dict) -> List[SagaStep]:\n        \"\"\"Define the saga steps.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @property\n    @abstractmethod\n    def saga_type(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Unique saga type identifier.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    async def start(self, data: Dict) -> Saga:\n        \"\"\"Start a new saga.\"\"\"\n        saga = Saga(\n            saga_id=str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            saga_type=self.saga_type,\n            state=SagaState.STARTED,\n            data=data,\n            steps=self.define_steps(data)\n        )\n        await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n        await self._execute_next_step(saga)\n        return saga\n\n    async def handle_step_completed(self, saga_id: str, step_name: str, result: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Handle successful step completion.\"\"\"\n        saga = await self.saga_store.get(saga_id)\n\n        # Update step\n        for step in saga.steps:\n            if step.name == step_name:\n                step.status = \"completed\"\n                step.result = result\n                step.executed_at = datetime.utcnow()\n                break\n\n        saga.current_step += 1\n        saga.updated_at = datetime.utcnow()\n\n        # Check if saga is complete\n        if saga.current_step >= len(saga.steps):\n            saga.state = SagaState.COMPLETED\n            await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n            await self._on_saga_completed(saga)\n        else:\n            saga.state = SagaState.PENDING\n            await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n            await self._execute_next_step(saga)\n\n    async def handle_step_failed(self, saga_id: str, step_name: str, error: str):\n        \"\"\"Handle step failure - start compensation.\"\"\"\n        saga = await self.saga_store.get(saga_id)\n\n        # Mark step as failed\n        for step in saga.steps:\n            if step.name == step_name:\n                step.status = \"failed\"\n                step.error = error\n                break\n\n        saga.state = SagaState.COMPENSATING\n        saga.updated_at = datetime.utcnow()\n        await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n\n        # Start compensation from current step backwards\n        await self._compensate(saga)\n\n    async def _execute_next_step(self, saga: Saga):\n        \"\"\"Execute the next step in the saga.\"\"\"\n        if saga.current_step >= len(saga.steps):\n            return\n\n        step = saga.steps[saga.current_step]\n        step.status = \"executing\"\n        await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n\n        # Publish command to execute step\n        await self.event_publisher.publish(\n            step.action,\n            {\n                \"saga_id\": saga.saga_id,\n                \"step_name\": step.name,\n                **saga.data\n            }\n        )\n\n    async def _compensate(self, saga: Saga):\n        \"\"\"Execute compensation for completed steps.\"\"\"\n        # Compensate in reverse order\n        for i in range(saga.current_step - 1, -1, -1):\n            step = saga.steps[i]\n            if step.status == \"completed\":\n                step.status = \"compensating\"\n                await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n\n                await self.event_publisher.publish(\n                    step.compensation,\n                    {\n                        \"saga_id\": saga.saga_id,\n                        \"step_name\": step.name,\n                        \"original_result\": step.result,\n                        **saga.data\n                    }\n                )\n\n    async def handle_compensation_completed(self, saga_id: str, step_name: str):\n        \"\"\"Handle compensation completion.\"\"\"\n        saga = await self.saga_store.get(saga_id)\n\n        for step in saga.steps:\n            if step.name == step_name:\n                step.status = \"compensated\"\n                step.compensated_at = datetime.utcnow()\n                break\n\n        # Check if all compensations complete\n        all_compensated = all(\n            s.status in (\"compensated\", \"pending\", \"failed\")\n            for s in saga.steps\n        )\n\n        if all_compensated:\n            saga.state = SagaState.FAILED\n            await self._on_saga_failed(saga)\n\n        await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n\n    async def _on_saga_completed(self, saga: Saga):\n        \"\"\"Called when saga completes successfully.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_publisher.publish(\n            f\"{self.saga_type}Completed\",\n            {\"saga_id\": saga.saga_id, **saga.data}\n        )\n\n    async def _on_saga_failed(self, saga: Saga):\n        \"\"\"Called when saga fails after compensation.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_publisher.publish(\n            f\"{self.saga_type}Failed\",\n            {\"saga_id\": saga.saga_id, \"error\": \"Saga failed\", **saga.data}\n        )\n```\n\n### Template 2: Order Fulfillment Saga\n\n```python\nclass OrderFulfillmentSaga(SagaOrchestrator):\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates order fulfillment across services.\"\"\"\n\n    @property\n    def saga_type(self) -> str:\n        return \"OrderFulfillment\"\n\n    def define_steps(self, data: Dict) -> List[SagaStep]:\n        return [\n            SagaStep(\n                name=\"reserve_inventory\",\n                action=\"InventoryService.ReserveItems\",\n                compensation=\"InventoryService.ReleaseReservation\"\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                name=\"process_payment\",\n                action=\"PaymentService.ProcessPayment\",\n                compensation=\"PaymentService.RefundPayment\"\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                name=\"create_shipment\",\n                action=\"ShippingService.CreateShipment\",\n                compensation=\"ShippingService.CancelShipment\"\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                name=\"send_confirmation\",\n                action=\"NotificationService.SendOrderConfirmation\",\n                compensation=\"NotificationService.SendCancellationNotice\"\n            )\n        ]\n\n\n# Usage\nasync def create_order(order_data: Dict):\n    saga = OrderFulfillmentSaga(saga_store, event_publisher)\n    return await saga.start({\n        \"order_id\": order_data[\"order_id\"],\n        \"customer_id\": order_data[\"customer_id\"],\n        \"items\": order_data[\"items\"],\n        \"payment_method\": order_data[\"payment_method\"],\n        \"shipping_address\": order_data[\"shipping_address\"]\n    })\n\n\n# Event handlers in each service\nclass InventoryService:\n    async def handle_reserve_items(self, command: Dict):\n        try:\n            # Reserve inventory\n            reservation = await self.reserve(\n                command[\"items\"],\n                command[\"order_id\"]\n            )\n            # Report success\n            await self.event_publisher.publish(\n                \"SagaStepCompleted\",\n                {\n                    \"saga_id\": command[\"saga_id\"],\n                    \"step_name\": \"reserve_inventory\",\n                    \"result\": {\"reservation_id\": reservation.id}\n                }\n            )\n        except InsufficientInventoryError as e:\n            await self.event_publisher.publish(\n                \"SagaStepFailed\",\n                {\n                    \"saga_id\": command[\"saga_id\"],\n                    \"step_name\": \"reserve_inventory\",\n                    \"error\": str(e)\n                }\n            )\n\n    async def handle_release_reservation(self, command: Dict):\n        # Compensating action\n        await self.release_reservation(\n            command[\"original_result\"][\"reservation_id\"]\n        )\n        await self.event_publisher.publish(\n            \"SagaCompensationCompleted\",\n            {\n                \"saga_id\": command[\"saga_id\"],\n                \"step_name\": \"reserve_inventory\"\n            }\n        )\n```\n\n### Template 3: Choreography-Based Saga\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nimport asyncio\n\n@dataclass\nclass SagaContext:\n    \"\"\"Passed through choreographed saga events.\"\"\"\n    saga_id: str\n    step: int\n    data: Dict[str, Any]\n    completed_steps: list\n\n\nclass OrderChoreographySaga:\n    \"\"\"Choreography-based saga using events.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, event_bus):\n        self.event_bus = event_bus\n        self._register_handlers()\n\n    def _register_handlers(self):\n        self.event_bus.subscribe(\"OrderCreated\", self._on_order_created)\n        self.event_bus.subscribe(\"InventoryReserved\", self._on_inventory_reserved)\n        self.event_bus.subscribe(\"PaymentProcessed\", self._on_payment_processed)\n        self.event_bus.subscribe(\"ShipmentCreated\", self._on_shipment_created)\n\n        # Compensation handlers\n        self.event_bus.subscribe(\"PaymentFailed\", self._on_payment_failed)\n        self.event_bus.subscribe(\"ShipmentFailed\", self._on_shipment_failed)\n\n    async def _on_order_created(self, event: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Step 1: Order created, reserve inventory.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"ReserveInventory\", {\n            \"saga_id\": event[\"order_id\"],\n            \"order_id\": event[\"order_id\"],\n            \"items\": event[\"items\"]\n        })\n\n    async def _on_inventory_reserved(self, event: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Step 2: Inventory reserved, process payment.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"ProcessPayment\", {\n            \"saga_id\": event[\"saga_id\"],\n            \"order_id\": event[\"order_id\"],\n            \"amount\": event[\"total_amount\"],\n            \"reservation_id\": event[\"reservation_id\"]\n        })\n\n    async def _on_payment_processed(self, event: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Step 3: Payment done, create shipment.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"CreateShipment\", {\n            \"saga_id\": event[\"saga_id\"],\n            \"order_id\": event[\"order_id\"],\n            \"payment_id\": event[\"payment_id\"]\n        })\n\n    async def _on_shipment_created(self, event: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Step 4: Complete - send confirmation.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"OrderFulfilled\", {\n            \"saga_id\": event[\"saga_id\"],\n            \"order_id\": event[\"order_id\"],\n            \"tracking_number\": event[\"tracking_number\"]\n        })\n\n    # Compensation handlers\n    async def _on_payment_failed(self, event: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Payment failed - release inventory.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"ReleaseInventory\", {\n            \"saga_id\": event[\"saga_id\"],\n            \"reservation_id\": event[\"reservation_id\"]\n        })\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"OrderFailed\", {\n            \"order_id\": event[\"order_id\"],\n            \"reason\": \"Payment failed\"\n        })\n\n    async def _on_shipment_failed(self, event: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Shipment failed - refund payment and release inventory.\"\"\"\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"RefundPayment\", {\n            \"saga_id\": event[\"saga_id\"],\n            \"payment_id\": event[\"payment_id\"]\n        })\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\"ReleaseInventory\", {\n            \"saga_id\": event[\"saga_id\"],\n            \"reservation_id\": event[\"reservation_id\"]\n        })\n```\n\n### Template 4: Saga with Timeouts\n\n```python\nclass TimeoutSagaOrchestrator(SagaOrchestrator):\n    \"\"\"Saga orchestrator with step timeouts.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, saga_store, event_publisher, scheduler):\n        super().__init__(saga_store, event_publisher)\n        self.scheduler = scheduler\n\n    async def _execute_next_step(self, saga: Saga):\n        if saga.current_step >= len(saga.steps):\n            return\n\n        step = saga.steps[saga.current_step]\n        step.status = \"executing\"\n        step.timeout_at = datetime.utcnow() + timedelta(minutes=5)\n        await self.saga_store.save(saga)\n\n        # Schedule timeout check\n        await self.scheduler.schedule(\n            f\"saga_timeout_{saga.saga_id}_{step.name}\",\n            self._check_timeout,\n            {\"saga_id\": saga.saga_id, \"step_name\": step.name},\n            run_at=step.timeout_at\n        )\n\n        await self.event_publisher.publish(\n            step.action,\n            {\"saga_id\": saga.saga_id, \"step_name\": step.name, **saga.data}\n        )\n\n    async def _check_timeout(self, data: Dict):\n        \"\"\"Check if step has timed out.\"\"\"\n        saga = await self.saga_store.get(data[\"saga_id\"])\n        step = next(s for s in saga.steps if s.name == data[\"step_name\"])\n\n        if step.status == \"executing\":\n            # Step timed out - fail it\n            await self.handle_step_failed(\n                data[\"saga_id\"],\n                data[\"step_name\"],\n                \"Step timed out\"\n            )\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Make steps idempotent** - Safe to retry\n- **Design compensations carefully** - They must work\n- **Use correlation IDs** - For tracing across services\n- **Implement timeouts** - Don''t wait forever\n- **Log everything** - For debugging failures\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t assume instant completion** - Sagas take time\n- **Don''t skip compensation testing** - Most critical part\n- **Don''t couple services** - Use async messaging\n- **Don''t ignore partial failures** - Handle gracefully\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Saga Pattern](https://microservices.io/patterns/data/saga.html)\n- [Designing Data-Intensive Applications](https://dataintensive.net/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:50:14.488Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Distributed System Agents requiring advanced transaction management and workflow orchestration capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级事务管理和工作流编排能力的分布式系统代理。","ja":"高度なトランザクション管理とワークフロー オーケストレーション機能を必要とする分散システム エージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 트랜잭션 관리 및 워크플로 오케스트레이션 기능이 필요한 분산 시스템 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de sistemas distribuidos que requieren administración de transacciones avanzada y capacidades de orquestación de flujo de trabajo.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de systèmes distribués nécessitant une gestion de transactions avancée et des capacités d''orchestration de flux de travail.","de":"Ideal für verteilte Systemagenten, die eine erweiterte Transaktionsverwaltung und Workflow-Orchestrierungsfähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuídos que exigem gestão de transações avançada e capacidades de orquestração de fluxo de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов распределенных систем, требующих продвинутого управления транзакциями и возможностей оркестровки рабочих процессов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء أنظمة التوزيع التي تتطلب إدارة معاملات متقدمة وقدرات توجيه سير العمل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage distributed transactions and long-running business processes using saga orchestration patterns, including choreography and orchestration types, to handle failures and implement compensating transactions through protocols like APIs and message queues.","zh":"赋予代理管理分布式事务和长时间运行的业务流程的能力，使用saga编排模式，包括编排和舞蹈类型，以处理故障并通过API和消息队列等协议实现补偿事务。","ja":"エージェントが分散トランザクションと長時間実行されるビジネス プロセスを管理できるようにします。サガ オーケストレーション パターン (choreography と orchestration のタイプ) を使用して、障害を処理し、API やメッセージ キューなどのプロトコルを介して補償トランザクションを実装します。","ko":"에이전트가 분산 트랜잭션 및 장기간 실행되는 비즈니스 프로세스를 관리할 수 있도록 합니다. 사가 오케스트레이션 패턴(chorography 및 오케스트레이션 유형)을 사용하여 장애를 처리하고, API 및 메시지 큐와 같은 프로토콜을 통해 보상 트랜잭션을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar transacciones distribuidas y procesos comerciales de larga duración utilizando patrones de orquestación de saga, incluidos tipos de coreografía y orquestación, para manejar errores e implementar transacciones compensatorias a través de protocolos como API y colas de mensajes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des transactions distribuées et des processus métier à long terme en utilisant des modèles d''orchestration de saga, notamment des types de chorégraphie et d''orchestration, pour gérer les défaillances et mettre en œuvre des transactions compensatoires via des protocoles tels que les API et les files d''attente de messages.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, verteilte Transaktionen und lang laufende Geschäftsprozesse mithilfe von Saga-Orchestrierungsmustern zu verwalten, einschließlich Choreographie- und Orchestrierungstypen, um Fehler zu handhaben und Ausgleichstransaktionen durch Protokolle wie APIs und Nachrichtenwarteschlangen umzusetzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar transações distribuídas e processos de negócios de longa execução usando padrões de orquestração de sagas, incluindo tipos de coreografia e orquestração, para lidar com falhas e implementar transações compensatórias por meio de protocolos como APIs e filas de mensagens.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять распределенными транзакциями и долгосрочными бизнес-процессами с помощью шаблонов оркестровки саг, включая типы хореографии и оркестровки, для обработки сбоев и реализации компенсирующих транзакций через протоколы, такие как API и очереди сообщений.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إدارة المعاملات الموزعة والعمليات التجارية طويلة المدى باستخدام أنماط توجيه سير العمل لسجلات الأعمال، بما في ذلك أنواع الكوريوغرافيا والتوجيه، لمعالجة الأعطال وتنفيذ معاملات التعويض من خلال بروتوكولات مثل واجهات برمجة التطبيقات وطوابير الرسائل."},"useCases":{"en":["Coordinating multi-service transactions for order fulfillment processes","Implementing approval workflows with compensating transactions","Debugging failures in distributed systems using saga logs and tracing","Automating long-running business workflows with retry mechanisms and timeouts"],"zh":["协调多服务事务以实现订单履行流程","实现具有补偿事务的审批工作流程","使用saga日志和跟踪调试分布式系统中的故障","使用重试机制和超时自动化长时间运行的业务工作流程"],"ja":["注文履行プロセスのためのマルチ サービス トランザクションの調整","補償トランザクションを使用した承認ワークフローの実装","サガ ログとトレーシングを使用した分散システムの障害のデバッグ","リトライ メカニズムとタイムアウトを使用した長時間実行されるビジネス ワークフローの自動化"],"ko":["주문 충족 프로세스에 대한 다중 서비스 트랜잭션의 조정","보상 트랜잭션을 사용한 승인 워크플로의 구현","사가 로그 및 추적을 사용한 분산 시스템의 장애 디버깅","재시도 메커니즘 및 타임아웃을 사용한 장기간 실행되는 비즈니스 워크플로의 자동화"],"es":["Coordinar transacciones multi-servicio para procesos de cumplimiento de pedidos","Implementar flujos de trabajo de aprobación con transacciones compensatorias","Depurar errores en sistemas distribuidos utilizando registros y seguimiento de saga","Automatizar flujos de trabajo comerciales de larga duración con mecanismos de reintento y timeouts"],"fr":["Coordonner des transactions multi-services pour les processus de traitement des commandes","Mettre en œuvre des flux de travail d''approbation avec des transactions compensatoires","Déboguer les défaillances dans les systèmes distribués en utilisant les journaux et le suivi de saga","Automatiser des flux de travail métier à long terme avec des mécanismes de réessai et des délais d''attente"],"de":["Koordinieren von Multi-Service-Transaktionen für Bestellabwicklungsprozesse","Implementieren von Genehmigungsworkflows mit Ausgleichstransaktionen","Fehler in verteilten Systemen mithilfe von Saga-Protokollen und -Nachverfolgung debuggen","Automatisieren von lang laufenden Geschäftsworkflows mit Wiederholungsmechanismen und Timeouts"],"pt":["Coordenar transações multi-serviço para processos de cumprimento de pedidos","Implementar fluxos de trabalho de aprovação com transações compensatórias","Depurar falhas em sistemas distribuídos usando logs e rastreamento de sagas","Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de negócios de longa execução com mecanismos de repetição e tempos limite"],"ru":["Координировать многосервисные транзакции для процессов выполнения заказов","Реализовывать рабочие процессы утверждения с компенсирующими транзакциями","Отлаживать сбои в распределенных системах с помощью журналов и трассировки саг","Автоматизировать долгосрочные бизнес-процессы с механизмами повторения и таймаутами"],"ar":["تنسيق معاملات متعددة الخدمات لعمليات إكمال الطلبات","تنفيذ سير عمل الموافقة مع معاملات التعويض","تصحيح الأعطال في الأنظمة الموزعة باستخدام سجلات وتحليل سجلات الأعمال","تأتمتة سير العمل التجارية طويلة المدى بأجهزة إعادة التشغيل ومؤقتات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of distributed system architecture","Needs compensation transaction logic for error handling","Limited to saga orchestration patterns, not applicable to all workflow types"],"zh":["需要理解分布式系统架构","需要补偿事务逻辑以处理错误","仅限于saga编排模式，不适用于所有工作流类型"],"ja":["分散システム アーキテクチャの理解が必要","エラー ハンドリングのために補償トランザクション ロジックが必要","サガ オーケストレーション パターンのみに限定され、すべてのワークフロー タイプに適用できない"],"ko":["분산 시스템 아키텍처에 대한 이해가 필요","오류 처리를 위해 보상 트랜잭션 로직이 필요","사가 오케스트레이션 패턴만으로限定되어 모든 워크플ロー 타입에 적용할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la arquitectura del sistema distribuido","Necesita lógica de transacción de compensación para el manejo de errores","Limitado a patrones de orquestación de saga, no aplicable a todos los tipos de flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de l''architecture du système distribué","Nécessite une logique de transaction de compensation pour la gestion des erreurs","Limité aux modèles d''orchestration de saga, non applicable à tous les types de flux de travail"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Architektur des verteilten Systems","Benötigt Ausgleichstransaktionslogik für die Fehlerbehandlung","Begrenzt auf Saga-Orchestrierungsmuster, nicht anwendbar auf alle Arten von Workflows"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da arquitetura do sistema distribuído","Necessita de lógica de transação compensatória para tratamento de erros","Limitado a padrões de orquestração de sagas, não aplicável a todos os tipos de fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["Требует понимания архитектуры распределенной системы","Требует логики компенсирующей транзакции для обработки ошибок","Ограничен шаблонами оркестровки саг, не применимы ко всем типам рабочих процессов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لعمارة النظام الموزع","يحتاج إلى منطق معاملة التعويض لمعالجة الأخطاء","محدود لأنماط توجيه سير العمل لسجلات الأعمال، لا ينطبق على جميع أنواع سير العمل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
